const BANK = [
  // ── D1 AIMSの基本原則と概念 ──
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 とは何の国際規格か？","qEn":"What international standard is ISO/IEC 42001?","o":["AIマネジメントシステム（AIMS）の要求事項を定める認証可能な規格","目先の売上のみを優先し利用者への影響や苦情を後回しにする","担当者個人の経験と勘だけに頼り客観的な基準や記録を用意しない","価格交渉の結果だけを重視し安全性や適合性の確認を省略する"],"oEn":["A certifiable standard defining requirements for an AI management system (AIMS)","Prioritize only near-term sales, deferring user impact and complaints","Rely solely on one staffer's experience and hunch, with no objective criteria or records","Focus only on the outcome of price negotiations and skip safety/compliance checks"],"a":0,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001 は、AIマネジメントシステム（AIMS）の要求事項を定め、第三者による認証が可能な国際規格である。売上優先や経験と勘だけに頼る運用は、客観的な基準と記録を求める規格の趣旨に反する。","eEn":"ISO/IEC 42001 sets out the requirements for an AI management system (AIMS), and organizations can be certified against it by a third party. Putting sales first or relying on gut feeling without objective criteria and records goes against the standard."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMS（AIマネジメントシステム）の目的に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the purpose of an AIMS?","o":["影響度の大小を問わず全てのAI用途を一律に低リスク扱いし、同じ確認書一枚で済ませる","AIの責任ある開発・提供・利用を体系的に管理する","経営層の承認を得ず現場だけで判断を完結させる","形式だけの手続きにとどめ実質的な検証はしない"],"oEn":["Treats every AI use case as low risk regardless of severity and clears them all with one identical checklist","Systematically manage responsible development, provision, and use of AI","Let the front line decide alone without leadership approval","Keep it a formality with no substantive verification"],"a":1,"e":"AIMSの目的は、AIの責任ある開発・提供・利用を体系的に管理することである。全用途を一律に低リスク扱いして確認書一枚で済ませる運用は、影響度に応じた管理を求める趣旨に合わない。","eEn":"The purpose of an AIMS is to manage the responsible development, provision and use of AI in a systematic way. Treating every use as low risk and settling it with a single confirmation sheet ignores the need to manage according to impact."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"マネジメントシステムとは？","qEn":"What is a management system?","o":["一部の担当者の主観だけで判断し基準を用いない","担当者が変わるたびに方針を作り直し一貫性を持たせない","方針・目的を確立し達成するための、相互に関連する要素の集まり","目に見える指標だけを追い定性的な影響は見ない"],"oEn":["Decide on one staffer's subjective view with no criteria","Redo the policy every time staff change, with no consistency maintained","A set of interrelated elements to establish policy and objectives and achieve them","Chase only visible metrics and ignore qualitative effects"],"a":2,"e":"マネジメントシステムとは、方針と目的を確立し、それを達成するための相互に関連する要素の集まりである。担当者の主観だけで判断し基準を用いない運用は、体系的な仕組みとは言えない。","eEn":"A management system is a set of interrelated elements used to establish policies and objectives and to achieve them. Relying on the subjective judgment of a few people without using criteria is not a systematic mechanism."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 を適用できる組織は？","qEn":"Which organizations can apply ISO/IEC 42001?","o":["外部委託先に丸投げし自社では何も確認しない","手順書に載っている場面だけを対象とし、記載のない新しいAI用途は一切扱わないと決める","規模・業種を問わずAIを開発／提供／利用する組織","人の関与を排除し全てを自動処理に置き換える"],"oEn":["Outsource entirely and verify nothing in-house","Covers only the situations printed in the manual and rules that any new AI use outside it is simply not handled","Any organization developing/providing/using AI, regardless of size/sector","Remove human involvement and automate everything instead"],"a":2,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001 は、規模や業種を問わず、AIを開発・提供・利用する組織に適用できる。外部委託先に丸投げして自社では何も確認しない姿勢は、組織自身の責任を求める規格と相容れない。","eEn":"ISO/IEC 42001 applies to any organization that develops, provides or uses AI, regardless of size or industry. Handing everything to an outside contractor and checking nothing in-house conflicts with the organization's own responsibility."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"責任あるAIの原則に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which are responsible-AI principles?","o":["初版の原則一覧を恒久的に凍結し、法規制やモデルの更新があっても改訂しないと定める","既存のやり方をそのまま踏襲し検証を行わない","好意的な結果だけを選んで報告し不都合は隠す","透明性・説明責任・公平性・人間の監督・説明可能性"],"oEn":["Freezes the first list of principles for good and forbids revision even when laws or the model itself change","Just repeat the existing practice without verification","Report only favorable results and hide inconvenient ones","Transparency, accountability, fairness, human oversight, explicability"],"a":3,"e":"責任あるAIの原則には、透明性・説明責任・公平性・人間の監督・説明可能性が含まれる。初版の原則を凍結して改訂しないという考え方は、法規制やモデルの変化に合わせて見直す姿勢に反する。","eEn":"Responsible AI principles include transparency, accountability, fairness, human oversight and explainability. Freezing the first list of principles and never revising it contradicts the need to review them as laws and models change."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSは他のマネジメントシステム（例：ISO/IEC 27001）と？","qEn":"How does an AIMS relate to other management systems (e.g., ISO/IEC 27001)?","o":["導入初日の点検記録だけを保存し、その後の運用期間中は監視指標を一切取得しない","共通の高位構造（HLS）で統合的に運用しうる","社内向けの説明だけを整え対外説明は省略する","利用者からの異議には一律で対応しないとする"],"oEn":["Keeps only the go-live inspection record and collects no monitoring metric for the rest of the system's life","Can be integrated via the common high-level structure (HLS)","Prepare only internal talking points and skip external disclosure","Refuse to respond to any user objections as a blanket policy"],"a":1,"e":"AIMS（ISO/IEC 42001）は、ISO/IEC 27001などと共通の高位構造（HLS）を持つため、一つの仕組みとして統合して運用できる。導入初日の記録だけで監視指標を取らない運用や、対外説明を省略する運用は、統合の利点ではない。","eEn":"An AIMS (ISO/IEC 42001) shares the common high-level structure (HLS) with ISO/IEC 27001 and similar standards, so they can be operated as one integrated system. Keeping only day-one records with no monitoring metrics, or omitting external explanation, is not a benefit of integration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIシステムの主なステークホルダーに含まれないのは？","qEn":"Who is NOT a key AI stakeholder?","o":["利用者","競合他社の株主","影響を受ける個人（データ主体）","提供者"],"oEn":["Users","A competitor's shareholders","Affected individuals (data subjects)","Providers"],"a":1,"e":"主なステークホルダーは、提供者、利用者、影響を受ける個人（データ主体）である。競合他社の株主はAIシステムの提供や利用、影響を受ける立場にないため、含まれない。","eEn":"Key stakeholders are providers, users and the individuals affected (data subjects). Shareholders of a competitor neither provide, use nor are affected by the AI system, so they are not included."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIガバナンスとAIMSの関係に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the relationship between AI governance and an AIMS?","o":["年間運用費の削減額だけを唯一の評価指標とし、出力品質の確認工程を丸ごと廃止する","担当者を決めず責任の所在をあいまいにする","AIMSはガバナンスを体系的に実装・運用する仕組み","処理速度の向上だけを狙いリスクは無視する"],"oEn":["Makes annual cost savings the only metric and scraps the output-quality review step entirely","Leave accountability ambiguous with no designated owner","An AIMS operationalizes governance systematically","Aim only for faster processing and ignore risk"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSは、AIガバナンスを体系的に実装し運用するための仕組みである。担当者を決めず責任の所在をあいまいにすると、ガバナンスの実装にならない。","eEn":"An AIMS is the mechanism that implements and operates AI governance in a systematic way. Leaving no named owner and keeping responsibility vague means governance is not actually put into practice."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 が『認証可能』であることの意味は？","qEn":"What does it mean that ISO/IEC 42001 is 'certifiable'?","o":["適合の判断を各現場責任者の裁量に全面委任し、共通の判定基準も記録様式も作らない","一度確認すれば十分としその後は見直さない","第三者認証機関の審査を受け適合を証明できる","問題が起きた後にだけ場当たり的に対応する"],"oEn":["Delegates conformity calls wholly to each site lead, with no shared criteria and no record format","Check once and never review it again","A third-party body can audit and certify conformity","React only after a problem occurs, on an ad hoc basis"],"a":2,"e":"認証可能とは、第三者認証機関の審査を受けて、規格への適合を証明できるという意味である。一度確認すれば十分で見直さないという考え方は、継続的な運用と審査を前提とする認証にそぐわない。","eEn":"Certifiable means an independent certification body can audit the organization and confirm conformity with the standard. Checking once and never reviewing again does not fit certification, which assumes ongoing operation and audits."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲（scope）を定める意義は？","qEn":"Why define the AIMS scope?","o":["対象範囲の決定を社内会議の口頭合意だけで終え、利用者向けの説明も公表も行わない","どの活動・AIシステムが対象かを明確にするため","情報を無制限に公開し機密性への配慮を欠く","量さえ確保すれば内容の質は問わないとする"],"oEn":["Settles the scope by a verbal nod in an internal meeting and never explains or publishes it to users","To clarify which activities and AI systems are covered","Disclose information without limit, ignoring confidentiality","As long as volume is secured, quality doesn't matter"],"a":1,"e":"適用範囲（scope）を定めるのは、どの活動やAIシステムが対象かを明確にするためである。範囲を口頭合意だけで決め、利用者への説明や公表をしないと、対象があいまいなままになる。","eEn":"The scope is defined so that it is clear which activities and AI systems are covered. Deciding it only by verbal agreement, with no explanation or publication to users, leaves the coverage ambiguous."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMS運用でトップマネジメントのコミットメントが重要な理由は？","qEn":"Why is top-management commitment important for an AIMS?","o":["AIの企画・開発・監査を情報システム部一つに集約し、独立した検証部門を置かない","契約前の確認だけで契約後は一切見直さない","価格の安さだけを基準に選び他は確認しない","方針・資源・優先順位を定め全社に浸透させるため"],"oEn":["Concentrates planning, development, and audit of AI in the IT department alone, leaving no independent review function","Check only before signing and never review afterward","Choose based on lowest price alone and check nothing else","It sets policy, resources, and priorities and drives org-wide adoption"],"a":3,"e":"トップマネジメントは、方針・資源・優先順位を定めて全社に浸透させる立場にあるため、そのコミットメントが重要である。開発と監査を一部署に集約し独立した検証部門を置かない体制では、牽制が働かない。","eEn":"Top management sets the policy, resources and priorities and spreads them across the company, so its commitment matters. Concentrating planning, development and audit in one department with no independent verification removes checks and balances."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIの便益とリスクの関係に対するAIMSの立場に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to an AIMS's stance on AI benefits vs risks?","o":["社内アンケートの多数意見のみを採用し、少数の利用者が訴える不利益は記録から外す","トラブルの兆候があっても様子見を優先する","価値を活かしつつリスクを体系的に管理し両立させる","承認の記録を残さず口頭のみでやり取りする"],"oEn":["Adopts only the majority answer from an internal survey and drops the harms a small group of users reports","Prioritize wait-and-see even when trouble signs appear","Realize value while systematically managing risk (balance both)","Keep no approval records and rely on verbal exchanges only"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSは、AIの価値を活かしつつリスクを体系的に管理し、両立させる立場に立つ。少数の利用者が訴える不利益を記録から外す運用は、影響を受ける人への配慮を欠く。","eEn":"An AIMS aims to capture the value of AI while managing its risks systematically, so that both are achieved together. Dropping the harms reported by a small number of users from the records ignores the people affected."},
  // ── D2 要求事項（Clause 4–10）──
  {"d":"D2","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 の要求事項の構成（Clause 4–10）に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the requirement structure (Clauses 4–10)?","o":["担当者個人の経験と勘だけに頼り客観的な基準や記録を用意しない","導入直後の一度きりの点検で満足し継続的な監視体制を作らない","組織の状況・リーダーシップ・計画・支援・運用・パフォーマンス評価・改善","特定の利害関係者の意向だけを反映し他の関係者の声を無視する"],"oEn":["Rely solely on one staffer's experience and hunch, with no objective criteria or records","Be satisfied with a single check at rollout and build no ongoing monitoring","Context, leadership, planning, support, operation, performance evaluation, improvement (Clauses 4-10)","Reflect only one stakeholder group's wishes and ignore everyone else's input"],"a":2,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001の要求事項は、組織の状況、リーダーシップ、計画、支援、運用、パフォーマンス評価、改善という、ISOのマネジメントシステム標準に共通の高位構造に沿う。経験と勘だけに頼る運用や、一度きりの点検は構成ではない。","eEn":"The requirements of ISO/IEC 42001 follow the high-level structure common to ISO management system standards: context, leadership, planning, support, operation, performance evaluation and improvement. Relying on individual experience and intuition, or a single inspection, is not the structure."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4『組織の状況』で行うのは？","qEn":"What happens under Clause 4 'context of the organization'?","o":["目先の売上のみを優先し利用者への影響や苦情を後回しにする","問題が起きた部署だけを責め全社的な原因分析を行わない","価格交渉の結果だけを重視し安全性や適合性の確認を省略する","内外の課題と利害関係者を把握しAIMSの適用範囲を定める"],"oEn":["Prioritize only near-term sales, deferring user impact and complaints","Blame only the department where the problem occurred, without any org-wide root-cause analysis","Focus only on the outcome of price negotiations and skip safety/compliance checks","Identify internal/external issues and stakeholders and set the AIMS scope"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 4の組織の状況では、内外の課題と利害関係者の要求を把握し、AIMSの適用範囲を定める。目先の売上のみを優先して苦情を後回しにしたり、価格交渉の結果だけを重視したりすることではない。","eEn":"Under Clause 4, Context of the organization, you identify internal and external issues and stakeholder needs and define the scope of the AIMS. It is not about prioritizing short-term sales and postponing complaints, or focusing only on the results of price negotiation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5『リーダーシップ』の要点に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the essence of Clause 5 'leadership'?","o":["外部の指摘があるまで内部での点検や是正を一切行わない","担当者が変わるたびに方針を作り直し一貫性を持たせない","方針の確立、役割・責任・権限の割当て、コミットメント","短期的な効率だけを重視し長期的な影響を無視する"],"oEn":["Do no internal review or correction until an outside party points it out","Redo the policy every time staff change, with no consistency maintained","Establish policy, assign roles/responsibilities, show commitment","Prioritize only short-term efficiency and ignore long-term effects"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 5のリーダーシップでは、経営層が方針を確立し、役割・責任・権限を割り当て、取組みへのコミットメントを示す。担当者が変わるたびに方針を作り直して一貫性を持たせないことや、外部の指摘があるまで点検しないことではない。","eEn":"Under Clause 5, Leadership, top management establishes the policy, assigns roles, responsibilities and authorities, and shows commitment. It is not about rewriting the policy every time the person in charge changes, or not checking until an outside party points out a problem."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6『計画』で扱うのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 6 'planning' address?","o":["苦情が一定件数に達するまで計画を立てず、目立つ不具合が出てから対応を始める","担当者の異動時に引継ぎ資料を作成しない","リスクと機会への取組み、目的の設定、変更の計画","初期設定のまま放置し定期点検を実施しない"],"oEn":["Draws up no plan until complaints pass some count threshold and acts only after a conspicuous failure","Skip handover documentation whenever staff change roles","Actions for risks and opportunities, objectives, and planning changes","Leave the initial setting untouched and skip periodic checks"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 6の計画では、リスクと機会への取組み、目的の設定、変更の計画を扱う。苦情が一定件数に達するまで計画を立てず、不具合が出てから対応を始めるのは、計画ではなく場当たり的な対応である。","eEn":"Clause 6, Planning, covers actions to address risks and opportunities, setting objectives, and planning changes. Not planning until complaints reach a certain number and starting only after defects appear is ad hoc reaction, not planning."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7『支援』に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is part of Clause 7 'support'?","o":["教育も文書も用意せず、担当者から質問が来たときだけ口頭で個別に回答して終える","リスクの大小を区別せず常に同じ対応で済ませる","資源・力量・認識・コミュニケーション・文書化情報","形式だけの手続きにとどめ実質的な検証はしない"],"oEn":["Provides no training and no documents, answering staff verbally one by one only when a question happens to arrive","Treat all risk levels the same regardless of severity","Resources, competence, awareness, communication, documented information","Keep it a formality with no substantive verification"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7『支援』には、資源・力量・認識・コミュニケーション・文書化情報が含まれる。教育も文書も用意せず、質問が来たときだけ口頭で答える運用は、支援の要求を満たさない。","eEn":"Clause 7 (Support) covers resources, competence, awareness, communication and documented information. Providing no training or documents and answering questions only verbally when asked does not meet the support requirements."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8『運用』でAIMSが求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 8 'operation' require in an AIMS?","o":["運用の可否を当日の担当者の印象だけで決め、影響評価の判定基準も記録様式も定めない","運用の計画・管理と、AIリスク対応・影響評価の実施","経営層の承認を得ず現場だけで判断を完結させる","目に見える指標だけを追い定性的な影響は見ない"],"oEn":["Decides whether to keep running on the duty officer's impression that day, defining neither impact-assessment criteria nor a record format","Operational planning/control and carrying out AI risk treatment and impact assessment","Let the front line decide alone without leadership approval","Chase only visible metrics and ignore qualitative effects"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 8『運用』では、運用の計画と管理に加え、AIリスク対応と影響評価の実施が求められる。当日の担当者の印象だけで可否を決め、判定基準も記録様式も定めない運用は、この要求に反する。","eEn":"Clause 8 (Operation) requires operational planning and control together with AI risk treatment and impact assessment. Deciding on the basis of the day's impression, with no criteria or record format, violates this requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9『パフォーマンス評価』に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is part of Clause 9 'performance evaluation'?","o":["担当者個人の経験と勘だけに頼り客観的な基準や記録を用意しない","導入直後の一度きりの点検で満足し継続的な監視体制を作らない","監視・測定・分析・評価、内部監査、トップマネジメントによるレビュー","特定の利害関係者の意向だけを反映し他の関係者の声を無視する"],"oEn":["Rely solely on one staffer's experience and hunch, with no criteria or records","Be satisfied with a single check at rollout and build no ongoing monitoring","Monitoring/measurement/analysis/evaluation, internal audit, and review by top management","Reflect only one stakeholder group's wishes and ignore everyone else's input"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9『パフォーマンス評価』には、監視・測定・分析・評価、内部監査、トップマネジメントによるレビューが含まれる。導入直後に一度点検しただけで継続的な監視体制を作らないのは、この要求を満たさない。","eEn":"Clause 9 (Performance evaluation) covers monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation, internal audit and management review. A single check right after introduction, with no ongoing monitoring, does not satisfy it."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10『改善』で扱うのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 10 'improvement' address?","o":["最安の見積りだけで改善策を選び中身は見ない","不適合・是正処置と継続的改善","結果が出るまで何もしない","形だけ整えて終わりにする"],"oEn":["Picks the improvement with the lowest quote and never looks at what it contains","Nonconformity, corrective action, and continual improvement","Do nothing until results happen to appear","Tidy up appearances only and stop there"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 10の改善では、不適合が見つかったときの是正処置と、マネジメントシステムの継続的改善を扱う。最安の見積りだけで改善策を選ぶことや、結果が出るまで何もしないこと、形だけ整えて終わりにすることではない。","eEn":"Clause 10, Improvement, covers corrective action when nonconformities are found and continual improvement of the management system. It is not choosing improvements by the cheapest quote alone, doing nothing until results appear, or only going through the motions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AI方針（AI policy）に含めるべきに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to what an AI policy should include?","o":["人の関与を排除し全てを自動処理に置き換える","外部委託先に丸投げし自社では何も確認しない","既存の業務マニュアルの手順を転記するだけで、例外申請の経路も見直し時期も定めない","責任あるAIの方向性・原則・遵守事項・責任の枠組み"],"oEn":["Remove human involvement and automate everything instead","Outsource entirely and verify nothing in-house","Just copies the steps from the existing operations manual, defining no exception route and no review cycle","Direction/principles for responsible AI, commitments, and responsibility framework"],"a":3,"e":"AI方針には、責任あるAIの方向性・原則・遵守事項・責任の枠組みを含める。既存の業務マニュアルを転記するだけで、例外申請の経路や見直し時期を定めない文書は、方針として不十分である。","eEn":"The AI policy should include the direction, principles, compliance commitments and responsibility framework for responsible AI. Simply copying an existing operations manual, with no exception route or review timing, is not an adequate policy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"文書化情報（documented information）の管理で重要なのは？","qEn":"Key to managing documented information?","o":["初版の文書を確定版として凍結し、法改正や運用変更があっても改訂履歴を残さない","既存のやり方をそのまま踏襲し検証を行わない","作成・更新・版・アクセス・保護を適切に管理する","好意的な結果だけを選んで報告し不都合は隠す"],"oEn":["Freezes the first edition as final and keeps no revision history even when law or operations change","Just repeat the existing practice without verification","Properly control creation, update, versioning, access, and protection","Report only favorable results and hide inconvenient ones"],"a":2,"e":"文書化情報の管理では、作成・更新・版・アクセス・保護を適切に管理することが重要である。好意的な結果だけを選んで報告し不都合を隠す扱いは、記録の信頼性を損なう。","eEn":"Documented information must be managed properly for creation, updates, versions, access and protection. Reporting only favorable results and hiding inconvenient ones destroys the reliability of the records."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"力量（competence）と認識（awareness）の違いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to competence vs awareness?","o":["利用者からの異議は窓口で一切受け付けないと定め、記録も残さずその場で却下する","力量は必要な能力の確保、認識は方針・自分の役割の理解","社内向けの説明だけを整え対外説明は省略する","導入時の一回限りの点検で運用中は監視しない"],"oEn":["Rules that the help desk accepts no user objection at all, rejecting each one on the spot without any record","Competence secures needed ability; awareness is understanding policy/one's role","Prepare only internal talking points and skip external disclosure","Inspect only once at rollout and never monitor operations"],"a":1,"e":"力量は業務に必要な能力を確保することで、認識は方針や自分の役割を理解していることである。利用者からの異議を窓口で一切受け付けず記録も残さない対応は、どちらの概念とも関係がない。","eEn":"Competence means securing the abilities the work requires, while awareness means understanding the policy and one's own role. Refusing all objections from users and keeping no record has nothing to do with either concept."},
  // ── D3 Annex A 管理策と SoA ──
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の性質に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the nature of Annex A?","o":["担当者を決めず責任の所在をあいまいにする","担当者の異動時に引継ぎ資料を作成しない","目的別に整理され、リスク対応時に参照する管理策の一覧","結果だけを見て過程の記録は一切残さない"],"oEn":["Leave accountability ambiguous with no designated owner","Skip handover documentation whenever staff change roles","A reference list of controls organized by objectives, consulted during risk treatment","Look only at outcomes and keep no record of the process"],"a":2,"e":"Annex A は、目的別に整理された管理策の一覧で、リスク対応のときに参照する。担当者を決めず責任の所在をあいまいにすることは管理策ではなく、むしろ統制の欠如である。","eEn":"Annex A is a list of controls organized by objective, to be consulted when treating risks. Leaving no named owner and keeping responsibility vague is not a control but a lack of control."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"適用宣言書（SoA）の役割は？","qEn":"Role of the Statement of Applicability (SoA)?","o":["推論の応答時間の短縮だけを目標に掲げ、管理策の適用可否やその理由は記載しない","各管理策の適用可否と理由（除外理由含む）を示す","コスト削減のみを目的として質の確認を省く","問題が起きた後にだけ場当たり的に対応する"],"oEn":["Lists only the target for cutting inference latency and records nothing about control applicability or its rationale","State each control's applicability and rationale (including exclusions)","Aim only at cost cutting and skip quality checks","React only after a problem occurs, on an ad hoc basis"],"a":1,"e":"適用宣言書（SoA）は、各管理策を適用するかどうかと、その理由（除外する場合は除外理由）を示す文書である。推論の応答時間の短縮だけを目標に掲げ、適用可否や理由を書かないものではない。","eEn":"A Statement of Applicability lists whether each control applies and why, including the reasons for any exclusion. It is not a document that sets only a goal of shortening inference response time and says nothing about applicability or reasons."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A が扱う領域に近いのは？","qEn":"Which areas does Annex A cover?","o":["AI方針・組織・資源・AIライフサイクル・データ・第三者関係 等","導入直後の一度きりの点検で満足し継続的な監視体制を作らない","特定の利害関係者の意向だけを反映し他の関係者の声を無視する","担当者個人の経験と勘だけに頼って各段階を判断し、客観的な基準も記録様式も一切用意しない"],"oEn":["AI policy, organization, resources, AI lifecycle, data, third-party relations","Be satisfied with a single check at rollout and build no ongoing monitoring","Reflect only one stakeholder group's wishes and ignore everyone else's input","Relies solely on one staffer's experience and hunch at every stage, preparing no objective criteria and no records"],"a":0,"e":"Annex A の領域には、AI方針、組織、資源、AIライフサイクル、データ、第三者関係などがある。経験と勘だけで判断して基準も記録様式も用意しない運用は、これらの管理策と逆の方向である。","eEn":"The Annex A areas include AI policy, organization, resources, the AI life cycle, data and third-party relationships. Judging by experience and intuition alone, with no criteria or record format, runs opposite to these controls."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムのライフサイクルに関する管理策の狙いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the aim of AI lifecycle controls?","o":["設計段階で一度確認すれば十分とし、運用開始後の再評価も廃棄時の対応も行わない","現場の裁量に完全に委ね基準を一切定めない","情報を無制限に公開し機密性への配慮を欠く","各段階（設計〜運用）で責任ある管理を組み込む"],"oEn":["Treats one check at design time as enough and does no re-assessment in operation or at retirement","Leave it entirely to local discretion with no defined criteria","Disclose information without limit, ignoring confidentiality","Embed responsible management at each stage (design to operation)"],"a":3,"e":"ライフサイクルの管理策は、設計から運用、廃棄に至る各段階で責任ある管理を組み込むことを狙う。設計時に一度確認すれば運用後の再評価も廃棄時の対応も行わないのでは、各段階の管理にならない。","eEn":"Lifecycle controls aim to build responsible management into each stage from design through operation and disposal. Checking once at design and never reassessing after operation begins or handling disposal does not provide management at each stage."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で重視されるのは？","qEn":"What do data-related controls emphasize?","o":["データの出所や前処理の内容を利用者に説明せず、社内の作業記録だけで完結させる","量さえ確保すれば内容の質は問わないとする","データの品質・出所・前処理・取扱いの適切さ","価格の安さだけを基準に選び他は確認しない"],"oEn":["Never explains data provenance or preprocessing to users, closing it out with internal work logs alone","As long as volume is secured, quality doesn't matter","Data quality, provenance, preparation, and proper handling","Choose based on lowest price alone and check nothing else"],"a":2,"e":"データの管理策では、品質・出所・前処理・取扱いが適切かどうかが重視される。データの出所や前処理を利用者に説明せず社内記録だけで完結させると、透明性を確保できない。","eEn":"Data controls focus on whether quality, origin, preprocessing and handling are appropriate. Finishing with internal work records only, without explaining where the data came from or how it was processed, fails to provide transparency."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの情報提供（利用者向け情報）に関する管理策の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of controls on information for AI-system users?","o":["問題が起きた部署の担当者だけを処分し、他部門への横展開や原因分析は行わない","担当者が変わるたびに方針を作り直し一貫性を持たせない","意図した利用・限界・条件を利用者に伝え適切な利用を促す","外部の指摘があるまで内部での点検や是正を一切行わない"],"oEn":["Disciplines only the staff in the department where the problem arose, with no root-cause analysis and no sharing across the organization","Redo the policy every time staff change, with no consistency maintained","Convey intended use, limits, and conditions so users use it appropriately","Do no internal review or correction until an outside party points it out"],"a":2,"e":"利用者向け情報の管理策は、意図した利用、限界、条件を利用者に伝え、適切な利用を促すためのものである。問題部署の担当者だけを処分し原因分析も横展開もしない対応は、この狙いと関係がない。","eEn":"Controls on information for users aim to convey the intended use, limits and conditions so that users use the system appropriately. Punishing only one department's staff, with no root-cause analysis or sharing of lessons, is unrelated to this aim."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者・供給者（サプライヤ）関係の管理策の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of third-party/supplier-relationship controls?","o":["供給者の選定も契約も検収も調達部一つに集約し、技術面の評価は誰も行わない","外部から調達するAI・データの責任と要件を管理する","契約前の確認だけで契約後は一切見直さない","多数派の意見だけを採用し少数派は無視する"],"oEn":["Concentrates supplier selection, contracting, and acceptance in the procurement team alone, so nobody reviews the technical side","Manage responsibilities and requirements for externally sourced AI/data","Check only before signing and never review afterward","Adopt only the majority view and ignore minority concerns"],"a":1,"e":"第三者・供給者関係の管理策は、外部から調達するAIやデータについて、責任と要件を管理するためのものである。調達部に集約して技術面の評価を誰も行わない体制では、要件を確認できない。","eEn":"Supplier and third-party controls manage responsibilities and requirements for AI and data obtained from outside. Centralizing everything in procurement with nobody evaluating the technical side leaves requirements unchecked."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoAで管理策を『除外』する場合に必要なのは？","qEn":"When excluding a control in the SoA, what is needed?","o":["理由は不要","全て適用しなければならない","除外の正当な理由を明記する","黙って除外する"],"oEn":["No reason needed","Every control must apply","Document a valid justification for the exclusion","Exclude silently"],"a":2,"e":"SoAで管理策を除外するときは、除外する正当な理由を明記する必要がある。理由は不要とすることや、黙って除外することは認められず、すべてを適用しなければならないわけでもない。","eEn":"When a control is excluded from the SoA, a justified reason for the exclusion must be stated. Saying no reason is needed, or excluding it silently, is not allowed, and it is also not true that every control must be applied."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"管理策の実施状況を確認する手段に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to a means of checking control implementation?","o":["内部監査・レビュー・証跡の確認","手順書の表紙と目次だけ整えて実施記録は残さない","一律に同じ扱いで済ませる","苦情が来た時だけ対応する"],"oEn":["Internal audit, review, and evidence checks","Tidies up the cover page and table of contents only, keeping no record of what was actually done","Treat every case identically regardless of risk","Act only when a complaint arrives"],"a":0,"e":"管理策が実施されているかは、内部監査やレビュー、実施の証跡を確認して判断する。手順書の表紙と目次だけ整えて実施記録を残さないことや、苦情が来た時だけ対応することでは、実施状況は確認できない。","eEn":"Whether controls are implemented is checked through internal audits, reviews, and evidence of execution. Polishing only the cover and table of contents of procedures with no execution records, or responding only when complaints arrive, cannot confirm implementation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"内部組織（役割・責任）の管理策の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of internal-organization (roles/responsibilities) controls?","o":["導入時に配られた権限設定をそのまま使い続け、異動や退職の際も棚卸しを行わない","承認の記録を残さず口頭のみでやり取りする","トラブルの兆候があっても様子見を優先する","AIに関する役割・責任・権限・報告経路を明確化する"],"oEn":["Keeps the access rights handed out at rollout untouched and never reviews them at transfers or departures","Keep no approval records and rely on verbal exchanges only","Prioritize wait-and-see even when trouble signs appear","Clarify AI roles, responsibilities, authorities, and reporting lines"],"a":3,"e":"内部組織の管理策の狙いは、AIに関する役割・責任・権限・報告経路を明確にすることである。導入時の権限設定を使い続けて異動や退職でも棚卸しをしない運用は、権限と責任を明確に保てない。","eEn":"The internal organization controls aim to clarify roles, responsibilities, authorities and reporting lines for AI. Keeping the permissions set at introduction with no review on transfers or departures cannot keep authority and responsibility clear."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"資源（resources）に関する管理策に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is part of resource controls?","o":["計算資源も人材確保も委託先任せにし、自社では稼働状況も費用も確認しない","人の関与を排除し全てを自動処理に置き換える","目立つ不具合が出るまで対応を先送りにする","データ・計算資源・人材・ツール等の適切な管理"],"oEn":["Leaves compute and staffing entirely to the vendor and checks neither utilization nor cost in-house","Remove human involvement and automate everything instead","Postpone action until a conspicuous failure appears","Proper management of data, compute, people, and tools"],"a":3,"e":"資源の管理策には、データ・計算資源・人材・ツールなどの適切な管理が含まれる。計算資源や人材確保を委託先任せにして稼働状況も費用も確認しない運用は、自組織による管理とは言えない。","eEn":"Resource controls include proper management of data, computing resources, people and tools. Leaving computing and staffing to a contractor and never checking utilization or cost is not management by the organization itself."},
  // ── D4 AIリスクと影響評価 ──
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクアセスメントの位置づけに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the role of AI risk assessment?","o":["短期的な効率だけを重視し長期的な影響を無視する","問い合わせがあった時だけ個別に場当たり対応する","目先の売上のみを優先し利用者への影響や苦情を後回しにする","AIに関するリスクを特定・分析・評価し、リスク対応につなげる"],"oEn":["Prioritize only short-term efficiency and ignore long-term effects","Respond only case-by-case when someone happens to ask","Prioritize only near-term sales, deferring user impact and complaints","Identify, analyze, and evaluate AI-related risks and feed them into risk treatment"],"a":3,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは、AIに関するリスクを特定・分析・評価し、リスク対応につなげる活動である。目先の売上を優先し利用者への影響や苦情を後回しにする姿勢は、リスクの特定を放棄している。","eEn":"AI risk assessment identifies, analyzes and evaluates AI-related risks and leads into risk treatment. Putting short-term sales first and postponing user impacts and complaints abandons the identification of risks."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステム影響評価（impact assessment）の目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of an AI system impact assessment?","o":["AIシステムがもたらす収益を最大化すること","AIの導入とは全く無関係な社内儀式に過ぎない","AIが個人・集団・社会に及ぼす潜在的影響を特定し対処する","AIの応答速度を極限まで高めることに主眼を置く"],"oEn":["To maximize the revenue the AI system brings in","It is an unrelated internal formality with no connection to AI","Identify and address the AI's potential impacts on individuals, groups, and society","To focus solely on maximizing the AI's response speed"],"a":2,"e":"影響評価の目的は、AIが個人や集団、社会に及ぼす潜在的な影響を事前に特定し、対処することである。収益の最大化や応答速度の向上が目的ではなく、導入と無関係な社内の儀式でもない。","eEn":"The purpose of an impact assessment is to identify in advance the potential effects of AI on individuals, groups and society and to address them. It is not about maximizing revenue or pushing response speed, and it is not an internal ritual unrelated to deployment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク基準（risk criteria）を定める意義は？","qEn":"Why define risk criteria?","o":["新商品の広告キャンペーンを企画するため","リスクの評価・受容の判断を一貫させるため","顧客への利用料金を自動的に計算し請求するため","内部監査の実施頻度と監査員の力量要件を定めるため"],"oEn":["To plan an advertising campaign for a new product","To make risk evaluation/acceptance decisions consistent","To automatically calculate and bill customers' usage fees","To define the frequency of internal audits and the competence requirements for auditors"],"a":1,"e":"リスク基準を定めておくと、リスクをどう評価し、どこまで受容するかの判断が人によってぶれず、一貫する。新商品の広告企画や利用料金の請求、内部監査の頻度と監査員の力量要件を決めるためのものではない。","eEn":"Defining risk criteria keeps judgments about how risks are evaluated and how much is accepted consistent from person to person. It is not for planning an ad campaign for a new product, calculating and billing usage fees, or setting audit frequency and auditor competence."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク対応（treatment）の選択肢に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is a risk-treatment option?","o":["人事・経理・総務・広報","色調・音量・処理速度","低減・移転（共有）・受容・回避","広告・仕入れ・出荷・保管"],"oEn":["HR, finance, admin, PR","Hue, volume, processing speed","Mitigate, transfer (share), accept, or avoid the risk","Advertising, procurement, shipping, storage"],"a":2,"e":"リスク対応の基本的な選択肢は、低減、移転（共有）、受容、回避である。人事・経理・総務・広報などの部署名や、色調・音量・処理速度、広告・仕入れ・出荷・保管といった業務は、対応の選択肢ではない。","eEn":"The basic options of risk treatment are reduction, transfer (sharing), acceptance and avoidance. Department names such as HR, accounting and general affairs, attributes such as tone, volume and speed, or business tasks such as advertising, purchasing and shipping are not treatment options."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価はライフサイクルのどこで行うのが望ましい？","qEn":"When in the lifecycle should impact assessment occur?","o":["運用開始後に一度だけ形式的に行う","設計初期から必要に応じ繰り返し実施する","新製品の広告を打つ直前の一回だけ、宣伝用の資料として実施する","影響評価は法律上完全に不要である"],"oEn":["Performed only once, as a formality, after deployment","From early design and repeatedly as needed","Runs it once only, just before the product ad goes out, as material for the campaign","Impact assessment is entirely unnecessary by law"],"a":1,"e":"影響評価は、設計の初期から必要に応じて繰り返し実施するのが望ましい。運用開始後に一度だけ形式的に行うのでは、設計段階で影響を防げず、変化にも追従できない。","eEn":"Impact assessment is best done from the early design stage and repeated as needed. Doing it once, as a formality, after operation starts cannot prevent impacts at design time and cannot keep up with change."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク所有者（risk owner）とは？","qEn":"What is a risk owner?","o":["自分の個人データを提供したデータ主体本人だけを指す","リスク対応に一切関与しない外部者","内部監査の実施だけを担当する監査員","特定リスクの管理に責任・権限を持つ者"],"oEn":["Only the data subject who provided their own personal data, and nobody inside the organization","An outside party with no involvement in risk treatment","An auditor responsible only for conducting internal audits","The person with responsibility/authority to manage a specific risk"],"a":3,"e":"リスク所有者は、特定のリスクを管理する責任と権限を持つ人である。データを提供した本人だけを指すわけではなく、リスク対応に関与しない外部者や、内部監査だけを担う監査員でもない。","eEn":"A risk owner is the person with responsibility and authority for managing a specific risk. The term does not refer only to the data subject who supplied personal data, to an outsider with no role in risk treatment, or to an auditor who only conducts internal audits."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"残余リスク（residual risk）の扱いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to handling residual risk?","o":["残余リスクは必ずゼロになるまで対策を重ねる義務があり、受容の判断は認められない","検出されたリスクをすべて無視して放置する","対応後に残るリスクを評価し受容判断・承認を行う","残余リスクの内容は一切記録しない方針とする"],"oEn":["There is a duty to keep adding controls until residual risk reaches exactly zero, and accepting any of it is not allowed","Ignore and leave unattended all detected risks","Evaluate the risk remaining after treatment and decide/approve acceptance","Adopt a policy of never recording residual risk details"],"a":2,"e":"残余リスクは、対応後になお残るリスクを評価し、受け入れてよいか判断して承認する。ゼロになるまで対策を重ねる義務があり受容は認められないとすることや、検出したリスクの無視、記録を残さない方針は誤りである。","eEn":"Residual risk is the risk left after treatment, and it is evaluated, judged for acceptability and approved. Saying controls must be added until it is zero with no acceptance, ignoring detected risks, or keeping no record of residual risk is wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ISO/IEC 42001のリスク管理と関連の深い規格は？","qEn":"Which standard closely relates to ISO/IEC 42001 risk management?","o":["JEDECが定める半導体メモリの封止材や実装工程に関する技術規格","ISO/IEC 23894（AIリスクマネジメント指針）","国際財務報告基準（IFRS）に基づく企業会計基準","労働基準法に基づく従業員の労働時間管理に関する規則"],"oEn":["JEDEC technical specifications for semiconductor memory packaging and mounting processes","ISO/IEC 23894 (AI risk management guidance)","Corporate accounting standards based on IFRS (International Financial Reporting Standards)","Employee working-hours management rules under the Labor Standards Act"],"a":1,"e":"ISO/IEC 23894 はAIリスクマネジメントの指針で、ISO/IEC 42001 のリスク管理と関連が深い。半導体メモリの封止材に関するJEDECの技術規格や、国際財務報告基準（IFRS）は、AIのリスク管理とは別分野である。","eEn":"ISO/IEC 23894 is guidance on AI risk management and is closely related to the risk management in ISO/IEC 42001. A JEDEC technical standard for semiconductor memory encapsulation and the IFRS accounting standards belong to different fields."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"変更（モデル・データ・用途）が生じたときのリスク・影響評価は？","qEn":"On change (model/data/use), what about risk/impact assessment?","o":["評価自体が不要になる","広告予算にのみ関係する","最初の評価だけで十分である","リスク・影響の再評価が必要になりうる"],"oEn":["Assessment itself becomes unnecessary","Relevant only to the advertising budget","The initial assessment alone suffices","A re-assessment of risks and impacts may be required"],"a":3,"e":"モデル・データ・用途が変わると、リスクや影響も変わるため、再評価が必要になることがある。最初の評価だけで十分とすることや、評価が不要になるとすること、広告予算にのみ関係するとすることは誤りである。","eEn":"A change in model, data or use can change the risks and impacts, so re-assessment may be needed. Saying the first assessment alone is sufficient, that assessment becomes unnecessary, or that it concerns only the advertising budget is wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の結果に対して求められるのは？","qEn":"What is expected regarding impact-assessment results?","o":["文書化し、対応・監督・改善に反映する","評価結果を製品広告の宣伝文句としてのみ使い、対応や改善には結び付けない","結果を経営層にも一切開示せず隠す","確認後ただちに破棄し記録を残さない"],"oEn":["Document them and feed into treatment, oversight, and improvement","Uses the assessment results only as marketing copy for product ads, never feeding them into treatment or improvement","Conceal the results, withholding them even from executives","Discard immediately after review, keeping no record"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価の結果は文書にまとめ、リスクへの対応、監督、改善に反映する。宣伝文句としてのみ使い対応や改善に結び付けないことや、経営層にも開示せず隠すこと、確認後すぐ破棄して記録を残さないことは誤りである。","eEn":"Impact assessment results should be documented and fed into mitigation, oversight and improvement. Using them only as advertising copy without linking them to action, hiding them even from management, or discarding them right after review with no record is wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクに含まれうるのは？","qEn":"Which can be an AI risk?","o":["推論の処理速度や応答時間、スループットが目標値に届かないことだけを指す","サーバーの稼働率・可用性の向上のみを指す","バイアス・安全・プライバシー・セキュリティ・誤用等","インフラ費用や人件費などのコスト削減のみ"],"oEn":["Only inference speed, latency, and throughput falling short of their target numbers","Refers only to improved server uptime and availability","Bias, safety, privacy, security, misuse, etc.","Only cost reductions such as infrastructure and labor expenses"],"a":2,"e":"AIリスクには、バイアス、安全、プライバシー、セキュリティ、誤用などが含まれうる。処理速度の目標未達やコスト削減だけをAIリスクと捉えるのは、利用者や社会への影響を見落とす狭い理解である。","eEn":"AI risks can include bias, safety, privacy, security and misuse. Treating only missed speed targets or cost reduction as AI risk is too narrow and overlooks effects on users and society."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"利害関係者・データ主体への影響を評価する理由は？","qEn":"Why assess impacts on stakeholders/data subjects?","o":["適用宣言書へ除外した管理策とその除外理由を記載するため","利害関係者向けの広告展開を強化するため","権利・利益への不利益を早期に把握し対処するため","データ主体ごとの利用料課金の体系を整え、請求書の送付先を確定させるため"],"oEn":["To record in the Statement of Applicability the controls excluded and the reasons for excluding them","To strengthen advertising campaigns aimed at stakeholders","To catch and address adverse effects on rights/interests early","To build a per-data-subject usage billing scheme and fix where each invoice is sent"],"a":2,"e":"影響評価を行うのは、利害関係者やデータ主体の権利・利益への不利益を早期に把握して対処するためである。データ主体ごとの利用料課金の体系を整えることは、不利益の把握とは別の目的である。","eEn":"Impact assessment is done to find early any harm to the rights and interests of stakeholders and data subjects, and to deal with it. Building a fee scheme for each data subject serves a different purpose."},
  // ── D5 PDCA・内部監査・継続的改善 ──
  {"d":"D5","q":"AIMSの継続的改善に用いられる考え方は？","qEn":"Which model drives continual improvement of an AIMS?","o":["計画を立てず場当たり的に対応する方式","不具合が一件でも出たらAIMS全体を破棄して作り直す方式","PDCA（計画・実行・評価・改善）サイクル","一度構築したら二度と変更しない方式"],"oEn":["An ad-hoc approach taken without any planning","Scrapping and rebuilding the whole AIMS the moment a single defect shows up","The PDCA (Plan-Do-Check-Act) cycle","A once-built, never-modified approach"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSの継続的改善には、計画、実行、評価、改善を繰り返すPDCAサイクルを使う。計画を立てずに場当たりに対応する方式や、一度構築したら二度と変更しない方式、不具合が一件出たら全体を破棄する方式では、改善が続かない。","eEn":"Continual improvement of an AIMS uses the PDCA cycle of plan, do, check and act, repeated. Responding ad hoc without a plan, never changing the system once built, or discarding the whole AIMS when a single defect appears cannot sustain improvement."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of internal audit?","o":["AIMSが要求事項に適合し有効に運用されているか確認する","顧客への利用料金の課金処理を正確に実行し、請求金額の誤りだけを点検すること","新商品の広告キャンペーンの効果を測定し報告すること","外部の第三者認証機関が行う初回審査の日程と審査工数を決めること"],"oEn":["Verify the AIMS conforms to requirements and is effectively operated","Accurately running the customer usage-fee billing process and checking only for errors in the invoiced amounts","Measuring and reporting the effectiveness of a new product's ad campaign","Deciding the schedule and the audit effort for the initial certification audit conducted by an external third-party body"],"a":0,"e":"内部監査は、AIMSが規格の要求事項と自組織の基準に適合し、有効に運用されているかを確認するために行う。利用料金の課金処理の点検や広告の効果測定、外部認証機関の初回審査の日程調整は、内部監査の目的ではない。","eEn":"An internal audit checks whether the AIMS conforms to the requirements and is operating effectively. Checking billing processing for usage fees, measuring ad campaign results, or scheduling an external certification body's initial audit are not its purposes."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューの狙いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the aim of a management review?","o":["トップがAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を評価し改善を決める","来期の社員旅行の行き先・日程・予算をすべて計画する","AIシステムの学習に用いる計算基盤の機種選定と購入手続きを進めること","次期マーケティングキャンペーンの広告予算案と出稿媒体の一覧を承認すること"],"oEn":["Top management evaluates AIMS suitability/adequacy/effectiveness and decides improvements","Plan every detail of next year's company trip: destination, schedule, and budget","Proceeding with the model selection and the purchasing procedures for the compute infrastructure used to train AI systems","Approving the ad-budget proposal and the list of media outlets for the next marketing campaign"],"a":0,"e":"マネジメントレビューは、トップがAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を評価し、改善を決める場である。社員旅行の計画や広告予算の承認は、AIMSの有効性とは関係のない業務である。","eEn":"Management review is where top management evaluates the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS and decides on improvements. Planning an employee trip or approving an advertising budget has nothing to do with AIMS effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"不適合（nonconformity）が見つかったときに求められるのは？","qEn":"When a nonconformity is found, what is required?","o":["不適合の存在を上司に隠して報告しない","不適合をそのまま無視して放置する","発見した不適合の記録を削除して消す","是正処置で不適合の根本原因を除去し再発を防ぐ"],"oEn":["Hide the nonconformity from supervisors without reporting it","Ignore the nonconformity and leave it unaddressed","Delete the record of the discovered nonconformity","Take corrective action to remove the root cause of the nonconformity and prevent recurrence"],"a":3,"e":"不適合が見つかったら、是正処置で根本原因を取り除き、再発を防ぐ。上司に隠して報告しない、そのまま無視して放置する、記録を削除して消すといった対応は、不適合を解決しないばかりか不正にあたる。","eEn":"When a nonconformity is found, corrective action removes the root cause and prevents recurrence. Hiding it from a superior without reporting, ignoring it and leaving it as it is, or deleting its record does not solve it and is improper."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査に求められる性質に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to a required quality of internal audit?","o":["監査結果を一切記録に残さない","監査対象から独立性・客観性を保って実施する","担当者が自分の業務を甘く自己評価する","不都合な監査結果を経営層に隠す"],"oEn":["Keep no record of the audit results at all","Conducted with independence and objectivity from the area being audited","The person leniently self-assesses their own work","Hide unfavorable audit results from management"],"a":1,"e":"内部監査は、監査対象から独立し、客観性を保って実施することが求められる。担当者が自分の業務を甘く自己評価することや、不都合な結果を経営層に隠すこと、結果を記録に残さないことは、監査として成立しない。","eEn":"Internal audits must be performed independently of the audited activity and with objectivity. Staff leniently evaluating their own work, hiding unfavorable results from management, or keeping no record of results does not qualify as an audit."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監視・測定（monitoring & measurement）の目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of monitoring and measurement?","o":["顧客への利用料金を毎月自動的に計算し請求するため","不適合が見つかった際の是正処置の手順と再発防止策を文書化するため","AIMS・AIシステムの状態と有効性を把握し改善に活かす","新サービスの広告展開の状況を確認し報告するため"],"oEn":["To automatically calculate and bill customers' usage fees every month","To document the corrective-action procedure and the recurrence-prevention measures for when a nonconformity is found","Understand the state/effectiveness of the AIMS/AI systems to improve","To check and report on the rollout status of a new service's advertising"],"a":2,"e":"監視・測定は、AIMSやAIシステムの状態と有効性を把握し、改善に生かすために行う。利用料金の自動計算と請求、広告展開の状況確認、是正処置の手順の文書化は、監視・測定の目的ではない。","eEn":"Monitoring and measurement grasp the state and effectiveness of the AIMS and AI systems so they can be improved. Automatically calculating and billing usage fees, checking ad rollout status, or documenting corrective action procedures are not its purposes."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置（corrective action）の有効性は？","qEn":"What about the effectiveness of corrective action?","o":["実施した事実さえあれば結果は記録に残さなくてよいとされる","実施後に有効性を確認することが求められる","是正処置を実施しさえすれば十分とされる","実施すればそれ以上の確認は一切不要"],"oEn":["As long as it was carried out, the outcome is said not to need recording at all","Its effectiveness should be reviewed after implementation","Simply implementing the corrective action is considered enough","No further review at all is needed once implemented"],"a":1,"e":"是正処置は、実施しただけでは足りず、実施後に本当に有効だったかを確認することが求められる。実施すれば十分とすることや、それ以上の確認は一切不要とすること、結果を記録に残さなくてよいとすることは誤りである。","eEn":"Corrective action is not enough just by being carried out; its effectiveness must be verified afterward. Saying that implementing it is sufficient, that no further checking is needed, or that results need not be recorded is wrong."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"第三者認証審査と内部監査の違いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the difference between certification audit and internal audit?","o":["前者は外部認証機関、後者は組織自身が行う","第三者認証審査も組織自身の内部監査部門が実施する","内部監査を外部の認証機関が実施する","両者は全く同一の審査手続きである"],"oEn":["Certification audit is by an external body; internal audit is by the organization itself","The organization's own internal audit department also conducts the third-party certification audit and issues the certificate","An external certification body conducts the internal audit","The two are entirely the same audit procedure"],"a":0,"e":"第三者認証審査は外部の認証機関が行い、内部監査は組織自身が行う。内部監査を外部の認証機関が実施するという説明は、この区別を逆にしており、両者を同一の手続きとみなすのも誤りである。","eEn":"A third-party certification audit is carried out by an external certification body, while an internal audit is carried out by the organization itself. Saying an outside certification body performs the internal audit reverses this distinction."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善（continual improvement）の意味に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the meaning of continual improvement?","o":["一度整備すれば以後は二度と見直さないこと","問題が見つかっても対応せず放置し続けること","AIMSの活動範囲と管理策の数を毎年段階的に縮小していくこと","AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に高める"],"oEn":["Never revisiting it once set up","Leaving problems unaddressed even when found","Progressively shrinking the scope of AIMS activities and the number of controls year by year","Continually enhance the AIMS's suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness"],"a":3,"e":"継続的改善とは、AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に高めていくことである。一度整備したら見直さない、あるいは管理策の数を毎年縮小するという考え方は、改善とは逆の方向である。","eEn":"Continual improvement means steadily raising the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS. Never reviewing it after the first setup, or shrinking the number of controls each year, goes in the opposite direction."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューのインプットに含まれうるのは？","qEn":"Which can be an input to management review?","o":["従業員のプライベートな趣味や嗜好の一覧のみ","製品パッケージのデザインと色見本の一覧のみ","当月のマーケティング広告費の支出額と媒体別の内訳の一覧のみ","監査結果・パフォーマンス・不適合と是正処置・利害関係者の状況等"],"oEn":["Only a list of employees' private hobbies and preferences","Only a list of product-packaging designs and color swatches","Only a list of this month's marketing ad spend with a breakdown by media outlet","Audit results, performance, nonconformities and corrective actions, stakeholder context, etc."],"a":3,"e":"マネジメントレビューのインプットには、監査結果、パフォーマンス、不適合と是正処置、利害関係者の状況などが含まれる。従業員の趣味の一覧や広告費の支出額は、AIMSの有効性を判断する材料にならない。","eEn":"Management review inputs include audit results, performance, nonconformities and corrective actions, and the status of stakeholders. A list of employees' hobbies or advertising spend gives no basis for judging AIMS effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"AIMSのパフォーマンス指標（KPI）を設ける意義は？","qEn":"Value of setting AIMS performance indicators (KPIs)?","o":["有効性を客観的に測り改善の優先順位を決める","新商品の広告キャンペーンの反響と来店者数を測るため","顧客への月次課金額を正確に計算するため","関連する利害関係者の一覧とその要求事項を洗い出すため"],"oEn":["Objectively measure effectiveness and prioritize improvements","To gauge the response to a new product's ad campaign and the resulting store traffic","To accurately calculate customers' monthly billing amounts","To draw up the list of interested parties and identify each of their requirements"],"a":0,"e":"AIMSのKPIは、有効性を客観的な数値で測り、どこから改善すべきか優先順位を決めるために設ける。広告キャンペーンの反響と来店者数や月次課金額の計算、利害関係者の一覧の洗い出しとは目的が違う。","eEn":"AIMS KPIs measure effectiveness objectively so priorities for improvement can be set. Their purpose differs from measuring ad campaign response and store visitors, calculating monthly charges, or listing stakeholders and their requirements."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査プログラム（audit programme）の役割は？","qEn":"Role of an audit programme?","o":["サービス利用者に月額料金を課金する","不適合に対する是正処置の実施記録を保管しておく","顧客向けにターゲット広告を配信する","一連の監査の頻度・範囲・方法・責任を計画的に管理する"],"oEn":["Charge service users a monthly fee","Retaining the records of corrective actions taken against nonconformities","Deliver targeted ads to customers","Plan and manage the frequency, scope, methods, and responsibilities of a set of audits"],"a":3,"e":"監査プログラムは、一連の監査の頻度・範囲・方法・責任を計画的に管理する仕組みである。是正処置の実施記録を保管することは大切だが、監査そのものの計画を管理する役割とは異なる。","eEn":"An audit programme plans and manages the frequency, scope, methods and responsibilities of a series of audits. Keeping records of corrective actions is important, but it is not the role of managing the audit plan itself."},
  // ===== 増量バッチ 1 =====
  // ── D1 基本原則と概念 ──
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIシステムの定義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Closest to the definition of an AI system?","o":["人間が入力した計算式をそのまま実行するだけの単純な表計算マクロ","与えられた目的に対し出力（予測・推奨・決定・コンテンツ等）を生成する機械ベースのシステム","現場の担当者が手作業で参照するだけの、改訂日も版管理もされない紙の手順書に過ぎない","内容が固定され更新されることのない静的なHTMLページに過ぎない"],"oEn":["A simple spreadsheet macro that merely executes formulas a person entered","A machine-based system that generates outputs (predictions, recommendations, decisions, content) for given objectives","Merely a paper procedure manual that staff consult by hand, with no revision date and no version control of any kind","Merely a static HTML page whose content is fixed and never updated"],"a":1,"e":"AIシステムとは、与えられた目的に対して予測・推奨・決定・コンテンツなどの出力を生成する機械ベースのシステムである。入力された計算式を実行するだけの表計算マクロや、内容が固定された静的なHTMLページは、これに当たらない。","eEn":"An AI system is a machine-based system that generates outputs such as predictions, recommendations, decisions or content for a given objective. A spreadsheet macro that just runs an entered formula, or a static HTML page with fixed content, does not qualify."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『AI提供者（provider）』と『AI利用者（user）』の違いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the difference between an AI provider and an AI user?","o":["提供者はAIを開発・提供し、利用者はそれを使う","AIの利用者は必ず同時にその開発者でもあり、両者を分けることはできない","提供者と利用者は完全に同一の役割を担う","提供者は自ら開発したAIを利用できない"],"oEn":["Providers develop/supply AI; users deploy/use it","An AI user is always also its developer, so the two roles can never be told apart","Providers and users play exactly the same role","Providers cannot use the AI they themselves developed"],"a":0,"e":"提供者はAIを開発して提供する側で、利用者はそれを使う側である。利用者が必ず開発者でもあるとか、両者が同一の役割だとかいう説明は、役割の区別を否定しており誤りである。","eEn":"A provider develops and supplies the AI, and a user is the party that uses it. Claiming that every user is also the developer, or that both roles are identical, denies the distinction between the roles."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける『組織の状況（context）』を把握する目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of understanding the organization's context in an AIMS?","o":["AIMSの目的達成に影響する内外の要因を踏まえ範囲・方針を定めるため","内部監査の結果と前回のマネジメントレビュー以降の処置状況をトップへ報告するため","既存顧客向けの月額課金プランを新たに設計し社内へ導入するため","新製品の発売時期に合わせた広告展開のタイミングと出稿媒体を検討し決定するため"],"oEn":["To set scope/policy considering internal/external factors affecting objectives","To report to top management the internal audit results and the status of actions since the previous management review","To newly design a monthly billing plan for existing customers and roll it out internally","To consider and decide the timing and the media outlets for the ad rollout that matches a new product's launch"],"a":0,"e":"組織の状況を把握するのは、AIMSの目的達成に影響する内外の要因を踏まえて、範囲と方針を定めるためである。内部監査の結果をトップへ報告することは、マネジメントレビューへのインプットにあたり、状況把握の目的ではない。","eEn":"The context of the organization is understood so that scope and policy can reflect internal and external factors affecting the AIMS objectives. Reporting internal audit results to top management is an input to the management review, not the purpose of understanding context."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"透明性（transparency）の原則が求めるのは？","qEn":"What does the transparency principle require?","o":["AIの利用や動作について適切に開示・説明できること","内部の仕組みや判断基準を一切外部に開示しないこと","AIの動作記録をいかなる場合も保持せず廃棄すること","AIが生成した出力結果を意図的に隠し続けること"],"oEn":["Appropriate disclosure/explanation of AI use and behavior","Never disclosing internal mechanisms or decision criteria to outsiders at all","Never retaining and discarding all records of the AI's behavior under any circumstance","Deliberately continuing to hide the outputs the AI generated"],"a":0,"e":"透明性の原則は、AIの利用や動作について適切に開示し、説明できることを求める。仕組みや判断基準を一切外部に開示しない、あるいは動作記録を保持せず廃棄するのは、この原則に反する。","eEn":"The transparency principle requires that the use and operation of AI can be disclosed and explained appropriately. Disclosing no mechanisms or criteria externally, or discarding operation records, goes against it."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明責任（accountability）の原則が意味するのは？","qEn":"What does the accountability principle mean?","o":["AIが下した判断には誰も一切責任を負わないこと","組織内の責任をすべて外部委託先へ転嫁すること","意思決定に関する記録を判断の当日中にすべて速やかに廃棄すること","AIの結果や意思決定に対し責任の所在を明確にすること"],"oEn":["No one bears any responsibility at all for decisions the AI made","Shifting all internal responsibility entirely onto an outside vendor","Promptly discarding every record about the decisions on the same day the call is made","Clear ownership of responsibility for AI outcomes/decisions"],"a":3,"e":"説明責任とは、AIの結果や意思決定について責任の所在を明確にすることである。誰も責任を負わない、責任をすべて外部委託先へ転嫁する、記録を当日中に廃棄するといった扱いは、この原則に反する。","eEn":"Accountability means making clear who is responsible for AI outcomes and decisions. Having nobody take responsibility, shifting all of it to an outside contractor, or discarding decision records the same day all violate the principle."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"公平性（fairness）の原則で避けるべきは？","qEn":"What does the fairness principle seek to avoid?","o":["AIサーバーが消費する電力量の多さ","AIシステムの運用にかかる月々のコストの高さだけ","推論結果が出るまでの処理時間の長さ","特定集団への不当な差別的影響（バイアス）"],"oEn":["The large amount of power AI servers consume","Only the high monthly cost of operating the AI system, nothing about its outcomes","The length of processing time until the inference result appears","Unjust discriminatory impact (bias) on particular groups"],"a":3,"e":"公平性の原則は、特定の集団に不当な差別的影響（バイアス）が及ぶことを避けるよう求める。電力消費量の多さや運用コストの高さ、処理時間の長さは効率の問題で、公平性の原則が避けるべきものではない。","eEn":"The fairness principle requires avoiding unjust discriminatory impact (bias) on particular groups. High power consumption, high monthly operating cost, and long processing time are efficiency issues, not what the fairness principle seeks to avoid."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"人間の監督（human oversight）が重要になるのは？","qEn":"When does human oversight matter most?","o":["社内でのみ完結する軽微な事務処理","顧客への広告バナーを配信する作業","個人や社会に重大な影響を与える判断","資料のテーマカラーを選ぶだけの作業"],"oEn":["Minor administrative tasks that stay internal","The task of delivering ad banners to customers","Decisions with significant impact on people or society","Merely choosing a document's theme color"],"a":2,"e":"人間の監督が重要になるのは、個人や社会に重大な影響を与える判断である。社内で完結する軽微な事務処理や、広告バナーの配信、資料の色選びは、影響が小さく、厳格な人間の監督は必須ではない。","eEn":"Human oversight matters most for decisions that have a major impact on individuals or society. Minor internal paperwork, serving ad banners or choosing a slide color have little impact and do not call for strict oversight."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明可能性（explicability/explainability）が支えるのは？","qEn":"What does explicability support?","o":["推論にかかる処理速度をひたすら高めることのみ","利害関係者がAIの挙動・根拠を理解し信頼できること","顧客への利用料金の課金処理と請求書発行を自動化する仕組みのみ","適用宣言書に記載した管理策の一覧を毎年更新できることのみ"],"oEn":["Only relentlessly increasing inference processing speed","Stakeholders understanding/trusting AI behavior and rationale","Only the mechanism that automates customer usage billing and invoice issuance","Only being able to update the list of controls recorded in the Statement of Applicability every year"],"a":1,"e":"説明可能性は、利害関係者がAIの挙動とその根拠を理解し、信頼できる状態を支える。推論速度を高めるだけのものや、課金処理と請求書発行の自動化、適用宣言書の管理策一覧の毎年の更新に限られるものではない。","eEn":"Explainability supports stakeholders in understanding the AI's behavior and its grounds, and so in trusting it. It is not limited to raising inference speed, automating billing and invoicing, or updating the list of controls in the statement of applicability each year."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSが『継続的』であるべき理由は？","qEn":"Why should an AIMS be 'continual'?","o":["AIを取り巻く環境は一切変化しないため","AIMSに関する記録はそもそも一切不要なため","AI・データ・規制・リスクが変化し続けるため","一度整備すれば以後は完璧であり続けるため"],"oEn":["Because the environment surrounding AI never changes at all","Because records related to the AIMS are entirely unnecessary to begin with","Because AI, data, regulation, and risk keep changing","Because once set up it remains perfect forever"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSが継続的であるべきなのは、AI、データ、規制、リスクが変化し続けるためである。環境が一切変化しないとか、一度整備すれば完璧であり続けるとか、記録が一切不要という前提は誤りである。","eEn":"An AIMS must be continual because AI, data, regulation and risks keep changing. The premises that the environment never changes, that a system stays perfect once set up, or that records are not needed at all are wrong."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲に含めるか判断する際に考慮するのは？","qEn":"What to consider when deciding AIMS scope inclusion?","o":["社内で作成する文書や資料に使用するフォントの種類と文字の大きさの指定","内部監査員として指名する要員の人数とその年次の研修の受講記録の有無","次年度に予定しているマーケティング広告予算の総額","組織の役割（提供/利用）・利害関係者の要求・対象AIシステム"],"oEn":["The font family and the point size specified for documents and materials created internally","The number of personnel designated as internal auditors and whether their annual training attendance records exist","The total marketing advertising budget planned for next year","Org role (provider/user), stakeholder requirements, covered AI systems"],"a":3,"e":"AIMSの適用範囲は、組織の役割（提供者か利用者か）、利害関係者の要求、対象となるAIシステムを考慮して決める。文書のフォントや文字の大きさ、内部監査員の人数と研修記録、次年度の広告予算の総額は判断材料ではない。","eEn":"The scope of an AIMS is decided by considering the organization's role (provider or user), stakeholders' requirements and the AI systems concerned. Fonts and character sizes in documents, the number of internal auditors and their training records, or next year's advertising budget are not factors."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『責任あるAI（responsible AI）』の考え方に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Closest to the idea of 'responsible AI'?","o":["規制当局による監視や監査を、拠点の移転や記録の非開示などあらゆる手段で回避すること","リスク管理のための人間による監督を完全に排除すること","倫理・法・安全に配慮しリスクを管理しつつAIの便益を実現する","利用者や規制当局への説明責任を意図的に果たさないこと"],"oEn":["Evading regulatory oversight and audits by any means, such as relocating sites or withholding records","Completely removing human oversight intended for risk management","Realize AI benefits while managing risk with ethics, law, and safety in mind","Deliberately failing to fulfill accountability to users and regulators"],"a":2,"e":"責任あるAIとは、倫理・法・安全に配慮してリスクを管理しつつ、AIの便益を実現する考え方である。人間による監督を排除したり、規制当局への説明責任を果たさなかったりするのは、これに反する。","eEn":"Responsible AI means realizing the benefits of AI while managing risk with regard to ethics, law and safety. Removing human oversight, or deliberately failing to explain to regulators, runs against it."},
  { d:"D1", q:"AIMSと品質・情報セキュリティのマネジメントシステムの共通点は？", qEn:"Commonality between AIMS and quality/security management systems?", o:["いずれもPDCAとISO共通の高位構造（HLS）に基づく","いずれも違反者への罰則を定める法令である","いずれもAI分野にのみ適用される専用規格である","いずれも財務諸表の作成に関する会計基準である"], oEn:["All are based on PDCA and the ISO-wide high-level structure (HLS)","All are laws that stipulate penalties for violators","All are specialized standards applicable only to the AI field","All are accounting standards for preparing financial statements"], a:0, e:"AIMS、品質、情報セキュリティのマネジメントシステムは、PDCAの考え方とISO共通の高位構造（HLS）に基づく点が共通する。いずれも罰則を定める法令ではなく、AI専用規格でも、会計基準でもない。", eEn:"AIMS and quality and information security management systems share the PDCA approach and the common ISO high-level structure (HLS). None of them is a law setting penalties for violators, a standard dedicated only to AI, or an accounting standard." },
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルの一般的な段階に含まれないのは？","qEn":"Which is NOT a typical AI lifecycle stage?","o":["広告の出稿・宣伝","設計・開発","運用・監視","検証・評価"],"oEn":["Ad placement and promotion","Design/development","Operation/monitoring","Verification/validation"],"a":0,"e":"AIライフサイクルの段階は、設計・開発、検証・評価、運用・監視などである。広告の出稿や宣伝はAIシステム自体の活動段階ではないため、ライフサイクルの一般的な段階には含まれない。","eEn":"Typical AI life cycle stages are design and development, verification and evaluation, and operation and monitoring. Placing ads and promotion is not a stage of the AI system itself, so it is not part of the life cycle."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMS導入の初期に行う『ギャップ分析』の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of an initial gap analysis for AIMS adoption?","o":["新商品発売時の広告効果を数値で測定する","倉庫にある部材や製品の在庫数を確認する","現状と規格要求の差を把握し実装計画に反映する","製品パッケージや広報物の色調と印刷の紙質を微調整する"],"oEn":["Numerically measure ad effectiveness at a new product's launch","Check the stock count of materials and products in the warehouse","Find the gap between current state and requirements to plan implementation","Fine-tuning the color tone and the paper stock of product packaging and PR materials"],"a":2,"e":"ギャップ分析は、現状と規格の要求事項との差を把握し、その差を埋める実装計画に反映するために行う。広告効果の数値測定や倉庫の在庫確認、パッケージの色調と紙質の調整とは目的が違う。","eEn":"Gap analysis identifies the difference between the current state and the standard's requirements and reflects it in the implementation plan. Its purpose differs from measuring advertising effect numerically, counting stock in a warehouse, or fine-tuning package colors and paper quality."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける『利害関係者のニーズと期待』を扱う理由は？","qEn":"Why address 'needs and expectations of interested parties'?","o":["社内資料のテーマカラーと表紙の様式を統一するため","適切な範囲・要求事項・統制を定めるため","顧客への月額課金体系を新たに作るため","新商品の広告展開をさらに強化するため"],"oEn":["To unify the theme color and the cover-page format of internal materials","To determine proper scope, requirements, and controls","To newly create a monthly billing scheme for customers","To further strengthen advertising for a new product"],"a":1,"e":"利害関係者のニーズと期待を扱うのは、AIMSの適用範囲、要求事項、統制を適切に定めるためである。社内資料のテーマカラーと表紙様式の統一や、月額課金体系の新設、広告展開の強化とは関係がない。","eEn":"Stakeholders' needs and expectations are addressed so the scope, requirements and controls of the AIMS can be set properly. This has nothing to do with unifying theme colors and cover formats of internal documents, creating a new monthly pricing scheme, or strengthening ad rollout."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIの『意図した目的（intended purpose）』を明確化する意義は？","qEn":"Value of clarifying an AI system's intended purpose?","o":["適切な利用範囲とリスク評価の基礎になるため","利用者ごとの課金額を個別に設定するため","製品パッケージのデザインと色を決めるため","新製品発売にあわせた広告文言を作成するため"],"oEn":["It grounds proper use boundaries and risk assessment","To individually set the billing amount for each user","To decide on the design and color of the product packaging","To draft advertising copy timed to a new product's launch"],"a":0,"e":"意図した目的を明確にすると、適切な利用範囲が定まり、リスク評価の基礎にもなる。利用者ごとの課金額の設定や広告文言の作成は、AIの用途とリスクを定める作業ではない。","eEn":"Defining the intended purpose fixes the appropriate scope of use and forms the basis of risk assessment. Setting charges per user or writing advertising copy does not define the AI's use or its risks."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける『プロセスアプローチ』の利点は？","qEn":"Benefit of the process approach in an AIMS?","o":["特定の担当者一人だけに手順を依存させ、引継ぎ資料も作らず属人化を進める","業務効率化と称して記録類をすべて減らしていく","相互に関連する活動を体系的に管理し一貫した結果を得る","関連のない単発作業をその場しのぎで寄せ集める"],"oEn":["Makes the procedure depend on one specific staff member and entrenches that reliance with no handover notes","Progressively reduce all records under the guise of efficiency","Systematically manage interrelated activities for consistent results","Haphazardly gather unrelated one-off tasks as stopgaps"],"a":2,"e":"プロセスアプローチの利点は、相互に関連する活動を体系的に管理して、一貫した結果を得られることである。特定の担当者だけに手順を依存させ引継ぎ資料も作らない運用は、属人化を進め一貫性を損なう。","eEn":"The benefit of the process approach is that interrelated activities are managed systematically and give consistent results. Making procedures depend on one person with no handover documents encourages personal dependence and loses consistency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの成功に不可欠な組織文化の要素は？","qEn":"Cultural element essential to AIMS success?","o":["責任あるAIへのコミットメントと学習・改善の姿勢","四半期ごとの短期的な利益のみを追求する姿勢","AIのリスクを現場任せにする経営層の無関心な姿勢と放任の慣行","問題を組織内外に一切明かさない秘匿主義の文化"],"oEn":["Commitment to responsible AI and a learning/improvement mindset","A stance of pursuing only short-term quarterly profit","Executives' indifference to AI risk and the habit of leaving it entirely to the front line","A culture of secrecy that never reveals problems inside or outside"],"a":0,"e":"AIMSの成功には、責任あるAIへのコミットメントと、学習・改善の姿勢という組織文化が欠かせない。短期的な利益だけを追い、問題を組織内外に明かさない文化では、リスクの管理も改善もできない。","eEn":"A culture of commitment to responsible AI and willingness to learn and improve is essential for AIMS success. A culture that chases short-term profit only and hides problems cannot manage risks or improve."},
  // ── D2 要求事項（Clause 4–10）──
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.1『組織及びその状況の理解』で特定するのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 4.1 identify?","o":["AIMSに関連する内外の課題","社内資料で使うフォントの種類","来期に予定する製品の値上げ額","新商品の広告キャッチコピー案"],"oEn":["Internal and external issues that are relevant to the AIMS","The font type used in internal materials","The planned price increase for the product next term","Draft ad catchphrases for a new product"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.1 では、AIMSに関連する内部と外部の課題を特定する。資料のフォントの種類や製品の値上げ額、広告のキャッチコピー案は、AIMSの目的達成に影響する課題には当たらない。","eEn":"Clause 4.1 requires identifying the internal and external issues relevant to the AIMS. Document fonts, planned price increases and advertising slogans are not issues that affect achieving the AIMS objectives."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2『利害関係者のニーズ及び期待の理解』で行うのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 4.2 involve?","o":["倉庫にある製品の在庫状況を確認する","利害関係者の一覧を宛先として広告メールを配信する","関連する利害関係者とその要求事項を特定する","内部監査の結果を踏まえて是正処置を計画し実施する"],"oEn":["Check the inventory status of products in the warehouse","Sending advertising emails using the list of interested parties as the mailing target","Identify relevant interested parties and their requirements","Planning and carrying out corrective actions based on the internal audit results"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 4.2では、AIMSに関連する利害関係者を特定し、その要求事項を明らかにする。倉庫の在庫確認や、利害関係者の一覧を宛先にした広告メールの配信、内部監査後の是正処置の計画は、この箇条の内容ではない。","eEn":"Clause 4.2 identifies the interested parties relevant to the AIMS and determines their requirements. Checking warehouse stock, sending ad emails to the stakeholder list, or planning corrective action after an internal audit is not what this clause covers."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.3『適用範囲の決定』で考慮しないのは？","qEn":"What is NOT considered in Clause 4.3 (scope)?","o":["利害関係者の要求","競合の広告予算","組織の活動・製品・サービス","内外の課題"],"oEn":["Interested-party requirements","A competitor's ad budget","The org's activities/products/services","Internal/external issues"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 4.3 で適用範囲を決めるときは、内外の課題、利害関係者の要求、組織の活動・製品・サービスを考慮する。競合の広告予算はAIMSの範囲に影響しないため、考慮しない。","eEn":"When setting the scope under Clause 4.3, the organization considers internal and external issues, stakeholder requirements, and its activities, products and services. A competitor's advertising budget does not affect the AIMS scope and is not considered."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.4 が求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 4.4 require?","o":["AIMSを確立・実施・維持・継続的に改善すること","AIMSに関する文書は一切作成しないこと","一度作ったAIMSは認証取得後に一切変更してはならないとすること","AIMSについて内部監査を一切実施しないこと"],"oEn":["Establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve the AIMS","Never creating any documentation related to the AIMS","Ruling that once built, the AIMS must never be changed after certification is obtained","Never conducting internal audits of the AIMS at all"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.4 は、AIMSを確立し、実施し、維持し、継続的に改善することを求める。文書を作成しない、認証後は一切変更しない、内部監査をしないといった扱いは、この要求に反する。","eEn":"Clause 4.4 requires the organization to establish, implement, maintain and continually improve the AIMS. Creating no documents, never changing it after certification, or skipping internal audits all contradict the requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1『リーダーシップ及びコミットメント』で経営層が示すのは？","qEn":"What must top management show under Clause 5.1?","o":["新商品発売キャンペーンの広告予算と媒体出稿計画の承認","内部監査の個々のチェックリスト項目を自ら記入すること","AIMSの有効性に対する責任とコミットメント","日常業務で使う事務用品の購入手続き"],"oEn":["Approving the ad budget and the media plan for a new-product launch campaign","Filling in each individual item of the internal audit checklist themselves","Accountability and commitment to AIMS effectiveness","The purchasing procedure for everyday office supplies"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 5.1 では、経営層がAIMSの有効性に対する責任とコミットメントを示す。内部監査のチェックリストを自ら記入することや、事務用品の購入手続きは、リーダーシップの発揮ではなく個別の業務である。","eEn":"Under Clause 5.1, top management shows responsibility and commitment for the effectiveness of the AIMS. Filling in internal audit checklist items or handling office supply purchases are individual tasks, not leadership."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.2『方針（AI policy）』の要件に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the requirement of Clause 5.2 (AI policy)?","o":["新製品の発売にあわせて大規模な広告キャンペーンを打つ","全社員に最新のブランドガイドラインと統一色見本、社名ロゴの使用規定を配布する","国内外すべての拠点倉庫にある部材在庫を一元的に管理する","目的に適し、枠組みを与え、コミットメントを含む方針を確立・伝達する"],"oEn":["Launch a large-scale ad campaign timed to a new product's release","Distributing the latest brand guidelines, unified color swatches, and logo usage rules to every employee","Centrally manage parts inventory across every domestic and overseas warehouse","Establish/communicate a policy that fits purpose, sets a framework, and includes commitments"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 5.2 は、組織の目的に適し、目的設定の枠組みを与え、コミットメントを含むAI方針を確立し、伝達することを求める。広告キャンペーンやブランドガイドラインの配布、在庫管理は、方針の要件ではない。","eEn":"Clause 5.2 requires an AI policy that suits the organization's purpose, gives a framework for objectives and includes commitments, and that is established and communicated. Ad campaigns, brand guidelines and inventory management are not policy requirements."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.3 が扱うのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 5.3 address?","o":["毎月発生する経理・会計処理をまとめて実施する","新商品の広告物のデザイン制作","組織の役割・責任・権限の割当てと伝達","製品カラーバリエーションの管理"],"oEn":["Batching and carrying out the accounting/bookkeeping that arises every month","Design and production of new-product ad materials","Assigning and communicating roles, responsibilities, and authorities","Management of product color variations"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 5.3は、組織内の役割・責任・権限を割り当て、関係者に伝達することを求める。毎月の経理・会計処理の実施や、広告物のデザイン制作、製品カラーバリエーションの管理を扱う箇条ではない。","eEn":"Clause 5.3 requires that roles, responsibilities and authorities within the organization be assigned and communicated. It does not deal with carrying out monthly bookkeeping and accounting, designing advertising materials, or managing product color variations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1『リスク及び機会への取組み』の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of Clause 6.1 (actions to address risks and opportunities)?","o":["新製品パッケージのテーマカラーを選ぶこと","望ましくない影響を防ぎ・低減し、望ましい効果を高める","SNS等を活用して新機能を積極的に広告すること","利用状況に応じて追加のオプション料金を毎月自動で課金すること"],"oEn":["Choosing the theme color of a new product's packaging","Prevent/reduce undesired effects and enhance desired ones","Actively advertising new features via social media","Automatically charging an extra optional fee each month according to usage"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.1 の狙いは、望ましくない影響を防ぎ・低減し、望ましい効果を高めることである。パッケージの色選びや広告展開、毎月の追加課金は、リスクと機会への取組みとは関係がない。","eEn":"The aim of Clause 6.1 is to prevent or reduce undesired effects and to enhance desired ones. Choosing package colors, advertising and monthly extra billing have no relation to addressing risks and opportunities."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1 に含まれるAIMS固有の活動は？","qEn":"AIMS-specific activity within Clause 6.1?","o":["製品パッケージや広報資料全般の色調整とデザイン確認作業","AIリスクアセスメントとAIリスク対応、AIシステム影響評価","全拠点の倉庫にある原材料と完成品の在庫数の確認作業","新商品発売キャンペーンの広告効果測定とSNS上の反響分析および費用対効果の算出"],"oEn":["Color adjustment and design review work for product packaging and PR materials","AI risk assessment/treatment and AI system impact assessment","Checking stock counts of raw materials and finished goods across all warehouses","Measuring ad effectiveness, analyzing social-media buzz, and computing ROI for a new-product campaign"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.1 に含まれるAIMS固有の活動は、AIリスクアセスメント、AIリスク対応、AIシステム影響評価である。パッケージの色調整、在庫確認、広告効果測定は、AIMS固有の計画活動ではない。","eEn":"The AIMS-specific activities in Clause 6.1 are AI risk assessment, AI risk treatment and AI system impact assessment. Adjusting package colors, checking inventory and measuring ad effectiveness are not AIMS planning activities."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2『AIMS目的』が満たすべき性質は？","qEn":"Property AIMS objectives (Clause 6.2) should have?","o":["測定可能・監視・伝達・更新が可能であること","一度設定したら二度と変更が利かない仕組みであること","内容が一切外部に公表されないこと","内容が抽象的で誰にも測定できないこと"],"oEn":["Measurable, monitored, communicated, and updated","Being a mechanism that, once set, can never be changed again","Never being disclosed externally at all","Being so abstract that no one can measure it"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 6.2 のAIMS目的は、測定可能で、監視・伝達・更新ができるものでなければならない。誰にも測定できない抽象的な目的や、変更が利かない仕組みでは、達成度を評価できない。","eEn":"AIMS objectives under Clause 6.2 must be measurable, monitored, communicated and updated. An abstract objective nobody can measure, or one that can never be changed, makes it impossible to evaluate achievement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.1『資源』が求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 7.1 (resources) require?","o":["来期のテレビCM向けの広告費を前年比で増やすこと","AIMSに必要な資源を決定し提供する","安全在庫を多めに持つよう指示する","製品ロゴやパッケージの色を決める"],"oEn":["Increasing next term's TV-commercial ad budget over the prior year","Determine and provide resources needed for the AIMS","Instruct that extra safety stock be kept","Decide the color of the product logo and packaging"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 7.1の資源は、AIMSの確立・実施・維持・改善に必要な資源を決定し、提供することを求める。テレビCMの広告費を前年比で増やすことや、安全在庫を多めに持つこと、ロゴやパッケージの色を決めることではない。","eEn":"Clause 7.1, Resources, requires determining and providing the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain and improve the AIMS. It is not about increasing TV commercial spending year on year, holding more safety stock, or choosing logo and package colors."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.2『力量』で求められるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 7.2 (competence) require?","o":["必要な力量を明確化し、教育・訓練等で確保・評価する","実施した教育・訓練の記録を一切残さない","必要な力量の有無を一切確認せず、空いている担当者を順番に配属する","担当者の知識や経験は一切問わないとする"],"oEn":["Define needed competence and ensure/evaluate it via training, etc.","Keeping no record at all of training that was conducted","Assigning whoever happens to be free, in turn, without ever checking the needed competence","Deciding that a person's knowledge or experience does not matter at all"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.2の力量では、必要な力量を明確にし、教育・訓練などで確保して、有効だったか評価する。力量の有無を確認せず空いている担当者を配属したり、知識や経験を問わなかったり、教育の記録を残さなかったりするのは不適合である。","eEn":"Clause 7.2, Competence, requires defining the needed competence, securing it through education or training, and evaluating it. Assigning whoever is free without checking competence, ignoring knowledge and experience, or keeping no training records is nonconforming."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.3『認識』で従業員が理解すべきは？","qEn":"What must staff understand under Clause 7.3 (awareness)?","o":["適用宣言書に記された管理策の除外理由の全文","自社が出稿する広告のクリック率","方針・自らの貢献・不適合の意味合い","同業他社の直近の四半期売上高"],"oEn":["The full text of the exclusion justifications recorded in the Statement of Applicability","The click-through rate of ads the company runs","The policy, their contribution, and implications of nonconformity","A competitor's most recent quarterly revenue"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.3 では、従業員が方針、AIMSの有効性に対する自らの貢献、不適合の意味合いを理解する必要がある。広告のクリック率や同業他社の売上高は、AIMSへの認識とは関係がない。","eEn":"Under Clause 7.3, employees need to understand the policy, their own contribution and the implications of nonconformity. Ad click rates and a competitor's quarterly sales are unrelated to awareness of the AIMS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.4『コミュニケーション』で決めるのは？","qEn":"What is decided under Clause 7.4 (communication)?","o":["何を・いつ・誰と・どのように伝えるか","内部監査を年に何回行い、誰が監査員を務めるか","社内資料で使うフォント種別だけ","承認済みの次年度広告予算総額だけ"],"oEn":["What, when, with whom, and how to communicate","How many times a year internal audits are run and who serves as the auditor","Only the font types used in internal materials","Only the approved total advertising budget for next year"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.4 では、何を、いつ、誰と、どのように伝えるかを決める。内部監査の回数や監査員の指名は監査の計画であり、コミュニケーションの取り決めとは別の事項である。","eEn":"Clause 7.4 requires deciding what to communicate, when, with whom and how. The number of internal audits per year and who serves as auditor belong to audit planning, not to communication arrangements."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5『文書化情報』で求められる管理は？","qEn":"What control is required under Clause 7.5 (documented information)?","o":["文書の作成も更新も承認も管理せず、保存場所も保持期間も定めずに放置する","従業員であれば誰でも自由に文書を削除してよい","作成・更新の管理と、識別・保護・アクセス・保持の管理","バージョン管理を行うかは各自の任意とする"],"oEn":["Leaves creation, update, and approval uncontrolled, fixing neither a storage location nor a retention period","Allowing any employee to freely delete documents","Control of creation/update and of identification/protection/access/retention","Leaving whether to apply version control up to each individual"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.5 では、作成・更新の管理に加えて、識別・保護・アクセス・保持の管理が求められる。誰でも自由に削除してよい、版管理は各自の任意とする、といった扱いは、管理の要求を満たさない。","eEn":"Clause 7.5 requires control of creation and updating, as well as identification, protection, access and retention. Letting anyone delete documents freely, or making version control optional, fails the control requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1『運用の計画及び管理』が求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 8.1 require?","o":["要求事項を満たすためのプロセスを計画・実施・管理する","トップマネジメントがAIMSの適切性と有効性を年次で評価し決定する","需要変動に備えて常に必要以上の在庫を持つ","新製品の発売に合わせて大々的に広告を打つ"],"oEn":["Plan, implement, and control processes to meet requirements","Top management evaluating the suitability and effectiveness of the AIMS annually and making decisions","Always keep more stock on hand than needed to prepare for demand fluctuations","Run a large-scale ad campaign to coincide with a new product's launch"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 8.1 は、要求事項を満たすために必要なプロセスを計画し、実施し、管理することを求める。トップによる年次の評価は9章のレビュー、必要以上の在庫を持つことや広告は運用計画の要求とは関係がない。","eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires planning, implementing and controlling the processes needed to meet the requirements. An annual evaluation by top management belongs to the review in Clause 9, and stock levels or advertising are unrelated."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.1『監視・測定・分析・評価』で決めるのは？","qEn":"What is decided under Clause 9.1?","o":["次回キャンペーン用の広告文と掲載媒体の候補だけを扱う","全社資料で統一するフォントの種類だけ","何を監視・測定し、いつ・どう分析・評価するか","AI方針をどの範囲まで組織の外部の関係者へ公開するか"],"oEn":["Dealing only with the ad copy and the placement for the next campaign","Only the font type to be unified across company materials","What to monitor/measure and when/how to analyze/evaluate","To what extent the AI policy is disclosed to parties outside the organization"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9.1 では、何を監視・測定するか、いつ、どのように分析・評価するかを決める。広告文の候補やフォントの種類、方針の公開範囲は、監視・測定の方法を定める内容ではない。","eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires deciding what to monitor and measure, and when and how to analyze and evaluate it. Advertising copy candidates, font choices and the range of policy disclosure do not define monitoring and measurement methods."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2『内部監査』の目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of Clause 9.2 (internal audit)?","o":["広報資料やパッケージ全般の色調を調整すること","新商品の広告キャンペーンの効果を媒体別に測定し集計して報告すること","AIMSが要求事項に適合し有効に実施されているか確認する","全拠点倉庫にある原材料の在庫数を確認すること"],"oEn":["Adjusting the color tone across PR materials and packaging","Measuring and tallying a new product's ad-campaign results by media outlet","Confirm the AIMS conforms and is effectively implemented","Checking raw-material stock counts at every warehouse site"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9.2の内部監査は、AIMSが要求事項に適合し、有効に実施・維持されているかを確認する。広報資料の色調の調整や、広告キャンペーンの媒体別の効果測定、各拠点の原材料の在庫確認を目的とするものではない。","eEn":"The internal audit in Clause 9.2 checks whether the AIMS conforms to requirements and is effectively implemented and maintained. Its purpose is not to adjust the color tone of PR materials, to measure ad campaign results by medium, or to count raw-material stock at every warehouse."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3『マネジメントレビュー』を行う主体は？","qEn":"Who performs the Clause 9.3 management review?","o":["契約している外部の広告代理店","一般利用者のみ","トップマネジメント","監査法人のみ"],"oEn":["The contracted external ad agency","End users only","Top management","Only auditors"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューは、組織の最高位であるトップマネジメントが、AIMSが適切で有効かを見直すために行う。外部の広告代理店や一般利用者、監査法人だけが行うものではない。","eEn":"The management review in Clause 9.3 is carried out by top management, the highest level of the organization, to check that the AIMS remains suitable and effective. It is not done by an outside advertising agency, by general users alone, or only by an audit firm."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.1『継続的改善』が求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 10.1 (continual improvement) require?","o":["問題が見つかっても改善活動は一切行わない","認証取得時に一度だけ改善を実施すれば、以後は完了とみなして打ち切る","過去の改善に関する記録をすべて消去する","AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に改善する"],"oEn":["Never taking improvement action even when problems are found","Deems it finished after a single round of improvement at certification and stops there for good","Erasing all records of past improvements","Continually improve the AIMS's suitability, adequacy, effectiveness"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 10.1 は、AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に改善することを求める。認証取得時に一度改善しただけで打ち切る、あるいは改善の記録を消去することは、継続性の要求に反する。","eEn":"Clause 10.1 requires continual improvement of the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS. Stopping after one improvement at certification, or erasing improvement records, goes against the continuity requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2『不適合及び是正処置』の流れに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the flow of Clause 10.2 (nonconformity and corrective action)?","o":["隠蔽→記録の改ざん→証拠の完全削除→担当者の口止め","広告制作→受注→出荷→請求書発行","対応→原因分析→是正処置→有効性レビュー","発見→放置→黙認→そのまま忘却"],"oEn":["Conceal, falsify the record, delete the evidence completely, then silence the staff involved","Ad production → order receipt → shipment → invoicing","React → analyze cause → corrective action → review effectiveness","Discover → leave it → tacitly accept → forget entirely"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 10.2 の流れは、不適合への対応、原因分析、是正処置、有効性のレビューである。発見しても放置して忘れる流れや、隠蔽と記録の改ざんは、是正処置の趣旨と正反対である。","eEn":"The Clause 10.2 flow is reacting to the nonconformity, analyzing its cause, taking corrective action and reviewing its effectiveness. Ignoring and forgetting a finding, or concealing it and falsifying records, is the opposite of corrective action."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『適合（conformity）』の意味に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the meaning of 'conformity'?","o":["要求事項を大幅に超過した状態のみ","要求事項を満たしている状態","罰金を払った状態","要求を無視した状態"],"oEn":["Only a state that far exceeds the requirements","A state of fulfilling requirements","Having paid a fine","Ignoring requirements"],"a":1,"e":"適合は、要求事項を満たしている状態を指す。要求事項を大幅に超過した状態に限らず、罰金を払った状態や、要求を無視した状態は、適合ではなく不適合に近い。","eEn":"Conformity means that requirements are fulfilled. It is not limited to a state of greatly exceeding the requirements, and a state of having paid a fine or ignoring the requirements is closer to nonconformity than conformity."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"要求事項における『shall』が示すのは？","qEn":"What does 'shall' indicate in the requirements?","o":["望ましいが任意の推奨事項","行ってもよいという許可事項","満たすべき必須の要求","起こりうる可能性を示す表現"],"oEn":["A desirable but optional recommendation","A matter that is merely permitted, not mandatory","A mandatory requirement to be met","An expression indicating something merely could occur"],"a":2,"e":"規格の要求事項でshallは、満たすべき必須の要求を示す。望ましいが任意の推奨事項はshould、行ってもよい許可事項はmay、起こりうる可能性を示す表現はcanが対応する。","eEn":"In a standard, shall expresses a mandatory requirement. A desirable but optional recommendation is expressed by should, a permission to do something by may, and an expression of possibility by can."},
  // ── D3 Annex A と SoA ──
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の管理策と本文の要求事項の関係に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the relation of Annex A controls to the main requirements?","o":["本文がリスク対応で必要な管理策の参照先としてAnnex Aを用いる","Annex Aは規格違反時に科される罰則と課徴金の額のみを列挙した一覧である","Annex Aと本文の要求事項は互いに全く無関係な別規格である","Annex Aの規定が本文の要求事項を常に上書きし優先される"],"oEn":["The main text uses Annex A as a reference set of controls for risk treatment","Annex A is merely a list of the penalties and fine amounts imposed for violating the standard","Annex A and the main text's requirements are entirely unrelated, separate standards","Annex A's provisions always override and take precedence over the main text's requirements"],"a":0,"e":"本文は、リスク対応で必要な管理策を決める際の参照先としてAnnex A を用いる。Annex A が本文の要求事項を常に上書きするわけではなく、罰則や課徴金を列挙した一覧でもなく、本文と無関係な別規格でもない。","eEn":"The main clauses use Annex A as a reference for the controls needed in risk treatment. Annex A does not always override the main requirements, is not a list of penalties and fines, and is not a separate unrelated standard."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoAに必要な最低限の記載事項に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the minimum contents of an SoA?","o":["会社設立からの沿革と主要な出来事、歴代経営者を並べた年表","次年度のテレビCMと広告出稿計画の全容","当期の売上高と営業利益をまとめた一覧","必要な管理策・実施状況・除外した管理策とその理由"],"oEn":["A timeline of the company's history, its key milestones, and its successive chief executives","The full details of next year's TV-commercial and ad-placement plan","A summary of the current period's revenue and operating profit","Necessary controls, implementation status, and excluded controls with rationale"],"a":3,"e":"適用宣言書（SoA）には、必要な管理策、その実施状況、除外した管理策とその理由を記載する。会社の沿革や年表、売上高と営業利益、テレビCMの出稿計画は、管理策の選択を示す文書の内容ではない。","eEn":"The Statement of Applicability (SoA) records the necessary controls, their implementation status and the controls excluded with reasons. A company history timeline, sales and operating profit, or a TV commercial plan is not what this document contains."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針に関するAnnex A管理策の狙いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the aim of Annex A controls on AI policy?","o":["責任あるAIの方針を確立し組織全体に適用する","顧客向けの課金体系に関する社内ルールを整備する","内部監査で見つかった不適合の件数を毎月集計し報告する","新製品の広告展開に関する方針を作成する"],"oEn":["Establish a responsible-AI policy applied across the organization","Establish internal rules for the customer-facing billing scheme","Tallying and reporting monthly the number of nonconformities found in internal audits","Draft a policy for a new product's advertising rollout"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針に関する管理策の狙いは、責任あるAIの方針を確立し、組織全体に適用することである。課金体系の社内ルール、不適合件数の集計、広告展開の方針は、AI方針の管理策とは別の話である。","eEn":"The control on AI policy aims to establish a responsible AI policy and apply it across the organization. Internal billing rules, monthly counts of nonconformities and an advertising policy are separate matters."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの影響に関する管理策が重視するのは？","qEn":"What do controls on AI system impacts emphasize?","o":["供給者との契約書に監査権を盛り込むことのみを扱う","個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響の評価と対処","広告キャンペーンの反響の大きさのみで判断する","推論処理の速度向上のみを重視する"],"oEn":["Deals solely with writing audit rights into the contracts concluded with suppliers","Assessing and addressing impacts on individuals, groups, and society","Judges based solely on the size of an ad campaign's response","Emphasizes only faster inference processing"],"a":1,"e":"AIシステムの影響に関する管理策は、個人・集団・社会への潜在的な影響を評価して対処することを重視する。供給者との契約に監査権を盛り込むことだけや、広告の反響の大きさ、推論速度の向上だけで判断するものではない。","eEn":"Controls on AI system impact stress assessing and addressing potential effects on individuals, groups and society. They are not judged only by writing audit rights into supplier contracts, by the size of ad campaign response, or by speeding up inference alone."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムのデータに関する管理策で扱うのは？","qEn":"What do data-related controls cover?","o":["月次のマーケティング広告費の予算管理と媒体別の実績集計","経営層が示すAI方針の文面を承認する手続きのみを扱う","データの取得・品質・出所・前処理・利用の管理","倉庫にある部材や完成品の在庫数管理"],"oEn":["Budget management of monthly marketing ad spend and tallying the results by media outlet","Covers the procedure by which top management approves the wording of the AI policy","Managing data acquisition, quality, provenance, preparation, and use","Stock-count management of parts and finished goods in the warehouse"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムのデータに関する管理策は、データの取得、品質、出所、前処理、利用を管理する。広告費の予算管理や在庫数の管理、AI方針の承認手続きは、データそのものの管理ではない。","eEn":"The data controls for AI systems manage the acquisition, quality, provenance, preparation and use of data. Advertising budget management, inventory counts and approval of the AI policy are not about managing the data itself."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIの開発（development）に関する管理策の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of controls on AI development?","o":["利用者に対し利用量に応じた従量課金を実施すること","製品のブランドカラーを決めること","責任ある設計・開発・検証・文書化を確保する","広告物の制作スピードを早めること"],"oEn":["Implementing usage-based billing for users according to how much they consume","Deciding the product's brand color","Ensure responsible design, development, verification, and documentation","Speeding up the production of ad materials"],"a":2,"e":"AIの開発に関する管理策の狙いは、責任ある設計・開発・検証・文書化を確保することである。従量課金の実施やブランドカラーの決定、広告物の制作の速さは、開発の責任ある進め方とは関係がない。","eEn":"Controls for AI development aim to ensure responsible design, development, verification and documentation. Pay-per-use billing, choosing brand colors and speeding up ad production have nothing to do with responsible development."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの運用に関する管理策が求めるのは？","qEn":"What do controls on AI system operation require?","o":["店舗にある商品の在庫を売れ行きに応じて随時補充すること","配信中の広告表示を常に最適化すること","監視・ログ・イベント対応など運用中の適切な管理","開発を始める前に学習データの収集方針を文書化しておくこと"],"oEn":["Restocking store merchandise as needed in line with how fast each item sells","Constantly optimizing ad display while it is being served","Proper operational management: monitoring, logging, event handling","Documenting the training-data collection policy in advance of development work"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムの運用に関する管理策は、運用中の監視、ログの取得、イベントへの対応といった適切な管理を求める。商品の在庫の補充や広告表示の最適化は事業の話で、学習データの収集方針の文書化は開発開始前の段階の話である。","eEn":"Controls on AI system operation require proper management during operation, such as monitoring, logging and event response. Replenishing store stock and optimizing ad display are business matters, and documenting the training-data collection policy is a pre-development matter."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報（information for users）の管理策が支えるのは？","qEn":"What do controls on information for users support?","o":["配信した広告バナーのクリック率を高め続けること","供給者が第三者へ再委託する際の事前承認の手順を契約で定めておくこと","利用者ごとの月額課金額を利用実績から正確に算出し請求書を送付すること","利用者が意図した利用・限界・条件を理解し適切に使えること"],"oEn":["Continually raising the click-through rate of ad banners served","Setting out in the contract the prior-approval procedure for when a supplier subcontracts to a third party","Accurately computing each user's monthly fee from usage records and billing it","Users understanding intended use/limits/conditions for proper use"],"a":3,"e":"利用者向け情報の管理策は、利用者が意図した利用、限界、条件を理解して適切に使えるように支える。広告のクリック率や請求書の発行、供給者の再委託承認は、利用者の理解を支える情報ではない。","eEn":"Controls on information for users help users understand the intended use, limits and conditions so they can use the system properly. Ad click rates, invoicing and approval of supplier subcontracting are not information that supports user understanding."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者・顧客との関係に関する管理策の狙いは？","qEn":"Aim of controls on third-party and customer relationships?","o":["広告代理店との年間出稿契約を締結すること","取引先とブランドカラーの情報を共有すること","顧客への月次請求業務と入金確認を第三者に代行させること","外部との責任分担・要件・情報授受を適切に管理する"],"oEn":["Concluding an annual placement contract with an ad agency","Sharing brand-color information with business partners","Outsourcing the monthly customer invoicing and payment reconciliation work entirely to a third-party agent","Properly manage responsibilities, requirements, and information exchange with external parties"],"a":3,"e":"第三者・顧客との関係に関する管理策の狙いは、外部との責任分担、要件、情報授受を適切に管理することである。広告代理店との契約や請求業務の代行は、AIに関する責任分担の管理とは別の業務である。","eEn":"Controls on relationships with third parties and customers aim to manage the sharing of responsibilities, requirements and information with outside parties. Contracts with an ad agency or outsourced billing are different tasks from managing AI responsibilities."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"管理策を選定する際の出発点に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the starting point for selecting controls?","o":["倉庫に保管する製品の在庫数","リスクアセスメント・影響評価の結果","次年度のテレビCM向け広告出稿の予算案の総額","前回のマネジメントレビューの議事録の写し"],"oEn":["The stock count of products stored in the warehouse","The results of risk and impact assessments","The proposed total TV-commercial ad-placement budget for next year","A copy of the minutes of the previous management review"],"a":1,"e":"管理策の選定は、リスクアセスメントと影響評価の結果を出発点とする。在庫数、広告出稿の予算案、前回のレビュー議事録の写しは、どの管理策が必要かを判断する根拠にならない。","eEn":"Control selection starts from the results of risk assessment and impact assessment. Inventory counts, an ad placement budget and a copy of the previous review minutes do not show which controls are needed."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"『管理策（control）』の定義に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the definition of a 'control'?","o":["月次決算のたびに毎回行う仕訳と会計処理の一連の手順のこと","新商品を効果的に売り込むための広告手法","規則違反者に一律に科される罰金や処分","リスクを修正する手段（方針・手順・技術的対策等）"],"oEn":["The set of journal-entry and accounting steps performed at every monthly closing","An advertising technique for effectively promoting a new product","A fine or sanction uniformly imposed on rule violators","A measure that modifies risk (policy, procedure, technical measure, etc.)"],"a":3,"e":"管理策は、リスクを修正（低減）するための手段で、方針、手順、技術的対策などを含む。月次決算の仕訳と会計処理の手順や、広告手法、規則違反者に科す罰金や処分を指す語ではない。","eEn":"A control is a measure that modifies risk, including policies, procedures and technical measures. The term does not mean the series of journal entries and accounting steps in monthly closing, an advertising technique, or fines and sanctions imposed on rule violators."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoAが監査で重要な理由に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to why the SoA matters in audits?","o":["顧客ごとの課金体系の詳細な内訳を示すため","社内で使用するブランドカラーと書体の統一基準を明示するため","次年度の広告展開計画とその予算を示すため","どの管理策を・なぜ適用/除外したかの根拠を示すため"],"oEn":["To show the detailed breakdown of each customer's billing scheme","To show the unified standard for the brand colors and typefaces used in-house","To show next year's advertising rollout plan and its budget","It documents which controls apply/are excluded and why"],"a":3,"e":"SoAは、どの管理策を適用し、どれを除外したか、その理由を示すため、監査では適用の根拠を確かめる中心文書になる。課金体系の内訳やブランドカラーと書体の基準、次年度の広告計画と予算を示す文書ではない。","eEn":"The SoA shows which controls are applied or excluded and why, so it is the central document in audits for checking the grounds of application. It is not a document showing a pricing breakdown, brand color and typeface standards, or next year's ad plan and budget."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の管理策は組織にとって？","qEn":"Annex A controls are, for an organization?","o":["違反時に科される罰則のみを定めた規定","リスクに応じて取捨選択・追加できる参照集","例外なく全項目を必ず実施すべき規則集","実施してもしなくてもよい、拘束力のない単なる参考資料"],"oEn":["A regulation that defines only the penalties imposed for violations","A reference set to select/augment based on risk","A rulebook where every item must be carried out without exception","Merely non-binding reference material that one may or may not act on"],"a":1,"e":"Annex A の管理策は、リスクに応じて取捨選択でき、必要なら追加もできる参照集である。例外なく全項目を実施する規則集でもなく、拘束力のない単なる参考資料でもなく、罰則の規定でもない。","eEn":"The Annex A controls are a reference set that can be selected from and added to according to risk. They are neither a rulebook where every item must be implemented without exception, nor non-binding material, nor penalty provisions."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIの責任配分（roles）に関する管理策が防ぐのは？","qEn":"What do controls on AI role allocation help prevent?","o":["AIの応答速度が繁忙期に遅くなるという問題","責任の空白や重複による統制の抜け","学習データを保管する記憶容量の慢性的な不足","同一顧客への広告の重複配信"],"oEn":["The problem of the AI's response speed slowing down at peak times","Gaps or overlaps in responsibility that weaken control","A chronic shortage of the storage capacity that holds the training data","Duplicate ad delivery to the same customer"],"a":1,"e":"責任配分に関する管理策は、責任の空白や重複による統制の抜けを防ぐ。応答速度の低下や記憶容量の不足、広告の重複配信は、責任がだれにあるかを定めても解決する問題ではない。","eEn":"Controls on allocating responsibilities prevent control gaps caused by gaps or overlaps in responsibility. Slow response times, shortage of storage capacity and duplicate ad delivery are not problems that defining responsibility would solve."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データ来歴（provenance）を管理する狙いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the aim of managing data provenance?","o":["配信済みの広告バナーの表示回数だけを毎週集計する","データの出所・加工履歴を追跡し品質・適法性を担保する","顧客ごとの課金履歴だけを月次で機械的に追跡すること","製品パッケージのカラー変更履歴だけを継続的に記録する"],"oEn":["Tallying weekly only the impression count of ad banners already served","Track data origin/processing to ensure quality and lawfulness","Mechanically tracking only each customer's billing history on a monthly basis","Continually logging only the change history of product packaging colors"],"a":1,"e":"データ来歴を管理するのは、データの出所と加工履歴を追跡して、品質と適法性を担保するためである。広告の表示回数や課金履歴、パッケージの色の変更履歴を記録しても、データの信頼性は確認できない。","eEn":"Data provenance is managed by tracking where data came from and how it was processed, which supports its quality and lawfulness. Recording ad impressions, billing history or package color changes does not verify data reliability."},
  // ── D4 AIリスクと影響評価 ──
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクアセスメントの一般的な流れに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the general flow of AI risk assessment?","o":["広告出稿→問い合わせ受付→見積り→受注→課金","リスク特定→リスク分析→リスク評価（→対応につなぐ）","定期バックアップ取得→削除→復元→整合性検証","仕入れ→検品→在庫登録→出荷→販売"],"oEn":["Place ad → receive inquiry → quote → take order → bill","Risk identification → risk analysis → risk evaluation (→ feed into treatment)","Take routine backup → delete → restore → verify integrity","Procure → inspect → register inventory → ship → sell"],"a":1,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは、リスクの特定、分析、評価の順に進み、その結果を対応につなぐ。広告出稿から課金までの受注の流れや、バックアップの取得から整合性検証までの流れ、仕入れから販売までの流れは、リスクアセスメントではない。","eEn":"AI risk assessment proceeds through risk identification, analysis and evaluation, and then leads into treatment. The flow from ad placement to billing in a sales process, the backup-to-integrity-check flow, and the purchasing-to-sales flow are not risk assessment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスク対応（risk treatment）の選択肢に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is an AI risk-treatment option?","o":["隠蔽・黙認・先送り・放置","低減・移転・受容（保有）・回避","作成・更新・削除・複製","仕入れ・販売・貸与・返品"],"oEn":["Concealment, tacit acceptance, deferral, neglect","Mitigate, transfer, accept (retain), avoid","Create, update, delete, duplicate","Procurement, sale, lease, return"],"a":1,"e":"リスク対応の選択肢は、低減、移転、受容（保有）、回避である。隠蔽や黙認、先送り、放置は対応の放棄にあたり、作成・更新・削除・複製はデータ操作、仕入れ・販売・貸与・返品は取引の種類で、選択肢ではない。","eEn":"The options for risk treatment are reduction, transfer, acceptance (retention) and avoidance. Concealment, tacit tolerance, postponement and neglect abandon treatment; create, update, delete and copy are data operations; purchase, sale, lending and return are transaction types."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステム影響評価が特に注目する対象は？","qEn":"What does an AI system impact assessment particularly focus on?","o":["供給者から提出された第三者認証の有効期限","AIモデルの推論処理にかかる平均の応答速度だけ","利用者に請求する月額課金額","個人・集団・社会への潜在的な悪影響"],"oEn":["The expiry date of the third-party certificate submitted by the supplier","Only the average inference response speed of the AI model at run time","The monthly amount billed to users","Potential adverse impacts on individuals, groups, and society"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、個人・集団・社会への潜在的な悪影響に注目する。第三者認証の有効期限、平均の応答速度、月額課金額は、AIが人や社会に与える影響を示す指標ではない。","eEn":"AI system impact assessment focuses on the potential adverse effects on individuals, groups and society. The expiry date of a third-party certificate, average response speed and monthly fees do not show the AI's effect on people or society."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価とリスクアセスメントの関係に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the relationship between impact assessment and risk assessment?","o":["影響評価の結果はリスク評価・対応の重要な入力になる","影響評価の結果が顧客への課金額を直接決定する","影響評価とリスク評価は互いに完全に独立しており、入力として使えない","リスク評価の結果次第で次回の広告出稿量が変わる"],"oEn":["Impact-assessment results are key inputs to risk evaluation/treatment","The impact-assessment result directly determines the amount billed to customers","Impact assessment and risk evaluation are entirely independent, so neither can feed the other","The volume of the next ad placement changes depending on the risk-evaluation result"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価の結果は、リスクアセスメントと対応の重要な入力になる。影響評価とリスク評価を完全に独立させて入力として使わないという考え方は誤りで、課金額や広告出稿量が決まるわけでもない。","eEn":"Impact assessment results are an important input to risk assessment and treatment. The idea that the two are fully independent and not used as input is wrong, and neither billing amounts nor ad volume are decided by it."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクの『可能性×影響』を用いる目的は？","qEn":"Purpose of using 'likelihood × impact' for AI risk?","o":["内部監査で収集する監査証拠の量をあらかじめ決めるため","課金プランの優先順位を決めるため","広告出稿の順番をあらかじめ決めるため","リスクの優先順位付けと対応の判断のため"],"oEn":["To decide in advance the volume of audit evidence to collect in internal audits","To decide the priority order of billing plans","To decide the order of ad placements in advance","To prioritize risks and decide treatment"],"a":3,"e":"リスクを可能性と影響の掛け合わせで見る目的は、リスクに優先順位を付け、どれにどう対応するかを判断することである。監査証拠の量の事前決定や、課金プランの優先順位、広告出稿の順番を決めるためではない。","eEn":"Combining likelihood and impact serves to rank risks and judge which to treat and how. It is not for deciding in advance the amount of audit evidence to collect, the priority of billing plans, or the order of ad placements."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"残留リスク（residual risk）に対して必要なのは？","qEn":"What is needed regarding residual risk?","o":["検出した記録を即時削除すること","検出した事実を隠蔽すること","権限を持つリスク所有者による受容の判断と記録","検出した事実を無視すること"],"oEn":["Immediately deleting the record that was detected","Concealing the fact that was detected","An acceptance decision and record by the authorized risk owner","Ignoring the fact that was detected"],"a":2,"e":"残留リスクは、対応後も残るリスクについて、権限を持つリスク所有者が受容を判断し、その判断を記録する必要がある。検出した事実を無視する、隠蔽する、記録を即時削除するといった扱いは認められない。","eEn":"For residual risk, the authorized risk owner must decide whether to accept it and record that decision. Ignoring what was detected, concealing it, or immediately deleting the records is not acceptable."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIバイアスに関するリスクを低減する手段に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to a way to reduce AI bias risk?","o":["推論速度をひたすら高速化すること","広告配信タイミングを最適化すること","データの代表性確保・公平性評価・人間の確認","AIが出力する結果の表示色と画面の書体を統一すること"],"oEn":["Relentlessly speeding up inference","Optimizing the timing of ad delivery","Ensure data representativeness, fairness testing, human review","Unifying the display color and the on-screen typeface of the results the AI outputs"],"a":2,"e":"AIバイアスのリスクは、データの代表性の確保、公平性の評価、人間による確認で低減できる。推論の高速化や広告配信のタイミング、画面の書体の統一は、出力の偏りを減らす手段ではない。","eEn":"Bias risk can be reduced by ensuring data representativeness, evaluating fairness and adding human review. Faster inference, ad delivery timing and unifying screen typefaces do not reduce bias in outputs."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIの安全性（safety）に関わるリスクの例は？","qEn":"Example of a safety-related AI risk?","o":["毎月のマーケティング広告費が年々増加し続ける傾向","誤作動・有害出力による物理的/社会的被害","印刷資料で頻発するフォント崩れの問題","適用宣言書の改訂履歴が長期間更新されていない状態"],"oEn":["The trend of monthly marketing ad spend continuing to rise year after year","Malfunction or harmful output causing physical/social harm","The problem of frequent font-rendering breakage in printed materials","A state in which the Statement of Applicability's revision history has gone unupdated for a long period"],"a":1,"e":"AIの安全性に関わるリスクの例は、誤作動や有害な出力が物理的・社会的な被害を生むことである。広告費の増加傾向やフォント崩れ、適用宣言書の改訂履歴の未更新は、人への被害とは別の問題である。","eEn":"An example of an AI safety risk is a malfunction or harmful output causing physical or social harm. Rising advertising spend, broken fonts and an outdated SoA revision history are different problems that do not harm people."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクアセスメントを繰り返す（反復する）理由は？","qEn":"Why iterate AI risk assessment?","o":["AIを取り巻く周囲の状況は決して変化しないため","実施した記録を残しておく必要が全くないため","最初に一度実施するだけで永遠に完璧なため","モデル・データ・利用状況・規制が時間とともに変化するため"],"oEn":["Because the circumstances surrounding AI never change","Because there is no need at all to keep a record of it having been done","Because doing it once at the start remains perfect forever","Models, data, usage, and regulation change over time, so reassessment is needed"],"a":3,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントを繰り返すのは、モデル、データ、利用状況、規制が時間とともに変化するからである。周囲の状況が決して変化しないとか、最初に一度実施すれば永遠に完璧とか、記録が不要という考えは誤りである。","eEn":"AI risk assessment is repeated because models, data, usage and regulations change over time. The notions that the surrounding situation never changes, that one initial assessment stays perfect forever, or that no record is needed are wrong."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク基準（risk criteria）を事前に定める意義は？","qEn":"Value of defining risk criteria in advance?","o":["顧客への月額課金体系を新たに整備するため","一貫した評価と優先順位付けの物差しにするため","各種報告書のテーマカラーと表紙様式を毎回選定するため","新製品の広告展開を大々的に強化するため"],"oEn":["To newly set up a monthly billing scheme for customers","A consistent yardstick for evaluation and prioritization","To pick the theme color and the cover format for each report every time","To greatly strengthen advertising for a new product"],"a":1,"e":"リスク基準を事前に定めておくと、リスクの評価や優先順位付けを一貫した物差しで行える。月額課金体系の整備や報告書のテーマカラーと表紙様式の選定、新製品の広告展開の強化を目的とするものではない。","eEn":"Defining risk criteria in advance gives a consistent yardstick for evaluating and prioritizing risks. They are not meant for building a monthly pricing scheme, choosing theme colors and cover formats of reports, or strengthening an advertising rollout."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIの利用状況（context of use）が影響評価で重要な理由は？","qEn":"Why is the context of use important in impact assessment?","o":["契約するプランによって課金体系の細部が異なるため","内部監査の監査員は必ず被監査部門から独立している必要があるため","同じモデルでも用途・対象により影響が大きく変わるため","ネットワーク環境によって通信速度が大きく上下するため"],"oEn":["Because the details of the billing scheme differ depending on the contracted plan","Because internal auditors must always be independent of the unit being audited","The same model's impact varies greatly by use and affected parties","Because communication speed fluctuates greatly depending on the network environment"],"a":2,"e":"同じモデルでも、使う用途や対象となる人によって影響の大きさが大きく変わるため、利用状況の把握が影響評価で重要になる。契約プランごとの課金の違いや通信速度の上下、監査員の独立性は理由ではない。","eEn":"Even the same model can have very different impact depending on its use and the people affected, so understanding the context of use matters in impact assessment. Differences in charges by contract plan, network speed fluctuation, or auditor independence are not the reason."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の結果を扱う適切な方法は？","qEn":"Appropriate way to handle impact-assessment results?","o":["評価結果が出ても対応も記録もせず、すべて無視して運用を続けること","評価結果を確認したらそのまま破棄すること","評価結果を経営層にも一切秘匿すること","文書化し対応策・監視につなげ、必要時に見直す"],"oEn":["Ignoring all assessment results, neither acting nor recording, and running on unchanged","Discarding the assessment results as soon as they are reviewed","Concealing the assessment results even from executives entirely","Document them, drive treatment/monitoring, and review as needed"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価の結果は、文書にまとめ、対応策や監視につなげ、状況が変われば見直す。評価結果が出ても無視して運用を続けたり、確認後に破棄したり、経営層にも秘匿したりしては、評価の意味がなくなる。","eEn":"Impact assessment results should be documented, linked to mitigation and monitoring, and reviewed when circumstances change. Ignoring the results and continuing operation, discarding them after review, or withholding them even from management makes the assessment meaningless."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクの所有者（risk owner）を定める意義は？","qEn":"Value of assigning a risk owner?","o":["顧客への課金額を算出するため","リスク対応の責任と権限を明確にし放置を防ぐため","新商品の広告展開を強化するため","部門ごとにテーマカラーを割り当てるため"],"oEn":["To calculate the billing amount for customers","Clarify responsibility and authority for treatment and prevent neglect","To strengthen advertising for a new product","To assign a theme color to each department"],"a":1,"e":"リスク所有者を定めると、リスク対応の責任と権限が明確になり、誰も対応しないまま放置されるのを防げる。課金額の算出や広告展開の強化、部門ごとのテーマカラーの割り当てのためではない。","eEn":"Naming a risk owner makes responsibility and authority for risk treatment clear and prevents risks from being left with nobody acting. It is not for calculating charges, strengthening ad rollout, or assigning theme colors to departments."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プライバシーに関するAIリスクの例に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to an example of a privacy-related AI risk?","o":["個人データの不適切な収集・利用・再識別","内部監査の実施頻度が年1回に固定されている点","同一顧客への広告メールの重複配信問題","AIモデルの推論処理速度の大幅な高速化"],"oEn":["Improper collection/use or re-identification of personal data","The point that the frequency of internal audits is fixed at once a year","The problem of duplicate advertising emails sent to the same customer","A substantial speedup of an AI model's inference processing"],"a":0,"e":"プライバシーに関するAIリスクの例は、個人データの不適切な収集や利用、匿名化したデータの再識別である。内部監査の頻度が年1回に固定されている点や、広告メールの重複配信、推論処理の高速化は、プライバシーのリスクではない。","eEn":"Examples of privacy-related AI risk include improper collection or use of personal data and re-identification of anonymized data. A fixed audit frequency of once a year, duplicate ad emails to the same customer, or a large speedup in inference are not privacy risks."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクと便益のバランスを取る際の考え方に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to balancing AI risk and benefit?","o":["得られる便益の最大化だけをひたすら追求する","便益もリスクも一切評価せず放置する方針をとる","便益を活かしつつ許容できない残留リスクは対応する","わずかなリスクが一つ見つかった時点で、便益を問わず即座に全面停止する"],"oEn":["Relentlessly pursuing only the maximization of the benefits gained","Adopting a policy of evaluating neither benefit nor risk and leaving it be","Realize benefits while treating unacceptable residual risk","Halting everything at once the moment a single slight risk appears, whatever the benefit"],"a":2,"e":"便益とリスクのバランスでは、便益を活かしつつ、許容できない残留リスクには対応する。便益の最大化だけを追う、評価せず放置する、小さなリスクで直ちに全面停止する、のいずれも釣り合いが取れていない。","eEn":"To balance benefits and risks, use the benefits while treating residual risk that is unacceptable. Maximizing benefit only, leaving everything unevaluated, or stopping completely at the first small risk are all unbalanced."},
  // ── D5 PDCA・内部監査・継続的改善 ──
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAサイクルの各段階に対応するClauseに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to how PDCA maps to the clauses?","o":["Plan=4–6, Do=7–8, Check=9, Act=10","Plan=Clause10、Do=Clause9、Check=Clause8、Act=Clause7 と逆順に対応する","全て4","全て9"],"oEn":["Plan=4–6, Do=7–8, Check=9, Act=10","Plan=Clause 10, Do=Clause 9, Check=Clause 8, Act=Clause 7 (the mapping runs in reverse order)","All 4","All 9"],"a":0,"e":"PDCAとの対応は、計画が4〜6章、実行が7〜8章、評価が9章、改善が10章である。Plan=Clause10、Do=Clause9 とする逆順の対応や、全てを4章や9章に当てはめるのは、規格の構成と合わない。","eEn":"PDCA maps to Clauses 4 to 6 for Plan, 7 to 8 for Do, 9 for Check and 10 for Act. A reversed order with Plan=Clause10 and Do=Clause9, or putting everything under Clause 4 or 9, does not match the structure of the standard."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の『客観性・独立性』が重要な理由は？","qEn":"Why are objectivity/independence important in internal audit?","o":["監査結果とその所見の信頼性を担保するため","顧客への課金額を正確に算出するため","報告書のテーマカラーを統一するため","新商品の広告展開を強化するため"],"oEn":["To ensure the credibility of the audit results and findings","To accurately calculate the billing amount for customers","To unify the theme color of reports","To strengthen advertising for a new product"],"a":0,"e":"内部監査の客観性と独立性が保たれていれば、監査結果とその所見が偏りなく信頼できるものになる。課金額の算出やテーマカラーの統一、広告展開の強化とは関係がない。","eEn":"Objectivity and independence in an internal audit make the results and findings unbiased and trustworthy. They have nothing to do with calculating charges, unifying theme colors, or strengthening ad rollout."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査で監査員が自分の業務を監査できない理由は？","qEn":"Why can't auditors audit their own work?","o":["外部委託の課金コストが増えるため","資料のテーマカラーが変わるため","監査に想定以上の時間がかかるため","監査の客観性・独立性が損なわれるため"],"oEn":["Because the billing cost of outsourcing increases","Because the theme color of materials changes","Because the audit takes more time than expected","It compromises the audit's objectivity and independence"],"a":3,"e":"自分の業務を自分で監査すると、甘い評価になりやすく、監査の客観性と独立性が損なわれるため、監査員は自分の業務を監査しない。外部委託の課金コストや資料の色、監査にかかる時間は理由ではない。","eEn":"An auditor auditing their own work tends to go easy, which undermines the objectivity and independence of the audit, so auditors do not audit their own work. The outsourcing fee, document theme colors, or time needed for the audit is not the reason."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューのアウトプットに含まれうるのは？","qEn":"Which can be an output of management review?","o":["全社員の氏名・所属部署・連絡先を記載した名簿","次回の内部監査で使用するチェックリストの設問文の原案そのもの","倉庫にある製品のカラー別・サイズ別の在庫状況をまとめた一覧表","改善の機会、変更の必要性、資源の必要性に関する決定"],"oEn":["A roster listing every employee's name, department, and contact details","The draft wording itself of the questions on the checklist to be used in the next internal audit","A table summarizing warehouse stock by product color and by size","Decisions on improvement, change needs, and resource needs"],"a":3,"e":"マネジメントレビューのアウトプットには、改善の機会、変更の必要性、資源の必要性に関する決定が含まれる。社員名簿や在庫状況の一覧表、チェックリスト設問の原案は、レビューの決定事項ではない。","eEn":"Management review outputs include decisions on improvement opportunities, needed changes and resource needs. An employee roster, an inventory table or a draft of checklist questions is not a decision of the review."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置（corrective action）と修正（correction）の違いに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to corrective action vs correction?","o":["是正処置とは当面しのぎの応急的な対応を指す言葉である","修正と是正処置は用語が違うだけで意味は全く同じである","修正こそが根本原因を除去し再発を防ぐ活動である","修正は不適合への当面の対処、是正処置は原因除去による再発防止"],"oEn":["Corrective action is a term for a stopgap, ad-hoc response","Correction and corrective action differ only in wording and mean exactly the same thing","Correction is the activity that removes the root cause and prevents recurrence","Correction is the immediate fix of the nonconformity; corrective action removes the cause to prevent recurrence"],"a":3,"e":"修正（correction）は検出した不適合への当面の対処で、是正処置は原因を除去して再発を防ぐ活動である。根本原因を除去するのが修正だとするのは逆で、是正処置を応急対応とするのも誤りであり、両者の意味は異なる。","eEn":"Correction is the immediate handling of a detected nonconformity, while corrective action removes the cause to prevent recurrence. Saying correction removes the root cause is backwards, calling corrective action a stopgap is wrong, and the two terms do not mean the same thing."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善の効果を測る手段に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to a way to measure continual improvement?","o":["目的・KPIに対する達成度の監視と評価","配信中の広告バナーのクリック率と表示回数のみ","適用宣言書に記載した管理策の総数の年ごとの増減","資料で使用しているフォントの種類数"],"oEn":["Monitoring/evaluating attainment against objectives/KPIs","Only the click-through rate and impression count of the banners now running","The year-on-year change in the total number of controls listed in the Statement of Applicability","The number of font types used in the materials"],"a":0,"e":"継続的改善の効果は、目的やKPIに対する達成度を監視し、評価することで測れる。広告のクリック率、管理策の総数の増減、フォントの種類数は、AIMSが改善しているかを示す指標にならない。","eEn":"The effect of continual improvement is measured by monitoring and evaluating achievement against objectives and KPIs. Ad click rates, changes in the number of controls and the number of fonts do not show whether the AIMS is improving."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の計画で考慮すべきに近いのは？","qEn":"Close to what to consider in planning internal audits?","o":["次年度に計上予定の広告出稿予算の総額と媒体別の配分","対象プロセスの重要性・過去の監査結果・リスク","社内資料で標準的に使用するフォント種別","監査担当者個人が持つデザインや色の好み"],"oEn":["The total next-year ad budget and how it is split across media outlets","Importance of processes, prior audit results, and risk","The font type standardly used in internal materials","The individual auditor's personal taste in design and color"],"a":1,"e":"内部監査の計画では、対象プロセスの重要性、過去の監査結果、リスクを考慮する。次年度の広告出稿予算や社内資料のフォント種別、監査担当者個人のデザインや色の好みは、計画の判断材料にならない。","eEn":"Internal audit planning considers the importance of the processes concerned, the results of past audits, and risk. Next year's advertising budget, the fonts used in internal documents, or an auditor's personal taste in design and color is not a planning factor."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『不適合』が見つかったときにまず行うのは？","qEn":"First step when a nonconformity is found?","o":["原因を調べる前に即時に認証を返上する","無視する","隠す","それを管理し結果に対処する"],"oEn":["Surrendering the certification at once, before any cause is looked into","Ignore it","Hide it","Control it and deal with the consequences"],"a":3,"e":"不適合が見つかったら、まずそれを管理し、その結果に対処する。無視したり隠したりするのは誤りで、原因を調べる前に認証を即時に返上するのは行き過ぎであり、規格が求める対応でもない。","eEn":"When a nonconformity is found, first control it and deal with its consequences. Ignoring or hiding it is wrong, and immediately surrendering certification before investigating the cause goes too far and is not what the standard requires."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューの頻度に関する考え方に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the idea of management-review frequency?","o":["計画された間隔で、変化に応じて実施する","実施する必要はそもそも全くないとされる","毎日欠かさず実施することが必須とされる","導入時に一度だけ実施すればそれで十分"],"oEn":["At planned intervals, responsive to change","It is deemed entirely unnecessary to do it in the first place","Doing it without fail every single day is deemed mandatory","It suffices to do it just once at the time of introduction"],"a":0,"e":"マネジメントレビューは、あらかじめ計画した間隔で行い、状況の変化に応じて見直す。実施が全く不要とすることや、毎日欠かさず行うことが必須とすること、導入時に一度だけ行えば十分とすることは誤りである。","eEn":"Management reviews are held at planned intervals and adjusted as circumstances change. Saying they are not needed at all, that they must be held every day, or that doing it once at introduction is enough is wrong."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査基準（audit criteria）に含まれうるのは？","qEn":"Which can be part of audit criteria?","o":["倉庫に保管されている部材と完成品の在庫数のみ","方針・手順・要求事項（規格の該当箇所）","従業員一人ひとりが持つ趣味や嗜好のみ","配信中の広告のクリック率実績のみ"],"oEn":["Only the stock counts of the parts and finished goods held in the warehouse","Policies, procedures, and requirements (relevant standard clauses)","Only each individual employee's hobbies and preferences","Only the click-through-rate track record of ads currently running"],"a":1,"e":"監査基準には、方針、手順、要求事項（規格の該当箇所）などが含まれる。在庫数、従業員の趣味、広告のクリック率は、AIMSが基準に適合しているかを照らして確かめる物差しにならない。","eEn":"Audit criteria can include policies, procedures and requirements (the relevant parts of the standard). Inventory counts, employees' hobbies and ad click rates are not yardsticks for checking whether the AIMS conforms."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査所見（audit finding）とは？","qEn":"What is an audit finding?","o":["直近の広告キャンペーンで得られた効果指標","収集した監査証拠を監査基準と照合した結果","監査を担当した監査員個人の私見や感想のみ","監査を開始する前に作成しておく監査計画の日程表"],"oEn":["The effectiveness metrics obtained from the most recent ad campaign","The result of evaluating audit evidence against the audit criteria","Only the personal opinions and impressions of the auditor who conducted it","The timetable within the audit plan that is drawn up before the audit itself begins"],"a":1,"e":"監査所見は、収集した監査証拠を監査基準と照合して得られた結果である。広告キャンペーンの効果指標や、監査員個人の私見や感想のみ、監査開始前に作る監査計画の日程表は、監査所見ではない。","eEn":"An audit finding is the result of evaluating collected audit evidence against audit criteria. Ad campaign effect metrics, an auditor's personal opinions and impressions alone, or the schedule in an audit plan made before the audit begins are not findings."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善の文化を支えるのに有効なのは？","qEn":"What supports a culture of continual improvement?","o":["教訓の共有・是正の追跡・指標に基づく振り返り","問題の存在を経営層にも一切秘匿すること","問題が起きても対応せず放置し続けること","四半期ごとの短期的な利益だけを追い求めること"],"oEn":["Sharing lessons, tracking remediation, and metric-based reviews","Concealing the existence of problems even from executives","Continuing to leave problems unaddressed even when they occur","Chasing only short-term quarterly profit"],"a":0,"e":"継続的改善の文化は、教訓の共有、是正の追跡、指標に基づく振り返りで支えられる。問題を経営層にも秘匿する、問題が起きても放置する、短期の利益だけを追うといった姿勢は、改善を妨げる。","eEn":"A culture of continual improvement is supported by sharing lessons, tracking corrections and reflecting on metrics. Hiding problems even from management, ignoring them or chasing only short-term profit obstructs improvement."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『有効性（effectiveness）』の意味に近いのは？","qEn":"Close to the meaning of 'effectiveness'?","o":["システムが処理を完了するまでの速さの度合い","AIMSの運用や維持、内部監査にかかる年間費用の低さの程度","計画した活動を実施し計画した結果を達成する程度","投入した資源の量に対して得られた結果の比率を示す程度"],"oEn":["The degree of speed with which the system completes processing","The degree to which the annual cost of operating and maintaining the AIMS stays low","The extent to which planned activities are realized and planned results achieved","The degree expressing the ratio of the results obtained to the amount of resources put in"],"a":2,"e":"有効性は、計画した活動を実施し、計画した結果を達成した程度を指す。処理を完了するまでの速さや、維持にかかる年間費用の低さは別の概念で、投入した資源に対する結果の比率は効率にあたる。","eEn":"Effectiveness is the extent to which planned activities are carried out and planned results achieved. The speed to finish processing and low annual cost of running the system are other concepts, and the ratio of results to resources invested is efficiency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「AI提供者(AI provider)」の役割を最もよく表すのは次のどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the role of an 'AI provider'?","o":["AIの認証を発行する審査機関","AIシステムを自組織の業務で使うだけの組織","AIの規制を策定する政府機関","AIシステムを開発・提供する組織"],"oEn":["A body that issues AI certifications","An organization that only uses an AI system in its own operations","A government body that formulates AI regulation","An organization that develops and provides an AI system"],"a":3,"e":"提供者はAIシステムを開発・提供する立場であり、単なる利用や規制・認証とは区別される。","eEn":"A provider develops and supplies the AI system, distinct from a mere user, a regulator, or a certifier."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001でいう「AI利用者/導入者(AI user/deployer)」に該当するのは？","qEn":"Which corresponds to an 'AI user/deployer' in ISO/IEC 42001?","o":["AIの倫理原則を研究する大学","AI規格を制定する国際標準化団体","提供されたAIシステムを自社の意思決定に組み込む組織","AIモデルを一から学習させて他社に販売する開発元のベンダー企業"],"oEn":["A university researching AI ethics principles","An international standards body that writes AI standards","An organization that incorporates a supplied AI system into its own business decisions","A company that trains AI models from scratch and sells them to other organizations"],"a":2,"e":"AI利用者（導入者）は、提供されたAIシステムを自組織の意思決定に組み込んで運用する組織である。一から学習させて販売する開発元ベンダーは提供者であり、倫理を研究する大学や標準化団体は役割が異なる。","eEn":"An AI user (deployer) is an organization that builds a supplied AI system into its own decisions. A vendor that trains a model from scratch and sells it is a provider, and a university studying AI ethics or a standards body has a different role."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001の認証が対象とするのは次のうちどれか？","qEn":"What does ISO/IEC 42001 certification apply to?","o":["使用しているアルゴリズムの精度","個々の開発者のスキル","組織のAIマネジメントシステム","特定のAI製品そのものの安全性"],"oEn":["The accuracy of the algorithm in use","The skills of individual developers","The organization's AI management system as a whole","The safety of a specific AI product itself"],"a":2,"e":"認証は製品や個人ではなく、組織が構築・運用するマネジメントシステムに対して与えられる。","eEn":"Certification is granted to the organization's management system, not to a product or individual."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"第三者認証機関(認証審査を行う機関)の主な役割は？","qEn":"What is the main role of a third-party certification body?","o":["AIシステムのソースコードを実際に開発し、顧客の環境に納品する","国や地域のAI規制法そのものを制定し施行する","組織に代わってAIポリシーの文言をすべて作成する","AIMSが規格要求に適合しているか独立に評価・認証する"],"oEn":["Developing the AI system's source code and delivering it to the customer","Enacting and enforcing a nation or region's AI regulatory law itself","Drafting all of the wording of the organization's AI policy on its behalf","Independently assess and certify whether the AIMS meets standard requirements"],"a":3,"e":"認証機関は、独立した立場で、AIMSが規格の要求に適合しているかを評価し認証する。AIシステムの開発や納品、AI規制法の制定、AIポリシーの文言の作成は、認証機関の役割ではない。","eEn":"A certification body independently assesses whether the AIMS conforms to the standard and certifies it. Developing and delivering AI systems, enacting AI regulation and drafting the AI policy wording are not its role."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"自己適合宣言(self-declaration)と第三者認証の違いとして正しいのは？","qEn":"Which correctly distinguishes self-declaration from third-party certification?","o":["どちらも必ず政府が実施する","第三者認証は独立した外部機関の審査を伴う","自己適合宣言の方が第三者認証より常に信頼性が高い","両者に違いはない"],"oEn":["Both are always performed by the government","Third-party certification involves assessment by an independent external body","Self-declaration is always more credible than third-party certification, whoever issues it","There is no difference between them"],"a":1,"e":"第三者認証は、独立した外部機関の審査を伴う点で、自己適合宣言と異なる。自己適合宣言の方が常に信頼性が高いとは言えず、どちらも必ず政府が実施するわけでもなく、両者に違いがないわけでもない。","eEn":"Third-party certification involves an audit by an independent external body, which is how it differs from self-declaration. Self-declaration is not always more reliable, neither is always run by the government, and the two do differ."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける「意図した目的(intended purpose)」とは何を指すか？","qEn":"What does 'intended purpose' refer to in an AIMS?","o":["AI開発を担当する個人のキャリア形成上の年間目標のこと","AIシステムが使われることを想定した用途・文脈","第三者認証機関が組む審査スケジュールの詳細","組織全体で設定する年間の売上目標値のこと"],"oEn":["The annual career-development goal of the individual who develops the AI","The use and context for which the AI system is intended to be used","The detailed audit schedule drawn up by the third-party certification body","The annual sales target figure set across the whole organization"],"a":1,"e":"意図した目的とは、AIシステムが使われることを想定した用途や文脈のことである。開発者個人の年間目標や認証機関の審査スケジュール、売上目標値は、AIシステムの用途を示すものではない。","eEn":"The intended purpose is the use and context in which an AI system is expected to be used. An individual developer's yearly career goal, a certification body's audit schedule and a sales target do not describe how the AI system is used."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける「利害関係者(interested party)」の例として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate example of an 'interested party' in an AIMS?","o":["データセンターに設置されたサーバー筐体の物理的な色","社内の休憩室に設置されている什器や設備の一覧","AIシステムの開発に使用しているプログラミング言語の種類","AIの影響を受ける利用者・規制当局・従業員など"],"oEn":["The physical color of the server chassis installed in the data center","A list of the furniture and equipment installed in the office break room","The type of programming language used to develop the AI system","Affected users, regulators, employees, and similar parties"],"a":3,"e":"利害関係者は組織のAIに関心や影響を持つ人・組織であり、利用者や規制当局が典型例。","eEn":"Interested parties are people/organizations affected by or concerned with the AI, e.g., users and regulators."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"規制当局(regulator)はAIMSの文脈でどう位置づけられるか？","qEn":"How is a regulator positioned in the context of an AIMS?","o":["AIシステムを納入した開発ベンダーのこと","要求や期待を持つ外部の利害関係者","無関係で考慮不要","組織の内部プロセスの一部"],"oEn":["The development vendor that supplied the AI system, counted as a supplier","An external interested party with requirements and expectations","Irrelevant and not to be considered","Part of the organization's internal processes"],"a":1,"e":"規制当局は、組織の外部にいて要求や期待を持つ利害関係者であり、AIMSはその要求や期待を考慮する。開発ベンダーではなく、無関係で考慮不要でもなく、組織の内部プロセスの一部でもない。","eEn":"A regulator is an external stakeholder with requirements and expectations, which the AIMS takes into account. It is not the development vendor, is not irrelevant, and is not part of the organization's internal processes."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001がマネジメントシステム規格として持つ特徴は？","qEn":"What characterizes ISO/IEC 42001 as a management system standard?","o":["特定ベンダーが提供する製品の使用をすべての組織に義務付ける","他のISOマネジメント規格と共通の高位構造(整合化された章立て)を採用","AIアルゴリズムの具体的な実装コードと使用すべき開発言語の版まで詳細に規定する","第三者による認証の取得を規格としてそもそも一切想定していない"],"oEn":["Mandating that every organization use a specific vendor's product","It adopts the common harmonized high-level structure shared by other ISO management standards","Prescribing in detail the concrete implementation code of the AI algorithm and even the version of the programming language to use","Never envisaging third-party certification as part of the standard to begin with"],"a":1,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001はISOの整合化された高位構造を採用し、他規格と統合しやすい。","eEn":"ISO/IEC 42001 uses ISO's harmonized high-level structure, easing integration with other standards."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"同一の組織が「AI提供者」と「AI利用者」の両方になり得るのはなぜか？","qEn":"Why can one organization be both an 'AI provider' and an 'AI user'?","o":["認証機関が両者を兼ねるようにと一律に定めているから","規格そのものが役割を区別することを明確に禁止しているから","提供者と利用者という用語は法律上完全に同義だから","自ら開発したAIを自組織でも運用する場合があるから"],"oEn":["Because the certification body uniformly requires holding both roles at once","Because the standard itself explicitly prohibits distinguishing roles","Because the terms provider and user are entirely synonymous under the law","Because it may operate the AI it developed within its own organization"],"a":3,"e":"同一の組織が提供者と利用者の両方になり得るのは、自ら開発したAIを自組織でも運用する場合があるからである。規格は役割の区別を禁止しておらず、両者は同義でもなく、認証機関が兼ねるよう定めてもいない。","eEn":"One organization can be both provider and user because it may operate in-house an AI it developed itself. The standard does not forbid distinguishing the roles, the terms are not synonyms, and no certification body requires combining them."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲(scope)を明文化した文書は、どのように扱うべきか？","qEn":"How should the documented scope of the AIMS be handled?","o":["組織ではなく認証機関のみが独占的に保持する","文書化された情報として維持し必要に応じ利用可能にする","一度決めたらその後は二度と見直さない方針とする","外部に一切公開しない口頭情報として管理する"],"oEn":["Held exclusively by the certification body not the organization","Maintained as documented information and made available as appropriate","Adopting a policy of never revisiting it again once decided","Managed as verbal information never disclosed externally"],"a":1,"e":"適用範囲は、文書化された情報として維持し、必要に応じて利用可能にする。認証機関だけが保持する、口頭情報として外部に出さない、一度決めたら見直さないという扱いは、文書化情報の要求に反する。","eEn":"The scope is kept as documented information and made available as appropriate. Letting only the certification body hold it, keeping it as verbal information, or never reviewing it after deciding contradicts the documented information requirements."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの主目的として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"What is the most appropriate primary purpose of an AIMS?","o":["AIに関わるリスクと機会を体系的に管理し責任ある利用を支えること","マーケティング活動にかかる広告費をとにかく最小限に抑えること","組織内におけるAIの利用そのものを、用途や影響度を問わず完全に禁止すること","業界内の競合他社に関する非公開情報を密かに収集し分析すること"],"oEn":["To systematically manage AI-related risks and opportunities and support responsible use","Keeping the advertising expenditure for marketing activities to an absolute minimum","Completely prohibiting any use of AI inside the organization, whatever the use case or its impact","Secretly gathering and analyzing non-public information about industry competitors"],"a":0,"e":"AIMSの主目的は、AIに関わるリスクと機会を体系的に管理し、責任ある利用を支えることである。広告費の最小化や、影響度を問わずAI利用を完全に禁止すること、競合の非公開情報の収集は、目的ではない。","eEn":"The main purpose of an AIMS is to manage AI-related risks and opportunities systematically and support responsible use. Minimizing advertising costs, banning all AI use regardless of impact, or secretly collecting competitors' information is not its purpose."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「マネジメントシステム」を構成する要素として適切なのは？","qEn":"Which appropriately describes the elements of a 'management system'?","o":["方針・目的・それらを達成するプロセスの相互に関連する要素の集合","業務を自動化するために導入した単一のソフトウェア製品とその画面のみを指す","壁に額装して飾られた認証書という一枚の紙のみを意味する","個々の従業員が心の中に抱く個人的な信条や価値観のみを指す"],"oEn":["A set of interrelated elements: policy, objectives, and processes to achieve them","Refers only to a single software product introduced to automate operations, and its screens","Means only the single sheet of paper that is the certificate framed on the wall","Refers only to the personal beliefs and values held privately by individual employees"],"a":0,"e":"マネジメントシステムは、方針、目的、それらを達成するプロセスなど、相互に関連する要素の集合である。単一のソフトウェア製品だけ、壁に飾る認証書の一枚だけ、個人の信条だけでは、体系を成さない。","eEn":"A management system is a set of interrelated elements such as policies, objectives and the processes to achieve them. A single software product, one framed certificate or personal beliefs alone do not form a system."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおいて「組織の役割」を明確にすることが重要なのはなぜか？","qEn":"Why is clarifying the 'organization's role' important in an AIMS?","o":["組織が担う役割は業務の都合に応じて毎日変更する必要があるから","役割(提供者/利用者など)により責任や適用される管理策が変わるから","組織がどの役割を担うかは認証の可否とは全く無関係だから","役割さえあらかじめ決めておけば規格の要求事項がすべて免除されるから"],"oEn":["Because the role the organization holds must be changed daily to suit operational convenience","Because responsibilities and applicable controls differ by role (provider/user)","Because which role the organization holds is entirely unrelated to whether it is certified","Because merely deciding the role in advance exempts the organization from all the standard's requirements"],"a":1,"e":"役割を明確にするのは、提供者か利用者かなどの役割によって、責任範囲と適用される管理策が変わるからである。役割を毎日変える必要はなく、認証の可否と無関係でも、要求事項が免除されるわけでもない。","eEn":"Roles must be clarified because whether the organization is a provider or a user changes its responsibilities and applicable controls. Roles need not change daily, they do relate to certification, and defining them does not waive any requirement."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲を決めるとき、境界と適用可能性の決定に含めないものは？","qEn":"When determining the AIMS scope, which is NOT considered for boundaries and applicability?","o":["利害関係者の要求","競合他社の株価の日々の変動","組織の活動・製品・サービス","組織の外部・内部の課題"],"oEn":["The requirements of interested parties","The daily fluctuation of a particular competitor's stock price","The organization's activities, products, and services","The organization's external and internal issues"],"a":1,"e":"適用範囲の決定では、内外の課題、利害関係者の要求、組織の活動・製品・サービスを考慮する。競合他社の株価の日々の変動は、AIMSの境界や適用可能性に影響しないため、含めない。","eEn":"Scope setting considers internal and external issues, stakeholder requirements, and the organization's activities, products and services. Daily movements in a competitor's share price do not affect the AIMS boundaries or applicability, so they are excluded."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001の認証を取得することが示すのは？","qEn":"What does obtaining ISO/IEC 42001 certification demonstrate?","o":["認証を取得したAIが今後決して誤らないことを保証するもの","組織がAIMSの要求を満たす仕組みを構築・運用していること","組織がAIに関するすべての法的責任から完全に免除されること","その組織が市場で販売しているAI製品の数が多いということ"],"oEn":["Something that guarantees the certified AI will never err going forward","That the organization has built and operates a management system meeting AIMS requirements","The organization being completely exempted from all legal liability related to AI","That the organization sells a large number of AI products on the market"],"a":1,"e":"認証の取得は、組織がAIMSの要求を満たす仕組みを構築し運用していることを示す。AIが今後決して誤らないことや、あらゆる法的責任の免除を保証するものではなく、製品数の多さを示すものでもない。","eEn":"Certification shows that the organization has built and operates a system that meets the AIMS requirements. It does not guarantee that the AI will never be wrong, does not exempt the organization from legal liability, and does not indicate the number of products."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIシステムの「ステークホルダー」として、影響を受ける側に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which counts as an affected stakeholder of an AI system?","o":["AIシステムが稼働しているサーバーのCPU型番と搭載メモリ量","社内で共有されているWi-Fiのパスワード情報","AIを運用しているデータセンターの延べ床面積","AIの判断によって不利益を被り得るエンドユーザー"],"oEn":["The CPU model and the installed memory of the server on which the AI system runs","The Wi-Fi password information shared within the office","The total floor area of the data center where the AI is operated","End users who may be disadvantaged by the AI's decisions"],"a":3,"e":"影響を受けるステークホルダーには、AIの判断によって不利益を被り得るエンドユーザーが含まれる。サーバーのCPU型番、Wi-Fiのパスワード、データセンターの延べ床面積は、AIの影響を受ける主体ではない。","eEn":"Affected stakeholders include end users who may be disadvantaged by an AI decision. Server CPU models, Wi-Fi passwords and data center floor area are not parties affected by the AI."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「AIシステム」という用語がマネジメントシステム規格で重要な理由は？","qEn":"Why is the term 'AI system' important in the management system standard?","o":["組織に在籍する従業員数を数えるための単位だから","認証審査にかかる費用の額を決める唯一の要素だから","AIMSが管理対象とする中心的な対象を定義するから","組織が保有するすべてのITシステムを指す言葉だから"],"oEn":["Because it is merely a unit for counting the number of employees at the organization","Because it is the sole factor determining the cost of the certification audit","Because it defines the central object the AIMS manages","Because it is a term referring to every IT system the organization owns"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムはAIMSが統治・管理する中心的対象であり、用語定義が管理範囲を定める。","eEn":"The AI system is the central object the AIMS governs, so its definition frames the scope of management."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AI提供者と利用者を区別する目的として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"What is the most appropriate purpose of distinguishing AI providers from users?","o":["役割を固定し変更を禁じるため","提供者の側だけが規格を守ればよいと決め、利用者を免責するため","それぞれの責任と適切な管理策を明確にするため","認証費用を二重に請求するため"],"oEn":["To fix roles and forbid changing them","To rule that only the provider side must follow the standard and to excuse the user","To clarify each party's responsibilities and appropriate controls","To double-charge certification fees"],"a":2,"e":"提供者と利用者を区別するのは、それぞれの責任と、適切な管理策を明確にするためである。役割の固定、利用者の免責、認証費用の二重請求は、区別の目的ではない。","eEn":"Providers and users are distinguished to make clear each side's responsibilities and the appropriate controls. Fixing roles permanently, exempting users, or charging certification fees twice is not the purpose of the distinction."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲が組織の全部門を必ずしも含まなくてよいのはなぜか？","qEn":"Why need the AIMS scope not necessarily cover all departments?","o":["適用範囲は組織の意向にかかわらず、認証機関が部門単位で勝手に決めてしまうから","適用範囲を狭めさえすれば関連する法規制が免除されるから","AIを使わない部門であっても抱えるリスクは常に同じだから","AIに関与する活動・製品・サービスに応じて範囲を定義できるから"],"oEn":["Because the certification body decides the scope department by department, regardless of the organization's wishes","Because merely narrowing the scope exempts the organization from related regulations","Because even departments that do not use AI always carry the same risk","Because scope can be defined by the AI-relevant activities, products, and services"],"a":3,"e":"適用範囲はAIに関わる活動・製品・サービスに基づき定義でき、全部門を強制しない。","eEn":"Scope is defined by AI-relevant activities, products, and services, so it need not span every department."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「認証は製品ではなくマネジメントシステムに与えられる」という理解の帰結は？","qEn":"What follows from 'certification is granted to the management system, not the product'?","o":["認証は特定AI製品の完全な安全性や無欠陥を保証するものではない","認証を取得した時点で利用者への説明は一切不要になる","認証を取得しさえすれば製品は自動的に無欠陥になる","認証は個々のAIアルゴリズムの中身を直接認可するものである"],"oEn":["Certification does not guarantee that a specific AI product is completely safe or defect-free","Once certified, no explanation to users is needed at all","Merely obtaining certification automatically makes the product defect-free","Certification directly approves the internal workings of each individual AI algorithm"],"a":0,"e":"認証はマネジメントの仕組みへの適合を示すもので、製品の完全な安全性は保証しない。","eEn":"Certification attests conformity of the management system, not the flawless safety of any product."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AI提供者が主に責任を持つライフサイクル段階に近いのは？","qEn":"Which lifecycle activity is an AI provider chiefly responsible for?","o":["他社から調達した既製AIの社内運用のみ","規制法の立案","認証書の発行","AIシステムの設計・開発・提供"],"oEn":["Only the in-house operation of AI procured from another company","The drafting of regulatory law","The issuance of certificates","The design, development, and provision of the AI system"],"a":3,"e":"AI提供者が主に責任を負うのは、AIシステムの設計・開発・提供の段階である。他社から調達した既製AIの社内運用は利用者の段階で、規制法の立案や認証書の発行は提供者の役割ではない。","eEn":"An AI provider is mainly responsible for designing, developing and supplying the AI system. Operating an off-the-shelf AI bought from another company is the user's stage, and drafting regulation or issuing certificates is not a provider's job."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSを導入する組織の「トップマネジメント」に相当するのは？","qEn":"Who constitutes 'top management' in an organization implementing an AIMS?","o":["現場業務を担うすべての一般従業員","組織が開発したAIモデルそのもの","審査のために派遣される外部の認証審査員","組織を最高位で指揮・管理する人々"],"oEn":["Every general employee who carries out front-line operations","The AI model itself that the organization developed","An external certification auditor dispatched to conduct the audit","The people who direct and control the organization at the highest level"],"a":3,"e":"トップマネジメントとは、組織を最高位で指揮し、管理する人々を指す。現場業務を担う一般従業員、組織が開発したAIモデル、外部から派遣される認証審査員は、組織の最高位で指揮する立場ではない。","eEn":"Top management means the people who direct and control the organization at the highest level. Rank-and-file employees doing field work, the AI model the organization developed, and external certification auditors do not hold that position."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの適用範囲を狭く限定しすぎた場合のリスクは？","qEn":"What is the risk of defining the AIMS scope too narrowly?","o":["重要なAI関連リスクが管理対象から漏れる","支払うべき認証費用が必ずゼロになる","存在していたリスクが自動的にすべて消える","規格そのものが即座に適用不能になる"],"oEn":["Significant AI-related risks fall outside management","The certification fee owed necessarily becomes zero","Every risk that existed automatically disappears","The standard itself immediately becomes inapplicable"],"a":0,"e":"適用範囲を狭く限定しすぎると、重要なAI関連リスクが管理対象から漏れ、見落とされるおそれがある。認証費用が必ずゼロになる、リスクが自動的にすべて消える、規格が適用不能になるといった結果にはならない。","eEn":"If the scope is too narrow, important AI-related risks may fall outside what is managed and be overlooked. Certification costs do not become zero, the risks do not disappear on their own, and the standard does not become inapplicable."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「AIシステム」と「従来のソフトウェア」を区別する一般的な特徴は？","qEn":"What generally distinguishes an 'AI system' from conventional software?","o":["稼働のためにサーバーの電力と冷却設備を継続的に消費する点","定期的な保守やソフトウェア更新が必要になる点","入力から予測・推奨・判断などの出力を生成し得る点","あらかじめ書かれたプログラムに従って動く点"],"oEn":["That keeping it running continually consumes server electricity and cooling-equipment capacity","Requiring periodic maintenance and software updates","It can generate outputs such as predictions, recommendations, or decisions from inputs","Operating according to a program written in advance"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムは入力から予測・推奨・判断などの出力を生成し得る点が、従来ソフトとの一般的な違い。サーバーの電力と冷却設備を消費する点や保守・更新が必要な点は従来のソフトウェアにも当てはまり、区別の決め手にならない。","eEn":"An AI system can generate outputs such as predictions, recommendations or decisions from its inputs, which is what generally sets it apart. Consuming server power and cooling, or needing maintenance and updates, applies to conventional software too."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの文脈で「意図した目的」を逸脱した利用(目的外使用)が問題となるのは？","qEn":"Why is use beyond the 'intended purpose' (off-purpose use) a concern in an AIMS?","o":["目的外の利用が増えることで売上が急に上がるから","目的外で使うほど性能が常に向上していくから","想定外の文脈で評価していない新たなリスクや害が生じ得るから","目的外使用を認めると認証機関の手数料が下がるから"],"oEn":["Because off-purpose use increasing causes revenue to suddenly rise","Because performance always keeps improving the more it is used off-purpose","Because unforeseen contexts can create new, previously unassessed risks or harms","Because permitting off-purpose use lowers the certification body's fee"],"a":2,"e":"目的外使用では、想定外の文脈で評価していない新たなリスクや害が生じ得るため問題になる。売上が急に上がる、性能が常に向上する、といった利点は根拠がなく、目的外使用が問題とされる理由の説明にならない。","eEn":"Use outside the intended purpose is a problem because it can create new risks and harms in contexts that were never assessed. Claims such as sudden sales growth or ever-improving performance have no basis and do not explain the concern."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおける利用者(deployer)の責任に含まれ得るのは？","qEn":"What can be part of a deployer's responsibilities under an AIMS?","o":["AIの学習アルゴリズムの収束性に関する数学的証明","自組織の利用文脈における適切な運用と監視","認証書の印刷","国際規格の起草"],"oEn":["Producing a mathematical proof of the convergence of the AI's learning algorithm","Appropriate operation and monitoring within its own use context","Printing the certificate","Drafting international standards"],"a":1,"e":"利用者は自組織の利用文脈に即してAIを適切に運用・監視する責任を負い得る。学習アルゴリズムの収束性に関する数学的証明は開発側の技術課題で、国際規格の起草も標準化団体の仕事であり、利用者の責任とは異なる。","eEn":"A deployer can be responsible for operating and monitoring the AI appropriately in its own usage context. A mathematical proof of learning-algorithm convergence is a developer's technical matter, and drafting international standards is the work of standards bodies."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"認証機関(certification body)と認定機関(accreditation body)の関係は？","qEn":"What is the relationship between a certification body and an accreditation body?","o":["認定機関がAIシステムそのものを開発する","認証機関がAIに関する法律を独自に制定する","認証機関と認定機関は常に同一の組織である","認定機関が認証機関の力量を認定する"],"oEn":["The accreditation body develops the AI system itself","The certification body independently enacts laws related to AI","The certification body and the accreditation body are always the same organization","The accreditation body accredits the competence of the certification body"],"a":3,"e":"認定機関は認証機関の力量を認定する立場で、認証の信頼性を裏づける。認証機関が法律を独自に制定することはなく、両者が常に同一の組織であるわけでもない。AIシステムを開発するのも認定機関の役割ではない。","eEn":"An accreditation body attests to the competence of certification bodies, which underpins the credibility of certification. Certification bodies do not enact laws on their own, the two are not always the same organization, and accreditation bodies do not develop AI systems."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"提供者と利用者の双方に関わる利害関係者として「影響を受ける個人」を考慮すべき理由は？","qEn":"Why consider 'affected individuals' as stakeholders relevant to both providers and users?","o":["AIの出力が個人の権利や生活に影響し得るから","個人が認証取得にかかる費用を直接支払うから","個人がAIのアルゴリズムをすべて独自に開発するから","個人が規格そのものを独自に制定しているから"],"oEn":["Because the AI's outputs can affect individuals' rights and lives","Because individuals directly pay the certification cost","Because individuals independently develop the entire AI algorithm","Because individuals themselves independently enact the standard"],"a":0,"e":"AIの出力は個人の権利や生活に影響し得るため、影響を受ける個人は重要な利害関係者。","eEn":"AI outputs can affect individuals' rights and lives, making affected individuals key stakeholders."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIシステムの「ライフサイクル全体」を通じてステークホルダーを考える理由は？","qEn":"Why consider stakeholders across the entire AI system lifecycle?","o":["初期段階には関係者がいないから","段階ごとに発生する費用の総額が変わるだけにすぎないから","認証は最終段階のみ関係するから","各段階で異なる関係者と影響が現れ得るから"],"oEn":["Because there are no parties in early phases","Because only the amount of cost incurred changes from phase to phase","Because certification concerns only the final phase","Because different parties and impacts can arise at each phase"],"a":3,"e":"開発から運用・廃止まで、各段階で関わる関係者も受ける影響も異なり得るため、ライフサイクル全体で考える。初期段階には関係者がいないという前提は誤りで、認証は最終段階のみ関係するという見方も成り立たない。","eEn":"Stakeholders and impacts can differ at each stage from development through operation to retirement, so the whole lifecycle must be considered. It is wrong that early stages have no stakeholders, and certification does not concern only the final stage."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「マネジメントシステム」と「AIシステム」の違いとして正しいのは？","qEn":"Which correctly distinguishes a 'management system' from an 'AI system'?","o":["マネジメントシステムは購入するソフトウェア製品で、AIシステムは紙の手順書のことである","両者は完全に同義である","AIシステムは組織の統治の枠組みを指す","マネジメントシステムは組織の管理の枠組み、AIシステムは管理される技術対象"],"oEn":["A management system is just a software product you purchase, while an AI system is merely a paper procedure manual","The two are entirely synonymous","An AI system is the organization's governance framework","A management system is the organizational framework; the AI system is the technical object it manages"],"a":3,"e":"マネジメントシステムは組織を管理する枠組み、AIシステムはその管理対象の技術である。","eEn":"A management system is the framework that governs the organization; the AI system is the technical object it manages."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"認証を取得・維持するために組織が継続的に行う必要があるのは？","qEn":"What must an organization do on an ongoing basis to obtain and maintain certification?","o":["取得した認証書を額装して飾ること","初回に受けた一度きりの審査結果のみ","AIの利用をいったん全面的に停止すること","サーベイランス審査など継続的な適合の実証"],"oEn":["Framing and displaying the certificate that was obtained","Only the result of the one-time initial audit","Suspending all use of AI entirely for a while","Ongoing demonstration of conformity such as surveillance audits"],"a":3,"e":"認証は取得して終わりではなく、サーベイランス審査などを通じて継続的に適合を実証し続ける必要がある。初回に受けた一度きりの審査結果のみでは維持できず、AIの利用を全面的に停止することも求められない。","eEn":"Certification is not a one-time event. The organization must keep demonstrating conformity, for example through surveillance audits. The result of a single initial audit alone is not enough, and stopping all AI use is not required."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSにおいて提供者が利用者に提供すべき情報の例は？","qEn":"Which is an example of information a provider should give to users under an AIMS?","o":["社内の内部監査で使用した監査チェックリストの原本一式","第三者認証機関の連絡先情報のみを提供する","AIMS担当従業員が持つ個人的な趣味や休日の過ごし方の情報","AIシステムの意図した目的や制限に関する情報"],"oEn":["The complete set of original audit checklists used in the organization's internal audits","Providing only the contact information of the third-party certification body","Information about the hobbies and weekend habits of the employee in charge of the AIMS","Information about the AI system's intended purpose and limitations"],"a":3,"e":"提供者は、AIシステムの意図した目的や制限に関する情報を利用者に伝え、適切な利用を支える。社内監査で使ったチェックリストの原本一式や、担当者の趣味などの個人的な情報は、利用者の適切な利用に役立たない。","eEn":"A provider should give deployers information on the system's intended purpose and limitations so it can be used appropriately. The original internal-audit checklists or employees' personal hobbies do nothing to support appropriate use."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIシステムの主要ステークホルダーの組み合わせとして最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which combination best represents key stakeholders of an AI system?","o":["オフィスの印刷機・スキャナー・複合機・裁断機一式","学習用データの保管容量・通信帯域・電源契約の内容","適用宣言書・リスク対応計画・内部監査報告書の一式","提供者・利用者・影響を受ける個人・規制当局"],"oEn":["The office set of printers, scanners, copiers, and paper cutters","The storage capacity for training data, the network bandwidth, and the power contract terms","The Statement of Applicability, the risk treatment plan, and the set of internal audit reports","Providers, users, affected individuals, regulators"],"a":3,"e":"主要なステークホルダーは、提供者・利用者・影響を受ける個人・規制当局である。複合機や裁断機などの事務機器、データの保管容量や電源契約、適用宣言書やリスク対応計画といった文書は、人や組織ではないためステークホルダーに当たらない。","eEn":"The main stakeholders are providers, deployers, affected individuals and regulators. Office machines such as copiers and shredders, storage capacity and power contracts, or documents like the statement of applicability are things, not stakeholders."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIの「意図した目的」を提供者が明確に定義することが利用者にとって重要なのは？","qEn":"Why is a provider clearly defining the AI's 'intended purpose' important for users?","o":["AIを導入する利用者が運用費用を削減できるから","適切な文脈で安全に利用でき、目的外使用による害を避けられるから","組織のISO/IEC 42001認証取得が免除されるから","利用するAIのアルゴリズムが自動的に改善されるから"],"oEn":["Because the user deploying the AI can cut operating costs","Because users can use it safely in the right context and avoid harm from off-purpose use","Because the organization is exempted from obtaining ISO/IEC 42001 certification","Because the algorithm of the AI in use improves automatically"],"a":1,"e":"提供者が意図した目的を明確に定義すれば、利用者は適切な文脈で安全に使え、目的外使用による害を避けられる。定義しても運用費用が下がるとは限らず、42001認証の取得が免除されることもない。","eEn":"When the provider clearly defines the intended purpose, deployers can use the AI safely in the right context and avoid harm from out-of-purpose use. It does not reduce running costs by itself, and it does not exempt anyone from ISO/IEC 42001 certification."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"責任あるAIの『堅牢性（robustness）』の原則が主に求めるものはどれか？","qEn":"What does the 'robustness' principle of responsible AI primarily require?","o":["AIの判断根拠を常に人間が理解できる形で提示すること","想定外の入力や環境変化・誤用に対してもAIが安定して機能すること","訓練データを最小限に抑えて保管コストを下げること","AIの出力と学習データをすべて公開し、誰でも自由に検証できるようにすること"],"oEn":["Always presenting the AI's reasoning in a human-understandable form","Ensuring the AI functions stably even under unexpected inputs, environmental change, or misuse","Minimizing training data to reduce storage cost","Publishing every AI output together with the training data so that anyone at all can verify them freely"],"a":1,"e":"堅牢性は、想定外の入力・ノイズ・環境変化・誤用があってもAIが期待どおり安定して動作し続ける能力を指す。透明性や説明可能性とは別の原則である。","eEn":"Robustness is the ability of an AI to keep functioning as expected despite unexpected inputs, noise, environmental change, or misuse. It is distinct from transparency or explainability."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"責任あるAIにおける『プライバシー』の原則に最も合致する取り組みはどれか？","qEn":"Which practice best aligns with the 'privacy' principle in responsible AI?","o":["出力の根拠を利用者に必ず開示する","モデルの精度を上げるため取得できる限りの個人データを集める","目的に必要な範囲へ個人データを限定し、適切に保護する","人間が全ての判断を最終承認する"],"oEn":["Always disclosing the basis of outputs to users","Collecting as much personal data as obtainable to raise model accuracy","Limiting personal data to what the purpose requires and protecting it appropriately","Having a human give final approval on every decision"],"a":2,"e":"プライバシー原則はデータ最小化と適切な保護を重視する。可能な限り集めるのは原則に反する。他は別原則（透明性・人間の監督）に対応する。","eEn":"The privacy principle emphasizes data minimization and appropriate protection. Collecting everything possible violates it; the other options map to different principles (transparency, oversight)."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『安全性（safety）』の原則がAIシステムに対して主に意図するのはどれか？","qEn":"What does the 'safety' principle mainly intend for an AI system?","o":["AIの開発から運用までにかかるコストを徹底的に最小化すること","人・財産・環境への危害を防ぎ、許容できないリスクを避けること","AIが生成する出力結果を必ず自然言語のみで説明すること","常に業界最新のアルゴリズムだけを採用し続けること"],"oEn":["Thoroughly minimizing the cost from AI development through operation","Preventing harm to people, property, or environment and avoiding unacceptable risk","Always explaining the AI's generated output solely in natural language","Continually adopting only the industry's newest algorithm at all times"],"a":1,"e":"安全性は、AIの動作が人・財産・環境に許容できない危害を及ぼさないことを目的とする。技術の新しさやコストは安全性の本質ではない。","eEn":"Safety aims to ensure the AI does not cause unacceptable harm to people, property, or the environment. Novelty of technology or cost is not the essence of safety."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『透明性（transparency）』と『説明可能性（explainability）』の違いとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the difference between 'transparency' and 'explainability'?","o":["透明性はAIモデルの予測精度の高さを、説明可能性は推論にかかる処理速度の速さを表す、いずれも性能を測る評価指標である","透明性はAIの利用や仕組みに関する情報を開示することで、説明可能性は個々の出力や判断の根拠を理解可能にすること","透明性も説明可能性も専門用語としては全く同じ意味であり、あえて区別して使い分ける必要は特にない","透明性は社内の開発者だけに関係する概念であり、説明可能性は外部の規制当局だけに関係する概念である"],"oEn":["Transparency is a metric for a model's prediction accuracy and explainability is a metric for the speed of inference, so both are simply performance measurements","Transparency is disclosing information about the AI's use and workings; explainability is making the basis of specific outputs or decisions understandable","As technical terms, transparency and explainability mean exactly the same thing, so there is no particular need to distinguish them","Transparency concerns only internal developers, while explainability concerns only external regulators"],"a":1,"e":"透明性はシステムの利用・仕組み・限界などの情報開示を指し、説明可能性は個々の判断や出力がなぜそうなったかを理解できるようにすることを指す。関連するが別概念。","eEn":"Transparency is disclosure of information about the system's use, workings, and limits; explainability is making the reasons for specific decisions or outputs understandable. Related but distinct."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"人間の監督（human oversight）を実装する形態の説明として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"Which correctly describes forms of implementing human oversight?","o":["人間が判断ループ内で関与する形態や、人間が介入・停止できる形態など複数の度合いがある","人間の監督とは、AIが出した結果を毎月まとめて必ず外部へ公表することだけを義務づける原則である","人間の監督とは、AIによる全自動化そのものを常に一律で禁止することを意味する","人間の監督は開発段階でのみ必要とされ、実際の運用段階に入れば一切不要になる"],"oEn":["There are multiple degrees, such as a human in the decision loop or a human able to intervene/stop the system","Human oversight is a principle that mandates only that the AI's results be compiled monthly and publicly disclosed, nothing more","Human oversight means uniformly prohibiting full automation by AI at all times","Human oversight is needed only during development and becomes entirely unnecessary once operation begins"],"a":0,"e":"人間の監督は human-in-the-loop / on-the-loop / in-command のように関与度に幅がある。全自動禁止や結果公表とは別概念。","eEn":"Human oversight spans degrees such as human-in-the-loop, on-the-loop, or in-command. It is not a blanket ban on automation nor a publication mandate."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルの一般的な流れとして最も自然な順序はどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most natural ordering of a typical AI lifecycle?","o":["着想・設計 → データ取得と準備 → 構築と検証 → 運用と監視 → 廃棄・撤去","構築と検証 → 着想・設計 → データ取得と準備 → 廃棄・撤去 → 運用と監視","データ取得と準備 → 廃棄・撤去 → 構築と検証 → 運用と監視 → 着想・設計","運用と監視 → 設計 → データ取得と準備 → 構築と検証 → 廃棄・撤去"],"oEn":["Inception/design → data acquisition and preparation → build and verify → operation and monitoring → retirement/decommission","Build/verify → inception/design → data acquisition/preparation → retirement/decommission → operation/monitoring","Data acquisition/preparation → retirement/decommission → build/verify → operation/monitoring → inception/design","Operation/monitoring → design → data acquisition/preparation → build/verify → retirement/decommission"],"a":0,"e":"一般的なAIライフサイクルは、着想・設計から始まりデータ準備、構築・検証、運用・監視、そして廃棄・撤去へと進む。","eEn":"A typical AI lifecycle proceeds from inception/design through data preparation, build/verify, operation/monitoring, and finally retirement/decommissioning."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 のAIMSを ISO/IEC 27001 の情報セキュリティマネジメントと統合する際の考え方として適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is an appropriate view when integrating an ISO/IEC 42001 AIMS with ISO/IEC 27001 information security management?","o":["共通のマネジメント構造を活かし、リスク評価・方針・監査などを整合させて重複を減らせる","AIシステムに関する情報セキュリティの要件はすべて無視してよいとされる","ISO/IEC 27001を完全に廃止しISO/IEC 42001だけに一本化する必要がある","両者は本質的に無関係な規格なので、必ず別々の組織体制で運用すべきである"],"oEn":["The shared management structure can be leveraged to align risk assessment, policies, and audits and reduce duplication","All information-security requirements relating to AI systems may be disregarded","ISO/IEC 27001 must be fully abolished and consolidated solely into ISO/IEC 42001","Since the two standards are unrelated, they must always be operated under separate organizational structures"],"a":0,"e":"両規格は共通の高レベル構造を持ち、方針・リスク評価・内部監査などを整合させて統合運用できる。置き換えや無視ではない。","eEn":"Both standards share a common high-level structure, so policies, risk assessment, and internal audits can be aligned for integrated operation—not replacement or neglect."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 42001、ISO/IEC 27001、ISO 9001 が容易に統合できる主な理由はどれか？","qEn":"What is the main reason ISO/IEC 42001, ISO/IEC 27001, and ISO 9001 can be integrated readily?","o":["いずれもAnnex SL（共通の上位構造・共通用語）に基づく同じマネジメントシステム構造を採用しているため","いずれの規格も、そもそも国内に存在するただ一つの同じ認証機関でなければ監査も認証も行えないと本文に定められているため","いずれの規格も対象範囲がAIに関する規制のみに限定されており、それ以外は扱わないため","いずれの規格も要求事項の文言が一言一句まで全く同一であり、内容がそのまま重複しているため"],"oEn":["They all adopt the same management-system structure based on Annex SL (harmonized high-level structure and common terms)","Because each standard states that only the one single certification body in the country may audit and certify against it, and no other body may","Because the scope of each standard is limited solely to AI-related regulation and covers nothing else","Because the wording of each standard's requirements is word-for-word identical, so the content simply duplicates"],"a":0,"e":"ISOのマネジメントシステム規格は共通の上位構造（Annex SL）を採用しており、章立てや用語が揃うため統合が容易になる。内容が同一なわけではない。","eEn":"ISO management system standards adopt a common high-level structure (Annex SL), aligning clauses and terminology and easing integration—though their contents are not identical."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの成功を支える組織文化の要素として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate element of an organizational culture that supports a successful AIMS?","o":["従業員が失敗や懸念を率直に言い出せず、隠してしまう文化を奨励する","リスクや懸念を率直に報告・議論でき、責任あるAIの価値観が共有されている","内部監査で指摘を受けないよう、あえて活動の記録を残さないようにする","AIに関する重要な意思決定を、ごく一部の技術者だけに閉じ、議事録も残さず他部門に共有しない"],"oEn":["Fostering a culture where employees cannot speak up about failures or concerns and instead hide them","One where risks and concerns can be openly reported and discussed and responsible-AI values are shared","Deliberately keeping no record of activities so as to avoid findings in internal audits","Confining important AI decisions to a handful of engineers, keeping no minutes and sharing nothing with other teams"],"a":1,"e":"責任あるAIの実践には、懸念を率直に共有でき価値観が共有される文化が不可欠。隠蔽や情報の閉鎖、記録回避は逆効果。","eEn":"Practicing responsible AI needs a culture where concerns are openly shared and values are common. Concealment, siloing, and avoiding records are counterproductive."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明責任（accountability）を組織で明確にするために有効な手法はどれか？","qEn":"Which technique helps make accountability explicit in an organization?","o":["誰がどの役割を担うかを文書化せず、暗黙の了解のままにしておく","役割・責任・権限を明確に割り当て（例：RACIのように）記録する","組織内のすべての判断をAIに自動化させ、承認者も記録も置かず人間の関与を完全に消す","案件が発生するたびに責任者をくじ引きなど無作為に選ぶ"],"oEn":["Leaving who holds which role undocumented, relying only on tacit understanding","Clearly assigning and recording roles, responsibilities, and authorities (e.g., via a RACI-style matrix)","Automating every decision in the organization with AI and removing human involvement entirely, with no approver and no record","Randomly selecting the responsible person, such as by lottery, every time a matter arises"],"a":1,"e":"説明責任は誰が何に責任を負うかを明確化し文書化することで確立される。暗黙化・無作為化・人間排除では責任の所在が不明確になる。","eEn":"Accountability is established by clearly defining and documenting who is responsible for what. Leaving it implicit, random, or human-free obscures where responsibility lies."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"公平性（fairness）の原則に照らして、特に注意すべきバイアスの発生源はどれか？","qEn":"In light of the fairness principle, which is a bias source to watch especially?","o":["モデルの学習に使用する計算資源の使用量が多いこと","訓練データの偏りや、特定集団を不利に扱う特徴量の利用","使用しているモデルの推論速度が非常に速いこと","AIの出力結果を常に自然言語で丁寧に説明していること"],"oEn":["The large amount of compute resources used to train the model","Skew in training data or use of features that disadvantage specific groups","The inference speed of the model in use being very fast","Always carefully explaining the AI's output in natural language"],"a":1,"e":"公平性の主要リスクは、偏った訓練データや差別的な特徴量による不当な扱い。速度・説明・計算量は公平性の直接要因ではない。","eEn":"A key fairness risk is unfair treatment from skewed training data or discriminatory features. Speed, explanation, or compute are not direct fairness factors."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"透明性の原則における『誰に対して』開示するかの考え方として適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Regarding 'to whom' disclosure applies under the transparency principle, which is appropriate?","o":["開発チームの内部だけに関連情報をすべて留め、外部には一切出さない","本来対象とすべき利用者や規制当局ではなく、競合他社に対してのみ詳細な情報を開示する","利用者や規制当局を含め、あらゆる情報を一切非公開のままにする","利用者・影響を受ける個人・規制当局など、対象に応じて必要な情報を提供する"],"oEn":["Keeping all related information solely within the development team and releasing nothing externally","Disclosing detailed information only to competitors rather than to the intended users or the regulators","Keeping every piece of information entirely non-public, including from users and regulators","Provide the information each audience needs—users, affected individuals, regulators, etc."],"a":3,"e":"透明性は相手（利用者・影響を受ける人・規制当局等）に応じて適切な情報を提供することを重視する。内部限定や全面非開示は原則に反する。","eEn":"Transparency emphasizes giving appropriate information to each audience—users, affected people, regulators. Restricting it internally or withholding entirely violates the principle."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルの『データ取得と準備』段階で品質を確保する意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What best captures the significance of ensuring quality in the 'data acquisition and preparation' stage of the AI lifecycle?","o":["データ品質は運用段階に入ってからのみ重要であり、準備段階の品質はモデルの結果と無関係である","準備段階で生じたデータの欠陥は、廃棄段階になれば自動的に修正される","データ品質はモデルの性能・公平性・信頼性に直接影響するため早期に管理すべき","収集するデータの量さえ十分に多ければ、品質のばらつきは全く問題にならない"],"oEn":["Data quality matters only once operation starts, and quality at the preparation stage has nothing to do with the model's results","Data defects arising at the preparation stage are automatically corrected once the retirement stage is reached","Data quality directly affects model performance, fairness, and reliability, so it should be managed early","As long as the volume of collected data is large enough, variation in quality is not a problem at all"],"a":2,"e":"データの品質・代表性・偏りは、後続段階のモデル性能や公平性・信頼性を左右するため、準備段階での管理が重要。量が多ければよいわけではない。","eEn":"Data quality, representativeness, and bias shape downstream model performance, fairness, and reliability, so managing it early is important. Volume alone is not enough."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSが PDCA（Plan-Do-Check-Act）サイクルを採用する狙いとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What best describes the aim of an AIMS adopting the PDCA (Plan-Do-Check-Act) cycle?","o":["計画・実施・点検・改善を繰り返し、継続的にシステムを改善するため","サイクルを回さず、文書化にかかる手間をとにかく省くため","AIMSを一度構築すれば、それ以後の見直しを一切不要にするため","ISO/IEC 42001の認証を取得したら運用そのものを停止するため"],"oEn":["To repeat plan, do, check, and act and continually improve the system","To avoid running the cycle at all and simply cut the effort of documentation","Because building the AIMS once makes all subsequent review unnecessary","Because operation itself is halted once ISO/IEC 42001 certification is obtained"],"a":0,"e":"PDCAは計画・実施・点検・改善を反復し、AIMSを継続的に改善するための枠組み。構築後放置や運用停止のためではない。","eEn":"PDCA is a framework for iterating plan-do-check-act to continually improve the AIMS—not for abandoning it after build or stopping operations."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『責任あるAI（responsible AI）』の考え方を最もよく表しているのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best expresses the notion of 'responsible AI'?","o":["コスト削減のため可能な限り自動化を進め、人間の関与を完全に排除すべきだとする方針","法規制が存在する地域だけで倫理的配慮を行い、それ以外では考慮しなくてよいとする発想","他の要素を一切顧みず、技術的な精度だけをひたすら最大化すればよいという考え","倫理・法・社会への影響を踏まえ、原則に沿ってAIを設計・開発・運用する包括的な考え"],"oEn":["The stance that automation should be pushed as far as possible to cut costs, completely removing human involvement","The notion that ethical consideration is needed only where regulation exists and can be skipped elsewhere","The idea that one need only maximize technical accuracy alone, disregarding all other factors","A holistic approach of designing, developing, and operating AI in line with principles, considering ethical, legal, and societal impact"],"a":3,"e":"責任あるAIは、精度だけでなく倫理・法・社会的影響を踏まえて原則に沿ってAIを扱う包括的な考え方。精度至上や自動化至上とは異なる。","eEn":"Responsible AI is a holistic approach that handles AI in line with principles considering ethical, legal, and societal impact—not accuracy-only or automation-only thinking."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明可能性（explicability）が組織や社会にもたらす主要な便益はどれか？","qEn":"What is a key benefit that explicability brings to organizations and society?","o":["AIに関するあらゆる法規制を将来的にすべて撤廃し不要にすること","AIの判断に対する信頼や、誤りの発見・是正・異議申し立てを可能にする","AIの学習から推論までにかかる計算コストと電力消費を常にゼロに近づけること","どのようなタスクでもAIの精度を無条件に100%にすること"],"oEn":["Eventually abolishing every piece of AI-related regulation and making it unnecessary","Enabling trust in AI decisions and the ability to detect, correct, and contest errors","Always driving the compute cost and the power draw from AI training through inference toward zero","Making AI's accuracy unconditionally 100% for any task whatsoever"],"a":1,"e":"説明可能性は判断根拠の理解を助け、信頼の醸成や誤りの発見・是正・異議申し立てを可能にする。コストや精度を保証するものではない。","eEn":"Explicability aids understanding of decision bases, building trust and enabling detection, correction, and contestation of errors. It does not guarantee cost or accuracy."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"『堅牢性（robustness）』と『レジリエンス（回復力）』の関係として適切な説明はどれか？","qEn":"Which appropriately describes the relationship between 'robustness' and 'resilience'?","o":["堅牢性とレジリエンスは学術的にも実務的にも完全に同義の用語で、どちらか一方を書けば足り、区別する意味はない","堅牢性は学習データの量に関する概念、レジリエンスは利用料金の設定に関する概念である","堅牢性は処理速度の速さを、レジリエンスはモデルの予測精度の高さを指す概念である","堅牢性は外乱下でも性能を維持する性質、レジリエンスは障害後に回復する性質で、相補的である"],"oEn":["Robustness and resilience are entirely synonymous in both academic and practical use, so writing either one suffices and distinguishing them is pointless","Robustness is a concept about the volume of training data, and resilience is a concept about setting usage fees","Robustness refers to the speed of processing, and resilience refers to the accuracy of a model's predictions","Robustness is maintaining performance under disturbance while resilience is recovering after failure; they are complementary"],"a":3,"e":"堅牢性は外乱・誤用下でも性能を保つ性質、レジリエンスは障害発生後に回復する性質で、両者は補い合う関係にある。","eEn":"Robustness is maintaining performance under disturbance/misuse; resilience is recovering after a failure. The two are complementary."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"プライバシー保護における『プライバシー・バイ・デザイン』の考え方に合致するのはどれか？","qEn":"Which aligns with 'privacy by design' in privacy protection?","o":["問題が起きてから事後的にのみ、後付けで対策を追加すること","設計・開発の初期からプライバシー保護を組み込む","個人データを匿名化せず常に平文で扱う","プライバシーは法務部門だけの責任とする"],"oEn":["Adding measures only after problems have occurred, bolting them on after the fact","Building privacy protection in from the earliest design and development","Always handling personal data in plaintext without anonymization","Making privacy solely the legal department's responsibility"],"a":1,"e":"プライバシー・バイ・デザインは、設計初期からプライバシー保護を組み込む予防的アプローチ。事後対応や特定部門任せ、平文常用は反する。","eEn":"Privacy by design is a preventive approach that embeds privacy protection from the earliest design—not after-the-fact fixes, siloing, or plaintext handling."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIにおける『安全性（safety）』と『セキュリティ（security）』の違いとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best distinguishes 'safety' from 'security' in AI?","o":["安全性とセキュリティはISO/IEC 42001において区別する必要のない完全に同一の概念であり、同じ管理策で足りる","安全性はAIが引き起こす危害の防止、セキュリティは悪意ある攻撃や不正アクセスからの保護を主眼とする","安全性は開発コストの管理を、セキュリティは利用者間の公平性の確保を意味する概念である","安全性はAI全体の推論処理速度を、セキュリティはモデルの予測精度の高さを表す指標である"],"oEn":["In ISO/IEC 42001, safety and security are entirely identical concepts needing no distinction, so one single control is enough to cover both","Safety focuses on preventing harm the AI may cause; security focuses on protection from malicious attack or unauthorized access","Safety refers to managing development cost, and security refers to ensuring fairness among users","Safety is a metric for the overall inference speed of AI, and security is a metric for the accuracy of a model's predictions"],"a":1,"e":"安全性はAIの動作が及ぼす危害の防止、セキュリティは攻撃・不正アクセスからの保護に主眼がある。関連するが異なる概念。","eEn":"Safety focuses on preventing harm the AI's operation may cause; security focuses on protection from attacks and unauthorized access. Related but distinct."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"人間の監督が『意味のある（meaningful）』ものであるために必要な条件はどれか？","qEn":"What condition is needed for human oversight to be 'meaningful'?","o":["監督者はAIの内部動作や判断根拠を全く理解していなくても問題ないこと","監督者がAIの動作を理解し、必要時に実際に介入・停止できる権限と能力を持つこと","人間の監督とは、AIが出した結果を四半期ごとに単に外部へ公表することだけを意味すること","監督者は内容を理解せず、書類に形式上の署名だけを行えばそれで十分であること"],"oEn":["It being fine for the overseer to have no understanding whatsoever of the AI's internal behavior or reasoning","The overseer understands the AI's behavior and actually has the authority and ability to intervene or stop it when needed","Human oversight meaning merely that the AI's results are published externally once each quarter, with no power to intervene at all","It being sufficient for the overseer to simply sign the paperwork as a formality without understanding the content"],"a":1,"e":"意味のある監督には、監督者がAIを理解し、必要時に実際に介入・停止できる権限と能力があることが不可欠。形式的署名や理解不要では実効性がない。","eEn":"Meaningful oversight requires the overseer to understand the AI and to genuinely have the authority and ability to intervene or stop it—not a mere formal sign-off."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルの『運用と監視』段階で継続的モニタリングが重要な理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is continuous monitoring important in the 'operation and monitoring' stage of the AI lifecycle?","o":["データ分布の変化（ドリフト）や性能劣化・新たなリスクを早期に検知して対応するため","継続的モニタリングは認証を取得するためだけの形式的な儀式に過ぎないから","モデルは運用開始後は入力が変わっても一切変化しないため、継続的な監視はそもそも不要だから","継続的にモニタリングしてさえいれば、モデルの精度は必ず上がり続けるから"],"oEn":["To detect data distribution shift (drift), performance degradation, and emerging risks early and respond","Because continuous monitoring is merely a formal ritual performed solely to obtain certification","Because the model never changes at all after go-live even as its inputs change, so continuous monitoring is unnecessary to begin with","Because as long as monitoring is continuous, the model's accuracy will necessarily keep improving"],"a":0,"e":"運用中はデータ分布の変化や性能劣化、新たなリスクが生じうるため、継続的な監視で早期に検知・対応することが重要。","eEn":"During operation, distribution shift, performance degradation, and new risks can arise, so continuous monitoring is important to detect and respond early."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルにおける『廃棄・撤去（retirement/decommissioning）』段階で考慮すべき事項はどれか？","qEn":"What should be considered in the 'retirement/decommissioning' stage of the AI lifecycle?","o":["データの安全な処理・記録の保持・後継システムへの移行・影響を受ける関係者への配慮","廃棄・撤去の段階ではモデルの性能指標のみを測定すればそれで十分である","データや記録の保持を考慮せず、関係者への連絡もせずに即座にサーバーを物理破壊すればよい","システムの撤去作業は、開発チームや関係部門に一切無断で進めてよい"],"oEn":["Secure handling of data, retention of records, migration to successor systems, and care for affected stakeholders","It being sufficient at the retirement/decommission stage to measure only the model's performance metrics","Physically destroying the servers at once, without considering record retention and without notifying any affected party","Proceeding with the system's decommissioning entirely without notifying the development team or related departments"],"a":0,"e":"廃棄段階では、データの安全な処理、必要な記録の保持、後継への移行、関係者への影響などを計画的に扱う必要がある。","eEn":"Retirement should be planned to cover secure data handling, retention of needed records, migration to successors, and impact on stakeholders."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSを ISO 9001（品質マネジメント）と統合することで得られる利点として適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is an advantage of integrating an AIMS with ISO 9001 (quality management)?","o":["統合を機に、AI固有のリスクに関する要求事項をすべて撤廃してしまってよい","ISO 9001が定める品質に関する要求事項も内部監査も、統合した後は一切無視できるようになる","品質マネジメントとAIMSを統合すれば内部監査そのものを完全に廃止できる","顧客満足・プロセス改善の考え方をAIの品質・信頼性向上に活かし、管理の一貫性を高められる"],"oEn":["Integration provides an opportunity to simply do away with all requirements concerning AI-specific risk","Once integrated, both the quality requirements set by ISO 9001 and its internal audit obligations can be disregarded entirely","Integrating quality management with the AIMS makes it possible to completely eliminate internal audits","Customer-satisfaction and process-improvement thinking can be applied to AI quality and reliability, improving management consistency"],"a":3,"e":"9001の顧客満足・プロセスアプローチ・継続的改善の考え方はAIの品質・信頼性向上と親和的で、統合により管理の一貫性が高まる。要求の撤廃ではない。","eEn":"ISO 9001's customer-satisfaction, process approach, and continual improvement mindset align with AI quality and reliability, and integration improves consistency—not removal of requirements."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIMSの導入を成功させる上でリーダーシップが示すべき『トップからの姿勢（tone at the top）』の意味に最も近いのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is closest to the meaning of 'tone at the top' that leadership should show for a successful AIMS?","o":["経営層は自らは一切関与せず、AIMSに関する判断や推進をすべて現場に丸投げする","経営層が責任あるAIの価値観を明確に示し、率先して行動・資源配分することで組織全体の規範を形づくる","経営層は責任あるAIの方針を美しく文書化して掲示するだけで、資源配分でも日々の行動でも何一つ示さないこと","AIの倫理に関する判断や責任はすべて外部の委託先やベンダーだけに任せてしまう"],"oEn":["Executives stay entirely uninvolved themselves, delegating all AIMS decisions and driving entirely to the front line","Executives clearly demonstrate responsible-AI values and lead by acting and allocating resources, shaping norms across the organization","Executives merely document and display the responsible-AI policy elegantly, demonstrating nothing through resource allocation or their daily conduct","Leaving all judgment and responsibility for AI ethics entirely to outside contractors and vendors"],"a":1,"e":"トップからの姿勢は、経営層が価値観を明示し率先垂範・資源配分することで組織の規範を形成すること。丸投げや口先だけでは文化は根づかない。","eEn":"Tone at the top means executives explicitly demonstrate values and lead by example and resourcing, shaping organizational norms. Delegation or words alone won't embed culture."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"透明性を実務で支える最も基本的な手段はどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most basic means of supporting transparency in practice?","o":["透明性は方針文書の中で宣言しさえすれば、それだけで十分である","AIシステムの目的・データ・限界・意思決定を適切に文書化し追跡可能にする","普段は文書化を行わず、内部監査の直前の数日だけ慌てて一時的に作成して取り繕うこと","AIシステムに関する情報を口頭のみで共有し、一切記録を残さない"],"oEn":["It being sufficient for transparency merely to be declared within a policy document","Appropriately documenting and making traceable the AI system's purpose, data, limits, and decisions","Doing no documentation as a rule, then hastily producing temporary papers in the few days before an internal audit","Sharing AI-system information only verbally and keeping no record at all"],"a":1,"e":"透明性は、目的・データ・限界・意思決定を文書化し追跡可能にすることで実務的に支えられる。口頭のみや宣言だけでは検証できない。","eEn":"Transparency is supported in practice by documenting and making traceable the purpose, data, limits, and decisions. Verbal-only or mere declarations can't be verified."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明責任の原則について正しい理解はどれか？","qEn":"Which is a correct understanding of the accountability principle?","o":["説明責任はAIの予測精度が九割など一定水準より高い場合にのみ限定的に発生するとする","AIが完全に自律的に判断した結果については、組織も個人も一切責任を負わない","AIの導入元であるベンダーに責任を移転しさえすれば、組織は一切免責される","組織や個人はAIの結果に対して責任を負い、その責任は自動化によって消滅しない"],"oEn":["Accountability arises only in the limited case where the AI's prediction accuracy exceeds some set level such as ninety percent","Neither the organization nor any individual bears any responsibility at all for outcomes the AI decided fully autonomously","The organization is entirely exempt once it merely transfers responsibility to the AI vendor","Organizations and individuals remain answerable for AI outcomes, and that responsibility is not erased by automation"],"a":3,"e":"説明責任は、AIを導入・運用する組織や個人が結果に責任を負う原則で、自動化やベンダーへの委託によって消えるものではない。","eEn":"Accountability means the organizations and individuals deploying AI remain answerable for outcomes; it is not erased by automation or by delegating to a vendor."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"公平性を高めるためにデータについて確認すべき点として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"To improve fairness, which is the most appropriate point to check about data?","o":["使用しているデータの保存形式やファイル拡張子が最新か","データが対象集団を偏りなく代表しているか（代表性・カバレッジ）","保存しているデータファイル一つ一つの容量が十分に小さく揃えられているか","収集した学習データの取得日ができるだけ直近で新しいか"],"oEn":["Whether the storage format or file extension of the data in use is the latest","Whether the data represents the target population without bias (representativeness/coverage)","Whether every one of the stored data files is sufficiently small and uniform in size on the storage volume","Whether the acquisition date of the collected training data is as recent as possible"],"a":1,"e":"公平性のためには、データが対象集団を偏りなく代表しているか（代表性・カバレッジ）を確認することが重要。保存形式や日付・サイズは公平性の本質ではない。","eEn":"For fairness, it is important to check whether the data represents the target population without bias (representativeness/coverage). Format, date, or size are not the essence."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"人間の監督において『オーバーライド（介入・上書き）能力』が重要になる典型的な状況はどれか？","qEn":"In human oversight, in which typical situation does 'override capability' become important?","o":["推論にかかるAIの計算処理速度を、サーバーやGPUの増設などハードウェアの増強によってできる限り上げていくため","AIMSの運用にともなって日々発生する各種文書の作成量をできるだけ減らすため","次回の更新審査で発生する第三者認証の費用や監査にかかる工数を少しでも下げるため","AIの推奨が明らかに誤りや有害と判断される場合に、人間が判断を止めたり覆したりできるようにするため"],"oEn":["To raise the AI's inference-processing speed as far as possible by upgrading hardware such as adding more servers","To reduce as much as possible the volume of various documents produced daily from operating the AIMS","To lower even slightly the third-party certification cost and the audit effort incurred at the next surveillance audit","So a human can stop or reverse a decision when the AI's recommendation appears clearly wrong or harmful"],"a":3,"e":"AIの出力が誤り・有害と判断される場面で人間が介入・上書きできることは、リスク低減と人間中心の統制に不可欠である。","eEn":"Being able to intervene or override when the AI's output appears wrong or harmful is essential to reducing risk and keeping human-centric control."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"説明可能性に関する『事後説明（post-hoc explanation）』と『本質的に解釈可能なモデル』の違いとして適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which correctly distinguishes 'post-hoc explanation' from an 'inherently interpretable model' in explainability?","o":["事後説明は社内の開発者だけが使う用語であり、解釈可能モデルは規制当局だけが使う専用の用語で、内容に違いはない","事後説明は複雑なモデルの判断を後から近似的に説明し、解釈可能モデルはそれ自体の構造が理解しやすい","事後説明と解釈可能なモデルは実務上も学術上も全く同じで、区別すること自体に意味がない","事後説明は推論の処理速度の速さを、解釈可能モデルは利用料金の安さを指す用語である"],"oEn":["Post-hoc explanation is a term used only by in-house developers and interpretable model is one used only by regulators, with no difference in what they mean","Post-hoc explanation approximates a complex model's decisions after the fact, while an interpretable model is understandable by its own structure","Post-hoc explanation and interpretable models are entirely the same both practically and academically, so distinguishing them is meaningless","Post-hoc explanation is a term for the speed of inference processing, and an interpretable model is a term for cheap usage fees"],"a":1,"e":"事後説明は複雑なモデルの判断を後から近似的に説明する手法、解釈可能モデルはその構造自体が理解しやすいモデルを指す。両者は説明可能性への異なるアプローチ。","eEn":"Post-hoc explanation approximates a complex model's decisions afterward; an interpretable model is understandable by its own structure. They are different approaches to explainability."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"堅牢性を脅かす『敵対的入力（adversarial input）』への対応として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the most appropriate response to 'adversarial inputs' that threaten robustness?","o":["意図的に細工された入力への耐性を評価・強化し、異常を検知する仕組みを設ける","敵対的入力への対策はプライバシー原則の一部として扱えばよく、堅牢性とは無関係である","敵対的入力は理論上の話なので無視してよい","精度が高ければ敵対的入力は自動的に無効化される"],"oEn":["Evaluate and strengthen resistance to deliberately crafted inputs and add mechanisms to detect anomalies","Handling adversarial inputs belongs under the privacy principle and has nothing to do with robustness","Adversarial inputs are theoretical and can be ignored","High accuracy automatically neutralizes adversarial inputs"],"a":0,"e":"意図的に細工された敵対的入力はモデルを誤らせうるため、耐性の評価・強化と異常検知が堅牢性確保に有効。精度だけでは防げない。","eEn":"Deliberately crafted adversarial inputs can mislead models, so evaluating/strengthening resistance and detecting anomalies supports robustness. Accuracy alone doesn't prevent them."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"プライバシー原則における『データ最小化』の考え方に最も合致するのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best aligns with 'data minimization' under the privacy principle?","o":["個人データは削除せず永久に保管する","将来使うかもしれない個人データをできるだけ多く保持する","データは常に第三者と共有して価値を高める","目的達成に必要な最小限の個人データのみを収集・保持する"],"oEn":["Never deleting personal data and keeping it forever","Retaining as much personal data as possible in case it is useful later","Always sharing data with third parties to increase value","Collecting and retaining only the minimum personal data necessary to achieve the purpose"],"a":3,"e":"データ最小化は、目的達成に必要な最小限の個人データのみを扱う原則。過剰収集・永久保管・無制限共有はこれに反する。","eEn":"Data minimization means handling only the minimum personal data needed for the purpose. Over-collection, indefinite retention, or unrestricted sharing violate it."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"複数のマネジメントシステムを『統合マネジメントシステム（IMS）』として運用する主な利点はどれか？","qEn":"What is a main advantage of running multiple management systems as an 'integrated management system (IMS)'?","o":["方針・監査・文書・改善活動を共通化し、重複作業や矛盾を減らして効率と一貫性を高められる","品質やセキュリティと統合したことで、AI固有のリスクは評価しなくてよくなる","IMSとして統合すれば、各規格が定める個別の要求事項を互いに無視してよくなる","複数の規格を一つに統合した時点で、どの規格についても外部審査も認証の維持も受けなくて済むようになる"],"oEn":["Common policies, audits, documents, and improvement activities reduce duplication and conflict, improving efficiency and consistency","Integration with quality and security means AI-specific risks no longer need to be assessed","Once integrated as an IMS, the individual requirements set by each standard may be mutually disregarded","Once the multiple standards are merged into a single system, neither an assessment nor a certificate is required for any of them ever again"],"a":0,"e":"IMSは共通構造を活かして方針・監査・文書・改善を統合し、重複や矛盾を減らして効率と一貫性を高める。要求の無視やリスク評価の省略ではない。","eEn":"An IMS leverages a common structure to unify policies, audits, documents, and improvement, cutting duplication and conflict for efficiency and consistency—not ignoring requirements or skipping risk assessment."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AIライフサイクルの『設計』段階でリスクを検討する意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What best captures the significance of considering risk in the 'design' stage of the AI lifecycle?","o":["リスクへの対応は、ライフサイクル最終段階の廃棄・撤去の時にまとめて扱えば十分である","意図した目的・想定利用者・潜在的な害を早期に検討することで、後段での是正コストと影響を抑えられる","設計段階ではモデルの予測性能を高めることだけをひたすら重視すればそれでよい","設計段階で見つかったリスクは、運用段階に入れば利用者の慣れと時間の経過とともに自動的に消えるため検討は不要"],"oEn":["It is sufficient to handle all risk treatment together only at the final retirement/decommission stage of the lifecycle","Considering intended purpose, expected users, and potential harms early reduces later remediation cost and impact","It is enough at the design stage to relentlessly emphasize only raising the model's predictive performance","Risks found at the design stage automatically disappear over time once operation begins and users get used to it, so no review is needed"],"a":1,"e":"設計段階で意図した目的・利用者・潜在的害を早期に検討することで、後段での手戻りコストや被害を抑えられる。リスクは後回しにできない。","eEn":"Considering intended purpose, users, and potential harms early in design reduces later rework cost and harm. Risk cannot be deferred to the end."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"責任あるAIを支える組織文化において『心理的安全性』が果たす役割はどれか？","qEn":"What role does 'psychological safety' play in an organizational culture supporting responsible AI?","o":["従業員が懸念を口にしないよう暗に沈黙を促し、問題を組織的に隠す","会議の場では経営層だけが発言でき、現場からの懸念や失敗の報告は一切拾わない状態を作る","懸念を報告した従業員を罰することで、組織全体の規律を高めようとする","従業員が懸念や失敗を安心して報告でき、問題を早期に表面化・是正できる"],"oEn":["Implicitly encouraging silence so employees do not voice concerns, systematically hiding problems","Creating a state where only executives may speak in meetings and no concern or failure report from the front line is ever picked up","Attempting to strengthen organization-wide discipline by punishing employees who report concerns","Employees can safely report concerns and failures, surfacing and correcting problems early"],"a":3,"e":"心理的安全性があると従業員が懸念や失敗を率直に報告でき、問題を早期に発見・是正できる。沈黙の助長や報告の懲罰は逆効果。","eEn":"With psychological safety, employees can candidly report concerns and failures, enabling early detection and correction. Encouraging silence or punishing reports is counterproductive."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"透明性・説明責任・公平性などの『責任あるAIの原則』の位置づけとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the standing of the 'responsible AI principles' such as transparency, accountability, and fairness?","o":["現場の個々の技術者が案件ごとに気分次第で採用するかどうかを選べる、拘束力のない単なる推奨事項にすぎない","AIを信頼でき倫理的・社会的に受容可能なものにするための、AIMSの土台となる価値・原則である","特定の一国の国内法だけに登場する、他国では通用しない限定的な法律用語である","モデルの予測精度や再現率といった評価指標を機械的に算出するための計算式に過ぎない"],"oEn":["Merely a non-binding recommendation that individual front-line engineers may adopt or ignore project by project as the mood takes them","Foundational values and principles of an AIMS that make AI trustworthy and ethically and socially acceptable","A limited legal term that appears only in one country's domestic law and does not apply elsewhere","Merely a formula for mechanically computing evaluation metrics such as a model's accuracy and recall"],"a":1,"e":"責任あるAIの原則は、AIを信頼でき社会的に受容可能にするためのAIMSの基盤となる価値・原則群であり、任意の推奨や単なる数式・一国限定用語ではない。","eEn":"The responsible-AI principles are foundational values of an AIMS that make AI trustworthy and socially acceptable—not optional tips, mere formulas, or single-country terms."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.1 で特定した「外部及び内部の課題」は、AIMS の何に影響するものとして考慮すべきか？","qEn":"The external and internal issues identified in Clause 4.1 should be considered as affecting what aspect of the AIMS?","o":["AIMS が意図した成果を達成する能力（有効性）","マーケティング広告の表示回数","データセンターの電力契約単価","AI モデルの学習率のハイパーパラメータ"],"oEn":["The ability of the AIMS to achieve its intended outcomes (its effectiveness)","The impression count of marketing advertisements","The unit price of the data center's electricity contract","The learning-rate hyperparameter of AI models"],"a":0,"e":"4.1 の課題は AIMS が意図した成果を達成する能力に影響し得るものとして特定・考慮する。","eEn":"Clause 4.1 issues are those that can affect the AIMS's ability to achieve its intended outcomes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2 において、利害関係者に関して組織が「決定する」べきものはどれか？","qEn":"Under Clause 4.2, what must the organization determine regarding interested parties?","o":["各利害関係者が保有する自社株式の比率とその推移","利害関係者が業務で使用する端末のOSとブラウザのバージョン情報","AIMS に関連する利害関係者と、その関連する要求事項","各利害関係者に対して割り当てる年間予算の配分計画"],"oEn":["Each interested party's shareholding ratio in the company and its trend over time","Version information for the OS and the browser on the devices interested parties use for work","The interested parties relevant to the AIMS and their relevant requirements","The annual budget allocation plan assigned to each interested party"],"a":2,"e":"4.2 では関連する利害関係者と、それらの関連要求事項（法令・契約含む）を決定する。","eEn":"Clause 4.2 requires determining the relevant interested parties and their relevant requirements, including legal and contractual ones."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.3 で適用範囲を決定する際、組織が考慮しなければならないものはどれか？","qEn":"When determining scope under Clause 4.3, which must the organization consider?","o":["使用しているサーバのブランド名と型番","直近1年における競合他社全体の売上高","内部監査員一人あたりの年間の監査工数の上限","4.1 の課題と 4.2 の要求事項"],"oEn":["The brand name and model number of the servers in use","The total revenue of competitors overall over the past year","The annual audit workload cap per individual internal auditor","The issues from 4.1 and the requirements from 4.2"],"a":3,"e":"適用範囲は 4.1 の課題、4.2 の要求事項、および組織が実施する活動を考慮して決める。","eEn":"Scope is set considering the 4.1 issues, the 4.2 requirements, and the organization's activities."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.3 が要求する適用範囲は、どのような形で保持すべきか？","qEn":"In what form must the scope required by Clause 4.3 be maintained?","o":["文書化した情報として利用可能にする","監査人だけが閲覧できる暗号ファイルにする","経営者の記憶として口頭で共有する","外部公開を禁じられた秘密として扱う"],"oEn":["Available as documented information","Kept as an encrypted file only auditors may view","Shared orally as management's memory","Treated as a secret forbidden from any disclosure"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.3 の適用範囲は、文書化した情報として利用可能にしておく必要がある。監査人だけが見られる暗号ファイルや、経営者の記憶による口頭共有では、文書化した情報とは言えない。外部公開を禁じる秘密扱いも求められていない。","eEn":"The scope under Clause 4.3 must be available as documented information. An encrypted file only auditors can open, or verbal sharing from the managers' memory, is not documented information, and the scope is not required to be a secret."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組織が AI システムに対して「提供者」と「利用者」の両方の役割を持つ場合、Clause 4 の文脈理解ではどう扱うべきか？","qEn":"When an organization acts as both provider and user of AI systems, how should Clause 4 context understanding treat this?","o":["利用者の役割は AIMS の対象外とする","該当する役割を特定し、それぞれの状況・要求を考慮する","提供者の役割だけを考慮すればよい","役割の区別はClause 8の運用段階に入るまで一切無視してよいとする"],"oEn":["The user role is out of AIMS scope","Identify the applicable roles and consider the context and requirements of each","Only the provider role need be considered","Treating the role distinction as ignorable until the Clause 8 operation stage is reached"],"a":1,"e":"組織は自らが担う AI の役割（提供者・利用者等）を特定し、それに応じて状況と要求を考慮する。","eEn":"The organization identifies the AI roles it plays (provider, user, etc.) and considers context and requirements accordingly."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.4『AIマネジメントシステム』が組織に求める基本要求はどれか？","qEn":"What is the fundamental requirement Clause 4.4 places on the organization?","o":["運用しているAIモデルを毎年必ず入れ替えること","組織内で使うすべてのAIを無条件に社外へ公開すること","本規格に従ってAIMSを確立・実施・維持し、継続的に改善すること","AIMSの運用そのものを外部認証機関へ丸ごと委託すること"],"oEn":["Necessarily replacing the AI model in operation every single year","Unconditionally publishing every AI used within the organization to the outside","Establish, implement, maintain and continually improve the AIMS in accordance with the standard","Outsourcing the entire operation of the AIMS wholesale to an external certification body"],"a":2,"e":"4.4 は本規格に従って AIMS を確立・実施・維持し、継続的に改善することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 4.4 requires establishing, implementing, maintaining and continually improving the AIMS per the standard."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.1 で言及される「AIの利用に関連する内部の課題」の例として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate example of an internal issue related to AI use, as referenced in Clause 4.1?","o":["海外から部材を調達する供給網に潜む地政学的リスクと為替変動","各国政府や国際機関が進めるAI規制の最新動向","組織のAI倫理に関する価値観や方針・ガバナンス構造","自社の主要顧客が属する業界全体の景気動向"],"oEn":["Geopolitical risk and currency swings in the supply chain that sources parts from overseas","The latest trends in AI regulation being advanced by national governments and international bodies","The organization's AI-ethics values, policies and governance structure","The overall economic climate of the industry to which the company's main customers belong"],"a":2,"e":"組織の価値観・文化・ガバナンス構造は内部の課題に該当する。規制動向や景気は外部の課題。","eEn":"An organization's values, culture and governance are internal issues; regulatory trends and economy are external."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2 の利害関係者の「要求事項」には、必ずしも組織が全て満たす義務があるわけではない。正しい理解はどれか？","qEn":"Interested parties' requirements under Clause 4.2 are not all necessarily obligations the organization must meet. Which understanding is correct?","o":["組織はどの要求事項を通じて取り組むかを決定できる","特定した要求事項はすべて法的義務になる","要求事項は一度決めたら変更できない","要求事項は利害関係者が組織を介さず直接AIMSの文書に書き込む"],"oEn":["The organization can decide which of these requirements it will address","All identified requirements become legal obligations","Requirements cannot change once set","Interested parties write their requirements straight into the AIMS documents themselves"],"a":0,"e":"組織は利害関係者の要求のうち、どれをAIMSを通じて取り組むかを決定する。全てが義務となるわけではない。","eEn":"The organization decides which interested-party requirements it will address through the AIMS; not all become obligations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"適用範囲（scope）の境界を決める際に含めるべき観点として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is a correct consideration when setting the boundaries of the AIMS scope?","o":["組織の活動間・他組織との相互依存関係","オフィスに保管している印刷用紙の在庫量","内部監査の報告書を配付する社内の宛先の一覧","競合他社が使用しているロゴのデザイン"],"oEn":["Interdependencies between the organization's activities and with other organizations","The stock level of printing paper kept in the office","The in-house distribution list of recipients to whom the internal audit report is circulated","The logo design used by a competitor"],"a":0,"e":"境界を決めるときは、組織が行う活動と他組織が行う活動との相互依存関係を考慮する。印刷用紙の在庫量や、競合他社のロゴのデザインは、AIMSの境界の判断に関係しない。","eEn":"When setting boundaries, the organization considers interdependencies between its own activities and those performed by other organizations. Stock of printing paper or a competitor's logo design has no bearing on the AIMS boundary."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4 の文脈理解と Clause 6 のリスクアセスメントの関係として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the relationship between Clause 4 context understanding and Clause 6 risk assessment?","o":["Clause 4の内容は、Clause 6の結果を一切無視したまま定期的に更新される","Clause 6のリスクアセスメントが完了してから、初めてClause 4を実施する","4 で理解した状況・利害関係者が 6 のリスク及び機会の決定の入力になる","Clause 4とClause 6は完全に独立しており、互いの結果を一切参照しない"],"oEn":["Clause 4's content is periodically updated while completely disregarding Clause 6's results","Clause 4 is carried out only after Clause 6's risk assessment has been completed","The context and parties understood in 4 feed the determination of risks and opportunities in 6","Clause 4 and Clause 6 are entirely independent and never reference each other's outputs"],"a":2,"e":"4.1/4.2 で理解した課題・要求事項が、6.1 のリスク及び機会の決定の入力となる。","eEn":"The issues and requirements understood in 4.1/4.2 are inputs to determining risks and opportunities in 6.1."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1『リーダーシップ及びコミットメント』でトップマネジメントに求められることとして誤っているのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is NOT required of top management under Clause 5.1 'Leadership and commitment'?","o":["内部監査の全チェックリストを自ら記入する","AIMSが意図した成果を達成することを確実にする","AI方針及びAIMS目的の確立を確実にする","AIMSの要求事項を組織のプロセスに統合する"],"oEn":["Personally fill in every internal-audit checklist","Ensure the AIMS achieves its intended outcomes","Ensure the AI policy and AIMS objectives are established","Integrate the AIMS requirements into the organization's processes"],"a":0,"e":"監査チェックリストを自ら記入することは 5.1 の要求ではない。方針確立・統合・成果確保などが求められる。","eEn":"Personally completing audit checklists is not a 5.1 requirement; establishing policy, integration, and ensuring outcomes are."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1 でトップマネジメントが「人々を指揮し支援する」ことが求められる目的として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Under Clause 5.1, top management directing and supporting people is required for what purpose?","o":["AIMSの有効性に貢献させるため","市場から競合他社を排除するため","内部監査の監査員を全員ほかの要員に交代させるため","マーケティング広告費を最適化するため"],"oEn":["To contribute to the effectiveness of the AIMS","To drive competitors out of the market","In order to replace every one of the internal auditors","To optimize the marketing advertising budget"],"a":0,"e":"5.1 は、人々がAIMSの有効性に貢献するよう指揮し支援することをトップマネジメントに求める。競合他社を市場から排除することや、広告費の最適化は、この要求の目的ではない。","eEn":"Clause 5.1 requires top management to direct and support people so that they contribute to the effectiveness of the AIMS. Driving competitors out of the market or optimizing advertising spend is not the purpose of this requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.2『AI方針』について、方針を「利用可能にする」対象として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"Regarding Clause 5.2 'AI policy', to whom must the policy be made available?","o":["文書化した情報として利用可能にし、組織内で伝達し、必要に応じ利害関係者へ","第三者認証審査の監査を受ける時にのみ一時的に開示する","AI方針の内容を一般消費者に対してのみ口頭で伝える","トップマネジメントのみが保持し、他の従業員は一切閲覧できない"],"oEn":["Available as documented information, communicated within the organization, and, as appropriate, to interested parties","Disclosed only temporarily, and only when undergoing a third-party certification audit","Communicating the AI policy's content orally, only to general consumers","Held only by top management, with no other employee permitted to view it at all"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針は文書化した情報として利用可能とし、組織内で伝達し、必要に応じ利害関係者に利用可能とする。","eEn":"The AI policy is available as documented information, communicated within the organization, and available to interested parties as appropriate."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.2 が AI方針に含めることを求めるコミットメントの組合せとして正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"Which combination of commitments does Clause 5.2 require the AI policy to include?","o":["コスト削減を目的とした従業員数の削減と拠点統合","組織が保有するすべてのAIのモデルとコードのオープンソース化と無償配布","全案件における最大利益と最短納期を無条件に保証すること","適用される要求事項を満たすこと、及びAIMSの継続的改善"],"oEn":["Reducing headcount and consolidating sites for the purpose of cost cutting","Open-sourcing and giving away for free every AI model and its code that the organization owns","Unconditionally guaranteeing maximum profit and the shortest delivery time on every project","Satisfying applicable requirements, and continual improvement of the AIMS"],"a":3,"e":"AI方針は、適用される要求事項を満たすことと、AIMSの継続的改善へのコミットメントを含む。従業員数の削減や拠点統合、全モデルのオープンソース化、最大利益と最短納期の無条件の保証は、方針に求められる内容ではない。","eEn":"The AI policy must include a commitment to satisfy applicable requirements and a commitment to continual improvement of the AIMS. Cutting staff, open-sourcing every model, or guaranteeing maximum profit and the shortest delivery are not required."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AI方針は組織のどの方針と整合していることが望ましいか？","qEn":"With which of the organization's directions should the AI policy be consistent?","o":["組織の目的（purpose）及び他の方針との整合","組織が所属する業界団体が毎月発行する会報や広報誌の内容","直近に発表された競合他社のプレスリリース","特定の顧客個人が私的に投稿したSNSの内容"],"oEn":["The organization's purpose and its other policies","The content of the monthly newsletter issued by the industry body the organization belongs to","A press release recently issued by a competitor","The content of a social-media post a specific individual customer made privately"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針は組織の目的に対して適切であり、他の関連方針と整合していることが求められる。","eEn":"The AI policy must be appropriate to the organization's purpose and consistent with its other relevant policies."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.3『組織の役割、責任及び権限』でトップマネジメントが確実にすべきことはどれか？","qEn":"Under Clause 5.3 'Organizational roles, responsibilities and authorities', what must top management ensure?","o":["関連する役割の責任及び権限が割り当てられ、伝達されること","組織内の権限はすべて外部監査機関が代わりに割り当てること","役職に関係なくすべての従業員が同一の権限を持つこと","誰がどの役割を担うか匿名にして誰にも特定できないこと"],"oEn":["Responsibilities and authorities for relevant roles are assigned and communicated","All authority within the organization being assigned by an external audit body","Every employee holding identical authority regardless of position","Anonymizing who holds which role so that no one can be identified"],"a":0,"e":"5.3 は関連役割の責任・権限を割り当て、組織内に伝達することを確実にするよう求める。","eEn":"Clause 5.3 requires ensuring responsibilities and authorities for relevant roles are assigned and communicated within the organization."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.3 で割り当てられる責任・権限の代表例として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is a representative example of the responsibilities/authorities assigned under Clause 5.3?","o":["全社員が取る昼食時間を一律に決める責任","AIMSが本規格に適合することを確実にする責任","毎年恒例の社内旅行の行き先と日程、宿泊先を企画する責任","外部の認証機関の審査員を自社の社員として採用する責任"],"oEn":["The responsibility of uniformly deciding the lunch hour all staff take","Ensuring the AIMS conforms to this standard","The responsibility for planning the destination, dates, and lodging for the annual company trip","The responsibility for hiring an external certification body's auditors as the company's own employees"],"a":1,"e":"5.3 では、AIMSが規格に適合することの確保や、パフォーマンスの報告などの責任・権限を割り当てる。","eEn":"Clause 5.3 assigns responsibilities such as ensuring AIMS conformity and reporting on AIMS performance."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.3 において、AIMS のパフォーマンスに関する報告先として想定されるのはどれか？","qEn":"Under Clause 5.3, to whom is the reporting on AIMS performance expected to go?","o":["一般公衆全員","トップマネジメント","競合企業","認証機関の一般職員"],"oEn":["The entire general public","Top management","Competitor companies","General staff of a certification body"],"a":1,"e":"AIMSのパフォーマンスをトップマネジメントに報告する責任・権限が割り当てられる。","eEn":"Responsibility/authority to report AIMS performance to top management is assigned."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AI方針が満たすべき性質のうち、Clause 5.2 に照らして誤っているのはどれか？","qEn":"Which property does Clause 5.2 NOT require of the AI policy?","o":["組織内で伝達される","組織の目的に対し適切である","AIMS目的の設定のための枠組みを与える","四半期ごとに必ず全面改訂される"],"oEn":["Is communicated within the organization","Is appropriate to the organization's purpose","Provides a framework for setting AIMS objectives","Is fully rewritten every quarter without exception"],"a":3,"e":"四半期ごとの全面改訂は要求されない。方針は必要に応じ見直すが強制的な周期は規定されない。","eEn":"A mandatory quarterly full rewrite is not required; the policy is reviewed as needed, with no prescribed cycle."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"トップマネジメントが「AIMSの要求事項を組織の事業プロセスに統合する」ことを確実にする意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the significance of top management ensuring AIMS requirements are integrated into business processes?","o":["AIMSが日常業務と切り離された形骸にならないようにする","内部監査や第三者認証審査の対象範囲から外し、意図的に回避できるようにする","将来的にAIMSそのものを段階的に廃止しやすくする","AIMSに関して作成する文書量を極力最小化すること"],"oEn":["To prevent the AIMS from becoming a hollow system detached from daily operations","Making it possible to keep it out of scope and deliberately evade internal audits and certification audits","Making it easier to eventually phase out and abolish the AIMS itself","Minimizing as much as possible the volume of documents produced for the AIMS"],"a":0,"e":"事業プロセスへ統合することで、AIMSが日常業務と切り離された形骸にならず、実効性を持つ。内部監査や第三者認証審査の対象から外して意図的に回避する、文書量を極力最小化する、といったことは統合の意義ではない。","eEn":"Integrating the AIMS requirements into business processes keeps it from becoming an empty system detached from daily work. Escaping internal audits or certification audits, or minimizing the volume of documents, is not the point of integration."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2 の「利害関係者」に含めるべき対象として最も広く適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most broadly appropriate set to include as 'interested parties' under Clause 4.2?","o":["トップマネジメントである経営者のみに限定する","AIシステムを保守運用するIT部門だけを対象にすること","議決権を持つ会社の大株主のみを唯一の対象とする","顧客・規制当局・従業員・供給者・AIの影響を受ける個人や社会"],"oEn":["Limiting it solely to the executives who make up top management","Making it apply only to the IT department that maintains and operates the AI system","Targeting solely the company's major shareholders who hold voting rights","Customers, regulators, employees, suppliers, and individuals or society affected by the AI"],"a":3,"e":"AIの影響を受ける個人・社会を含む幅広い利害関係者を考慮するのがAIMSの特徴。","eEn":"AIMS considers a broad set of parties, including individuals and society affected by the AI."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.1 で「関連する場合には、AIの利用に伴う気候変動やその他の課題」を考慮する趣旨に最も近いのはどれか？","qEn":"What best reflects the intent of considering, where relevant, climate change and other issues from AI use in Clause 4.1?","o":["AIモデルの計算精度をひたすら高めることだけを指す","AI関連システムの画面表示における色調と明るさの設定を最適化すること","AIの利用が及ぼす広範な社会的・環境的側面を状況として捉える","AIモデルの推論にかかる速度のみを継続的に測ること"],"oEn":["Refers only to relentlessly raising an AI model's computational accuracy","Optimizing the color-tone and brightness settings of AI-related systems' screen display","Capturing the broad societal and environmental aspects of AI use as context","Continually measuring only the speed of an AI model's inference"],"a":2,"e":"4.1は、AI固有の広範な社会的・環境的影響を組織の状況として捉えることを促す。","eEn":"Clause 4.1 encourages capturing AI's broad societal and environmental impacts as organizational context."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AIMSの適用範囲から特定の活動を除外する場合、正しい扱いはどれか？","qEn":"When excluding a particular activity from the AIMS scope, which handling is correct?","o":["適用範囲は文書化情報として維持し、その境界と適用可能性を明確に反映させる","除外は範囲文書に記さず監査員への口頭申告だけで完結させてよい","除外した活動は適用範囲の文書化情報から完全に削除し記録を残さない","除外の判断は現場担当者のみで完結させ経営層の承認は求めない"],"oEn":["The scope is maintained as documented information, clearly reflecting its boundaries, exclusions, and applicability","Exclusion is completed by a verbal notice to the auditor alone, without recording it in the scope document","Excluded activities are erased entirely from the scope's documented information with no record retained","The exclusion decision is completed by frontline staff alone, without seeking top management's approval"],"a":0,"e":"除外する場合も、適用範囲は文書化した情報として維持し、境界と適用可能性を明確に反映させる。口頭申告だけで済ませる、範囲文書から削除して記録を残さない、経営層の承認を求めない、といった扱いは不適切。","eEn":"Even when an activity is excluded, the scope must be kept as documented information that clearly reflects its boundaries and applicability. Settling it by verbal notice alone, deleting it without a record, or skipping management approval is improper."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"リーダーシップ（Clause 5）とマネジメント（管理）の違いを Foundation 観点で述べたものとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"From a Foundation perspective, which best states the difference between leadership (Clause 5) and management?","o":["管理という語はトップマネジメントの職位のみに限定して使われる","リーダーシップは方針文書の作成手続きのみを指す狭い概念である","リーダーシップと管理は規格の本文上まったく同じ意味であり、章ごとに使い分ける必要はない","リーダーシップは方向性・コミットメント・文化醸成を担い、管理は日々の統制を担う"],"oEn":["The term management is used only to denote the position of top management","Leadership refers only to the narrow procedure of drafting the policy document","Leadership and management carry an identical meaning in the text of the standard, so no clause needs to tell them apart","Leadership sets direction, commitment and culture; management handles day-to-day control"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 5はトップの方向づけ・関与・文化醸成を扱い、日常統制の管理と区別される。","eEn":"Clause 5 concerns top-level direction, engagement and culture, distinct from day-to-day management control."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1 でトップマネジメントが「AIMSに必要な資源が利用可能であることを確実にする」ことは、どの後続要求と最も関係が深いか？","qEn":"Top management ensuring resources for the AIMS are available under Clause 5.1 most closely relates to which later requirement?","o":["Clause 4.3『適用範囲』","Clause 7.1『資源』","Clause 10.2『不適合及び是正処置』","Clause 9.2『内部監査』"],"oEn":["Clause 4.3 'Scope'","Clause 7.1 'Resources'","Clause 10.2 'Nonconformity and corrective action'","Clause 9.2 'Internal audit'"],"a":1,"e":"5.1の資源確保のコミットメントは、7.1で具体的な資源の決定・提供として展開される。","eEn":"The 5.1 commitment to resources is operationalized in 7.1 where resources are determined and provided."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組織が AIMS を確立する初期段階で、Clause 4 の活動を先に行う理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is it most appropriate to perform Clause 4 activities early when establishing an AIMS?","o":["認証費用が下がるという経済的な動機が何よりも重視されるから","監査を省略できるという認証上の利点が得られるから","文書量を最小化できるという事務効率の理由が優先されるから","状況・利害関係者・適用範囲の理解が方針や計画の土台になるから"],"oEn":["Because the economic motive of lowering certification fees is valued above all else","Because it yields the certification benefit of allowing audits to be skipped","Because the priority reason is administrative efficiency in minimizing document volume","Understanding context, interested parties and scope forms the basis for policy and planning"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 4の理解が、Clause 5の方針やClause 6の計画の前提・入力となる。","eEn":"Clause 4 understanding is the prerequisite and input for Clause 5 policy and Clause 6 planning."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.2 の AI方針が「AIの責任ある開発・利用に関する組織の意図」を反映する意義に最も近いのはどれか？","qEn":"What best reflects the significance of the Clause 5.2 AI policy expressing the organization's intent on responsible development and use of AI?","o":["組織全体に一貫した価値観と方向性を示す","販売価格表を提示する","個々のモデルの実装コードと設定値をすべて記載する","AIの技術仕様を詳細に規定する"],"oEn":["Providing consistent values and direction across the organization","Presenting a price list","Listing the implementation code and the configuration values of every individual model","Specifying detailed technical specs of the AI"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針は、責任あるAIに関する組織の意図を示し、組織全体に一貫した価値観と方向性を与える。個々のモデルの実装コードや設定値の記載、AIの技術仕様の詳細な規定は方針の役割ではない。","eEn":"The AI policy expresses the organization's intent on responsible AI and gives the whole organization consistent values and direction. Listing implementation code and settings for each model, or detailing technical specifications, is not its role."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2 で考慮する利害関係者の要求事項に含まれ得るものとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is most appropriately included among interested-party requirements considered in Clause 4.2?","o":["競合の広告予算に関するマーケティング分析資料","内部監査を実施する具体的な日程と監査会場の割り当て","適用される法令・規制上の要求及び契約上の義務","従業員の私的な趣味に関する任意のアンケート結果"],"oEn":["Marketing analysis materials concerning competitors' advertising budgets","The concrete dates for conducting internal audits and the allocation of audit venues","Applicable legal/regulatory requirements and contractual obligations","Voluntary survey results about employees' private hobbies"],"a":2,"e":"利害関係者の関連要求事項には、適用される法令・規制上の要求や契約上の義務が含まれ得る。競合の広告予算の分析資料や、内部監査の日程と会場の割り当て、従業員の趣味に関するアンケートは、要求事項に当たらない。","eEn":"Relevant requirements of interested parties can include applicable legal and regulatory requirements and contractual obligations. Analysis of a competitor's ad budget, audit schedules and venues, or a survey of employees' hobbies are not such requirements."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AIMSの適用範囲を決める際、AIシステムに対する組織の役割（提供者・開発者・利用者等）を考慮する理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"When setting AIMS scope, why is it appropriate to consider the organization's role toward the AI system (provider, developer, user, etc.)?","o":["役割は競合他社を分析するための指標にすぎないから","担う役割により適用される管理策の妥当性や責任の範囲が変わるから","役割を明記すると適用範囲の文書がかえって短くなるから","役割は認証審査の判定に一切影響しない形式的事項だから"],"oEn":["Because the role is merely a metric used to analyze competitors","Because the applicable controls' relevance and responsibility boundaries differ by the role played","Because stating the role actually shortens the scope document","Because the role is a mere formality that has no bearing on the certification decision"],"a":1,"e":"組織が担う役割によって、責任範囲や適用すべき管理策の妥当性が変わるため考慮する。","eEn":"The role determines responsibility boundaries and which controls are applicable, so it must be considered."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1 が求める「AIガバナンス文化の醸成を促進する」ことに最も近い行動はどれか？","qEn":"Which action best fits promoting an AI-governance culture as encouraged by Clause 5.1?","o":["AIに関する意思決定をすべて自動化し、関与する人を排除する","方針を金庫にしまい誰にも見せない","AI利用を全面的に禁止する","責任あるAIの価値観を組織全体で共有・奨励する"],"oEn":["Fully automating every AI-related decision and removing the people involved from it","Locking the policy in a safe hidden from all","Banning all AI use entirely","Sharing and encouraging responsible-AI values across the organization"],"a":3,"e":"責任あるAIの価値観を組織全体で共有し奨励することが、AIガバナンス文化の醸成につながる。意思決定をすべて自動化して人を排除すること、方針を金庫にしまうこと、AI利用の全面禁止は、文化の醸成とは逆の行動。","eEn":"Sharing and encouraging responsible-AI values across the organization fosters an AI governance culture. Automating every decision to exclude people, locking the policy in a safe, or banning all AI use runs counter to building such a culture."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"「AIMSの意図した成果」の理解として Foundation 観点で最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"From a Foundation perspective, which best describes the 'intended outcomes' of the AIMS?","o":["AIモデルの推論レイテンシなど個別の性能指標のみを継続的に測定すること","組織がAIMSを通じて達成しようとする成果・目的（責任あるAIの実現等）","データセンターのPUE値のみを継続的に監視すること","広告のクリック率のみを毎月最大化しようとする短期的な目標"],"oEn":["Continually measuring only individual performance metrics such as the AI model's inference latency","The outcomes and objectives the organization seeks through the AIMS (e.g. responsible AI)","Continually monitoring only the data center's PUE value","A short-term goal aimed solely at maximizing the ad click-through rate every month"],"a":1,"e":"意図した成果とは、組織がAIMSを通じて達成しようとする成果や目的で、責任あるAIの実現などを指す。推論レイテンシのような個別の性能指標や、PUE値、広告のクリック率だけでは、AIMS全体の成果を表せない。","eEn":"Intended outcomes are what the organization aims to achieve through the AIMS, such as realizing responsible AI. Individual metrics like inference latency, data-center PUE, or advertising click-through rate alone cannot represent the outcomes of the whole AIMS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.3 で役割・責任・権限を「伝達する」ことが重要な理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is communicating roles, responsibilities and authorities important under Clause 5.3?","o":["各人が自らの役割と権限を理解し実行できるようにするため","組織図を美しく描き直して外部の来訪者に見せるための体裁を整えるため","責任を分散して誰も負わないようにするため","権限の所在をあえて曖昧にして責任追及を避けるため"],"oEn":["So each person understands and can act on their role and authority","To tidy up the org chart so that it looks polished when shown to outside visitors","To diffuse responsibility so no one bears it","To deliberately keep the locus of authority ambiguous and avoid being held responsible"],"a":0,"e":"役割・責任・権限を伝達することで、各人が自分の役割と権限を理解し、実行できるようになる。組織図を外部の来訪者向けに整えることや、責任を分散して誰も負わないようにすること、権限の所在を曖昧にすることは目的ではない。","eEn":"Communicating roles, responsibilities and authorities lets each person understand and carry out their own role. Tidying the org chart for visitors, spreading responsibility so nobody bears it, or keeping authority vague is not the aim."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.1 と 4.2 のアウトプットを維持・更新すべき理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is it appropriate to maintain and update the outputs of Clauses 4.1 and 4.2?","o":["規格が毎年名称を変更するので追随する必要があるから","組織の状況や利害関係者の要求は時間とともに変化するから","一度決定した内容は将来にわたって一切変わらないから","監査官が審査のたびに内容を消去してしまうから"],"oEn":["Because the standard renames itself every year and must be followed","Because the organization's context and interested-party requirements change over time","Because whatever is decided once never changes in the future","Because the auditor erases the content at every audit"],"a":1,"e":"組織の状況や利害関係者の要求は時間とともに変化するため、4.1 と 4.2 の結果は維持・更新する必要がある。一度決めた内容が将来にわたって変わらない、という前提は誤りで、規格が毎年名称を変えるから追随するわけでもない。","eEn":"The organization's context and the needs of interested parties change over time, so the outputs of 4.1 and 4.2 must be maintained and updated. It is wrong to assume they never change, and the reason is not that the standard renames itself every year."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AI方針を「組織内で伝達する（communicate）」ことと「文書化情報として利用可能にする（available）」ことの関係として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the correct relationship between 'communicating' the AI policy within the organization and making it 'available' as documented information?","o":["伝達は不要で文書化のみでよい","文書化は不要で口頭のみでよい","どちらか一方だけでよい","両方が求められ、補完的である"],"oEn":["Communication is unnecessary; documentation suffices","Documentation is unnecessary; oral suffices","Only one of the two is needed","Both are required and complementary"],"a":3,"e":"5.2は方針を文書化情報として利用可能にし、かつ組織内で伝達することの両方を求める。","eEn":"Clause 5.2 requires both making the policy available as documented information and communicating it internally."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組織が Clause 4.4 で AIMS を「維持する（maintain）」ことに最も近い意味はどれか？","qEn":"What does 'maintaining' the AIMS under Clause 4.4 most nearly mean?","o":["確立した仕組みを外部の事業者に売却して手放すこと","確立した仕組みを継続的に機能させ有効な状態に保つこと","一度確立した仕組みをそのまま放置し見直さないこと","確立した仕組みを毎回すべてゼロから作り直すこと"],"oEn":["Selling off the established system to an external provider","Keeping the established system functioning and effective over time","Leaving the system as established, without any further review","Rebuilding the established system entirely from scratch every time"],"a":1,"e":"維持するとは、確立したAIMSを継続的に機能させ、有効な状態に保つこと。外部の事業者に売却して手放すことや、見直さず放置すること、毎回ゼロから作り直すことは、維持の意味ではない。","eEn":"To maintain the AIMS means to keep what has been established functioning and effective on an ongoing basis. Selling it to an outside business, leaving it without review, or rebuilding it from scratch each time is not maintenance."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 5.1 でトップマネジメントが「継続的改善を促進する」ことは、どの Clause の活動を後押しするか？","qEn":"Top management promoting continual improvement under Clause 5.1 supports the activities of which clause?","o":["Clause 7.4『コミュニケーション』","Clause 4.3『適用範囲』","Clause 10『改善』","Clause 8.1『運用の計画』"],"oEn":["Clause 7.4 'Communication'","Clause 4.3 'Scope'","Clause 10 'Improvement'","Clause 8.1 'Operational planning'"],"a":2,"e":"リーダーシップの継続的改善の促進は、Clause 10の改善活動の推進力となる。","eEn":"Leadership's promotion of continual improvement drives the improvement activities of Clause 10."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AI方針とAIMS目的（objectives）の関係として正しいのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the correct relationship between the AI policy and the AIMS objectives?","o":["目的が方針の上位に立ち方針を破棄できる","方針が目的設定のための枠組みを提供する","両者は無関係である","目的が方針を無視して設定される"],"oEn":["Objectives supersede and can discard the policy","The policy provides a framework for setting objectives","They are unrelated","Objectives are set ignoring the policy"],"a":1,"e":"5.2 の方針は、AIMS目的を設定するための枠組みを与える。目的が方針の上位に立って方針を破棄できるわけではなく、両者は無関係でもなく、目的が方針を無視して設定されることもない。","eEn":"The policy in 5.2 provides the framework for setting AIMS objectives. Objectives do not outrank the policy or let it be discarded, the two are not unrelated, and objectives are not set while ignoring the policy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.2 において「AIに固有の利害関係者」を考慮する必要性が高い理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is considering AI-specific interested parties particularly necessary in Clause 4.2?","o":["AIは株主の投資判断にのみ影響を及ぼす技術だから","AIは影響を受ける個人・社会など従来と異なる利害関係者を新たに生むから","AIは従来の利害関係者と本質的に同一で新たな関係者を生まないから","AIは開発技術者の業務にしか関係しない専門領域だから"],"oEn":["Because AI is a technology that affects only shareholders' investment decisions","AI newly creates interested parties beyond the traditional ones, such as affected individuals and society","Because AI is essentially identical to traditional interested parties and creates no new ones","Because AI is a specialty concerning only the work of development engineers"],"a":1,"e":"AI特有の影響（個人・社会・被影響者）ゆえ、従来より広い利害関係者の考慮が必要になる。","eEn":"AI's distinctive impacts on individuals and society require considering a broader set of parties than usual."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"トップマネジメントが AIMS のリーダーシップを「委譲」できる範囲について、Clause 5 の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Regarding how far top management may 'delegate' AIMS leadership, what best reflects the intent of Clause 5?","o":["リーダーシップに関する説明責任も含め、権限のすべてを下位の管理職に委譲できる","日常の実務は委譲できるが、リーダーシップの説明責任はトップに残る","委譲さえすれば規格への適合を証明する必要がなくなる","リーダーシップの委譲はいかなる場合も一切認められない"],"oEn":["Everything, including accountability for leadership itself, can be handed down to subordinate managers","Day-to-day tasks may be delegated, but accountability for leadership remains with top management","Delegating alone removes the need to demonstrate conformity to the standard","Delegation of leadership is not permitted under any circumstances whatsoever"],"a":1,"e":"日常の実務は委譲できても、リーダーシップとコミットメントの説明責任はトップマネジメントに残る。説明責任まで含めて権限のすべてを下位の管理職に委譲できるわけではなく、委譲すれば適合の証明が不要になるわけでもない。","eEn":"Day-to-day tasks can be delegated, but accountability for leadership and commitment stays with top management. Authority cannot be handed down entirely, including accountability, and delegating does not remove the need to demonstrate conformity."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 4.3 で決定した適用範囲が Clause 6.1 のリスク及び機会の決定に与える影響として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"How does the scope set in Clause 4.3 most appropriately affect the determination of risks and opportunities in Clause 6.1?","o":["適用範囲はリスク及び機会の検討とは独立して決められる","適用範囲を確定させれば内部監査は不要になる","範囲がリスク・機会を検討する対象境界を画定する","適用範囲を広げるほどリスクは自動的に消去される"],"oEn":["The scope is determined independently, unrelated to the consideration of risks and opportunities","Once the scope is fixed, internal audits become unnecessary","The scope delimits the boundary within which risks and opportunities are considered","The wider the scope, the more risks are automatically eliminated"],"a":2,"e":"適用範囲は、どの活動やシステムについてリスクと機会を検討するかの境界を定める。リスク・機会の検討と独立に決まるものではなく、範囲を広げればリスクが自動的に消えるわけでも、内部監査が不要になるわけでもない。","eEn":"The scope defines the boundary of the activities and systems for which risks and opportunities are considered. It is not decided independently of that work, and widening it neither removes risks automatically nor makes internal audits unnecessary."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.2『AIリスクアセスメント』が組織に求める第一歩に最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best describes the first step required by Clause 6.1.2 (AI risk assessment)?","o":["リスク基準を定める前に、リスク対応計画と予算をまず承認してしまう","基準を定めず内部監査プログラムだけを先に策定する","AIリスク基準（受容基準・実施基準）を確立し維持する","評価前の暫定段階で残留リスクを利害関係者に開示する"],"oEn":["Approving the risk treatment plan and its budget first, before any risk criteria have been set","Drafting only the internal audit programme first, without setting any criteria","Establish and maintain AI risk criteria (acceptance and performance criteria)","Disclosing residual risk to interested parties at a provisional stage before evaluation"],"a":2,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは、まずリスク基準（受容基準と実施のための基準）を確立・維持し、繰り返し実施しても一貫し妥当で比較可能な結果が得られるようにすることから始まる。","eEn":"AI risk assessment begins by establishing and maintaining AI risk criteria so that repeated assessments yield consistent, valid, and comparable results."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.4『AIシステム影響評価』が主として評価対象とするのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 6.1.4 (AI system impact assessment) primarily assess?","o":["組織のブランド認知度を測る顧客調査の結果","調達先サプライヤの財務健全性を示す信用格付けと直近の決算情報","競合他社の市場シェアを比較した業界レポート","個人・個人の集団・社会に対する潜在的な影響（帰結）"],"oEn":["The results of a customer survey measuring the organization's brand awareness","Credit ratings and recent financial statements showing a supplier's financial health","An industry report comparing competitors' market share","Potential consequences to individuals, groups of individuals, and societies"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、AIシステムが個人・個人の集団、及び社会にもたらしうる帰結（影響）を評価するプロセスであり、通常のリスクアセスメントを補完する。","eEn":"The AI system impact assessment evaluates potential consequences to individuals, groups of individuals, and societies, complementing the risk assessment."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.3『AIリスク対応』で作成が求められる、選択した管理策と適用理由をまとめた文書は？","qEn":"Which document, summarizing selected controls and justification, is required by Clause 6.1.3 (AI risk treatment)?","o":["経営層が承認したマネジメントレビューの議事録一式を、そのまま開催日順に綴じて保管したもの","トップマネジメントが単独で策定し公開しているAI方針の全文そのもの","各従業員の力量評価を年次で記録した個別の人事評価記録一式のみ","適用宣言書（Statement of Applicability）に相当する文書"],"oEn":["The full set of management review minutes approved by top management, filed in order of meeting date","The full text of the AI policy, drafted and published by top management alone","Only the full set of individual HR evaluation records that annually track each employee's competence","A Statement of Applicability-type document"],"a":3,"e":"AIリスク対応では、必要な管理策を決定し、Annex A の参照管理策と比較したうえで、選択・除外の理由と実施状況をまとめた適用宣言書に相当する文書を作成する。","eEn":"Risk treatment requires determining controls, comparing them against Annex A reference controls, and producing a Statement of Applicability documenting inclusion/exclusion justifications."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.3 において、決定した管理策を『参照管理策の一覧』と比較する主な目的は？","qEn":"In Clause 6.1.3, why compare the determined controls against the reference list of controls?","o":["リスク対応に必要な管理策が見落とされていないか検証するため","比較を省いて監査員の作業量を減らすため","比較を省略して文書量を最小限に削減するため","認証費用を抑えるために管理策の数を最大化するため"],"oEn":["To verify that no control necessary for risk treatment has been overlooked","To skip the comparison and reduce the auditor's workload","To omit the comparison and minimize the amount of documentation","To maximize the number of controls to hold down certification fees"],"a":0,"e":"Annex A などの参照管理策と比較するのは、リスク対応で必要な管理策が漏れなく考慮されていることを確認するためである。","eEn":"Comparing against reference controls (e.g., Annex A) ensures no necessary control has been inadvertently omitted from treatment."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.3『変更の計画』が求めているのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 6.3 (planning of changes) require?","o":["AIMSへのいかなる変更も理由を問わず一律に禁止すること","AIMSへの変更が必要と組織が判断した場合に計画的な方法で実施すること","変更の内容をトップマネジメントには事前にも事後にも一切知らせないこと","変更を実施した後もその結果に関する記録を一切残さないこと"],"oEn":["Prohibiting any change to the AIMS uniformly, regardless of the reason","When the organization determines changes to the AIMS are needed, carrying them out in a planned manner","Never informing top management of the change, either before or after it is made","Keeping no record whatsoever of the outcome even after a change has been carried out"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.3 は、AIMSに変更が必要と組織が判断したとき、その変更を計画的に（planned manner）行うことを求める。","eEn":"Clause 6.3 requires that when the organization determines a need to change the AIMS, the changes be carried out in a planned manner."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.1『一般』において、リスク及び機会への取組みを組織に統合する意図として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Under Clause 6.1.1 (general), what is the intended purpose of addressing risks and opportunities?","o":["リスクへの責任のすべてを外部委託先だけに一方的に移し、組織側は監督にも報告にもまったく関与しないこと","AIMSが意図した成果を達成でき望ましくない影響を防止・低減できるという確信を得ること","文書の書式をすべての部門で例外なく統一し内容の差異を一切無視すること","内部監査の実施頻度を状況に関わらず一律にあらかじめ固定してしまうこと"],"oEn":["Unilaterally shifting all responsibility for risk onto the outsourced provider while the organization takes no part in oversight or reporting","Giving assurance the AIMS can achieve intended outcomes and prevent/reduce undesired effects","Standardizing the document format without exception across every department, ignoring all differences in content","Fixing the frequency of internal audits uniformly in advance, regardless of any circumstances"],"a":1,"e":"6.1.1 の狙いは、AIMSが意図した成果を達成でき、望ましくない影響を防止または低減し、継続的改善を達成できるという確信を得ることにある。","eEn":"The aim of 6.1.1 is to give assurance the AIMS can achieve intended outcomes, prevent or reduce undesired effects, and achieve continual improvement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2『AIMS目的』が満たすべき性質として誤っているのは？","qEn":"Which is NOT a required characteristic of AIMS objectives under Clause 6.2?","o":["一度定めたら状況が変わっても決して更新しないこと","AI方針と整合していること","（実行可能な場合）測定可能であること","監視されること"],"oEn":["Never being updated once set, even when circumstances change","Being consistent with the AI policy","Being measurable (if practicable)","Being monitored"],"a":0,"e":"AIMS目的は方針と整合し、（実行可能なら）測定可能で、監視・伝達され、必要に応じて更新されなければならない。『決して更新しない』は誤り。","eEn":"AIMS objectives must be consistent with policy, measurable if practicable, monitored, communicated, and updated as appropriate — 'never updated' is wrong."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2 が、目的達成の『計画』を立てるときに決めるよう求めていないのは？","qEn":"When planning to achieve objectives, which item does Clause 6.2 NOT require the organization to determine?","o":["必要な資源（人員・予算・計算資源）","何を行うか","責任者","競合他社の目的値"],"oEn":["What resources are required (people, budget, and compute)","What will be done","Who is responsible","Competitors' target values"],"a":3,"e":"6.2 は、何を行うか・必要な資源・責任者・完了時期・結果の評価方法を計画するよう求める。競合他社の目標値は要求事項に含まれない。","eEn":"6.2 requires planning what will be done, resources, responsibility, completion timing, and how results are evaluated — competitors' targets are not a requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.2 で、AIリスクアセスメントを『繰り返し実施しても一貫し妥当で比較可能な結果』が得られるようにする狙いは？","qEn":"Why must AI risk assessments per Clause 6.1.2 produce consistent, valid, and comparable results when repeated?","o":["評価結果を外部に公開せず監査そのものを不要にするため","時間や担当者が変わってもリスク評価の再現性・比較可能性を確保するため","十分な検討や担当者間の比較をせず、リスクをすべて無条件に受容する方針を固定するため","評価にまつわる文書化情報のすべてを一律に破棄し保持しないため"],"oEn":["To withhold results from external disclosure and make audits themselves unnecessary","To ensure reproducibility and comparability of results across time and personnel","To adopt a fixed policy of accepting every risk unconditionally, without any comparison or sufficient consideration","To discard every piece of documented information tied to the evaluation across the board, keeping none of it"],"a":1,"e":"一貫性・妥当性・比較可能性を求めるのは、評価者や時点が変わってもリスク評価の結果を再現・比較でき、意思決定の信頼性を保つためである。","eEn":"Requiring consistency, validity, and comparability ensures results can be reproduced and compared across assessors and time, keeping decisions reliable."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.3 の残留リスクについて、AIMSが求める扱いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"How does the AIMS expect residual risks to be handled under Clause 6.1.3?","o":["残留リスクは外部への公表を一切禁止する","残留リスクは承認を得ず力量記録として保管する","リスク所有者による承認（受容）を得る","評価後は残留リスクを自動的にゼロとみなす"],"oEn":["Disclosure of residual risk to outsiders is prohibited entirely","Residual risk is filed as a competence record without obtaining any approval","Obtain acceptance/approval by risk owners","Once evaluation is finished, residual risk is automatically treated as zero"],"a":2,"e":"リスク対応後に残る残留リスクは、リスク所有者（risk owners）の承認を得たうえで受容するのが要求事項に沿った扱いである。","eEn":"After treatment, residual risks are to be accepted with the approval of risk owners, as required by the standard."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.1『資源』が組織に求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 7.1 (resources) require of the organization?","o":["内部の資源は一切使わず外部の資源にのみ全面的に依存すること","資源に関する計画も予算枠もあえて作らず、状況に応じて場当たり的に対応し続けること","品質や適合性は一切問わず最も安価な資源のみを選定し続けること","AIMSの確立・実施・維持・継続的改善に必要な資源を決定し提供すること"],"oEn":["Relying entirely on external resources alone, using no internal resources whatsoever","Deliberately drawing up neither a resource plan nor a budget envelope, and responding on an ad hoc basis as each situation happens to arise","Continuing to select only the cheapest resources, without any regard for their quality or suitability","Determining and providing the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve the AIMS"],"a":3,"e":"7.1 は、AIMSの確立・実施・維持・継続的改善に必要な資源を組織が決定し、提供することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.1 requires the organization to determine and provide the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve the AIMS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.2『力量』において、力量の根拠として認められるのは？","qEn":"Under Clause 7.2 (competence), on what basis may competence be established?","o":["勤続年数のみ","適切な教育・訓練・経験","役職の高さのみ","本人の自己申告のみ"],"oEn":["Length of service only","Appropriate education, training, or experience","Seniority of position only","Self-declaration only"],"a":1,"e":"力量は、適切な教育・訓練・経験に基づいて確保する。必要に応じて力量を得るための処置をとり、その証拠を文書化情報として保持する。","eEn":"Competence is established on the basis of appropriate education, training, or experience, with actions taken and evidence retained as documented information."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.2 が、必要な力量を持たせるためにとった処置について求めるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 7.2 require regarding actions taken to acquire necessary competence?","o":["処置を非公開にして評価対象からも外すこと","処置の有効性は三年ごとの外部監査でのみ確認すればよいこと","処置の内容を記録に残さず口頭でのみ伝えること","処置の有効性の証拠として文書化情報を保持すること"],"oEn":["Keeping the actions confidential and excluding them from evaluation as well","Confirming the effectiveness of the actions only at the external audit held every three years","Communicating the content of the actions only verbally, without any written record","Retaining documented information as evidence of competence"],"a":3,"e":"7.2 は、力量を得るための処置をとり、その有効性を評価し、力量の証拠として適切な文書化情報を保持することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.2 requires taking actions to acquire competence, evaluating their effectiveness, and retaining appropriate documented information as evidence."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.3『認識』で、組織の管理下で働く人々が理解すべきに含まれないのは？","qEn":"Under Clause 7.3 (awareness), which is NOT something persons must be aware of?","o":["要求事項に適合しない場合の意味（影響）","AIMSの有効性への自らの貢献","AI方針","競合製品の販売価格"],"oEn":["The implications of not conforming with requirements","Their contribution to the effectiveness of the AIMS","The AI policy","Competitor product pricing"],"a":3,"e":"認識では、AI方針、AIMSへの自らの貢献（性能改善の便益を含む）、不適合の意味を理解させる。競合製品の価格は含まれない。","eEn":"Awareness covers the AI policy, one's contribution (including benefits of improved performance), and implications of nonconformity — not competitor pricing."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.4『コミュニケーション』で組織が決定すべき事項に該当しないのは？","qEn":"Which is NOT among the items Clause 7.4 (communication) requires the organization to determine?","o":["組織内で誰が何をいつ伝達するか","どの手段でいつ伝達するかという媒体の選定","伝達内容を事前に承認する外部監査機関はどこか","誰と、どの部門を通じて伝達するか"],"oEn":["Who communicates what, and when, within the organization","The choice of medium — by what means to communicate","Which external audit body approves the content in advance","With whom, and through which department, to communicate"],"a":2,"e":"7.4 は、AIMSに関する内部・外部のコミュニケーションについて、何を・いつ・誰と・どのように伝達するかを決めることを求める。外部監査機関の承認は要求事項ではない。","eEn":"Clause 7.4 requires determining what, when, with whom, and how to communicate about the AIMS — external audit body approval is not required."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5.3『文書化情報の管理』が扱う典型的な事項に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches typical items addressed by Clause 7.5.3 (control of documented information)?","o":["AI方針を記述する言語の選定に関する事項","配付・アクセス・検索・保管・変更管理・保持・廃棄","トップマネジメントに就任している役員の人数と在任期間の記録","目的に設定された具体的な数値目標の一覧"],"oEn":["Matters concerning the choice of language used to write the AI policy","Distribution, access, retrieval, storage, change control, retention, disposition","Records of how many officers sit in top management and how long each of them has served","A list of the specific numeric targets set for the objectives"],"a":1,"e":"7.5.3 は、文書化情報が必要なときに利用可能で保護されるよう、配付・アクセス・検索・保管・変更の管理・保持・廃棄を管理することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.5.3 addresses distribution, access, retrieval, storage, change control, retention, and disposition so documented information is available and protected."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5.2『作成及び更新』で文書化情報に求められるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 7.5.2 (creating and updating) require for documented information?","o":["組織の使用言語にかかわらず英語での作成を義務づける","媒体を問わず常に紙媒体でのみ保管すること","適切な識別・記述（表題・日付等）、形式・媒体、レビュー及び承認","作成者名や更新履歴を意図的に秘匿すること"],"oEn":["Mandating that it be written in English regardless of the organization's working language","Always keeping records only on paper, regardless of the medium","Appropriate identification/description (title, date, etc.), format/media, and review and approval","Deliberately concealing the author's name and the revision history"],"a":2,"e":"7.5.2 は、文書化情報に適切な識別と記述（表題・日付など）、適切な形式・媒体、及び適切性・妥当性のためのレビューと承認を求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.5.2 requires appropriate identification and description, suitable format and media, and review and approval for suitability and adequacy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5.1『一般』でAIMSに含めるべき文書化情報に該当するのは？","qEn":"Under Clause 7.5.1 (general), which documented information must be included in the AIMS?","o":["規格が要求するものと、有効性のために組織が必要と判断したもの","競合他社から入手した内部資料と価格表だけを、継続的に蓄積して保持すること","トップマネジメントの私的なメモのみに限定して含めること","顧客が個人的に送付したメールだけを収集して保持すること"],"oEn":["That required by the standard and that determined necessary by the organization for effectiveness","Continually accumulating and retaining only the internal materials and price lists obtained from a competitor","Including only top management's personal notes and nothing else","Collecting and retaining only emails that customers sent personally"],"a":0,"e":"7.5.1 は、規格が要求する文書化情報に加え、AIMSの有効性のために組織が必要と判断した文書化情報を含めることを求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.5.1 requires including documented information required by the standard plus that the organization determines necessary for AIMS effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.2 の『リスクの評価（evaluation）』段階で行うのは？","qEn":"What is done in the risk evaluation stage of Clause 6.1.2?","o":["評価の結果を待たずに管理策を先に実装する","分析や基準との比較に先立ち、リスクの候補をひととおり識別するだけの段階","評価とは別の手続きとして監査員を任命する","分析結果をリスク基準と比較し対応の優先順位を決める"],"oEn":["Implementing the controls in advance, without waiting for the evaluation result","Merely identifying the candidate risks one by one, before any analysis or comparison against criteria","Appointing an auditor as a separate procedure unrelated to the evaluation","Comparing analysis results against risk criteria and prioritizing risks for treatment"],"a":3,"e":"リスク評価では、分析したリスクレベルを確立したリスク基準と比較し、対応の優先順位付けを行う。識別・分析はその前段である。","eEn":"Risk evaluation compares analyzed risk levels against established criteria and prioritizes risks for treatment; identification and analysis precede it."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.4 のAIシステム影響評価の結果は、AIMSにおいてどう扱うのが適切か？","qEn":"How should the results of the AI system impact assessment (Clause 6.1.4) be handled in the AIMS?","o":["口頭でのみ共有する","破棄する","結果を文書化情報として保持する","トップマネジメントに見せない"],"oEn":["Share them only verbally","Discard them","Retain the results as documented information","Hide them from top management"],"a":2,"e":"影響評価は定めたプロセスに従って実施し、その結果を文書化情報として保持することが求められる。","eEn":"The impact assessment is carried out per a defined process and its results are retained as documented information."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.2 の力量マネジメントの流れとして最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which best represents the competence management flow in Clause 7.2?","o":["教育や訓練の処置だけを実施し評価も証拠の記録も一切行わない","必要な力量を決定→教育/訓練/経験で確保→処置の有効性を評価→証拠を保持","証拠となる受講記録だけをまず保持しておき、力量の決定と有効性の評価はどちらも省略する","力量の有無は一切無視し役職の高さだけで人選をすべて判断する"],"oEn":["Carry out only education or training actions, with no evaluation and no records kept at all","Determine needed competence → ensure via education/training/experience → evaluate effectiveness → retain evidence","Retaining only the attendance records as evidence first, and skipping both the determination of competence and the evaluation of effectiveness","Ignore entirely whether competence exists and judge every personnel choice solely by seniority of rank"],"a":1,"e":"7.2 は、必要な力量の決定、教育・訓練・経験による確保（不足時は処置）、処置の有効性評価、証拠の文書化という流れを求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.2 flows: determine required competence, ensure it (act if lacking), evaluate action effectiveness, and retain documented evidence."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2 が、AIMS目的を組織内でどう扱うよう求めているか？","qEn":"How does Clause 6.2 require AIMS objectives to be handled within the organization?","o":["目的の内容は経営層のみが保管し他者には示さない","目的は組織の内外を問わず秘密として扱い、更新も共有も一切しない","目的は監査が実施される時だけ限定的に開示する","伝達（communicate）し、必要に応じて更新する"],"oEn":["Only top management retains the objectives and shows them to no one else","Treating the objectives as secret both inside and outside the organization, never updating or sharing them","Disclosing the objectives only in a limited way, and only at the time of an audit","Communicate them and update as appropriate"],"a":3,"e":"AIMS目的は、監視され、伝達され、必要に応じて更新されなければならない。関係者への伝達が明確に求められる。","eEn":"AIMS objectives must be monitored, communicated, and updated as appropriate; communication to relevant parties is explicitly required."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1 全体が、Clause 4.1・4.2 で特定した事項とどう関係するか？","qEn":"How does Clause 6.1 relate to the items identified in Clauses 4.1 and 4.2?","o":["4.1の課題と4.2の要求事項を考慮してリスク及び機会を決定する","4.1・4.2で特定した事項とは完全に無関係である","4.1・4.2は6.1が実施された後に廃止される","6.1のリスク及び機会の決定が4.1の課題と4.2の要求事項をそのまま置き換え、以後は4.1・4.2を参照しなくなる"],"oEn":["It determines risks and opportunities considering the issues (4.1) and requirements (4.2)","It is entirely unrelated to the matters identified in 4.1 and 4.2","Clauses 4.1 and 4.2 are abolished once 6.1 has been carried out","Clause 6.1's determination of risks and opportunities simply replaces the content of 4.1 and 4.2, so those clauses are no longer referred to afterwards"],"a":0,"e":"6.1 は、4.1で特定した内外の課題と、4.2で特定した利害関係者の要求事項を考慮して、取り組むべきリスク及び機会を決定する。","eEn":"Clause 6.1 determines the risks and opportunities to address by considering the issues from 4.1 and the requirements from 4.2."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5.3 で『文書化情報は必要なときに、必要な場所で、利用に適した状態で』とされる理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Why does Clause 7.5.3 require documented information to be available and suitable for use when and where needed?","o":["AIMSの運用時に必要な情報へ確実にアクセスできるようにするため","文書化情報の分量を意図的に増やして体裁だけを整えるため","必要な文書化情報を隠すことで監査そのものを回避するため","文書化情報の保管場所を一箇所に集約し、印刷部数と保管にかかるコストを削減することだけを目的としているため"],"oEn":["To ensure reliable access to needed information during AIMS operation","To deliberately increase the volume of documented information, merely for appearance's sake","To avoid the audit itself by hiding the documented information that is needed","Because the sole aim is to cut printing volume and storage costs by consolidating all documented information into a single storage location"],"a":0,"e":"文書化情報を利用可能かつ利用に適した状態に保つのは、AIMSの運用に必要な情報へ確実にアクセスできるようにするためである。","eEn":"Keeping documented information available and suitable ensures reliable access to information needed to operate the AIMS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.3 の『認識』で、従業員が理解すべき『不適合の意味』とは？","qEn":"In Clause 7.3, what does understanding 'implications of nonconformity' mean for employees?","o":["不適合が生じた場合に科される罰金の正確な金額","不適合が起きた際の競合他社の対応方針の内容","AIMS要求事項に従わない場合に生じうる悪影響や帰結","不適合を最初に発見した監査員個人の氏名を記録すること"],"oEn":["The exact amount of the fine imposed when a nonconformity occurs","The content of a competitor's response policy to a nonconformity there","Adverse effects/consequences that may arise from not meeting AIMS requirements","Recording the individual name of the auditor who first found the nonconformity"],"a":2,"e":"認識では、AIMSの要求事項に適合しないことが引き起こしうる悪影響・帰結を従業員が理解していることが求められる。","eEn":"Awareness requires employees to understand the potential adverse effects of not conforming to AIMS requirements."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.3 の『リスク対応の選択肢』の考え方に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects the concept of 'risk treatment options' in Clause 6.1.3?","o":["リスクには対応せず記録だけを残して終える","どのような状況でもリスクは常に受容するのみとする","回避・低減・移転・受容などから適切な選択肢を選ぶ","選択肢を比較せず必ず外部委託先に対応を任せる"],"oEn":["Concluding by merely keeping a record, without treating the risk at all","Treating every risk as something to simply accept, regardless of the situation","Select appropriate options such as avoid, reduce, transfer, or accept","Always leaving treatment to an outsourced provider without comparing options"],"a":2,"e":"リスク対応では、リスクの回避・低減（管理策）・移転（共有）・受容など適切な選択肢を選び、必要な管理策を決定する。","eEn":"Risk treatment involves selecting appropriate options — avoid, reduce, transfer/share, or accept — and determining the necessary controls."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2 の目的は、どの上位要素と『整合』していなければならないか？","qEn":"With which higher-level element must the objectives in Clause 6.2 be consistent?","o":["毎年変動する競合他社のKPIの実績値","AI方針（AI policy）","外部の供給者と締結した個別の契約書","監査部門が策定する年間の監査計画"],"oEn":["Competitors' KPI figures, which fluctuate every year","The AI policy","An individual contract concluded with an external supplier","The annual audit plan drawn up by the audit department"],"a":1,"e":"AIMS目的はAI方針と整合していなければならない。方針が示す方向性を具体的な目的へ落とし込む。","eEn":"AIMS objectives must be consistent with the AI policy, translating the policy's direction into concrete objectives."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.1 の資源には一般に何が含まれると考えられるか？","qEn":"What is generally understood to be included in the resources of Clause 7.1?","o":["過去に外部審査機関が発行した監査報告書のみが該当する","トップマネジメントに支払われる役員報酬と賞与の明細のみが対象で、要員やデータは含まれない","人的資源・データ・計算資源・ツールなどAIMS運用に必要な資源","競合他社が自社工場に保有する生産設備の内訳が該当する"],"oEn":["Only audit reports previously issued by an external certification body fall under this","Only the pay slips for executive salaries and bonuses paid to top management are covered, and personnel or data are not included","Human resources, data, computing resources, tools needed to operate the AIMS","The breakdown of production equipment a competitor owns at its own factory falls under this"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSの資源には、人・データ・計算資源・ツールなど、AIシステムのライフサイクルとAIMS運用に必要な各種資源が含まれうる。","eEn":"AIMS resources may include people, data, computing resources, and tools needed for the AI lifecycle and AIMS operation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.2 の『リスク所有者（risk owners）』の役割に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the role of 'risk owners' in Clause 6.1.2/6.1.3?","o":["方針を他言語へ翻訳する専門担当者を意味する","監査を実施する独立した外部機関のことを指す","リスクの管理と対応に責任・権限を持ち、残留リスクを承認する者","文書を印刷し配付するだけの事務担当者を指す"],"oEn":["It means a specialist who translates the policy into other languages","It denotes the independent external body that conducts the audit","Those with accountability and authority to manage and treat the risk, who approve residual risk","It denotes merely a clerical staff member who prints and distributes documents"],"a":2,"e":"リスク所有者は、当該リスクの管理・対応に対する責任と権限を持つ者であり、対応計画や残留リスクの承認に関与する。","eEn":"Risk owners have accountability and authority to manage a risk and are involved in approving treatment plans and residual risks."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.3 の『計画的な方法』で変更を行う際に考慮するとよいのは？","qEn":"When making changes 'in a planned manner' per Clause 6.3, what is appropriate to consider?","o":["今回の変更とは無関係な競合他社の株価の日々の終値と出来高の推移だけを指標とすること","変更の計画とは別枠で決める監査員の休暇予定","変更の内容に関係のない印刷用紙の色の選定","変更の目的とその潜在的な影響、資源、責任・権限の配分"],"oEn":["Considering, as the sole indicator, the day-to-day closing prices and trading volumes of a competitor's stock, which are unrelated to this change","The auditor's vacation schedule, decided separately from the change plan","Choosing the color of printing paper, unrelated to the content of the change","The purpose of changes and their potential consequences, resources, and allocation of responsibilities"],"a":3,"e":"変更を計画的に行うには、変更の目的と潜在的影響、必要な資源、責任及び権限の配分などを考慮する。","eEn":"Planned changes should consider the purpose and potential consequences of the change, required resources, and allocation of responsibilities and authorities."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.4 の外部コミュニケーションの例として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate example of external communication under Clause 7.4?","o":["監査員が個人的な連絡を利害関係者と交わすこと","利害関係者へのAIシステムに関する情報提供","開発チーム内で交わされる業務外の雑談の内容","社内の内部監査チームへ監査計画の原案を回付すること"],"oEn":["An auditor exchanging private, personal messages with an interested party","Providing information about the AI system to interested parties","The content of off-topic chatter exchanged within the development team","Circulating the draft audit plan to the internal audit team inside the company"],"a":1,"e":"外部コミュニケーションには、規制当局・顧客・一般など利害関係者へのAIシステムに関する適切な情報提供が含まれうる。","eEn":"External communication may include appropriately providing information about the AI system to regulators, customers, and other interested parties."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1 で『機会（opportunities）』を扱う意義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best captures the significance of addressing 'opportunities' in Clause 6.1?","o":["AIMSの成果を高めうる好ましい要素も特定し活かすため","好ましい要素は無視し脅威のみを列挙するため","機会を扱うことで既存のリスクを無視するため","機会を検討したことを理由に、その期の内部監査そのものを次回まで省略してよいとするため"],"oEn":["To identify and pursue favorable factors that can enhance AIMS outcomes","To ignore favorable factors and list only threats","To make handling opportunities a pretext for ignoring existing risks","So that, on the grounds that opportunities were considered, the internal audit itself may be skipped until the next cycle"],"a":0,"e":"6.1 はリスクだけでなく機会も扱い、AIMSの成果向上や望ましい影響の拡大につながる好ましい要素を特定・活用することを意図する。","eEn":"Clause 6.1 addresses opportunities as well as risks, aiming to identify and leverage favorable factors that enhance AIMS outcomes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5 で『文書化情報』という用語が『文書』と『記録』を統合して使われる理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Why does Clause 7.5 use the single term 'documented information' for both documents and records?","o":["媒体を紙媒体だけに限定して指す狭い用語だから","規格を各国語へ翻訳する手間と用語集の維持を不要にすることだけをねらった表現だから","記録という概念そのものを廃止する目的があるから","形式や媒体を問わず管理すべき情報を一体的に扱うため"],"oEn":["Because the term is a narrow one referring only to paper media","Because the wording was aimed solely at removing the effort of translating the standard into each language and of maintaining a glossary","Because the purpose is to abolish the concept of records altogether","To treat information to be controlled as one concept regardless of form/media"],"a":3,"e":"『文書化情報』は、手順書などの文書と実施証拠である記録を、媒体や形式を問わず管理対象として一体的に扱う用語である。","eEn":"'Documented information' unifies documents (e.g., procedures) and records (evidence) as one controlled concept, regardless of media or form."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.2 と 7.3 の主な違いとして最も適切なのは？","qEn":"What best distinguishes Clause 7.2 from Clause 7.3?","o":["7.2はAI方針の策定を扱い、7.3は資源の確保のみを扱う","7.2と7.3は表現が異なるだけで要求事項は完全に同一であり、どちらか一方を満たせば他方も自動的に満たされる","7.2は力量（能力の確保）、7.3は認識（方針・貢献・不適合の意味の理解）","7.2は内部監査の実施を扱い、7.3は継続的改善の実施を扱う"],"oEn":["7.2 covers drafting the AI policy, and 7.3 covers only securing resources","7.2 and 7.3 differ only in wording; their requirements are entirely identical, so satisfying either one automatically satisfies the other as well","7.2 is competence (ensuring capability); 7.3 is awareness (understanding policy, contribution, nonconformity implications)","7.2 covers conducting internal audits, and 7.3 covers carrying out continual improvement"],"a":2,"e":"7.2は業務遂行に必要な力量を確保することを、7.3は方針・自らの貢献・不適合の意味を理解している状態（認識）を求める。","eEn":"Clause 7.2 ensures the competence to perform work; Clause 7.3 ensures awareness of the policy, one's contribution, and implications of nonconformity."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.4 の影響評価を『いつ』行うのが適切と考えられるか？","qEn":"When is it appropriate to perform the impact assessment of Clause 6.1.4?","o":["組織が定めたプロセスに従い、適切な時点で（例：AIシステムの重要な変更時）","AIシステムの影響評価そのものを決して実施しない方針を貫く","外部審査機関の監査が実際に行われる当日に限り実施し、AIシステムに重要な変更があっても改めては実施しない","組織を設立した時点でのみ一度だけ実施しその後は二度と行わない"],"oEn":["Per the organization's defined process, at appropriate times (e.g., on significant changes to the AI system)","Adhering to a policy of never performing the AI system's impact assessment at all","Performed only on the day an external certification body's audit actually takes place, and never repeated even when the AI system undergoes a significant change","Performed only once, at the moment the organization was founded, and never repeated after that"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価は組織が定めたプロセスに従って実施し、AIシステムやその状況に重要な変化がある場合など適切な時点で見直す。","eEn":"The impact assessment follows the organization's defined process and is performed/revisited at appropriate times, such as on significant changes."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.2 で目的が『測定可能（if practicable）』であることが望ましい理由は？","qEn":"Why is it desirable for objectives in Clause 6.2 to be measurable (if practicable)?","o":["目的を測定可能にしたことを根拠として、内部監査の対象からその目的を外せるようにするため","進捗評価を伴わず文書の分量だけを増やすため","測定可能にすることで方針の内容を隠すため","達成度を評価・監視し進捗を判断できるようにするため"],"oEn":["So that, on the grounds that objectives were made measurable, they can be excluded from the scope of internal audit","To merely increase the volume of documentation, without any progress evaluation","To hide the content of the policy by making it measurable","To evaluate and monitor achievement and judge progress"],"a":3,"e":"測定可能な目的は、達成度の監視・評価を可能にし、目的が実際に達成されているかを客観的に判断できるようにする。","eEn":"Measurable objectives enable monitoring and evaluation of achievement, allowing objective judgment of whether they are being met."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7.5.3 で外部で作成された（外部由来の）文書化情報について求められるのは？","qEn":"For documented information of external origin, what does Clause 7.5.3 require?","o":["必要性を判断せずすべて機械的に破棄する","内部文書と外部文書をあえて区別せずに扱う","必要と判断したものを識別し適切に管理する","出所を確認せず一律にすべて無視する"],"oEn":["Discarding it all mechanically without judging whether it is needed","Handling it without deliberately distinguishing it from internal documents","Identify and appropriately control that determined necessary","Ignoring it entirely across the board without checking its origin"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSの計画・運用に必要と組織が判断した外部由来の文書化情報は、適切に識別し管理することが求められる。","eEn":"Documented information of external origin determined necessary for the AIMS must be identified and appropriately controlled."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 6.1.1 で決定したリスク及び機会への取組みは、どこに統合・実施することが求められるか？","qEn":"Where must the actions to address risks and opportunities (Clause 6.1.1) be integrated and implemented?","o":["AIMSのプロセスへ統合して実施し、取組みの有効性を評価する","AIMSとは別枠の競合他社の業務プロセスへ統合する","外部の監査機関にのみ委ね組織内では実施しない","トップマネジメント個人の私的な計画にのみ組み込む"],"oEn":["Into the AIMS processes — implemented, with the effectiveness of the actions evaluated","Integrated into a competitor's business processes, separate from the AIMS","Entrusted solely to an external audit body and never carried out in the organization","Incorporated only into top management's own private plan"],"a":0,"e":"6.1.1 は、リスク・機会への取組みをAIMSのプロセスに統合して実施し、それらの取組みの有効性を評価することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 6.1.1 requires integrating the actions into AIMS processes, implementing them, and evaluating their effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 7 全体（支援）が Clause 8（運用）に対して果たす役割に最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best describes the role of Clause 7 (support) toward Clause 8 (operation)?","o":["資源・力量・認識・コミュニケーション・文書化情報という運用の土台を提供する","Clause8の運用を明確な理由なく一律に禁止し、資源や力量が整うまで運用開始を無期限に停止させる役割","Clause8の運用の担当者をそのまま完全に代替してしまう役割","Clause8の運用の妥当性のみを独立して監査し続ける役割"],"oEn":["Providing the foundation for operation — resources, competence, awareness, communication, documented information","It plays the role of prohibiting Clause 8 operation uniformly without any clear reason, suspending the start of operation indefinitely until resources and competence are in place","It plays the role of entirely replacing the personnel who carry out Clause 8 operation","It plays the role of continually and independently auditing only the validity of Clause 8 operation"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7は、資源・力量・認識・コミュニケーション・文書化情報を整えることで、Clause 8の運用を支える基盤を提供する。","eEn":"Clause 7 provides the foundation — resources, competence, awareness, communication, documented information — that supports the operation in Clause 8."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1『運用の計画及び管理』でAIMSがまず行うべきことに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Under Clause 8.1 (Operational planning and control), what should the AIMS do first?","o":["運用の状況に関する記録を意図的に一切残さない","すべてのリスクがゼロになるまで運用を停止する","プロセスの基準を確立し、その基準に従ってプロセスを管理する","運用手順とプロセスの基準は経営層だけが把握し、実際に運用する現場の要員には共有しないでおく"],"oEn":["Deliberately keeping no record whatsoever concerning the state of operations","Halt operations until all risks are reduced to zero","Establish criteria for the processes and control the processes in accordance with those criteria","Having only top management grasp the operating procedures and process criteria, keeping them from the staff who actually carry out the operation"],"a":2,"e":"8.1はプロセスの基準を確立し、その基準に従ってプロセスを管理することを求める。","eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires establishing process criteria and controlling processes in accordance with them."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1における外部委託（outsourced）プロセスの扱いとして正しいのは？","qEn":"Regarding outsourced processes under Clause 8.1, which is correct?","o":["外部委託は一律に禁止される","外部委託したプロセスは契約を結んだ時点で自動的にAIMSの適用範囲から除外される","組織に関連する外部委託プロセスが管理されていることを確実にする","外部委託先には一切要求事項を伝えない"],"oEn":["Outsourcing is prohibited across the board","Outsourced processes are automatically excluded from the scope of the AIMS at the moment the contract is signed","Ensure that outsourced processes relevant to the organization are controlled","Communicate no requirements to the outsourced provider"],"a":2,"e":"8.1 は、組織に関連する外部委託プロセスが管理されていることを確実にするよう求める。外部委託を一律に禁止するのではなく、契約を結んだだけで適用範囲から自動的に除外されることもなく、委託先に要求事項を伝えないのも不適切。","eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires the organization to ensure that outsourced processes relevant to it are controlled. Outsourcing is not banned outright, a contract does not automatically remove a process from the scope, and withholding requirements from the supplier is improper."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1が求める変更の管理として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"What best describes the control of changes required by Clause 8.1?","o":["計画した変更を管理し、意図しない変更の結果をレビューして必要な処置をとる","変更が実際に生じてしまってから初めて事後的に計画を立て、意図しない変更の結果はレビューしない","計画されていたかどうかを問わずいかなる変更も一律に許可しない","変更を実施した後もその影響については一切評価を行わない"],"oEn":["Control planned changes and review the consequences of unintended changes, taking action as needed","Only beginning to draw up a plan in hindsight after the change has already occurred, and never reviewing the consequences of unintended changes","Permitting no change at all, regardless of whether it had been planned","Never carrying out any assessment of a change's impact, even after it has been made"],"a":0,"e":"8.1 は、計画した変更を管理し、意図しない変更の結果をレビューして必要な処置をとることを求める。事後に初めて計画を立てて結果をレビューしない、いかなる変更も一律に許可しない、実施後の影響を評価しない、といった扱いは求められない。","eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires controlling planned changes and reviewing the consequences of unintended changes, taking action where needed. Planning only after changes occur, banning every change outright, or never evaluating their effects is not what it asks for."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1で文書化情報を保持する主な目的は？","qEn":"What is the main purpose of retaining documented information under Clause 8.1?","o":["運用に関するすべての会話を漏れなく録音するため","外部審査の直前にだけ運用の記録をまとめて作成し、審査が終われば速やかに破棄するため","文書化情報はAIMSにおいて本来まったく不要である","プロセスが計画どおりに実施されたという確信を得るため"],"oEn":["To record every single conversation related to operations without exception","To compile operational records in bulk only just before an external audit and to discard them promptly once the audit is over","Documented information is, by nature, entirely unnecessary in the AIMS","To have confidence that the processes have been carried out as planned"],"a":3,"e":"文書化情報を保持する目的は、プロセスが計画どおりに実施されたという確信を得ること。運用中の会話をすべて録音することや、審査直前にだけ記録をまとめて審査後に破棄すること、文書化情報を不要とみなすことは目的に合わない。","eEn":"Documented information is retained to give confidence that processes were carried out as planned. Recording every conversation, compiling records only before an audit and discarding them afterwards, or treating documentation as unnecessary does not serve that purpose."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.2『AIリスクアセスメント』の実施時期として正しいのは？","qEn":"When should the AI risk assessment under Clause 8.2 be performed?","o":["重大インシデントが実際に発生した後にのみ実施し、重大な変更が提案された段階では実施しない","初回の認証を取得した時点でのみ一度だけ実施すればそれで足りる","あらかじめ定めた間隔で、また重大な変更が提案・発生したときに実施する","AIリスクアセスメントは外部委託先のみが独占的に実施するもの"],"oEn":["It is performed only after a major incident has actually occurred, and never at the stage where a significant change is merely proposed","It is sufficient to perform it just once, only at the time initial certification is obtained","At planned intervals, and when significant changes are proposed or occur","The AI risk assessment is something performed exclusively by an outsourced provider alone"],"a":2,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは、あらかじめ定めた間隔で実施し、重大な変更が提案または発生したときにも実施する。インシデント後にのみ行う、認証取得時に一度だけ行う、外部委託先だけが独占して行う、といった運用は不適切。","eEn":"AI risk assessments are carried out at planned intervals and also when significant changes are proposed or occur. Doing them only after an incident, only once at certification, or leaving them solely to an outsourced party is not appropriate."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.3『AIリスク対応』でAIMSが行うのは？","qEn":"What does the AIMS do under Clause 8.3 (AI risk treatment)?","o":["リスク対応は文書化してはならない","策定したAIリスク対応計画を実施する","すべてのリスクを第三者に移転する","リスクはすべて受容し対応しない"],"oEn":["Risk treatment must not be documented","Implement the AI risk treatment plan that was drawn up","Transfer all risks to a third party","Accept all risks and take no treatment"],"a":1,"e":"8.3 は、策定したAIリスク対応計画を実施することを求める。リスク対応を文書化してはならない、すべてのリスクを第三者に移転する、すべて受容して何も対応しない、といった扱いは要求と合わない。","eEn":"Clause 8.3 requires implementing the AI risk treatment plan that was established. Forbidding documentation of risk treatment, transferring every risk to a third party, or accepting all risks and doing nothing does not match the requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.4『AIシステム影響評価』でAIMSが適用するプロセスの焦点は？","qEn":"What is the focus of the process applied under Clause 8.4 (AI system impact assessment)?","o":["財務的な影響のみに限定して評価を行うプロセスである","個人及び社会に対するAIシステムの潜在的影響を評価する","AIシステム影響評価という手続き自体が不要である","競合他社の事業と市場シェアへの影響のみを重点的に評価し、個人や社会への影響は対象外とする"],"oEn":["It is a process whose assessment is limited solely to financial impacts","Assess the potential impacts of the AI system on individuals and society","The procedure of AI system impact assessment itself is unnecessary","A process that focuses solely on impacts to a competitor's business and market share, leaving impacts on individuals and society out of scope"],"a":1,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、個人および社会に対するAIシステムの潜在的な影響を評価するプロセス。財務的な影響や、競合他社の市場シェアへの影響だけに限定するものではなく、手続き自体が不要でもない。","eEn":"The AI system impact assessment evaluates the potential consequences of an AI system for individuals and society. It is not limited to financial impact or effects on competitors' market share, and the procedure itself is not unnecessary."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.1『監視・測定・分析・評価』で組織が決定すべき事項に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best captures what an organization must determine under Clause 9.1?","o":["監視の対象項目が何かは経営層のみが秘密として保持しておく","監視も測定も年に一度だけ実施すれば十分であり、方法や実施者を定めておく必要はまったくない","測定に用いる方法や基準についてはどれを選んでも問わない","何を、どの方法で、いつ監視・測定し、いつ誰が結果を分析・評価するか"],"oEn":["Only top management keeps what the monitoring targets are as a secret","Both monitoring and measurement need only be carried out once a year, and there is no need at all to determine the methods or who performs them","Whichever method or criterion is chosen for measurement does not matter at all","What to monitor/measure, by what methods, when, and when and by whom results are analyzed and evaluated"],"a":3,"e":"9.1 は、何を、どの方法で、いつ監視・測定するか、そしていつ誰が結果を分析・評価するかを決めることを求める。年に一度で足りるとして方法や実施者を定めないこと、測定方法を問わないこと、監視項目を秘密にすることは合わない。","eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires determining what to monitor and measure, by which methods and when, and when and by whom results are analyzed and evaluated. Doing it once a year with no methods or owners, or keeping the items secret, does not fit."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.1で監視・測定の結果について求められるのは？","qEn":"What is required regarding the results of monitoring and measurement under Clause 9.1?","o":["結果の証拠として適切な文書化情報を保持する","結果の証拠となる文書化情報は外部委託先だけが保管し、組織側は保持しない","結果は記録を残さず口頭でのみ共有する","結果は確認後ただちにすべて破棄する"],"oEn":["Retain appropriate documented information as evidence of the results","The documented information evidencing the results is kept only by the outsourced provider, and the organization itself retains none","Results are shared only verbally, with no record kept","Results are all discarded immediately after being checked"],"a":0,"e":"9.1 は、監視・測定の結果の証拠として、適切な文書化情報を保持することを求める。結果を口頭でのみ共有する、確認後にすべて破棄する、外部委託先だけが保管して組織側は保持しない、といった扱いは不適切。","eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires retaining appropriate documented information as evidence of monitoring and measurement results. Sharing results only verbally, discarding them after review, or letting only an outsourced party keep them is not appropriate."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.1の監視・測定・分析・評価の目的として正しいのは？","qEn":"What is the purpose of monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation under Clause 9.1?","o":["短期的な売上のみを最大化しようとするため","AIMSのパフォーマンス及び有効性を評価するため","規律違反をした従業員を特定して懲戒するため","実施済みの広告施策とキャンペーンの費用対効果だけを測定し評価するため"],"oEn":["To try to maximize short-term sales alone","To evaluate the performance and effectiveness of the AIMS","To identify and discipline employees who have violated conduct rules","To measure and evaluate only the cost-effectiveness of advertising campaigns that have already been run"],"a":1,"e":"監視・測定・分析・評価の目的は、AIMSのパフォーマンスと有効性を評価すること。短期的な売上の最大化や、従業員の懲戒、広告施策の費用対効果の測定だけを目的とするものではない。","eEn":"Monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation exist to assess the performance and effectiveness of the AIMS. They are not meant to maximize short-term sales, to discipline employees, or merely to measure the cost-effectiveness of ad campaigns."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2『内部監査』が判定する適合の基準に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Against what criteria does the internal audit under Clause 9.2 judge conformity?","o":["AIMSが組織自身の要求事項と本規格の要求事項の両方に適合しているか","本規格の要求事項のみを確認し組織側が定めたものは見ない","財務諸表に記載された数値の正確性のみを厳密に確認する","組織自身が定めた社内手順への適合のみを確認し、本規格の要求事項への適合は一切確認しない"],"oEn":["Whether the AIMS conforms to both the organization's own requirements and the standard's requirements","Checking only the standard's requirements while disregarding those the organization itself set","Rigorously checking only the numerical accuracy of the figures recorded in financial statements","Checking only conformity to the organization's own internal procedures, without ever checking conformity to the requirements of this standard"],"a":0,"e":"内部監査は、AIMSが組織自身の要求事項と本規格の要求事項の両方に適合しているかを判定する。規格だけを見て組織側の定めを見ない、あるいは社内手順だけを見て規格を確認しない、というのは片方に偏っていて不適切。財務諸表の数値の確認が目的でもない。","eEn":"An internal audit determines whether the AIMS conforms to both the organization's own requirements and the requirements of the standard. Checking only the standard, or only internal procedures, is one-sided, and verifying financial statement figures is not its purpose."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2で監査員の選定・監査実施に関して求められるのは？","qEn":"What does Clause 9.2 require regarding auditor selection and conduct of audits?","o":["監査員に独立性や客観性を求める必要はまったくないとされる","監査は常にトップマネジメントのメンバーのみが実施する","監査員は自らが日頃担当している業務を優先して監査してよく、独立性や公平性は求められない","監査プロセスの客観性・公平性を確保し、監査員は自らの業務を監査しない"],"oEn":["It is held that there is no need whatsoever to require independence or objectivity of auditors","Audits are always conducted only by members of top management","Auditors may give priority to auditing the very work they themselves handle day to day, and no independence or impartiality is required of them","Ensure objectivity and impartiality of the audit process; auditors do not audit their own work"],"a":3,"e":"内部監査は、プロセスの客観性と公平性を確保し、監査員が自らの業務を監査しないことを求める。独立性や公平性が不要とすることや、自分の担当業務を優先して監査することは認められず、監査をトップのメンバーのみが行う必要もない。","eEn":"Internal audits must ensure objectivity and impartiality, and auditors must not audit their own work. Independence is not optional, auditing one's own regular duties is not allowed, and audits are not always conducted solely by top management."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2の監査プログラムについて正しいのは？","qEn":"Which is correct regarding the audit programme under Clause 9.2?","o":["内部監査は外部の審査機関のみが常に代わりに実施する","内部監査は最初に一度実施すればそれ以後は一切不要である","監査プログラムの頻度・方法・責任はあえて文書化せず、口頭の申し合わせだけで運用する","あらかじめ定めた間隔で監査プログラムを計画・確立・実施・維持する"],"oEn":["Internal audit is always conducted on the organization's behalf only by an external certification body","Once internal audit has been performed the first time, no further audit is ever needed","The audit programme's frequency, methods and responsibilities are deliberately left undocumented and are run on verbal understandings alone","Plan, establish, implement and maintain an audit programme at planned intervals"],"a":3,"e":"組織は、あらかじめ定めた間隔で監査プログラムを計画・確立・実施・維持する。最初に一度だけ実施して以後は不要とすることや、外部の審査機関が常に代行すること、頻度や責任を文書化せず口頭の申し合わせだけにすることは合わない。","eEn":"The organization plans, establishes, implements and maintains an audit programme at planned intervals. Auditing once and never again, always leaving it to an external certification body, or relying on verbal agreements without documentation does not fit."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2で内部監査の結果はどこへ報告するか？","qEn":"To whom are internal audit results reported under Clause 9.2?","o":["監査結果は次回の内部監査が終わるまで管理層には開示しない","監査結果を関連する管理層に報告する","監査結果は公開してはならない","監査結果は監査員のみが保持する"],"oEn":["Audit results are withheld from management until the next internal audit has been completed","Report audit results to relevant management","Audit results must never be disclosed","Only the auditors keep the results"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 9.2では、内部監査の結果を関連する管理層に報告する。次回の内部監査が終わるまで管理層に開示しないことや、公開してはならないこと、監査員のみが保持することは、要求に反する。","eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires internal audit results to be reported to relevant management. Not disclosing them to management until the next internal audit is finished, forbidding disclosure, or having only the auditor keep them contradicts the requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3『マネジメントレビュー』のインプットに含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is an input to the management review under Clause 9.3?","o":["インプットは組織全体の売上高の実績のみに限られる","インプットとして何を扱うかは経営層が独断で決定する","前回までのマネジメントレビューの結果とった処置の状況","前回までのレビュー内容はいっさい考慮に入れずに進める"],"oEn":["The inputs are limited solely to the organization's overall revenue figures","What is treated as input is decided unilaterally by top management","The status of actions from previous management reviews","The proceedings advance without taking the content of prior reviews into account at all"],"a":2,"e":"前回までのマネジメントレビューでとった処置の状況は、インプットの一つ。インプットを売上高の実績だけに限ることや、経営層の独断で決めること、前回までの内容を考慮せずに進めることは、要求と合わない。","eEn":"The status of actions from previous management reviews is one of the inputs. Limiting inputs to sales figures, letting management decide them arbitrarily, or proceeding without considering earlier reviews does not match the requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューの実施頻度として正しいのは？","qEn":"How often should the management review under Clause 9.3 be conducted?","o":["重大な問題が実際に起きたときにだけ実施する","あらかじめ定めた間隔で実施する","実施頻度は定めない","認証取得時のみ実施する"],"oEn":["Only when a serious problem has actually arisen","At planned intervals","Frequency is not defined","Only at certification"],"a":1,"e":"マネジメントレビューは、あらかじめ定めた間隔で実施する。重大な問題が起きたときだけ、認証取得時のみ、といった実施では間隔を定めたことにならず、頻度を定めないことも要求に反する。","eEn":"Management reviews are conducted at planned intervals. Holding them only when a serious problem occurs, or only at certification, is not a planned interval, and leaving the frequency undefined also conflicts with the requirement."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューのアウトプットに含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is an output of the management review under Clause 9.3?","o":["アウトプットは従業員の評価点である","マネジメントレビューにはアウトプットが存在せず、議事の記録を残す必要もない","アウトプットは翌年の監査計画のみに限られる","改善の機会及びAIMSの変更の必要性に関する決定"],"oEn":["The output is employee performance scores","The management review has no outputs at all, and there is no need to keep any record of what was discussed","The outputs are limited solely to next year's audit plan","Decisions related to opportunities for improvement and the need for changes to the AIMS"],"a":3,"e":"マネジメントレビューのアウトプットには、継続的改善の機会およびAIMSの変更の必要性に関する決定が含まれる。従業員の評価点がアウトプットになるわけではなく、アウトプットが存在せず議事の記録も不要とすることも誤り。","eEn":"The outputs of a management review include decisions on opportunities for continual improvement and any need for changes to the AIMS. Employee evaluation scores are not outputs, and it is wrong to say there are no outputs or records."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.1『継続的改善』の対象として正しいのは？","qEn":"What is the object of continual improvement under Clause 10.1?","o":["AIMSでは認証を取得した後の継続的な改善は一切求められていない","継続的改善の実施そのものは認証機関が代行する","コストの削減のみを唯一かつ最終的な目的とする","AIMSの適切性、妥当性及び有効性を継続的に改善する"],"oEn":["Continual improvement is not required at all within the AIMS once certification has been obtained","Carrying out continual improvement itself is delegated to the certification body","Cost reduction alone is treated as the sole and final objective","Continually improve the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS"],"a":3,"e":"組織はAIMSの適切性、妥当性、有効性を継続的に改善する。認証取得後は改善が一切求められないという見方や、コスト削減だけを最終目的とする見方は誤りで、改善を認証機関が代行することもない。","eEn":"The organization continually improves the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS. It is wrong that no improvement is required after certification, that cost reduction is the sole goal, or that a certification body does the improving."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2で不適合が発生したとき最初にとるべき対応は？","qEn":"When a nonconformity occurs, what is the first response under Clause 10.2?","o":["不適合への対応は次回の監査まで放置する","不適合に対して処置をとり、その結果に対処する","不適合は経営層へ報告するだけで、処置も結果への対処も行わない","発生した不適合はそのまま何もせず無視する"],"oEn":["Handling the nonconformity is left untouched until the next audit","React to the nonconformity and deal with its consequences","The nonconformity is merely reported to top management, with neither action taken nor consequences dealt with","The nonconformity that occurred is simply ignored as is, with no action taken"],"a":1,"e":"不適合が発生したら、まず不適合に処置をとり、生じた結果に対処する。次回の監査まで放置すること、経営層へ報告するだけで処置をとらないこと、無視することは、対応として不適切。","eEn":"When a nonconformity occurs, the organization first takes action to control and correct it and deals with the consequences. Leaving it until the next audit, merely reporting it to management without acting, or ignoring it is not an adequate response."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2における是正処置（corrective action）の目的は？","qEn":"What is the purpose of corrective action under Clause 10.2?","o":["不適合の症状を一時的に隠す","責任者を処罰する","不適合の原因を除去し、再発を防止する","不適合の内容を記録として残すだけで原因は調べない"],"oEn":["Temporarily hide the symptoms","Punish the responsible person","Eliminate the cause of the nonconformity and prevent recurrence","Merely to keep a record of the nonconformity without investigating its cause"],"a":2,"e":"是正処置の目的は、不適合の原因を除去し、再発を防止すること。症状を一時的に隠すことや、責任者を処罰すること、内容を記録するだけで原因を調べないことは、是正処置ではない。","eEn":"The purpose of corrective action is to eliminate the cause of a nonconformity and prevent recurrence. Temporarily hiding symptoms, punishing the person responsible, or merely recording it without investigating the cause is not corrective action."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『修正（correction）』と『是正処置（corrective action）』の違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best distinguishes correction from corrective action?","o":["修正は検出された不適合そのものへの処置、是正処置は原因を除去する処置である","修正と是正処置は表現の違いにすぎず完全に同義な用語である","修正も是正処置もどちらも予防処置のみを意味する言葉である","修正は不適合の原因を除去する処置を、是正処置は現れた症状のみへの一時的な対応を意味する"],"oEn":["Correction addresses the detected nonconformity itself; corrective action eliminates its cause","Correction and corrective action differ only in wording and are entirely synonymous terms","Both correction and corrective action are words that mean only preventive action","Correction is the action that eliminates the cause of the nonconformity, while corrective action is a temporary response to the symptom alone"],"a":0,"e":"修正は検出された不適合そのものへの処置で、是正処置はその原因を除去する処置。逆に説明する選択肢は取り違えで、両者を完全な同義とみなすことも、どちらも予防処置のみを指すとするのも誤り。","eEn":"Correction deals with the detected nonconformity itself, whereas corrective action removes its cause. Reversing the two is a mix-up, and it is wrong to treat them as fully synonymous or to say both mean only preventive action."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2で是正処置を実施した後に求められるのは？","qEn":"What is required after implementing corrective action under Clause 10.2?","o":["是正処置後は何もしない","是正処置の有効性は外部委託先だけが判断する","有効性の評価は禁止されている","とった是正処置の有効性をレビューする"],"oEn":["Do nothing after corrective action","The effectiveness of the corrective action is judged only by the outsourced provider","Evaluating effectiveness is prohibited","Review the effectiveness of the corrective action taken"],"a":3,"e":"是正処置をとったら、その有効性をレビューする必要がある。何もしなくてよい、外部委託先だけが判断する、有効性の評価が禁止されている、といった扱いは、再発防止の確認ができず不適切。","eEn":"After taking corrective action, the organization must review its effectiveness. Doing nothing afterwards, leaving the judgment solely to an outsourced party, or prohibiting the evaluation would leave no way to confirm recurrence is prevented."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2における是正処置の大きさについて正しいのは？","qEn":"Which is correct about the extent of corrective action under Clause 10.2?","o":["是正処置は常に最大限の対応をとる","是正処置は、遭遇した不適合の影響に応じたものとする","是正処置は影響が小さければ常に不要である","是正処置の内容は不適合の影響の大きさと無関係に、常に同じ手順で一律に実施する"],"oEn":["Corrective action is always the maximum possible response","Corrective action is appropriate to the effects of the nonconformities encountered","Corrective action is never needed for small impacts","Corrective action is always carried out by the same uniform procedure, regardless of the magnitude of the nonconformity's effects"],"a":1,"e":"是正処置は、遭遇した不適合の影響に応じたものとする。常に最大限の対応をとるわけでも、影響が小さければ常に不要とするわけでもなく、影響の大きさと無関係に一律の手順で行うわけでもない。","eEn":"Corrective actions must be appropriate to the effects of the nonconformities encountered. They are not always maximal, not always unnecessary for small effects, and not carried out by one uniform procedure regardless of the size of the effect."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2で保持すべき文書化情報に含まれるのは？","qEn":"What documented information must be retained under Clause 10.2?","o":["不適合の性質・とった処置、及び是正処置の結果","発生した不適合の性質やとった処置についての記録はいっさい残さない","記録は内部監査員だけが独占的に保持する","記録は書面化せず口頭のみで十分である"],"oEn":["The nature of the nonconformities, actions taken, and the results of corrective actions","No record whatsoever is kept of the nature of the nonconformities that occurred or of the actions taken in response","Records are kept exclusively by internal auditors alone","Records need not be put in writing; verbal notice alone is sufficient"],"a":0,"e":"10.2 では、不適合の性質ととった処置、および是正処置の結果を文書化情報として保持する。記録を残さない、内部監査員だけが独占的に保持する、書面化せず口頭のみで足りるとする扱いは、要求と合わない。","eEn":"Clause 10.2 requires keeping documented information on the nature of nonconformities, the actions taken, and the results of corrective action. Keeping no record, letting only internal auditors hold it, or relying on verbal communication alone does not meet it."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"要求事項における助動詞『shall』が示すのは？","qEn":"In requirements, what does the modal verb 'shall' indicate?","o":["順守するかどうかが任意である推奨事項","何かを行うことについての許可（してもよい）","何かを実現できる可能性や能力を示す語","適合のために順守しなければならない要求事項（義務）"],"oEn":["A recommendation for which whether to comply is optional","Permission regarding doing something (may)","A word denoting possibility or capability of achieving something","A requirement that must be complied with for conformity (obligation)"],"a":3,"e":"『shall』は、適合のために満たさなければならない要求事項、つまり義務を示す。順守が任意の推奨事項は『should』、許可は『may』、可能性や能力は『can』が示すもので、『shall』とは意味が異なる。","eEn":"The word 'shall' indicates a requirement that must be met to conform, in other words an obligation. Optional recommendations are expressed by 'should', permission by 'may', and possibility or capability by 'can', all of which differ from 'shall'."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"規格文で『should』が示すのは？","qEn":"In the standard, what does 'should' indicate?","o":["何かを行うことへの明確な禁止を示す語","必ず順守しなければならない絶対的な義務","推奨事項（望ましいが順守は必須ではない）","本規格の適用範囲そのものの外を示す語"],"oEn":["A word indicating a clear prohibition against doing something","An absolute obligation that must without fail be complied with","A recommendation (desirable, but compliance is not strictly mandatory)","A word indicating something outside the standard's scope itself"],"a":2,"e":"『should』は推奨事項を示し、望ましいが順守は必須ではない。必ず順守しなければならない絶対的な義務は『shall』が示し、明確な禁止や適用範囲の外を示す語ではない。","eEn":"'Should' indicates a recommendation: desirable, but compliance is not mandatory. An absolute obligation is what 'shall' expresses, and 'should' is not a word for a clear prohibition or for matters outside the scope."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『適合（conformity）』の意味に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches the meaning of 'conformity'?","o":["要求事項を満たしていること","要求事項で定められた水準を上回ること","監査に合格すること","認証を取得すること"],"oEn":["Fulfilment of a requirement","Exceeding the level set by a requirement","Passing an audit","Obtaining certification"],"a":0,"e":"適合とは、要求事項を満たしていること。水準を上回ることまで含むわけではなく、監査に合格することや認証を取得することは適合の結果であって、適合の定義そのものではない。","eEn":"Conformity means fulfilment of a requirement. It does not mean exceeding the stated level, and passing an audit or obtaining certification are outcomes related to conformity, not its definition."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『不適合（nonconformity）』の意味に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches the meaning of 'nonconformity'?","o":["あらかじめ定めた期間に内部監査が実施されないこと","リスクが顕在化すること","要求事項を満たしていないこと","目的が未達成であること"],"oEn":["An internal audit not being conducted within the planned period","A risk materializing","Non-fulfilment of a requirement","An objective not being achieved"],"a":2,"e":"不適合とは、要求事項を満たしていないこと。内部監査が定めた期間に実施されないことは不適合の一例になり得るが定義そのものではなく、リスクの顕在化や目的の未達成も、それ自体は不適合の定義ではない。","eEn":"A nonconformity is the non-fulfilment of a requirement. A missed internal audit may be one example, but it is not the definition, and a risk materializing or an objective going unmet is not by itself the definition either."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『継続的改善（continual improvement）』の定義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches the definition of 'continual improvement'?","o":["パフォーマンスを向上させるために繰り返し行う活動","不適合の存在を監査員から隠すためにあえて繰り返し行われる活動","認証を維持するためだけに行う形式的な活動","一度きりで完結する大規模な変革のこと"],"oEn":["A recurring activity to enhance performance","A recurring activity deliberately carried out to hide the existence of nonconformities from auditors","A formal activity performed solely to maintain certification","A large-scale transformation that is completed just once"],"a":0,"e":"継続的改善とは、パフォーマンスを向上させるために繰り返し行う活動。認証を維持するためだけの形式的な活動や、一度きりで完結する大規模な変革ではなく、不適合を監査員から隠すための活動でもない。","eEn":"Continual improvement is a recurring activity to enhance performance. It is not a formality done only to keep certification, not a one-off large transformation, and not an activity meant to hide nonconformities from auditors."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『有効性（effectiveness）』の定義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches the definition of 'effectiveness'?","o":["計画した活動を実行し、計画した結果を達成する程度","設定した目的の数に対する方針の数の比率","投入した資源の量に対して得られた結果の比率、すなわち費用対効果の度合い","内部監査で発見された不適合の件数の総数"],"oEn":["The extent to which planned activities are realized and planned results achieved","The ratio of the number of policies to the number of objectives set","The ratio of the results obtained to the quantity of resources invested, that is, the degree of cost-efficiency","The total tally of nonconformity cases found in an internal audit"],"a":0,"e":"有効性は計画した活動を実行し計画した結果を達成する程度。効率(efficiency)とは異なる。","eEn":"Effectiveness is the extent planned activities are realized and results achieved, distinct from efficiency."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.2の内部監査と認証審査の関係として正しいのは？","qEn":"What is the correct relationship between the internal audit of Clause 9.2 and certification audit?","o":["内部監査は第一者監査であり、認証（第三者）審査とは異なる","内部監査は外部の認証審査と手続きも判定基準も完全に同一であり、いずれか一方で足りる","内部監査は必ず外部の認証機関が代わりに実施する","内部監査を実施した担当者自身が認証書を発行する"],"oEn":["The internal audit is a first-party audit and differs from third-party certification audit","Internal audit is entirely identical to an external certification audit in both procedure and judgment criteria, so performing either one alone suffices","Internal audit is always carried out in place of the organization by an external certification body","The very person who performed the internal audit issues the certificate"],"a":0,"e":"内部監査は組織自身が行う第一者監査で、第三者による認証審査とは別物。両者の手続きと判定基準が完全に同一とは言えず、内部監査を認証機関が代行するものでも、担当者が認証書を発行するものでもない。","eEn":"An internal audit is a first-party audit carried out by the organization and is distinct from third-party certification audits. The two do not share identical procedures and criteria, a certification body does not perform the internal audit on the organization's behalf, and the internal auditor does not issue certificates."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューのアウトプットの一つに含まれるのは？","qEn":"Which is included among the outputs of the management review under Clause 9.3?","o":["従業員の解雇リスト","来期の広告予算の配分方針","資源の必要性に関するトップマネジメントの決定","外部の競合分析レポート一式"],"oEn":["A list of employees to dismiss","The policy for allocating next term's advertising budget","Top management's decisions related to AIMS resource needs","A full set of external competitor-analysis reports"],"a":2,"e":"資源の必要性に関するトップマネジメントの決定は、マネジメントレビューのアウトプットに含まれる。従業員の解雇リストや来期の広告予算の配分方針、外部の競合分析レポートは、AIMSのレビューの出力ではない。","eEn":"Top management's decisions on resource needs are among the outputs of the management review. A list of employees to dismiss, next year's advertising budget allocation, or an external competitor analysis report are not outputs of the AIMS review."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AIリスクアセスメント（8.2）とAIシステム影響評価（8.4）の違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best distinguishes AI risk assessment (8.2) from AI system impact assessment (8.4)?","o":["両者は名称が異なるだけで対象も手順も完全に同一のプロセスであり、片方だけ実施すればよい","リスクアセスメントは影響評価の後にのみ行う","影響評価は、個人及び社会集団への影響に焦点を当てる点で異なる","影響評価は財務上のリスクのみを対象として扱うプロセス"],"oEn":["The two differ only in name; their subject and procedure are entirely the same process, so performing just one of them is enough","Risk assessment is done only after impact assessment","The impact assessment focuses on impacts to individuals and groups of society","The impact assessment is a process that treats only financial risk as its subject"],"a":2,"e":"影響評価は、個人および社会集団への影響に焦点を当てる点で、リスクアセスメントと異なる。両者が完全に同一で片方だけ実施すればよいとする見方や、影響評価は財務上のリスクのみを扱うとする見方は誤り。","eEn":"Impact assessment differs from risk assessment in focusing on effects on individuals and groups of society. It is wrong to say the two are identical so that only one is needed, or that impact assessment covers only financial risk."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 8.1でプロセスの計画・実施・管理の対象となるのは？","qEn":"What processes are to be planned, implemented and controlled under Clause 8.1?","o":["要求事項を満たし、Clause 6で決めた取組みを実施するために必要なプロセス","内部監査の実施だけに必要となるごく限られたプロセスのみに限定される","トップマネジメントが案件ごとに個別に指示したプロセスのみが対象で、Clause 6で決めた取組みは含まれない","外部に委託しているプロセスはすべて一律に対象外として除外される"],"oEn":["Processes needed to meet requirements and to implement the actions determined in Clause 6","Limited only to the very narrow set of processes needed solely to conduct internal audits","Only processes that top management individually directed case by case are covered, and the actions determined in Clause 6 are not included","Every outsourced process is uniformly excluded from the scope without exception"],"a":0,"e":"要求事項を満たしClause 6の取組みを実施するために必要なプロセスを管理する。","eEn":"Control processes needed to meet requirements and implement Clause 6 actions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"『監視（monitoring）』と『測定（measurement）』の違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best distinguishes 'monitoring' from 'measurement'?","o":["監視と測定はどちらも意味の違わない完全に同義な用語であり、規格中では入れ替えて使ってよい","監視は数値の決定を行い、測定は対象の状態を確認する作業である","監視は対象の状態を確認すること、測定は対象の値を決定することである","監視は外部のみで、測定は内部のみで実施するものである"],"oEn":["Monitoring and measurement are entirely synonymous terms with no difference in meaning, and may be used interchangeably throughout the standard","Monitoring determines a numerical value, and measurement is the task of checking a status","Monitoring checks the status of something; measurement determines a value","Monitoring is performed only externally, and measurement only internally"],"a":2,"e":"監視は対象の状態を確認すること、測定は対象の値を決定すること。数値の決定を監視とし状態の確認を測定とする説明は逆で、完全な同義語として入れ替えてよいわけでも、外部と内部で分かれるわけでもない。","eEn":"Monitoring is determining the status of something, and measurement is determining a value. Describing monitoring as deciding numbers and measurement as checking status reverses them, and they are neither fully interchangeable nor split between external and internal."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューのインプットとして適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is an appropriate input to the management review under Clause 9.3?","o":["競合他社の日々の株価の変動記録","社員個人の私生活に関する情報全般","AIMSに関する利害関係者からのフィードバック","レビュー当日のオフィスの天候記録"],"oEn":["A record of a competitor's day-to-day stock price fluctuations","General information concerning an individual employee's private life","Feedback from interested parties on the AIMS","A record of the office's weather on the day of the review"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSに関する利害関係者からのフィードバックは、マネジメントレビューのインプットの一つ。競合他社の株価の変動記録や、社員の私生活に関する情報、当日の天候記録は、AIMSのレビューの材料にならない。","eEn":"Feedback from interested parties relevant to the AIMS is one input to the management review. Records of a competitor's share-price moves, employees' private-life information, or the weather on the day of the review are not material for the AIMS review."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2で不適合の原因を明確にする際に併せて行うのは？","qEn":"When determining the cause of a nonconformity under Clause 10.2, what is also done?","o":["不適合は個別の事案として扱い、類似の不適合が他に存在する可能性はいっさい検討しない","類似の不適合が他に存在するか、又は発生する可能性があるかを明確にする","不適合の原因をあえて究明すること自体が禁止されている","類似する不適合が他にないかは確認せず自動的に無視して進める"],"oEn":["Treating the nonconformity as an isolated case and never examining whether similar nonconformities might exist elsewhere","Determine whether similar nonconformities exist or could potentially occur","Deliberately investigating the cause of the nonconformity itself is prohibited","Proceeding by automatically ignoring, without checking, whether similar nonconformities exist elsewhere"],"a":1,"e":"原因を明確にする際は、類似の不適合が他に存在するか、または発生する可能性があるかも併せて明確にする。個別の事案として扱い類似の不適合を検討しないことや、原因の究明を禁止することは、是正処置の趣旨に反する。","eEn":"When determining the causes, the organization also determines whether similar nonconformities exist or could potentially occur. Treating each case in isolation without considering similar ones, or forbidding cause investigation, contradicts the purpose of corrective action."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 9の結果とClause 10の継続的改善の関係に最も近いのは？","qEn":"What best describes the relationship between Clause 9 results and continual improvement in Clause 10?","o":["改善の内容はマネジメントレビューの場でのみ決定する","監視・測定・分析・評価の結果を継続的改善の入力として活用する","継続的改善はいかなる監視結果とも無関係に実施する","監視・測定の結果を継続的改善の入力として決して使ってはならず、改善は別に決める"],"oEn":["The content of improvement is decided only during the management review meeting","Use monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation results as input to continual improvement","Continual improvement is carried out independently of any monitoring results whatsoever","Monitoring and measurement results must never be used as an input to continual improvement, which is decided entirely separately"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 9 の監視・測定・分析・評価の結果は、継続的改善の入力として活用する。改善の内容がマネジメントレビューでのみ決まるわけではなく、監視結果と無関係に改善する、結果を決して使わない、という扱いも誤り。","eEn":"The results of monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation in Clause 9 are used as inputs to continual improvement. Improvement is not decided only in the management review, nor carried out independent of monitoring results or in defiance of them."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Clause 10.2で是正処置の一環として必要になり得るのは？","qEn":"What may be needed as part of corrective action under Clause 10.2?","o":["是正処置があってもAIMSは決して変更しない","変更は認証機関が行う","必要な場合には、AIMSに変更を加える","AIMSへの変更は経営層に無断で実施する"],"oEn":["Even when there is corrective action, the AIMS is never changed","Changes are made by the certification body","Make changes to the AIMS if necessary","Changes to the AIMS are carried out without informing top management"],"a":2,"e":"是正処置の一環として、必要な場合にはAIMSに変更を加える。是正処置があってもAIMSを決して変更しないという立場や、変更は認証機関が行うという立場、経営層に無断で実施するという立場は、要求と合わない。","eEn":"As part of corrective action, the AIMS is changed where necessary. Never changing the AIMS despite corrective action, leaving changes to the certification body, or making them without management's knowledge does not match the requirement."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の管理策が「方針」「内部組織」「資源」などの見出しでまとめられていることは何を意味するか。","qEn":"What does it mean that the Annex A controls are organized under headings such as 'policies', 'internal organization', and 'resources'?","o":["見出しごとに別々の認証が発行される","管理策がテーマ別に分類され参照しやすくなっている","管理策は見出しに並ぶ順序どおりに上から必ず実装しなければならない","各見出しが法的強制力の順位を示す"],"oEn":["A separate certificate is issued for each heading","The controls are grouped by theme, making them easier to reference","The controls must always be implemented from the top, strictly in the order the headings are listed","Each heading indicates a ranking of legal enforceability"],"a":1,"e":"Annex A はテーマ別の見出しに管理策を整理した参照集であり、俯瞰と選定を容易にする。","eEn":"Annex A organizes controls under thematic headings as a reference set, making overview and selection easier."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 本文の要求事項に対し、Annex A のすべての管理策を必ず実装しなければならないか。","qEn":"Regarding the requirements in the body of ISO/IEC 42001, must all Annex A controls always be implemented?","o":["組織はリスクにかかわらずAnnex Aに列挙されたすべての管理策を無条件に実装する義務を負う","適用する管理策はすべて監査人が一方的に選定し組織は関与しない","Annex A は単なる任意の付録なので一切参照してはならない","組織はリスクに基づき必要な管理策を選び、Annex A は参照リストとして使う"],"oEn":["The organization bears an obligation to implement every control listed in Annex A unconditionally, irrespective of risk","Every control to apply is unilaterally selected by the auditor, and the organization has no involvement","Annex A is merely an optional appendix, so it must never be referenced at all","The organization selects necessary controls based on risk, using Annex A as a reference list"],"a":3,"e":"組織はリスクアセスメント・対応に基づき必要な管理策を選定し、Annex A を照合用の参照として用いる。","eEn":"The organization selects necessary controls based on risk assessment and treatment, using Annex A as a reference for comparison."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"組織が Annex A に列挙されていない独自の管理策を導入したい場合、正しいのは。","qEn":"When an organization wants to introduce its own control not listed in Annex A, which is correct?","o":["追加する場合は Annex A の管理策をすべて削除する","認証機関の事前許可がなければ追加できない","Annex A 以外の管理策は一切認められない","リスク対応に必要なら追加してよい"],"oEn":["If added, all Annex A controls must be removed","It cannot be added without prior approval from the certification body","No control outside Annex A is ever permitted","It may be added if needed for risk treatment"],"a":3,"e":"Annex A は網羅を意図した参照集だが排他的ではなく、必要なら組織独自の管理策を追加できる。","eEn":"Annex A is a comprehensive reference set but not exclusive; organizations may add their own controls where necessary."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A における「管理目的（control objective）」の役割に最も近いのは。","qEn":"Which best describes the role of a 'control objective' in Annex A?","o":["管理策を実装する詳細な技術手順と設定値を規定する","認証の有効期限を定める","管理策が達成しようとする狙い・意図を示す","罰則の金額を定める"],"oEn":["Specifies the detailed technical procedures and configuration values for implementing a control","Sets the validity period of certification","States the aim or intent the control seeks to achieve","Sets the monetary amount of penalties"],"a":2,"e":"管理目的は、管理策が達成しようとする狙いや意図を示し、実装の方向づけとなる。実装の詳細な技術手順と設定値を規定するものではなく、認証の有効期限や罰則の金額を定めるものでもない。","eEn":"A control objective states the aim a control is meant to achieve and gives direction to its implementation. It does not specify detailed technical procedures and settings, and it does not set a certificate's validity period or penalty amounts."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針（AI policy）を承認する責任を負うのは誰か。","qEn":"Who is responsible for approving the AI policy?","o":["データ提供ベンダー","トップマネジメント","外部監査人","一般の利用者"],"oEn":["The data-supplying vendor","Top management","The external auditor","General users"],"a":1,"e":"AI方針は、トップマネジメントが確立し承認する責任を負う。データ提供ベンダーや外部監査人、一般の利用者は、組織の方針を承認する立場にない。","eEn":"Top management is responsible for establishing and approving the AI policy. A data-providing vendor, an external auditor, or general users are not in a position to approve the organization's policy."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針に関する管理策で、方針の「見直し（review）」について求められるのは。","qEn":"For controls related to the AI policy, what is required regarding 'review' of the policy?","o":["AI方針は一度策定したら二度と変更してはならない","あらかじめ定めた間隔または重大な変化があったときに見直す","AI方針を見直すこと自体が規格上禁止されている","AI方針は内容の変化の有無にかかわらず毎日必ず全面的に書き換える"],"oEn":["Once the AI policy is drafted, it must never be changed again","Review it at planned intervals or when significant changes occur","Reviewing the AI policy at all is prohibited under the standard","The AI policy must be completely rewritten every single day, whether or not anything has changed"],"a":1,"e":"AI方針は、あらかじめ定めた間隔で、または重大な変化があったときに見直し、適切性を維持する。二度と変更しない運用や、見直し自体を禁止する運用、毎日全面的に書き換える運用は、いずれも現実的でも要求でもない。","eEn":"The AI policy is reviewed at planned intervals or when significant changes occur, to keep it suitable. Never changing it again, prohibiting review altogether, or rewriting it completely every day is neither realistic nor required."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針が組織の他の方針や事業目的と整合していることが求められる理由。","qEn":"Why is the AI policy required to align with the organization's other policies and business objectives?","o":["AIの取り組みが組織全体の方向性と矛盾しないようにするため","審査機関に毎年支払っている認証料金を下げるため","方針に記載する文字数をできるだけ多く増やすため","自社のAI方針の詳しい内容を競合他社にも同じ条件で開示していくため"],"oEn":["So the AI effort does not conflict with the overall direction of the organization","To lower the certification fee that is paid to the certification body every year","To increase, by as much as possible, the number of characters written in the policy","To disclose the detailed content of one's own AI policy to competitors as well, on the very same terms"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針を組織の他の方針や事業目的と整合させるのは、AIの取り組みが組織全体の方向性と矛盾しないようにするため。認証料金を下げるためでも、文字数を増やすためでも、競合他社に開示するためでもない。","eEn":"The AI policy is aligned with other policies and business objectives so that AI efforts do not conflict with the organization's overall direction. It is not meant to lower certification fees, to lengthen the text, or to disclose it to competitors."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針を「関係者へ伝達（communicate）」する管理策の狙い。","qEn":"What is the aim of the control to 'communicate' the AI policy to relevant parties?","o":["関係する人々が方針を理解し行動に反映できるようにする","方針の内容を機密として扱い、関係する要員や取引先には一切見せないため","方針の文章に対する著作権を強く主張すること","社内に配付するために印刷する枚数を決めること"],"oEn":["Enable relevant people to understand the policy and reflect it in their actions","To treat the policy's content as confidential and never show it to relevant staff or business partners at all","Strongly asserting copyright over the wording of the policy","Deciding the number of copies to print for internal distribution"],"a":0,"e":"方針を伝達する狙いは、関係する人々が方針を理解し、行動に反映できるようにすること。内容を機密として要員や取引先に一切見せない扱いや、著作権の主張、配付する印刷枚数の決定は、伝達の目的ではない。","eEn":"Communicating the policy aims to let relevant people understand it and reflect it in their actions. Treating it as confidential and showing it to no staff or partners, asserting copyright, or deciding how many copies to print is not the purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIに関する「懸念（concern）を報告する仕組み」を設ける管理策の狙い。","qEn":"What is the aim of a control that establishes a mechanism to 'report concerns' about AI?","o":["報告された内容を確認せず外部に自動公開する","懸念を報告してきた従業員を理由を問わず必ず解雇する","問題や懸念を適切な相手に伝えられる報告経路を確保する","寄せられる懸念は一切受け付けないようにする"],"oEn":["Automatically publishing reported content externally without checking it","Always dismissing the employee who reported the concern","Ensure a reporting route to raise issues and concerns to the appropriate party","Ensuring that concerns raised are never accepted at all"],"a":2,"e":"懸念を適切な相手に届ける報告経路を整えることで、問題の早期把握と対応を可能にする。","eEn":"Providing a route to raise concerns to the right party enables early awareness and response to problems."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムに関する役割と責任を明確に文書化しないと生じやすい問題。","qEn":"What problem is likely if roles and responsibilities for AI systems are not clearly documented?","o":["AIシステムのソースコードが自動的に暗号化されて読めなくなる","データ量が減る","電気料金が上がる","誰が何に責任を持つか曖昧になり対応が漏れる"],"oEn":["The source code of the AI system is automatically encrypted and can no longer be read by anyone","The amount of data decreases","Electricity costs rise","It becomes unclear who is responsible for what, and actions fall through the cracks"],"a":3,"e":"役割・責任が曖昧だと対応の抜けや重複が生じるため、明確な割当と文書化が求められる。","eEn":"Ambiguous roles cause gaps and overlaps in response, so clear allocation and documentation are required."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"内部組織の管理策が、複数の部門・機能間の「調整（coordination）」を重視する理由。","qEn":"Why do internal-organization controls emphasize 'coordination' across departments and functions?","o":["部門間で開かれる調整会議の開催回数と延べ出席者数を最大化するため","AIに関わる意思決定や責任が部門間で一貫するようにするため","部門ごとに独立した別々のAIを必ず開発するため","部門をまたぐ連絡や情報共有を一律に禁止するため"],"oEn":["To maximize the number of coordination meetings held between departments and the number of attendees","So decisions and responsibilities for AI are consistent across departments","To ensure each department always develops its own separate, independent AI","To uniformly prohibit communication and information sharing across departments"],"a":1,"e":"AIは複数の部門や機能にまたがるため、調整によってAIに関わる意思決定や責任が部門間で一貫するようにする。調整会議の開催回数や出席者数の最大化が目的ではなく、部門ごとに別々のAIを開発することや連絡の禁止でもない。","eEn":"AI spans several departments and functions, so coordination keeps decisions and responsibilities consistent across them. The goal is not to maximize meeting counts or attendance, nor to build separate AIs per department or ban cross-department contact."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"「AIシステムのための資源（resources）」に関する管理策が対象とする資源の例として適切なのは。","qEn":"Which is an appropriate example of resources addressed by controls on 'resources for AI systems'?","o":["データ・ツール・システム（計算）資源・人的資源","顧客が個人的に抱く私的な感情","競合他社が保有する営業秘密の情報","開発を行った当日のオフィスの天候状況"],"oEn":["Data, tooling, system (computing) resources, and human resources","A customer's own private, personal feelings","Trade-secret information held by a competitor","The weather conditions at the office on the day the development took place"],"a":0,"e":"資源にはデータ、ツール、システム・計算資源、人的資源などが含まれ、これらを特定・管理する。","eEn":"Resources include data, tooling, system/computing resources, and human resources, which are identified and managed."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"資源に関する管理策で、組織が保有・利用する資源を「文書化（document）」する目的。","qEn":"What is the purpose of 'documenting' the resources an organization holds or uses, under resource controls?","o":["作成した資源の文書の枚数の多さだけを部門間で比べ、その多寡で優劣を競うため","どの資源がAIシステムに影響するかを把握し管理できるようにする","資源に付けられる呼び名を意図的に長くするだけのため","保有している資源の存在そのものを意図的に隠すため"],"oEn":["To compete for superiority by comparing across departments solely the sheer number of pages of resource documents produced","To understand and manage which resources affect the AI system","Merely to deliberately make the names given to resources longer","To deliberately hide the very existence of resources being held"],"a":1,"e":"資源を文書化すると、どの資源がAIシステムに影響するかを把握し、管理できる。文書の枚数の多さを部門間で競うことや、呼び名を長くすること、資源の存在を隠すことは、文書化の目的ではない。","eEn":"Documenting resources lets the organization see which resources affect the AI system and manage them. Competing between departments over the number of documents, lengthening resource names, or hiding the existence of resources is not the purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの資源として「人的資源（human resources）」を扱うとき重視されるのは。","qEn":"When treating 'human resources' as a resource for AI systems, what is emphasized?","o":["配置する従業員の人数を最小化すること","保有していた人員の情報を配置の完了後ただちに破棄すること","担当者全員を定期的な交代制にすること","役割に必要な力量（コンピテンス）を確保すること"],"oEn":["Minimizing the number of employees assigned","Discarding the information on personnel held as soon as assignment is complete","Putting every person in charge on a regular rotation","Ensuring the competence needed for the roles"],"a":3,"e":"人的資源では、担当する役割に必要な力量（コンピテンス）を確保することが重視される。人数の最小化や、配置後に人員の情報を破棄すること、担当者全員を定期的な交代制にすることは、力量の確保と結びつかない。","eEn":"For human resources, the emphasis is on ensuring the competence needed for each role. Minimizing headcount, discarding staff information after assignment, or rotating everyone on a regular schedule does not ensure competence."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"「システム及び計算資源（system and computing resources）」に関する管理策が示すもの。","qEn":"What do controls on 'system and computing resources' address?","o":["マーケティング部門が独自に管理する広告予算の配分方法と媒体ごとの出稿計画","AIシステムの開発・運用に必要な計算基盤やインフラを特定・管理する","オフィス内の装飾やレイアウトに関する社内方針の細則","従業員一人ひとりに毎年新たに付与される年間の休暇日数"],"oEn":["The way the marketing department independently allocates its own advertising budget and plans placements per medium","Identifying and managing the computing infrastructure needed to develop and operate AI systems","Internal policy details concerning the decoration and layout of the office interior","The number of annual vacation days newly granted to each individual employee every year"],"a":1,"e":"システム・計算資源の管理策は、AIの開発・運用に必要な計算基盤の特定と管理を扱う。","eEn":"Controls on system and computing resources cover identifying and managing the computing infrastructure needed for AI development and operation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"適用宣言書（SoA）と「リスク対応（risk treatment）の結果」の関係として正しいのは。","qEn":"Which correctly describes the relationship between the Statement of Applicability (SoA) and the results of risk treatment?","o":["SoA はリスクを増やすために使う","リスク対応で決めた管理策の選定結果を反映して作成する","SoAはリスクアセスメントを行う前に完成させ、その後は更新しない","SoA はリスク対応と無関係に作る"],"oEn":["The SoA is used to increase risk","It is created reflecting the control selection determined in risk treatment","The SoA is completed before risk assessment is performed, and is not updated thereafter","The SoA is created independently of risk treatment"],"a":1,"e":"SoA は、リスク対応で決めた管理策の選定・除外の結果を反映して作成される。リスク対応と無関係に作る、リスクアセスメントの前に完成させて更新しない、リスクを増やすために使う、といった扱いは誤り。","eEn":"The SoA is prepared to reflect the results of risk treatment, namely which controls were selected or excluded. Making it unrelated to risk treatment, finishing it before risk assessment and never updating it, or using it to increase risk is wrong."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA において、採用する管理策について記載すべき「含める理由（justification for inclusion）」とは。","qEn":"In the SoA, what is the 'justification for inclusion' to be recorded for adopted controls?","o":["管理策に用いる色やデザインの好み","管理策を製造した企業の所在地と担当窓口の連絡先","なぜその管理策が必要と判断したかの根拠","導入する管理策の購入価格の総額"],"oEn":["A preference for the color or design used in the control","The address of the company that manufactured the control and its contact desk","The rationale for why the control was judged necessary","The total purchase price of the control being introduced"],"a":2,"e":"含める理由とは、なぜその管理策が必要と判断したかの根拠で、SoA に記載する。色やデザインの好み、管理策を製造した企業の所在地と連絡先、購入価格の総額は、必要と判断した根拠にならない。","eEn":"The justification for inclusion is the reason the control was judged necessary, recorded in the SoA. Colour or design preference, the manufacturer's address and contact, or the total purchase price is not a basis for that judgment."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA に「実施状況（implementation status）」を記載する意義。","qEn":"What is the significance of recording 'implementation status' in the SoA?","o":["各管理策が現時点でどこまで実装されているかを示す","実施状況の内容は競合他社にのみ開示する","実施状況はSoAではなく監査報告書にのみ記載する事項である","すべての管理策を必ず実装しないと宣言すること"],"oEn":["It shows how far each control is currently implemented","The content of the implementation status is disclosed only to competitors","Implementation status is a matter to be recorded only in the audit report, not in the SoA","Declaring that every control will definitely not be implemented"],"a":0,"e":"実施状況を記載すると、各管理策が現時点でどこまで実装されているかが分かる。実施状況は競合他社にのみ開示するものではなく、監査報告書にのみ記載する事項でもなく、すべての管理策を必ず実装すると宣言するものでもない。","eEn":"Recording implementation status shows how far each control is currently implemented. It is not disclosed only to competitors, not a matter for the audit report alone, and not a declaration that every control must be implemented."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA を「維持・更新（maintain）」し続ける必要がある理由。","qEn":"Why must the SoA be continually 'maintained' and updated?","o":["SoAを更新すると取得済みの認証が無効になるから","SoAの更新は関係法令によって禁止されているから","SoAは一度作成してしまえば、リスクが変化しても以後の変更は一切不要だから","リスクや管理策の状況が変われば内容も最新に保つ必要があるから"],"oEn":["Because updating the SoA invalidates the certification already obtained","Because updating the SoA is prohibited by applicable law","Because once the SoA has been drafted, no further change is ever needed even if the risks change","Because when risks or control status change, the content must be kept current"],"a":3,"e":"リスクや管理策の状況は変化するため、SoA は内容を最新の状態に保つ必要がある。更新すると認証が無効になる、関係法令で禁止されている、一度作れば変更は一切不要、といった説明は事実ではない。","eEn":"Risks and the status of controls change, so the SoA must be kept up to date. Claims that updating it invalidates certification, that laws forbid updating it, or that it never needs changing once created are not true."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA で管理策を「除外（exclude）」する際に、正当な除外理由として最も適切なのは。","qEn":"When 'excluding' a control in the SoA, which is the most appropriate valid justification?","o":["該当リスクが存在しない等、合理的で説明可能な根拠","「担当者が忙しいから」という都合","「文書を短くしたいから」という理由","「担当者がなんとなく不要と感じたから」という主観的な印象"],"oEn":["A reasonable, explainable basis such as the relevant risk not existing","The convenience that 'the person in charge is busy'","The reason 'we want to shorten the document'","The subjective impression that 'the person in charge somehow felt it was unnecessary'"],"a":0,"e":"除外は主観や都合ではなく、該当リスクが存在しない等の合理的で説明可能な理由に基づく必要がある。","eEn":"Exclusion must rest on a reasonable, explainable basis such as the relevant risk not existing, not on subjectivity or convenience."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA を承認する立場として適切なのは。","qEn":"Who is appropriate to approve the SoA?","o":["外部の一般公衆が投票によって承認を決める","競合他社が承認する","承認という手続きは不要で誰も内容を見なくてよい","権限を持つ管理層（マネジメント）が承認し責任を明確にする"],"oEn":["Members of the general public outside decide approval by vote","Competitors approve it","No approval procedure is needed, and no one has to review the content","Management with appropriate authority approves it, making responsibility clear"],"a":3,"e":"SoA は、権限を持つ管理層（マネジメント）が承認し、責任を明確にする。外部の一般公衆の投票や競合他社が承認することはなく、誰も内容を見なくてよいとして承認を不要にすることも不適切。","eEn":"The SoA is approved by management with the appropriate authority, which makes responsibility clear. A public vote by outsiders or approval by competitors makes no sense, and skipping approval so that nobody reviews it is inappropriate."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA が示す全体像として最も近いのは。","qEn":"Which best captures the overall picture the SoA provides?","o":["リスク対応の担当者と実施時期、必要となる資源をまとめた計画書","学習をすべて終えたAIモデルの重みパラメータと層構成の一覧表","どの管理策を適用し、どれを除外したか（理由付き）の一覧","顧客ごとに個別に詳細記録された購買履歴の一覧"],"oEn":["A plan document compiling the owner, the implementation timing, and the resources required for each risk treatment","A table listing the weight parameters and layer structure of an AI model that has finished all of its training","A list, with justifications, of which controls are applied and which are excluded","A detailed list of purchase history recorded individually for each customer"],"a":2,"e":"SoA は、どの管理策を適用し、どれを除外したかを理由付きで一覧にした文書。リスク対応の担当者や実施時期、必要資源をまとめた計画書はリスク対応計画であり、AIモデルの重みパラメータや購買履歴の一覧でもない。","eEn":"The SoA lists which controls are applied and which are excluded, with reasons. A document summarizing who treats risks, when, and with which resources is the risk treatment plan, and the SoA is neither a list of model weight parameters nor purchase histories."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"「管理策（control）」の一般的な性質として最も近いのは。","qEn":"Which best describes the general nature of a 'control'?","o":["審査機関が認証番号を発行するための装置","リスクを意図的に増大させるための手段","リスクを修正（低減など）するために講じる手段","組織の当期の純利益を最大化するための会計処理の手法"],"oEn":["A device the certification body uses to issue a certificate number","A means used to deliberately increase risk","A measure taken to modify (e.g., reduce) risk","An accounting technique used to maximize the organization's profit for the current period"],"a":2,"e":"管理策とは、リスクを修正（低減・回避など）するために講じる手段。リスクを意図的に増大させる手段ではなく、認証番号を発行する装置でも、純利益を最大化する会計処理の手法でもない。","eEn":"A control is a measure that modifies risk, for example by reducing or avoiding it. It is not a means of deliberately increasing risk, not a device for issuing certification numbers, and not an accounting method for maximizing net profit."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"リスク対応の過程で Annex A と選定した管理策を照合する主な目的。","qEn":"What is the main purpose of comparing selected controls against Annex A during risk treatment?","o":["審査機関に毎年支払う認証料金の総額を計算するため","Annex A の誤字を探すため","必要な管理策の見落としがないか確認するため","管理策の数をできるだけ減らすため"],"oEn":["To calculate the total annual certification fee paid to the certification body","To find typos in Annex A","To verify that no necessary control has been overlooked","To reduce the number of controls as much as possible"],"a":2,"e":"Annex A との照合は、必要な管理策の見落としがないかを確認するために行う。","eEn":"Comparing against Annex A checks that no necessary control has been overlooked."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針を文書化された情報として維持する理由。","qEn":"Why is the AI policy maintained as documented information?","o":["方針の存在と内容を確認・参照できるようにするため","方針の文書をあえて頻繁に紛失させるため","方針の内容を誰も読めない非公開の暗号文にしてしまうため","従業員全員に方針の全文を暗記させるため"],"oEn":["So the policy's existence and content can be verified and referenced","To deliberately have the policy document go missing frequently","To turn the policy's content into an undisclosed encrypted text that no one can read","To make every employee memorize the full text of the policy"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針を文書化された情報として維持するのは、方針の存在と内容を確認・参照できるようにするため。方針を頻繁に紛失させることや、非公開の暗号文にすること、全文を暗記させることは、文書化の目的に反する。","eEn":"The AI policy is kept as documented information so that its existence and content can be checked and referred to. Losing it often, turning it into a secret ciphertext, or making staff memorize the full text contradicts that purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"内部組織の管理策で「権限（authority）」を割り当てることが重要な理由。","qEn":"Why is assigning 'authority' important in internal-organization controls?","o":["権限は多いほど混乱するので割り当てないほうがよいから","権限は外部委託先だけが持つべきだから","権限があいまいだと必要な意思決定や対応が滞り責任も不明確になるから","権限は毎週入れ替えるべきだから"],"oEn":["Because more authority causes confusion, so none should be assigned","Because only outsourcers should hold authority","Because ambiguous authority stalls necessary decisions and actions and blurs responsibility","Because authority should be swapped every week"],"a":2,"e":"権限があいまいだと、必要な意思決定や対応が滞り、責任の所在も不明確になるため、権限を明確に割り当てる。権限は多いほど混乱するから割り当てないという考えや、外部委託先だけに持たせる、毎週入れ替えるという考えは誤り。","eEn":"Unclear authority stalls needed decisions and responses and blurs accountability, so authority is clearly assigned. It is wrong to avoid assigning authority because more of it causes confusion, to give it only to outsourced parties, or to swap it weekly."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"資源に関する管理策で「ツール（tooling）資源」に該当する例。","qEn":"Which is an example of 'tooling' resources under resource controls?","o":["顧客が寄せた個人的な感想のコメント","従業員が私的な趣味のために個人的に持ち込む道具","オフィスの建物の外壁に使われている塗料","モデルの開発・検証・運用に使うソフトウェアや開発環境"],"oEn":["A comment expressing a customer's personal impression","Items an employee personally brings in for a private hobby","The paint used on the exterior wall of the office building","Software and development environments used to build, verify, or operate models"],"a":3,"e":"ツール資源には、モデルの開発・検証・運用に使うソフトウェアや開発環境が含まれる。顧客の個人的な感想のコメントや、従業員が私的に持ち込む道具、オフィス外壁の塗料は、AIシステムのツール資源ではない。","eEn":"Tooling resources include software and development environments used to develop, verify and operate models. Customers' personal comments, tools employees bring in for private hobbies, or the paint on the office walls are not tooling resources of an AI system."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムのための「データ資源」を資源管理の観点で扱う意義。","qEn":"What is the significance of treating 'data resources' for AI systems from a resource-management perspective?","o":["保有しているデータ量の多さだけを競うことが目的である","データは資源に該当しないため管理の対象外として扱う","AIシステムが依存するデータも管理すべき資源として位置づける","データは利用後ただちに常に破棄し、記録も残さないことが唯一の目的である"],"oEn":["The sole aim is to compete only on the sheer volume of data held","Data does not qualify as a resource and is therefore treated as outside the scope of management","Data on which the AI system depends is positioned as a resource to be managed","The sole aim is always to discard data immediately after use and to keep no record of it either"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムが依存するデータも、管理すべき資源として位置づけ、特定して管理する。データは資源に該当しないという見方や、データ量の多さを競う目的、利用後に常に破棄し記録も残さないという扱いは誤り。","eEn":"The data an AI system depends on is also positioned as a resource to be identified and managed. It is wrong to say data is not a resource, to compete on data volume, or to always discard data after use without keeping any record."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の管理策と本文の要求事項をつなぐ文書はどれか。","qEn":"Which document links the Annex A controls with the requirements in the main body?","o":["議事録","就業規則（社内の労務規程）","財務諸表","適用宣言書（SoA）"],"oEn":["Meeting minutes","Work rules (the internal labor regulations)","Financial statements","The Statement of Applicability (SoA)"],"a":3,"e":"SoA は選定・除外した管理策を示し、リスク対応と Annex A をつなぐ文書である。","eEn":"The SoA records selected and excluded controls, linking risk treatment with Annex A."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA を作成する前提として必要な作業。","qEn":"What work is a prerequisite for producing the SoA?","o":["SoAを作成する前にまず全従業員をいったん解雇して一斉に再雇用すること","認証を取得する前にまず大々的な広告を出しておくこと","審査そのものを経ずにまず認証書だけを受け取ること","リスクアセスメントとリスク対応を行い、必要な管理策を決めること"],"oEn":["Dismissing all employees once and rehiring them all simultaneously, before the SoA is drafted","Running a large advertisement first and getting it out before obtaining certification","Receiving only the certificate first, without going through any assessment at all","Perform risk assessment and treatment and determine the necessary controls"],"a":3,"e":"SoA はリスクアセスメント・対応で必要な管理策を決めた結果に基づいて作成する。","eEn":"The SoA is produced based on the necessary controls determined through risk assessment and treatment."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI方針が扱う内容として最も適切なのは。","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate content for the AI policy to address?","o":["個々のサーバーに割り当てたIPアドレスとポート番号の一覧","組織のAIに対する基本的な方向性やコミットメント","個々のAIシステムごとに定める詳細な試験手順と合否基準","従業員が月次で行う経費精算の提出締切日"],"oEn":["A list of the IP addresses and port numbers assigned to individual servers","The organization's basic direction and commitment regarding AI","The detailed test procedures and pass/fail criteria defined for each individual AI system","The monthly deadline by which employees must submit expense reimbursements"],"a":1,"e":"AI方針が扱うのは、組織のAIに対する基本的な方向性やコミットメント。IPアドレスやポート番号の一覧、個々のAIシステムの詳細な試験手順と合否基準、経費精算の締切日は、方針ではなく個別の手順や運用の細目。","eEn":"The AI policy covers the organization's basic direction and commitments on AI. Lists of IP addresses and port numbers, detailed test procedures and pass criteria for individual systems, or expense-claim deadlines are operational details, not policy."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"内部組織の管理策における「役割の分離・独立性」を考慮する狙いの一つ。","qEn":"What is one aim of considering 'segregation and independence of roles' in internal-organization controls?","o":["誰も責任を持たないよう役割分担をあいまいにする","利益相反や偏りがAIに関する意思決定に影響するのを抑える","部門内の役割をあえて全員同一にしてしまう","定例会議の開催時間を無意味に長くする"],"oEn":["Blurring the division of roles so that no one bears responsibility","To limit conflicts of interest or bias from affecting AI-related decisions","Deliberately making everyone's role within the department identical","Making the duration of regular meetings pointlessly longer"],"a":1,"e":"役割の適切な分離や独立性を考慮するのは、利益相反や偏りがAIに関する意思決定に影響するのを抑えるため。役割分担をあいまいにして誰も責任を持たないようにすることや、全員を同一の役割にすることは逆効果。","eEn":"Considering separation of roles and independence helps keep conflicts of interest and bias from affecting AI-related decisions. Making roles vague so nobody is accountable, or giving everyone the same role, has the opposite effect."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"資源管理の管理策が最終的に支えるもの。","qEn":"What do resource-management controls ultimately support?","o":["オフィス全体の内装や装飾を統一すること","AIシステムを適切に開発・運用するための基盤の確保","契約上の優越的地位を用いて競合他社の事業活動を妨害すること","決算発表の前後に自社の株価を意図的に短期操作すること"],"oEn":["Unifying the interior decoration across the entire office","Securing the foundation to properly develop and operate AI systems","Using a superior contractual position to obstruct a competitor's business activities","Deliberately short-term manipulating the company's own stock price around earnings announcements"],"a":1,"e":"資源の特定と管理は、AIシステムを適切に開発・運用するための基盤を支える。オフィスの内装を統一することや、優越的地位を使って競合他社の事業を妨害すること、株価の短期操作は、資源管理の目的ではない。","eEn":"Identifying and managing resources underpins the proper development and operation of AI systems. Unifying office decor, using a dominant position to obstruct competitors, or manipulating the share price in the short term is not the aim of resource management."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SoA の記載が監査・レビューで参照されるとき、確認できることは。","qEn":"When the SoA is referenced during audit or review, what can be confirmed?","o":["サーバー室内の気温と湿度の時間ごとの変化がわかる","各管理策の適用/除外の判断と理由をたどれる","従業員個人の血液型の情報がわかる","顧客個人の位置情報の履歴がわかる"],"oEn":["Reveals the hour-by-hour fluctuations in the temperature and humidity of the server room","The decision and rationale for applying or excluding each control can be traced","Reveals information about an individual employee's blood type","Reveals the history of an individual customer's location data"],"a":1,"e":"SoA を参照すると、各管理策の適用・除外の判断とその理由をたどることができる。サーバー室の温度と湿度の変化や、従業員の血液型、顧客の位置情報の履歴は、SoA に書かれる内容ではない。","eEn":"Looking at the SoA lets reviewers trace the decision to apply or exclude each control and the reasons behind it. Server-room temperature and humidity changes, employees' blood types, or customers' location histories are not recorded in the SoA."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Annex A の構成を理解することが実務で役立つ理由。","qEn":"Why is understanding the structure of Annex A useful in practice?","o":["管理策の名称をすべて漏れなく暗記して同僚と競うため","どの領域の管理策があるか俯瞰でき、抜け漏れを防げる","外部審査機関による認証の取得そのものを回避するため","作成し提出する文書の分量をとにかく最小化するため"],"oEn":["To memorize the names of every control without omission and compete with colleagues over it","To overview which areas of controls exist and prevent omissions","To avoid obtaining certification through an external assessment body altogether","To minimize, above all else, the volume of documentation produced and submitted"],"a":1,"e":"構成を理解すると、方針・組織・資源など各領域の管理策を俯瞰でき、抜け漏れを防げる。","eEn":"Understanding the structure gives an overview of controls across areas like policy, organization, and resources, preventing omissions."},
  { d:"D3", q:"AI方針・内部組織・資源の管理策が互いに関係する点。", qEn:"How do controls for AI policy, internal organization, and resources relate to one another?", o:["方針が方向を示し、組織が責任を割り当て、資源がそれを支えるという一貫性","方針・組織・資源の三者は完全に無関係で相互に干渉しない","方針・組織・資源のいずれか一つだけを選び他は切り捨てる","AI方針・組織体制・資源という三者の内容は常に矛盾させておくべきである"], oEn:["Consistency: policy sets direction, the organization allocates responsibility, and resources support it","Policy, organization, and resources are three entirely unrelated elements that never interact","Choosing only one of policy, organization, or resources and discarding the others","The content of policy, organizational structure, and resources should always be kept in deliberate contradiction"], a:0, e:"方針が方向を示し、内部組織が責任を割り当て、資源がそれを支えるという一貫した関係にある。", eEn:"They form a consistent chain: policy sets direction, internal organization allocates responsibility, and resources support it." },
  {"d":"D3","q":"管理策を「必要（necessary）」と判断する主な根拠。","qEn":"What is the main basis for judging a control 'necessary'?","o":["リスクアセスメントの結果や要求事項に基づいて必要性を判断する","管理策の名称に使われている文字数の長さのみで判定する","他社が公表している管理策の一覧をそのまま自社の一覧として写すだけにとどめる","どの管理策が必要かをくじ引きで機械的に決めてしまう"],"oEn":["Judge necessity based on risk assessment results and requirements","Judging based solely on the length, in characters, of the name used for the control","Merely copying the list of controls another company has published as one's own list, as it is","Deciding mechanically, by drawing lots, which control is necessary"],"a":0,"e":"管理策の必要性は、リスクアセスメントの結果や適用される要求事項に基づいて判断する。","eEn":"The necessity of a control is judged based on risk assessment results and applicable requirements."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムのライフサイクル全体にわたる管理策を設ける主な狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the main aim of controls that span the entire AI system lifecycle?","o":["マーケティング資料の作成を標準化すること","各段階で品質・リスク・責任を一貫して管理すること","ハードウェア調達の価格交渉を有利に進め、調達単価を引き下げること","開発コストを最小化し納期を短縮すること"],"oEn":["To standardize the creation of marketing materials","To consistently manage quality, risk and accountability across each stage","To gain leverage in hardware procurement price negotiations and drive down the unit purchase price","To minimize development cost and shorten delivery time"],"a":1,"e":"ライフサイクル管理策は着想から廃止までの各段階を一貫して統制し、品質・リスク・責任を維持することを狙う。","eEn":"Lifecycle controls aim to govern each stage from conception to retirement consistently, preserving quality, risk management and accountability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの品質に関する管理策が確保しようとする特性として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which characteristic do data quality controls most appropriately seek to ensure?","o":["データが常に最大量まで収集されること","学習データが常に単一のベンダーからのみ取得されていること","データが暗号化されて外部に共有されること","データが正確・完全で意図した用途に代表的であること"],"oEn":["That data is always collected up to the maximum volume","That the training data is always obtained from only a single vendor, and from no other source","That data is encrypted and shared externally","That data is accurate, complete and representative for the intended use"],"a":3,"e":"データ品質管理策は、正確性・完全性・意図した用途に対する代表性など、AIの目的に適合した品質を確保する。","eEn":"Data quality controls ensure fitness for the AI's purpose, including accuracy, completeness and representativeness for the intended use."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの出所（provenance）に関する管理策の主目的に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the primary purpose of data provenance controls?","o":["データの表示色を統一して可読性を高めること","データの出所・取得経緯・変遷を追跡可能にすること","データの容量を圧縮して保管コストを下げること","データを匿名化して再識別を完全に不可能にすること"],"oEn":["To unify display colors of data for readability","To make the origin, acquisition and transformations of data traceable","To compress data volume and reduce storage cost","To anonymize data so re-identification becomes wholly impossible"],"a":1,"e":"来歴管理策は、データがどこから来てどう扱われたかを追跡可能にし、信頼性と説明責任を支える。","eEn":"Provenance controls make it traceable where data came from and how it was handled, supporting trust and accountability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの前処理に関する管理策で求められることに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects what data preparation (preprocessing) controls require?","o":["前処理はモデル学習後にのみ実施すること","前処理は自動化されていれば手法も根拠も記録する必要がない","前処理の手法と根拠を文書化し再現可能にすること","前処理では常に全欠損値を平均値で埋めること"],"oEn":["To perform preprocessing only after model training","Preprocessing need not have either its methods or its rationale recorded, as long as it is automated","To document the methods and rationale of preprocessing so it is reproducible","To always fill all missing values with the mean"],"a":2,"e":"前処理管理策は、実施した加工の手法・根拠を記録し、再現性と透明性を確保することを求める。","eEn":"Preprocessing controls require recording the methods and rationale of transformations to ensure reproducibility and transparency."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報（information for users）に関する管理策が提供を求める内容として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which content do controls on information for users most appropriately require to be provided?","o":["競合他社が保有する内部設計の詳細情報","システムの意図された用途・能力・限界","供給者と締結した契約書に含まれる金額条項の全文","将来の株価予測に関する保証"],"oEn":["Detailed internal design information held by a competitor","The system's intended use, capabilities and limitations","The full text of the pricing clauses contained in the contract concluded with the supplier","Guarantees about future stock price forecasts"],"a":1,"e":"利用者向け情報の管理策は、意図された用途・能力・限界を伝え、適切な利用と誤用防止を支える。","eEn":"Controls on user information convey intended use, capabilities and limitations, supporting appropriate use and preventing misuse."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者・供給者（サプライヤ）関係に関する管理策で、契約締結前に重要とされるのは？","qEn":"In third-party/supplier relationship controls, what is important before entering a contract?","o":["契約の締結前に供給者へ無条件で全データへのアクセス権を付与しておくこと","供給者のAI関連能力とリスクを評価し要求事項を合意すること","供給者の選定を価格のみで決定すること","供給者へのすべての責任移転を口頭で確認すること"],"oEn":["Granting the supplier unconditional access rights to all data in advance, before the contract is concluded","Assessing the supplier's AI-related capabilities and risks and agreeing requirements","Deciding supplier selection on price alone","Confirming the full transfer of responsibility to the supplier verbally"],"a":1,"e":"供給者管理策は、能力・リスクの評価と要求事項の合意を通じて外部依存に伴うリスクを統制する。","eEn":"Supplier controls govern outsourcing risk by assessing capabilities and risks and agreeing on requirements."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの影響（impact）に関する管理策が主に着目する対象として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate focus of controls concerning the impact of AI systems?","o":["サーバ機器の電力消費量と冷却費用の推移のみ","AIシステムの開発言語の選択","アプリのUIに使うフォントサイズ","個人・集団・社会に及ぶ潜在的な影響"],"oEn":["Only the trend in server equipment's power consumption and cooling costs","The choice of programming language for the AI system's development","The font size used in the app's UI","Potential impacts on individuals, groups and society"],"a":3,"e":"影響に関する管理策は、AIが個人・集団・社会に及ぼしうる影響を特定・評価し対応することを狙う。","eEn":"Impact controls aim to identify, assess and address the effects an AI system may have on individuals, groups and society."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で扱う『代表性（representativeness）』の意味に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the meaning of 'representativeness' addressed by data controls?","o":["データが対象とする母集団や利用文脈を適切に反映していること","データが最大のサンプル数を持つこと","データが単一の地域からのみ収集されていること","データが常に最新のファイル形式に変換され最新の媒体に保存されていること"],"oEn":["That data adequately reflects the target population or usage context","That data has the maximum number of samples","That data is collected from only a single region","That the data is stored in the latest file format and on the newest storage media"],"a":0,"e":"代表性は、データが対象母集団や利用文脈を適切に反映しているかを問う概念で、偏りの抑制につながる。","eEn":"Representativeness concerns whether data adequately reflects the target population or usage context, helping to reduce bias."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの検証（verification）と妥当性確認（validation）に関する管理策の狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the aim of verification and validation controls for AI systems?","o":["供給者から購入した開発ツールの保守契約を毎年度更新すること","設計仕様への適合と意図した目的への適合を確認すること","経営層がAI方針の文面を承認し社内へ周知する手順を定めること","データセンター内の物理鍵の管理を徹底すること"],"oEn":["Renewing every fiscal year the maintenance contract for the development tools purchased from the supplier","To confirm conformance to design specs and fitness for the intended purpose","Defining the procedure by which top management approves the wording of the AI policy and communicates it internally","Thoroughly managing the physical keys within the data center"],"a":1,"e":"検証は仕様適合を、妥当性確認は意図した目的への適合を確認するもので、両者はリリース前の品質保証に不可欠。","eEn":"Verification confirms conformance to specifications and validation confirms fitness for intended purpose; both are essential pre-release quality assurance."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報の管理策が、システムの『限界』を開示することで直接支えるのは？","qEn":"By disclosing the system's 'limitations', controls on user information directly support what?","o":["競合製品の分析を容易にすること","過度な信頼や不適切な用途への使用を防ぐこと","製品の販売価格を限界まで一気に大幅に引き上げること","収集したデータの保存量を削減すること"],"oEn":["Easing analysis of competitor products","Preventing over-reliance and use in inappropriate contexts","Raising the product's sales price substantially, to the greatest extent possible","Reducing the volume of collected data that is stored"],"a":1,"e":"限界の開示は、利用者が能力を過信せず、意図された範囲で適切に利用できるよう支援する。","eEn":"Disclosing limitations helps users avoid over-trusting capabilities and use the system appropriately within intended bounds."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"供給者から取得したAIコンポーネントに関し、管理策として適切なのは？","qEn":"Regarding AI components obtained from suppliers, which is an appropriate control?","o":["供給者の全ソースコードを社内の保管庫にそのまま複製しておくこと","組込み前に要求事項への適合や既知のリスクを確認すること","供給者側の管理策を一切確認しないこと","導入後にのみリスクを検討すること"],"oEn":["Copying all of the supplier's source code into an in-house repository beforehand","Verifying conformance to requirements and known risks before integration","Never checking the supplier's own controls","Considering risks only after deployment"],"a":1,"e":"外部コンポーネントは、組込み前に要求事項適合・既知リスクを確認し、供給者側の統制状況も踏まえて扱う。","eEn":"External components should be checked for conformance and known risks before integration, considering the supplier's own controls."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの運用段階に関する管理策で求められることに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects what controls for the AI system operation stage require?","o":["運用中の性能・挙動を監視し逸脱に対応すること","運用開始後は一切変更を加えないこと","運用ログの取得を任意とすること","運用中の監視は契約で触れずに外部委託先へ暗黙に委ねること"],"oEn":["Monitoring performance and behavior in operation and responding to deviations","Making no changes at all after go-live","Making the capture of operational logs optional","Implicitly leaving monitoring during operation to an outsourcer, without touching on it in the contract"],"a":0,"e":"運用の管理策は、稼働中の性能・挙動を継続的に監視し、逸脱や劣化に対応することを求める。","eEn":"Operation controls require continuous monitoring of live performance and behavior, and responding to deviations or degradation."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI影響に関する管理策で『AIシステム影響評価』を実施する主な目的は？","qEn":"What is the main purpose of conducting an 'AI system impact assessment' under impact controls?","o":["従業員個人の人事評価における順位を決定すること","マーケティングのターゲット層を選定すること","クラウドの利用にかかる月々の費用を継続的に最適化し削減すること","利害関係者への潜在的な悪影響を体系的に特定・評価すること"],"oEn":["Determining an individual employee's ranking in the HR performance evaluation","To select target segments for marketing","Continuously optimizing and cutting the monthly costs incurred from the use of cloud services","To systematically identify and assess potential adverse effects on stakeholders"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価は、AIが利害関係者に及ぼしうる悪影響を体系的に特定・評価し、対応につなげるための管理策。","eEn":"Impact assessment is a control to systematically identify and evaluate potential adverse effects on stakeholders and drive responses."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの設計・開発に関する管理策が要求事項として組み込むよう求める代表例は？","qEn":"Which is a representative requirement that AI design and development controls call to be built in?","o":["セキュリティ・信頼性など非機能要求も設計に反映すること","開発期間中はいかなる文書も一切作成しないこと","機能要求のみを実装し他は後回しにすること","要求事項は文書化せず、担当者間の口頭合意のみで管理し続けること"],"oEn":["Reflecting non-functional requirements such as security and reliability in design","Never producing any documentation whatsoever during the development period","Implementing only functional requirements and deferring the rest","Continuing to manage requirements solely through verbal agreement between the people involved, never documenting them"],"a":0,"e":"設計・開発の管理策は、機能要求だけでなくセキュリティ・信頼性等の非機能要求も設計へ反映するよう求める。","eEn":"Design and development controls require reflecting non-functional requirements such as security and reliability, not only functional ones."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で、学習データと運用データの整合を保つ狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the aim of keeping training data and operational data aligned under data controls?","o":["データの保存に使うストレージの容量と運用コストを削減すること","管理画面上のデータの色分けを統一すること","契約するベンダーの数を意図的に増やすこと","分布のずれ（データドリフト）による性能劣化を防ぐこと"],"oEn":["Reducing both the capacity and the cost of the storage used to hold the data","Unifying the color-coding of data on the management screen","Deliberately increasing the number of vendors under contract","Preventing performance degradation in operation from distribution shift (data drift)"],"a":3,"e":"学習時と運用時のデータ分布のずれ（ドリフト）は性能劣化を招くため、整合の維持が管理策の狙いとなる。","eEn":"Drift between training and operational data distributions degrades performance, so maintaining alignment is a control aim."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者関係の管理策において『責任分担の明確化』が重要とされる主な理由は？","qEn":"In third-party relationship controls, why is 'clarifying the allocation of responsibilities' important?","o":["供給者への支払いをあえて遅延させるため","第三者による外部監査を意図的に回避するため","障害や不適合時に対応主体が曖昧になる事態を防ぐため","供給者と締結する契約書の条項と別紙の分量をあえて増やすため"],"oEn":["To deliberately delay payments to the supplier","To deliberately avoid an external audit by a third party","To prevent ambiguity over who responds when failures or nonconformities occur","To deliberately increase the volume of clauses in the contract concluded with the supplier"],"a":2,"e":"責任分担が曖昧だと障害時に対応主体が定まらないため、事前の明確化がリスク統制上重要となる。","eEn":"Ambiguous responsibility leaves no clear owner when failures occur, so clarifying it up front is important for risk control."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報の管理策が対象とする『人間による監督』の情報提供に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best matches the 'human oversight' information addressed by user information controls?","o":["利用者にモデルの重みを公開すること","利用者へ全ログを収めた物理媒体を毎月郵送で送付すること","利用者が結果を検証・介入できる方法を伝えること","利用者に開発費の内訳を示すこと"],"oEn":["Disclosing model weights to users","Sending users physical media containing all of the logs, by post","Informing users how they can review results and intervene","Showing users the breakdown of development costs"],"a":2,"e":"利用者向け情報の管理策には、結果の検証や必要時の介入など人間による監督を可能にする情報提供が含まれる。","eEn":"User information controls include providing information that enables human oversight, such as how to review results and intervene."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIライフサイクルの『退役（retirement）・廃止』段階に関する管理策で考慮すべきなのは？","qEn":"Which should be considered in controls for the 'retirement/decommissioning' stage of the AI lifecycle?","o":["退役後もモデルを無期限に稼働させ続けること","データやモデルの安全な処分と関係者への影響の管理","廃止判断を利用者に一任すること","退役の記録を残さないこと"],"oEn":["Keeping the model running indefinitely after retirement","Secure disposal of data and models and management of impacts on stakeholders","Delegating the retirement decision entirely to users","Leaving no record of retirement"],"a":1,"e":"退役段階の管理策は、データ・モデルの安全な処分や関係者への影響を適切に管理することを求める。","eEn":"Retirement-stage controls require secure disposal of data and models and proper management of impacts on stakeholders."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの管理策における『データの意図された用途の記述』が果たす役割に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the role of 'describing the intended use of data' in data controls?","o":["収集するデータの量を最大化すること","保有するデータをすべて匿名化したうえで保存すること","保有するデータをすべて暗号化すること","データを目的外に流用するリスクを抑えること"],"oEn":["Maximizing the volume of data collected","Anonymizing every piece of data that is held before it is stored","Encrypting all data that is held","Curbing the risk of using data beyond its intended purpose"],"a":3,"e":"意図された用途を明記することで、目的外利用（ファンクションクリープ）のリスクを抑制できる。","eEn":"Documenting intended use helps curb the risk of function creep, i.e. using data beyond its purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AI影響に関する管理策で、影響評価の結果を扱う望ましい方法に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects the desirable handling of impact assessment results under impact controls?","o":["評価の結果を関係者に一切共有せず、そのまま即時に破棄すること","結果の内容を営業目標に都合よく読み替えること","結果は評価者本人のみが記憶に留めておくこと","結果を文書化し、リスク対応や意思決定に反映すること"],"oEn":["Never sharing the result with anyone concerned and discarding it immediately, just as it is","Conveniently reinterpreting the result's content as a sales target","Having only the evaluator themself keep the result in memory","Documenting results and reflecting them in risk treatment and decisions"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価の結果は文書化し、リスク対応や設計・運用の意思決定に反映することで管理策として機能する。","eEn":"Impact assessment results should be documented and fed into risk treatment and design/operation decisions to function as a control."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"供給者管理の管理策で、AIサービスを外部に委託する際に契約へ含めるべき典型的な要素は？","qEn":"When outsourcing an AI service, which is a typical element to include in the contract under supplier controls?","o":["データの取扱い・セキュリティ・監査権などの要求事項","供給者の組織に所属する従業員個人の私的な連絡先と住所の一覧","供給者社内で毎月開催されるイベントの予定表","自社の内部監査チームが用いる監査チェックリストの記入様式"],"oEn":["Requirements on data handling, security and audit rights","A list of the private contact details of individual employees belonging to the supplier's organization","The schedule for events held internally at the supplier's company every month","The entry form of the audit checklist used by the organization's own internal audit team"],"a":0,"e":"外部委託契約には、データ取扱い・セキュリティ・監査権など、リスクを統制するための要求事項を含める。","eEn":"Outsourcing contracts should include requirements such as data handling, security and audit rights to control risk."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの技術文書に関する管理策の主な狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the main aim of controls on AI system technical documentation?","o":["作成する技術文書の量を競合他社より多くすること","技術者が書いた個人的なメモを非公開にすること","実際にかかった開発費と人件費の総額を対外的にすべて秘匿し続けること","設計・データ・評価結果を記録し理解と説明責任を支えること"],"oEn":["Producing a greater volume of technical documentation than a competitor","Keeping an engineer's personal notes undisclosed","Continuing to conceal from outside parties the total development costs and personnel costs actually incurred","Recording design, data and evaluation results to support understanding and accountability"],"a":3,"e":"技術文書の管理策は、設計・データ・評価等を記録し、システムの理解可能性と説明責任を支える。","eEn":"Technical documentation controls record design, data and evaluations to support understandability and accountability of the system."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で、ラベル付け（アノテーション）の品質を管理する狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the aim of managing labeling (annotation) quality under data controls?","o":["アノテーターの人数を最大化すること","ラベル付けの作業を、作業者も判定基準も記録せずに行うこと","ラベルの誤りがモデルの学習を歪めるのを防ぐこと","付与するラベルの表示色を統一すること"],"oEn":["Maximizing the number of annotators","Carrying out all labeling work without recording either the annotators or the criteria used","Preventing labeling errors from distorting model training","Unifying the display color of labels being assigned"],"a":2,"e":"ラベルの誤りは学習結果を歪めるため、アノテーション品質の管理はデータ管理策の重要な狙いとなる。","eEn":"Labeling errors distort learning, so managing annotation quality is a key aim of data controls."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報の管理策で、提供情報の『理解可能性』が重視される理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Why is 'understandability' of the provided information emphasized in user information controls?","o":["対象利用者が情報を正しく解釈し適切に行動できるようにするため","複数言語対応にかかる翻訳コストを大幅に削減するため","情報提供の義務をあくまで形式的にのみ満たし、理解できたかは確認しないため","利用者に提供する文書をあえて専門用語で難解にするため"],"oEn":["So that intended users can correctly interpret the information and act appropriately","To substantially reduce the translation costs involved in multi-language support","To satisfy the obligation to provide information only as a mere formality, never checking whether it was understood","To deliberately make the document provided to users hard to follow with technical jargon"],"a":0,"e":"提供情報は対象利用者が正しく解釈し適切に行動できてこそ意味を持つため、理解可能性が重視される。","eEn":"Provided information is meaningful only if intended users can interpret it correctly and act appropriately, so understandability matters."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIライフサイクル管理策における『変更管理』の狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the aim of 'change management' within AI lifecycle controls?","o":["運用開始後はモデルやデータへの変更をすべて禁止してしまうこと","変更内容を記録せず即時に反映してしまうこと","変更の可否判断を外部業者に丸投げすること","モデルやデータの変更が及ぼす影響を評価し統制すること"],"oEn":["Prohibiting every change to the model or the data once operation has begun","Applying changes immediately without recording their content","Leaving the decision on whether to change entirely to an external vendor","Assessing and controlling the impact of changes to models or data"],"a":3,"e":"変更管理は、モデル・データ・環境の変更が性能やリスクに及ぼす影響を評価し統制する狙いを持つ。","eEn":"Change management aims to assess and control the impact of changes to models, data or environment on performance and risk."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者関係の管理策で、供給者の履行状況を継続的に確認する意義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best captures the significance of continuously monitoring supplier performance in third-party controls?","o":["時間経過に伴うリスクや要求事項からの逸脱を早期に把握するため","供給者へ毎月支払う委託料の額を、正当な理由なく毎回見直して変更するため","供給者との契約期間をあえて不必要に長期化させるため","供給者に対して自社の社名を頻繁に変更させるため"],"oEn":["To detect risks and deviations from requirements over time early","To review and change, every single time and without any legitimate reason, the monthly fee paid to the supplier","To deliberately and unnecessarily prolong the contract term with the supplier","To have the supplier frequently change its own company name"],"a":0,"e":"供給者の履行は時間とともに変化しうるため、継続的な確認で逸脱やリスクの増大を早期に把握する。","eEn":"Supplier performance can change over time, so continuous monitoring detects deviations and rising risk early."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で、機密・個人データの取扱いに関して求められることに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Regarding sensitive or personal data, which best reflects what data controls require?","o":["個人データを匿名化せず自由に共有すること","データの取扱いに関する記録を作成しないこと","機密性の高い個人データを保護せずに学習用データへ最大限投入すること","適用される要求事項に沿って適切な保護と取扱いを行うこと"],"oEn":["Freely sharing personal data without anonymization","Not producing any record concerning the handling of the data","Feeding highly confidential personal data into the training data to the maximum extent, without protecting it","Applying appropriate protection and handling in line with applicable requirements"],"a":3,"e":"機密・個人データは、適用される法的・組織的要求事項に沿って適切に保護・取扱いすることが求められる。","eEn":"Sensitive or personal data must be appropriately protected and handled in line with applicable legal and organizational requirements."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの影響に関する管理策で、利害関係者からのフィードバックを扱う仕組みの狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"What is the aim of a mechanism to handle stakeholder feedback under AI impact controls?","o":["苦情を記録せずに処理を完了させること","利害関係者の連絡を遮断すること","寄せられたフィードバックを新規の営業機会の発掘にのみ利用すること","実運用で顕在化した影響を把握し是正につなげること"],"oEn":["To close cases without recording complaints","To block contact from stakeholders","To use the feedback received only for uncovering new sales opportunities","To capture impacts surfacing in real use and drive corrections"],"a":3,"e":"フィードバックの仕組みは、実運用で顕在化した影響を把握し是正・改善につなげる影響管理策の一部。","eEn":"A feedback mechanism captures impacts that surface in real use and drives corrective and improvement actions as part of impact controls."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの開発に関する管理策で『テスト』を要求する主な理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best explains why development controls require 'testing'?","o":["テスト担当者の作業量をいたずらに増やすため","AIシステムの開発期間を意図的に延長するため","提出する設計文書の見栄えだけをことさら良くして体裁を整えるため","リリース前に不具合や意図しない挙動を検出・是正するため"],"oEn":["To needlessly increase the workload of the testing staff","To deliberately extend the AI system's development period","To make only the appearance of the submitted design document look conspicuously better","To detect and correct defects and unintended behavior before release"],"a":3,"e":"テストは、リリース前に不具合や意図しない挙動を検出・是正し、品質と信頼性を確保するための管理策。","eEn":"Testing is a control to detect and correct defects and unintended behavior before release, ensuring quality and reliability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報の管理策で、システムの『意図された利用者・利用文脈』を示すことが役立つのは？","qEn":"Specifying the 'intended users and context of use' under user information controls helps to do what?","o":["利用するデータセンターの立地と回線の契約先を決定すること","想定外の利用者や文脈での不適切な使用を抑えること","採用する開発言語の選択を正当化すること","契約する供給者の価格を引き下げること"],"oEn":["Deciding the location of the data center to be used and which carrier to contract for lines","Curbing inappropriate use by unintended users or in unintended contexts","Justifying the choice of the development language adopted","Lowering the price charged by the contracted supplier"],"a":1,"e":"意図された利用者・文脈を示すことで、想定外の環境での不適切な使用を抑え、安全な利用を促す。","eEn":"Specifying intended users and context curbs inappropriate use in unforeseen settings and promotes safe use."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データに関する管理策で、データの選定基準を定めることの意義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best captures the significance of establishing data selection criteria under data controls?","o":["目的適合性や品質・偏りを踏まえ一貫した基準でデータを選べること","入手可能なデータをすべて無条件に採用できること","収集したすべてのデータの保存形式を統一できること","品質や偏りは問わず、必要なデータの取得作業をとにかく最速で完了できること"],"oEn":["Selecting data consistently based on fitness, quality and bias considerations","Adopting all available data unconditionally","Being able to unify the storage format of all the collected data","Being able to complete the work of acquiring the needed data at maximum speed, regardless of quality or bias"],"a":0,"e":"選定基準を定めることで、目的適合性・品質・偏りを踏まえた一貫したデータ選定が可能になる。","eEn":"Defining selection criteria enables consistent data selection informed by fitness, quality and bias considerations."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"第三者・顧客との関係に関する管理策で、AIの利用に関する情報や責任を顧客と共有する狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"In controls on relationships with third parties/customers, why share information and responsibilities about AI use with customers?","o":["顧客との契約の解除をことさら積極的に促し早期に打ち切るため","適切な利用と役割分担を促し誤用やリスクを抑えるため","顧客企業の内部情報をひそかに取得するため","AI利用に伴う追加費用を顧客に請求するため"],"oEn":["To conspicuously and actively encourage termination of the contract with the customer and end it early","To promote appropriate use and clear role-sharing and curb misuse and risk","To secretly obtain the internal information of the customer company","To bill the customer for additional costs arising from AI use"],"a":1,"e":"顧客との情報・責任の共有は、適切な利用と役割分担を促し、誤用やリスクの発生を抑える狙いを持つ。","eEn":"Sharing information and responsibilities with customers promotes appropriate use and role clarity, curbing misuse and risk."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIライフサイクル管理策で、各段階に判定基準（例：フェーズゲート）を設ける狙いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the aim of setting decision criteria (e.g., phase gates) at each stage under lifecycle controls?","o":["次の段階への移行を審査なしに無条件で承認し、開発を加速させること","各段階で求められる文書化を一律に省略すること","要件やリスク基準を満たさない状態での次段階移行を防ぐこと","各段階に置くべき判定責任者を意図的に減らすこと"],"oEn":["Approving the move to the next stage unconditionally without any review, so as to accelerate development","Uniformly omitting the documentation required at every stage","Preventing progression to the next stage when requirements or risk criteria are unmet","Deliberately reducing the decision-makers who ought to be placed at each stage"],"a":2,"e":"段階ごとの判定基準は、要件やリスク基準を満たさないまま次段階へ進むことを防ぐための管理策。","eEn":"Stage decision criteria prevent moving to the next phase before requirements or risk criteria are met."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの前処理に関する管理策で、特徴量エンジニアリングの記録が重要とされる理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Why is recording feature engineering important under preprocessing controls?","o":["データの前処理作業を高速化するため","特徴量の設計における開発者個人の裁量を無制限に広げるため","保存しておくデータ量を削減するため","モデル挙動の再現・説明・検証を可能にするため"],"oEn":["To speed up the data preprocessing work","To expand an individual developer's discretion over feature design without any limit","To reduce the volume of data kept in storage","To enable reproduction, explanation and verification of model behavior"],"a":3,"e":"特徴量の生成・変換を記録することで、モデル挙動の再現・説明・検証が可能となり透明性が高まる。","eEn":"Recording how features are created and transformed enables reproduction, explanation and verification of model behavior, improving transparency."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"利用者向け情報の管理策で提供が望まれる『インシデント時の連絡・対応方法』が支えるのは？","qEn":"What does providing 'how to report and respond to incidents' under user information controls support?","o":["提供する製品の価格改定を容易にすること","蓄積しておくデータ保存量を増やすこと","問題発生時に利用者が適切に通報・対応できること","新たな供給者を選定する際の手続きと審査を簡略化すること"],"oEn":["Making it easier to revise the price of the product offered","Increasing the volume of data kept in accumulated storage","Enabling users to report and respond appropriately when problems occur","Simplifying the procedure and the screening involved in selecting a new supplier"],"a":2,"e":"インシデント時の連絡・対応方法の提供は、問題発生時に利用者が適切に通報・対応できるよう支える。","eEn":"Providing incident reporting and response procedures supports users in reporting and responding appropriately when problems occur."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AIシステムの影響に関する管理策で、影響評価を『反復的に』見直す必要がある主な理由は？","qEn":"Why do impact controls require impact assessments to be revisited 'iteratively'?","o":["影響評価を担当する評価者を一定期間ごとに交代させるため","用途・データ・環境の変化で影響が変わりうるため","作成が必要な評価文書の量を増やすため","予定していた内部監査を先延ばしにするため"],"oEn":["To rotate out the evaluator in charge of the impact assessment at fixed intervals","Because impacts can change as use, data or environment change","To increase the volume of the assessment documentation that needs to be produced","To postpone an internal audit that had been scheduled"],"a":1,"e":"用途・データ・運用環境は時間とともに変化し影響も変わりうるため、影響評価は反復的に見直す必要がある。","eEn":"Use, data and operating environment change over time and so can impacts, so impact assessments must be revisited iteratively."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"供給者関係の管理策で、供給されたAIモデルの再学習や更新に関して重要な考慮事項に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Regarding retraining or updating a supplied AI model, which is a key consideration under supplier controls?","o":["モデルが更新されるたびに供給者を入札で頻繁に切り替えていくこと","更新が自組織のリスクや要求事項に与える影響を確認すること","実施した更新の内容についていっさい記録しないこと","更新を利用者に断りなく一方的に強制適用すること"],"oEn":["Frequently switching suppliers through competitive bidding every time the model is updated","Verifying the impact of updates on the organization's risks and requirements","Never recording anything at all about the content of an update that has been carried out","Unilaterally forcing an update onto users without notice"],"a":1,"e":"供給者側の再学習・更新は自組織のリスクや要求事項適合に影響しうるため、その影響確認が重要となる。","eEn":"A supplier's retraining or updates can affect the organization's risks and requirement conformance, so verifying their impact is key."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクアセスメントにおける『リスク特定（risk identification）』の主な狙いは？","qEn":"What is the main aim of 'risk identification' in AI risk assessment?","o":["AIに関連するリスク源・事象・原因・潜在的な結果を洗い出すこと","リスクを洗い出す前の段階で、すべてのリスクをただちに受容してしまうこと","特定作業に先立ち残留リスクの承認者を任命すること","特定より先に各リスクの金銭的損失額を確定すること"],"oEn":["To find and list risk sources, events, causes, and potential consequences related to AI","Accepting every risk immediately, at a stage before any of them have even been identified and listed","Appointing the approver of residual risk prior to the identification work","Fixing each risk's monetary loss amount before identification even occurs"],"a":0,"e":"リスク特定は、まずリスク源・事象・原因・結果を網羅的に洗い出す段階であり、評価や受容はその後に行う。","eEn":"Identification is the step of comprehensively surfacing risk sources, events, causes, and consequences; evaluation and acceptance come later."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"『リスク分析（risk analysis）』の段階で主に行うことは？","qEn":"What is primarily done during the 'risk analysis' stage?","o":["対応すべきリスクを組織方針で最終決定すること","リスクの特性を理解し、そのレベル（可能性と結果）を見積もること","分析の結果を待たずに新しいAIの用途をそのまま市場へ投入してしまうこと","分析したリスクの内容を意図的に一切文書化しないこと"],"oEn":["To make the final organizational decision on which risks to treat","To understand the nature of the risk and estimate its level (likelihood and consequence)","Launching a new AI use case onto the market as it is, without waiting for the results of the analysis","Deliberately never documenting the content of the risks that were analyzed"],"a":1,"e":"分析はリスクの性質を理解しそのレベルを見積もる段階。どのリスクを扱うかの決定は評価段階に属する。","eEn":"Analysis is about understanding the nature of a risk and estimating its level; deciding which risks to act on belongs to the evaluation stage."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"『リスク評価（risk evaluation）』の役割を最もよく表すのは？","qEn":"Which best describes the role of 'risk evaluation'?","o":["評価に先立ちリスク源を新たに発見し洗い出すこと","分析結果をリスク基準と照合し、対応の要否・優先度を決めること","AIモデルのハイパーパラメータを調整すること","発生した損失額の全額を保険会社へ直接請求して補填を受け、記録を閉じること"],"oEn":["Newly discovering and identifying risk sources prior to evaluation","To compare analysis results against risk criteria and decide whether and how urgently to treat","To tune the AI model's hyperparameters","Directly claiming the full amount of the resulting loss from an insurance company, receiving the payout and closing the record"],"a":1,"e":"評価は分析で得たリスクレベルをあらかじめ定めたリスク基準と比較し、対応の要否や優先順位を判断する段階。","eEn":"Evaluation compares the risk levels from analysis against predefined risk criteria to decide whether treatment is needed and its priority."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク対応（risk treatment）の選択肢のうち、『リスクの回避（avoidance）』に該当するのは？","qEn":"Which corresponds to 'risk avoidance' among risk treatment options?","o":["内容を評価したうえでリスクをそのまま保有し続け、活動も従来どおり継続する","民間の保険に加入してリスクを他者へ移転する","そのリスクを生じさせる活動を開始しない、または中止する","追加の管理策を導入してリスクの水準を低減する"],"oEn":["Continuing to retain the risk as is after evaluating its content, and carrying on the activity just as before","Taking out private insurance to transfer the risk to another party","Not starting or discontinuing the activity that gives rise to the risk","Introducing additional controls to reduce the level of risk"],"a":2,"e":"回避は、リスクを生む活動をそもそも行わない／やめる選択。移転・低減・保有はそれぞれ別の対応オプション。","eEn":"Avoidance means not undertaking or ceasing the risk-generating activity; transfer, reduction, and retention are distinct options."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク対応の選択肢としての『リスクの共有・移転（sharing/transfer）』の例に近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to an example of 'risk sharing/transfer' as a treatment option?","o":["入力値の検証を強化して発生するエラーの件数を減らす","リスクを受容して記録に残す","契約や保険により第三者とリスクを分担する","脆弱なAI機能の提供を取りやめる"],"oEn":["Strengthening input validation to reduce the number of errors that occur","Accepting the risk and recording it","Sharing the risk with a third party via contracts or insurance","Withdrawing a vulnerable AI feature"],"a":2,"e":"共有・移転は契約・保険などで第三者とリスクを分担する対応。取りやめは回避、検証強化は低減、受容は保有。","eEn":"Sharing/transfer distributes risk with a third party via contracts or insurance; withdrawal is avoidance, validation is reduction, and acceptance is retention."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク基準（risk criteria）はいつ定めるのが望ましいか？","qEn":"When should risk criteria preferably be established?","o":["外部監査で指摘を受けたときにのみ限って","すべての残留リスクを受容し終えてから初めて定める","リスク対応をすべて実施し終えた段階になって初めて","リスクアセスメントを始める前（プロセスの初期に）"],"oEn":["Only, and exclusively, when pointed out by an external audit","Only ever setting them after finishing acceptance of all residual risks","Only at the stage after finishing all risk treatment activities","Before starting risk assessment (early in the process)"],"a":3,"e":"リスク基準はアセスメント開始前に定めておくことで、リスクの重大性を一貫した尺度で評価できる。","eEn":"Setting risk criteria before assessment begins enables consistent judgment of risk significance."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの影響評価（impact assessment）とリスクアセスメントの主な違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best captures the main difference between an AI system impact assessment and a risk assessment?","o":["両者は用いられる呼び方が異なるだけで実質的な内容はまったく同一である","影響評価は個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響に焦点、リスクは組織目的に対する不確かさに焦点","リスクアセスメントは開発前のみ、影響評価は廃棄後にのみ実施するものである","影響評価は財務面の損益への影響のみを、リスクアセスメントは技術面の不具合のみを対象として扱うものである"],"oEn":["The two differ only in the name used, and their substantive content is completely identical","Impact assessment focuses on potential effects on individuals/groups/society, while risk focuses on uncertainty to organizational objectives","Risk assessment is performed only before development, and impact assessment only after disposal","The impact assessment covers only financial profit-and-loss impacts, while the risk assessment treats only technical defects as its subject matter, and the two never overlap"],"a":1,"e":"影響評価は個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響に着目し、リスクアセスメントは目的達成への不確かさに着目する。両者は補完的。","eEn":"Impact assessment centers on potential effects on people and society, while risk assessment centers on uncertainty to objectives; they are complementary."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク所有者（risk owner）に割り当てられる主な責任は？","qEn":"What is the main responsibility assigned to a risk owner?","o":["あらゆる利害関係者から個別に毎回同意を得ること","特定のリスクとその対応を管理する説明責任・権限をもつこと","作成した内部監査報告書を外部へ広く公表すること","AIモデルの学習用コードと前処理のコードを自らすべて実装すること"],"oEn":["Obtaining individual consent from every interested party each and every time","To hold the accountability and authority to manage a specific risk and its treatment","Widely publishing the internal audit report that was produced to the outside","Personally implementing all of the AI model's training code and its preprocessing code as well"],"a":1,"e":"リスク所有者は特定リスクとその対応を管理する説明責任と権限をもつ役割で、実装作業者とは限らない。","eEn":"A risk owner holds the accountability and authority to manage a specific risk and its treatment, not necessarily the implementer."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"残留リスク（residual risk）の定義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the definition of 'residual risk'?","o":["対応前の当初のリスクの全量","リスク対応を実施した後になお残るリスク","リスク対応の前に特定されなかった未知のリスクのみ","リスク基準そのもの"],"oEn":["The full original risk before any treatment","The risk that remains after risk treatment has been applied","Only the unknown risks that were never identified before risk treatment","The risk criteria themselves"],"a":1,"e":"残留リスクは対応実施後になお残るリスクを指す。当初リスクや基準そのものとは異なる。","eEn":"Residual risk is what remains after treatment has been applied, distinct from the original risk or the criteria."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"残留リスクの受容（acceptance）について適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is appropriate regarding acceptance of residual risk?","o":["誰の承認も要らず暗黙に受容してよい","開発者が個人的判断で口頭承認すれば十分","権限をもつ者が承認し、その決定を記録・保持する","いったん受容した残留リスクは状況が変わっても見直してはならない"],"oEn":["It can be accepted implicitly without anyone's approval","Verbal approval at a developer's personal discretion is sufficient","An authorized person approves it and the decision is recorded and retained","Once residual risk has been accepted, it must never be reviewed again even if circumstances change"],"a":2,"e":"残留リスクは権限者による承認と、その決定の文書化・保持が求められる。受容後も変化に応じ見直す。","eEn":"Residual risk requires approval by an authorized person and documented, retained decisions, and remains subject to later review."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクアセスメントを『反復（iterative）』に行う主な理由に最も近いのは？","qEn":"What is closest to the main reason for performing AI risk assessment iteratively?","o":["データ・モデル・用途・環境の変化に応じてリスク像が変わるから","外部の審査機関が定期的に行う監査を回避するため","一度アセスメントを実施すれば用途が変わっても永久に有効であり続けるから","作成する文書の量を増やすことそのものが目的だから"],"oEn":["Because the risk picture changes with data, model, use, and environment","To avoid the periodic audit conducted by an external certification body","Because once an assessment has been performed, it remains valid forever even if the use changes","Because increasing the volume of documentation produced is itself the goal"],"a":0,"e":"AIはデータ・モデル・用途・運用環境が変化しやすく、リスク像も変わるため反復的な再評価が必要。","eEn":"AI's data, model, use, and operating environment change over time, shifting the risk picture and requiring iterative reassessment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク基準を構成しうる要素として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is most appropriate as an element that risk criteria may comprise?","o":["リスクの重大性を測る尺度と、受容可能なリスクレベル","内部監査を実施する対象部門の一覧と、各監査報告書の提出先","マーケティング部門の広告クリック率目標","契約しているAIベンダーのブランドカラー"],"oEn":["A scale to measure risk significance and the acceptable level of risk","A list of the departments subject to internal audit and where each audit report is submitted","The marketing department's advertising click-through-rate target","The brand color of the contracted AI vendor"],"a":0,"e":"リスク基準には、リスクの重大性を評価する尺度や受容可能なリスクレベルなどが含まれる。","eEn":"Risk criteria include the scale for judging risk significance and the level of risk considered acceptable."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AI固有のリスク源として特に考慮すべきものに近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to an AI-specific risk source that deserves particular consideration?","o":["サーバ室の入退室記録の保管期間と物理鍵の受け渡し手順が未整備であること","社内ネットワークの通信帯域の不足とバックアップ装置の老朽化による停止","文書管理システムにおける版管理の不徹底と、承認記録の保管期間が短すぎること","学習データの偏りや品質、モデルの不透明性、自動的意思決定の影響"],"oEn":["That the retention period for server-room entry logs and the handover procedure for physical keys are not established","Insufficient bandwidth on the internal network and outages caused by the ageing of the backup equipment","Lax version control in the document management system and the short retention period for approval records","Bias/quality of training data, model opacity, and the effects of automated decision-making"],"a":3,"e":"AIでは学習データの偏り・品質、モデルの不透明性、自動的意思決定の影響などがリスク源として重要。","eEn":"For AI, training-data bias/quality, model opacity, and impacts of automated decisions are key risk sources."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスクアセスメントの結果に関して適切な扱いは？","qEn":"What is the appropriate handling of risk assessment results?","o":["結果はそのつどすべて破棄し評価を毎回ゼロからやり直す","文書化された情報として保持し、必要に応じて更新・参照できるようにする","アセスメントの結果は関係者への口頭での共有のみとし、記録はいっさい残さない","結果は担当者個人の手元にあるメモにのみひそかに保存する"],"oEn":["Discarding all the results each time and redoing the evaluation from scratch every time","Retain them as documented information, updatable and referenceable as needed","Sharing the assessment result only verbally with those concerned and keeping no record of it whatsoever","Secretly saving the result only in the individual staff member's own personal notes"],"a":1,"e":"アセスメント結果は文書化された情報として保持し、変化に応じて更新・参照できるようにする。","eEn":"Assessment results should be retained as documented information that can be updated and referenced as conditions change."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク分析で『リスクレベル（level of risk）』を求める一般的な考え方に近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the general approach to determining the 'level of risk' in analysis?","o":["リスクレベルの評価結果を、発生可能性とは無関係にその日の気温だけで決めてしまう","発生しうるすべての結果の中から、発生の可能性をまったく考慮せずに常に最大の被害額のみを機械的に採用してしまう","リスクレベルの数値を何の分析も行わずに偶然やくじ引きに任せて割り当ててしまう","結果（consequence）の大きさと発生の可能性（likelihood）を組み合わせて見積もる"],"oEn":["Deciding the risk-level evaluation result based only on that day's temperature, unrelated to the likelihood of occurrence","Mechanically adopting only the maximum damage amount among all possible consequences, every time, without considering the likelihood of occurrence at all","Assigning the risk-level figure by leaving it to chance or a lottery, without performing any analysis at all","Estimate it by combining the magnitude of consequence with the likelihood of occurrence"],"a":3,"e":"リスクレベルは、結果（consequence）の大きさと発生の可能性（likelihood）を組み合わせて見積もる。発生可能性を考えずに最大の被害額だけを採用することや、くじ引きで割り当てること、その日の気温で決めることは分析とは言えない。","eEn":"The level of risk is estimated by combining the magnitude of the consequence with the likelihood of occurrence. Using only the largest loss while ignoring likelihood, assigning numbers by lottery, or basing it on the day's temperature is not risk analysis."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク対応計画（risk treatment plan）に含めるべき内容に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to what a risk treatment plan should include?","o":["内部監査で用いる監査基準の一覧と、監査員に求められる力量と経験の要件","競合他社の将来の株価動向に関する詳細な予測資料","選択した対応、担当・責任、必要資源、実施時期などの計画事項","AIチップに関する物理的な回路設計図そのもの一式"],"oEn":["A list of the audit criteria used in internal audits and the competence requirements demanded of auditors","A detailed forecast document concerning a competitor's future stock price trends","The selected treatment, responsibilities, required resources, and timing","The complete set of physical circuit design drawings for the AI chip itself"],"a":2,"e":"対応計画には、選択した対応・責任者・必要資源・実施時期などを含め、実行と追跡を可能にする。","eEn":"A treatment plan includes the chosen treatment, responsibilities, resources, and timing to enable execution and tracking."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスクアセスメントとAIシステム管理策（controls）の関係に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best captures the relationship between risk assessment and AI system controls?","o":["評価の結果が高リスクであるほど管理策を一切設けなくてよい","適用する管理策とリスクアセスメントは完全に無関係である","アセスメント結果が、どの管理策を適用・実装するかの判断根拠になる","管理策はアセスメントを行う前にあらかじめランダムに選び、以後は見直さない"],"oEn":["The higher the evaluated risk, the less any control needs to be put in place at all","The controls to apply and the risk assessment are entirely unrelated","Assessment results inform which controls to apply and implement","Controls should be chosen randomly in advance, before the assessment is carried out, and never revisited"],"a":2,"e":"リスクアセスメントの結果は、どの管理策を適用・実装するかを判断する根拠になる。管理策をアセスメント前にランダムに選んで見直さない運用や、高リスクほど管理策を設けなくてよいとする考えは誤りで、両者は無関係でもない。","eEn":"The results of risk assessment are the basis for deciding which controls to apply and implement. Picking controls at random before assessment and never revisiting them, or setting none for higher risks, is wrong, and the two are not unrelated."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク所有者（risk owner）と管理策所有者（control owner）の違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the difference between a risk owner and a control owner?","o":["管理策所有者という役割はリスクに関するいかなる問題も一切扱わず、管理策の運用状況にも責任を負わないとされている","リスク所有者と管理策所有者はいかなる場合も必ず同一人物でなければならない","リスク所有者はリスク全体の管理に説明責任をもち、管理策所有者は特定の管理策の運用に責任をもつ","リスク所有者という役割自体は本来存在せず管理策所有者のみを置いておけばよい"],"oEn":["The control-owner role is held never to deal with any risk-related matter whatsoever, and to bear no responsibility for how the control is operated either","The risk owner and the control owner must, in every case, always be the same person","The risk owner is accountable for managing the risk overall, while the control owner is responsible for operating a specific control","The role of risk owner does not inherently exist at all; only a control owner needs to be appointed"],"a":2,"e":"リスク所有者はリスク管理の説明責任を負い、管理策所有者は個別管理策の運用責任を負う。両者は役割が異なる。","eEn":"The risk owner is accountable for managing the risk, while a control owner is responsible for operating a particular control; the roles differ."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"次のうち、リスク対応の4つの一般的選択肢に『含まれない』ものは？","qEn":"Which of the following is NOT among the four common risk treatment options?","o":["リスクを生む活動自体を回避すること","リスクの発生確率を意図的に隠蔽し記録しないこと","リスクの水準を段階的に低減すること","リスクを保険等で共有・移転すること"],"oEn":["Avoiding the very activity that gives rise to the risk","Deliberately concealing the risk's likelihood and leaving it unrecorded","Progressively reducing the level of the risk","Sharing or transferring the risk, such as via insurance"],"a":1,"e":"一般的な対応は回避・低減・共有(移転)・保有(受容)。確率の隠蔽は正当な対応ではなく不適切。","eEn":"Common options are avoid, reduce, share/transfer, and retain/accept; concealing likelihood is not a legitimate treatment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスクアセスメントの再実施を促す『トリガー』として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate 'trigger' prompting re-performance of a risk assessment?","o":["モデルの再学習・用途拡大・新たな法規制やインシデントの発生","毎年恒例となっている社員旅行の日程と宿泊先の予約をまとめて調整すること","適用宣言書の書式が最新の様式に差し替えられ、体裁だけが変わること","内部監査の報告書の配付先の一覧に新しい部署名が一つだけ加わること"],"oEn":["Model retraining, expanded use, new regulation, or an incident","Coordinating the schedule for the customary annual employee trip and the accommodation bookings","The Statement of Applicability's form being swapped for the latest template, changing only its appearance","One new department name being added to the distribution list for the internal audit report"],"a":0,"e":"モデル再学習・用途拡大・法規制やインシデントなど、リスク像を変えうる変化は再評価のトリガーになる。","eEn":"Changes that can alter the risk picture—retraining, expanded use, new regulation, incidents—trigger reassessment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク分析における『定性的（qualitative）』手法の特徴に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best characterizes a 'qualitative' method in risk analysis?","o":["高・中・低などの記述的尺度で数値を用いずリスクレベルを表現する","発生確率という要素を一切考慮に入れない","必ず金銭的な金額の精密な計算のみを用いる","リスクの結果はいかなる場合も評価してはならないと定める"],"oEn":["Expressing risk levels with descriptive scales such as high/medium/low rather than numbers","Never takes the factor of likelihood into account at all","Always uses only precise monetary calculations","Stipulates that a risk's consequence must never be evaluated under any circumstances"],"a":0,"e":"定性的手法は高・中・低のような記述的尺度でリスクレベルを表す。定量的手法は数値を用いる。","eEn":"Qualitative methods express risk levels with descriptive scales like high/medium/low, whereas quantitative methods use numeric values."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスク基準を組織全体で一貫させる意義に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the significance of keeping risk criteria consistent across the organization?","o":["各担当者がそれぞれ独自の尺度で判断し、システム間でリスクの大きさを比較不能にしてしまうため","実際のリスクの水準を経営層や監査員に対して常に低く見せかけるため","提出する文書の記述をあえて複雑にして監査自体を難しくするため","異なるAIシステム間でリスクの重大性を比較・優先順位付けできるようにするため"],"oEn":["Because each person in charge judges by their own scale, making the magnitude of risk impossible to compare across systems","To always make the actual level of risk appear lower than it is to management and auditors","To deliberately make the wording of submitted documents complex and make the audit itself difficult","So risk significance can be compared and prioritized across different AI systems"],"a":3,"e":"一貫したリスク基準により、異なるAIシステム間でもリスクを比較し優先順位を付けられる。","eEn":"Consistent risk criteria let risks be compared and prioritized across different AI systems."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価とリスクアセスメントを統合的に運用する利点に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to a benefit of operating impact assessment and risk assessment in an integrated way?","o":["一度実施した評価であれば二度と更新しなくてよくなってしまうこと","個人・社会への影響と組織目的への不確かさを相互に参照し、抜け漏れを減らせること","影響評価とリスクアセスメントを完全に切り離して別々に行い、両者の間で情報を一切共有しないこと","評価やアセスメントを担当する責任者をあえて置かずに済ませられること"],"oEn":["Once an evaluation has been performed, never needing to update it again at all","Cross-referencing effects on people/society and uncertainty to objectives to reduce gaps","Completely separating the impact assessment from the risk assessment, performing them apart and sharing no information at all between them","Being able to deliberately dispense with appointing anyone responsible for the evaluation or assessment"],"a":1,"e":"影響評価とリスクアセスメントを相互参照することで、人・社会への影響と目的への不確かさを統合的に捉え、見落としを減らせる。","eEn":"Cross-referencing the two lets the organization view effects on people/society alongside uncertainty to objectives, reducing blind spots."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リスクアセスメントのプロセス全体の一般的な順序に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the general order of the overall risk assessment process?","o":["対応 → 受容 → 特定 → 分析（対応から始め最後に分析する順序）","受容 → 分析 → 特定 → 評価","分析 → 特定 → 対応 → 評価","特定 → 分析 → 評価（→ その後に対応）"],"oEn":["Treatment → acceptance → identification → analysis (starting from treatment, analyzing last)","Acceptance → analysis → identification → evaluation","Analysis → identification → treatment → evaluation","Identification → analysis → evaluation (→ then treatment)"],"a":3,"e":"リスクアセスメントは特定→分析→評価の順で行い、その結果に基づいて対応を実施する。","eEn":"Risk assessment proceeds identification → analysis → evaluation, and treatment follows based on the results."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ISO/IEC 42001 における「AIシステム影響評価」の主眼として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the primary focus of an 'AI system impact assessment' in ISO/IEC 42001?","o":["個人・集団・社会に対してAIシステムが及ぼしうる影響を体系的に特定・評価すること","開発チーム内の個々のメンバーが持つ生産性指標のみを測定すること","AIシステムが推論結果を出力するまでの応答速度とスループットそのものを最適化して短縮すること","組織における四半期ごとの売上への財務的な影響のみを予測すること"],"oEn":["Systematically identifying and evaluating the potential impacts of the AI system on individuals, groups, and society","Measuring only the productivity metrics of each individual member of the development team","Optimizing and shortening the very response speed and throughput with which the AI system outputs its inference results, and nothing else","Forecasting only the financial impact on the organization's quarterly revenue figures"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価は技術性能や財務ではなく、個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響の特定と評価を主眼とする。","eEn":"Impact assessment focuses on identifying and evaluating potential effects on individuals, groups, and society, not on technical performance or finance."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステム影響評価の「対象範囲（スコープ）」を最初に定める理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is defining the 'scope' of an AI system impact assessment an important first step?","o":["競合他社が市場に提供している製品の詳細な仕様と価格の一覧をひとつずつ比較していくため","どのシステム・利用状況・影響を受ける主体を評価対象に含めるかを明確にするため","影響評価の実施に用いるプログラミング言語をあらかじめ選定するため","次期に向けたマーケティング部門の予算を新たに割り当てるためだけに行う"],"oEn":["To compare, one by one, the lists of detailed specifications and prices of the products a competitor offers on the market","To clarify which systems, contexts of use, and affected parties are included in the assessment","To select, in advance, the programming language used to carry out the impact assessment","Carried out solely to newly allocate the marketing department's budget for the coming term"],"a":1,"e":"スコープの明確化により、対象システム・利用状況・影響を受ける主体の範囲が定まり、評価の抜け漏れを防げる。","eEn":"Defining scope clarifies which systems, contexts, and affected parties are covered, preventing gaps in the assessment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価において「利用状況（context of use）」を考慮すべき理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why should the 'context of use' be considered in an impact assessment?","o":["利用状況の違いは実装するソースコードの行数に直接影響するから","利用状況の違いだけがサーバーの運用費用と保守費用の総額のすべてを決めてしまうものだから","利用状況はどの案件であっても常に無視してよい一定の定数だから","同じAIシステムでも用途・利用者・環境が変われば生じる影響が大きく変わるから"],"oEn":["Because differences in the context of use directly affect the number of lines of source code implemented","Because differences in the context of use alone determine the entirety of the server's operating and maintenance costs, and nothing else does","Because the context of use is a fixed constant that may always be ignored in any project","Because the same AI system can produce very different impacts depending on purpose, users, and environment"],"a":3,"e":"同一システムでも用途・利用者・運用環境が異なれば影響が変化するため、利用状況を踏まえた評価が必要。","eEn":"The same system can have very different impacts depending on purpose, users, and environment, so context of use must be assessed."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの「プライバシー影響」を評価する際に最も直接的に関係する事項はどれか？","qEn":"Which is most directly relevant when assessing the 'privacy impact' of an AI system?","o":["AIモデルの学習全体を通じてトータルで要した時間","モデルの学習に用いるGPUの一日あたりの消費電力量と冷却にかかる効率","利用者が操作するアプリ画面のUIカラーテーマ設定","個人データの収集・利用・保存・共有が個人の権利に及ぼす影響"],"oEn":["The total time required across the entire training of the AI model","The daily amount of power consumed by the GPU used to train the model and the efficiency of its cooling","The UI color-theme setting of the app screen users interact with","How the collection, use, storage, and sharing of personal data affects individuals' rights"],"a":3,"e":"プライバシー影響評価は、個人データの取扱いが個人の権利・自由に与える影響に着目する。","eEn":"Privacy impact assessment focuses on how the handling of personal data affects individuals' rights and freedoms."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの「安全影響（safety impact）」の例として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the best example of a 'safety impact' of an AI system?","o":["システムが出力するログファイルの命名規則とタイムスタンプ形式が不統一であること","医療診断支援AIの誤出力が患者の身体的危害につながりうること","毎週開催される定例の社内会議の議事録が毎回長すぎること","スマートフォンアプリで使用するアイコンの解像度が低いこと"],"oEn":["The naming convention and the timestamp format of the log files output by the system being inconsistent with each other","An erroneous output from a diagnostic-support AI potentially leading to physical harm to a patient","The minutes of a weekly regular internal meeting being too long every time","The resolution of icons used in the smartphone app being low"],"a":1,"e":"安全影響は人の身体・生命・健康への危害の可能性に関わる。医療AIの誤出力による危害はその典型例。","eEn":"Safety impact concerns potential harm to people's body, life, or health; harm from a medical AI's erroneous output is a typical example."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムがもたらす「集団（グループ）への影響」を評価する意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is it meaningful to assess impacts on 'groups' from an AI system?","o":["評価対象となる集団に属している人々全員の平均年齢と居住地域の分布を集計して算出するため","特定の属性を持つ集団に向けた割引価格を新たに設定するため","特定の属性を持つ集団が持つSNSのフォロワー数を増やすため","特定の属性を持つ集団に不公平・差別的な結果が集中していないかを把握するため"],"oEn":["To tabulate and calculate the average age and the distribution of residential areas of every person belonging to the group being evaluated","To newly set a discounted price aimed at a group sharing a specific attribute","To increase the number of social-media followers a group sharing a specific attribute has","To detect whether unfair or discriminatory outcomes are concentrated on groups sharing certain attributes"],"a":3,"e":"個人単位では見えにくい、特定属性の集団に偏る不公平・差別的影響を把握するために集団影響の評価が重要。","eEn":"Assessing group impacts reveals unfair or discriminatory effects concentrated on groups with certain attributes that may be invisible at the individual level."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの「バイアス影響」を評価する目的として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the purpose of assessing the 'bias impact' of an AI system?","o":["推論を実行するAPIエンドポイントの応答時間と待ち行列の長さをわずかに短縮すること","学習済みモデルのファイルサイズをできるだけ小さくすること","利用者が使うアプリのUIに多言語対応の機能を追加すること","不当な偏りが特定の個人・集団に不利益を与えていないかを明らかにすること"],"oEn":["Slightly shortening the response time and the queue length of the API endpoint that executes inference","Making the file size of a trained model as small as possible","Adding multilingual support functionality to the UI of the app that users use","Revealing whether unfair bias disadvantages particular individuals or groups"],"a":3,"e":"バイアス影響評価は、不当な偏りが特定の個人・集団に不利益を及ぼしていないかを明らかにすることを目的とする。","eEn":"Bias impact assessment aims to reveal whether unfair bias causes disadvantage to particular individuals or groups."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価と「リスクアセスメント」の関係として最も適切な説明はどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the relationship between impact assessment and 'risk assessment'?","o":["影響評価はリスクアセスメントを禁止する","両者は同一で、どちらか一方を行えばもう一方は不要になる","影響評価はリスクアセスメントの完了後にのみ許可され、結果を互いに参照しない単独作業である","影響評価の結果はリスクの特定・分析の入力として活用され、両者は補完的に機能する"],"oEn":["Impact assessment prohibits risk assessment","They are identical, so performing one makes the other unnecessary","Impact assessment is a standalone task permitted only after the risk assessment is complete, and the two never reference each other's results","The results of impact assessment feed into risk identification and analysis, and the two are complementary"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価で把握した潜在的影響はリスクの特定・分析の入力となり、両者は補完的に連携する。","eEn":"Potential impacts identified in impact assessment feed into risk identification and analysis; the two are complementary."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステム影響評価を「文書化」して維持すべき主な理由はどれか？","qEn":"Why should an AI system impact assessment be 'documented' and maintained?","o":["適用宣言書に記載する管理策の数を増やし、認証審査での指摘件数を少しでも減らすため","作成した評価文書をそのままマーケティング資料として外部の顧客に販売できるようになるから","評価の前提・判断根拠・結果を追跡可能にし、説明責任とレビューを支えるため","作成する文書の分量が多ければ多いほど監査で高評価になるから"],"oEn":["In order to increase the number of controls listed in the Statement of Applicability and thereby reduce findings at the certification audit","Because the assessment documents produced can be sold, just as they are, to external customers as marketing material","To make the assumptions, rationale, and results traceable, supporting accountability and review","Because the greater the volume of documentation produced, the higher the audit evaluation becomes"],"a":2,"e":"文書化により前提・根拠・結果が追跡可能になり、説明責任の確保や後続のレビュー・更新を支える。","eEn":"Documentation makes assumptions, rationale, and results traceable, supporting accountability and later review or update."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価で「影響を受ける利害関係者（affected stakeholders）」を特定する意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is identifying 'affected stakeholders' important in an impact assessment?","o":["評価を担当する要員に必要な力量と、その教育訓練の実施記録をそろえておくため","特定した利害関係者へ広告メールを一斉送信するため","誰にどのような影響が及ぶかを踏まえて評価と対応を適切に行うため","競合他社が提供している製品の市場シェアと販売価格の推移を詳しく推計するため"],"oEn":["To put in order the competence required of the personnel performing the assessment and their training records","To send a mass advertising email to the identified interested parties","To perform assessment and treatment appropriately based on who is affected and how","To closely estimate the market share of a product a competitor offers and how its selling price has moved"],"a":2,"e":"影響を受ける主体を特定することで、誰にどのような影響が及ぶかを踏まえた適切な評価・対応が可能になる。","eEn":"Identifying affected parties enables appropriate assessment and treatment based on who is affected and how."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの「社会への影響」の例として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the best example of a 'societal impact' of an AI system?","o":["広く使われる推薦システムが世論形成や情報アクセスに影響を及ぼすこと","アプリケーションのビルド処理が更新のたびに毎回数秒ずつ遅くなっていくこと","開発環境で使う特定のAPIキーの有効期限が切れること","ソースコード内で使われる内部変数の命名が長すぎること"],"oEn":["A widely used recommendation system influencing public opinion or access to information","The application's build process becoming a few seconds slower every single time it is updated","A specific API key used in the development environment expiring","The naming of internal variables used within the source code being too long"],"a":0,"e":"社会的影響は、個人・集団を超えて社会全体（世論・情報アクセス等）に及ぶ広範な影響を指す。","eEn":"Societal impact refers to broad effects reaching society at large (e.g., public opinion, access to information) beyond individuals and groups."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価を実施するタイミングとして最も適切な考え方はどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate view on when to conduct an impact assessment?","o":["設計・開発の早い段階から行い、重要な変更時に見直す","リリースの当日に一度だけ実施し、その後は変更があっても行わない","影響評価は任意で全く実施しなくてよい","システムを廃棄した後にのみ実施する"],"oEn":["Conduct it early in design and development and revisit it upon significant changes","Performing it only once on release day and never again thereafter, even when changes occur","Impact assessment is optional and need not be performed at all","Only after the system has been decommissioned"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価はライフサイクルの早期から実施し、重要な変更が生じたときに見直すことが望ましい。","eEn":"Impact assessment should begin early in the lifecycle and be revisited when significant changes occur."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価における「潜在的な便益」と「潜在的な害」を併せて検討する理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why should both 'potential benefits' and 'potential harms' be considered together in an impact assessment?","o":["便益と害はまったく無関係なので、どちらもそれぞれ別々に無視してよいため","便益と害の双方を踏まえてバランスの取れた判断と対応を行うため","便益のみを記録して害は文書化しないため","害だけを見ると評価が早く終わるため"],"oEn":["Because benefits and harms are entirely unrelated, so each of them may simply be ignored separately","To make balanced decisions and treatment considering both benefits and harms","To record only benefits and never document harms","Because looking only at harms finishes the assessment faster"],"a":1,"e":"便益と害の双方を踏まえることで、偏りのないバランスの取れた判断と対応が可能になる。","eEn":"Considering both benefits and harms enables balanced, unbiased decisions and treatment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"「影響を受ける個人」に対する影響評価で特に重視される観点はどれか？","qEn":"Which perspective is especially emphasized when assessing impacts on 'affected individuals'?","o":["評価対象となる個人のデバイスのバッテリー残量","評価対象となる個人のタイピング速度","評価対象の個人が普段使うブラウザの種類","個人の権利・自由・尊厳・公平な取扱いへの影響"],"oEn":["The remaining battery level of the device belonging to the individual being evaluated","The typing speed of the individual being evaluated","The type of browser the individual being evaluated ordinarily uses","Effects on the individual's rights, freedoms, dignity, and fair treatment"],"a":3,"e":"個人への影響評価では、個人の権利・自由・尊厳や公平な取扱いへの影響が中心となる。デバイスのバッテリー残量やタイピング速度、普段使うブラウザの種類は、個人が受ける影響の評価に関係しない。","eEn":"Impact assessment for individuals centres on effects on their rights, freedoms, dignity and fair treatment. Device battery level, typing speed, or the browser they usually use have no bearing on evaluating the impact on individuals."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の結果、重大な潜在的影響が特定された場合の適切な対応として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"When an impact assessment identifies a significant potential impact, what is the most appropriate response?","o":["リスクアセスメントや対応（低減・回避等）に反映し、必要な管理策を検討する","評価結果をそのまま破棄して開発を予定どおり進めてしまう","評価の結果を非公開の個人的なメモにのみ残し、組織内の誰とも一切共有しないでおくこと","影響を受ける主体への配慮という手続きをすべて省略してしまう"],"oEn":["Feed it into risk assessment and treatment (mitigation, avoidance, etc.) and consider necessary controls","Simply discarding the assessment result and proceeding with development as originally planned","Keeping the assessment result only in an undisclosed personal note and never sharing it with anyone within the organization at all","Omitting entirely the procedure of giving consideration to the affected parties"],"a":0,"e":"特定された重大な影響はリスクアセスメント・対応に反映し、適切な管理策の検討につなげる必要がある。","eEn":"Significant identified impacts should feed into risk assessment and treatment, leading to appropriate controls."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステム影響評価を支援する国際規格として最も関連が深いのはどれか？","qEn":"Which international standard is most directly related to supporting AI system impact assessment?","o":["ISO 9001（品質マネジメントシステム）","ISO/IEC 42005（AIシステム影響評価のガイダンス）","ISO 50001（エネルギーマネジメント）","ISO 14001（組織の環境側面を扱う環境マネジメントシステムの規格）"],"oEn":["ISO 9001 (Quality management systems)","ISO/IEC 42005 (Guidance on AI system impact assessment)","ISO 50001 (Energy management)","ISO 14001 (Environmental management systems, covering an organization's environmental aspects)"],"a":1,"e":"ISO/IEC 42005 はAIシステム影響評価の実施に関するガイダンスを提供し、42001の実装を支援する。","eEn":"ISO/IEC 42005 provides guidance on conducting AI system impact assessments, supporting the implementation of ISO/IEC 42001."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価で「意図された使用」と「合理的に予見可能な誤用」の双方を考慮する理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why should an impact assessment consider both 'intended use' and 'reasonably foreseeable misuse'?","o":["意図された使用だけを見れば十分だから","誤用の検討はコストが高いので常に省略すべきだから","現実には想定外・不適切な使われ方でも影響が生じうるため","誤用は絶対に起こらないので、形式的に一文を書くだけで十分なため"],"oEn":["Because considering only intended use is sufficient","Because considering misuse is costly and should always be omitted","Because impacts can arise from unforeseen or improper use in reality","Because misuse never happens at all, so writing a single formal sentence about it is enough"],"a":2,"e":"実運用では意図外・不適切な使われ方が起こりうるため、予見可能な誤用も評価対象に含める。","eEn":"Because unintended or improper use can occur in practice, reasonably foreseeable misuse must also be assessed."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価において影響の「深刻度」と「発生可能性」を検討する目的として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the purpose of considering the 'severity' and 'likelihood' of impacts in an impact assessment?","o":["影響の重要度を相対的に判断し、優先順位付けと対応の意思決定を支えるため","関係するすべての利害関係者の詳しい連絡先情報と所属先の一覧を収集して整理するため","開発チームが今後新たに採用する予定の開発言語を決定するため","提出する評価文書のページ数をとにかく多く水増しするため"],"oEn":["To judge the relative significance of impacts and support prioritization and treatment decisions","To collect and organize a list of the detailed contact information and affiliations of every relevant interested party","To decide on the development language the development team plans to newly adopt going forward","To pad out, above all else, the number of pages in the submitted assessment document"],"a":0,"e":"深刻度と発生可能性を組み合わせて評価することで、影響の重要度を判断し優先順位付けと対応判断につなげられる。","eEn":"Combining severity and likelihood helps gauge the significance of impacts, supporting prioritization and treatment decisions."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AIシステムの用途変更（例：内部業務用から一般消費者向けへ）が生じたときの影響評価の扱いとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"How should impact assessment be handled when an AI system's use changes (e.g., from internal use to consumer-facing)?","o":["過去の評価を修正せずそのまま流用する","用途変更は影響評価に無関係なので何もしない","一度承認された評価は用途が変わっても永久に有効なので更新は不要である","新たな利用状況・利用者・影響を踏まえて影響評価を見直す"],"oEn":["Reuse the past assessment unchanged","Do nothing, since a change of use is irrelevant to impact assessment","Once approved, an assessment is valid forever even if the use changes, so no update is needed","Revisit the impact assessment in light of the new context, users, and impacts"],"a":3,"e":"用途変更は利用状況・利用者・生じる影響を変えるため、影響評価を見直す必要がある。","eEn":"A change of use alters the context, users, and resulting impacts, so the impact assessment must be revisited."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の実施主体・役割を明確にすることの意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is it important to clarify who is responsible for performing the impact assessment?","o":["評価に用いた計算資源の使用量と処理時間を記録し、次年度の設備投資の予算計画を立てるため","作成したすべての評価文書を必ず外部の第三者機関へ提出するため","評価の実施・レビュー・承認の責任を明確にし、確実な運用と説明責任を確保するため","影響評価という手続きそのものを自動的かつ完全に不要にするため"],"oEn":["To record the amount of compute resources and the processing time used for the assessment, and to use those figures to draw up next year's capital investment plan for equipment","To always submit every assessment document produced to an outside third-party body","To clarify responsibility for performing, reviewing, and approving the assessment, ensuring reliable operation and accountability","To automatically and completely render the procedure of impact assessment unnecessary"],"a":2,"e":"役割・責任を明確にすることで、評価の実施・レビュー・承認が確実に行われ説明責任も確保される。","eEn":"Clarifying roles and responsibilities ensures the assessment is reliably performed, reviewed, and approved, and supports accountability."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"次のうち、AIシステム影響評価の「範囲外」として扱うのが最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which of the following is most appropriately treated as 'out of scope' for an AI system impact assessment?","o":["集団に対する差別的影響","安全に関わる潜在的な危害","個人のプライバシーと権利への潜在的な影響","社内カフェテリアのメニュー構成"],"oEn":["Discriminatory impacts on groups","Potential safety-related harms","Potential impacts on individuals' privacy and rights","The menu composition of the company cafeteria"],"a":3,"e":"社内カフェテリアのメニューはAIシステムの個人・集団・社会・安全・プライバシーへの影響とは無関係で範囲外。","eEn":"The cafeteria menu is unrelated to the AI system's impacts on individuals, groups, society, safety, or privacy, and is out of scope."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の結果を組織のリスク管理プロセスに「連携」させることの利点として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the benefit of 'integrating' impact assessment results into the organization's risk management process?","o":["影響評価とリスク管理のプロセスを完全に切り離しておける","作成したあらゆる文書類をいつでもすべて破棄してしまえる","すでに実施済みの影響評価であっても、担当者が代わるたびに毎回ゼロからやり直せること","特定された影響が管理策・リスク対応へ一貫して反映され、抜け漏れを防げる"],"oEn":["Being able to keep the impact assessment and risk management processes completely separate","Being able to discard every piece of documentation produced, all of it, at any time","Being able to redo even an already-completed impact assessment from scratch every time the person in charge changes","Identified impacts are consistently reflected in controls and risk treatment, preventing gaps"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価とリスク管理を連携させることで、特定された影響が管理策や対応へ一貫して反映され抜け漏れを防げる。","eEn":"Integrating the two ensures identified impacts are consistently reflected in controls and treatment, preventing gaps."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価において「透明性・説明可能性の欠如」がもたらす影響を検討する理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why should the impact of a 'lack of transparency or explainability' be considered in an impact assessment?","o":["透明性が欠如している状態はどのような場合でも常に便益だけを増やすから","透明性というものは結局のところモデルの性能指標そのものにすぎないから","説明可能性の水準は結局のところサーバーのストレージ容量と通信帯域の確保にそのまま直結してしまうから","判断根拠が不明だと、影響を受ける個人が結果を理解・異議申立てできず不利益が拡大しうるから"],"oEn":["Because a state lacking transparency always increases only the benefits, no matter the situation","Because transparency is, in the end, nothing more than the model's performance metric itself","Because the level of explainability ends up directly determining how much server storage capacity and network bandwidth must be secured","Because when the basis of decisions is unclear, affected individuals cannot understand or contest outcomes, amplifying harm"],"a":3,"e":"透明性・説明可能性が欠けると、影響を受ける個人が結果を理解・異議申立てできず不利益が拡大しうるため、評価対象となる。","eEn":"Lack of transparency prevents affected individuals from understanding or contesting outcomes, potentially amplifying harm, so it is assessed."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"影響評価の結果に基づく「継続的モニタリング」を計画する意義として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Why is it meaningful to plan 'ongoing monitoring' based on impact assessment results?","o":["継続的な監視は運用コストを増やすだけで効果がまったくないから","継続的な監視は影響評価がひとたび完了した時点で不要となり、以後は記録も残さなくてよいから","継続的な監視を行うことで影響評価という手続きそのものが不要になるから","一度きりの評価では時間経過やデータ・環境の変化に伴う新たな影響を捉えられないから"],"oEn":["Because continuous monitoring only increases operating costs and has no effect whatsoever","Because continuous monitoring becomes unnecessary the very moment the impact assessment is completed, and no records need be kept thereafter","Because performing continuous monitoring itself renders the procedure of impact assessment unnecessary","Because a one-off assessment cannot capture new impacts arising over time or from changing data and environments"],"a":3,"e":"時間経過やデータ・環境変化で新たな影響が生じうるため、影響評価に基づく継続的モニタリングが重要となる。","eEn":"New impacts can emerge over time or from changing data and environments, so ongoing monitoring based on the assessment is important."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAの『Plan（計画）』段階に最もよく対応するAIMSのClause群はどれか？","qEn":"Which group of AIMS clauses best corresponds to the 'Plan' stage of PDCA?","o":["運用（Clause 8）－確立した計画をDoとして実行する段階","改善（Clause 10）－是正処置により再発防止を図るAct段階","組織の状況・リーダーシップ・計画（Clause 4〜6）","パフォーマンス評価（Clause 9）－監視測定を行うCheck段階"],"oEn":["Operation (Clause 8) – the Do stage that carries out the established plan","Improvement (Clause 10) – the Act stage that prevents recurrence via corrective action","Context, leadership and planning (Clauses 4–6)","Performance evaluation (Clause 9) – the Check stage of monitoring and measurement"],"a":2,"e":"『Plan』は状況把握・方針・リスクと目標の計画に対応し、Clause 4〜6が該当する。","eEn":"'Plan' maps to establishing context, policy, and planning of risks and objectives, i.e. Clauses 4–6."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAの『Do（実行）』段階に最もよく対応するAIMSのClauseはどれか？","qEn":"Which AIMS clause best corresponds to the 'Do' stage of PDCA?","o":["改善（Clause 10）","マネジメントレビュー（Clause 9.3）","運用（Clause 8）","計画（Clause 6）"],"oEn":["Improvement (Clause 10)","Management review (Clause 9.3)","Operation (Clause 8)","Planning (Clause 6)"],"a":2,"e":"『Do』は計画した管理策やプロセスを実際に運用する段階で、Clause 8が対応する。","eEn":"'Do' is the actual operation of planned controls and processes, corresponding to Clause 8."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAの『Check（点検）』段階に最もよく対応するAIMSのClauseはどれか？","qEn":"Which AIMS clause best corresponds to the 'Check' stage of PDCA?","o":["パフォーマンス評価（Clause 9）","支援（Clause 7）－資源確保に関わる箇条","運用（Clause 8）－Do段階の箇条","計画（Clause 6）－Plan段階の箇条"],"oEn":["Performance evaluation (Clause 9)","Support (Clause 7) – the clause concerned with securing resources","Operation (Clause 8) – the Do-stage clause","Planning (Clause 6) – the Plan-stage clause"],"a":0,"e":"『Check』は監視・測定・内部監査・マネジメントレビューによる評価で、Clause 9が対応する。","eEn":"'Check' is evaluation via monitoring, measurement, internal audit and management review, i.e. Clause 9."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAの『Act（改善）』段階に最もよく対応するAIMSのClauseはどれか？","qEn":"Which AIMS clause best corresponds to the 'Act' stage of PDCA?","o":["改善（Clause 10）","パフォーマンス評価（Clause 9）","支援（Clause 7）","運用（Clause 8）"],"oEn":["Improvement (Clause 10)","Performance evaluation (Clause 9)","Support (Clause 7)","Operation (Clause 8)"],"a":0,"e":"『Act』は不適合への対応や是正処置、継続的改善を扱うClause 10に対応する。","eEn":"'Act' addresses handling of nonconformity, corrective action and continual improvement, i.e. Clause 10."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査プログラム』と『個々の監査計画』の関係として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the relationship between an 'audit programme' and an 'individual audit plan'?","o":["監査プログラムは外部審査のみを、監査計画は内部監査のみを指す用語である","監査プログラムは一定期間の監査群の枠組みで、監査計画は個々の監査の具体的手配である","両者は同一で、監査プログラムと監査計画は単に呼称が異なるだけである","監査計画が複数の監査プログラムを束ねる上位概念であり、組織全体の年間計画としての役割を果たす"],"oEn":["The audit programme means only external audits and the audit plan means only internal audits","The audit programme is the framework for a set of audits over a period, while the audit plan details the arrangements for a single audit","They are identical; audit programme and audit plan are merely different names for the same thing","The audit plan is the higher-level concept that bundles several audit programmes, and it serves as the annual plan for the whole organization over the year"],"a":1,"e":"監査プログラムは期間内の一連の監査を管理する枠組み、監査計画は特定の監査の実施手配を指す。","eEn":"The audit programme manages a set of audits over a period; the audit plan details the conduct of one specific audit."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査における『客観的証拠（objective evidence）』の説明として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes 'objective evidence' in auditing?","o":["是正処置の実施予定を示す将来の計画であり、まだ実行されていない事項","検証可能で、記録・事実の記述・情報などの裏付けとなるデータ","被監査部門の管理者の口頭での保証のみで、記録や事実の裏付けは求めない","監査員の経験に基づく主観的な印象であり、裏付けとなる記録は不要である"],"oEn":["A future plan indicating intended corrective action that has not yet been carried out","Verifiable data supporting records, statements of fact or information","Only the verbal assurance of the audited department's manager, with no records or facts backing it","The auditor's subjective impression based on experience, with no need for supporting records"],"a":1,"e":"客観的証拠は検証可能な事実に基づくデータであり、記録・事実の記述・観察などから得られる。","eEn":"Objective evidence is verifiable data based on facts, obtained from records, statements of fact or observations."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査員に求められる『力量（competence）』として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the 'competence' required of internal auditors?","o":["被監査部門の全業務を自ら実行できる実務遂行能力そのもの","監査対象とAIMS要求事項を理解し、監査を適切に遂行できる知識・技能","経営層と同等の意思決定権限を持ち、方針を独自に決定できること","法的な認証機関の資格を必ず保有し、外部審査員として登録されていること"],"oEn":["The practical ability to personally perform all tasks of the audited department oneself","Knowledge and skills to understand the audit subject and AIMS requirements and conduct the audit properly","Holding decision-making authority equal to top management and setting policy independently","Mandatorily holding a legal certification body's qualification and registration as an external auditor"],"a":1,"e":"監査員の力量とは、対象と要求事項を理解し監査を適切に実施できる知識・技能を指す。","eEn":"Auditor competence is the knowledge and skill to understand the subject and requirements and conduct the audit properly."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の『監査範囲（scope）』を定める主な目的として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the main purpose of defining the internal audit 'scope'?","o":["認証マークのデザインを決めるため","監査で発見してよい不適合の総数と指摘の件数をあらかじめ決めておくため","どの部門・プロセス・場所・期間を対象とするかを明確にするため","監査員の報酬額を確定するため"],"oEn":["To decide the design of the certification mark","To predetermine the total number of nonconformities and findings that may be raised in the audit","To clarify which units, processes, locations and periods are covered","To fix the auditors' remuneration"],"a":2,"e":"監査範囲を定めるのは、どの部門・プロセス・場所・期間を対象とするかを明確にするため。認証マークのデザインを決めることや、監査で発見してよい不適合の総数を決めておくこと、監査員の報酬額の確定は目的ではない。","eEn":"The audit scope is set to make clear which departments, processes, locations and periods are covered. Deciding the design of a certification mark, fixing in advance the number of nonconformities that may be found, or setting auditors' fees is not the purpose."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査基準（audit criteria）』の例として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the best example of 'audit criteria'?","o":["組織の方針・手順・法的要求事項・ISO/IEC 42001の要求事項","監査員が抱いた印象であり、文書化された要求事項とは無関係である","監査中に収集した客観的証拠そのものであり、基準ではなく結果を指す","監査後に作成される是正処置計画であり、監査前には存在しない文書"],"oEn":["The organization's policies, procedures, legal requirements and ISO/IEC 42001 requirements","Impressions formed by the auditor, unrelated to any documented requirement","The objective evidence collected during the audit itself, referring to a result rather than a criterion","The corrective action plan produced after the audit, a document that does not exist before it"],"a":0,"e":"監査基準の例は、組織の方針・手順・法的要求事項・ISO/IEC 42001の要求事項など、証拠を照合する参照点。監査員の印象は基準ではなく、収集した客観的証拠は基準に照らす対象であり、是正処置計画は監査後に作られる。","eEn":"Examples of audit criteria are the organization's policies and procedures, legal requirements and ISO/IEC 42001 requirements, which are the reference points against which evidence is compared. An auditor's impression is not a criterion, and corrective action plans come after the audit."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査所見（audit finding）』は必ず不適合であるという理解は正しいか？","qEn":"Is it correct that an 'audit finding' is always a nonconformity?","o":["正しい。所見はすべて不適合を意味し、適合の所見という概念は存在しない","正しい。所見は必ず是正処置を伴い、伴わない所見は所見と呼べない","正しくない。所見は監査基準そのものを指し、証拠とは無関係である","正しくない。所見は適合・不適合・改善の機会のいずれにもなり得る"],"oEn":["Correct: all findings mean nonconformity, and there is no such thing as a conformity finding","Correct: a finding always entails corrective action, and one without it cannot be called a finding","Incorrect: a finding means the audit criteria themselves, unrelated to evidence","Incorrect: a finding can be conformity, nonconformity or an opportunity for improvement"],"a":3,"e":"監査所見は監査証拠を監査基準に照らした評価結果で、適合・不適合・改善の機会のいずれにもなり得る。","eEn":"A finding is the result of evaluating evidence against criteria, and may be conformity, nonconformity or an opportunity for improvement."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査員の独立性を確保する具体的な方法として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate way to ensure internal auditor independence?","o":["監査を毎回同じ一人の監査員だけに任せ、担当を固定して継続させる","監査結果を経営層に報告させず、被監査部門内だけで処理させる","監査員に被監査部門への改善提案を一律に禁止し、指摘のみ許可する","監査対象の作業に直接関与していない者を監査員に選ぶ"],"oEn":["Always assign audits to the same single auditor, fixing the assignment continuously","Prevent auditors from reporting results to top management, handling them only within the audited unit","Uniformly prohibit auditors from proposing improvements to the audited unit, allowing only findings","Select auditors not directly involved in the work being audited"],"a":3,"e":"自分の業務を監査すると客観性が損なわれるため、対象業務に関与しない者を監査員に選ぶ。","eEn":"Auditing one's own work harms objectivity, so auditors should not be involved in the work being audited."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査プログラムを計画する際に考慮すべき事項として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which should be considered when planning the audit programme?","o":["監査員が使うノートPCの色","対象プロセスの重要性と前回監査の結果","被監査部門に所属する従業員の私的な趣味や交友関係","組織のロゴの更新時期"],"oEn":["The color of the laptops auditors use","The importance of the processes concerned and the results of previous audits","The private hobbies and personal friendships of the staff belonging to the audited unit","The timing of updating the organization's logo"],"a":1,"e":"監査プログラムはプロセスの重要性や過去の監査結果などのリスクに基づき頻度・範囲を決める。","eEn":"The audit programme sets frequency and scope based on risk, such as process importance and prior audit results."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査証拠（audit evidence）』に求められる性質として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which property is required of 'audit evidence'?","o":["被監査部門に有利であること","検証可能であること","監査員個人の意見であること","公表済みであること"],"oEn":["Being favorable to the audited unit","Being verifiable","Being the auditor's personal opinion","Being already published"],"a":1,"e":"監査証拠は、監査基準に照らして検証可能で、事実に基づくものでなければならない。被監査部門に有利であること、監査員個人の意見であること、公表済みであることは、証拠に求められる性質ではない。","eEn":"Audit evidence must be verifiable and based on facts, so that it can be assessed against the audit criteria. Being favourable to the auditee, being the auditor's personal opinion, or being already published is not a required property of evidence."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の実施頻度を決める考え方として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes how the frequency of internal audits should be decided?","o":["対象プロセスの重要性・変更・前回結果に応じて計画する","すべてのプロセスを重要度に関わらず常に毎日監査する体制を組む","監査は認証取得時の一度だけで十分であり、以後は実施しない","頻度は監査員個人の空き時間だけで決め、重要性は考えない"],"oEn":["Plan according to process importance, changes and previous results","Set up a system to audit every process daily regardless of its importance","A single audit at certification time is sufficient, with none conducted afterward","Frequency is decided solely by auditors' spare time, without considering importance"],"a":0,"e":"頻度は、対象プロセスの重要性・変更・前回の結果に応じて計画する。重要度に関わらず毎日すべてを監査することや、認証取得時の一度だけで済ませること、監査員の空き時間だけで決めることは合理的ではない。","eEn":"Frequency is planned according to the importance of the processes, changes, and previous results. Auditing everything daily regardless of importance, auditing once at certification only, or deciding by auditors' free time alone is not reasonable."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査プログラムの実施と結果に関して、組織が保持すべきものは何か？","qEn":"What should the organization retain regarding the implementation and results of the audit programme?","o":["顧客向けに作成された広告予算表とその見積書","監査プログラムの実施と監査結果の証拠となる文書化した情報","監査員が業務の合間に書き留めた個人的な日記のようなメモの原本とその写し","契約関係のない競合他社が実施した監査の記録一式"],"oEn":["An advertising budget sheet and its estimate prepared for customers","Documented information as evidence of the audit programme's implementation and audit results","The original of a memo like the auditors' personal diary jotted down between tasks, together with its copy","A full set of audit records from a competitor with no contractual relationship"],"a":1,"e":"組織は監査プログラムの実施と結果の証拠として文書化した情報を保持する必要がある。","eEn":"The organization must retain documented information as evidence of programme implementation and audit results."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の結果は誰に報告されるべきか、最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"To whom should the results of internal audits be reported, most appropriately?","o":["監査員本人のみ","関連する管理層（マネジメント）","被監査部門を除く全部門に匿名で","一般公衆すべてに公開"],"oEn":["Only the auditor themselves","The relevant management","Anonymously to all units except the audited one","Disclosed to the entire general public"],"a":1,"e":"監査結果は、是正などの判断ができる関連する管理層（マネジメント）に報告される。監査員本人のみ、被監査部門を除く全部門への匿名通知、一般公衆への公開では、必要な処置を決める人に届かない。","eEn":"Audit results are reported to the relevant management, who can decide on corrective action. Telling only the auditor, notifying all departments except the auditee anonymously, or publishing to the general public would not reach the people who decide what to do."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査結論（audit conclusion）』と『監査所見（audit finding）』の関係として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the relationship between an 'audit conclusion' and an 'audit finding'?","o":["監査結論は監査目的と全所見を考慮して監査チームが導く総合的な判断結果である","監査所見は監査結論を短く言い換えた要約に過ぎず、独立した意味を持たない","監査結論は監査開始前にあらかじめ決められ、所見の内容によって変わらない","両者は完全に同義であり、報告書上で区別して用いる必要はない"],"oEn":["The audit conclusion is the overall judgment the audit team reaches after considering the audit objectives and all findings","A finding is merely a paraphrased summary of the conclusion and has no independent meaning","The audit conclusion is decided before the audit begins and does not change based on findings","They are entirely synonymous and need not be distinguished in a report"],"a":0,"e":"監査結論は、監査目的と全ての所見を踏まえて監査チームが導く総合的な判断結果。所見を言い換えただけの要約ではなく、監査開始前に決められるものでもなく、所見と完全な同義でもない。","eEn":"An audit conclusion is the overall result the audit team reaches considering the audit objectives and all audit findings. It is not a mere short restatement of the findings, not decided before the audit begins, and not fully synonymous with a finding."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の計画段階で監査員の割り当てを行う際、最も重視すべきなのはどれか？","qEn":"When assigning auditors during audit planning, what should be most emphasized?","o":["監査員が被監査部門の担当者と親しい関係にあることを優先する","監査員の勤続年数の長さのみを基準に割り当てを決める","割り当てが監査プロセスの客観性・公平性を確保すること","監査員が最も忙しくない閑散期であることのみを基準に割り当てる"],"oEn":["Prioritize assigning auditors who are on close personal terms with the audited unit's staff","Assign audits based solely on the length of the auditor's tenure","That the assignment ensures the objectivity and impartiality of the audit process","Assign audits based solely on whether it is the auditor's least busy period"],"a":2,"e":"監査員の選定・割り当ては、監査プロセスの客観性と公平性を確保するよう行う。被監査部門の担当者と親しいことを優先したり、勤続年数や閑散期だけで決めたりすると、客観性や公平性が損なわれる。","eEn":"Auditors are selected and assigned to ensure the objectivity and impartiality of the audit process. Prioritizing familiarity with the auditee's staff, or deciding only by length of service or quiet periods, would undermine objectivity and impartiality."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ISO/IEC 42001において『内部監査』を要求している主なClauseはどれか？","qEn":"Which clause of ISO/IEC 42001 primarily requires 'internal audit'?","o":["Clause 8.1（運用の計画及び管理）","Clause 6.1（リスク及び機会への取組み）","Clause 7.2（力量）","Clause 9.2（内部監査）"],"oEn":["Clause 8.1 (Operational planning and control)","Clause 6.1 (Actions to address risks and opportunities)","Clause 7.2 (Competence)","Clause 9.2 (Internal audit)"],"a":3,"e":"内部監査を要求しているのは Clause 9.2（内部監査）で、パフォーマンス評価の一部にあたる。Clause 8.1 は運用の計画及び管理、6.1 はリスク及び機会への取組み、7.2 は力量を扱っており、内部監査の条項ではない。","eEn":"Internal audit is required by Clause 9.2, part of performance evaluation. Clause 8.1 covers operational planning and control, 6.1 addresses risks and opportunities, and 7.2 covers competence, so none of them is the internal audit clause."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"個々の内部監査計画に含めるべき事項として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which should be included in an individual internal audit plan?","o":["組織が販売する製品カタログの全文とその価格表","被監査部門を訪れた来客の氏名を記した名簿","適用宣言書で除外した管理策の除外理由の全文","監査の目的・範囲・基準・スケジュール"],"oEn":["The full text of the organization's product catalog and its price list","A visitor list recording the names of guests to the audited unit","The full text of the justifications for the controls excluded in the Statement of Applicability","The objectives, scope, criteria and schedule of the audit"],"a":3,"e":"個々の内部監査計画には、監査の目的・範囲・基準・スケジュールなど、実施に必要な事項を含める。製品カタログの全文と価格表や、来客の氏名の名簿、除外理由の全文は、監査計画に含める事項ではない。","eEn":"Each internal audit plan includes what is needed to carry out the audit, such as objectives, scope, criteria and schedule. The full product catalogue and price list, a visitor name register, or the full text of exclusion reasons does not belong in the audit plan."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"『監査基準』と『監査証拠』の関係として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"Which best describes the relationship between 'audit criteria' and 'audit evidence'?","o":["監査基準は監査の終了後に集めた監査証拠をもとに作られる","両者は同じもので、順番が違うだけ","監査証拠を監査基準に照らして評価し、所見を導く","監査証拠が監査基準を定義する"],"oEn":["The criteria are created from the evidence gathered after the audit has ended","They are the same, only in different order","Evidence is evaluated against the criteria to derive findings","Evidence defines the criteria"],"a":2,"e":"監査では、集めた監査証拠を監査基準（参照点）に照らして評価し、監査所見を導く。基準は証拠の収集後に作られるものではなく、証拠が基準を定義するわけでもなく、両者は同じものでもない。","eEn":"In an audit, the collected audit evidence is evaluated against the audit criteria, which serve as the reference, to derive audit findings. Criteria are not created from evidence after collection, evidence does not define criteria, and the two are not the same thing."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"内部監査が『マネジメントシステムが自らの要求事項に適合しているか』を確認する際、比較の基準となるのはどれか？","qEn":"When internal audit checks whether the management system conforms to the organization's own requirements, what serves as the reference?","o":["監査員がその場の雰囲気から感じ取った漠然とした印象","契約関係のない競合他社が独自に定めた内部規程","無作為に集めた一般公衆へのアンケート調査の結果","組織自身が定めた方針・手順などの要求事項"],"oEn":["A vague impression the auditor picked up from the atmosphere on site","Internal regulations independently set by a competitor with no contractual relation","Results of a survey randomly collected from members of the general public","The organization's own defined requirements such as policies and procedures"],"a":3,"e":"比較の基準になるのは、組織自身が定めた方針・手順などの要求事項（および規格の要求事項）。監査員がその場で感じた漠然とした印象や、競合他社が定めた内部規程、一般公衆へのアンケート結果は基準にならない。","eEn":"The basis for comparison is the organization's own requirements such as its policies and procedures, along with the standard's requirements. An auditor's vague impression of the atmosphere, a competitor's internal rules, or public survey results cannot serve as criteria."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"監査における『サンプリング』を用いる主な理由として最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the main reason for using 'sampling' in auditing?","o":["限られた時間・資源で合理的な確信を得るため","監査にとって都合の悪い証拠を意図的に避けて通るため","不適合を隠すため","監査を必ず全数調査にするため"],"oEn":["To gain reasonable confidence within limited time and resources","To deliberately steer clear of evidence that is inconvenient for the audit","To hide nonconformities","To make every audit a 100% inspection"],"a":0,"e":"全数確認は現実的でないため、限られた時間・資源で、代表的なサンプルから合理的な確信を得るためにサンプリングを用いる。都合の悪い証拠を避けるためでも、不適合を隠すためでも、全数調査にするためでもない。","eEn":"A full check is impractical, so sampling is used to gain reasonable confidence from representative samples within limited time and resources. It is not used to avoid inconvenient evidence, to hide nonconformities, or to force a full inspection."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善を要求するISO/IEC 42001のClauseはどれか？","qEn":"Which clause of ISO/IEC 42001 requires continual improvement?","o":["Clause 8（運用）","Clause 7（支援）","Clause 10（改善／継続的改善）","Clause 4（組織及びその状況の理解に関する条項）"],"oEn":["Clause 8 (Operation)","Clause 7 (Support)","Clause 10 (Improvement / continual improvement)","Clause 4 (Understanding the organization and its context)"],"a":2,"e":"継続的改善はClause 10で要求され、AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に高める。","eEn":"Continual improvement is required in Clause 10 to continually enhance the AIMS's suitability, adequacy and effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"PDCAサイクルをAIMSに適用する狙いとして最も適切なのはどれか？","qEn":"What is the main aim of applying the PDCA cycle to an AIMS?","o":["一度構築したら二度と見直さない固定的な仕組みにするため","内部監査にかかる負担を減らすことを理由に、監査という仕組み自体を将来的に廃止するため","認証取得の審査を受ける瞬間だけ性能を一時的に高めるため","計画・実行・点検・改善を繰り返し、システムを継続的に維持・向上させるため"],"oEn":["To make the system fixed and never revisited once built","To eventually abolish the very mechanism of internal audit, on the grounds of reducing the burden it involves","To temporarily boost performance only at the moment of the certification audit","To repeat plan-do-check-act so the system is continually maintained and improved"],"a":3,"e":"PDCAは反復サイクルであり、繰り返しを通じてAIMSを継続的に維持・向上させる。","eEn":"PDCA is an iterative cycle; through repetition the AIMS is continually maintained and improved."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューのインプットとして、特に「前回からの継続性」を確認するために含めるべきものは？","qEn":"Which item should be included as a management review input specifically to confirm 'continuity since the last review'?","o":["次年度に新しく導入する学習用計算基盤の機種選定の比較表","組織のロゴやブランドカラーを見直すためのデザイン案","データセンターの電力契約に関する入札結果の一覧","前回までのマネジメントレビューで決めた処置の状況"],"oEn":["A comparison table for selecting the model of training compute infrastructure to be newly introduced next year","A design proposal to revise the organization's logo and brand colors","A list of bid results for the data center's electricity contract","The status of actions decided in previous management reviews"],"a":3,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001のマネジメントレビューでは、前回までのレビューで決定した処置の状況（フォローアップ）をインプットとして扱い、PDCAの連続性を確保する。","eEn":"Management review takes the status of actions from previous reviews as an input, ensuring continuity of the PDCA cycle."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューの実施頻度に関する規格の考え方に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects the standard's view on how often management reviews should be performed?","o":["四半期ごとに実施することが法律で厳密に義務付けられている","あらかじめ定めた間隔（planned intervals）で実施する","監査で不適合が出た場合にのみ臨時に一度だけ実施すればよい","一度確立して実施すれば、その後は状況が変わっても二度と実施する必要がなくなる"],"oEn":["It is strictly mandated by law to be conducted every quarter","It is performed at planned intervals","It only needs to be done once, on an ad hoc basis, whenever an audit finds a nonconformity","Once established and conducted a single time, it never needs to be performed again thereafter"],"a":1,"e":"規格はトップマネジメントが「あらかじめ定めた間隔」でレビューを行うことを求めており、頻度そのものは組織が決める。","eEn":"The standard requires top management to review at 'planned intervals'; the actual frequency is decided by the organization."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"「修正（correction）」と「是正処置（corrective action）」の役割の違いを最もよく表しているのは？","qEn":"Which best captures the difference in role between 'correction' and 'corrective action'?","o":["是正処置は資格を持つ監査員のみが実施できる特別な処置である","どちらも全く同じ意味であるため、規格上使い分ける必要はない","修正は不適合の原因そのものを除去する処置であり、是正処置は表面化した現象だけを直す処置である","修正は検出された不適合そのものへの即時対応、是正処置は原因を除去する処置"],"oEn":["Corrective action is a special action that only a qualified auditor may perform","They mean exactly the same thing, so the standard does not require distinguishing them","Correction is the action that removes the root cause itself, while corrective action is the action that only fixes the symptom that has surfaced","Correction is the immediate action on the detected nonconformity, while corrective action removes its cause"],"a":3,"e":"修正は目の前の不適合を直す即時対応、是正処置は原因を除去し再発を防ぐ処置。両者は補完的だが目的が異なる。","eEn":"Correction is the immediate action on the detected nonconformity, whereas corrective action eliminates the cause to prevent recurrence; they are complementary but distinct."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置を実施した後に、規格が組織に求めている確認は？","qEn":"After implementing a corrective action, what does the standard require the organization to confirm?","o":["その不適合を最初に発見した監査員を評価すること","とった是正処置の有効性をレビューすること","処置に要した費用が予算内であったか","以後は一切文書を残さないこと"],"oEn":["Evaluating the auditor who first found the nonconformity","Reviewing the effectiveness of the corrective action taken","Whether the cost of the action stayed within budget","That no documentation is kept from then on"],"a":1,"e":"是正処置は実施して終わりではなく、その有効性（原因が除去され再発が防げているか）をレビューすることが求められる。","eEn":"A corrective action is not complete once implemented; the organization must review its effectiveness in eliminating the cause and preventing recurrence."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"不適合が発生したとき、原因除去の前にまず組織が行うべき対応の組み合わせに最も近いのは？","qEn":"When a nonconformity occurs, which pair best describes what the organization should do first, before eliminating the cause?","o":["その不適合を管理・修正し、生じた結果に対処する","監査プログラム全体を白紙に戻す","次回のマネジメントレビューが開かれるまでは何もしないでおく","認証機関へただちに通報する"],"oEn":["Control and correct the nonconformity and deal with its consequences","Scrap the entire audit programme","Doing nothing at all until the next management review meeting is convened","Immediately notify the certification body"],"a":0,"e":"不適合が生じたら、まずそれを管理・修正し結果に対処する。原因除去（是正処置）はその後に必要性を評価して行う。","eEn":"On a nonconformity, first control/correct it and deal with the consequences; eliminating the cause comes afterward, once the need is evaluated."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"AIMSのパフォーマンス指標（KPI）が備えるべき基本的な性質に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best describes a basic property that an AIMS performance indicator (KPI) should have?","o":["主観的で人によって解釈が変わること","経営層だけが理解できる専門用語であること","毎回必ず100%を示すよう設計されていること","測定可能で、目的の達成度を客観的に示せること"],"oEn":["Being subjective so interpretations vary by person","Being jargon understandable only by executives","Being designed to always show 100%","Being measurable and objectively showing the degree of objective achievement"],"a":3,"e":"KPIは測定可能で、目的やプロセスの達成度を客観的に示せることが重要。主観的で比較不能な指標は有効性評価に使えない。","eEn":"A KPI must be measurable and objectively indicate how well objectives or processes are met; subjective, non-comparable indicators cannot support effectiveness evaluation."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善が対象とする「AIMSの何」を維持・向上させることか、最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Continual improvement aims to maintain and enhance 'what' about the AIMS — which is most appropriate?","o":["社員数の増加率","広告予算の消化率","オフィスの賃料水準と月々の光熱費","適切性・妥当性・有効性"],"oEn":["The rate of headcount growth","The utilization rate of the advertising budget","The office rent level and the monthly utility costs","Suitability, adequacy and effectiveness"],"a":3,"e":"継続的改善は、AIMSの適切性（suitability）・妥当性（adequacy）・有効性（effectiveness）を継続的に高めることを目的とする。","eEn":"Continual improvement targets the ongoing enhancement of the AIMS's suitability, adequacy and effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューの「アウトプット」に含まれるものとして最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is most appropriate as an 'output' of a management review?","o":["内部監査で収集した監査証拠の原本をそのまま添付しただけの記録","前回のマネジメントレビューの議事録をそのまま読み上げること","監査チェックリストの原本を保管しているだけの記録","継続的改善の機会やAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定"],"oEn":["A record to which the originals of the audit evidence collected in the internal audit are attached as they are","Simply reading aloud the minutes of the previous management review","Just a record consisting of the original audit checklist kept in storage","Decisions on continual improvement opportunities and any need to change the AIMS"],"a":3,"e":"マネジメントレビューのアウトプットには、改善の機会、AIMS変更の必要性、資源の必要性などに関する決定が含まれる。","eEn":"Outputs of a management review include decisions on improvement opportunities, any need to change the AIMS, and resource needs."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置の中核となる目的を最も正確に述べているのは？","qEn":"Which most accurately states the core purpose of a corrective action?","o":["不適合をなかったことにして記録を削除すること","不適合の根本原因を除去し、同種の再発を防止すること","責任者を特定して懲戒すること","認証の有効期限を延長すること"],"oEn":["Erasing the nonconformity and deleting records","Eliminating the root cause of the nonconformity to prevent its recurrence","Identifying and disciplining the responsible person","Extending the validity period of the certification"],"a":1,"e":"是正処置の目的は原因を除去して再発を防ぐこと。個人の処罰や記録の削除は目的ではない。","eEn":"The purpose of corrective action is to eliminate the cause and prevent recurrence, not to punish individuals or delete records."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"「修正（correction）」の例として最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate example of a 'correction'?","o":["不適合の根本原因を分析する","同種の不適合が二度と出ないよう手順を再設計する","検出された誤ったAI出力を直ちに正しいものへ差し替える","将来のリスクを見越して監査計画を作る"],"oEn":["Analyzing the root cause of the nonconformity","Redesigning a procedure so the same nonconformity never recurs","Immediately replacing the detected erroneous AI output with a correct one","Building an audit plan anticipating future risk"],"a":2,"e":"修正は検出された不適合そのものへの即時対応。誤出力の差し替えは典型例で、原因分析や再発防止（是正処置）とは区別される。","eEn":"A correction is the immediate action on the detected nonconformity itself; replacing an erroneous output is a typical example, distinct from root-cause analysis (corrective action)."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ISO用語における「有効性（effectiveness）」の意味に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which is closest to the meaning of 'effectiveness' in ISO terminology?","o":["投入した資源に対して得られた成果の比率を示す割合","計画した活動が実行され、計画した結果が達成された程度","作成された文書やマニュアルの分量が多いことそのもの","監査で指摘された不適合の件数が多いこと自体を示す数値"],"oEn":["A ratio showing the results obtained relative to the resources invested","The extent to which planned activities are carried out and planned results achieved","The sheer volume of the documents and manuals produced, by itself","A figure merely showing many nonconformities were raised in an audit"],"a":1,"e":"有効性は「計画した活動を実行し計画した結果を達成した程度」。資源対成果の比率は効率（efficiency）であり別概念。","eEn":"Effectiveness is the extent to which planned activities are realized and planned results achieved; the ratio of results to resources is efficiency, a different concept."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"「効率（efficiency）」と「有効性（effectiveness）」の違いとして最も適切なのは？","qEn":"Which best distinguishes 'efficiency' from 'effectiveness'?","o":["どちらも同義であり区別しない","効率は計画した結果の達成度、有効性は資源の使い方の巧拙を指す","有効性は速度、効率は品質を指す","効率は資源と結果の関係、有効性は計画した結果の達成度"],"oEn":["They are synonyms and not distinguished","Efficiency is the degree to which planned results are achieved, while effectiveness refers to how skillfully the resources are used","Effectiveness means speed and efficiency means quality","Efficiency is the relationship between resources and results; effectiveness is the degree of achieving planned results"],"a":3,"e":"効率は投入資源と結果の関係、有効性は計画した結果をどれだけ達成したか。KPI設計では両者を混同しないことが重要。","eEn":"Efficiency concerns the relationship between resources used and results; effectiveness concerns how well planned results are achieved. KPI design must not conflate the two."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"パフォーマンス評価における「監視（monitoring）」と「測定（measurement）」の違いに最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best reflects the difference between 'monitoring' and 'measurement' in performance evaluation?","o":["両者は同一の概念であり、規格上は単なる言い換えに過ぎない","監視は状態を継続的に把握すること、測定は値を求めること","監視は認証機関だけが担う役割で、測定は組織だけが担う役割である","監視は年1回、測定は毎日行うと規格で厳密に定められている"],"oEn":["The two are the same concept and merely a paraphrase of one another in the standard","Monitoring is continually observing status; measurement is determining a value","Monitoring is a role only the certification body performs, while measurement is only the organization's role","The standard strictly mandates monitoring once a year and measurement every day"],"a":1,"e":"監視は対象の状態を継続的に確認すること、測定は特定の量に値を割り当てること。両者を組み合わせてパフォーマンスを評価する。","eEn":"Monitoring is continually observing the status of something, while measurement assigns a value to a quantity; both together support performance evaluation."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"不適合と是正処置に関して、規格が保持を求める文書化した情報に含まれるのは？","qEn":"Regarding nonconformity and corrective action, which does the standard require to be retained as documented information?","o":["不適合の性質・とった処置・その結果","競合他社が自社で実施した是正処置の記録の一式","経営者個人のプライベートな予定表","監査員個人の感想を書いたメモ"],"oEn":["The nature of the nonconformity, actions taken, and their results","A full set of records of the corrective actions a competitor took at its own company","The manager's own private personal schedule","A memo of the auditor's own personal impressions"],"a":0,"e":"組織は、不適合の性質やとった処置、及び是正処置の結果を文書化した情報として保持する必要がある。","eEn":"The organization must retain documented information on the nature of nonconformities, actions taken, and the results of corrective actions."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューを実施する主体として規格が想定しているのは？","qEn":"Who does the standard expect to conduct the management review?","o":["AIモデルの利用者全員","内部監査員のみ","組織のトップマネジメント","外部の認証審査員"],"oEn":["All users of the AI model","Internal auditors only","The organization's top management","An external certification auditor"],"a":2,"e":"マネジメントレビューはトップマネジメントが、あらかじめ定めた間隔でAIMSの状況をレビューする活動である。","eEn":"The management review is conducted by top management, who review the AIMS at planned intervals."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"継続的改善の性質を最も正しく表しているのは？","qEn":"Which most correctly describes the nature of continual improvement?","o":["トップマネジメントの承認をいっさい必要としない非公式の現場活動","繰り返し行い、パフォーマンスを段階的に高めていく活動","監査で不適合が出た年だけ行う活動","認証取得時に一度だけ行う一過性の活動"],"oEn":["An informal shop-floor activity that needs no top management approval at all","A recurring activity that incrementally raises performance","An activity done only in years with audit findings","A one-time activity done only at certification"],"a":1,"e":"継続的改善（continual improvement）は一度きりではなく繰り返し行い、AIMSのパフォーマンスを段階的に高めていく。","eEn":"Continual improvement is not a one-off; it is a recurring activity that progressively raises the AIMS's performance."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"不適合発生から是正処置に至る一般的な流れとして最も適切な順序は？","qEn":"Which is the most appropriate general sequence from a nonconformity to corrective action?","o":["是正処置→原因分析→修正→不適合を無視して終了","修正して結果に対処→原因を評価→是正処置→有効性のレビュー","有効性のレビュー→修正→原因を無視→そのまま終了","原因を先に除去→その後で不適合を発見→発見後は記録も残さず放置する"],"oEn":["Corrective action → root-cause analysis → correction → ignore the nonconformity and close","Correct and deal with consequences → evaluate the cause → corrective action → review effectiveness","Review effectiveness → correction → ignore the cause → close as is","Eliminate the cause first → only afterward detect the nonconformity → leave it unaddressed and unrecorded after detection"],"a":1,"e":"まず修正して結果に対処し、次に原因除去の必要性を評価して是正処置を行い、最後にその有効性をレビューする。","eEn":"First correct and address consequences, then evaluate the need to eliminate the cause and take corrective action, and finally review its effectiveness."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"パフォーマンス指標のうち「先行指標（leading indicator）」の特徴に最も近いのは？","qEn":"Which best characterizes a 'leading indicator' among performance indicators?","o":["文書の総ページ数を数える","将来の成果を予測・先取りして示唆する","すでに起きた結果のみを事後的に集計して示す","監査の合否だけを表す"],"oEn":["It counts the total pages of documents","It anticipates and signals future performance","It only tallies and reports results that have already happened, after the fact","It shows only audit pass/fail"],"a":1,"e":"先行指標は将来の成果を予測・先取りする指標。すでに起きた結果を示すのは遅行指標（lagging indicator）。","eEn":"A leading indicator anticipates future outcomes, whereas a lagging indicator reports results that have already occurred."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューのインプットとして、組織の状況変化を反映するために考慮すべきものは？","qEn":"Which should be considered as a management review input to reflect changes in the organization's context?","o":["AIMSに関連する外部・内部の課題の変化","管理策の適用宣言書の様式","リスク対応計画の承認者","前回のマネジメントレビューで決めた処置の実施状況"],"oEn":["Changes in external and internal issues that are relevant to the AIMS","The form of the Statement of Applicability","The approver of the risk treatment plan","The status of actions decided at the previous management review"],"a":0,"e":"マネジメントレビューでは、AIMSに関連する外部・内部の課題の変化をインプットとして考慮し、方針や目標の妥当性を見直す。","eEn":"Management review considers changes in external and internal issues relevant to the AIMS to reassess the adequacy of policy and objectives."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置の結果として、規格が「必要に応じて」行うことを認めている対応は？","qEn":"As a result of corrective action, which response does the standard allow 'if necessary'?","o":["将来の全監査を免除する","不適合を隠すためログを削除する","AIMSそのものへの変更を行う","是正処置を無効化する"],"oEn":["Exempting all future audits","Deleting logs to hide the nonconformity","Making changes to the AIMS itself","Nullifying the corrective action"],"a":2,"e":"是正処置の結果として、必要に応じてリスクや機会の更新、及びAIMSへの変更を行うことが認められている。","eEn":"As a result of corrective action, the organization may, if necessary, update risks and opportunities and make changes to the AIMS itself."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"不適合を検出した際、是正処置に進む前に組織が評価すべきことは？","qEn":"Upon detecting a nonconformity, what should the organization evaluate before proceeding to corrective action?","o":["原因を除去する処置が必要かどうか","次の広告キャンペーンの予算","取得した認証マークをどこに掲示するかの決定","誰を責めるべきか"],"oEn":["Whether action to eliminate the cause is needed","The budget for the next ad campaign","The decision of where to display the certification mark obtained","Whom to blame"],"a":0,"e":"是正処置は自動的に発動されるのではなく、まず「原因を除去する処置が必要か」を評価してから実施する。","eEn":"Corrective action is not automatic; the organization first evaluates whether action to eliminate the cause is needed."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ISO/IEC 42001において、監視・測定・分析・評価やマネジメントレビューを主に扱う箇条（Clause）は？","qEn":"In ISO/IEC 42001, which clause primarily covers monitoring, measurement, analysis, evaluation and management review?","o":["支援（Support）の箇条－資源や力量、文書化を扱う箇条","パフォーマンス評価（Performance evaluation）の箇条","計画（Planning）の箇条－目的やリスク対応の計画を定めるPlan段階の箇条","運用（Operation）の箇条－計画を実行するDo段階を扱う箇条"],"oEn":["The Support clause – the clause covering resources, competence, and documentation","The Performance evaluation clause","The Planning clause - the Plan stage that sets objectives and plans risk treatment","The Operation clause – the clause covering the Do stage that executes the plan"],"a":1,"e":"監視・測定・分析・評価、内部監査、マネジメントレビューはパフォーマンス評価（箇条9）にまとめられている。","eEn":"Monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation, internal audit and management review fall under Performance evaluation (Clause 9)."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"ISO/IEC 42001において、不適合・是正処置・継続的改善を主に扱う箇条（Clause）は？","qEn":"In ISO/IEC 42001, which clause primarily covers nonconformity, corrective action and continual improvement?","o":["計画の箇条（リスク及び機会への取組み）","リーダーシップの箇条（方針や役割分担）","組織の状況の箇条（内外の課題）","改善（Improvement）の箇条"],"oEn":["The Planning clause (risk and opportunity treatment)","The Leadership clause (policy and role assignment)","The Context of the organization clause (internal/external issues)","The Improvement clause"],"a":3,"e":"継続的改善と、不適合が出たときの是正処置は、改善の箇条で扱う。計画の箇条はリスク及び機会への取組みを定める箇条で、組織の状況の箇条は内外の課題を把握する箇条であり、是正処置の置き場ではない。","eEn":"Nonconformity, corrective action and continual improvement are handled in the Improvement clause. The planning clause deals with addressing risks and opportunities, and the context clause deals with internal and external issues, so neither is where corrective action sits."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置の「有効性のレビュー」で確認したい主要な点は？","qEn":"What is the key point to confirm in the 'review of effectiveness' of a corrective action?","o":["原因が除去され同じ原因による不適合が再発していないか","処置を承認した役員の氏名とその所属部署","処置に使用した書式の色や見た目のデザイン","処置の実施にかかった作業時間の長さそのもの"],"oEn":["Whether the cause was removed and nonconformities from the same cause have not recurred","The name and department of the executive who approved the action","The color and visual design of the form used for the action","The sheer length of working hours the action itself took"],"a":0,"e":"有効性レビューの核心は、原因が本当に除去され、同じ原因による不適合が再発していないかを確認すること。","eEn":"The essence of the effectiveness review is confirming that the cause was truly eliminated and that nonconformities from the same cause have not recurred."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"是正処置が「不適合の影響に見合っている（appropriate）」とは、どういう考え方に最も近いか？","qEn":"What does it mean for corrective actions to be 'appropriate to the effects' of the nonconformities?","o":["どの不適合にも一律に最大限の処置を課し、影響の大小を考慮しない","影響の小さい不適合ほど、あえて厳しい処置を課す方針にする","処置の内容は不適合の影響とは無関係に、担当者の裁量だけで決める","処置の大きさを、不適合が及ぼす影響の重大さに釣り合わせる"],"oEn":["Impose the same maximum-severity action on every nonconformity, disregarding the size of the effect","Deliberately impose harsher action the smaller the effect of the nonconformity is","Decide the content of the action solely at the handler's discretion, unrelated to the effects","Scaling the action to match the severity of the nonconformity's effects"],"a":3,"e":"規格は是正処置を「遭遇した不適合の影響に見合ったもの」とすることを求める。影響の重大さに応じて処置の程度を釣り合わせる。","eEn":"The standard requires corrective actions to be appropriate to the effects of the nonconformities encountered, scaling the action to the severity of those effects."},
];

function buildSets(bank, plan, nSets){
  const by = {}; bank.forEach(q => { (by[q.d] = by[q.d] || []).push(q); });
  const sets = {};
  for (let s = 0; s < nSets; s++) { const arr = []; Object.entries(plan).forEach(([dom, n]) => { const pool = by[dom] || []; if (!pool.length) return; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) arr.push(pool[(i + s * n) % pool.length]); }); sets[s + 1] = arr; }
  return sets;
}
SECGOV_REG.push({ code: "ISO 42001 F", hue: "#0E8A6E", bank: BANK });
const ISO42001F_HARD = [
// ===== D1: AIMS fundamental principles & concepts (responsible AI) ×16 =====
{"d":"D1","q":"あるフィンテック企業のCISOが、社内で使うAIチャットボットについて「モデルの内部構造を数式レベルで完全に開示できないため、当社は説明可能性(explicability)の原則を満たせない」と主張しました。ISO/IEC 42001の責任あるAIの考え方に照らして、この主張への最も適切な反論はどれですか。","o":["説明可能性はソースコードとモデル構造全体の公開と完全に同義であり、商用の生成AIモデルでは原理的に達成不能な要求である","説明可能性は必ずモデルの重みと数式レベルの内部構造を残らず全面開示することを規格が明示的に要求しており、CISOの主張は規格の定義どおり正しい","説明可能性は利害関係者が意思決定を理解・信頼できるよう適切な説明を提供することを指し、内部の完全開示ではなく文脈に応じた説明で満たせる","説明可能性はISO/IEC 42001に規定される公式の原則ではなく、各社が独自の社内基準として任意に定義すればよい事項である"],"a":2,"e":"責任あるAIにおける説明可能性(explicability)は、対象の利害関係者が結果や意思決定を理解し信頼できるよう、目的に応じた説明を提供することを意味し、必ずしもモデル内部の完全開示を要求しません。ソース公開と同義とする説明や、重みや数式の全面開示を規格が要求するとする説明は過剰解釈です。公式の原則ではないとする説明は、中核原則である事実に反します。","qEn":"A fintech CISO argues that because the company cannot fully disclose an internal AI chatbot's model internals at the level of equations, it 'cannot meet the principle of explicability.' Under ISO/IEC 42001's view of responsible AI, what is the best rebuttal?","oEn":["Explicability is entirely synonymous with publishing the full source code and model architecture, an unachievable requirement for generative AI models","Explicability requires disclosing every internal weight and formula in full, so per the standard's definition the CISO's claim is correct","Explicability means providing appropriate, context-suitable explanations so stakeholders can understand and trust decisions—not full internal disclosure","Explicability is not an official principle defined in ISO/IEC 42001 and is a matter each company may define arbitrarily as its own standard"],"eEn":"Explicability means giving stakeholders understandable, purpose-appropriate explanations so they can trust outcomes; it does not require exposing full model internals. Equating it with total disclosure or source release, or claiming the standard demands full disclosure of weights and formulas, over-reads it; denying that it is an official principle contradicts its status as a core responsible-AI principle."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある製造業がAIマネジメントシステム(AIMS)の構築を検討しています。経営企画部は『AIMSは高性能なAIモデルを開発するための技術フレームワークだ』と理解し、データサイエンス部門にだけ責任を割り当てようとしています。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で、この理解の誤りを最もよく指摘しているのはどれですか。","o":["AIMSはモデルの推論精度を最大化するための純粋な技術標準にすぎず、Clause 5のリーダーシップ要求もモデル精度KPIの管理に読み替えられるため、責任の所在はデータサイエンス部門のみが単独で担うのが適切である","AIMSはIT部門が担うサーバやネットワークのセキュリティ設定・脆弱性対応にのみ限定される社内規程にすぎない","AIMSは組織がAIを責任を持って開発・提供・利用するための経営管理の仕組みであり、トップマネジメントを含む組織横断の関与が必要である","AIMSは外部の認証コンサルタントに全面委託すべき、認証取得のためだけの事務手続きに過ぎず社内の関与は不要である"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSはAIを責任を持ってガバナンスするマネジメントシステムであり、方針・役割・リスク管理・運用・改善を組織全体で回します。トップマネジメントのリーダーシップ(Clause 5)が明示的に求められるため、単一部門への丸投げは不適切。技術標準との混同、セキュリティ設定への矮小化、外部委託で足りるとする説明はいずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A manufacturer treats an AIMS as 'a technical framework for building high-performance AI models' and assigns responsibility only to its data-science team. Which statement best identifies the flaw under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["An AIMS is a purely technical standard for maximizing model inference accuracy, and Clause 5's leadership requirements merely restate accuracy KPI management, so responsibility appropriately rests with the data-science team alone","An AIMS is merely an internal regulation limited to the IT department's server/network security settings and vulnerability response","An AIMS is a management framework for responsibly developing/providing/using AI and requires organization-wide involvement including top management","An AIMS is merely paperwork for obtaining certification, fully outsourced to an external consultant with no internal involvement needed"],"eEn":"An AIMS governs responsible AI through policy, roles, risk management, operation, and improvement across the whole organization. Clause 5 explicitly requires top-management leadership, so delegating to one team is wrong. Confusing it with a technical standard, shrinking it to server security settings, and saying outsourcing suffices are all wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある病院が、放射線画像から病変候補を提示するAIを導入します。倫理委員会は『最終診断は必ず専門医が確認し、AIの提示は補助にとどめる』方針を定めました。この方針が最も強く体現している責任あるAIの原則はどれですか。","o":["公平性(fairness)－偏りのない扱いを確保する原則","可用性(availability)－常時利用可能に保つ原則","データ最小化－個人データ収集を絞る原則","人間による監督(human oversight)－最終判断を人が保持する原則"],"a":3,"e":"最終判断を人間(専門医)が保持し、AIを補助に位置づける設計は、人間による監督/人間中心の統制(human oversight)の中核です。公平性は集団間の不当な差の回避、データ最小化はプライバシー原則、可用性はセキュリティ属性であり、この事例の主眼ではありません。","qEn":"A hospital deploys AI that flags candidate lesions in radiology images, with an ethics board policy that a specialist must confirm every diagnosis and the AI only assists. Which responsible-AI principle does this most strongly embody?","oEn":["Fairness – the principle of ensuring unbiased treatment","Availability – keeping the system usable at all times","Data minimization – limiting personal data collection","Human oversight, the principle that humans retain the final decision"],"eEn":"Keeping the final decision with a human (the specialist) and positioning AI as assistance is the essence of human oversight. Fairness concerns unjustified group differences, data minimization is a privacy principle, and availability is a security attribute, so none is the focus here."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるEC企業の採用AIが、過去の採用データで学習した結果、特定の性別の応募者を体系的に低く評価していることが判明しました。ISO/IEC 42001の責任あるAIの観点から、この状況が主に損なっている原則と、AIMSが求める対応の組み合わせとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["説明責任(accountability)のみが損なわれており、学習データに由来する偏りはClause 6.1.4の影響評価の対象外とされるため、追加の対応は不要である","可搬性が損なわれており、モデルを別クラウドへ移行する","透明性が損なわれており、モデルを非公開にする","公平性(fairness)が損なわれており、影響評価とリスク対応を通じて偏りを特定・低減する"],"a":3,"e":"属性に基づく体系的な不利益は公平性の問題です。AIMSはAIシステム影響評価(6.1.4)とリスクアセスメント/対応(6.1.2-6.1.3)を通じて、偏りの源を特定し是正・低減することを求めます。追加対応は不要とする説明は誤り、可搬性は無関係な属性、モデルの非公開化はバイアス自体を解決しないため不適切です。","qEn":"An e-commerce recruiting AI, trained on historical hiring data, systematically scores applicants of a certain gender lower. Which pairing of the principle chiefly harmed and the AIMS-required response is best?","oEn":["Only accountability is harmed; bias originating in the training data falls outside the Clause 6.1.4 impact assessment, so no further action is needed","Portability is harmed; migrate the model to another cloud","Transparency is harmed; make the model private","Fairness is harmed; identify and reduce bias via impact assessment and risk treatment"],"eEn":"Systematic disadvantage by attribute is a fairness problem. An AIMS requires identifying and reducing bias sources via the AI system impact assessment (6.1.4) and risk assessment/treatment (6.1.2-6.1.3). Saying no action is needed is wrong, portability is an irrelevant attribute, and keeping the model non-public does not fix the bias itself."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業が『当社はAI倫理憲章をWebに掲載しているので、ISO/IEC 42001の説明責任(accountability)の要件は十分に満たしている』と主張します。この主張の弱点を最も的確に突いているのはどれですか。","o":["憲章をWebに掲載した時点で説明責任の要求は充足済みと扱われ、役割・権限の割当てや意思決定の追跡可能性、証拠の保持といった運用面での裏付けはそれ以上求められない","説明責任には、役割・責任・権限の割当て、意思決定の追跡可能性、証拠の保持など運用の裏付けが必要で、方針掲示だけでは不十分である","説明責任はモデルの応答速度や精度など純粋な技術指標のみで測定されるものであり、文書や役割分担とは無関係の概念である","説明責任は外部の第三者監査人のみが単独で負うべき概念であり、組織内の役割や権限には一切割り当てられない"],"a":1,"e":"説明責任は、誰が何に責任を持つかを明確化し(役割・権限)、意思決定や措置を追跡・立証できる状態を維持することを含みます。Webへの憲章掲示は透明性に寄与しますが、運用上の責任割当てや記録がなければ説明責任は満たされません。掲示で足りるとする説明は誤り、技術指標との混同、外部監査人への限定も誤りです。","qEn":"A company claims that because it posts an AI ethics charter on its website, it 'fully meets ISO/IEC 42001's accountability requirement.' What best exposes the flaw?","oEn":["Posting the charter on the website is treated as fully discharging accountability, so no further operational backing such as assigned roles and authorities, traceable decisions, or retained evidence is required","Accountability needs operational backing—assigned roles/authorities, traceable decisions, retained evidence—so a posted policy alone is insufficient","Accountability is measured purely by technical metrics like response speed or accuracy, unrelated to documents or role assignment","Accountability is a concept that only an external third-party auditor alone should bear, and can never be assigned to internal roles or authorities"],"eEn":"Accountability requires clarifying who is responsible for what (roles/authorities) and keeping decisions and actions traceable and demonstrable. A posted charter aids transparency but does not satisfy accountability without operational assignment and records. Saying posting suffices is wrong, confusing accountability with a technical metric is wrong, and limiting it to external auditors is wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"AIの用語について、あるプロジェクトで議論が混乱しています。『AIステークホルダー』『AIシステムのライフサイクル』『AIプロバイダ/AIユーザ』などの用語の共通定義を参照したい場合、ISO/IEC 42001の実装を支える基礎として最も適切な規格はどれですか。","o":["ISO/IEC 27001（ISMS要求事項）","ISO 9001（品質マネジメント）","ISO/IEC 22989（AIの概念と用語）","ISO/IEC 20000（ITサービス管理）"],"a":2,"e":"ISO/IEC 22989はAIの概念と用語を定義する基礎規格であり、42001が用いるAI関連用語の共通理解を支えます。27001は情報セキュリティ、ISO 9001は品質、20000はITサービス管理であり、AI固有の用語定義の一次参照ではありません。","qEn":"A project is confused over terms like 'AI stakeholder,' 'AI system life cycle,' and 'AI provider/AI user.' Which standard best provides the shared definitions underpinning an ISO/IEC 42001 implementation?","oEn":["ISO/IEC 27001 (ISMS requirements)","ISO 9001 (quality management)","ISO/IEC 22989 (AI concepts and terminology)","ISO/IEC 20000 (IT service management)"],"eEn":"ISO/IEC 22989 defines AI concepts and terminology and underpins the AI vocabulary 42001 relies on. 27001 is information security, ISO 9001 is quality, and 20000 is IT service management, so none is the primary source for AI-specific terms."},
{"d":"D1","q":"経営層が『ISO/IEC 42001とISO/IEC 23894はどちらもAI関連なので、片方だけ実装すれば認証を取得できる』と考えています。両規格の位置づけの違いを最も正確に説明しているのはどれですか。","o":["ISO/IEC 23894が認証取得の対象となる要求事項規格であり、42001はその実務を補うだけの参考ガイダンス文書に過ぎないため単独では認証できない","ISO/IEC 42001はAIMSの認証可能な要求事項規格であり、ISO/IEC 23894はAIリスクマネジメントのガイダンスで認証対象ではない","どちらも第三者認証機関による審査を経て取得できる、同格かつ相互互換の要求事項規格として位置づけられており、片方を実装すれば足りる","両者は規格番号が異なるだけで内容はまったく同一であり、実質的には一つの規格を二つの番号で呼んでいるにすぎない重複規格である"],"a":1,"e":"42001はAIMSの要求事項を定める認証可能な規格、23894はAIリスクマネジメントに関するガイダンス(ISO 31000のAI適用)で認証制度はありません。両者は補完関係にありますが役割が異なります。23894を認証対象とし42001を参考文書とする説明は役割の逆転、両者を同格の認証可能な規格とする説明や内容が同一とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"Leadership assumes ISO/IEC 42001 and ISO/IEC 23894 are interchangeable and implementing either yields certification. Which best states the difference in their roles?","oEn":["ISO/IEC 23894 is the certifiable requirements standard, while 42001 is merely a reference guidance document supplementing its practice, so 42001 alone cannot be certified","ISO/IEC 42001 is the certifiable AIMS requirements standard; ISO/IEC 23894 is AI risk-management guidance and is not certifiable","Both are positioned as equal, mutually interchangeable requirements standards obtainable via third-party certification audit, so implementing just one is enough","The two differ only in their standard numbers and are entirely identical in content, effectively a duplicated standard called by two numbers"],"eEn":"42001 states certifiable AIMS requirements; 23894 is guidance on AI risk management (applying ISO 31000 to AI) with no certification scheme. They are complementary but distinct. Making 23894 the certifiable standard and 42001 mere guidance reverses their roles; calling both equal certifiable standards, or claiming their content is identical, is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるスタートアップは『透明性(transparency)を高める＝あらゆる情報を全公開する』と解釈し、モデルの学習に使った個人データも含めて全て開示しようとしています。責任あるAIの観点でこの解釈の問題点はどれですか。","o":["透明性はいかなる情報も外部の利害関係者に開示しないことを意味する、極めて消極的で閉鎖的な原則である","透明性は開示する情報量に上限を設けない無制限の全公開を意味し、学習に使った個人データもそのまま公開対象に含めるべきで、プライバシー等の他原則との均衡は一切考慮する必要がない","透明性は売上高や成長率など経営指標の一つに分類される事項であり、責任あるAIの原則には本来含まれない","透明性は適切・必要な情報を対象者に開示することであり、プライバシー等の他原則との均衡が必要で、個人データの無制限公開は不適切である"],"a":3,"e":"透明性は利害関係者に対し目的に応じた適切な情報を提供することを指し、プライバシー・安全・知的財産などとのバランスを取ります。学習データ中の個人データを無制限公開することはプライバシーを侵害し、責任あるAIに反します。無制限公開を是とする説明は誤り、何も開示しない原則とする説明は意味の反転、経営指標とする説明は原則性の否定です。","qEn":"A startup reads 'increasing transparency' as 'disclosing everything,' and plans to publish all training data including personal data. What is the flaw under responsible AI?","oEn":["Transparency is an extremely passive, closed principle meaning that no information whatsoever is disclosed to external interested parties","Transparency means unlimited full disclosure with no cap on the amount of information, so personal data used in training must also be published as-is, and balancing against principles such as privacy need never be considered","Transparency is classified as one of the business metrics like revenue or growth rate, and is not properly among the responsible-AI principles","Transparency means giving appropriate, necessary information to relevant parties, balanced with other principles like privacy—so unlimited disclosure of personal data is improper"],"eEn":"Transparency means providing appropriate, purpose-fit information to stakeholders while balancing privacy, safety, and IP. Publishing personal data without limits violates privacy and responsible AI. Endorsing unlimited disclosure is wrong, defining transparency as disclosing nothing inverts it, and classing it as a business metric denies that it is a principle."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある自治体がAIによる生活保護の適格性スクリーニングを導入予定です。市民団体は『自動判定だけで給付が却下されるのは問題だ』と懸念しています。ISO/IEC 42001の責任あるAIの観点で、この懸念に応える設計上の中核原則はどれですか。","o":["モデルサイズの縮小－推論コストを抑える軽量化の方針","APIレイテンシの削減－応答までの待ち時間を短縮する施策","処理速度の最大化－判定を迅速に返すことを最優先する設計方針","人間による監督と、影響を受ける個人の権利・尊厳への配慮(人間中心)"],"a":3,"e":"個人に重大な影響を及ぼす自動判定には、人間による監督(意義ある人的関与)と影響を受ける個人の権利・尊厳への配慮が求められます。速度・モデルサイズ・レイテンシは性能面の話であり、市民の懸念に応える責任あるAIの中核ではありません。","qEn":"A municipality plans AI screening for welfare eligibility. Citizens worry that people could be denied benefits by an automated decision alone. Which core responsible-AI principle addresses this in the design?","oEn":["Reducing model size – a policy of lightweighting the model to cut inference cost","Cutting API latency – a measure to shorten the wait time before a response","Maximizing processing speed – a design priority focused on returning decisions as fast as possible","Human oversight and consideration for the rights and dignity of affected individuals (human-centricity)"],"eEn":"Automated decisions with significant impact on individuals require meaningful human oversight and regard for affected people's rights and dignity. Speed, model size, and latency are performance matters, not the responsible-AI core addressing the citizens' concern."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業がAIMSの適用範囲を検討中です。CTOは『当社はAIモデルを自社開発しておらず、外部SaaSのAIを業務利用しているだけなので、42001は無関係だ』と述べました。この見解の妥当性として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["42001はクラウドインフラを提供する事業者のみを対象とし、それを利用するだけの一般企業には無関係の規格である","42001はAIを一切使用していない組織のためのガバナンス規格であり、AIを利用する組織には適用が想定されていない","AIを利用するだけの組織は42001の適用対象外とされており、CTOの見解は規格の適用範囲を正しく説明したものである","42001はAIの開発者だけでなく提供者・利用者にも適用され得るため、外部SaaSのAIを業務利用する組織にもAIMSは関係する"],"a":3,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001はAIを開発する組織だけでなく、AIを提供・利用する組織にも適用可能です。外部SaaSのAIを業務で利用する組織も、利用に伴うリスク・影響を管理する責任があり、AIMSの対象となり得ます。利用者を対象外とする説明は誤り、クラウド事業者のみに限る説明は適用範囲の過度な限定、AI未使用の組織向けとする説明は規格の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"A CTO says 42001 is irrelevant because the company does not build AI models—it only uses external SaaS AI in operations. How valid is this?","oEn":["42001 applies only to organizations that provide cloud infrastructure and is irrelevant to ordinary companies that merely use it","42001 is a governance standard for organizations that use no AI at all, and is not intended to apply to AI-using organizations","Organizations that merely use AI are outside 42001's scope, making the CTO's view a correct account of the standard's applicability","42001 can apply to providers and users of AI, not only developers, so an organization using external SaaS AI in its operations is within an AIMS's concern"],"eEn":"ISO/IEC 42001 applies to organizations that develop, provide, or use AI. An organization using external SaaS AI in operations still must manage the resulting risks and impacts and can be within an AIMS's scope. Excluding users is wrong, limiting the standard to cloud providers over-limits its scope, and calling it a standard for organizations that use no AI contradicts its intent."},
{"d":"D1","q":"AIガバナンスの研修で、ある受講者が『安全性(safety)とセキュリティ(security)は同じことなので区別は不要』と述べました。責任あるAIの観点で、両者の違いを最も正確に説明しているのはどれですか。","o":["安全性はサーバやネットワーク機器などハードウェアのみを対象とし、セキュリティはソフトウェアのみを対象とする区分であり、両者の管理策は重ならない","安全性は開発にかかる予算コストの指標であり、セキュリティは応答までの処理速度を測る性能指標であって、どちらも危害の防止とは無関係である","両者は完全に同義の言葉であり、規格上も実務上も区別して用いる必要はないため、統一した用語だけで研修を進めればよい","安全性はAIが個人・社会・環境に危害を与えないこと、セキュリティは機密性・完全性・可用性など資産を脅威から守ることで、目的が異なる"],"a":3,"e":"安全性はAIシステムが人・社会・環境に危害を及ぼさないことを重視し、セキュリティは資産を脅威から保護し機密性・完全性・可用性を維持することを重視します。両者は関連するが焦点が異なります。同義とする説明は誤り、ハード/ソフトへの切り分けは誤った区分、予算や処理速度の指標とする説明は指標の混同です。","qEn":"In training, a participant says 'safety' and 'security' are the same and need no distinction. Which most accurately explains the difference under responsible AI?","oEn":["Safety is a category applying only to hardware like servers, and security applies only to software, so their controls never overlap","Safety is a metric for development budget cost, and security a performance metric for response speed, neither related to preventing harm","The two are entirely synonymous terms that need not be distinguished in either the standard or practice, so training can proceed using a single unified term","Safety is about the AI not causing harm to individuals/society/the environment; security is about protecting assets from threats (confidentiality, integrity, availability)—different objectives"],"eEn":"Safety emphasizes the AI not harming people, society, or the environment; security emphasizes protecting assets and preserving confidentiality, integrity, and availability. They are related but focus differently. Calling them synonyms is wrong, splitting them into hardware and software is a wrong division, and treating them as budget or speed metrics confuses metrics."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある組織が生成AIを顧客対応に使い始めましたが、モデルが誤った断定的回答（ハルシネーション）を出すことがあります。責任あるAIの観点から、まず組織が確立すべき考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["ハルシネーションの発生自体は無視し、応答速度の最適化だけをサービスの唯一のKPIとして追求する","AIには限界・不確実性があることを前提に、信頼性(reliability)と人間による確認・監督の仕組みを設計する","生成AIは学習データが十分であれば常に正確な回答を返し、ハルシネーションは学習量が不足した初期モデルに固有の現象にすぎないため、出力内容を検証せずそのまま顧客に提示してよい","誤った回答が一件でも顧客に出るたびに、モデル全体をゼロから作り直すことを標準の運用手順とする"],"a":1,"e":"責任あるAIでは、AIの限界・不確実性を前提に、信頼性を確保し、重要な場面では人間の確認・監督を組み込みます。ハルシネーションを無視して速度だけを追う運用は限界を無視した危険な運用、出力を検証せず提示する運用は信頼性の軽視、誤りのたびに作り直す運用は非現実的で根本対処になりません。","qEn":"An organization uses generative AI for customer service but the model sometimes gives confident wrong answers (hallucinations). What should the organization establish first under responsible AI?","oEn":["Ignore the occurrence of hallucinations entirely and pursue only response-speed optimization as the service's sole KPI","Assume AI has limits/uncertainty and design for reliability plus human review/oversight where it matters","Generative AI always returns accurate answers given sufficient training data, and hallucination is merely a phenomenon peculiar to early under-trained models, so its output can be presented to customers as-is without verification","Make it the standard operating procedure to rebuild the entire model from scratch every single time a wrong answer reaches a customer"],"eEn":"Responsible AI assumes AI has limits and uncertainty, designs for reliability, and embeds human review/oversight where stakes are high. Ignoring hallucinations and chasing speed alone ignores limits dangerously, presenting unverified output neglects reliability, and rebuilding the model after every error is impractical and not a root fix."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるグローバル企業が、AI方針の中で『privacy(プライバシー)』を扱う際、他のISO規格との関係を整理したいと考えています。AIに関わる個人データ保護の管理策・拡張を扱う規格として、42001の実装と関連づけて参照すると有用なのはどれですか。","o":["ISO 14001（環境マネジメント）－環境負荷の低減が対象","ISO 50001（エネルギー管理）－エネルギー効率の改善が対象","ISO 45001（労働安全衛生）－労働災害の防止が対象","ISO/IEC 27701（プライバシー情報マネジメント）－個人データ保護が対象"],"a":3,"e":"ISO/IEC 27701はISMSを拡張しプライバシー情報マネジメント(PIMS)を扱う規格で、AIに伴う個人データ保護の観点で42001の実装と関連づけられます。14001は環境、45001は労働安全衛生、50001はエネルギーで、プライバシーの一次参照ではありません。","qEn":"A global company wants to relate 'privacy' in its AI policy to other ISO standards. Which is useful to reference alongside a 42001 implementation for managing personal data protection related to AI?","oEn":["ISO 14001 (environmental management) – targets reducing environmental impact","ISO 50001 (energy management) – targets improving energy efficiency","ISO 45001 (occupational health & safety) – targets preventing accidents","ISO/IEC 27701 (privacy information management), covering personal data protection"],"eEn":"ISO/IEC 27701 extends an ISMS to privacy information management (PIMS) and relates to 42001 for personal-data protection around AI. 14001 (environment), 45001 (OH&S), and 50001 (energy) are not the primary privacy reference."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業の役員が『AIMSを導入すればAIのリスクはゼロになる』と社内で説明しました。ISO/IEC 42001の考え方に照らして、この説明の誤りを最も適切に正しているのはどれですか。","o":["AIMSはリスクの特定・評価・対応とは無関係な、単に体裁を整えるための文書作成の事務作業にすぎない","AIMSはリスクを体系的に特定・評価・対応し許容可能な水準に管理する仕組みであり、リスクの完全排除を保証するものではない","AIMSはリスクを体系的な統制によって完全にゼロへ収束させる仕組みであり、役員の説明は規格の趣旨に沿った正しい説明である","AIMSは管理策を追加すればするほど組織の対応負荷が増し、かえってリスクを増加させる副作用を持つ仕組みである"],"a":1,"e":"マネジメントシステムはリスクを特定・評価し、リスク対応を通じて許容可能な水準に管理・低減しますが、リスクの完全なゼロ化を保証するものではありません。ゼロ化を是とする説明は誤り、管理策を増やすほどリスクが増えるとする説明は逆、リスクと無関係な体裁だけの事務とする説明はリスク管理の役割を否定する誤りです。","qEn":"An executive tells staff that adopting an AIMS 'reduces AI risk to zero.' Which best corrects this under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["An AIMS is mere clerical paperwork for keeping up appearances, unrelated to identifying, assessing, or treating risk","An AIMS systematically identifies, assesses, and treats risk to an acceptable level—it does not guarantee eliminating all risk","An AIMS is a mechanism that, through systematic controls, converges risk to exactly zero, so the executive's explanation correctly reflects the standard's intent","An AIMS is a mechanism that, the more controls are added, increases organizational burden and actually has the side effect of raising risk"],"eEn":"A management system identifies and assesses risk and treats it to an acceptable level, but does not guarantee zero risk. Endorsing zero risk is wrong, claiming that more controls increase risk reverses the point, and calling it cosmetic paperwork unrelated to risk denies its risk role."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるAI開発企業は『responsible AI(責任あるAI)は倫理の話であって、マネジメントシステムの認証には関係ない』と考えています。ISO/IEC 42001の観点でこの見解を最も適切に評価しているのはどれですか。","o":["42001は倫理的な配慮に一切触れず、モデルの計算アルゴリズムなど技術仕様のみを規定する規格であり、責任あるAIを扱わない","責任あるAIは個人の倫理観のみに関わる主観的な概念であり、Clause 6のリスク管理やAnnex Aの管理策には一切反映されないため、認証審査の対象にはなり得ず、見解は妥当である","責任あるAIはモデルの応答速度や精度などの技術指標を指す専門用語であり、組織の方針や体制とは無関係である","42001は責任あるAIの原則を、方針・目的・リスク管理・管理策・改善という管理システムの要求として具体化し、認証で検証可能にしている"],"a":3,"e":"42001は責任あるAIの原則（透明性・公平性・説明責任等）を、AI方針・目的、リスク/影響評価、Annex A管理策、継続的改善といった検証可能なマネジメント要求へ落とし込みます。したがって認証を通じて第三者が実装状況を評価できます。倫理と認証を切り離す説明は誤り、規格が技術仕様のみを定めるとする説明は趣旨の否定、責任あるAIを技術指標に矮小化する説明も誤りです。","qEn":"An AI developer believes 'responsible AI is about ethics and has nothing to do with management-system certification.' How should this be evaluated under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["42001 touches on no ethical considerations at all and prescribes only technical specifications like computational algorithms, not addressing responsible AI","Responsible AI is a subjective concept concerned only with personal ethics and is reflected nowhere in the Clause 6 risk requirements or the Annex A controls, so it can never be a certification-audit subject and the view is valid","Responsible AI is a technical term referring to metrics like a model's response speed or accuracy, unrelated to organizational policy or structure","42001 operationalizes responsible-AI principles as verifiable management requirements—policy, objectives, risk management, controls, improvement—so certification can assess them"],"eEn":"42001 translates responsible-AI principles (transparency, fairness, accountability, etc.) into verifiable management requirements: AI policy/objectives, risk/impact assessment, Annex A controls, continual improvement. So a third party can assess implementation via certification. Divorcing ethics from certification is wrong, saying the standard sets only technical specifications denies its intent, and shrinking responsible AI to a metric is wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある組織のAI倫理委員会が、責任あるAIの原則同士が衝突する場面（例：透明性を高めると一部の個人データが露出しプライバシーが低下する）にどう対処すべきか議論しています。ISO/IEC 42001の考え方に沿った最も適切な方針はどれですか。","o":["常に透明性の確保だけを機械的に最優先し、プライバシー等の他の原則は文脈にかかわらず一律に無視する","衝突が起きた場合は、影響の大きさや利害関係者の状況にかかわらず常にプライバシーの保護だけを優先して守る","原則同士の衝突はISO/IEC 42001の枠組みの下では理論上決して起こり得ないため、方針の策定自体が不要である","文脈・利害関係者・影響を考慮して原則間のトレードオフを評価し、影響評価を踏まえリスクベースで均衡のとれた対応を決定する"],"a":3,"e":"責任あるAIの原則は文脈依存で、時に相互に緊張関係になります。42001はリスクベースの考え方に基づき、影響評価・利害関係者の考慮を通じてトレードオフを評価し均衡ある対応を決めることを支援します。透明性だけ、またはプライバシーだけを機械的に最優先する方針は不適切で、原則の衝突は起こり得ないとする立場は非現実的です。","qEn":"An AI ethics board debates how to handle conflicts between responsible-AI principles (e.g., more transparency exposing some personal data, reducing privacy). Which approach fits ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Always mechanically prioritize ensuring transparency alone, uniformly ignoring other principles like privacy regardless of the context","Whenever a conflict arises, always protect privacy alone as the priority, regardless of the magnitude of impact or stakeholders involved","Conflicts between principles can theoretically never occur under the ISO/IEC 42001 framework, so formulating a policy is unnecessary","Evaluate trade-offs using context, stakeholders, and impacts, and decide a balanced, risk-based response informed by the impact assessment"],"eEn":"Responsible-AI principles are context-dependent and can be in tension. 42001's risk-based approach uses impact assessment and stakeholder consideration to weigh trade-offs and reach a balanced response. Mechanically prioritizing only transparency, or only privacy, absolutizes one principle; claiming conflicts cannot occur is unrealistic."},
// ===== D2: ISO/IEC 42001 requirements Clauses 4-10 ×24 =====
{"d":"D2","q":"あるSaaS企業がAIMSの構築を開始し、まずClause 4『組織の状況』に取り組んでいます。プロジェクトマネージャは『適用範囲(scope)は当社のAI製品名を列挙すれば十分だ』と考えています。Clause 4の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["適用範囲はAIMS構築の最終段階であるClause 8の運用計画に至って初めて検討すればよい事項である","適用範囲は自社が展開するAI製品名を単に一覧化するだけで足り、内外の課題や利害関係者の要求はClause 8の運用段階で扱うため、境界や適用可能性についての記述は求められない","内外の課題・利害関係者のニーズと期待・他組織との関係を踏まえてAIMSの適用範囲(境界と適用可能性)を決定し文書化する","適用範囲はトップマネジメントが口頭で合意すれば足りるものであり、文書化した情報として残す必要はない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 4では、内外の課題(4.1)、利害関係者のニーズと期待(4.2)を踏まえ、AIMSの適用範囲(境界と適用可能性)を決定し(4.3)、AIMSを確立・実施・維持・改善する(4.4)ことを求めます。適用範囲は文書化が必要で、単なる製品名の列挙では不十分。口頭合意で足りるとする説明は文書化不要とする誤り、Clause 8で初めて検討するとする説明は検討時点の誤りです。","qEn":"A SaaS company starts its AIMS with Clause 4 (context). The PM thinks 'scope is just a list of our AI product names.' What does Clause 4 actually require?","oEn":["Scope is a matter that only needs to be considered once reaching the Clause 8 operational planning, the final stage of building the AIMS","Scope is satisfied merely by listing the company's AI product names; internal/external issues and interested-party requirements belong to the Clause 8 operation stage, so no description of boundaries or applicability is required","Determine and document the AIMS scope (boundaries and applicability) considering internal/external issues, interested parties' needs/expectations, and relationships with others","Scope only needs verbal agreement from top management and does not need to be retained as documented information"],"eEn":"Clause 4 requires determining internal/external issues (4.1), interested parties' needs/expectations (4.2), the AIMS scope/boundaries and applicability (4.3), and establishing/maintaining/improving the AIMS (4.4). Scope must be documented; a product list is insufficient. Settling scope orally wrongly drops documentation, and deferring it to Clause 8 misplaces the timing."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるメーカーのトップマネジメントは、AI方針を策定しましたが『方針は掲示しておくので、実務は各部門に任せる』として、それ以上関与しない方針です。Clause 5『リーダーシップ』の要求に照らして、この姿勢の不足点はどれですか。","o":["方針を社内ポータルに掲示さえすればトップマネジメントの責務はそれだけで完了しており、それ以上の関与に不足はない","トップマネジメントはAI方針に基づく技術的な実装作業そのものを、担当部門に任せず自らの手で実行しなければならない","トップマネジメントはリーダーシップとコミットメントを実証し、AIMSを組織のプロセスに統合し、資源を提供し、有効性に説明責任を負う必要がある","リーダーシップの実証や資源提供へのコミットメントはClause 5では一切要求されておらず、Clause 7の支援に属する事務的な手配として現場の管理職が処理すべき事項である"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 5はトップマネジメントに対し、リーダーシップとコミットメントの実証、AI方針の確立、役割・責任・権限の割当て、資源提供、AIMSの事業プロセスへの統合、有効性への説明責任などを求めます。方針掲示だけでは不足。Clause 5は要求していないとする説明は要求の否定、トップが技術作業を自ら行うべきとする説明は誤り(役割割当てで足りる)です。","qEn":"A manufacturer's top management issues an AI policy but says 'we post it and leave execution to departments,' with no further involvement. What is missing under Clause 5 (leadership)?","oEn":["Once the policy is simply posted on the internal portal, top management's duty is complete on that alone, with no further involvement lacking","Top management must personally carry out the technical implementation work based on the AI policy itself, rather than delegating it to a department","Top management must demonstrate leadership/commitment, integrate the AIMS into business processes, provide resources, and be accountable for effectiveness","Leadership and committing resources are not required by Clause 5; they are clerical matters belonging to Clause 7 support that line managers should handle"],"eEn":"Clause 5 requires top management to demonstrate leadership and commitment, establish the AI policy, assign roles/responsibilities/authorities, provide resources, integrate the AIMS into business processes, and be accountable for effectiveness. Posting alone is insufficient. Saying Clause 5 does not require this denies the requirement; saying top management must do the technical work personally is wrong, since assigning roles suffices."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるフィンテック企業がClause 6.1（リスク及び機会への取組み）に取り組んでいます。担当者は『情報セキュリティのリスクアセスメント結果を流用すれば、AI固有のリスクアセスメントは不要だ』と考えました。この考えの問題点として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIに関するリスクはその性質上どのようなシステムや利用文脈であっても常にゼロとみなされ、情報セキュリティのリスクアセスメント結果さえ残っていれば、評価という工程自体がそもそも不要である","リスクアセスメントという工程はClause 6の適用範囲外に位置づけられ、AIMS構築においては扱う必要のない事項である","情報セキュリティのリスク評価結果をそのまま転用すればAI固有のリスク源も含め全てを代替でき、追加の評価は不要である","AIMSではAI固有のリスク源(公平性・安全性・透明性・自律性等)を対象にAIリスクアセスメントを行い、さらにAIシステム影響評価も実施する必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 6.1はAIMSにおいてAI固有のリスク源を対象としたリスクアセスメント(6.1.2)・リスク対応(6.1.3)を求め、加えて6.1.4でAIシステム影響評価を要求します。情報セキュリティのリスク評価はセキュリティ資産中心で、AI固有の公平性・安全性・社会影響等を網羅しません。リスクアセスメントをClause 6の範囲外とする説明は要求の否定、AIリスクをゼロとみなす説明は誤った前提、結果の流用で足りるとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A fintech firm addressing Clause 6.1 assumes it can reuse its information-security risk assessment and skip an AI-specific one. What is the flaw?","oEn":["Risk related to AI is by its very nature deemed always zero regardless of the system or context of use, so as long as the information-security risk assessment results are on file, the assessment process itself is unnecessary","The risk-assessment process is positioned outside the scope of Clause 6 and need not be addressed when building the AIMS","Simply reusing the information-security risk assessment results substitutes for everything including AI-specific risk sources, with no additional assessment needed","An AIMS must perform an AI risk assessment covering AI-specific risk sources (fairness, safety, transparency, autonomy) plus an AI system impact assessment"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1 requires an AIMS risk assessment (6.1.2) and treatment (6.1.3) over AI-specific risk sources, plus an AI system impact assessment (6.1.4). A security risk assessment centers on security assets and won't cover AI-specific fairness/safety/societal impacts. Placing risk assessment outside Clause 6 denies the requirement, treating AI risk as zero assumes a false premise, and reusing the security results as a full substitute is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるヘルスケア企業が、AIMSのリスク対応(6.1.3)の一環で、どのAnnex A管理策を採用/除外したかとその理由を示す文書を求められました。この文書は何であり、どのClauseで要求されますか。","o":["内部監査計画のことであり、Clause 9.2で監査員の担当割当てを示すために要求される文書である","マネジメントレビュー議事録のことであり、Clause 9でトップマネジメントの審議の記録として要求される文書である","インシデント報告書のことであり、システム障害が起きた後にClause 10の枠組みでのみ要求される文書である","適用宣言書(SoA)。Clause 6.1.3で、リスク対応に必要な管理策とその実施状況、採用/除外の正当化を含めて要求される"],"a":3,"e":"適用宣言書(SoA)はClause 6.1.3で要求され、リスク対応に必要な管理策、それらを実施しているか、Annex A管理策の採用/除外とその正当化を含みます。インシデント報告、レビュー議事録、内部監査計画はいずれも別の要求で、SoAではありません。","qEn":"A healthcare company must produce, as part of risk treatment (6.1.3), a document showing which Annex A controls it included/excluded and why. What is it and where is it required?","oEn":["This is the internal audit plan, a document required under Clause 9.2 to show the assignment of auditors","This is the management review minutes, a document required under Clause 9 as a record of top management's deliberations","This is the incident report, a document required only under the Clause 10 framework after a system failure occurs","A Statement of Applicability (SoA), required in Clause 6.1.3, including the controls necessary for risk treatment, their implementation status, and justification for inclusions/exclusions"],"eEn":"The Statement of Applicability is required in Clause 6.1.3 and includes the controls necessary for risk treatment, whether they are implemented, and justification for including/excluding Annex A controls. Incident reports, review minutes, and audit plans are other requirements, not the SoA."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるスタートアップがClause 6.2『AIの目的』を設定しました。目的として『AIをもっと活用する』とだけ記載しています。Clause 6.2の要求に照らして、この目的の不備を最もよく指摘しているのはどれですか。","o":["目的はAIMS運用が進んだ後半段階にあたるClause 9のパフォーマンス評価になって初めて設定すればよい事項である","目的の内容はトップマネジメントの承認さえ得られれば、達成計画や責任者・期限の設定はClause 8の運用計画で初めて扱われるため、測定可能性の有無や監視・伝達の仕組みは一切不問とされる","目的は抽象的なスローガンとして掲げておけば規格上足り、資源・責任者・期限を伴う具体的な計画への落とし込みは不要である","目的はAI方針と整合し、測定可能で(実行可能な場合)、監視され、伝達され、更新され、達成のための計画(何を・資源・責任者・期限・評価方法)を伴う必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 6.2はAIの目的が方針と整合し、測定可能(実行可能な範囲で)、監視・伝達・更新され、達成計画(実施事項・必要資源・責任者・完了期限・結果評価方法)を備えることを求めます。『もっと活用する』は測定不能で計画も欠くため不備。抽象的なスローガンで足りるとする説明は誤り、承認さえあれば測定可能性や計画は不問とする説明は内容要件を落とす誤り、Clause 9で初めて設定するとする説明は時点の誤りです。","qEn":"A startup sets a Clause 6.2 AI objective that merely says 'use AI more.' What best identifies the deficiency?","oEn":["Objectives are a matter that only needs to be set once reaching Clause 9's performance evaluation, the later stage of AIMS operation","Once top management approves the wording, plans, owners, and deadlines are first handled in Clause 8 operational planning, so whether the objective is measurable or has any monitoring and communication mechanism is never questioned","Objectives are sufficient as an abstract slogan under the standard, with no need to translate them into a concrete plan with resources, an owner, and a deadline","Objectives must align with the AI policy, be measurable (where practicable), be monitored/communicated/updated, and have plans (what, resources, responsible party, deadline, evaluation)"],"eEn":"Clause 6.2 requires objectives consistent with the policy, measurable where practicable, monitored, communicated, updated, and supported by plans (actions, resources, responsibility, timeline, evaluation of results). 'Use AI more' is unmeasurable and unplanned. Endorsing abstract slogans is wrong, ignoring measurability and plans once approved drops content requirements, and setting objectives only at Clause 9 misplaces the timing."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるIT企業がClause 7『支援』に取り組んでいます。人事部は『力量(competence)は資格証を集めれば足りる』と考えています。Clause 7.2の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["資格証を人事部が収集して保管しておくだけで、教育・訓練・経験の確保という力量要求はすべて自動的に満たされる","力量に関する事項はClause 7の対象外とされ、別の箇条において個別に規定される独立した要求事項である","AIMSの有効性に影響する業務を行う人の必要な力量を決定し、教育・訓練・経験で確保し、有効性を評価し、証拠を保持する","力量の確保が求められるのはトップマネジメント個人の能力に対してのみであり、一般従業員については資格証の写しを人事部が保管しさえすれば、教育訓練や有効性の評価までは要求が及ばない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.2は、AIMSのパフォーマンスに影響する人の力量を明確化し、適切な教育・訓練・経験に基づき力量を確保し、必要なら是正措置を取り、その有効性を評価し、証拠として文書化情報を保持することを求めます。資格証の収集は一手段に過ぎず、決定・評価・証拠保持を伴う必要があります。トップだけに対象を限る説明は誤り、力量をClause 7の対象外とする説明は要求の否定です。","qEn":"An IT company on Clause 7 (support) assumes 'competence is satisfied by collecting certificates.' What does Clause 7.2 actually require?","oEn":["Simply having HR collect and file certificates automatically satisfies the entire competence requirement of education, training, and experience","Competence-related matters are excluded from Clause 7's scope and are a separate requirement individually prescribed elsewhere","Determine the competence needed for persons affecting AIMS effectiveness, ensure it via education/training/experience, evaluate effectiveness, and retain evidence","Ensuring competence is required only of top management's individual ability; for general employees it is enough for HR to file copies of certificates, with no requirement for training or for evaluating its effectiveness"],"eEn":"Clause 7.2 requires determining necessary competence for persons affecting AIMS performance, ensuring it through education/training/experience, taking action where needed, evaluating effectiveness, and retaining documented evidence. Certificates are one means; the determination, evaluation, and evidence are required. Limiting the requirement to top management over-limits its scope, and excluding competence from Clause 7 denies the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるメディア企業がClause 8『運用』を計画しています。開発部門は『AIシステム影響評価は6.1で計画したので、運用段階では何も文書化しなくてよい』と考えました。Clause 8の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["運用とはトップマネジメントが自らキーボードを操作して直接実行する作業のみに限定される経営層専属の技術的な活動であり、変更管理や外部委託の管理も含めて部下への権限委譲は一切認められない","6.1で決めた取組みを実施するためのプロセスを計画・実施・管理し、プロセスが計画どおり実施された確信を得るのに必要な文書化情報を維持し、変更を管理し外部委託を管理する","運用段階では計画どおり実施された確信を得るための文書化は一切不要であり、担当者間の口頭での申し送りだけで規格要求を満たせるとされる","運用に関する一連の取組みは、Clause 4における組織の状況の分析さえ終えていれば、その時点ですでに完了しているとみなされる"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 8はリスク対応や目的達成のためのプロセスの運用計画・管理(8.1)、AIリスクアセスメント(8.2)、AIシステム影響評価(8.3)の実施などを求め、計画どおり実施された確信を得るための文書化情報の維持、変更管理、外部委託の管理を含みます。文書化不要とする説明は誤り、運用をトップの直接作業に限る説明は過度な限定、Clause 4の分析で完了とする説明は時点の誤りです。","qEn":"A media company planning Clause 8 (operation) assumes it need not document anything at the operation stage because impact assessment was planned in 6.1. What does Clause 8 require?","oEn":["Operation is limited solely to work top management performs directly at the keyboard, a technical activity exclusive to executives, and no delegation to subordinates is permitted, including for change control or outsourced processes","Plan, implement, and control processes to meet 6.1 actions; keep documented information to have confidence processes were carried out as planned; and control changes and outsourced processes","At the operation stage, documentation to gain confidence that processes ran as planned is unnecessary at all; verbal handover between staff alone is deemed to satisfy the standard","The whole set of operational actions is deemed already complete the moment Clause 4's analysis of organizational context is finished"],"eEn":"Clause 8 requires operational planning and control (8.1), performing the AI risk assessment (8.2) and AI system impact assessment (8.3), keeping documented information to be confident processes were done as planned, and controlling changes and outsourced processes. Dropping documentation is wrong, limiting operation to top management's direct work over-limits it, and treating Clause 4 analysis as completing operation misplaces completion."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるクラウド事業者がClause 9.1『監視・測定・分析・評価』を計画しています。担当者は『とりあえず全ての指標を測って後で考える』方針です。Clause 9.1の要求に照らして、まず決定すべき事項として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["監視測定はマネジメントレビューが開催される当日のみ、その場限りの臨時対応として実施すればよく、測定方法や分析評価の時期をあらかじめ決めておく必要はない","測定対象・方法・実施時期・結果の分析評価時期を含め、何を・どのように監視測定し、いつ・誰が分析評価するかを決定する","監視測定の対象や方法は組織自身ではなく、外部の認証審査員が一方的に決定するものとされる","何も決めないまま、手元にある全ての指標をとりあえず無差別に測定し、分析は後で考える方針にする"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 9.1は、何を監視・測定するか、妥当な結果を得るための方法、いつ実施するか、いつ・誰が結果を分析・評価するかを決定することを求めます。無差別に測定して分析を後回しにする方針は要求に反し、レビュー当日のみの監視や外部審査員任せの決定も不適切です。","qEn":"A cloud provider planning Clause 9.1 (monitoring, measurement, analysis, evaluation) intends to 'measure everything and decide later.' What must it determine first per 9.1?","oEn":["Monitoring and measurement need only be carried out on the single day the management review is held, as a one-off ad hoc response, with no need to decide methods or the timing of analysis in advance","Determine what to monitor/measure, the methods for valid results, when to do it, and when/who analyzes and evaluates the results","The subject and method of monitoring and measurement are deemed to be decided unilaterally by an external certification auditor, not the organization","Decide nothing in advance and just indiscriminately measure whatever metrics are on hand, leaving analysis for later"],"eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires determining what needs monitoring/measuring, the methods ensuring valid results, when it is performed, and when and by whom results are analyzed and evaluated. Indiscriminate measurement, monitoring only on review day, and deferring to auditors are all wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業がClause 9.2『内部監査』を実施予定です。AIMS構築を主導したAIガバナンス責任者が、自らの担当領域を自分で監査することを提案しました。Clause 9.2の要求に照らした問題点として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["内部監査という工程自体が形式的な儀礼にすぎないため、責任者の提案は実施しても意味を持たない","監査プロセスの客観性・公平性を確保する必要があり、監査員は自らの業務を監査すべきでない(独立性の欠如)","内部監査は組織の外部にある認証機関に所属する審査員のみが実施できる活動とされ、社内の要員は担当領域にかかわらず監査員になれないため、この提案は認められない","自分の担当領域を自分自身で監査するのが最も効率的であり、独立性の観点からも特段の問題は生じない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 9.2は、監査基準・範囲の決定、監査員の選定と監査の実施が客観性・公平性を確保することを求めます。自身の担当領域を自ら監査すると独立性が損なわれ、客観性が確保できません。内部監査を形式的な儀礼として不要とみなす説明は誤り、内部監査を外部機関に限定する説明も誤り(内部監査は組織自身または委託で実施)です。","qEn":"For Clause 9.2 (internal audit), the AI governance lead who built the AIMS proposes auditing his own area. What is the problem under 9.2?","oEn":["The internal-audit process itself is merely a formal ritual, so the manager's proposal carries no meaning even if implemented","The audit process must be objective and impartial; auditors should not audit their own work (lack of independence)","Internal audit is held to be performable only by auditors belonging to an external certification body, and in-house personnel can never act as auditors regardless of their area, so the proposal is not allowed","Auditing one's own area oneself is the most efficient approach and raises no particular problem from an independence standpoint"],"eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires audits conducted to ensure objectivity and impartiality; auditing one's own work undermines independence. Calling internal audit a mere formality that is unnecessary is wrong, and restricting internal audits to external bodies is also wrong (they are done by the organization itself or on its behalf)."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるSaaS企業がClause 9.3『マネジメントレビュー』の準備をしています。CTOは『技術的KPIだけを報告すれば十分だ』と考えています。Clause 9.3の入力(インプット)として本来含めるべきものとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["技術的なKPIの数値だけをCTOが淡々と報告すれば、前回レビューの処置状況、内外の課題の変化、利害関係者のフィードバック、リスク対応状況を含むClause 9.3のインプット要求全体を十分に満たすことができる","財務諸表に記載された数値のみを唯一のインプットとして扱い、AIMSの不適合や監視測定の結果、監査結果、利害関係者のフィードバックは一切考慮しない","マネジメントレビューという工程自体が規格上は任意の推奨事項にとどまり、計画された間隔で実施するかどうかは組織の裁量に完全に委ねられている","前回レビューの処置状況、AIMSに関連する内外の課題の変化、パフォーマンス情報(不適合・監視測定結果・監査結果等)、利害関係者のフィードバック、リスク対応状況、改善機会などを含める"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 9.3のインプットには、前回までの処置状況、AIMSに関連する内外課題の変化、パフォーマンス情報(不適合・是正、監視測定結果、監査結果、目的達成度)、利害関係者からのフィードバック、リスクアセスメント結果とリスク対応計画の状況、継続的改善の機会などが含まれます。技術KPIのみや財務諸表のみは不十分、マネジメントレビューを任意とする説明は要求の否定です。","qEn":"Preparing Clause 9.3 (management review), a CTO thinks reporting only technical KPIs suffices. What should the review inputs properly include?","oEn":["Having the CTO report only the technical KPI figures is enough to fully satisfy the Clause 9.3 input requirement, including changes in internal and external issues, interested-party feedback, and risk-treatment status","Treat only the figures in the financial statements as the sole input, never considering the AIMS's nonconformities, monitoring results, audit results, or stakeholder feedback","The management review process itself remains merely an optional recommendation under the standard, entirely left to the organization's discretion whether to hold it at planned intervals","Status of prior actions, changes in internal/external issues, performance information (nonconformities, monitoring/measurement, audit results), interested-party feedback, risk-treatment status, and improvement opportunities"],"eEn":"Clause 9.3 inputs include status of actions from previous reviews, changes in internal/external issues relevant to the AIMS, performance information (nonconformities and corrective actions, monitoring/measurement results, audit results, objective achievement), stakeholder feedback, risk-assessment/treatment status, and opportunities for continual improvement. Technical KPIs alone or financials alone are insufficient; calling management review optional denies the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業でAIモデルが誤作動しインシデントが発生しました。担当者はモデルを再起動して復旧させ、記録を残さずに完了としました。Clause 10.2『不適合及び是正処置』の観点で、この対応に欠けている要素として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["不適合が発生した際は、原因や結果の記録も含めて、いかなる場合も一切の記録を残してはならないと規格は定めている","是正処置はいかなる不適合であってもトップマネジメントの個別承認を得なければ、現場の判断で実施することはできない","再起動によって復旧できた以上、原因の分析や是正処置の有効性レビューを含む追加の対応は一切不要であり、記録もインシデント管理台帳への起票をもって代えられるため、対応はすでに完結している","不適合への対処に加え、原因を除去し再発防止するため原因分析・是正処置の必要性評価・処置の実施・有効性レビューを行い、結果を文書化する必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 10.2は、不適合の修正だけでなく、原因をレビューして除去し再発を防ぐため、是正処置の必要性を評価し、必要な処置を実施し、その有効性をレビューし、不適合の性質・とった処置・結果を文書化情報として保持することを求めます。再起動のみで記録なしは是正処置と証拠保持を欠きます。追加対応不要とする説明は誤り、記録を禁じる説明も誤り、個別承認を必須とする説明は要件の捏造です。","qEn":"After an AI model malfunction/incident, staff restart the model to recover and close it with no record. What does this response lack under Clause 10.2 (nonconformity and corrective action)?","oEn":["The standard mandates that whenever a nonconformity occurs, absolutely no record—including its cause or results—may ever be kept","Corrective action, whatever the nonconformity, can never be taken at the front line's own judgment without individual approval from top management","Since the restart achieved recovery, no additional response including cause analysis or a review of corrective-action effectiveness is needed at all, and raising a ticket in the incident log substitutes for any record, so the response is already complete","Beyond correcting the nonconformity, they must analyze the cause, evaluate the need for corrective action, implement it, review its effectiveness, and document the nonconformity and actions"],"eEn":"Clause 10.2 requires not only correcting the nonconformity but reviewing its cause to prevent recurrence, evaluating the need for corrective action, implementing it, reviewing effectiveness, and retaining documented information on the nonconformity, actions, and results. A restart with no record lacks corrective action and evidence. Saying nothing more is needed is wrong, banning records is wrong, and requiring individual top-management approval invents a requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある組織がClause 7.5『文書化した情報』を整備中です。担当者は『バージョンや保護は気にせず、とにかく大量に文書を作れば適合する』と考えました。Clause 7.5の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["文書は識別や版管理を気にせず作成量を増やせば増やすほど、Clause 7.5の要求に自動的に適合していくと考えてよい","作成・更新時の識別と記述・レビュー承認を管理し、必要な場所で利用可能かつ適切に保護されるよう、配付・アクセス・保管・変更管理・保持・廃棄を管理する","文書は一度作成したら内容の正確性を保つため、組織や利用文脈が変化しリスクが増した場合でも、配付先やアクセス権の見直しを含めて以後は絶対に版を変更・改訂してはならない","文書化した情報の作成・更新・保護に関する管理はClause 7.5の対象外であり、規格上まったく求められていない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 7.5は文書化情報の作成・更新(適切な識別・形式・レビュー承認)と管理(配付・アクセス・検索・利用可能性・保管・保存・変更管理・保持・廃棄)を求めます。量の多さは適合の基準ではありません。文書の管理は対象外とする説明は要求の否定、版の改訂を一切禁じる説明は変更管理の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"An organization building Clause 7.5 (documented information) thinks 'just create lots of documents to conform, ignoring versions and protection.' What does 7.5 require?","oEn":["The more documents are produced without regard to identification or version control, the more automatically it conforms to Clause 7.5's requirements","Control creation/update (identification, description, review, approval) and control of documented information (distribution, access, storage, change control, retention, disposition) so it is available and protected where needed","Once a document is created, to preserve the accuracy of its content it must never be reversioned or revised afterward, even when the organization or the context of use changes and risk increases, and this ban extends to revising its distribution list and access rights","Managing the creation, update, and protection of documented information falls outside Clause 7.5's scope and is not required at all by the standard"],"eEn":"Clause 7.5 requires controlling creation/update (appropriate identification, format, review and approval) and control (distribution, access, retrieval, availability, storage, preservation, change control, retention, disposition). Volume is not the criterion. Saying document control is outside Clause 7.5 denies the requirement; forbidding any revision contradicts change control."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるグローバル企業がClause 4.2『利害関係者(interested parties)のニーズと期待』を検討しています。担当者は『利害関係者は顧客だけを考えれば十分だ』としました。AIMSの文脈でこの範囲設定の問題点として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIの影響を受ける個人・社会、規制当局、従業員、供給者・パートナー、投資家など、AIMSに関連する利害関係者とその関連要求事項を広く特定する必要がある","AIMSの文脈における利害関係者は、契約関係にある顧客のニーズと期待だけをClause 4.2で考慮すれば足り、規制当局や従業員、AIの影響を受ける個人までを特定する必要はない","利害関係者という語は、AIMSの構築を主導する社内のトップマネジメントのみを指す限定的な用語であり、従業員や供給者は含まれない","利害関係者という語は、モデル開発を担う技術部門のスタッフのみを指す、専ら技術的な範囲に限定された用語であり、経営層は含まれない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.2は、AIMSに関連する利害関係者と、その関連する要求事項(法令・規制含む)を決定することを求めます。AI特有の性質上、影響を受ける個人・社会、規制当局、従業員、供給者、投資家など顧客以外も含む広い視野が必要です。顧客だけ、トップマネジメントのみ、技術部門のスタッフのみとする説明はいずれも利害関係者を不当に狭く限定しています。","qEn":"A global company on Clause 4.2 (interested parties' needs and expectations) decides 'considering only customers is enough.' What is the problem in an AIMS context?","oEn":["It must broadly identify interested parties relevant to the AIMS and their requirements—affected individuals/society, regulators, employees, suppliers/partners, investors","In the AIMS context, Clause 4.2 is satisfied by considering only the needs and expectations of customers under contract, with no need to identify regulators, employees, or the individuals affected by the AI","The term interested parties is a narrow term referring only to the internal top management leading the AIMS's construction, excluding employees or suppliers","The term interested parties is a term confined purely to a technical scope, referring only to the technical department's development staff, excluding leadership"],"eEn":"Clause 4.2 requires determining the interested parties relevant to the AIMS and their relevant requirements (including legal/regulatory). Given AI's nature, this spans affected individuals/society, regulators, employees, suppliers, and investors, not just customers. Limiting them to customers only, top management only, or technical staff only unduly narrows the scope."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業がClause 5.3『組織の役割・責任・権限』を割り当てました。しかし『誰がAIMSの各要素に責任を持つか』が曖昧なまま運用を始めました。Clause 5.3の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIMSに関わる役割・責任・権限は、トップマネジメントへのパフォーマンス報告の義務まで含めてすべて外部委託先の担当者に割り当て、社内の要員には権限を一切持たせないようにすべき事項である","トップマネジメントは、AIMSが要求事項に適合することの確保と、AIMSのパフォーマンスをトップに報告することなどの責任・権限を割り当て、組織内に伝達する","役割が曖昧なまま運用を始めても、現場が実務を進めるうちに責任の所在やAIMSへの適合確保の担当は自然と定まっていくため特段の問題はない","役割・責任・権限の割当ては、パフォーマンス評価を扱うAIMS運用の後半段階であるClause 9になって初めて行えばよい事項である"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 5.3は、トップマネジメントが関連する役割に責任と権限を割り当て、組織内に周知することを求めます。特にAIMSが規格要求に適合することの確保、AIMSのパフォーマンスのトップへの報告などの責任・権限を明確にします。曖昧なまま運用してよいとする説明は誤り、Clause 9で初めて割り当てるとする説明は時点の誤り、責任を全面的に外部委託先へ割り当てる説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company assigned roles under Clause 5.3 but began operating with it unclear 'who is responsible for each AIMS element.' What does 5.3 require?","oEn":["All AIMS roles, responsibilities, and authorities, including the duty to report AIMS performance to top management, should be assigned to an outsourcing provider's staff, leaving in-house personnel with no authority whatsoever","Top management assigns and communicates responsibilities/authorities, including ensuring the AIMS conforms to requirements and reporting AIMS performance to top management","Even starting operation with vague roles poses no particular problem, since responsibility and who ensures AIMS conformity naturally sort themselves out as work proceeds","Assigning roles, responsibilities, and authorities is a matter that only needs to happen once reaching Clause 9, the later performance-evaluation stage of AIMS operation"],"eEn":"Clause 5.3 requires top management to assign and communicate relevant responsibilities and authorities, notably ensuring the AIMS conforms to the standard and reporting AIMS performance to top management. Letting roles stay vague is wrong, assigning them only at Clause 9 misplaces timing, and outsourcing all responsibility to an external party is wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるAI企業が『Clause 6.3 変更の計画(planning of changes)』を軽視し、AIMSに影響する重大な変更を場当たり的に行っています。この要求の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["変更はトップマネジメントの承認なく実施できない領域に限る","AIMSの変更が必要と判断された場合、その変更を計画的に(目的・影響・資源・責任・権限を考慮して)実施する","AIMSの変更は自由・無手順に行ってよい","変更は一切許されない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.3は、AIMSの変更の必要性を組織が決定した場合、その変更を計画的な方法で実施することを求め、変更の目的とその潜在的影響、AIMSの完全性、資源の利用可能性、責任・権限の割当てを考慮させます。場当たり的な変更も、変更を一切認めない運用も、この要求の趣旨に合いません。","qEn":"An AI company downplays Clause 6.3 (planning of changes), making major AIMS-affecting changes ad hoc. What is the intent of this requirement?","oEn":["Changes are limited to areas requiring no top-management approval","When the organization determines a need to change the AIMS, the changes shall be carried out in a planned manner (considering purpose, potential consequences, resources, responsibilities/authorities)","AIMS changes may be made freely with no process","No changes are ever permitted"],"eEn":"Clause 6.3 requires that when the organization determines a need for changes to the AIMS, they be carried out in a planned manner, considering purpose and potential consequences, integrity of the AIMS, availability of resources, and allocation of responsibilities and authorities. Neither ad hoc change nor forbidding all change fits the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるスタートアップが『Clause 7.4 コミュニケーション』を軽視し、AIMSに関する内部・外部の情報伝達を無計画に行っています。7.4が決定を求める事項として最も適切な組み合わせはどれですか。","o":["コミュニケーションは一切行わないと決定する","コミュニケーションの対象はトップマネジメントの発言のみに限り、時期や方法は決めないと決定する","何を・いつ・誰と・どのように・誰がコミュニケーションするかを決定する","広報予算と広告媒体のみを決定する"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.4は、AIMSに関連する内部・外部のコミュニケーションについて、何を、いつ、誰と、どのように、誰がコミュニケーションするか(what/when/with whom/how/who)を決定することを求めます。広報予算に矮小化する説明、コミュニケーション自体を行わないとする説明、対象をトップの発言のみに限定する説明は、いずれも不適切です。","qEn":"A startup neglects Clause 7.4 (communication), handling internal/external AIMS communication without planning. What must 7.4 determine?","oEn":["To communicate nothing at all","That communication is limited to top-management statements only, with no timing or method decided","What, when, with whom, how, and who communicates","Only the PR budget and ad media"],"eEn":"Clause 7.4 requires determining the internal and external communications relevant to the AIMS: what, when, with whom, how, and who communicates. Shrinking it to a PR budget, deciding not to communicate at all, and restricting it to top management's statements are all inappropriate."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業が『Clause 10.1 継続的改善』について、『改善は不適合が起きたときだけ行えばよい』と理解しています。この理解の誤りを最もよく正しているのはどれですか。","o":["継続的改善はAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に高める取組みであり、不適合対応に限らず監視測定・監査・レビューの結果を活用して能動的に進める","継続的改善という要求事項はClause 10のどの項にも規定されておらず、監視測定やレビューを扱う別の箇条の範囲に属する事項である","改善は不適合が実際に発生したときにのみ受動的に行えば十分であり、監視測定や監査の結果を能動的に活用する必要はないという理解は規格の趣旨と一致している","改善を行うかどうかは、監視測定や監査の結果、レビューの決定によらず、トップマネジメントのその時々の気分だけで決めればよい"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 10.1はAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に改善することを求めます。是正処置(10.2)は不適合対応ですが、継続的改善はそれに限らず、監視・測定・分析評価、監査、マネジメントレビューの結果を用いて能動的・恒常的に進めます。改善を不適合時に限定する説明は誤り、継続的改善の要求が存在しないとする説明は存在の否定、トップの気分で決める運用は恣意的で不適切です。","qEn":"A company reads Clause 10.1 (continual improvement) as 'improve only when a nonconformity occurs.' What best corrects this?","oEn":["Continual improvement continually enhances the suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness of the AIMS—driven proactively by monitoring, audits, and reviews, not just nonconformities","The continual-improvement requirement is not prescribed anywhere in Clause 10 and instead belongs to a different clause dealing with monitoring and review","Improvement need only be carried out passively when a nonconformity arises, with no need to proactively use monitoring or audit results—matching the standard's intent","Whether to carry out improvement should be decided solely by top management's mood at the time, regardless of monitoring results, audits, or review decisions"],"eEn":"Clause 10.1 requires continually improving the suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness of the AIMS. Corrective action (10.2) handles nonconformities, but continual improvement goes beyond them, using monitoring/measurement/analysis, audits, and management review results proactively. Limiting improvement to nonconformities is wrong, claiming no such requirement exists denies it, and deciding on a whim is arbitrary."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるコンサルタントが『ISO/IEC 42001はISO/IEC 27001とは全く無関係で、共通点はない』と説明しました。両規格の構造上の関係として最も正確なのはどれですか。","o":["両者ともISOのマネジメントシステム規格の共通構造(高位構造/HLS、Clause 4-10)を採用しており、統合運用しやすい","両者は目的も対象もまったく無関係な規格であり、箇条番号の構成、要求事項の並び、統合運用の可否といった面において、共通する点は一切存在しない","27001はマネジメントシステム規格ではなく、あくまで技術的な暗号仕様のみを定めた仕様書として位置づけられる","42001は共通の高位構造(HLS)を採用しておらず、他のISOマネジメントシステム規格とは独立した固有の構造を持つ"],"a":0,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001とISO/IEC 27001はともにISOのマネジメントシステム規格に共通する高位構造(HLS: Clause 4-10)を採用しており、章立てや管理システムの考え方が共通するため統合的に運用しやすいという関係にあります。両者を無関係とする説明は誤り、42001がHLSを採用していないとする説明は構造の誤解、27001を暗号仕様書とする説明は位置づけの誤りです。","qEn":"A consultant claims 'ISO/IEC 42001 is entirely unrelated to ISO/IEC 27001 and shares nothing.' What is the most accurate structural relationship?","oEn":["Both use ISO's common management-system structure (High-Level Structure, Clauses 4-10), making integrated operation easier","The two are standards with entirely unrelated purposes and scopes, sharing no common point whatsoever in clause numbering, the ordering of requirements, or the feasibility of integrated operation","27001 is not a management-system standard and is positioned merely as a specification defining only technical cryptographic requirements","42001 does not adopt the common High-Level Structure (HLS) and instead has its own structure independent of other ISO management-system standards"],"eEn":"Both ISO/IEC 42001 and ISO/IEC 27001 adopt ISO's common High-Level Structure (Clauses 4-10), sharing clause layout and management-system logic, which eases integrated operation. Calling them unrelated is wrong, saying 42001 lacks the HLS misreads its structure, and calling 27001 a cryptographic specification misclassifies it."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業がClause 8.3『AIシステム影響評価』を運用段階で実施する際、担当者は『一度実施すれば以後は不要』と考えました。この理解の誤りを最も適切に正しているのはどれですか。","o":["AIシステムやその利用文脈が変化した場合など、適切な間隔・トリガーで影響評価を実施・見直し、結果を文書化情報として保持する必要がある","影響評価はモデルを開発したベンダーだけが初回の納品時に実施できる工程であり、利用する組織の担当者が運用段階で実施や見直しを行うことは規格上認められず不適合となる","影響評価はシステム導入時に一度実施すれば足り、その後の利用文脈の変化があっても改めて見直す必要は生じない","影響評価という取組みはClause 8の運用管理では一切扱われず、もっぱらリスクアセスメントの箇条だけの範囲である"],"a":0,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、システム・データ・利用文脈・利害関係者への影響が変化し得るため、あらかじめ定めた間隔や重要な変更などのトリガーで実施・見直しし、結果を文書化情報として保持する必要があります。一度きりでは変化に追随できません。Clause 8では扱わないとする説明は要求の否定、ベンダーだけが初回に実施できるとする説明は実施主体を不当に限定しています。","qEn":"Performing Clause 8.3 (AI system impact assessment) at the operation stage, staff assume 'once done, never again.' What best corrects this?","oEn":["Impact assessments must be performed/reviewed at appropriate intervals or triggers (e.g., when the system or its use context changes) and results retained as documented information","The impact assessment is a step only the vendor that developed the model may perform, and only at initial delivery; the using organization's staff performing or reviewing it during operation is a nonconformity under the standard","Impact assessment need only be performed once at system introduction, with no need to revisit it even if the context of use later changes","Impact assessment as an activity is never addressed under Clause 8's operational control and belongs solely to the risk-assessment clause"],"eEn":"An AI system impact assessment must be performed and reviewed at defined intervals or on triggers such as significant changes, because impacts on data, use context, and stakeholders can change; results are retained as documented information. One-off cannot track change. Saying Clause 8 does not cover it denies the requirement; saying only the vendor can do it at first delivery unduly restricts who performs it."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるSaaS企業のトップマネジメントが『AI方針(AI policy)は年に一度でも作れば十分で、内容は他社のコピーでよい』と考えています。Clause 5.2の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AI方針の内容は他社が公開している文面をそのまま流用してよく、自社の目的や文脈、要求事項順守との整合性は一切問われない","AI方針はトップマネジメントではなく、実務を担う一般従業員が主体となって独自に作成し、承認から利害関係者への伝達まで現場だけで完結させるべき文書であり、組織の目的への適合は問われない","AI方針はAIMS運用が進んだ段階であるClause 8の運用計画に至って、初めて作成に着手すればよい文書である","AI方針は組織の目的に適し、AIの目的の枠組みを与え、要求事項順守と継続的改善のコミットメントを含み、文書化・伝達・利害関係者に応じ入手可能にする"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 5.2はトップマネジメントがAI方針を確立することを求め、方針は組織の目的に適し、AIの目的設定の枠組みを与え、要求事項を満たすコミットメントとAIMSの継続的改善のコミットメントを含みます。さらに文書化し、組織内に伝達し、必要に応じ利害関係者が入手できるようにします。他社文面の流用は組織の状況に適さず不適切、現場だけでの作成は作成主体の誤り、Clause 8で初めて着手する説明は時点の誤りです。","qEn":"A SaaS firm's top management thinks the AI policy 'just needs to exist once a year and can be copied from another company.' What does Clause 5.2 require?","oEn":["The AI policy's content may simply be copied verbatim from another company's published text, with its alignment to the organization's purpose, context, or compliance never questioned","The AI policy is a document that general employees doing the day-to-day work should draft on their own initiative rather than top management, completing approval and communication to interested parties entirely at the working level, with no question of whether it suits the organization's purpose","The AI policy is a document that only needs to have its drafting begun once reaching the Clause 8 operational planning stage of AIMS operation","The AI policy must be appropriate to the organization's purpose, provide a framework for AI objectives, include commitments to meeting requirements and continual improvement, and be documented, communicated, and available to interested parties as appropriate"],"eEn":"Clause 5.2 requires top management to establish an AI policy appropriate to the organization's purpose, providing a framework for setting AI objectives, including commitments to satisfy applicable requirements and to continually improve the AIMS, documented, communicated internally, and available to interested parties as appropriate. A copied policy does not fit the organization's context; frontline-only authorship misstates who writes it; starting only at Clause 8 misplaces timing."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業がClause 8.1『運用の計画及び管理』で外部委託先(サブサービス)を使っています。担当者は『委託したのだから責任も全て委託先に移る』と考えました。この理解の問題点として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["業務を外部委託すれば説明責任も含めて完全に委託先へ移転するため、組織側にはそれ以上何の管理責任も残らない","外部委託先が担うプロセスについては、契約上どのような取り決めがあっても組織側が監査を行うことは認められない","外部委託という業務形態自体が、ISO/IEC 42001の要求事項によって一律かつ全面的に禁止されている","外部委託したプロセスも組織が決定し管理下に置く必要があり、委託しても組織の説明責任は残る"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 8.1は外部委託(outsourced)プロセスも組織が決定し、管理下に置くことを求めます。委託によって作業の実施は移転しても、AIMSの要求事項適合や成果に対する組織の説明責任は残ります。責任の完全移転とする説明は誤り、委託を一律禁止とする説明も誤り、委託先への監査を認めないとする説明は委託先の管理・監査を否定する誤りです。","qEn":"Under Clause 8.1 (operational planning and control) a company uses an outsourced sub-service and assumes 'having outsourced, all responsibility transfers to the provider.' What is the flaw?","oEn":["Outsourcing the work transfers accountability entirely to the provider, leaving no management responsibility for the organization","Regarding processes an outsourced provider carries out, the organization is never permitted to audit them, whatever the contractual terms","Outsourcing itself as a business arrangement is uniformly and entirely prohibited by ISO/IEC 42001's requirements","Outsourced processes must still be determined and controlled by the organization; accountability remains with the organization despite outsourcing"],"eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires the organization to determine and control outsourced processes. Outsourcing may transfer execution, but the organization's accountability for AIMS conformity and outcomes remains. Claiming full transfer is wrong, banning outsourcing outright is wrong, and denying any audit of providers denies control of providers."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業が認証取得を目指し、Clause 4-10のうち『どれかを選んで実装すればよい』と誤解しています。ISO/IEC 42001の要求事項の性質として最も正確なのはどれですか。","o":["Clause 4-10は認証審査の際に参考として読まれるだけの情報にとどまり、適合性の判定対象には含まれない","Clause 4-10の要求事項は原則としてすべて適合が必要で、Annex A管理策はリスクに応じて採用/除外を正当化できる(SoAで示す)","Annex Aの管理策はいかなるリスク状況であっても全て必須の要求事項であり、除外という選択肢自体が規格上存在しない","Clause 4-10は自由に選べる任意メニューであり、適用しない箇条の正当化をSoAに記載しさえすれば、自社が実装したいと考える箇条だけを選んで満たすことで認証を取得できる"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 4-10の『要求事項(shall)』は認証の適合対象で原則すべて満たす必要があります。一方Annex A管理策はリスクアセスメント/対応の結果に応じて採用・除外でき、その正当化を適用宣言書(SoA)で示します。要求事項を任意の選択メニューとする説明は誤り、管理策を全て必須で固定とする説明も誤り、要求事項を参考扱いとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"Aiming for certification, a company thinks it can 'pick and choose which of Clauses 4-10 to implement.' What is the accurate nature of the requirements?","oEn":["Clauses 4-10 remain merely informative reading during the certification audit and are not included in the scope of conformity assessment","The Clause 4-10 requirements must generally all be met; Annex A controls may be included/excluded based on risk, justified in the SoA","All Annex A controls are mandatory requirements regardless of risk circumstances, and the option to exclude any of them does not exist under the standard","Clauses 4-10 are a freely selectable optional menu, and as long as the clauses not applied are justified in the SoA, certification can be obtained by meeting only the clauses the company wants to implement"],"eEn":"The 'shall' requirements of Clauses 4-10 are subject to conformity and must generally all be met; by contrast, Annex A controls may be included or excluded based on the risk assessment/treatment, justified in the Statement of Applicability. Treating the requirements as an optional menu is wrong, making all controls mandatory is wrong, and treating the requirements as merely informative is wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるヘルスケアAI企業が『Clause 7.1 資源』を軽視し、AIMSに必要な人員・予算・計算資源・データを確保しないまま運用を始めました。Clause 7.1の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIMSの確立・実施・維持・継続的改善に必要な資源を決定し、提供する","資源は不足が顕在化してから都度確保すればよく、必要な資源を事前に決定して提供する必要はない","資源はトップマネジメントが個人的に負担する","資源はClause 10で初めて検討する"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.1は、AIMSの確立・実施・維持・継続的改善に必要な資源を組織が決定し提供することを求めます。AI特有の計算資源・データ・専門人材なども含まれます。不足が顕在化してから確保すればよいとする説明は事前確保の否定、トップの個人負担とする説明は誤り、Clause 10で初めて検討するとする説明は時点の誤りです。","qEn":"A healthcare AI firm neglects Clause 7.1 (resources), operating without securing people, budget, compute, or data. What is the intent of 7.1?","oEn":["Determine and provide the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve the AIMS","Resources need only be secured case by case once a shortage becomes visible, with no need to determine and provide the required resources in advance","Top management personally funds the resources","Resources are first considered in Clause 10"],"eEn":"Clause 7.1 requires the organization to determine and provide the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain, and continually improve the AIMS, including AI-specific compute, data, and expertise. Securing resources only after shortages appear denies advance provision, making it the top manager's personal burden is wrong, and considering it only at Clause 10 misplaces the timing."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業が『Clause 7.3 認識(awareness)』を軽視し、従業員にAI方針や自らの貢献・逸脱の影響を伝えていません。Clause 7.3の要求として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["組織の管理下で働く人々がAI方針、自らのAIMSへの貢献(有効性向上の便益)、要求事項に適合しないことの意味を認識するようにする","認識(awareness)に関する事項はClause 4の組織の状況の分析においてまとめて扱われる、独立した項目ではない事項である","認識の確保が求められるのは組織の外部にいる利害関係者のみに限定され、内部の従業員には要求が及ばない","従業員へのAI方針の周知は特に必要とされておらず、方針の内容は経営層だけが把握していれば十分とされる"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.3は、組織の管理下で働く人々が、AI方針、AIMSの有効性向上に対する自らの貢献(便益を含む)、AIMS要求事項に適合しないことの意味を認識することを求めます。方針の周知は不要とする説明は誤り、認識をClause 4でまとめて扱うとする説明は扱う章の誤り、外部の利害関係者のみに限る説明は対象の誤りです。","qEn":"A company neglects Clause 7.3 (awareness), not communicating the AI policy or the implications of nonconformity to employees. What does 7.3 require?","oEn":["Persons doing work under the organization's control shall be aware of the AI policy, their contribution to AIMS effectiveness (benefits), and the implications of not conforming","Awareness-related matters are handled together within Clause 4's analysis of organizational context, not as an independent item","Ensuring awareness is required only of interested parties external to the organization, and the requirement does not extend to internal employees","Communicating the AI policy to employees is not particularly required; it is deemed sufficient for only leadership to be aware of its content"],"eEn":"Clause 7.3 requires persons working under the organization's control to be aware of the AI policy, their contribution to the effectiveness of the AIMS (including benefits of improved performance), and the implications of not conforming. Saying the policy need not be communicated is wrong, folding awareness into Clause 4 misplaces the clause, and limiting it to external parties is wrong."},
// ===== D3: Annex A controls & Statement of Applicability ×16 =====
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がAnnex Aの管理策を検討中で、担当者は『Annex Aの38すべての管理策を必ず実装しなければ認証できない』と考えています。Annex AとSoAの関係として最も正確なのはどれですか。","o":["Annex Aに列挙された38の管理策はすべて必須であり、いずれか一つでも除外すれば認証を取得できなくなる","Annex Aの管理策はリスクアセスメント/対応の結果に基づき採用/除外でき、除外にも正当な理由が必要で、それらをSoAに記載する","Annex Aは規格本文に添付された参考情報にすぎず、SoAという文書自体を作成する必要はまったくない","SoAはAnnex Aの38の管理策をすべて実装し終えた後、Clause 9.3のマネジメントレビューの場で初めて作成すればよい文書であり、除外の正当な理由は記載しない"],"a":1,"e":"Annex A管理策はリスク対応の必要性に応じて選択(採用/除外)可能で、除外する場合もその正当化が必要です。これらを適用宣言書(SoA)にまとめ、必要な管理策・実施状況・採用/除外の理由を示します。全て必須とする説明は誤り、SoA自体が不要とする説明も誤り、全実装後のマネジメントレビューで初めて作るとする説明は作成時点(6.1.3)の誤りです。","qEn":"Considering Annex A, a staffer believes 'all 38 Annex A controls must be implemented or you cannot certify.' What is the accurate relationship of Annex A and the SoA?","oEn":["All 38 controls listed in Annex A are mandatory, and excluding even a single one makes certification impossible","Annex A controls may be included/excluded based on the risk assessment/treatment, with justification for exclusions, all recorded in the SoA","Annex A is merely reference material attached to the standard's body text, and there is no need whatsoever to create an SoA document at all","The SoA is a document first created at the Clause 9.3 management review, only after all 38 Annex A controls have been implemented, and it does not record justifications for exclusions"],"eEn":"Annex A controls are selected (included/excluded) based on risk-treatment needs, and exclusions must be justified. These are captured in the Statement of Applicability, showing necessary controls, implementation status, and inclusion/exclusion rationale. Making all controls mandatory is wrong, dropping the SoA is wrong, and creating it only after full implementation at management review misplaces its creation (it is 6.1.3)."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業のSoAで、あるAnnex A管理策が『適用対象外(除外)』とされていますが、理由欄が空白です。認証審査の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["除外すると決めた管理策については、そもそもSoAの一覧に記載してはならないとされている","除外の理由は記載が任意とされており、理由欄が空白であっても審査上は問題が生じない","SoAには採用した管理策のみを記載すればよく、除外した管理策は記載の対象外とされる","除外した管理策にも正当化(当該リスクになぜ不要か)が必要であり、理由欄の空白は不適合となり得る"],"a":3,"e":"SoAは各Annex A管理策について、必要か否か、実施しているか、採用/除外の正当化を示す必要があります。除外する場合もその理由(なぜ当該リスクに不要か)を記載しなければならず、空白は不適合の指摘対象となり得ます。除外理由を任意とする説明や、除外した管理策を載せてはならないとする説明はSoAの要件を誤り、採用分のみ記載すればよいとする説明も除外管理策を載せない誤りです。","qEn":"In a company's SoA, an Annex A control is marked 'excluded' but the justification field is blank. What is the best audit observation?","oEn":["A control decided for exclusion must not even be listed in the SoA's list to begin with","Stating the reason for exclusion is optional, so a blank reason field causes no problem in the audit","The SoA only needs to list included controls; excluded ones are held to be outside its scope","Excluded controls also require justification (why they are not needed for the risk); a blank field can be a nonconformity"],"eEn":"The SoA must show, for each Annex A control, whether it is necessary, whether implemented, and the justification for inclusion/exclusion. Exclusions require a rationale (why not needed for the risk); a blank is a potential nonconformity. Calling the rationale optional or forbidding excluded controls in the SoA misstates its requirements, and listing only adopted controls wrongly omits excluded controls."},
{"d":"D3","q":"あるAI企業が、学習・運用に用いるデータの出所・品質・準備・来歴を管理したいと考えています。Annex Aの管理目的のうち、最も直接的に関係するのはどれですか。","o":["AIシステムのためのデータ(データの取得・品質・準備・来歴等の管理)に関する管理策","AIのための資源に関する管理策のうち計算資源のみ","AIシステムのための情報(利用者への説明資料や問合せ窓口の提供)に関する管理策","第三者・顧客関係に関する管理策"],"a":0,"e":"Annex Aには『AIシステムのためのデータ』に関する管理目的があり、データの取得・品質・準備・来歴(provenance)などデータガバナンスを扱います。利用者等への情報提供、第三者関係、計算資源に関する管理策は、データそのものの管理には該当しません。","qEn":"An AI firm wants to manage the source, quality, preparation, and provenance of data used in training and operation. Which Annex A objective is most directly relevant?","oEn":["Controls on data for AI systems (management of data acquisition, quality, preparation, provenance, etc.)","Controls on resources for AI, but only compute resources","Controls on information for AI systems (providing user-facing explanations and a contact point)","Controls on third-party and customer relationships"],"eEn":"Annex A includes an objective on 'data for AI systems' covering data acquisition, quality, preparation, and provenance, i.e., data governance. Controls on information to users and other parties, third-party relationships, and compute resources do not target data itself."},
{"d":"D3","q":"あるAI企業が、AIシステムの企画・設計・検証・運用・監視・廃棄という一連の段階を体系的に管理したいと考えています。Annex Aの管理目的のうち最も適合するのはどれですか。","o":["AIシステムのライフサイクルに関する管理策(責任ある設計・開発・検証・運用・監視等)","第三者・顧客関係に関する管理策のみがこれに該当し、自社内の開発工程は対象に含まれない","AI方針に関する管理策のみがこれに該当し、開発・検証といった工程は別枠で扱われる","組織の内部体制に関する管理策のみがこれに該当し、廃棄までの一連の工程は対象外である"],"a":0,"e":"Annex Aには『AIシステムのライフサイクル』に関する管理目的があり、責任ある設計・開発、検証・妥当性確認、デプロイ、運用・監視、文書化などライフサイクル全体の管理を扱います。AI方針、組織の内部体制、第三者関係の管理目的はいずれも別の管理目的で、ライフサイクル全体の直接の受け皿ではありません。","qEn":"An AI firm wants to systematically manage the stages of planning, design, verification, operation, monitoring, and retirement of AI systems. Which Annex A objective fits best?","oEn":["Controls on the AI system life cycle (responsible design/development/verification/operation/monitoring)","Only the controls on third-party and customer relationships apply here, excluding development stages","Only the controls on AI policy apply here, with development and verification handled separately","Only the controls on internal organization apply here, excluding the whole sequence through disposal"],"eEn":"Annex A includes an objective on the 'AI system life cycle' covering responsible design and development, verification and validation, deployment, operation and monitoring, and documentation. The objectives on AI policy, internal organization, and third parties are other objectives, not the direct home for the whole life cycle."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業が生成AIをベンダーのAPI経由で組み込みます。ベンダーの責務・契約・データ取扱い・供給リスクを管理したい場合、Annex Aの管理目的のうち最も直接的に関係するのはどれですか。","o":["AI方針に関する管理策のみが該当し、供給者との責任分担は方針文書の対象外とされる","AIのための資源に関する管理策のみが該当し、契約や責任分担の統制は対象外とされる","AIシステム影響評価に関する管理策のみが該当し、ベンダーとの契約関係は対象外とされる","第三者及び顧客関係に関する管理策(供給者・顧客との責任分担・契約等)"],"a":3,"e":"Annex Aには『第三者及び顧客関係』に関する管理目的があり、供給者・第三者・顧客との責任分担、契約、リスク配分などを扱います。ベンダーAPI利用に伴うベンダー管理はここに直接該当します。AIのための資源、影響評価、AI方針の管理目的は関連はしても、第三者関係の直接の受け皿ではありません。","qEn":"A company embeds generative AI via a vendor API and wants to manage the vendor's responsibilities, contracts, data handling, and supply risk. Which Annex A objective is most directly relevant?","oEn":["Only the controls on AI policy apply here, with supplier responsibility sharing outside the policy document's scope","Only the controls on resources for AI apply here, excluding controls over contracts and responsibility sharing","Only the controls on AI system impact assessment apply here, excluding the contractual relationship with the vendor","Controls on third-party and customer relationships (responsibility sharing, contracts with suppliers/customers)"],"eEn":"Annex A includes an objective on 'third-party and customer relationships' covering responsibility allocation, contracts, and risk sharing with suppliers/third parties/customers, the direct home for managing a vendor API. The objectives on resources, impact assessment, and AI policy are related but not the direct home for third-party management."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある組織が、Annex Aの実装にあたり、各管理策をどう具体化すべきか実装のヒントを探しています。ISO/IEC 42001における管理策の実装指針(ガイダンス)を提供するのは主にどこですか。","o":["ISO 9001の付属書","Annex B(Annex Aの各管理策をどう実装するかのガイダンス)","本文Clause 4-10のみ","Annex Aの表と管理目的の一覧のみで、実装ガイダンスは存在しない"],"a":1,"e":"ISO/IEC 42001では、Annex Aに管理策の一覧(目的と管理策)が示され、Annex Bにそれら管理策の実装に関するガイダンスが置かれています。本文Clause 4-10は要求事項本体で実装ヒント集ではなく、実装ガイダンスは存在しないとする説明は誤り、ISO 9001の付属書は無関係な別規格です。","qEn":"An organization implementing Annex A seeks guidance on how to realize each control. In ISO/IEC 42001, where is implementation guidance for the controls primarily provided?","oEn":["An annex of ISO 9001","Annex B (guidance on how to implement each of the Annex A controls)","Only the main body, Clauses 4-10","Only the Annex A table and its list of control objectives; no implementation guidance exists"],"eEn":"In ISO/IEC 42001, Annex A lists the controls (objectives and controls), and Annex B provides implementation guidance for those controls. The body Clauses 4-10 are the requirements, not implementation hints; saying no guidance exists is wrong; an annex of ISO 9001 belongs to an unrelated standard."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がSoAの記載内容について議論しています。適用宣言書(SoA)に含めるべき事項として最も適切な組み合わせはどれですか。","o":["採用した管理策の一覧のみを記載すればよく、除外の判断やその正当化についての記述は特に求められていない","会社全体の売上目標の達成率と、従業員個々の人事評価の結果をまとめて記載する社内向けの文書である","従業員の氏名や住所など個人情報の一覧を、審査官への提出に備えてあらかじめ記載しておく文書である","リスク対応に必要な管理策とその採用の是非、採用したものの実施状況、Annex A管理策の採用/除外の正当化"],"a":3,"e":"SoAには、リスク対応に必要な管理策、それらを採用しているか(および実施状況)、Annex A管理策の採用/除外とその正当化を含めます。採用分のみで除外の正当化を欠く記載は不十分、売上目標や人事評価は経営指標、従業員の個人情報は無関係で、いずれもSoAの内容ではありません。","qEn":"A company debates SoA contents. What should the Statement of Applicability include?","oEn":["Only a list of included controls needs to be recorded, with no particular requirement to note exclusion decisions or their justification","An internal document summarizing the company's overall revenue-target achievement rate and each employee's HR appraisal results","A document listing employees' personal information such as name and address, prepared in advance for submission to the auditor","The controls necessary for risk treatment and whether they are included, the implementation status of included ones, and justification for including/excluding Annex A controls"],"eEn":"The SoA includes the controls necessary for risk treatment, whether they are included (and implementation status), and justification for including/excluding Annex A controls. Listing only adopted controls omits exclusion justification, sales targets and HR evaluations are business metrics, and employees' personal data is unrelated, so none is the SoA content."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がAnnex Aの『AI方針』に関する管理目的を実装します。担当者は『経営理念を1文追加すれば十分だ』と考えました。この管理目的の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AI方針を正式に策定した場合であっても、その内容を適用宣言書(SoA)に記載することは規格上禁止されている","経営理念を記した既存文書に一文を書き加えて社内ポータルに置くだけで、AI方針に関するこの管理目的も、セキュリティやプライバシーの方針との整合も十分に満たされる","AIの責任ある開発・提供・利用を方向づけるAI方針を確立・伝達し、必要に応じ関連方針(セキュリティ・プライバシー等)と整合させる","AI方針は技術仕様書とまったく同一の内容を指す語であり、別立ての文書として作成する必要は生じない"],"a":2,"e":"Annex Aにおける『AI方針』に関する管理目的は、組織のAIに関する意図・方向性を示すAI方針を確立し、伝達し、必要に応じて他の方針(情報セキュリティ・プライバシー等)と整合させることを扱います。理念に1文追加するだけでは不十分。AI方針を技術仕様と同一視する説明は混同、SoAへの記載を禁ずる説明は誤りです。","qEn":"Implementing the Annex A objective on 'AI policy,' a staffer thinks 'adding one sentence to the corporate philosophy is enough.' What is the intent of this objective?","oEn":["Even after formally formulating an AI policy, recording its content in the Statement of Applicability (SoA) is prohibited under the standard","Merely adding one sentence to the existing corporate-philosophy document and placing it on the intranet fully satisfies this control objective on AI policy and its alignment with the security and privacy policies","Establish and communicate an AI policy directing responsible development/provision/use of AI, aligned as needed with related policies (security, privacy)","The AI policy is a term referring to content entirely identical to a technical specification, with no need to create it as a separate document"],"eEn":"The Annex A objective on 'AI policy' concerns establishing and communicating an AI policy that directs the organization's responsible development/provision/use of AI, aligned with related policies (security, privacy) as needed. One sentence is insufficient. Equating the AI policy with a technical spec confuses the two; banning it from the SoA is wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がAnnex Aの『AIシステムの影響評価』に関する管理目的を実装します。担当者は『影響評価はClause 6の要求で扱うので、Annex Aに同種の管理策があるのは矛盾だ』と述べました。この理解の誤りを最も適切に正しているのはどれですか。","o":["影響評価という取組みはClause 6でのみ扱われるべき事項であり、Annex Aにある同種の管理策は規格の編集上の矛盾なので、SoAで採用の要否を検討せずに無視してよい","影響評価という取組みはClause 8の運用管理にのみ規定されており、Clause 6のリスク及び機会には存在しない","Annex Aには影響評価に関する管理目的自体がそもそも存在しないため、担当者の指摘はまったくの誤りである","Clause 6の要求(影響評価プロセスの確立)とAnnex Aの管理策(影響評価の実施・文書化等の統制)は相互補完的で、矛盾ではない"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 6.1.4はAIシステム影響評価のプロセス確立を要求し、Annex Aには影響評価の実施・文書化・活用に関する管理策があります。両者は矛盾せず、要求事項(何を達成すべきか)と管理策(具体的統制)として相互補完します。同種の管理策を矛盾として無視してよいとする説明は誤り、影響評価の管理目的が存在しないとする説明は存在の否定、Clause 8にのみ規定されるとする説明は所在の誤りです。","qEn":"Implementing the Annex A objective on 'AI system impact assessment,' a staffer says 'impact assessment is a Clause 6 requirement, so having similar controls in Annex A is contradictory.' What best corrects this?","oEn":["Impact assessment is a matter to be addressed only in Clause 6, and the similar Annex A controls are an editorial contradiction in the standard, so they may be ignored without even considering their inclusion in the SoA","Impact assessment as an activity is prescribed only under Clause 8's operational control and does not exist within Clause 6's risk and opportunity requirements","No control objective for impact assessment exists in Annex A in the first place, so the person's claim is entirely mistaken","The Clause 6 requirement (establishing the impact-assessment process) and the Annex A controls (performing/documenting the assessment) are complementary, not contradictory"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.4 requires establishing the AI system impact-assessment process, while Annex A provides controls on performing, documenting, and using assessments. They complement each other as requirement (what to achieve) and controls (how), not a contradiction. Ignoring the similar controls as an editorial conflict is wrong, saying the objective does not exist denies it, and saying it appears only in Clause 8 misplaces it."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がAnnex Aの『AIのための資源(resources for AI systems)』に関する管理目的を実装します。この管理目的が扱う資源として最も網羅的に正しいのはどれですか。","o":["この管理目的が扱う資源は広告予算のみとされ、人的資源までは含まない","この管理目的が扱う資源は現金のみとされ、データや計算資源までは含まない","この管理目的が扱う資源はオフィスの物理的スペースと什器のみとされ、データや計算資源、人的資源は対象外である","データ・ツール・システム(計算)・人的資源など、AIシステムに必要な資源とその文書化"],"a":3,"e":"Annex Aにおける『AIのための資源』に関する管理目的は、AIシステムに必要な資源(データ、ツール、システム資源〔計算・インフラ〕、人的資源〔力量〕など)を特定し文書化することを扱います。現金のみ、広告予算のみ、オフィスの物理スペースのみとする説明は、いずれもこの管理目的が中心的に扱う資源ではありません。","qEn":"Implementing the Annex A objective on 'resources for AI systems,' which best captures the resources it addresses?","oEn":["The resources this control objective covers are held to be advertising budget alone, not including human resources","The resources this control objective covers are held to be cash alone, not including data or compute resources","The resources this control objective covers are held to be physical office space and furniture alone, excluding data, compute, and human resources","Data, tooling, system (compute) resources, and human resources needed for AI systems, and their documentation"],"eEn":"The Annex A objective on 'resources for AI systems' addresses identifying and documenting the resources needed for AI systems: data, tooling, system/compute resources, and human resources (competence). Cash only, ad budget only, and office space only are not the core resources it addresses."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業がAnnex Aの『利害関係者への情報提供(information for interested parties)』の管理目的を検討中です。この管理目的が主に扱う内容として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIシステムの利用者や影響を受ける者に対し、システムの目的・能力・限界・適切な利用・問合せ手段等の情報を適切に提供する","計算資源の割当てスケジュールの社内管理のみを扱う管理目的であり、利用者への説明責任は対象範囲に含まれない","競合他社が保有する内部資料を入手し、自社の戦略立案に流用することが目的である","AIシステムの学習に用いた計算資源の使用量と電力消費量を毎月集計し、経営層だけに内部報告することを目的とする"],"a":0,"e":"この管理目的は、AIシステムの利用者や影響を受ける利害関係者に対し、システムの目的・能力・限界、適切な利用方法、問い合わせ手段などの情報を適切に提供することを扱い、透明性の実装に寄与します。計算資源の割当てや使用量の社内集計、競合他社の内部資料の流用は該当しません。","qEn":"Considering the Annex A objective on 'information for interested parties,' what does it primarily address?","oEn":["Providing appropriate information to users and affected parties about the system's purpose, capabilities, limitations, proper use, and contact channels","A control objective concerned only with internally managing the compute-resource allocation schedule, with accountability to users not included in its scope","The aim is obtaining a competitor's internal documents and diverting them to the organization's own strategic planning","The aim is to tally monthly the compute resource usage and the power consumption used to train the AI system, and to report those figures internally to top management only"],"eEn":"This objective addresses appropriately providing users and affected stakeholders with information about the AI system's purpose, capabilities, limitations, proper use, and contact means, implementing transparency. Internal scheduling or tallying of compute resources and reusing competitors' internal documents do not apply."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業が、SoAを作成せずにリスク対応だけ実施し『管理策は選んで実装したのでSoAは省略した』としています。認証審査での扱いとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["SoAはAnnex Bに掲載された管理策についてのみ作成が不要とされている文書である","SoAはClause 4において作成が任意とされる、単なる参考資料に位置づけられる文書である","SoAは規格上あくまで任意の参考文書とされ、省略しても不適合とはみなされない","SoAはClause 6.1.3で要求される必須の文書化情報であり、作成を省略すれば不適合となり得る"],"a":3,"e":"適用宣言書(SoA)はClause 6.1.3で要求される必須の文書化情報で、必要な管理策・実施状況・採用/除外の正当化を示します。省略は要求事項違反として不適合の対象となり得ます。任意の参考文書とする説明は誤り、Annex B掲載の管理策についてのみ不要とする説明はSoAの対象の誤り、Clause 4で作成が任意とする説明は作成根拠と任意性の誤りです。","qEn":"A company performed risk treatment but skipped the SoA, saying 'we selected and implemented controls, so we omitted the SoA.' How is this treated in a certification audit?","oEn":["The SoA is a document that only need not be created for controls listed in Annex B","The SoA is positioned as merely a reference document, optional to create under Clause 4","The SoA is merely an optional reference document, and omitting it is not a nonconformity","The SoA is mandatory documented information required by Clause 6.1.3; omitting it can be a nonconformity"],"eEn":"The Statement of Applicability is mandatory documented information required by Clause 6.1.3, showing necessary controls, implementation status, and inclusion/exclusion justification. Omitting it can be a nonconformity. Calling it an optional reference document is wrong, exempting only the Annex B controls misstates its scope, and calling it optional under Clause 4 misstates its basis and optionality."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業のAI開発チームが、モデルの検証・妥当性確認(verification and validation)をライフサイクル管理の一部として位置づけるべきか迷っています。Annex Aの観点で最も適切な考え方はどれですか。","o":["検証・妥当性確認を実施した結果は、開発の内部資料にとどめ、SoAには一切含めてはならない事項とされる","検証・妥当性確認はライフサイクル管理とは切り離され、リリース後に品質保証部門が任意で行う、開発工程とは無関係の独立した工程として位置づけられる","検証・妥当性確認はライフサイクル管理ではなく、AI方針に関する管理目的の枠内で扱われるべき事項である","責任あるAIシステムのライフサイクル管理の一部として、開発段階で検証・妥当性確認を計画・実施し、その結果を文書化する"],"a":3,"e":"Annex Aに定めるAIシステムライフサイクルの管理目的には、責任ある設計・開発の一環として検証・妥当性確認(V&V)を計画・実施し文書化する管理策が含まれます。ライフサイクルと無関係な任意の工程とする説明は誤り、AI方針の管理目的で扱うとする説明は管理目的の誤り、結果をSoAに含めてはならないとする説明はSoA記載可否の誤りです。","qEn":"An AI dev team is unsure whether model verification and validation belongs to life-cycle management. What is the best view under Annex A?","oEn":["Results of performing verification and validation are to be kept as internal development material only and must never be included in the SoA","Verification and validation sit outside life-cycle management, as an independent process that QA may optionally run after release","Verification and validation should be addressed not under life-cycle management but within the scope of the AI policy control objective instead","As part of responsible AI system life-cycle management, plan and perform verification and validation during development and document the results"],"eEn":"The Annex A AI-system-life-cycle objective includes controls to plan, perform, and document verification and validation as part of responsible design and development. Calling it an optional process unrelated to the life cycle is wrong, assigning it to the AI policy objective misassigns the objective, and banning results from the SoA misstates SoA coverage."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業が『Annex Aの管理策を実装すれば、Clause 4-10の要求事項は満たさなくてよい』と考えています。両者の関係として最も正確なのはどれですか。","o":["Clause 4-10はAnnex Aに含まれる数ある管理策のうちの一部にすぎない、附属的で下位に位置づけられる項目にとどまるとされる","Clause 4-10の要求事項(マネジメントシステムの枠組み)は満たす必要があり、Annex A管理策はリスク対応の具体手段として要求事項の中で用いられる","Annex Aの管理策さえ実装すれば、Clause 4-10が定める適用範囲の決定やリスクアセスメント、内部監査といった要求事項は満たさなくてもよいものとみなされる","Annex AとClause 4-10は互いに排他的な枠組みであり、規格上両者を組織のAIMSに同時に適用することは想定されていない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 4-10はAIMSの枠組み(状況・リーダーシップ・計画・支援・運用・評価・改善)を定める要求事項で、必ず満たす必要があります。Annex A管理策はリスク対応(6.1.3)の中で選択・適用される具体的手段であり、要求事項の代替ではありません。管理策の実装で代替できるとする説明は誤り、Clause 4-10を管理策の一部とする説明は包含関係の誤り、両者を排他とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company thinks 'implementing Annex A controls means Clauses 4-10 need not be met.' What is the accurate relationship?","oEn":["Clauses 4-10 are deemed merely one subordinate part among the many controls contained within Annex A, positioned as lesser items","The Clause 4-10 requirements (the management-system framework) must be met; Annex A controls are concrete means used within risk treatment","Simply implementing the Annex A controls is deemed to mean the Clause 4-10 requirements, such as determining scope, risk assessment, and internal audit, need not be met at all","Annex A and Clauses 4-10 are mutually exclusive frameworks, and applying both to an organization's AIMS at the same time is not envisaged under the standard"],"eEn":"Clauses 4-10 define the AIMS framework (context, leadership, planning, support, operation, evaluation, improvement) and must be met; Annex A controls are concrete means selected within risk treatment (6.1.3), not a substitute for the requirements. Claiming controls can substitute is wrong, treating Clauses 4-10 as part of the controls misstates containment, and calling the two exclusive is wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある企業のSoAレビューで、リスクアセスメントで特定された重大なAIリスクに対応する管理策が『除外』とされ、理由が『実装コストが高いため』とだけ書かれています。審査上の最も適切な評価はどれですか。","o":["重大リスクに必要な管理策をコストのみを理由に除外するのは正当化が不十分で、残余リスクの受容根拠が示されない限り不適合となり得る","コストを理由にした除外は、対応するリスクの重大性にかかわらずSoA上の正当な理由として常に認められ、残余リスクの受容根拠やリスクオーナーの承認を示す必要はない","管理策を除外するという判断自体は経営上の裁量事項であり、認証審査の確認対象にはそもそも含まれない","除外の理由を記載する欄はSoAの様式上もともと不要とされており、空欄のまま提出しても審査上差し支えない"],"a":0,"e":"管理策の除外は、当該リスクに不要であること等の妥当な正当化が必要です。重大リスクに対して『コストが高い』だけでは、残余リスクの評価・受容(適切な権限者による承認)の根拠が示されず、不適合となり得ます。コスト理由を常に正当とする説明は誤り、除外理由の記載を不要とする説明も誤り、除外判断を審査対象外とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"In an SoA review, a control addressing a significant AI risk is 'excluded' with the sole reason 'implementation cost is high.' What is the best audit evaluation?","oEn":["Excluding a control needed for a significant risk solely on cost is insufficient justification; absent a basis for accepting residual risk, it can be a nonconformity","An exclusion justified by cost is always accepted as a valid reason in the SoA regardless of the severity of the corresponding risk, with no need to show a basis for accepting the residual risk or the risk owner's approval","The decision to exclude a control is purely a matter of managerial discretion and is not included within the scope of certification audit review to begin with","The field for stating the exclusion reason was never required in the SoA format to begin with, so submitting it blank causes no problem in the audit"],"eEn":"Excluding a control needs valid justification (e.g., not needed for the risk). For a significant risk, 'high cost' alone lacks a basis for evaluating and formally accepting residual risk (by an appropriate authority) and can be a nonconformity. Always accepting cost as a reason is wrong, dropping the justification is wrong, and excluding the decision from audit scope is wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"あるAI企業が、AIシステムの運用中に予期せぬ挙動が起きた際の対応手順や監視をライフサイクル管理の管理策として整備したいと考えています。この取組みはAnnex Aのどの管理目的に最も適合しますか。","o":["AIシステムのライフサイクル(運用・監視を含む)に関する管理目的","第三者・顧客関係に関する管理目的が該当し、運用時の監視は別枠の管理目的で扱われる","AIのための資源に関する管理目的が該当し、対応手順は対象外とされる","利害関係者への情報提供に関する管理目的が該当し、監視体制の整備は対象外とされる"],"a":0,"e":"運用中の監視や予期せぬ挙動への対応は、AIシステムのライフサイクルに関する管理目的(責任ある運用・監視)に含まれます。第三者関係、資源、情報提供の管理目的はいずれも運用・監視そのものの直接の受け皿ではありません。","qEn":"An AI firm wants controls for monitoring and responding to unexpected behavior during AI operation, as part of life-cycle management. Which Annex A objective fits best?","oEn":["AI system life cycle (including operation and monitoring)","The third-party and customer relationship control objective applies here, with operational monitoring handled under a separate objective","The resources-for-AI control objective applies here, excluding response procedures","The information-for-interested-parties control objective applies here, excluding building a monitoring system"],"eEn":"Monitoring during operation and responding to unexpected behavior fall under the AI-system-life-cycle objective (responsible operation and monitoring). The objectives on third parties, resources, and information are not the direct home for operation/monitoring itself."},
// ===== D4: AI risk & impact assessment ×12 =====
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業が、AIリスクアセスメント(6.1.2)とAIシステム影響評価(6.1.4/8.3)を同一視し、片方だけ実施すればよいと考えています。両者の違いを最も正確に説明しているのはどれですか。","o":["両者は評価の対象も手法も焦点も完全に同一の取組みであり、6.1.2のリスクアセスメントさえ実施すれば、8.3の影響評価まで規格上は満たしたことになり、別の記録も不要である","リスクアセスメントは主に組織の目的達成へのリスクを評価し、影響評価は個人・集団・社会へのAIの潜在的影響を評価する点で焦点が異なる","リスクアセスメントという工程自体が規格上不要とされており、影響評価だけを実施すれば要求は満たされる","AIシステム影響評価は、個人や社会への影響ではなく財務上のリスクのみを対象として扱う限定的な工程である"],"a":1,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは組織やそのAIMSの目的達成に対するリスク(発生源・起こりやすさ・結果)を評価します。一方AIシステム影響評価は、AIが個人・集団・社会に及ぼし得る潜在的影響(権利・安全・公平性等)を評価します。両者は関連するが焦点が異なり、42001は双方を求めます。同一視する説明、リスクアセスメント不要とする説明、影響評価を財務に限定する説明はいずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A company conflates the AI risk assessment (6.1.2) with the AI system impact assessment (6.1.4/8.3), thinking one suffices. Which best explains the difference?","oEn":["The two are activities entirely identical in subject, method, and focus, so performing the 6.1.2 risk assessment alone is deemed under the standard to satisfy the 8.3 impact assessment as well, and no separate record is required","Risk assessment mainly evaluates risks to the organization's objectives; impact assessment evaluates the AI's potential impacts on individuals, groups, and society—different focus","The risk-assessment process itself is deemed unnecessary under the standard, and performing only the impact assessment satisfies the requirement","AI system impact assessment is a limited process addressing only financial risk, rather than impacts on individuals or society"],"eEn":"The AI risk assessment evaluates risks (sources, likelihood, consequences) to the organization's/AIMS's objectives, while the AI system impact assessment evaluates potential impacts on individuals, groups, and society (rights, safety, fairness). They are related but differ in focus, and 42001 requires both. Conflating them, dropping risk assessment, and limiting impact assessment to finance are all wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"あるスタートアップがAIリスクアセスメントのプロセスを設計しています。担当者は『リスクは大きさだけ見て、基準や再現性は気にしない』方針です。ISO/IEC 42001(および23894の考え方)に照らして、まず確立すべきものとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["基準や再現性は規格上気にする必要がなく、担当者個人の直感だけで毎回その場の判断を下せばよい","リスクアセスメントは組織の外部にいる第三者監査人だけが認証審査の場で実施できる活動であり、リスク基準の設定も含めて社内で内製することはできない","リスクの大きさにかかわらず、どのような場面でもリスクは常に無視してよいものとして扱われる","再現性のある一貫した結果を生むよう、リスク基準(受容基準・評価基準)を含むリスクアセスメントプロセスを確立・維持する"],"a":3,"e":"リスクアセスメントは、一貫性があり妥当・比較可能な結果を生むよう、リスク受容基準やリスクアセスメント実施基準を含むプロセスを確立・維持する必要があります(6.1.2)。基準なしの直感判断は再現性を欠き不適切、リスクを常に無視する扱いは誤り、第三者監査人のみが実施できるとする説明は実施主体の誤りです。","qEn":"A startup designs its AI risk-assessment process but intends to 'look only at magnitude and ignore criteria or repeatability.' Under ISO/IEC 42001 (and 23894 thinking), what should be established first?","oEn":["Criteria and repeatability need not be considered under the standard; judging by the handler's own intuition alone each time on the spot is fine","Risk assessment is an activity only a third-party auditor external to the organization can perform, and only during the certification audit, so nothing including the setting of risk criteria can be done in-house","Regardless of its size, risk is to be treated as something that may always be ignored in any situation whatsoever","Establish and maintain a risk-assessment process, including risk criteria (acceptance and assessment criteria), to produce consistent, repeatable results"],"eEn":"A risk assessment must be established and maintained with a process, including risk-acceptance and risk-assessment criteria, to yield consistent, valid, comparable results (6.1.2). Criteria-free intuition lacks repeatability, ignoring risk is wrong, and saying only third-party auditors can perform it misstates who performs it."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業がAIシステム影響評価を実施すべきタイミングを検討しています。担当者は『本番リリース後に問題が起きてから評価すればよい』と考えました。ISO/IEC 42001の考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIシステムのライフサイクルの適切な段階(設計・開発段階を含む事前)で影響を評価し、重要な変更時にも見直す","影響評価はAIシステムを廃棄する段階になって初めて実施すればよいライフサイクル終盤限定の工程であり、設計・開発段階や重要な変更時には不要である","本番リリース後に実際に問題が発生してから、初めて事後的に評価を行えば規格上は十分である","影響評価は不要である"],"a":0,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、潜在的な悪影響を未然に特定・対処するため、ライフサイクルの適切な段階(可能な限り事前の設計・開発段階を含む)で実施し、システムや利用文脈の重要な変更時にも見直します。リリース後の事後評価のみでは予防的意義を欠き、不要とする説明は誤り、廃棄時のみとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company debates when to perform the AI system impact assessment; a staffer says 'assess only after problems occur post-release.' What best fits ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Assess impacts at appropriate life-cycle stages (including proactively in design/development) and review upon significant changes","Impact assessment is a step confined to the end of the life cycle, first performed once the AI system is being decommissioned, and is unnecessary at design and development or on significant change","It is sufficient under the standard to perform the assessment for the first time after the fact, only once a problem actually occurs following the production release","Impact assessment is unnecessary"],"eEn":"To pre-empt adverse effects, the AI system impact assessment is performed at appropriate life-cycle stages, including proactively during design/development, and reviewed on significant changes to the system or its use context. Post-release assessment only loses prevention, calling it unnecessary is wrong, and limiting it to retirement is wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある医療AI企業のリスク対応(6.1.3)で、残余リスクが受容基準を上回っています。担当者は『とりあえず運用を始めて様子を見る』と提案しました。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["残余リスクは適切な権限を持つ者(リスクオーナー等)が受容を承認する必要があり、基準を超える場合は追加のリスク対応か受容の正式承認が求められる","残余リスクという概念自体、リスク対応(6.1.3)の後にAIMSの運用において改めて評価する必要のない事項である","残余リスクは受容基準を超えていたとしても、追加のリスク対応や正式な受容承認を経ることなく、特に何もせず無視してよい","残余リスクが受容基準を明確に超えていたとしても、運用開始後の監視で検知できる範囲であれば、リスクオーナーによる受容の承認手続きを経ずに本番運用を開始して差し支えない"],"a":0,"e":"リスク対応後の残余リスクは、適切な権限を持つリスクオーナー等の承認を得る必要があります。受容基準を超えるなら、追加の管理策等でリスクを低減するか、正当な根拠に基づき正式に受容承認を得るべきで、無承認で運用開始するのは不適切です。基準超過のリスクを無視する説明や、監視で検知できるなら承認なしでよいとする説明は安易な受容で誤り、残余リスクの再評価を不要とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"In a medical AI firm's risk treatment (6.1.3), residual risk exceeds the acceptance criteria, and a staffer proposes 'just start operating and see.' What best fits ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Residual risk must be approved by an appropriate authority (e.g., risk owner); if it exceeds criteria, additional treatment or formal acceptance approval is required","The concept of residual risk itself is not something that needs to be reassessed in AIMS operation after risk treatment (6.1.3)","Even if residual risk exceeds the acceptance criteria, it may simply be ignored without any additional risk treatment or formal acceptance approval","Even where residual risk clearly exceeds the acceptance criteria, production operation may be started without the risk owner's formal acceptance approval, provided post-launch monitoring could detect the issue"],"eEn":"Residual risk after treatment must be approved by an appropriate authority such as the risk owner; if it exceeds acceptance criteria, either reduce it further with controls or obtain formal, justified acceptance. Starting operation without approval is improper. Ignoring over-criteria risk, or skipping approval because monitoring can detect it, casually accepts risk; dismissing residual-risk evaluation is also wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業のAIシステム影響評価が、利用者の利便性だけを評価し、影響を受ける第三者(非利用者)や社会への影響を評価していません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["影響評価は利用者に限らず、影響を受ける個人・集団・社会(非利用者を含む)への潜在的影響を対象とすべきである","影響評価は資本関係のある競合他社への影響のみを対象とし、社会全体への波及は評価対象外とする","影響評価は社内で雇用契約を結んでいる従業員のみを対象とし、外部の第三者は評価範囲に含めない","利用者の利便性という単一の指標のみを評価すれば、影響を受ける非利用者や社会への影響を扱わなくても、この影響評価は規格上十分に完了したことになる"],"a":0,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、直接の利用者だけでなく、AIの結果によって影響を受ける個人・集団・社会(非利用者を含む)への潜在的影響を対象とします。利用者の利便性のみを評価する説明は範囲が狭すぎ、従業員のみ、競合他社のみに限定する説明も、いずれも影響評価の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"A company's AI system impact assessment evaluates only user convenience, not impacts on affected third parties (non-users) or society. What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["The impact assessment should cover potential impacts on affected individuals, groups, and society (including non-users), not just users","Impact assessment covers only effects on capital-linked competitors, excluding any broader ripple effects on society from its scope","Impact assessment covers only employees under an internal employment contract, excluding any external third party from its scope","Evaluating only the single metric of user convenience is deemed under the standard to fully complete this impact assessment, even without addressing affected non-users or society"],"eEn":"The AI system impact assessment covers potential impacts on individuals, groups, and society affected by the AI's outcomes, including non-users, not just direct users. Assessing only user convenience is too narrow, and limiting it to employees or to competitors is contrary to its intent."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業が、AIリスクの発生源やリスクの類型を体系的に洗い出す参考として、AI固有のリスクマネジメントの詳細なガイダンスを求めています。42001の実装を補完するために参照する規格として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["ISO 26000（社会的責任の手引）","ISO/IEC 27017（クラウドサービスの情報セキュリティ管理策）","ISO/IEC 23894（ISO 31000に基づくAIリスクマネジメントの手引）","ISO 22301（事業継続）"],"a":2,"e":"ISO/IEC 23894はAIに関するリスクマネジメントのガイダンス(ISO 31000をAIに適用)で、AI固有のリスク源・プロセスの詳細を提供し、42001のリスクアセスメント実装を補完します。ISO 22301(事業継続)、ISO/IEC 27017(クラウドセキュリティ)、ISO 26000(社会的責任)はAIリスクマネジメントの一次参照ではありません。","qEn":"A company wants detailed guidance on AI-specific risk management to systematically enumerate AI risk sources and types, complementing its 42001 implementation. Which standard is most appropriate?","oEn":["ISO 26000 (guidance on social responsibility)","ISO/IEC 27017 (information security controls for cloud services)","ISO/IEC 23894 (AI risk management guidance based on ISO 31000)","ISO 22301 (business continuity)"],"eEn":"ISO/IEC 23894 provides guidance on AI risk management (applying ISO 31000 to AI), detailing AI-specific risk sources and processes, complementing 42001's risk-assessment implementation. ISO 22301 (business continuity), ISO/IEC 27017 (cloud security), and ISO 26000 (social responsibility) are not the primary AI-risk-management reference."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業が、リスクアセスメントの結果を『高・中・低』のラベルだけで記録し、リスク源やリスク所有者(オーナー)を記録していません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な改善はどれですか。","o":["リスクを高・中・低というラベルだけで記録すれば十分であり、リスク源や所有者の割当ては文書化情報の対象外なので、それ以上の見直しは必要とされない","リスクはその性質上、いかなる形式であっても記録として残してはならないとされている","リスクの特定(源・事象・結果)、分析・評価に加え、各リスクの所有者を割り当て、文書化情報として保持する","リスクの所有者(オーナー)を割り当てる工程は規格上不要であり、担当を決めずに放置してよい"],"a":2,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントでは、リスクの特定(発生源・事象・結果)、分析、評価を行い、各リスクの所有者(オーナー)を明確化して責任を割り当て、結果を文書化情報として保持します。高中低のラベルのみでは追跡・責任が不十分。オーナー割当てを不要とする説明や、リスクの記録を禁じる説明は誤りです。","qEn":"A company records risk-assessment results only as 'high/medium/low' labels, without risk sources or risk owners. What is the best improvement under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Recording risks with only high, medium, or low labels is sufficient, and because risk sources and the assignment of risk owners fall outside documented information, no further review is needed","Risk, by its nature, must never be retained as a record in any form whatsoever, it is held","In addition to identifying (sources, events, consequences), analyzing, and evaluating risks, assign a risk owner to each and retain documented information","The process of assigning a risk owner is unnecessary under the standard, and leaving it undecided is acceptable"],"eEn":"An AI risk assessment identifies risks (sources, events, consequences), analyzes and evaluates them, assigns an owner to each risk to allocate responsibility, and retains the results as documented information. High/medium/low labels alone are insufficient for traceability/accountability; dropping owners and banning records are both wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業のトップマネジメントが『AIシステム影響評価は法規制がある国だけで行えばよい』と考えています。ISO/IEC 42001の考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["影響評価はどの国であっても、AIが個人・社会に及ぼし得る影響の性質にかかわらずその必要性自体が制度上一切認められていないとされる","法規制が明確に存在する国だけで実施すれば足り、規制のない国では個人・社会への潜在的影響を評価する必要はまったくないとされる","影響評価は組織内部の担当者ではなく各国の規制当局のみが、組織が定めた基準とは無関係に、AI規制法のある国に限定して単独で実施すべき取組みであり、組織は結果の通知を待てばよい","影響評価は、法規制の有無にかかわらず、AIが個人・社会に及ぼし得る影響を組織の基準に基づき評価する取組みであり、規制の有無だけで実施要否を決めるべきではない"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、責任あるAIの一環として、法規制の有無に関わらずAIが個人・社会に及ぼす潜在的影響を組織のプロセス・基準に基づいて評価するものです。規制の有無のみで要否を決めるのは不適切です。規制のある国に限る説明は規制依存の限定、必要性が一切認められないとする説明は全面不要とする誤り、規制当局のみが実施するとする説明は実施主体の誤りです。","qEn":"A company's top management thinks 'the AI system impact assessment need only be done in countries with regulation.' What best fits ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Impact assessment is held to have no institutional basis for its necessity in any country, regardless of the nature of the potential impact AI may have on individuals or society","Performing the assessment only in countries with clear existing regulation is deemed sufficient, with no need whatsoever to assess potential impacts on individuals or society where regulation is absent","Impact assessment is an activity that only each country's regulatory authority should carry out alone, independently of the organization's own criteria and only in countries that have AI legislation, with the organization simply awaiting notification of the results","Regardless of regulation, the impact assessment evaluates potential impacts on individuals/society using the organization's criteria; the presence of regulation alone should not decide whether to perform it"],"eEn":"As part of responsible AI, the AI system impact assessment evaluates potential impacts on individuals/society using the organization's processes and criteria regardless of whether regulation exists; regulation alone should not decide necessity. Limiting it to countries with regulation ties it to regulation, saying its necessity is never recognized denies it entirely, and assigning it only to regulators wrongly limits who performs it."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業がAIリスクアセスメントの結果とAIシステム影響評価の結果を、リスク対応や設計判断に全く反映せず、報告書として棚上げしています。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["評価結果はリスク対応(6.1.3)や設計・運用の判断に反映し、必要な管理策の選定・改善につなげる必要がある","評価結果は例外なく外部の利害関係者へ全面公開することが規格上の義務として定められている","評価結果は活用の対象ではなく、記録として保持した後は速やかに破棄すべき性質の情報である","評価さえ実施して報告書を保管していれば規格上は十分であり、その結果をリスク対応や設計・運用の判断に活用しなくても問題はない"],"a":0,"e":"リスクアセスメントと影響評価の結果は、リスク対応計画の策定・管理策の選定・設計や運用の判断に反映され、AIMSの改善につながることに意味があります。実施して棚上げでは目的を果たしません。結果を活用しなくてよいとする説明、速やかに破棄すべきとする説明、全面公開を義務とする説明は、いずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A company performs the AI risk assessment and impact assessment but shelves the reports, never reflecting them in risk treatment or design decisions. What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["The results should inform risk treatment (6.1.3) and design/operation decisions, driving control selection and improvement","Fully disclosing assessment results to external interested parties without exception is prescribed as a mandatory obligation under the standard","Assessment results are not meant to be used and are, by their nature, information that should be promptly discarded once recorded","Performing the assessments and filing the reports is sufficient under the standard, and there is no problem even if the results are never used in risk treatment or in design and operation decisions"],"eEn":"Risk-assessment and impact-assessment results are meaningful only when they inform risk-treatment planning, control selection, and design/operation decisions, driving AIMS improvement. Shelving them defeats the purpose. Saying they need not be used, saying they should be discarded promptly, and mandating full publication are all wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業が、生成AIの新機能を追加する重大な変更を行いましたが、既存の影響評価・リスクアセスメントを見直していません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["AIシステムやその利用文脈に重要な変更がある場合は、リスクアセスメントと影響評価を見直し・更新する必要がある","一度実施した評価は、生成AIの新機能追加のような重大な変更があっても内容が有効であり続けるため、リスクアセスメントも影響評価も見直しは不要である","評価が必要とされるのは新規導入するシステムに限られ、既存システムの変更時には求められない","評価の見直しはマネジメントレビューが開催される年1回のタイミングでのみ行えば十分である"],"a":0,"e":"AIシステムの機能追加など重要な変更は、新たなリスクや影響を生み得るため、リスクアセスメントとAIシステム影響評価を見直し・更新する必要があります。変更後も無条件に有効とする説明、新規導入時のみ必要とする説明、見直しのトリガーを年1回に固定する説明は、いずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A company makes a significant change adding a new generative-AI feature but does not revisit its existing impact assessment or risk assessment. What best fits ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["When there are significant changes to the AI system or its use context, the risk assessment and impact assessment should be reviewed and updated","An assessment performed once remains valid even after a significant change such as adding a new generative-AI feature, so neither the risk assessment nor the impact assessment needs to be reviewed","Assessment is required only for newly introduced systems and is not called for when an existing system is changed","Reviewing the assessment need only occur at the single annual timing when the management review is held"],"eEn":"Significant changes such as adding features can introduce new risks and impacts, so the risk assessment and AI system impact assessment should be reviewed and updated. Assuming unconditional validity after a change, requiring assessment only for new systems, and fixing the review trigger to once a year are all wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業が、AIリスクの『起こりやすさ』と『結果の重大さ』の両面を考慮せず、結果の重大さだけでリスクを評価しています。ISO/IEC 42001/23894の考え方として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["リスク分析はデータや基準を用いず、担当者の主観的な感覚のみに基づいて行うべきである","リスク分析は起こりやすさ(尤度)という一つの軸だけを見れば足り、結果の大きさは考慮不要である","結果の重大さという一つの軸だけを見れば、リスクレベルの見積もりとして十分である","リスク分析は、起こりやすさ(尤度)と結果(影響)の双方を考慮してリスクレベルを見積もるべきである"],"a":3,"e":"リスク分析は、リスクの起こりやすさ(尤度)と結果(影響)の双方を考慮してリスクレベルを見積もります。結果の重大さのみ、あるいは起こりやすさのみでは偏った評価となり、主観のみの分析は一貫性を欠きます。","qEn":"A company evaluates AI risk using only consequence severity, ignoring likelihood. What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001/23894?","oEn":["Risk analysis should be based purely on the handler's subjective feel, without using any data or criteria","Risk analysis need only look at the single axis of likelihood, with the magnitude of consequences unnecessary to consider","Looking at only the single axis of the severity of consequences is sufficient for estimating the risk level","Risk analysis should estimate risk level considering both likelihood and consequences (impact)"],"eEn":"Risk analysis estimates the level of risk considering both likelihood and consequences. Consequence only or likelihood only is biased, and purely subjective analysis lacks consistency."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある企業のAIシステム影響評価が、潜在的な悪影響のみを列挙し、影響を受ける利害関係者の特定や、影響の緩和策・監視方法を含んでいません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な改善はどれですか。","o":["影響評価には緩和策の記述を含めてはならず、あくまで悪影響を列挙するだけにとどめる","影響評価では影響を受ける利害関係者を特定してはならず、緩和策や監視方法の記載も規格が明確に禁止しているため、悪影響の性質のみを列挙すればよい","影響を受ける利害関係者の特定、影響の性質・程度、緩和策や監視・是正の方針を含め、結果を文書化情報として保持する","影響評価は影響を受ける利害関係者を特定してはならず、悪影響の性質だけを書き記す"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、影響を受ける利害関係者の特定、潜在的な影響の性質・範囲・程度、そしてそれらへの対処(緩和・監視・是正)方針を含め、結果を文書化情報として残すことが望まれます。悪影響の列挙のみでは対処につながらず、利害関係者の特定や緩和策・監視方法を禁じる説明は、影響評価の要素を否定しており誤りです。","qEn":"A company's AI system impact assessment lists only potential adverse effects, omitting identification of affected stakeholders and any mitigation or monitoring approach. What is the best improvement under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Impact assessment must never include a description of mitigation measures, remaining a mere listing of adverse effects","The standard expressly forbids identifying the interested parties affected in an impact assessment and likewise bars recording mitigation or monitoring approaches, so listing only the nature of the adverse effects is enough","Include identifying affected stakeholders, the nature/extent of impacts, and mitigation/monitoring/remediation approaches, and retain results as documented information","Impact assessment must never identify the interested parties affected, recording only the nature of the effects"],"eEn":"An AI system impact assessment should identify affected stakeholders, characterize the nature and extent of potential impacts, and set out mitigation/monitoring/remediation approaches, retaining the results as documented information. Listing adverse impacts alone leads nowhere; forbidding stakeholder identification or mitigation and monitoring denies core elements of the assessment."},
// ===== D5: PDCA & continual improvement ×12 =====
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、AIMSの各要求事項をPDCAサイクルに対応づけようとしています。『Plan(計画)』段階に最もよく対応するClauseの組み合わせはどれですか。","o":["Clause 9と10－Check・Act段階の組み合わせ","Clause 8(運用)のみ－計画を実行に移すDo段階に対応する箇条","Clause 4-6(状況・リーダーシップ・計画)を中心とした、AIMSの計画(Plan)段階","Clause 10(改善)のみ－不適合の是正を扱うAct段階に対応する箇条"],"a":2,"e":"PDCAとの一般的対応では、Plan=Clause 4(状況)・5(リーダーシップ)・6(計画)、Do=Clause 7(支援)・8(運用)、Check=Clause 9(パフォーマンス評価)、Act=Clause 10(改善)となります。したがってPlanは主に4-6です。Clause 9と10はCheck/Act、Clause 8のみはDo、Clause 10のみはActに当たり、Planには対応しません。","qEn":"Mapping AIMS requirements to PDCA, which clauses best correspond to the 'Plan' stage?","oEn":["Clauses 9 and 10 – the Check/Act combination","Clause 8 (operation) alone – the clause corresponding to the Do stage that executes the plan","The planning (Plan) stage of the AIMS, centered on Clauses 4-6 (context, leadership, planning)","Clause 10 (improvement) alone – the clause corresponding to the Act stage"],"eEn":"In the common mapping: Plan = Clauses 4 (context), 5 (leadership), 6 (planning); Do = Clauses 7 (support), 8 (operation); Check = Clause 9 (performance evaluation); Act = Clause 10 (improvement). So Plan is mainly 4-6. Clauses 9 and 10 are Check/Act, Clause 8 alone is Do, and Clause 10 alone is Act."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業のマネジメントレビュー(9.3)の議事録には、報告された内容の要約はあるが、決定事項(改善の機会・変更の必要性・資源の必要性等)が記録されていません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["マネジメントレビューのアウトプットには、継続的改善の機会やAIMSの変更の必要性に関する決定を含め、文書化情報として保持する必要がある","レビューでは報告されたインプットの情報のみを記録すればよく、そこから導かれる決定事項は記録対象外である","マネジメントレビューの議事録という文書化した情報を作成することは、規格の要求としてそもそも禁止されている","報告内容の要約さえ議事録に記載していれば、改善の機会やAIMSの変更の必要性、資源の必要性といった決定事項そのものの記録は特に求められていない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 9.3のアウトプットには、継続的改善の機会、AIMSの変更の必要性(必要な資源を含む)に関する決定が含まれ、これらを文書化情報として保持する必要があります。要約のみで決定事項が欠けるのは不適合となり得ます。決定事項の記録を不要とする説明、議事録の作成を禁じる説明、インプットのみ記録すればよいとする説明は、いずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A management-review record (9.3) summarizes what was reported but records no decisions (improvement opportunities, need for changes, resource needs). What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Management-review outputs must include decisions on continual-improvement opportunities and needs for changes to the AIMS, retained as documented information","The review need only record the information presented as input, with the decisions derived from it excluded from the recording scope","Creating the documented information that is the management review's minutes is, to begin with, prohibited as a requirement under the standard","As long as the minutes summarize what was reported, no particular record of the decisions themselves, such as improvement opportunities, the need for AIMS changes, or resource needs, is required"],"eEn":"Clause 9.3 outputs include decisions on continual-improvement opportunities and on needs for changes to the AIMS (including needed resources), retained as documented information. A summary lacking decisions can be a nonconformity. Dropping decision records, banning minutes, and recording only inputs are all wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、同種のAIインシデントを何度も繰り返しています。是正処置は毎回『再起動と一時対処』のみで、根本原因の除去をしていません。継続的改善(Act段階)の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["是正処置は不適合の根本原因を除去して再発を防ぐことを目的とし、原因分析と有効性レビューを伴う必要がある","是正処置は不適合の内容や実施した対応の記録を一切残さず、根本原因の分析も行わないまま、口頭の申し送りのみで完結させて実施するものである","同種のインシデントが繰り返し起きても、一時対処を淡々と繰り返していれば規格上は問題ない","同じ不適合が何度再発しても、原因が偶然であるため是正処置という工程自体が不要である"],"a":0,"e":"是正処置(10.2)は、不適合の修正に加え、原因をレビューして除去し、再発を防止することを目的とします。原因分析・処置の実施・有効性レビュー・記録が伴わなければ、同種インシデントの再発は止まりません。一時対処の反復を是とする説明、是正処置を不要とする説明、記録を残さず口頭で済ませる説明は、いずれも誤りです。","qEn":"A company repeatedly suffers the same type of AI incident; each corrective action is only 'restart and a temporary fix,' never removing the root cause. What is the best observation for the Act stage?","oEn":["Corrective action aims to eliminate the root cause to prevent recurrence and must include cause analysis and effectiveness review","Corrective action is carried out purely as a verbal handover, retaining no record whatsoever of the nonconformity or the response taken and doing no root-cause analysis","Even if similar incidents keep recurring, simply repeating the same stopgap fix each time poses no problem under the standard","Since the cause is deemed coincidental, the corrective-action process itself is unnecessary no matter how many times the same nonconformity recurs"],"eEn":"Corrective action (10.2) corrects the nonconformity and reviews/eliminates its cause to prevent recurrence, requiring cause analysis, implementation, effectiveness review, and records. Without these, the same incidents keep recurring. Endorsing repeated patching, dropping corrective action, and handling it orally with no records are all wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が『内部監査は認証審査の直前に一度だけ行えばよい』と考えています。PDCAのCheck段階と内部監査の趣旨に照らして最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["内部監査という工程は、いったん認証を取得した後は、AIMSの適合状況や有効性にかかわらず、次回の更新審査の直前まで規格上一切不要になるとされている","内部監査は外部の第三者による認証審査によって完全に代替できるため、社内で計画的に実施する意味を持たない","内部監査は計画された間隔で実施し、AIMSが要求事項に適合し有効に実施・維持されているかを継続的に確認する必要がある","認証審査の直前という限られたタイミングで一度だけ実施すれば、内部監査の要求は十分に満たされる"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9.2は、AIMSが規格要求・組織自身の要求に適合し、有効に実施・維持されているかを判断するため、計画された間隔で内部監査を実施することを求めます。審査直前の一度きり、認証後の廃止、外部審査での代替はいずれもCheck段階の継続性・独立性の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"A company thinks 'internal audit need be done only once, just before the certification audit.' What is the best observation for the Check stage and internal audit?","oEn":["The internal-audit process is held to become entirely unnecessary under the standard once certification has been obtained, right up until just before the next renewal audit, regardless of the AIMS's conformity or effectiveness","Internal audit can be fully substituted by the external third-party certification audit, so conducting it in-house on a planned basis carries no meaning","Internal audits must be conducted at planned intervals to continually confirm the AIMS conforms to requirements and is effectively implemented and maintained","Performing it just once, only at the limited timing right before the certification audit, is deemed to fully satisfy the internal-audit requirement"],"eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires internal audits at planned intervals to determine whether the AIMS conforms to the standard's and the organization's own requirements and is effectively implemented and maintained. A one-off before certification, dropping audits after certification, or replacing them with external audits all violate the Check stage's continuity and independence."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が『継続的改善は、新しい管理策を毎年たくさん追加すること』だと理解しています。ISO/IEC 42001の継続的改善の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["改善とは、監視測定やレビューの結果を参照せず、既存の管理策を見直すことなく毎年新しい管理策だけを大量に追加し続けることである","改善はトップマネジメントが一切関与せず、現場の担当者だけが独自の判断で監視やレビューの結果とは無関係に個別に進める活動である","改善とは、リスクの変化や監視測定の結果、監査結果、マネジメントレビューでの決定を一切考慮せず、毎年決まった割合の既存の管理策を機械的に削除し続けることである","改善はAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を高めることであり、監視測定・監査・レビュー結果に基づき必要な変更・是正・最適化を行うこと(必ずしも追加ではない)"],"a":3,"e":"継続的改善(10.1)はAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を高める取組みで、監視・測定・分析評価、監査、マネジメントレビューの結果に基づき、必要な変更・是正・最適化を行います。必ずしも管理策の大量追加や機械的な削除を意味しません。トップマネジメントの関与なしに現場だけで進めるとする説明は誤りです(9.3等でトップが関与)。","qEn":"A company understands 'continual improvement' as 'adding many new controls every year.' What is the intent of continual improvement in ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Improvement means continually adding a large volume of new controls every year, without referring to monitoring or review results or ever reviewing existing controls","Improvement is an activity carried out solely by front-line staff individually on their own judgment, unrelated to monitoring or review results, with no involvement from top management","Improvement means mechanically deleting a fixed proportion of the existing controls every year, without any regard whatsoever to changes in risk, monitoring and measurement results, audit findings, or management-review decisions","Improvement enhances the suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness of the AIMS, making needed changes/corrections/optimizations based on monitoring, audits, and reviews—not necessarily additions"],"eEn":"Continual improvement (10.1) enhances the AIMS's suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness, making needed changes/corrections/optimizations based on monitoring/measurement, audits, and management review, not necessarily adding controls. Fixating on mass additions or mechanical deletions is wrong, and denying top-management involvement is wrong (it appears in 9.3, etc.)."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、AIモデルの公平性指標が運用中に徐々に劣化(ドリフト)していることに気づきました。PDCAの観点で、この状況に最も適合する対応の流れはどれですか。","o":["公平性指標の劣化を検知しても、次のマネジメントレビューが開催されるまでは何もせず様子を見るべきである","Plan段階で対応方針を一度定めておけば十分であり、その後の継続的な監視測定やドリフト検知は不要である","Check段階(監視・測定)でドリフトを検知し、Act段階(是正・改善)で原因分析と対応を行い、必要ならPlanに反映して再計画する","Do段階で公平性指標を用いずにモデルを再学習させさえすれば十分であり、Check段階での監視・測定やAct段階での原因分析、Planへの反映は省略してよい"],"a":2,"e":"運用中の指標劣化(ドリフト)は、Check段階の監視・測定で検知し、Act段階で原因分析・是正・改善を行い、必要に応じてPlan(目的・管理策の見直し)に反映して再計画するという、PDCAの循環で対処します。再学習だけでCheckとActを省く説明、Planで一度定めれば監視不要とする説明、次のレビューまで放置する説明は、いずれも不適切です。","qEn":"A company notices its AI model's fairness metric gradually degrading (drift) during operation. Which flow best fits PDCA?","oEn":["Even after detecting the fairness metric's degradation, nothing should be done and the situation merely watched until the next management review is held","Once a response policy is set at the Plan stage, it is sufficient, and ongoing monitoring/measurement or drift detection thereafter is unnecessary","Detect drift in Check (monitoring/measurement), analyze causes and act in Act (correction/improvement), and feed back into Plan to re-plan if needed","Simply retraining the model at the Do stage without reference to the fairness metric is sufficient, so monitoring at Check, cause analysis at Act, and feeding back into Plan may all be skipped"],"eEn":"Metric drift during operation is detected via Check (monitoring/measurement), addressed in Act (cause analysis, correction, improvement), and fed back into Plan (revising objectives/controls) as needed, which is the PDCA loop. Retraining alone while skipping Check and Act, claiming monitoring is unnecessary once Plan is set, and waiting passively until the next review are all inappropriate."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、監視・測定の結果を分析・評価する担当や時期を決めておらず、データは溜まるものの活用されていません。PDCAのCheck段階の趣旨に照らして最も適切な改善はどれですか。","o":["何を・どう監視測定し、いつ・誰が結果を分析評価するかを定め、評価結果を改善やレビューの入力として活用する","分析評価はトップマネジメントが個人的に、他の担当者に任せず手作業だけで行うべき業務である","監視測定のデータはひとまず蓄積しておけば十分であり、分析評価の担当や時期を定める工程は、次回の認証審査で指摘されてから決めればよい","監視測定という活動そのものを、データが活用されていないことを理由に廃止すべきである"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 9.1は、監視・測定の対象・方法・時期に加え、結果を分析・評価する時期と担当を定めることを求めます。評価結果はマネジメントレビューや改善の入力として活用されて初めて意味を持ちます。蓄積だけで分析を不要とする説明、監視測定を廃止する説明は誤り、トップが個人的に手作業で分析する説明は非現実的で要求の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"A company has not decided who analyzes/evaluates monitoring results or when, so data accumulates unused. What is the best improvement for the Check stage?","oEn":["Define what/how to monitor and measure and when/who analyzes and evaluates results, and use the evaluation as input to improvement and review","Analysis and evaluation are a task that top management should perform personally by hand alone, without delegating to any other staff","Simply accumulating the monitoring and measurement data is sufficient, and deciding who analyzes and evaluates it and when can wait until the next certification audit raises the point","The monitoring/measurement activity itself should be abolished on the grounds that the data goes unused"],"eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires determining what/how/when to monitor and measure and when and by whom results are analyzed and evaluated; evaluation matters only when it feeds management review and improvement. Merely accumulating data without analysis is wrong, abolishing monitoring is wrong, and having top management hand-analyze everything is impractical and contrary to the requirement."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、AIMSの内部監査で複数の不適合を検出しましたが、マネジメントレビューにその結果を報告せず、改善の意思決定にもつなげていません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["監査で不適合を検出した場合であっても、その内容を記録として残してはならないとされる","監査結果はトップマネジメントに一切知らせず、現場の担当部門内だけで秘匿すべきである","監査結果はマネジメントレビューのインプットに含め、改善機会や変更の必要性の意思決定につなげるべきである","内部監査で検出した不適合の結果は、是正処置が完了しているか否かにかかわらず、マネジメントレビューのインプットには含めなくてよいとされる"],"a":2,"e":"内部監査の結果は、マネジメントレビュー(9.3)のインプットに含め、継続的改善や是正、AIMSの変更の必要性に関する意思決定につなげることで、PDCAが機能します。インプットに含めなくてよいとする説明、記録を禁じる説明、トップに知らせず秘匿する説明は、いずれも継続的改善の趣旨に反します。","qEn":"A company's internal audit finds several nonconformities but does not report them to the management review or use them for improvement decisions. What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Even when a nonconformity is detected in an audit, its content is deemed something that must never be kept as a record","Audit results should be kept entirely secret within the responsible department alone, never disclosed to top management","Audit results should be included as management-review inputs and drive decisions on improvement opportunities and needs for changes","The results of nonconformities detected in internal audit are held not to require inclusion in the management-review inputs, whether or not corrective action has been completed"],"eEn":"Internal audit results should feed the management review (9.3) as input and drive decisions on continual improvement, corrective action, and needs for AIMS changes, keeping PDCA working. Leaving them out of the review, banning records, and hiding them from top management are all contrary to continual improvement."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が『マネジメントレビューは有効性の確認だけで、AIMSの適切性(suitability)や妥当性(adequacy)は対象外だ』と考えています。Clause 9.3の趣旨として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["レビューはAIMSの妥当性という一側面のみを対象とし、有効性や適切性は特に問わないとされる","マネジメントレビューはトップマネジメント以外の一般従業員が主体となって実施すべきもので、確認する対象はAIMSの有効性のみに限られ、適切性や妥当性は含めない","レビューはAIMSの有効性という一側面のみを対象とし、適切性や妥当性は特に問わないとされる","マネジメントレビューはAIMSの継続的な適切性・妥当性・有効性を確実にするため、計画された間隔でトップマネジメントがレビューする"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 9.3は、AIMSが引き続き適切(suitable)・妥当(adequate)・有効(effective)であることを確実にするため、トップマネジメントが計画された間隔でAIMSをレビューすることを求めます。有効性のみ、あるいは妥当性のみへの限定は誤りで、トップ以外が主体となって実施するとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company thinks 'management review checks only effectiveness, not the AIMS's suitability or adequacy.' What is the intent of Clause 9.3?","oEn":["The review is held to cover only the single aspect of adequacy, without particularly questioning effectiveness or suitability","The management review should be conducted mainly by general employees rather than top management, and what it checks is limited to the AIMS's effectiveness, excluding suitability and adequacy","The review is held to cover only the single aspect of effectiveness, without particularly questioning suitability or adequacy","Management review ensures the continuing suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness of the AIMS, performed by top management at planned intervals"],"eEn":"Clause 9.3 requires top management to review the AIMS at planned intervals to ensure its continuing suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness. Limiting the review to effectiveness only, or to adequacy only, is wrong, and assigning it to people other than top management is also wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、継続的改善の一環として、是正処置(reactive)だけに頼り、予防的・能動的な改善(監視傾向の分析やレビュー由来の改善)を行っていません。ISO/IEC 42001の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["改善という取組みが許されるのは、インシデントが実際に発生した直後の限られた期間のみである","予防的・能動的な改善活動という考え方は、Clause 10.1の要求事項によって明確に禁止されており、改善は是正処置のみによって行わなければならない","是正処置という一つの手段だけで、規格が求める継続的改善の取組みは完全に完結する","継続的改善(10.1)は是正処置に限らず、監視・分析・監査・レビューの結果を用いた能動的な改善も含む"],"a":3,"e":"継続的改善(10.1)は不適合対応の是正処置(10.2)に限らず、監視・測定・分析評価、監査、マネジメントレビューの結果に基づく能動的・予防的な改善も含みます。是正処置のみでは受動的で不十分。予防的改善を禁止とする説明は誤り、改善をインシデント直後の期間に限る説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company relies only on reactive corrective action and does no proactive improvement (analyzing monitoring trends, review-driven improvements). What is the best observation under ISO/IEC 42001?","oEn":["Improvement activity is permitted only during the limited period immediately following an incident that has actually occurred","Proactive, preventive improvement is prohibited by the Clause 10.1 requirements, and improvement must be pursued through corrective action alone","Corrective action alone, as a single measure, is deemed to fully complete the continual-improvement activity the standard requires","Continual improvement (10.1) is not limited to corrective action; it includes proactive improvement using monitoring, analysis, audit, and review results"],"eEn":"Continual improvement (10.1) is not limited to corrective action (10.2) for nonconformities; it includes proactive improvement based on monitoring/measurement/analysis, audits, and management review. Corrective action alone is reactive and insufficient; banning proactive improvement is wrong, and limiting improvement to the period right after an incident is wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、AIの目的(6.2)に対する達成度を測定・監視せず、目的が形骸化しています。PDCAの観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["目的は方針として掲げておけば十分であり、監視・測定を通じた達成度の評価という工程は特に求められない","目的の達成度は組織の外部にいる監査人だけが評価でき、Check段階における社内での評価は認められない","目的は測定可能な形で設定し、監視・測定(Check)を通じて達成度を評価し、必要に応じ改善(Act)や再計画(Plan)につなげる","目的は一度設定したら、監視測定の結果からAct段階での見直しの必要性が生じた場合でも、次回の認証審査が終わるまでは決して変更してはならないとされる"],"a":2,"e":"AIの目的(6.2)は測定可能な形で設定し、監視・測定(9.1/Check)を通じ達成度を評価し、結果を改善(Act)や再計画(Plan)へ反映させることでPDCAが機能します。達成度の測定を不要とする説明は誤り、目的の更新を禁じる説明も誤り(6.2は必要に応じ更新を求める)、評価を外部監査人に限る説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company neither measures nor monitors achievement of its AI objectives (6.2), so they become hollow. What is the best observation for PDCA?","oEn":["Setting the objective as a stated policy is deemed sufficient, with no process of evaluating achievement through monitoring and measurement required","The achievement of objectives can be evaluated only by an auditor external to the organization, with internal evaluation at the Check stage not permitted","Objectives should be set measurably, evaluated for achievement via monitoring/measurement (Check), and feed improvement (Act) or re-planning (Plan) as needed","Once an objective is set, it must never be changed until the next certification audit, even when the monitoring results make an Act-stage revision necessary"],"eEn":"AI objectives (6.2) should be set measurably, evaluated for achievement via monitoring/measurement (9.1/Check), and fed into improvement (Act) or re-planning (Plan) to keep PDCA working. Dropping measurement is wrong, forbidding updates is wrong (6.2 requires updating as appropriate), and limiting evaluation to external auditors is wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある企業が、AIMSの文書(方針・手順・記録)を一度作成した後、組織やAI利用の変化に合わせて更新せず放置しています。継続的改善とPDCAの観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["文書化情報は組織・リスク・利用文脈の変化に応じてレビュー・更新し、AIMSの適切性・有効性を維持する必要がある","文書は最初に作成した時点の内容のまま、組織やリスクの変化があっても一切更新せず維持し続ければ十分である","文書は組織やAI利用の変化にかかわらず、内容を毎日書き換え続けることが規格上求められる","文書の更新という作業は、AIMSの適切性や有効性を維持する目的とは完全に独立した事務であり、組織や利用文脈が変化しても継続的改善の対象にはならない"],"a":0,"e":"文書化情報(方針・手順・記録)は、組織の状況・リスク・AI利用文脈の変化に応じてレビュー・更新し、AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を維持することが継続的改善の一部です。更新不要とする説明は誤り、毎日書き換えるとする説明は非現実的、文書更新を改善と無関係の事務とする説明は関係の否定で誤りです。","qEn":"A company created its AIMS documents (policies, procedures, records) once and never updates them as the organization and AI use change. What is the best observation for continual improvement and PDCA?","oEn":["Documented information should be reviewed and updated as the organization, risks, and use context change, to maintain the AIMS's suitability and effectiveness","It is sufficient for a document to remain exactly as first created, kept unchanged and never updated even as the organization or risk changes","The standard is held to require that a document's content be rewritten every single day regardless of any change in the organization or AI use","Updating documents is clerical work entirely independent of the purpose of maintaining the AIMS's suitability and effectiveness, and it never falls within continual improvement even when the organization or use context changes"],"eEn":"Reviewing and updating documented information (policies, procedures, records) as context, risks, and AI use change, maintaining the AIMS's suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness, is part of continual improvement. Denying updates is wrong, demanding daily rewrites is unrealistic, and calling updates paperwork unrelated to improvement denies the link."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある製造業のAI推進室が、社内で使うAI関連の用語（AIシステム、AI提供者、影響を受ける個人など）の解釈が部署ごとにずれて困っています。用語を揃える拠り所として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["AIの概念と用語の共通基盤であるISO/IEC 22989を参照し、社内の用語集を揃える","AIリスクマネジメントの指針であるISO/IEC 23894の認証を取得し、用語の統一を図る","情報セキュリティの要求事項であるISO/IEC 27001の用語定義を、AI用語として流用する","ISO 31000のリスクマネジメント指針に載る用語を採用し、AI固有の語は各部署がその拡張として定義する"],"a":0,"e":"ISO/IEC 22989はAIの概念・用語の共通基盤で、用語の整合の拠り所になります。23894は認証対象ではないリスク管理の指針、27001は情報セキュリティの規格でAI用語の定義元ではありません。ISO 31000は一般的なリスクマネジメントの指針で、AI固有の語を各部署の定義に任せると、解釈のずれが残ります。","qEn":"A manufacturer's AI office is struggling because departments interpret terms such as AI system, AI provider and affected individual differently. What is the most appropriate reference for aligning the terminology?","oEn":["Refer to ISO/IEC 22989, the shared basis for AI terms, and align the internal glossary","Obtain certification to ISO/IEC 23894, the AI risk management guidance, to unify the terminology","Reuse the term definitions of ISO/IEC 27001, the information security requirements, as AI terms","Adopt the terms of the ISO 31000 risk management guidance and let each department define AI-specific terms as extensions of it"],"eEn":"ISO/IEC 22989 is the common basis for AI concepts and terminology, so it anchors term alignment. 23894 is risk guidance and not a certification target, and 27001 is an information security standard, not the source of AI definitions. ISO 31000 is general risk management guidance, and leaving AI-specific terms to each department's own definitions keeps the interpretation gaps."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある保険会社の担当者が「ISO/IEC 23894の認証を取れば、AIMSの第三者認証を取ったことになる」と社内で説明し、認証取得の計画を立て始めています。この説明への最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["23894は42001と同一内容の要求事項規格であり、どちらの認証でもAIMSの認証として扱われる","23894はAIリスク管理のガイダンス文書で認証の対象外であり、認証可能なのは42001のみである","23894の認証は42001の認証より上位に位置づけられ、取得すれば42001の審査は免除される","23894は認証可能だが対象はAIの個別製品であり、AIMSの認証とは別に必ず両方が必要となる"],"a":1,"e":"23894はAIリスクマネジメントの指針（ガイダンス）で、認証できる要求事項規格は42001です。両者を同一視する説明、23894が上位で42001の審査が免除されるとする説明、23894が製品認証だとする説明はいずれも根拠のない誤りです。","qEn":"An insurance company's staff member explains internally, 'If we obtain ISO/IEC 23894 certification, we will have obtained third-party certification of our AIMS,' and has begun planning the certification. What is the most appropriate correction?","oEn":["23894 is a requirements standard with the same content as 42001, so either certification counts as AIMS certification","23894 is guidance on AI risk management and not a certification target; the certifiable requirements standard is 42001","23894 certification ranks above 42001 certification, and obtaining it exempts the organization from the 42001 audit","23894 is certifiable but covers individual AI products, so both certifications are always needed separately from the AIMS"],"eEn":"23894 is guidance on AI risk management, and the certifiable requirements standard is 42001. Treating them as the same, claiming 23894 is superior and exempts a 42001 audit, or claiming 23894 is a product certification are all unfounded."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ISO/IEC 27001のISMS認証を運用している企業が、新たにAIMSの構築を始めます。経営層は工数と重複を抑えたい意向です。両規格の関係を踏まえた進め方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["共通の高位構造を活かして文書管理は共有するが、内部監査とマネジメントレビューはISMSのものをそのまま使い、AI固有の観点は加えない","両規格は構造が全く異なるため、文書管理も内部監査も完全に別の仕組みとして新設する","共通の高位構造を活かし、文書管理・内部監査・レビューを共有してAI固有の要求を足す","ISMSの文書体系を流用し、AIMSの適用範囲もISMSの適用範囲と必ず同一に定める"],"a":2,"e":"42001と27001は共通の高位構造を持つため、共通プロセスを統合しつつAI特有の要求（影響評価、AI方針など）を加えるのが合理的です。内部監査やレビューにAI固有の観点を加えない進め方は不十分で、AIMSの適用範囲はAIに関する目的と状況から独立に決めるものでありISMSと同一に固定しません。構造が全く異なるとする説明も、共通構造があるため誤りです。","qEn":"A company operating ISO/IEC 27001 ISMS certification is starting to build an AIMS, and management wants to limit effort and duplication. Which approach, given the relationship between the standards, is most appropriate?","oEn":["Share document control through the common structure, but reuse the ISMS internal audit and management review as they are, adding no AI-specific viewpoints","Build entirely separate document control and internal audit, since the two standards have completely different structures","Share document control, internal audit and management review via the common structure, and add AI-specific requirements","Reuse the ISMS document set and always define the AIMS scope to be identical to the ISMS scope"],"eEn":"42001 and 27001 share a high-level structure, so common processes can be integrated while AI-specific requirements such as impact assessment and the AI policy are added. Reusing the ISMS audit and review without AI viewpoints is insufficient, and the AIMS scope is decided independently from the AI context rather than fixed to the ISMS scope. Claiming totally different structures is wrong because a common structure exists."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるAIベンダーの営業部が、広告に「当社のAI製品はISO/IEC 42001認証取得済みのため、精度と安全性が第三者に保証されています」と書こうとしています。法務の指摘として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["認証は製品ごとに審査されるため、製品の精度と安全性の保証を示すとして記載してよい","認証機関が製品の出力を継続的に試験するため、精度の保証として記載しても誤りではない","認証は審査時点でAIの精度を測定して合格を確認したものなので、審査時点の精度値に限って保証として記載できる","認証は組織のAIMSの適合を示すもので、個別の製品の精度や安全性の保証にはならない"],"a":3,"e":"認証対象はマネジメントシステムであり、製品の精度や安全性を保証するものではないため、AIMSの適合を述べる表現に改めるべきです。製品ごとの審査だとする説明、出力の継続試験だとする説明、審査時点の精度を測って合格としたとする説明はいずれも、認証がAIMSの適合を確認するものだという点を取り違えています。","qEn":"An AI vendor's sales department plans to write in an advertisement, 'Our AI product is ISO/IEC 42001 certified, so its accuracy and safety are guaranteed by a third party.' What is the most appropriate point from Legal?","oEn":["Certification is assessed product by product, so it may be stated as showing a guarantee of the product's accuracy and safety","The certification body continuously tests product outputs, so stating it as an accuracy guarantee is not wrong","The certification confirmed a pass by measuring AI accuracy at the audit, so it may be stated as a guarantee limited to the accuracy value at that time","Certification shows the AIMS conforms to the standard; it does not guarantee a product's accuracy or safety, so reword"],"eEn":"What is certified is the management system, not product accuracy or safety, so the wording should describe AIMS conformity. Claiming product-by-product assessment, continuous output testing, or an accuracy measurement at the audit all misread certification as confirming AIMS conformity."},
{"d":"D1","q":"従業員15名のAIスタートアップの代表が「42001は大企業向けで、うちのような小規模組織には適用できない」と述べ、検討を見送ろうとしています。規格の適用に関する最も適切な説明はどれですか。","o":["AIを提供または利用するあらゆる規模の組織に適用でき、運用は規模に応じて設計する","従業員数が一定数を超える組織にだけ適用でき、小規模組織は対象外と規格に明記されている","AIを自社開発する組織にだけ適用でき、他社のAIを利用するだけの組織は対象外である","営利企業にだけ適用でき、NPOや自治体のような非営利組織は規格の対象外である"],"a":0,"e":"42001はAIを提供または利用するあらゆる規模・種類の組織に適用でき、運用の深さは規模や状況に応じて設計します。従業員数での制限、自社開発のみへの限定、営利企業のみへの限定は、いずれも規格の考え方と合いません。","qEn":"The head of a 15-employee AI startup said, '42001 is for large companies and cannot be applied to small organizations like ours,' and is about to drop the idea. Which explanation about applicability is most appropriate?","oEn":["It applies to organizations of any size that provide or use AI, with operations designed proportionately","It applies only to organizations above a certain headcount, and the standard explicitly excludes small organizations","It applies only to organizations that develop AI in-house, not to those merely using other companies' AI","It applies only to for-profit companies, and non-profits and municipalities are outside the standard's scope"],"eEn":"42001 applies to organizations of any size or type that provide or use AI, and the depth of operation is designed to fit size and context. Headcount limits, restriction to in-house development, and restriction to for-profit companies do not match the standard's approach."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある病院が、他社製の画像診断支援AIを購入して院内で使うだけで、自らは開発をしていません。「開発していないのでAIMSは関係ない」という意見に対する最も適切な見解はどれですか。","o":["AIMSの責任は購入元ベンダーの側にあるため、病院はベンダーの認証書の写しを保管すれば要求を満たす","AIを利用する組織もAIMSの対象となり得て、用途と影響に応じた方針や評価を整えられる","病院は利用者としてAIMSの対象になるが、ベンダーの選定は通常の購買手続きに委ね、AI固有の評価基準は設けない","利用者は方針と体制を整えるが、導入前の影響評価はAIの開発者だけが実施できるため、病院は導入後の監視に専念する"],"a":1,"e":"42001はAIを提供する組織だけでなく利用する組織にも適用でき、利用目的や患者への影響に応じて方針、影響評価、監視を整備します。ベンダーの認証書の保管は利用者側の整備の代わりになりません。購買手続きだけでAI固有の評価基準を持たない進め方や、影響評価は開発者だけが行えるとする説明も、利用者の責務を狭く捉えた誤りです。","qEn":"A hospital buys an image-diagnosis support AI from another company and only uses it internally; it develops nothing itself. What is the most appropriate view on the opinion 'We don't develop AI, so the AIMS is irrelevant'?","oEn":["The AIMS responsibility lies with the seller, so the hospital meets the requirements by keeping a copy of the vendor's certificate","Organizations that use AI can also fall under the AIMS and set up policy, impact assessment and monitoring for their use","The hospital falls under the AIMS as a user but leaves vendor selection to ordinary purchasing and sets no AI-specific evaluation criteria","A user sets up policy and structure, but only the AI developer can perform pre-introduction impact assessment, so the hospital concentrates on monitoring after introduction"],"eEn":"42001 applies to organizations that use AI as well as those that provide it, and the hospital sets up policy, impact assessment and monitoring suited to the use and patient impact. Keeping the vendor's certificate does not replace the user's own arrangements. Relying on ordinary purchasing without AI-specific criteria, or claiming only a developer can do impact assessment, narrows the user's responsibility wrongly."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある人事部門が採用スクリーニングAIを使ったところ、特定の属性の応募者の通過率が著しく低いことが判明しました。責任あるAIの原則に照らして、最初に取るべき対応として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["通過率の差が出た属性の応募者だけに別の基準値を設定して通過率を揃え、偏りの原因となるデータの調査は後回しにする","属性の列を学習データから外せば偏りは必ず消えるため、結果の検証は省略して再学習する","公平性の観点から、属性別の結果の偏りをデータと出力の両面から調べ、緩和策を検討する","公平性の判断は半年分の採用結果が蓄積するまで保留し、それまでは通過率を月次で集計するだけにとどめる"],"a":2,"e":"公平性の観点では、属性別の結果の偏りをデータと出力の両面から調べ、原因に応じた緩和策を検討します。属性ごとに基準値を変えて見かけの通過率を揃えるのは症状への対処で、原因の調査が伴いません。結果の蓄積を待って判断を保留するのは対応の順序が逆です。属性の列を外せば偏りは必ず消えるとする説明は代理変数を見落としています。","qEn":"An HR department found that applicants with a certain attribute have a markedly low pass rate in an AI screening tool. In light of responsible AI principles, what is the most appropriate first response?","oEn":["Set a separate threshold only for applicants of the affected attributes to even out pass rates, postponing any investigation of the data that causes the bias","Remove the attribute column from the training data, since that always eliminates bias, and retrain without verifying results","From a fairness view, investigate the cause of group disparities in both data and outputs and consider mitigation","Hold the fairness judgment until six months of hiring results accumulate and meanwhile only tabulate pass rates monthly"],"eEn":"From a fairness viewpoint, examine the bias in results by attribute from both the data and the outputs, and consider mitigation matching the cause. Setting different thresholds to even out pass rates treats the symptom without investigating the cause, and holding judgment until results accumulate reverses the order. Claiming that removing the attribute column always removes bias overlooks proxy variables."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある金融会社が、与信判断AIの内部ロジックは営業秘密だとして、顧客からの問い合わせに一切説明しない方針を決めました。透明性の観点で最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["内部ロジックのソースコードとモデルの重みを全顧客に公開し、秘密を持たない形にする","個別の判断理由は規制当局への報告書に集約し、顧客からの問い合わせにはその報告書を写して回答する","説明の内容と詳しさは顧客ごとに変えず、社内の技術文書を全問い合わせに同一の内容で渡す","営業秘密は守りつつ、AI利用の事実・目的・主な判断要素・限界を相手に応じた形で丁寧に伝えておく"],"a":3,"e":"透明性は、営業秘密を守りつつ、AI利用の事実、目的、主な判断要素、限界を相手に応じて伝えることで満たします。ソースコードや重みの全面公開は過剰です。規制当局向けの報告書の転記や社内技術文書の一律配布は、受け手に応じた説明になっておらず、顧客が理解できる説明にもなりません。","qEn":"A financial company decided, treating its credit-decision AI logic as a trade secret, never to explain anything in response to customer inquiries. What is the most appropriate revision from the transparency viewpoint?","oEn":["Publish the internal logic's source code and model weights to all customers, leaving no secrets","Consolidate the reasons for individual decisions in a report to the regulator and answer customer inquiries by copying that report","Do not vary the content or level of detail by customer and hand the same internal technical document to every inquiry","Protect the trade secret but tell customers, suitably, that AI is used, its purpose, main factors and limits"],"eEn":"Transparency is met by protecting trade secrets while telling the audience, as suited, the fact of AI use, its purpose, the main decision factors and its limits. Publishing source code and weights is excessive. Copying a regulator report or handing out one internal technical document to everyone is not an explanation tailored to the recipient and customers cannot understand it."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある小売業のチャットボットが誤った返金条件を案内し、顧客に損害が出ました。担当部署は「モデルの提供元の責任だ」と主張しています。説明責任の観点で最も適切な見方はどれですか。","o":["導入した自社が説明責任を負い、提供元との責任分担は契約と社内の役割で明確に定める","モデルの提供元がすべての責任を負うため、自社はAIの出力について顧客への説明義務を負わない","顧客に最終確認を促す画面表示を出していれば、AIの出力に対する自社の説明責任は表示によって免除される","責任は自社と提供元で誤りの割合に応じて事後に按分されるため、役割や契約上の責任分担を事前に定める必要はない"],"a":0,"e":"導入して顧客に提供した自社が説明責任を負い、提供元との責任分担は契約と社内の役割で事前に明確にします。提供元が全責任を負うとする見方、画面表示で免責されるとする見方、同意で顧客側へ移るとする見方、事後に按分すればよいとする見方はいずれも、自社の説明責任と事前の役割整理を欠いています。","qEn":"A retailer's chatbot gave incorrect refund terms and caused customer losses. The responsible department claims, 'It's the model provider's responsibility.' What is the most appropriate view on accountability?","oEn":["As deployer, the company is accountable, and splits responsibility with the provider by contract and internal roles","The model provider bears all responsibility, so the company has no duty to explain the AI's outputs to customers","If the screen prompts the customer to confirm the result, the company's accountability for the AI output is waived by that display","Responsibility is apportioned afterwards by error share between the company and the provider, so roles and contractual allocation need not be set in advance"],"eEn":"The company that deployed it and offers it to customers bears accountability, and the split with the provider is clarified in advance through contracts and internal roles. Views that the provider bears all, that a screen prompt waives it, that consent shifts it to the customer, or that it can be apportioned afterwards all lack the company's own accountability and advance role definition."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある工場の外観検査AIが、ラインの照明を新型に交換した直後から誤判定を増やし、不良品の見逃しも出ました。責任あるAIの堅牢性の原則と運用の観点から、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["導入時の精度試験に合格していれば堅牢性は永続的に保たれるため、環境が変わっても再確認の対象には含めない","環境変化でも想定性能を保てるか検証・継続監視し、照明変更のような変更時に再確認する","誤判定の増加を受けて判定の閾値を厳しく調整し直し、照明変更後の入力での性能検証は次回の定期見直しまで行わない","照明は入力環境の変更なので設備部門が管理すれば足り、AIの性能の確認は年次のレビューで行う"],"a":1,"e":"堅牢性の原則では、環境が変わっても想定性能を保てるかを検証し、継続的に監視し、照明変更のような変更時に再確認します。閾値の調整だけで検証を先送りする対応や、年次レビューまで確認を待つ対応は、変更を契機とした再確認になっていません。導入時の試験の合格だけで堅牢性が永続するとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A factory's visual-inspection AI began producing more misjudgments, including missed defects, right after the line lighting was replaced with a new type. From the robustness principle and operations viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Passing the initial accuracy test keeps robustness permanently, so re-confirmation is not included even when the environment changes","Verify and monitor performance under environmental change, and recheck when changes such as lighting occur","Tighten the decision threshold in response to the rise in errors and do not verify performance on post-change inputs until the next periodic review","Lighting is an input environment change that the facilities department can manage, and AI performance is checked at the annual review"],"eEn":"Under robustness, verify that expected performance holds despite environmental change, monitor continuously, and re-confirm at changes such as the lighting replacement. Only tuning the threshold and deferring verification, or waiting for an annual review, is not a re-check triggered by the change. Claiming that passing the initial test keeps robustness permanent is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるEC事業者が、問い合わせ対応のために収集した顧客のチャットログを、本人への通知なしに新しいレコメンドAIの学習へ流用しようとしています。プライバシーの観点で最初に確認すべき事項はどれですか。","o":["ログは自社が保有しているため、利用目的の確認なしに学習へ自由に流用できるという前提の妥当性","学習データの量と質が十分か、およびデータの分割方法が妥当かどうかの技術的な検証","当初の収集目的と新たな利用目的の整合、および適用される法令上の根拠や本人への通知の要否","レコメンドの精度向上が見込めるかどうか、およびモデルの推論速度が十分かどうか"],"a":2,"e":"最初に確認すべきは、収集時の目的と新しい利用目的の整合、法令上の根拠、本人への通知の要否です。学習データの量・質や分割方法の検証は必要ですが、利用の適否を確かめる前に技術面から入るのは順序が逆です。自社保有だから自由に使えるとする前提や、レコメンドの精度や速度の確認も、プライバシーの確認ではありません。","qEn":"An e-commerce operator plans to reuse customer chat logs collected for inquiry handling to train a new recommendation AI, without notifying the individuals. From the privacy viewpoint, what should be confirmed first?","oEn":["The validity of the premise that, since the company holds the logs, they can be freely reused for training without checking the purpose","Technical checks that the training data is sufficient in quantity and quality and that the data split method is sound","Whether the new purpose fits the original collection purpose, plus the legal basis and any need to notify individuals","Whether recommendation accuracy is expected to improve and whether the model's inference speed is sufficient"],"eEn":"The first thing to confirm is the consistency between the original collection purpose and the new use, the legal basis, and whether notice to individuals is needed. Checking data quantity, quality and splitting is necessary but starting from technical matters before confirming that the use is permissible reverses the order. Assuming free use of owned data, or checking accuracy and speed, is not a privacy check."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある製造業のエンジニアが「ISO/IEC 42001は、AIモデルが満たすべき精度の数値基準を定めているはずだ」と考え、規格に具体的な合格ラインを探しています。この理解への最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["規格には業種別の精度の下限値が付属書に表で示されており、組織はそれを必ず採用しなければならない","規格は精度の数値を定めていないが、基準を決めるのは開発者であり、利用組織は提供元の公称値をそのまま採用する","精度の基準は認証機関が審査のたびに組織ごとに指示するので、組織が自ら設定することはできない","42001はマネジメントシステム規格であり、精度の数値は定めず、組織が用途に応じた基準値を設定して管理する"],"a":3,"e":"42001はマネジメントシステム規格であり、精度の数値は定めず、組織が用途とリスクに応じて基準を設定し管理します。業種別の下限値が付属書にあるとする説明や、認証機関が組織ごとに指示するとする説明は事実に反します。提供元の公称値を無条件に採用する運用は、自らの用途に即した基準設定になっていません。","qEn":"An engineer at a manufacturer assumes 'ISO/IEC 42001 must set numeric accuracy criteria that AI models must meet' and is looking for specific pass marks in the standard. What is the most appropriate correction?","oEn":["The standard's annex gives a table of industry-specific minimum accuracy values that the organization must adopt","The standard sets no accuracy figure, but developers set the criteria, so a user organization adopts the provider's stated value as is","The certification body dictates accuracy criteria for each organization at every audit, so the organization cannot set them itself","42001 sets no accuracy figures; the organization sets criteria from its risks and objectives and manages against them"],"eEn":"42001 is a management system standard that sets no accuracy figures; the organization sets and manages criteria according to use and risk. Claims of sector-specific lower limits in an annex, or of the certification body instructing each organization, are untrue. Adopting the provider's stated value unconditionally is not criteria setting based on the organization's own use."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある経営会議で、役員が「AIのリスクがゼロになったと確認できるまで、AIの本番導入は認めない」と発言しました。AIMSの考え方に沿った最も適切な応答はどれですか。","o":["ゼロにするのではなく、リスク基準に照らして評価・対応し、残余リスクを受容可能に管理する","規格はリスクゼロの達成を認証の条件としているため、役員の方針どおりゼロ確認まで導入を延期する","リスクがゼロにならない場合に備えて、受容基準は定めずに、導入後に発生した損害の大きさを見て受容するか判断する","残余リスクはAIの運用部門が決めてよい事項であり、リスク所有者や経営層の承認は求められない"],"a":0,"e":"AIMSはリスクをゼロにするのではなく、リスク基準に照らして評価・対応し、残余リスクを受容可能な水準に管理します。規格がゼロを認証条件とするという説明は誤りです。受容基準を定めず損害を見てから判断するのは順序が逆で、残余リスクの受容を運用部門に任せ所有者の承認を不要とする説明も責任の所在を誤っています。","qEn":"At an executive meeting, a director said, 'We won't allow production deployment of AI until we can confirm AI risk has reached zero.' What is the most appropriate response in line with AIMS thinking?","oEn":["Rather than reaching zero, assess and treat risk against risk criteria and manage residual risk at an acceptable level","The standard makes zero risk a condition of certification, so defer deployment until zero is confirmed, as the director says","Define no acceptance criteria and decide whether to accept after seeing the size of damage that occurs after introduction","Residual risk may be decided by the AI operating department, and approval by the risk owner or management is not required"],"eEn":"The AIMS does not eliminate risk but evaluates and treats it against risk criteria and manages residual risk to an acceptable level. Claiming the standard requires zero risk is wrong. Setting no acceptance criteria and judging after damage reverses the order, and letting the operating department accept residual risk without owner approval misplaces responsibility."},
{"d":"D1","q":"EU域内で事業を行う企業が「42001の認証を取得すれば、AIに関する各国の法規制にも自動的に適合したと証明できる」と考え、法規制の調査を縮小しようとしています。最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["認証の審査では適用法令の遵守状況も合否の対象になるため、取得後は審査機関が法令適合を保証した状態になる","認証は法令適合を自動的には証明しないので、適用される法令を特定して遵守を継続的に管理していく必要がある","法令は外部の課題として一度特定すれば、認証期間中に新たな規制が制定されても見直さなくてよい","42001は法令遵守を扱うが、対象は自国の国内法に限られ、海外の法規制は適用範囲の検討に含めない"],"a":1,"e":"認証は法令適合を自動的に証明するものではなく、組織が適用される法令を特定し、遵守を管理し続ける必要があります。審査機関が法令適合を保証するとする説明、一度の特定で見直さないとする説明、国内法に限るとする説明は、いずれも組織の継続的な責務を狭めています。","qEn":"A company operating in the EU believes, 'Obtaining 42001 certification automatically proves compliance with national laws and regulations on AI,' and is about to scale down its legal research. What is the most appropriate correction?","oEn":["Compliance with applicable law is also a pass/fail item in the audit, so after certification the certification body has assured legal compliance","Certification does not automatically prove legal compliance; identify applicable laws and manage compliance","Once laws are identified as external issues they need not be revisited during the certification period even if new regulations are enacted","42001 covers legal compliance but only domestic law, and foreign regulations are not considered in the scope"],"eEn":"Certification does not automatically prove legal compliance; the organization must identify applicable laws and keep managing compliance. Claims that the certification body assures compliance, that one identification suffices, or that only domestic law matters all narrow the organization's continuing duty."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある通信会社が、リコメンドAIの旧モデルを廃止して新モデルへ移行します。AIシステムのライフサイクル全体を対象とするAIMSの観点で、廃止時に考慮すべきこととして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["廃止は新モデルの影響評価に統合されるため、旧モデル固有の周知や記録保管は個別に計画しない","旧モデルは停止後すぐに全データと記録を削除すれば、説明責任の問題も法令上の保管義務も生じない","旧モデルの記録保管、データの取扱い、関係者への周知、依存業務への影響を計画的に処理する","廃止の計画は新モデルの導入チームが立て、旧モデルの責任者は運用中の監視に専念して廃止時の関係者への周知には関与しない"],"a":2,"e":"AIMSはライフサイクル全体を対象とし、廃止時にも記録保管、データの取扱い、関係者への周知、依存業務への影響を計画的に処理します。旧モデル固有の対応を新モデルの評価に含めて済ませる扱いや、旧モデルの責任者が廃止に関与しない分担は不十分です。直ちの全削除で問題が生じないとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A telecom company will retire an old recommendation model and move to a new one. From the AIMS viewpoint covering the whole AI system life cycle, what is the most appropriate consideration at retirement?","oEn":["Retirement is folded into the new model's impact assessment, so notification and record retention specific to the old model are not planned separately","Deleting all data and records immediately after stopping the old model avoids accountability issues and legal retention duties","Handle in a planned way records, data handling, notice to stakeholders, and effects on dependent operations","The new model's team plans the retirement and the old model's owner focuses on monitoring during operation, not involving themselves in notifying stakeholders at retirement"],"eEn":"The AIMS covers the whole life cycle, so at retirement records, data handling, stakeholder notification and impact on dependent operations are handled in a planned way. Folding old-model matters into the new model's assessment, or having the old model's owner stay out of retirement, is inadequate. Claiming immediate deletion of everything causes no problem is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある銀行の与信AIでは、融資を申し込んだ個人は銀行のシステム利用者ではありません。AIMSの利害関係者の考え方に照らして、この個人の扱いとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["システムを直接操作しない個人は利害関係者に当たらないため、影響の評価や配慮の対象にならない","契約上の顧客になった時点で初めて利害関係者となるため、申込み段階の個人は評価の対象に含めない","影響を受ける個人は、苦情を申し立てた場合にだけ利害関係者として扱えばよい","AIの決定の影響を受ける個人として、利用者でなくても利害関係者に含め、影響を評価・考慮する"],"a":3,"e":"AIの出力や決定の影響を受ける個人は、システムの利用者でなくても利害関係者であり、影響を評価・考慮する対象です。操作しない者は対象外とする説明、契約後に初めて対象になるとする説明、苦情時のみ扱うとする説明は誤りです。","qEn":"In a bank's credit-scoring AI, individuals who apply for loans are not users of the bank's system. Under the AIMS notion of interested parties, what is the most appropriate treatment of these individuals?","oEn":["Individuals who do not operate the system are not interested parties and are not subjects of impact assessment or consideration","They become interested parties only once they are contracted customers, so applicants are not considered","Affected individuals need be treated as interested parties only if they file a complaint","Include them as interested parties as individuals affected by the AI's decisions, and assess the impact on them"],"eEn":"Individuals affected by an AI's outputs or decisions are interested parties even if they are not users, and the organization assesses and considers impact on them. Excluding non-operators, counting only after contract, or counting only upon complaint are wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある会社で、社員が会社の許可なく外部の生成AIサービスに顧客情報を含む業務データを入力していることが、調査で判明しました。AIMSの考え方に沿った最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["外部AIサービスも対象に含めた利用ルールを定め、周知・教育し、承認済みサービスを監視する","社員個人の判断による利用は本人の責任なので、会社は利用ルールを設けず、機密情報の取扱規程の改訂だけで対応する","事故を避けるため一律に禁止を通知するだけで十分であり、教育や承認済みサービスの用意には踏み込まない","利用ルールは定めるが、承認済みサービスの利用状況の把握はログ保管にとどめ、教育は新入社員研修の一度だけにする"],"a":0,"e":"外部AIサービスも含めた利用ルールを定め、周知・教育し、承認済みサービスを用意して監視することが、AIMSの考え方に沿った対応です。規程の改訂だけで済ませる対応、禁止通知だけで済ませる対応、教育を一度だけにしてログ保管に頼る対応は、いずれも周知・教育・監視の継続性を欠きます。","qEn":"An investigation found that employees at a company were entering business data, including customer information, into external generative AI services without permission. What is the most appropriate response in line with AIMS thinking?","oEn":["Set use rules covering external AI services, train staff, and provide and monitor approved services","Treat individual use as the employee's own responsibility and respond only by revising the confidential information handling rules, without usage rules","Simply announcing a blanket ban is enough, with no training and no approved service provided","Set usage rules but limit visibility of approved services to log retention and give training only once in new-hire orientation"],"eEn":"Setting usage rules that include external AI services, communicating and training, and providing and monitoring approved services fits the AIMS. Revising rules only, issuing only a ban, or training once and relying on log retention all lack continuing communication, training and monitoring."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある医療機器メーカーで、AIの予測精度を最優先にするチームと、判断根拠の説明しやすさを重視するチームが対立しています。責任あるAIの原則どうしの調整として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["精度は常にあらゆる原則に優先すると規格が定めているため、説明可能性は考慮せず精度で決める","用途とリスクに応じて優先度を比べ、根拠を記録し、適切な階層で承認を得る","原則の優先順位は開発チームの多数決で決め、判断に至った根拠の記録や上位の承認は、速度を保つため求めない","説明可能性を優先する場合は精度の低下を許容すると利用者との契約書に記載すれば、社内での優先度の検討は省ける"],"a":1,"e":"責任あるAIの原則どうしが衝突する場合は、用途とリスクに応じて優先度を比べ、根拠を記録し、適切な階層で承認を得ます。多数決で決め記録も承認も求めない方法や、契約書への記載で社内検討を省く方法は、根拠と承認を欠きます。精度が常に優先するとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"At a medical device maker, a team prioritizing AI prediction accuracy and a team valuing explainability of decision grounds are in conflict. What is the most appropriate way to reconcile responsible AI principles?","oEn":["The standard states that accuracy always takes priority over all principles, so decide on accuracy without considering explainability","Weigh priorities by use and risk, record the grounds, and have it approved at an appropriate level","Decide priorities by majority vote in the development team and require no record of the rationale or higher-level approval, to keep speed","Stating in the user contract that lower accuracy is tolerated when explainability is prioritized lets the company skip internal priority review"],"eEn":"When responsible AI principles conflict, compare priorities according to use and risk, record the rationale and obtain approval at an appropriate level. Deciding by majority without record or approval, or skipping internal review by a contract clause, lacks rationale and approval. Claiming accuracy always prevails is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある自治体が住民向け手当の判定を支援するAIを導入します。担当課は「最終判断はAIの出力どおりにすれば効率的」と考えています。人間による監督の観点で最も適切な設計はどれですか。","o":["出力を確認する担当者に覆す権限は与えず、AIの出力を記録するだけの役割とする","確認者の力量は問わず、AIの出力に異議がない場合だけ承認ボタンを押せばよい手順とする","確認が必要な判断を定め、確認者が出力を覆せる権限と力量を持つよう、役割と手順を整える","確認は低信頼度と自己判定された案件のみを対象とし、確認者の力量や出力を覆す権限は特に定めない"],"a":2,"e":"人間による監督では、確認が必要な判断を定め、確認者が出力を覆せる権限と力量を持つよう役割と手順を整えます。覆す権限のない確認、力量を問わず承認する確認、AIの自己判定の低信頼度案件だけを対象にして権限や力量を定めない確認は、実質的な監督になりません。事後対応のみとする運用も事前の確認手順を欠きます。","qEn":"A municipality will introduce an AI that supports allowance determinations for residents. The responsible section thinks 'Following the AI output for final decisions is efficient.' What is the most appropriate design from the human oversight viewpoint?","oEn":["Give the reviewing staff no authority to override and make their role merely recording the AI output","Ignore reviewer competence and make the procedure a button press when there is no objection to the AI output","Define which decisions people must review, with roles and procedures so reviewers can override","Review only cases the AI self-rates as low confidence and set no particular competence or authority for reviewers to override outputs"],"eEn":"Human oversight defines which decisions need review and sets roles and procedures so reviewers have the authority and competence to override outputs. Reviews without override authority, approvals regardless of competence, or reviewing only AI self-rated low-confidence cases without setting authority or competence are not real oversight."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある会社の製品に、クラウド経由の学習型スパム判定モジュールが組み込まれています。担当者は「AIMSの対象は単独のAI製品だけで、組込み部品は含めなくてよい」と主張します。最も適切な見解はどれですか。","o":["製品の一部として組み込まれた時点でAIシステムではなくなるため、AIMSの管理対象から外れる","組込み部品も適用範囲に含めるが、管理策は製品全体で共通の品質管理手順を適用すればよく、AI固有の評価は要求されない","組込み部品がAIMSの対象となるのは、その部品を自社で開発した場合に限られる","AIシステムの定義に当たる組込みの学習型部品も、適用範囲の検討に含め、影響に応じて管理する"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステムの定義に当たる組込みの学習型部品も適用範囲の検討に含め、影響に応じて管理します。製品の一部になった時点でAIMSの対象外になるという説明、自社開発の場合に限るという説明、共通の品質管理だけでAI固有の評価を省く説明は、いずれも組込み部品のAI固有のリスクを見落とします。","qEn":"A company's product has an embedded cloud-based learning spam-detection module. The staff member argues, 'The AIMS covers only standalone AI products, so embedded components need not be included.' What is the most appropriate view?","oEn":["Once embedded as part of a product it ceases to be an AI system, so it falls outside AIMS control","Include the embedded component in scope but apply the product-wide quality procedures, with no AI-specific evaluation required","An embedded component falls under the AIMS only when the company developed that component itself","Include an embedded learning component that fits the AI system definition in the scope review and manage it by impact"],"eEn":"An embedded learning component that meets the AI system definition is considered in scope and managed according to its impact. Claims that it leaves the AIMS once embedded, that only in-house development counts, or that common quality procedures replace AI-specific evaluation all overlook the AI-specific risks of embedded components."},
{"d":"D1","q":"あるSaaS事業者がAI機能を顧客企業に提供しています。顧客が想定外の用途で利用して問題が起きました。提供者の立場でAIMSの観点から最も適切な事前の備えはどれですか。","o":["想定用途・性能・限界・禁止用途を顧客に伝え、責任配分を契約等で事前に明確にする","顧客の用途は顧客の責任であることを利用規約に記載すれば足り、性能や限界に関する情報の提供は求められない","顧客の利用状況を提供者が常時監視し、想定外の用途が見つかった場合は提供者の判断で顧客のアカウントを停止する運用を定める","責任配分は問題発生後に当事者間で協議して決めるため、事前に契約で定める必要はない"],"a":0,"e":"提供者は、想定用途・性能・限界・禁止用途を顧客に伝え、責任配分を契約等で事前に明確にしておくのが最も適切な事前の備えです。利用規約への責任転嫁のみや、問題発生後の協議は事前の備えになりません。利用状況の監視と停止は検知後の対応で、情報提供と責任配分という事前の備えの代わりにはなりません。","qEn":"A SaaS operator provides AI functions to corporate customers. A customer used it for an unintended purpose and a problem arose. As the provider, what is the most appropriate advance preparation from the AIMS viewpoint?","oEn":["Tell customers the intended use, performance, limits and prohibited uses, and allocate responsibility by contract","Stating in the terms that the customer's use is the customer's responsibility suffices, and no information on performance or limits is required","The provider continuously monitors customer use and suspends the customer account at its own discretion when unintended use is found","Responsibility is decided in discussion after a problem occurs, so it need not be set by contract in advance"],"eEn":"The most appropriate advance preparation is for the provider to tell customers the intended use, performance, limits and prohibited uses, and to clarify responsibility allocation by contract beforehand. A terms-only shift of responsibility or discussion after problems is not preparation. Monitoring and suspension are post-detection responses and do not replace advance information and allocation."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある開発チームが、規格本文の要求事項は理解したものの、Annex Aの各管理策を具体的にどう実装すればよいか分からず困っています。参照すべき資料として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["ISO/IEC 23894のリスクマネジメント指針を参照し、各管理策の実装手順をそこから導く","Annex Aの各管理策の実装に関するガイダンスを示すAnnex Bを参照する","ISO/IEC 22989の用語定義が各管理策の実装手順そのものを示しているため、これを参照する","適用宣言書（SoA）が実装方法を詳細に規定しているため、SoAの雛形を参照する"],"a":1,"e":"Annex Aの各管理策の実装に関するガイダンスはAnnex Bに示されます。23894はリスクマネジメントの指針で、管理策ごとの実装手順を示すものではありません。22989は用語の共通基盤であり、SoAは採否と理由を示す文書で、実装方法を規定するものではありません。","qEn":"A development team understands the requirements in the main clauses but cannot tell how to implement each Annex A control concretely. What is the most appropriate reference?","oEn":["Refer to the ISO/IEC 23894 risk management guidance and derive the implementation steps for each control from it","Refer to Annex B, which gives guidance on how to implement each Annex A control","The term definitions of ISO/IEC 22989 are themselves the implementation steps for each control, so refer to them","The Statement of Applicability prescribes implementation in detail, so refer to an SoA template"],"eEn":"Guidance on implementing each Annex A control is given in Annex B. 23894 is risk management guidance and does not give per-control implementation steps. 22989 is a terminology basis, and the SoA records what is applied and why, not how to implement."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業が「AIは法令に違反しなければ十分で、倫理や社会への影響の検討は規格の対象外だ」と考え、AI方針にも法令順守しか書いていません。責任あるAIの考え方に沿った最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["責任あるAIの意味は国内の関係法令に適合することと定められ、倫理的な期待への配慮は組織が任意で行う追加の活動である","倫理や社会への影響の検討はAIが個人の権利に関わる領域で使われる場合に限ればよく、それ以外の用途では法令順守で足りる","責任あるAIは、法令順守に加えて倫理的・社会的な期待や潜在的な影響も考慮する考え方である","社会への影響は事故が発生した後に初めて検討すれば足り、導入前の検討は規格の趣旨に反する"],"a":2,"e":"責任あるAIは、法令順守に加えて倫理的・社会的な期待や潜在的な影響も考慮する考え方です。法令適合に限る定義とする説明や、個人の権利に関わる領域に限る説明は範囲を狭めています。導入前の検討が趣旨に反するとする説明は逆で、事後にだけ検討する扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company believes, 'It is enough that AI does not violate laws; ethics and social impact are outside the standard,' and its AI policy mentions only legal compliance. What is the most appropriate point in line with responsible AI thinking?","oEn":["Responsible AI is defined as conformity to domestic law, and consideration of ethical expectations is an optional extra activity of the organization","Ethical and societal consideration is needed only where AI touches individual rights, and legal compliance suffices for other uses","Responsible AI means developing and using AI per ethical and social expectations as well as law, considering impacts","Social impact need only be considered after an accident occurs, and pre-introduction consideration is contrary to the standard's intent"],"eEn":"Responsible AI considers ethical and societal expectations and potential impacts in addition to legal compliance. Defining it as legal conformity, or limiting it to areas touching individual rights, narrows the scope. Claiming pre-introduction consideration runs against the intent is backwards, and considering only afterwards is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある通販会社が、大規模モデルの学習に伴う電力消費の増大を懸念する株主から質問を受け、回答を求められています。AIMSの組織の状況の考え方に照らして、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["環境面はAIシステムの特性と無関係な事業継続の課題なので、AIMSの外部課題には含めず、サステナビリティ報告書だけで扱う","株主の関心は経営判断の事項なので、AIMSの利害関係者の要求事項としては取り扱わず、取締役会の議事録に記録するにとどめる","環境負荷の削減を、すべてのAIMSで必ず満たすべき固定の数値目標として規格が定めている","環境面を含む外部課題と株主の期待として特定し、関連する範囲で目的や運用に反映する"],"a":3,"e":"環境面を含む外部課題と株主の期待として特定し、関連する範囲で目的や運用に反映するのが適切です。環境面をAIMSの外部課題から外す扱いや、株主の関心を利害関係者の要求事項として扱わない扱いは、組織の状況の理解の範囲を狭めます。規格が環境負荷の固定の数値目標を定めるという説明も誤りです。","qEn":"An online retailer received a question from shareholders concerned about growing power consumption in training large models and is asked to respond. In light of the AIMS notion of organizational context, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Environmental matters are business continuity issues unrelated to AI system characteristics, so exclude them from AIMS external issues and handle them only in sustainability reporting","Shareholder concerns are management decisions, so do not treat them as AIMS stakeholder requirements and only record them in board minutes","The standard sets reducing environmental load as a fixed numeric target that every AIMS must meet","Treat it as an external issue and shareholder expectation, identify what is relevant, and reflect it"],"eEn":"It is appropriate to identify environmental aspects as external issues and shareholder expectations and reflect them in objectives and operation as relevant. Excluding environmental matters from external issues, or not treating shareholder concerns as stakeholder requirements, narrows the understanding of context. Claiming a fixed numeric environmental target is set by the standard is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある金融機関が採用AIの公平性対策として「性別の列を学習データから削除したので、性別による偏りは起こり得ない」と経営層に報告しました。最も適切な評価はどれですか。","o":["他の変数が代理として働き得るため、列の削除だけでは足りず属性別の結果を検証する","削除後は公平性の検証を全体の精度指標だけで行い、属性別の集計は個人情報の目的外利用になるので行わない","性別以外の属性は代理変数にならないので、性別の列さえ削除すれば公平性は確実に担保される","公平性の検証は学習データに属性の列が残っている場合にのみ意味を持ち、削除後は検証できない"],"a":0,"e":"性別の列を削除しても、他の変数が代理として働き得るため、偏りが残る可能性があり、属性別の結果を検証する必要があります。全体の精度指標だけでは属性間の差は見えません。削除すれば確実に担保されるとする説明や、削除後は検証できないとする説明は誤りです。","qEn":"A financial institution reported to management on fairness measures for its hiring AI: 'We removed the gender column from the training data, so gender bias cannot occur.' What is the most appropriate evaluation?","oEn":["Other variables can act as proxies, so removing the column is not enough; verify results by attribute","After deletion verify fairness by overall accuracy metrics only and do not tabulate by attribute since that would be secondary use of personal information","Attributes other than gender cannot become proxy variables, so deleting the gender column surely guarantees fairness","Fairness verification is meaningful only when the attribute column remains in the data, and cannot be done after deletion"],"eEn":"Even after deleting the gender column other variables can act as proxies, so bias may remain and results by attribute must be verified. Overall accuracy does not reveal differences between attributes. Claims that deletion ensures fairness or that verification is impossible afterwards are wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業は、社内文書の要約チャットボットと、融資可否を左右するAIの両方に、まったく同じ水準の管理策を一律に適用しようとしています。AIMSの考え方に沿った最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["影響の小さいAIにも最大水準の管理策を一律に求め、リスクの大小による区別はしない","用途やAIによる影響の大きさに応じ、リスクに比例して管理策の厳格さを決める","影響の大きさに応じて管理策を区別するが、区別の判断は各AIの開発担当者に任せ、リスクアセスメントの結果には基づかせない","管理策の厳格さは利用者数の多寡で決め、影響を受ける個人への危害の大きさは判断材料としない"],"a":1,"e":"AIMSでは、用途やAIによる影響の大きさに応じ、リスクに比例して管理策の厳格さを決めます。最大水準の一律適用は過大で、判断を開発担当者に任せてリスクアセスメントに基づかせない扱い、利用者数だけで決める扱いは、根拠が影響やリスクになっていません。","qEn":"A company plans to apply exactly the same level of controls uniformly to both an internal-document summarization chatbot and an AI that determines loan approvals. What is the most appropriate revision in line with AIMS thinking?","oEn":["Demand the highest level of controls for even low-impact AI uniformly, making no distinction by risk size","Set control stringency in proportion to risk, by use and the size of the AI's impact","Differentiate controls by impact but leave the decision to each AI's developers rather than basing it on the risk assessment results","Set control strictness by the number of users and ignore the magnitude of harm to affected individuals"],"eEn":"The AIMS sets control strictness in proportion to risk according to use and AI impact. A uniform maximum level is excessive, and leaving the call to developers without a risk basis, or using only user numbers, does not rest on impact or risk."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある企業が、顧客向けAIの説明資料を作成しています。開発者向け、一般顧客向け、監査人向けに同一の技術文書を配布する計画です。透明性の観点で最も適切な改善はどれですか。","o":["受け手を区別せず最も詳細な技術文書を全員に配布すれば、透明性は最大化されると考える","顧客向けには一般的なAIの仕組みを説明する共通パンフレットを用意すれば足り、個々のAIシステムの用途や限界は開発者向け資料にとどめる","受け手に応じて内容と詳しさを変え、顧客には用途と限界を、技術者には技術情報を示す","技術文書は監査人向けを基準に作成し、開発者と顧客向けには同じ文書から機密部分を黒塗りしたものを配布する"],"a":2,"e":"透明性は、受け手に応じて内容と詳しさを変え、顧客には用途と限界を、技術者には技術情報を示すことで高まります。最も詳細な文書の一律配布、一般的なパンフレットだけの提供、黒塗りした同一文書の配布は、受け手のニーズに合わせた説明になっていません。","qEn":"A company is preparing explanatory materials for a customer-facing AI. It plans to distribute the same technical document to developers, ordinary customers and auditors. What is the most appropriate improvement from the transparency viewpoint?","oEn":["Distribute the most detailed technical document to everyone without distinguishing audiences, thinking this maximizes transparency","A common brochure explaining how AI works in general suffices for customers, and each system's purpose and limits stay in developer materials","Vary content and detail by audience: use and limits for customers, technical information for engineers and auditors","Write technical documents to auditor level and give developers and customers the same document with confidential parts redacted"],"eEn":"Transparency improves when content and detail are adapted to the audience: purpose and limits for customers and technical information for engineers. Uniform detailed documents, a generic brochure, or a redacted copy of one document do not fit the recipients' needs."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある組織が、42001認証を取得した後は「一度認証を得たので、運用の改善活動や監視は終了してよい」と考えています。AIMSがマネジメントシステムであることを踏まえた最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["認証取得によりAIMSは完成するため、以降は内部監査もマネジメントレビューも求められなくなる","認証後は年次の内部監査だけを行えばよく、マネジメントレビューとAIリスクの再評価は次回の更新審査の前に行えばよい","認証後の改善は認証機関の指摘事項への対応に限られ、組織自身が目的の達成状況を監視して改善する必要は規格上ない","AIMSは継続的に運用・改善するもので、認証後も監視・監査・レビュー・改善を続ける"],"a":3,"e":"AIMSはマネジメントシステムとして継続的に運用・改善するものであり、認証後も監視・内部監査・マネジメントレビュー・改善を続けます。審査の前にまとめて行う扱いや、認証機関の指摘への対応に限る扱いは、継続的な運用を欠きます。認証で完成するという説明も誤りです。","qEn":"After obtaining 42001 certification, an organization thinks, 'We got certified once, so we can stop improvement and monitoring.' What is the most appropriate point given that the AIMS is a management system?","oEn":["Certification completes the AIMS, so internal audit and management review become unnecessary afterwards","After certification only an annual internal audit is needed, and management review and risk reassessment can wait until before the next renewal audit","Post-certification improvement is limited to responding to the certification body's findings, and the standard does not require the organization to monitor objectives and improve","The AIMS is continually operated and improved, so monitoring, audit and review continue after certification"],"eEn":"The AIMS is a management system operated and improved continually, so monitoring, internal audit, management review and improvement continue after certification. Bunching activities before audits or limiting improvement to the certification body's findings lacks continuity. Claiming certification completes the system is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある研究機関が公開データで学習した画像認識AIを、自社の研究用途のみで使っています。営業部門が同じAIを医療機関向けに販売したいと言い出しました。AIMSの観点で最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["用途の変更として、新たな利害関係者と影響を踏まえ、リスクアセスメントと影響評価をやり直す","AIの性能試験は新用途のデータで再実施するが、影響評価は研究用途で実施済みのため医療機関向けでは省略できる","影響評価は医療機関との販売契約を結んだ後に導入先と共同で行えばよく、販売前には研究用の評価結果を流用できる","販売前の評価は営業部門が行えばよく、AIMSの責任者やリスク評価担当は関与しない"],"a":0,"e":"用途が変わるため、新たな利害関係者と影響を踏まえてリスクアセスメントと影響評価をやり直します。性能試験だけを再実施して影響評価を省く扱いや、契約後に評価する扱いは、販売前に新用途の影響を把握するという順序に反します。営業部門だけで評価する扱いも責任体制を欠きます。","qEn":"A research institute uses an image-recognition AI trained on public data only for its own research. The sales department wants to sell the same AI to medical institutions. What is the most appropriate response from the AIMS viewpoint?","oEn":["Treat it as a change of use: redo risk and impact assessment for the new parties and impacts, and review controls","Rerun performance tests on data for the new use, but impact assessment already done for research use can be omitted for medical institutions","Impact assessment can be done jointly with the buyer after the sales contract, reusing the research evaluation until then","Sales alone may perform the pre-sale assessment, and the AIMS owner and risk assessors are not involved"],"eEn":"Because the use changes, redo the risk assessment and impact assessment based on the new stakeholders and impacts. Rerunning only performance tests, or assessing after contract, violates grasping the new use's impacts before sale. Having sales alone assess also lacks proper responsibility."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある会社の監査部門が、複数の認証（ISO 9001、27001、42001）を持つ組織で内部監査を計画しています。高位構造の観点から最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["共通の箇条は統合して監査するが、AI固有の要求事項はAI開発部門の担当者が自部門の運用を自己点検して代替する","共通する箇条は統合して監査し、AI固有の要求事項はAIに関する力量を持つ監査員が確認する","共通の箇条を監査すれば42001固有の要求事項も自動的に確認できるため、AI固有の確認を別に行う必要はないとみなす","42001の内部監査は認証機関の審査に含まれるため、組織の監査部門による計画的な内部監査は省略できる"],"a":1,"e":"高位構造を共有する規格では、共通箇条は統合して監査し、AI固有の要求事項はAIに関する力量を持つ監査員が確認するのが効率的です。自部門による自己点検は客観性・公平性を欠き、内部監査を認証審査で代替する扱いも誤りです。共通箇条の確認だけで固有要求も満たすとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company's audit department is planning an internal audit at an organization holding multiple certifications (ISO 9001, 27001, 42001). From the high-level structure viewpoint, what is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["Audit common clauses together, but AI-specific requirements are replaced by self-checks by the AI development department of its own operations","Audit common clauses together, and have auditors with AI competence verify AI-specific requirements","Auditing the common clauses automatically confirms 42001-specific requirements, so no AI-specific checks are needed","The 42001 internal audit is covered by the certification body's audit, so planned internal audits by the organization's audit function can be omitted"],"eEn":"For standards sharing the high-level structure, common clauses are audited together and AI-specific requirements are checked by auditors competent in AI. Self-checks by the audited department lack objectivity and impartiality, and substituting certification audits for internal audits is wrong. Claiming common-clause checks cover specific requirements is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある通信会社の顧客が、AI提供者である同社に「AIの判断に納得できないので、苦情や懸念を申し立てる窓口を知りたい」と求めています。責任あるAIとAIMSの観点で最も適切な備えはどれですか。","o":["窓口は法令で義務づけられた場合にのみ設ければよく、任意で設置するとかえってリスクが増える","窓口は設けて周知するが、苦情の結果は担当者の個人メモに残し、AIMSの改善やリスクの見直しにはつなげない","利害関係者が懸念や苦情を報告できる窓口と対応手順を整え、周知し、対応結果を記録して改善にも使うようにする","窓口は顧客に限って設け、従業員や取引先などその他の利害関係者からの懸念は受け付けない"],"a":2,"e":"利害関係者が懸念や苦情を報告できる窓口と対応手順を整え、周知し、結果を記録して改善に使います。個人メモにとどめて改善に使わない扱いや、受付対象を顧客だけに限る扱いは、窓口の目的を果たしません。法令上の義務がある場合に限るとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A customer of a telecom company, which is the AI provider, asks, 'I cannot accept the AI's decision; I want to know where to file a complaint or concern.' From the responsible AI and AIMS viewpoint, what is the most appropriate preparation?","oEn":["Set up a channel only when a law requires it, since voluntary setup instead raises risk","Set up and publicize a channel but keep complaint results in the handler's personal notes and do not feed them into AIMS improvement or risk review","Set up and publicize a channel and process for concerns or complaints, and record outcomes for improvement","Set a channel for customers only and do not accept concerns from employees, partners or other stakeholders"],"eEn":"Provide a channel and procedure for stakeholders to raise concerns or complaints, publicize it, record results and use them for improvement. Keeping results in personal notes, or limiting intake to customers, fails the channel's purpose. Limiting it to legal obligation is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある通販会社のカスタマーサポートAIは、公開後も利用者との会話から継続的に学習して応答を更新します。担当者は「リリース時の試験に合格したので、以後の性能確認は不要だ」と考えています。AIMSの観点で最も適切な見解はどれですか。","o":["学習結果の更新は年1回の定期レビューで確認し、その間の応答品質の監視は利用者からの苦情を待って行う","性能の変化は初期のモデルの欠陥だけで起こるので、リリース時に試験すれば運用中の確認は省ける","性能の確認は開発部門が学習の更新時に行えば足り、運用中の応答の変化の継続的な監視はAIMSでは求められない","公開後にも挙動が変わり得るので、運用中の継続的な監視と変更の管理をあらかじめ計画に組み込んでおく必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"継続学習するAIは公開後も挙動が変わり得るため、運用中の継続的な監視と変更の管理を計画に組み込む必要があります。年1回の確認や苦情待ちの監視、更新時だけの確認は、挙動の変化をタイムリーにとらえられません。継続学習AIはAIMSの対象外とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"An online retailer's customer-support AI keeps learning from conversations with users after release and updates its responses. The staff member thinks, 'It passed the release tests, so later performance checks are unnecessary.' What is the most appropriate view from the AIMS viewpoint?","oEn":["Check learning updates at an annual review and, in between, monitor response quality only after complaints from users","Performance change arises only from initial model defects, so testing at release lets operation-time checks be skipped","Performance checks by the development department at updates suffice, and continuous monitoring of response changes in operation is not required by the AIMS","Behavior can change after release, so build continual monitoring and change management into the plan"],"eEn":"Continuously learning AI can change behavior after release, so ongoing monitoring and change management in operation must be planned. Annual checks, complaint-driven monitoring or checks only at updates cannot catch behavior change in time. Claiming learning AI is outside the AIMS is also wrong."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある物流会社が、倉庫内で人と同じ通路を走る搬送ロボットの経路選択にAIを導入します。責任あるAIの安全の観点から、設計段階で優先して確認すべき事項として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["人への危害につながる状況の想定、異常時に安全側へ移行する動作、人が停止させられる手段を設計に含める","人との接触の想定は搬送の効率を損なわない範囲に限って設計に含め、効率と安全が両立しない場合は効率を優先する","異常時の動作はロボットの機構部の安全装置に任せ、AIの経路選択の設計では想定外の入力に対する挙動の検証を省く","人への危害は保守点検と作業員の安全教育で防ぐ事項とし、AIの設計では経路選択の性能を優先して安全側への移行動作は運用開始後に検討する"],"a":0,"e":"安全の観点では、人への危害につながる状況の想定、異常時に安全側へ移行する動作、人が停止させられる手段を設計段階から含めます。効率を優先する設計、機構部の安全装置への依存、保守と教育への依存、運用後に安全側の動作を検討する扱いは、いずれもAI自体の設計での安全確認を欠きます。","qEn":"A logistics company will introduce AI for route selection of transport robots that share aisles with people in a warehouse. From the responsible AI safety viewpoint, what is the most appropriate item to confirm first at the design stage?","oEn":["Include in the design the anticipation of situations that could harm people, behavior shifting to a safe state on abnormality, and a means for people to stop the robot","Include contact with people in the design only to the extent that it does not impair efficiency, prioritizing efficiency when the two conflict","Leave abnormal behavior to the robot's mechanical safety devices and omit verifying the AI route selection against unexpected inputs","Treat harm to people as a matter for maintenance and worker safety training, prioritize route selection performance in AI design and consider fail-safe behavior after operation starts"],"eEn":"For safety, include from the design stage the assumption of situations leading to harm, fail-safe behavior on abnormality, and means for humans to stop the system. Prioritizing efficiency, relying on mechanical devices, relying on maintenance and training, or deferring fail-safe behavior until after operation all lack safety verification in the AI design itself."},
{"d":"D1","q":"ある小売業が、ベンダーの大規模言語モデルを自社データで調整し、自社ブランドの接客AIとして顧客に提供しています。AIの役割の観点で、この小売業の立場として最も適切な理解はどれですか。","o":["ベンダーのモデルを使っているので提供者にはならず、顧客への情報提供や責任の整理はベンダーだけが行えばよい","自社データで調整した時点で自社は開発者になるので、利用者としての責任はなくなり、ベンダーへの管理も求められなくなる","AIの利用者であると同時に顧客へAIシステムを提供する側でもあり、提供者としての情報提供や責任の整理が必要だ","顧客に提供する場合でも自社は単なる販売仲介にすぎず、AIの用途や限界に関する説明の責任は顧客が負う"],"a":2,"e":"他社のモデルを基に自社ブランドで顧客へAIシステムを提供する組織は、利用者であると同時に提供者でもあり、提供者としての情報提供と責任の整理が必要です。ベンダーだけが負うとする説明、利用者の責任がなくなるとする説明、顧客が説明責任を負うとする説明は誤りです。","qEn":"A retailer adjusts a vendor's large language model with its own data and provides it to customers as its own-brand service AI. In terms of AI roles, what is the most appropriate understanding of the retailer's position?","oEn":["It uses the vendor's model so it is not a provider, and only the vendor need provide customer information and organize responsibilities","By tuning with its own data it becomes the developer, so user responsibilities vanish and managing the vendor is unnecessary","It is both a user and a provider of an AI system to customers, so it must organize provider-side information and responsibilities","Even when providing to customers it is a mere sales intermediary, and the customer bears responsibility for explaining AI use and limits"],"eEn":"An organization that provides an AI system to customers under its own brand based on another's model is both a user and a provider, and must organize provider-side information and responsibilities. Claims that only the vendor bears this, that user duties vanish, or that customers bear explanation duty are wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある保険会社が、新たなAI関連の法規制の公表と、顧客のAIへの不信感の高まりを受けて、AIMSの検討を始めました。Clause 4.1「組織及びその状況の理解」の観点で最も適切な扱いはどれですか。","o":["法規制は外部の課題だが顧客の不信感は課題に当たらないため、法規制の対応だけを特定して以後は固定する","課題の特定は年1回の定期見直しで行えばよく、法規制の公表のような外部の変化は次回の年次見直しまで反映を待つ","内部課題は経営層のレビューで特定済みとし、外部の課題はリスクアセスメントの中で特定するため4.1では特定しない","AIMSの意図した成果に影響する内外の課題として特定し、状況の変化に応じて見直す"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 4.1では、AIMSの意図した成果に影響する内外の課題を特定し、状況の変化に応じて見直します。年1回の見直しまで外部の変化の反映を待つ扱いや、外部の課題をリスクアセスメントの中で特定するとして4.1から外す扱いは、課題の特定という4.1の要求を満たしません。顧客の不信感も課題に当たり得ます。","qEn":"An insurance company began considering an AIMS after new AI-related regulation was announced and customer distrust of AI grew. Under Clause 4.1 'understanding the organization and its context', what is the most appropriate handling?","oEn":["Regulation is an external issue but customer distrust is not, so identify only regulation and fix it from then on","Identify issues at an annual periodic review and wait until the next annual review to reflect external changes such as new regulations","Internal issues are already identified at management review and external issues are identified within risk assessment, so they are not identified in 4.1","Identify them as internal and external issues affecting the intended outcomes of the AIMS, and review them as circumstances change"],"eEn":"Clause 4.1 requires identifying internal and external issues that affect the intended outcomes of the AIMS and reviewing them as circumstances change. Waiting for an annual review, or moving external issues out of 4.1 into the risk assessment, does not meet the requirement to identify issues. Customer distrust can also be an issue."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある製造業の情報システム部が、AIMSの課題を洗い出しています。「AI人材の不足」と「古い基幹システムのデータ品質の低さ」を挙げましたが、課題は外部要因だけだと主張する部員もいます。Clause 4.1の考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["対象は外部の課題と内部の課題の両方だが、人材やデータの状況は課題ではなく利害関係者のニーズとして4.2で特定する","人材不足やデータ品質のような組織内の事情も、AIMSに関連する内部の課題として特定する対象になる","内部の事情は課題ではなくAIMSの資源の問題なので、Clause 7.1で扱えばよく、Clause 4.1では特定しない","内部の課題は内部監査で見つかった不適合として扱い、4.1の時点では特定せず、是正処置の対象として10.2で扱う"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 4.1は内部と外部の課題の両方を特定する要求で、人材不足やデータ品質のような組織内の事情も内部の課題に当たります。これを4.2の利害関係者のニーズに置き換える扱い、7.1の資源の問題とする扱い、不適合として10.2の是正処置で扱う扱いは、いずれも箇条の役割を取り違えています。","qEn":"A manufacturer's IT department is listing AIMS issues. It raised 'shortage of AI talent' and 'poor data quality in legacy core systems,' but a member argues issues are only external factors. What is the most appropriate view under Clause 4.1?","oEn":["Both external and internal issues are covered, but staffing and data status are identified in 4.2 as stakeholder needs rather than as issues","Internal circumstances such as talent shortage and data quality are also identified as internal issues relevant to the AIMS","Internal circumstances are resource matters, not issues, so handle them in Clause 7.1 and do not identify them in Clause 4.1","Internal issues are treated as nonconformities found by internal audit, not identified at 4.1 but handled in 10.2 as corrective action"],"eEn":"Clause 4.1 requires identifying both internal and external issues, so organizational matters like staffing and data quality are internal issues. Relabeling them as 4.2 stakeholder needs, 7.1 resources, or nonconformities handled under 10.2 corrective action confuses the roles of the clauses."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある医療系ベンチャーが、Clause 4.2「利害関係者のニーズ及び期待の理解」で、顧客・株主・規制当局を挙げました。患者や従業員の期待は挙げていません。この進め方への最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["利害関係者は契約関係のある相手に限られるので、契約のない患者の期待は特定の対象から外してよい","利害関係者の特定はAIMSの適用範囲を決定した後に行えばよく、運用の開始以降に特定しても要求を満たせる","AIMSに関連する利害関係者と、その要求事項を、AIの影響を受ける患者や従業員も含めて漏れなく特定する","利害関係者のニーズは顧客満足度の調査で代替できるため、規制当局以外の期待は個別に特定する必要がない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 4.2では、AIMSに関連する利害関係者とその要求事項を、AIの影響を受ける患者や従業員も含めて漏れなく特定します。契約関係に限定する扱いや、顧客満足度調査で代替する扱いは範囲が狭すぎます。適用範囲の決定は利害関係者の要求事項を考慮して行うため、特定を範囲決定の後に回す順序も誤りです。","qEn":"A medical venture listed customers, shareholders and regulators under Clause 4.2 'understanding the needs and expectations of interested parties' but omitted patients and employees. What is the most appropriate point about this approach?","oEn":["Interested parties are limited to those with contracts, so patients' expectations with no contract may be left out","Stakeholders can be identified after the scope is set, even after operation begins, and still meet the requirement","Identify the interested parties relevant to the AIMS and their requirements, including patients and employees the AI affects","Interested parties' needs can be replaced by satisfaction surveys, so expectations other than regulators need not be individually identified"],"eEn":"Clause 4.2 requires identifying the stakeholders relevant to the AIMS and their requirements, including patients and employees affected by AI. Limiting to contractual parties or substituting customer surveys is too narrow. Scope is decided considering stakeholder requirements, so deferring identification until after scoping reverses the order."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業は、Clause 4.2で特定した利害関係者の要求事項が多岐にわたるため、すべてを自動的に法的義務として扱うのか、悩んでいます。規格の考え方として最も適切な扱いはどれですか。","o":["特定した要求事項はすべて自動的に法的義務となるため、取捨選択の余地はなく全部をAIMSで満たす","特定した要求事項のうち、どれをAIMSで取り組む対象として採用するかを組織が決定する","要求事項は法令・規制の要求と契約上の要求に限られ、法的拘束力のない利害関係者の期待はAIMSでは扱えない","要求事項の採否は経営層ではなく内部監査員が決め、結果は内部監査報告書に記録する"],"a":1,"e":"特定した利害関係者の要求事項のうち、どれをAIMSで取り組む対象とするかは組織が決定します。すべてを自動的な法的義務とする扱い、法令・契約上の要求に限る扱いは範囲を誤っており、内部監査員や認証機関が採否を決める扱いは、組織自身の責任と役割を取り違えています。","qEn":"A company is unsure whether it must treat all of the wide-ranging interested party requirements identified under Clause 4.2 as automatic legal obligations. What is the most appropriate handling in the standard's thinking?","oEn":["All identified requirements automatically become legal obligations, leaving no room to choose, so satisfy all through the AIMS","The organization decides which of the identified requirements it will adopt as subjects to address through the AIMS","Requirements are limited to legal, regulatory and contractual ones, and non-binding stakeholder expectations cannot be handled in the AIMS","The adoption of requirements is decided by internal auditors rather than management and recorded in the internal audit report"],"eEn":"The organization decides which stakeholder requirements it will address through the AIMS. Treating all as automatic legal obligations, or limiting to legal and contractual ones, misjudges the scope, and having auditors or the certification body decide confuses the organization's own responsibility and roles."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、AIMSの適用範囲を決める際に、AI機能の開発を外部の委託先に任せている領域をどう扱うか迷っています。Clause 4.3「適用範囲の決定」の考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["委託先の活動は適用範囲から除外し、委託先との関係は適用範囲ではなく利害関係者のニーズの一つとして4.2で扱えば足りる","委託している領域は自動的に自社の適用範囲に含まれるため、境界や適用可能性を文書で示す必要がなくなる","適用範囲は組織内外の課題と利害関係者の要求を考慮して決めるが、委託先が実施する活動は契約書の条文の範囲で自動的に定まる","自社が行う活動と他の組織が行う活動との間のインタフェースおよび依存関係を十分に考慮して、境界と適用可能性を決定しておく"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 4.3では、自社の活動と他組織が行う活動とのインタフェースや依存関係を考慮して、境界と適用可能性を決めます。委託先の活動を範囲から外して4.2だけで扱う扱いや、契約書の条文で自動的に定まるとする扱いは、境界と依存関係の検討を欠きます。自動的に含まれ文書化も不要とする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company is unsure how to treat an area where AI function development is entrusted to an external contractor when determining its AIMS scope. What is the most appropriate view under Clause 4.3 'determining the scope'?","oEn":["Exclude the contractor's activities from scope and treat the relationship only as a stakeholder need under 4.2","The entrusted area is automatically included in the company's scope, so there is no need to document boundaries or applicability","Scope considers issues and requirements, but the contractor's activities are determined automatically within the contract text","Determine the boundaries and applicability considering the interfaces and dependencies between the company's activities and those of other organizations"],"eEn":"Clause 4.3 decides boundaries and applicability considering interfaces and dependencies between the organization's own activities and those of other organizations. Excluding the contractor and handling it only under 4.2, or letting the contract text decide automatically, lacks consideration of boundaries and dependencies. Claiming automatic inclusion without documentation is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業が、AIMSの適用範囲を社内の稟議資料の形でまとめましたが、認証審査の場でその資料を提示できませんでした。Clause 4.3の要求の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["適用範囲は文書化した情報として利用可能にしておく必要があり、審査で示せる形で維持する","適用範囲は審査員が口頭で質問した際に担当者が説明できれば足り、文書化した情報として残すことまでは要求されない","適用範囲の文書化は認証取得の後に初めて必要になるため、審査の時点で提示できなくても要求の不適合にはならない","適用範囲は文書化するが、秘密情報の観点から審査員にも原文は提示せず、要約だけを提示すれば要求を満たす"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.3では、適用範囲を文書化した情報として利用可能にし、審査で示せる形で維持します。口頭説明で足りるとする扱い、認証取得後に初めて必要になるとする扱い、原文を審査員に示さず要約のみとする扱いは、いずれも要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company compiled its AIMS scope as an internal approval memo but could not present it at the certification audit. From the Clause 4.3 requirement, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["The scope must be available as documented information, maintained in a form that can be shown at audit","It suffices that staff can explain the scope orally when an auditor asks; keeping it as documented information is not required","Documenting the scope becomes necessary only after certification, so being unable to show it at audit is not a nonconformity","Document the scope but, for confidentiality, show auditors only a summary rather than the original, which meets the requirement"],"eEn":"Clause 4.3 requires the scope to be available as documented information and maintained so it can be shown at audit. Oral explanation, deferring until after certification, or showing auditors only a summary does not meet the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある社内プロジェクトは、AIMSの計画書を作成して一度承認を得た後、運用や改善の仕組みを検討せずに終了しました。Clause 4.4「AIマネジメントシステム」の要求として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["必要なプロセスとその相互作用を含め、AIMSを確立・実施・維持し、継続的に改善することが求められる","AIMSは計画書の作成と承認で確立されたとみなされるため、実施や維持の仕組みは次期の予算が付いた段階で整えればよい","必要なプロセスとその相互作用はAIMSの確立時に一度決めれば、運用中に変更があっても見直さなくてよい","AIMSの継続的改善は10章で扱う事項で、4.4はAIMSの確立と実施のみを求め、維持や改善までは求めない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 4.4では、必要なプロセスとその相互作用を含め、AIMSを確立・実施・維持し、継続的に改善することが求められます。プロセスを一度決めれば足りるとする扱いや、4.4は確立と実施のみとして維持や改善を10章に委ねる扱いは、4.4の要求を狭めています。計画書の承認だけで確立とみなす扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"An internal project drafted an AIMS plan, got it approved once, and ended without considering operation or improvement mechanisms. What is the most appropriate point under Clause 4.4 'AI management system'?","oEn":["The organization must establish, implement, maintain and continually improve the AIMS, including the needed processes and their interactions","The AIMS is deemed established upon plan approval, so implementation and maintenance mechanisms can be arranged when next period's budget is allocated","Decide the necessary processes and interactions once when establishing the AIMS and do not revisit them even if operation changes","Continual improvement is a Clause 10 matter, and 4.4 only requires establishing and implementing, not maintaining or improving"],"eEn":"Clause 4.4 requires establishing, implementing, maintaining and continually improving the AIMS, including the necessary processes and their interactions. Deciding processes once, or reading 4.4 as only establish and implement while leaving maintenance and improvement to Clause 10, narrows the requirement. Treating plan approval alone as establishment is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社のトップマネジメントが「AIMSは情報システム部の仕事だ」として、事業部門の業務プロセスとの統合には関与していません。Clause 5.1「リーダーシップ及びコミットメント」の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["トップマネジメントは方針と目的の承認に関与すれば足り、事業プロセスへの統合は情報システム部の責任として5.3で担当者に割り当てればよい","AIMSの要求事項を組織の事業プロセスに統合し、資源を確保し、有効性への貢献を人々に促すことが求められる","事業プロセスへの統合は各事業部門の判断に任せるべき事項であり、トップマネジメントが促すと自律性を損なう","資源の確保は事業部門の予算で個別に行われるため、トップマネジメントは資源が利用可能であることを確認する責任を負わない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 5.1では、トップマネジメントがAIMSの要求事項を事業プロセスに統合し、資源が利用可能であるようにし、有効性への貢献を人々に促すことが求められます。統合を担当者に割り当てて済ませる扱い、資源を各部門の予算に任せる扱い、事業部門の自律性を理由に促さない扱いは、いずれもトップマネジメントの責任を移し替えています。","qEn":"A company's top management says, 'The AIMS is the IT department's job,' and is not involved in integrating it with business departments' processes. What is the most appropriate point under Clause 5.1 'leadership and commitment'?","oEn":["Top management need only approve policy and objectives, and integration into business processes is assigned to the IT department's staff under 5.3","Top management must integrate AIMS requirements into business processes, ensure resources, and encourage people to contribute to effectiveness","Integration into business processes should be left to each department's judgment, and top management prompting it would harm autonomy","Resources are secured individually by business unit budgets, so top management has no responsibility to ensure resources are available"],"eEn":"Clause 5.1 requires top management to integrate AIMS requirements into business processes, ensure resources are available and encourage people to contribute to effectiveness. Assigning integration to staff, leaving resources to unit budgets, or not encouraging for autonomy shifts top management's responsibility elsewhere."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業のAI方針は、本社の金庫にしまわれた文書で、従業員も取引先も内容を知りません。Clause 5.2「方針」の要求の観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["AI方針は経営層の内部資料にとどめ、従業員への伝達は問い合わせがあった場合に個別に行うこととする","AI方針は利害関係者に利用可能にするが、組織内への伝達は5.3の役割を持つ者に限ればよい","AI方針を文書化情報として利用可能にし、組織内に伝達し、適切な場合は利害関係者にも利用可能にする","AI方針の伝達は年度初めの全社会議で一度行えば足り、期中に改訂したときの再伝達は次年度の会議まで待ってよい"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 5.2では、AI方針を文書化情報として利用可能にし、組織内に伝達し、適切な場合は利害関係者にも利用可能にします。組織内への伝達を役割を持つ者に限る扱いや、改訂時の再伝達を翌年まで待つ扱い、問い合わせ時にだけ伝える扱いは、いずれも伝達の要求を満たしません。利害関係者への利用可能化は禁止されていません。","qEn":"A company's AI policy is a document locked in a head-office safe, unknown to employees and business partners. From the Clause 5.2 'policy' requirement, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Keep the AI policy as an internal management document and convey it to employees individually only when they ask","Make the AI policy available to stakeholders but communicate it within the organization only to those with roles under 5.3","Make the AI policy available as documented information, communicate it internally, and share it with interested parties as appropriate","Communicate the AI policy once at the annual all-hands meeting and wait until next year's meeting to re-communicate a mid-year revision"],"eEn":"Clause 5.2 requires the AI policy to be available as documented information, communicated within the organization and, where appropriate, available to stakeholders. Limiting internal communication to role holders, waiting a year to re-communicate revisions, or telling only on inquiry fails the requirement. Making it available to stakeholders is not prohibited."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業のAI方針は「利用者のデータは広く活用する」と定めていますが、既存のプライバシー方針は目的外利用の制限を定めています。AI方針の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["AI方針は独立した文書なので、既存のプライバシー方針と矛盾しても、AI方針のほうを優先して運用を続ける","AI方針と既存の方針の整合は6.1のリスクアセスメントの結果が出た後で確認すれば足り、策定時点では整合の確認は求められない","矛盾を解消するため、AI方針の側を既存のプライバシー方針の文言と同一にし、AI固有の方針事項は別途定めない","AI方針を既存の組織の方針と整合させ、必要ならどちらかを改訂して矛盾を解消する"],"a":3,"e":"AI方針は既存の組織の方針と整合させ、矛盾があれば必要に応じてどちらかを改訂して解消します。矛盾を残して運用する扱い、整合の確認をリスクアセスメント後に回す扱い、AI方針を既存方針と同一にしてAI固有事項を定めない扱いは、AI方針の策定と整合の要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's AI policy states 'user data is to be used broadly,' while its existing privacy policy restricts use beyond the original purpose. From the AI policy viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["The AI policy is an independent document, so keep operating with it taking priority even if it contradicts the existing privacy policy","Alignment of the AI policy with existing policies can be checked after the 6.1 risk assessment results, not at drafting","To resolve the contradiction, make the AI policy identical to the existing privacy policy wording and define no AI-specific policy matters","Align the AI policy with the organization's existing policies and revise one of them if needed to resolve the contradiction"],"eEn":"The AI policy should be aligned with existing organizational policies, revising either as needed to resolve contradictions. Operating with the contradiction, deferring alignment until after risk assessment, or making the AI policy identical to the existing one with no AI-specific matters does not meet the policy and alignment requirements."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社では、AIの不具合が起きたとき、誰が判断し誰が経営層へ報告するのかが決まっておらず、対応が遅れました。Clause 5.3「組織の役割、責任及び権限」の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["AIMSの関連する役割の責任と権限を割り当てて伝達し、AIMSの状況を経営層へ報告する責任も定める","役割の割当ては各部門の運用手順書に任せ、AIの不具合時の判断者と報告先は不具合の発生後に責任部署の協議で決める","責任と権限はAIMS責任者に集中させ、各部門長にはAIMSに関する報告の責任だけを割り当て、判断の権限は与えない","役割の割当ては人事部門の職務分掌で足りるため、AIMSの状況を経営層に報告する責任は内部監査員に一括して割り当てる"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 5.3では、トップマネジメントがAIMSに関連する役割の責任と権限を割り当てて伝達し、AIMSの状況を経営層へ報告する責任も定めます。発生後に協議で決める扱い、判断権限を与えず報告だけを割り当てる扱い、報告責任を内部監査員に割り当てる扱いは、事前の明確な責任と権限の割当てになっていません。","qEn":"At a company, when an AI malfunction occurred, who decides and who reports to management had not been set, so the response was delayed. Under Clause 5.3 'organizational roles, responsibilities and authorities', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Assign and communicate responsibilities and authorities for relevant AIMS roles within the organization, and define who reports AIMS status to management","Leave role assignment to each department's operating procedures and decide the judge and reporting line after a failure by consultation among responsible departments","Concentrate responsibility and authority in the AIMS manager and give department heads only reporting duties with no decision authority","Role assignment is covered by HR duty allocation, so responsibility to report AIMS status to management is assigned to internal auditors"],"eEn":"Under Clause 5.3 top management assigns and communicates responsibilities and authorities for AIMS roles, including responsibility to report AIMS status to management. Deciding after a failure, giving reporting duty without decision authority, or assigning reporting to internal auditors is not clear advance assignment of responsibility and authority."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業のAIMS担当者は、Clause 6.1「リスク及び機会への取組み」を、リスクの洗い出しだけの作業と理解しています。規格の考え方として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["6.1は脅威となるリスクだけを扱う箇条であり、事業上の機会の検討は、AIMSの計画の対象から外れる","リスクだけでなく機会も決定し、AIMSの意図した成果への確信を与え、望ましくない影響を防ぎ低減する","リスクと機会は4.1・4.2の結果ではなく直近の事故事例から決めるべきで、課題や利害関係者の要求事項の見直しとは連動させない","6.1で決めた取組みはAIMSのプロセスに統合して実施するが、その有効性の評価は9.1の対象外であり、実施結果の確認も求められない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.1では、4.1・4.2で特定した課題と要求事項を考慮して、リスクだけでなく機会も決定し、AIMSの意図した成果への確信を与え、望ましくない影響を防ぎ低減します。事故事例だけから決める扱いや、取組みの有効性を評価しない扱いは、計画の要求を損ないます。脅威のみを扱う理解も誤りです。","qEn":"An AIMS staff member understands Clause 6.1 'actions to address risks and opportunities' as merely listing risks. What is the most appropriate point about the standard's thinking?","oEn":["Clause 6.1 handles only threatening risks, and consideration of business opportunities falls outside AIMS planning","Determine opportunities as well as risks, give confidence in intended outcomes, and prevent or reduce undesired effects","Risks and opportunities should be determined from recent incident cases rather than the results of 4.1 and 4.2, without linking to issue or requirement reviews","Actions decided in 6.1 are integrated into AIMS processes, but evaluating their effectiveness is outside 9.1 and results are not checked"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1 considers the issues and requirements from 4.1 and 4.2 to determine both risks and opportunities, giving assurance of intended outcomes and preventing or reducing undesired effects. Deciding only from incident cases, or not evaluating the effectiveness of actions, undermines planning. Treating only threats is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社で、同じAIシステムの同じリスクを、チームAは「高」、チームBは「低」と評価し、結果が一致しませんでした。Clause 6.1.2「AIリスクアセスメント」の観点で最も適切な改善はどれですか。","o":["評価の方法はチームごとに最適化してよいが、結果の比較のため評価後に点数だけを共通の尺度へ換算して集計する","常に厳しいほうの評価を採用する運用に統一すれば、リスク基準を定めなくても、評価の一貫性は確保される","リスク基準を含む評価プロセスを定め、繰り返しても一貫した妥当で比較可能な結果を得られるようにする","評価の一貫性は評価者の経験年数で確保できるので、最も経験の長い担当者の評価を毎回採用し、評価基準の文書化は省く"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 6.1.2では、リスク基準を含む評価プロセスを定め、繰り返しても一貫した、妥当で比較可能な結果が得られるようにします。方法がばらばらなまま事後に点数だけを換算する扱いや、経験年数に頼って基準を文書化しない扱い、常に厳しい方を採る扱いは、プロセスの定義と基準による一貫性を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company, Team A rated the same risk of the same AI system 'high' and Team B rated it 'low,' with inconsistent results. From the Clause 6.1.2 'AI risk assessment' viewpoint, what is the most appropriate improvement?","oEn":["Each team may optimize its method, and for comparison scores are converted to a common scale and tallied after assessment","Standardizing on always taking the stricter rating secures consistency without defining risk criteria","Define an assessment process including risk criteria so that repeated assessments produce consistent, valid and comparable results","Consistency is secured by evaluator experience, so always adopt the most experienced person's evaluation and skip documenting criteria"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.2 requires defining an assessment process including risk criteria so that repeated assessments yield consistent, valid and comparable results. Converting scores afterwards from differing methods, relying on experience without documented criteria, or always taking the stricter result lacks a defined process and criteria-based consistency."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社のAIリスクアセスメントは、AIシステムが誤作動した場合に自社の売上が減るリスクだけを列挙しています。Clause 6.1.2の観点で、見直すべき点として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["個人や社会への影響は6.1.4のAIシステム影響評価で扱うため、リスクアセスメントでは自社の事業目的に対するリスクに限定してよい","結果の特定は影響評価で行うものなので、リスクアセスメントではリスク源の特定と発生可能性の推定を行えば足りる","リスクの評価は、結果の大きさを数値化できる場合に限って行えばよく、数値化できない影響は、評価の対象から外す","リスク源と起こり得る結果を特定し、結果の影響が自社だけでなく個人や社会に及ぶ場合も考慮して分析・評価する"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 6.1.2では、リスク源と起こり得る結果を特定し、結果の影響が自社だけでなく個人や社会に及ぶ場合も考慮して分析・評価します。影響評価で扱うからとして個人や社会を除く扱いや、結果の特定を影響評価に委ねる扱いは、リスクアセスメントと影響評価の役割の取り違えです。数値化できる影響に限る扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company's AI risk assessment lists only the risk that revenue would fall if the AI system malfunctioned. From the Clause 6.1.2 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate point to revisit?","oEn":["Impact on individuals and society is handled by the 6.1.4 impact assessment, so the risk assessment may be limited to risks to the organization's business objectives","Identifying consequences belongs to the impact assessment, so the risk assessment need only identify risk sources and estimate likelihood","Risk evaluation need only be done where the size of consequences can be quantified, and effects that cannot be quantified are excluded","Identify risk sources and consequences, then analyze and evaluate them, including consequences reaching individuals and society"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.2 identifies risk sources and potential consequences and analyzes and evaluates them, also considering effects on individuals and society, not only the organization. Excluding individuals and society because of the impact assessment, or leaving consequence identification to it, confuses the roles of risk and impact assessment. Limiting to quantifiable effects is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の担当者が、AIリスクアセスメントを行わずに、Annex Aの管理策の中から使いやすいものを選んで実装し、「これでリスク対応は完了した」と報告しています。Clause 6.1.3の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["リスクアセスメントの結果に基づいて必要な管理策を決め、Annex Aと照らして必要な管理策の漏れがないか確認する","使いやすい管理策を選んでも、リスク対応計画に実装時期と責任者が記載されていれば、リスクアセスメントの結果との対応づけは省略できる","Annex Aの管理策に載っていないものは、リスク対応として採用してはならないため、独自の管理策は検討しない","リスク対応の完了は、Annex Aの全管理策を採用した時点で判断でき、適用しない管理策を決める必要もその理由を記録する必要もない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 6.1.3では、リスクアセスメントの結果に基づいて必要な管理策を決め、Annex Aと照らして必要な管理策の漏れがないか確認します。結果との対応づけを省く扱いや、Annex A全採用で完了とし不採用の理由を記録しない扱いは、リスク対応とSoAの考え方に反します。載っていない管理策は採用できないとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A staff member implemented easy-to-use controls selected from Annex A without performing an AI risk assessment and reported, 'Risk treatment is complete.' What is the most appropriate point under Clause 6.1.3?","oEn":["Determine the necessary controls based on risk assessment results and compare with Annex A to confirm no necessary control is omitted","Choosing easy controls is acceptable if the plan lists timing and owners, and linking to risk assessment results can be omitted","Controls not listed in Annex A must not be adopted as risk treatment, so do not consider original controls","Risk treatment is complete once all Annex A controls are adopted, with no need to decide non-applicable controls or record reasons"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.3 determines necessary controls from the risk assessment results and compares them with Annex A to check nothing necessary is omitted. Omitting the link to results, or declaring completion by adopting all of Annex A without recording reasons for exclusion, contradicts risk treatment and SoA thinking. Claiming controls absent from Annex A cannot be adopted is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社のリスク対応計画では、残余リスクの一部が受容基準を上回ったまま、担当課長の判断だけで運用開始が決まりました。Clause 6.1.3の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["残余リスクの受容は担当課長が行ってよく、受容基準を上回る場合は追加の対策を講じる前にリスク所有者へ事後報告する","リスク対応計画と残余リスクの受容について、リスク所有者の承認を得る手順にする","受容基準を上回る残余リスクは、運用開始後の最初のマネジメントレビューで経営層に報告して受容の可否を判断すればよい","残余リスクの受容は内部監査員が承認する事項であり、リスク所有者の承認は求められない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.1.3では、リスク対応計画と残余リスクの受容について、リスク所有者の承認を得る手順にします。担当課長が受容して事後報告にとどめる扱い、運用開始後のマネジメントレビューまで受容の判断を待つ扱いは、運用開始前の承認という順序を欠きます。内部監査員が承認する扱いも責任者を取り違えています。","qEn":"At a company, the risk treatment plan left some residual risk above the acceptance criteria, yet the section manager alone decided to start operation. Under Clause 6.1.3, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["The section chief may accept residual risk, and when it exceeds the criteria a post-hoc report goes to the risk owner before further controls","Make it a procedure to obtain the risk owner's approval of the risk treatment plan and acceptance of residual risk","Residual risk exceeding criteria can be reported to management at the first management review after operation starts to decide on acceptance","Acceptance of residual risk is approved by the internal auditor, and the risk owner's approval is unnecessary"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.3 makes the risk treatment plan and acceptance of residual risk subject to approval by the risk owner. Acceptance by the section chief with only a post-hoc report, or waiting for a post-launch management review, lacks approval before operation. Having an internal auditor approve also mistakes the responsible person."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある医療AIの開発会社が、リスク対応のために必要と判断した対策が、Annex Aの管理策には見当たりませんでした。Clause 6.1.3の考え方として最も適切な扱いはどれですか。","o":["Annex Aに載っていない対策は採用できないため、最も近いAnnex Aの管理策に置き換えて、リスク対応の内容をその範囲に合わせる","Annex A以外の管理策を採用するときは、認証機関の事前承認を得なければならず、承認が得られるまで採用を保留する","必要な管理策は自社で設計したり他から採用したりでき、Annex Aは漏れの確認に用いる","Annex Aは管理策の完全なリストであり、必要な管理策がそこに見当たらないことは、規格上起こり得ない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 6.1.3では、必要な管理策は自社で設計したり他から採用したりでき、Annex Aは必要な管理策の漏れを確認するために用います。Annex Aの範囲に合わせて置き換える扱いや、認証機関の事前承認が必要とする扱いは誤りです。Annex Aを完全なリストとみなす扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"An AI medical device developer found that a measure it judged necessary for risk treatment does not appear among the Annex A controls. What is the most appropriate handling under Clause 6.1.3?","oEn":["Controls not in Annex A cannot be adopted, so replace them with the nearest Annex A control and fit the risk treatment to that range","Adopting a control outside Annex A requires prior approval of the certification body, so hold adoption until approved","Controls can be designed in-house or adopted elsewhere, and Annex A is used to check for omissions","Annex A is a complete list of controls, so a necessary control not appearing there cannot occur under the standard"],"eEn":"Under Clause 6.1.3 necessary controls can be designed by the organization or taken from other sources, and Annex A is used to check nothing necessary is omitted. Replacing with the nearest Annex A control, or requiring certification body prior approval, is wrong. Treating Annex A as a complete list is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある通信会社のAIシステム影響評価は、技術担当者が自社の都合だけで作成しており、利用状況や影響を受ける人々の観点が入っていません。Clause 6.1.4の観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["影響評価は技術担当者が実施してよいが、評価の対象は自社の事業への影響に限り、個人や社会への影響はリスクアセスメントで扱うので含めない","影響評価の結果はリスク対応に反映するが、評価は最初の導入時に一度行えば足り、用途や状況が変わっても繰り返さない","影響評価は導入時に実施するが、結果は記録として残さず、リスクアセスメントの結果にだけ反映すればよい","意図した用途と利用状況を踏まえ、個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響を評価し、その結果を文書化して残す"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 6.1.4では、意図した用途と利用状況を踏まえ、個人・集団・社会への潜在的影響を評価し、その結果を文書化して残します。評価対象を自社の事業影響に限る扱い、用途や状況が変わっても繰り返さない扱い、結果を記録に残さない扱いは、いずれも影響評価の要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A telecom company's AI system impact assessment was written by an engineer solely from the company's perspective, without usage context or the viewpoint of affected people. Under Clause 6.1.4, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["A technical staff member may do the impact assessment, but it covers only business impact and leaves effects on individuals and society to the risk assessment","Reflect impact assessment results in risk treatment but perform it once at first deployment and do not repeat it when use or circumstances change","Perform impact assessment at deployment but keep no record and only reflect it in the risk assessment results","Assess potential impacts on individuals, groups and society from the intended use and context, and keep the results documented"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.4 assesses potential impacts on individuals, groups and society based on intended use and usage context, and documents the results. Limiting scope to business impact, not repeating on changes, or keeping no record all fail the impact assessment requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"あるスタートアップは、AI目的として「優れたAI企業になる」と定めました。Clause 6.2「AI目的及びそれを達成するための計画策定」の観点で最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["AI方針と整合し、実行可能な範囲で測定可能にし、監視・伝達・更新できる目的へ具体化する","目的は理念的な表現のほうが従業員の創造性を高めるため、達成度は測定せず、定性的な表現にとどめる","目的は一度設定すれば監視は求められず、達成状況の確認は内部監査の時点にまとめて行えばよい","目的の達成計画は、何を行うか、必要な資源、責任者、期限、評価方法のうち、何を行うかだけを定めておけばよい"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 6.2では、AI目的をAI方針と整合させ、実行可能な範囲で測定可能にし、監視・伝達・更新できるものとし、達成計画では実施事項、資源、責任者、期限、評価方法を決めます。監視を内部監査まで先送りする扱い、実施事項だけを定める扱い、測定せず定性的にとどめる扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A startup set its AI objective as 'become an excellent AI company.' Under Clause 6.2 'AI objectives and planning to achieve them', what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Make it consistent with the AI policy, measurable where practicable, and monitored, communicated and updated","Ideal wording raises employees' creativity more, so do not measure achievement and keep it qualitative","Once objectives are set no monitoring is needed, and achievement can be checked together at internal audit","Of what will be done, the resources needed, who is responsible, the deadline and how results are evaluated, the plan need only define what will be done"],"eEn":"Clause 6.2 requires AI objectives consistent with the AI policy, measurable where practicable, monitored, communicated and updated, with plans defining actions, resources, responsibility, timing and evaluation. Postponing monitoring to internal audit, defining only actions, or staying qualitative without measurement fails the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、AIシステムを旧基盤から新しいクラウド基盤へ移行します。移行は事業に影響し、AIMSの運用にも関わります。Clause 6.3「変更の計画策定」の観点で、最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["移行は技術的な作業なので、AIMSの変更には当たらず、現場の判断で随時進めてよい","変更の目的と結果、AIMSの完全性、資源、責任と権限を考慮して計画的に実施する","変更の計画は移行の実施前に作成するが、AIMSへの影響の確認は移行後の内部監査で行えば足りる","変更の責任と権限は移行を実施するインフラ部門の部門長に一任し、AIMS責任者は結果を事後に受け取るだけでよい"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 6.3では、AIMSの変更が必要なとき、変更の目的と結果、AIMSの完全性、資源の利用可能性、責任と権限の割当てを考慮して、計画的に実施します。影響確認を事後の内部監査に回す扱いや、責任をインフラ部門に一任する扱いは、計画段階での考慮を欠きます。技術作業だから現場判断でよいとする扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company will migrate an AI system from an old platform to a new cloud platform. The migration affects the business and the AIMS's operation. Under Clause 6.3 'planning of changes', what is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["Migration is technical work and not a change to the AIMS, so the field may proceed as it judges from time to time","Carry it out in a planned manner, considering purpose, consequences, AIMS integrity, resources and responsibilities","Prepare the change plan before the migration but check impact on the AIMS later at internal audit","Entrust responsibility and authority for the change to the infrastructure department head, with the AIMS manager only receiving results afterwards"],"eEn":"Clause 6.3 requires AIMS changes to be carried out in a planned manner, considering purpose and consequences, AIMS integrity, resource availability and allocation of responsibilities and authorities. Deferring impact checks to later internal audit, or leaving responsibility to the infrastructure head, lacks planning-stage consideration. Treating it as ad hoc technical work is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"AIMSの責任者が、Clause 7.1「資源」に基づき予算を要求したところ、経営層は「AIMSは既存の担当者の兼務で運用できる」と答えました。規格の考え方として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["資源が兼務で賄えるかどうかは内部監査で判断するため、予算の要求は監査で資源不足が指摘された後に行う","資源の提供は認証取得の審査の段階でのみ必要になるため、取得後の維持に必要な資源は求められない","AIMSの確立・実施・維持および継続的改善に必要な資源を、組織自らが決定して提供しなければならない","資源の決定は、外部のコンサルタントが行う事項であり、組織が自ら必要な資源を決定する必要はない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.1では、AIMSの確立・実施・維持・継続的改善に必要な資源を、組織が決定して提供します。資源の要否を内部監査の指摘まで待つ扱いは、必要な資源を事前に決定するという要求に反します。審査段階でのみ必要とする説明や、外部コンサルタントが決めるとする説明も誤りです。","qEn":"The AIMS owner requested a budget under Clause 7.1 'resources,' but management replied, 'Existing staff can run the AIMS as a side duty.' What is the most appropriate point about the standard's thinking?","oEn":["Whether resources can be covered by concurrent duties is judged by internal audit, so request budget only after audit points out shortages","Providing resources is needed only at the certification audit stage, and resources for maintenance after obtaining it are not required","The organization must determine and provide the resources needed to establish, implement, maintain and continually improve the AIMS","Determining resources is a matter for an outside consultant, and the organization need not determine the needed resources itself"],"eEn":"Clause 7.1 requires the organization to determine and provide resources needed for establishing, implementing, maintaining and continually improving the AIMS. Waiting for an audit to point out shortages conflicts with determining needs in advance. Claiming resources are needed only at audit, or decided by external consultants, is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社で、AIモデルのリスク評価を担当する社員が、AIの基礎知識や評価手法の教育を受けておらず、評価の質にばらつきが出ています。Clause 7.2「力量」の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["必要な力量の決定は行うが、力量の確保は有資格者の新規採用に限られ、教育・訓練や経験による確保は認められない","力量の証拠は口頭で確認できれば十分であるため、受講の記録や資格などは、文書化情報として保持しない","教育・訓練は全社員に一律に実施し、評価担当者に必要な力量は決定せず、受講の有無だけを記録する","必要な力量を明確に決定し、教育・訓練や実務経験で確保する処置をとり、その証拠を文書化情報として保持しておく"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 7.2では、必要な力量を決定し、教育・訓練や経験により力量を確保する処置をとり、その有効性を評価し、証拠を文書化情報として保持します。採用に限る扱い、必要な力量を決めず受講の有無だけを記録する扱い、口頭確認で足りるとする扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company, the employee in charge of AI model risk assessment has had no training in AI fundamentals or assessment methods, and assessment quality varies. Under Clause 7.2 'competence', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Determine required competence but secure it only by hiring qualified people, with training or experience not permitted","Oral confirmation suffices as evidence of competence, so do not retain attendance records or qualifications as documented information","Train all employees uniformly, do not determine competence needed by risk assessors, and record only attendance","Determine the necessary competence, secure it through education, training or experience, and retain evidence as documented information"],"eEn":"Clause 7.2 requires determining necessary competence, taking actions such as training or experience to secure it, evaluating effectiveness and retaining evidence as documented information. Limiting to hiring, recording only attendance without determining needed competence, or verbal confirmation fails the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の営業部員は、自社のAI方針の存在も、自分の行動が方針の達成にどう関わるかも知りません。Clause 7.3「認識」の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["AI方針、自らのAIMSへの貢献、要求事項に適合しない場合の意味を、働く人々が認識するようにする","認識は教育・訓練を受けたAIの専門部署の担当者だけが持てばよく、営業部員のような非専門職は対象から外れる","AI方針の存在さえ知らせれば認識は満たされるので、自らの貢献や不適合の意味まで周知する必要はない","認識は方針の改訂時にのみ周知すればよく、個人の貢献や要求事項に適合しない場合の意味は懲戒規程で別途扱う"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.3では、働く人々がAI方針、自らのAIMSの有効性への貢献、要求事項に適合しない場合の意味を認識するようにします。専門部署に限る扱い、方針の存在だけを知らせる扱い、改訂時にのみ周知して不適合の意味は懲戒規程に任せる扱いは、認識の要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's sales staff know neither of the company's AI policy nor how their actions relate to achieving it. Under Clause 7.3 'awareness', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Make people aware of the AI policy, their contribution to AIMS effectiveness, and the implications of nonconformity","Awareness need only be held by staff of the AI specialist department who received training, and non-specialist roles such as sales are excluded","Awareness is satisfied by merely informing them the AI policy exists, without communicating their contribution or implications of nonconformity","Awareness is communicated only when the policy is revised, and the meaning of nonconformity and personal contribution is handled separately in disciplinary rules"],"eEn":"Clause 7.3 requires people working under the organization's control to be aware of the AI policy, their contribution to AIMS effectiveness and the implications of nonconformity. Limiting to specialist departments, announcing only the policy's existence, or communicating only at revisions and leaving implications to disciplinary rules does not meet the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社で、顧客に影響するAIの不具合が起きましたが、誰が・いつ・誰に・どの手段で伝えるかが決まっておらず、顧客への連絡が遅れました。Clause 7.4「コミュニケーション」の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["コミュニケーションの計画は事故対応手順書の連絡先リストで足り、通常時の内部・外部コミュニケーションの内容や時期までは決定までは求められない","AIMSに関連する内部・外部のコミュニケーションについて、何を、いつ、誰に、どのように伝えるかを決定する","外部へのコミュニケーションは規制当局への報告だけに限られるので、顧客への連絡は決定の対象に含まれない","コミュニケーションは何を伝えるか、誰に伝えるかを決めればよく、時期と方法は担当者がその都度選んでよい"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 7.4では、AIMSに関連する内部・外部のコミュニケーションについて、何を、いつ、誰に、どのように伝えるかを決定します。連絡先リストだけで済ませる扱い、時期と方法を決めない扱い、外部の相手を規制当局に限る扱いは、4つの観点の決定を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company, an AI malfunction affecting customers occurred, but who communicates what, when, to whom and by what means had not been set, so contacting customers was delayed. Under Clause 7.4 'communication', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["The communication plan is covered by the incident response contact list, and the content and timing of routine internal and external communication need not be determined","Determine for internal and external communications relevant to the AIMS what to communicate, when, with whom and how","External communication is limited to reporting to regulators, so contacting customers is not included in what is determined","Determine only what and to whom, and let staff choose timing and method case by case"],"eEn":"Clause 7.4 requires determining internal and external communications relevant to the AIMS: what, when, with whom and how. Relying only on a contact list, not setting timing and method, or limiting external parties to regulators lacks determination on all four aspects."},
{"d":"D2","q":"従業員30名の会社が、AIMSの文書を最小限にしようとして、規格が要求する文書化情報も含めて「小規模だから文書は不要」と判断しました。Clause 7.5.1の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["規格が要求する文書化情報のうち、方針と適用範囲は小規模でも必要だが、そのほかの要求された記録は口頭で代替できる","文書化情報の範囲は、規模や活動の種類にかかわらず、大規模な組織と全く同一でなければならない","規格が要求する文書化情報に加え、有効性のために組織が必要と決めたものを含み、範囲は規模等で異なる","文書化情報は、規格が要求するものだけを作成すればよく、組織が有効性のために必要と判断した文書を加えることはできない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.5.1では、規格が要求する文書化情報に加え、AIMSの有効性のために組織が必要と決めた文書化情報を含め、その範囲は組織の規模や活動の種類などで異なります。小規模でも免除されず、一部を口頭で代替する扱い、範囲を全組織で同一にする扱い、組織の判断で加えられないとする扱いは誤りです。","qEn":"A 30-employee company tried to minimize AIMS documents and judged 'we are small, so documents are unnecessary,' including those the standard requires. What is the most appropriate point under Clause 7.5.1?","oEn":["Of the documented information required, policy and scope are needed even for small firms but other required records can be replaced by oral means","The extent of documented information must be exactly the same as for a large organization regardless of size or type of activities","Include documented information required by the standard plus what the organization deems necessary; the extent varies with size","Documented information need only be what the standard requires, and documents the organization judges necessary for effectiveness cannot be added"],"eEn":"Clause 7.5.1 covers documented information required by the standard plus what the organization determines necessary for AIMS effectiveness, with extent varying by size and activities. Small firms are not exempt, and substituting oral means, uniform extent across organizations, or forbidding additions is wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社では、AI運用手順書の改訂版が共有フォルダに複数存在し、作成者名も更新日も記載がないため、現場がどれを使うべきか分かりません。Clause 7.5.2「作成及び更新」の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["識別は文書の保管場所で代替できるため、共有フォルダの階層を整理すれば、表題や日付や作成者を文書自体に記述する必要まではない","文書の承認は、文書の内容が最新であるかを確認する必要がなくなるので、作成者が口頭で伝えれば足りる","文書の形式は電子媒体でもよいが、更新時の妥当性の確認と承認は重要な文書に限って行えばよい","文書化情報の作成・更新時に、識別と記述（表題、日付、作成者など）、適切な形式の選択、妥当性の確認と承認を必ず行うこと"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 7.5.2では、文書化情報の作成・更新時に、識別と記述（表題、日付、作成者など）、適切な形式、妥当性と適切性の確認と承認を行います。保管場所で識別を代替する扱い、承認を重要な文書に限る扱い、口頭の周知で足りる扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company, multiple revised versions of the AI operating procedure exist in a shared folder with no author name or update date, so the field cannot tell which to use. Under Clause 7.5.2 'creating and updating', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Identification can be replaced by storage location, so organizing folders means title, date and author need not be stated in the document","Approval removes the need to confirm that content is current, so the author telling people orally suffices","The format may be electronic, but review and approval at update are needed only for important documents","On creating and updating, ensure identification and description (title, date, author), suitable format, and review and approval for suitability"],"eEn":"Clause 7.5.2 requires identification and description (title, date, author), suitable format, and review and approval for suitability and adequacy when creating and updating documented information. Substituting storage location for identification, limiting approval to important documents, or oral notification does not meet the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社では、機微な内容を含むAIリスク評価の記録に、関係のない社員も自由にアクセスして書き換えられる状態になっていました。Clause 7.5.3「文書化情報の管理」の観点で最も適切な対策はどれですか。","o":["アクセスは必要な人だけに限定するが、変更の管理は作成者の自己管理に任せて、変更履歴や版の管理までは求められない","必要な人々が必要なときに利用できるようにしつつ、機密の喪失や不適切な使用から保護し、アクセスと変更の管理を行う","記録の保護は、情報システム部が定期的にバックアップを取ることだけで足り、アクセス権や変更の管理は求められない","機微な記録は暗号化して保管するが、閲覧できる人は情報システム部の管理者に限り、必要な担当者にも提供しない"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 7.5.3では、文書化情報を必要な人々が必要なときに利用できるようにしつつ、機密の喪失や不適切な使用から保護し、配付・アクセス・変更の管理を行います。変更履歴や版の管理を省く扱い、必要な担当者にも提供しない扱い、バックアップだけに頼る扱いは、利用可能性と保護の両立を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company, AI risk assessment records containing sensitive content could be freely accessed and rewritten by unrelated employees. Under Clause 7.5.3 'control of documented information', what is the most appropriate measure?","oEn":["Limit access to those who need it but leave change control to authors' own care, with no change history or version control required","Keep it available to those who need it, protect it from loss of confidentiality and misuse, and control access and changes","Protection of records is satisfied only by IT making periodic backups, and access rights and change control are unnecessary","Store sensitive records encrypted but limit viewing to IT administrators and do not provide them even to staff who need them"],"eEn":"Clause 7.5.3 requires documented information to be available to those who need it when needed while protected from loss of confidentiality and misuse, with control of distribution, access and change. Skipping change history and version control, withholding from staff who need it, or relying only on backups fails to balance availability and protection."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、AI運用の外部委託先が提供する「モデルの仕様書」を、自社のAIMSの運用に必要な外部由来の文書として扱うべきか迷っています。Clause 7.5.3の考え方として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["外部由来の文書化情報は、自社が作成したものではないので、AIMSの文書化情報の管理の対象とはならない","外部由来の文書は、委託先から受領した時点の版を保管すれば足り、その後の更新版の識別や配付の管理は委託先に任せる","AIMSの計画と運用に必要と判断した外部由来の文書化情報は、適切に識別し、管理する","外部由来の文書化情報は、規格が要求する範囲に限られ、組織が運用に必要と判断したものは含めない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 7.5.3では、AIMSの計画と運用に必要と判断した外部由来の文書化情報を、適切に識別し、管理します。自社が作成していないことを理由に対象から外す扱いや、受領時点の版だけを保管して更新の管理を委託先に任せる扱い、規格要求の範囲に限る扱いは、要求に合いません。","qEn":"A company is unsure whether a 'model specification' provided by an external AI operations contractor should be treated as an external document needed for its AIMS operation. What is the most appropriate view under Clause 7.5.3?","oEn":["Externally originated documented information was not created by the company, so it is not subject to AIMS control of documented information","Keep the version of external documents as received and leave identification and distribution of later versions to the contractor","Documented information of external origin judged necessary for AIMS planning and operation is appropriately identified and controlled","Externally originated documented information is limited to what the standard requires, and does not include what the organization judges necessary"],"eEn":"Clause 7.5.3 requires externally originated documented information judged necessary for AIMS planning and operation to be appropriately identified and controlled. Excluding it because the organization did not create it, keeping only the received version and leaving updates to the contractor, or limiting to what the standard requires does not fit."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、運用中のAIシステムの設計変更を現場の判断で随時行い、その結果が意図せず運用に悪影響を与えましたが、レビューや対策は行われませんでした。Clause 8.1「運用の計画及び管理」の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["運用中の設計変更は現場の裁量で行ってよいが、変更の内容は四半期ごとの定例会議で事後報告すれば足りる","意図しない変更の結果は、次回の内部監査で監査員が確認するまでレビューせず、緩和の処置も監査後に計画する","変更の管理は、計画した変更に限られるため、意図しない変更についてのレビューや処置は求められない","計画した変更を管理して、意図しない変更の結果をレビューして、有害な影響を緩和する処置を必要に応じてとる"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 8.1では、計画した変更を管理し、意図しない変更の結果をレビューして、必要に応じて有害な影響を緩和する処置をとります。事後報告だけにする扱いや、意図しない変更のレビューを内部監査まで待つ扱いは、運用の管理として不十分です。意図しない変更が対象外という説明も誤りです。","qEn":"At a company, design changes to AI systems in operation were made ad hoc at the field's discretion; the results unintentionally harmed operations, but no review or countermeasures followed. Under Clause 8.1 'operational planning and control', what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Operational design changes may be made at the site's discretion with a report after the fact at a quarterly meeting","Review the results of unintended changes only when the next internal audit checks them, planning mitigation after the audit","Change control covers only planned changes, so review and action for unintended changes are not required","Control planned changes, review the effects of unintended ones, and act to mitigate adverse effects"],"eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires controlling planned changes and reviewing the consequences of unintended changes, taking action to mitigate adverse effects as necessary. After-the-fact reporting, or waiting for internal audit to review unintended changes, is inadequate operational control. Claiming unintended changes are out of scope is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、Clause 8.1に基づき、AIの運用プロセスが計画どおりに実施されたと確信するために、どの程度の記録を残すかを検討しています。最も適切な考え方はどれですか。","o":["記録は規格の全条項について同じ分量を作成することを基準に決め、運用プロセスの重要性や確信に必要な程度は考慮しない","運用の記録は、問題が発生した場合に限って作成するもので、通常の運用時には保持しない","運用の確信は上長の口頭確認で得られるため、記録は監査で問われた場合にだけ作成する","プロセスが計画どおりに実施されたという確信を持つために必要な範囲で、文書化情報を保持する"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 8.1では、プロセスが計画どおりに実施されたという確信を持つために必要な範囲で、文書化情報を保持します。全条項に同じ分量を課す扱い、口頭確認に頼り監査時にだけ記録を作る扱い、問題発生時にだけ作成する扱いは、確信に必要な範囲という基準に合いません。無制限の保存も誤りです。","qEn":"A company is considering how many records to keep, under Clause 8.1, to be confident that its AI operational processes were carried out as planned. What is the most appropriate thinking?","oEn":["Decide records by producing the same volume for every clause, without considering process importance or the degree needed for confidence","Operating records are created only when problems occur, and are not kept during ordinary operation","Confidence comes from a supervisor's verbal confirmation, and records are created only when asked at audit","Retain documented information to the extent necessary to have confidence that processes were carried out as planned"],"eEn":"Clause 8.1 requires retaining documented information to the extent necessary to have confidence that processes were carried out as planned. Uniform volume for every clause, relying on verbal confirmation and creating records only at audit, or creating records only after problems does not fit the extent-needed standard. Unlimited retention is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある保険会社は、導入時に実施したAIリスクアセスメントの後、基盤モデルをまったく別のモデルへ差し替えましたが、リスクアセスメントを再実施せず、旧結果をそのまま使っています。Clauseの運用要求の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["AIリスクアセスメントは年に1回の定期実施で足り、基盤モデルの差し替えのような重大な変更が生じた時点での臨時の再実施までは求められない","AIリスクアセスメントは、事前に計画した間隔で、あるいは重大な変更が提案・発生した場合に実施し、その結果を文書化情報として保持しておく","基盤モデルの差し替えは技術的な変更にすぎないので、リスクの再評価ではなくAIシステム影響評価の再実施だけで足りる","再実施の間隔は組織が計画できるが、結果の保持は求められず、再実施のたびに担当者が口頭で経営層に報告すれば足りる"],"a":1,"e":"AIリスクアセスメントは、計画した間隔で、または重大な変更が提案・発生した場合に実施し、結果を文書化情報として保持します。年1回に限る扱い、結果の保持を求めない扱いは不十分で、基盤モデルの差し替えはリスクの再評価が必要です。影響評価の再実施だけで足りるとする扱いはリスクアセスメントと影響評価の取り違えです。","qEn":"An insurance company, after the AI risk assessment done at introduction, swapped the foundation model for a completely different one but did not redo the risk assessment and uses the old result. In terms of the operational requirement, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["An annual AI risk assessment suffices, and an ad hoc reassessment at a significant change such as swapping the foundation model is not required","Perform AI risk assessment at planned intervals or when significant changes are proposed or occur, and retain the results as documented information","Swapping the foundation model is merely a technical change, so redoing only the AI system impact assessment suffices instead of reassessing risk","The organization may plan the interval, but retaining results is not required and an oral report to management each time suffices"],"eEn":"The AI risk assessment is performed at planned intervals or when significant changes are proposed or occur, and the results are retained as documented information. An annual-only schedule or no retention is inadequate, and swapping the foundation model requires risk reassessment. Substituting only an impact assessment confuses risk assessment with impact assessment."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、AIリスク対応計画を策定して承認まで終えましたが、計画の内容は実装されず、管理策の実施状況の記録もありません。Clause 8のAIリスク対応の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["策定したAIリスク対応計画を実施し、その結果を文書化情報として保持する必要がある","リスク対応は管理策の実装をもって完了とみなされ、実施の結果を文書化情報として保持するのは、監査で求められた場合に限る","リスク対応の実施結果の記録は、監査の直前にまとめて作成すればよく、実施の時点で保持する必要はない","リスク対応計画の実施は年度の予算が確定した後に着手し、予算確定前の実施状況の記録は保持までは求められない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 8では、策定したAIリスク対応計画を実施し、その結果を文書化情報として保持します。計画の承認だけで完了とみなす扱い、実施結果の記録を監査時や予算確定後に限る扱い、リスク顕在化後に限る扱いは、計画の実施と記録の保持という要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company completed and approved an AI risk treatment plan, but the plan's content was not implemented and there are no records of control implementation. Under Clause 8 AI risk treatment, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["The established AI risk treatment plan must be implemented and the results retained as documented information","Risk treatment is complete with control implementation, and keeping results as documented information is needed only when asked at audit","Records of risk treatment results can be compiled just before an audit and need not be retained at the time of implementation","Implementation of the plan starts after the annual budget is fixed, and records before that need not be kept"],"eEn":"Clause 8 requires implementing the AI risk treatment plan and retaining the results as documented information. Treating approval alone as completion, keeping records only at audit or after budget approval, or implementing only after risks materialize fails to meet plan implementation and record retention."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムの用途を一般消費者向けへ拡大するにあたり、導入時のAIシステム影響評価をそのまま使い続けようとしています。Clause 8の影響評価の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["AIシステム影響評価は導入時と認証更新時に実施すれば足り、用途の拡大のような途中の変更に応じた再実施は求められない","用途の拡大は営業上の判断なので、影響評価の再実施の要否を決める権限は、営業部門だけにある","AIシステム影響評価は、計画した間隔で、または重大な変更が提案・発生した場合に実施し、その結果を文書化して保持する","用途の拡大後に一定期間運用して実績データが集まってから、影響評価の再実施の要否を検討すれば足りる"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステム影響評価は、計画した間隔で、または重大な変更が提案・発生した場合に実施し、結果を保持します。更新時だけにする扱いや、運用実績が集まってから検討する扱いは、用途が拡大する時点での評価という順序を欠きます。営業部門だけが再実施の要否を決める扱いも責任を取り違えています。","qEn":"A company is expanding an AI system's use to general consumers and plans to keep using the impact assessment done at introduction. Under the Clause 8 impact assessment requirement, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Impact assessment at deployment and certification renewal suffices, and reassessment for mid-term changes such as expanded use is not required","Expanding use is a sales decision, so only the sales department has authority to decide whether to redo the impact assessment","Perform AI system impact assessment at planned intervals or when significant changes are proposed or occur, and retain the results","Consider whether to redo the impact assessment only after operating for a period and collecting performance data following the expanded use"],"eEn":"The AI system impact assessment is performed at planned intervals or when significant changes are proposed or occur, and results are retained. Limiting to renewal, or waiting for operational data, lacks assessment at the time of the expansion. Letting only sales decide whether to redo it also misplaces responsibility."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社は、AIMSの有効性の指標として「作成した規程の件数」だけを監視しています。Clause 9.1「監視、測定、分析及び評価」の観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["監視・測定の対象と方法、実施時期、結果の分析・評価の時期を決め、AIMSの有効性を示す指標も使う","規程の件数に加えて導入したAIシステムの数を指標に追加すれば、AIMSの有効性を十分に示せる","監視・測定の対象と方法は決めるが、実施時期と分析・評価の時期は結果が出そろった時点で担当者が決める","AIMSの有効性は、内部監査だけで確認され、9.1の監視や測定による評価は、規格上は求められない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 9.1では、監視・測定の対象と方法、実施時期、結果の分析・評価の時期を決め、AIMSの有効性を示す指標も使います。件数に導入数を足しただけでは有効性を示す指標になりません。時期を担当者が後から決める扱いは要求を満たさず、有効性の確認を内部監査だけに委ねる扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company monitors only 'the number of regulations created' as its AIMS effectiveness indicator. Under Clause 9.1 'monitoring, measurement, analysis and evaluation', what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Determine what to monitor and measure, methods, timing and when to analyze and evaluate, and use indicators of effectiveness","Adding the number of AI systems deployed to the policy count is enough to show the effectiveness of the AIMS","Decide what and how to monitor and measure, but let staff decide the timing of monitoring and of analysis and evaluation once results are in","AIMS effectiveness is confirmed by internal audit alone, and evaluation by Clause 9.1 monitoring and measurement is not required by the standard"],"eEn":"Clause 9.1 requires determining what and how to monitor and measure, when to do so, and when to analyze and evaluate, and also using indicators that show AIMS effectiveness. Adding deployment counts does not show effectiveness, deciding timing afterwards does not meet the requirement, and leaving effectiveness to internal audit alone is wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の内部監査は毎回、同じ部門・同じチェックリストで形式的に実施されており、前回の監査で見つかった弱点も監査計画に反映されていません。Clause 9.2の観点で最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["プロセスの重要性と前回までの監査結果を考慮し、頻度、方法、責任、計画を定めた監査プログラムを計画する","内部監査は毎回同一の範囲と方法で実施するほうが、結果の比較に有利であるため、過去の監査結果は計画に反映しない","監査プログラムの頻度と方法は組織が定めるが、前回までの監査結果は考慮せず、プロセスの重要性だけで決める","重要性の高いプロセスだけを監査の対象にし、その他のプロセスは、AIMSの内部監査の対象から外すこと"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 9.2では、プロセスの重要性と前回までの監査結果を考慮して、頻度、方法、責任、計画を定めた監査プログラムを計画します。毎回同じ範囲にして過去の結果を反映しない扱い、重要性だけで決める扱い、重要なプロセスのみを対象とする扱いは、要求を満たしません。認証機関が策定するという説明も誤りです。","qEn":"A company's internal audits are performed formally each time with the same departments and checklist, and weaknesses found in the previous audit are not reflected in the audit plan. Under Clause 9.2, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Plan an audit programme with frequency, methods and responsibilities, considering process importance and prior audits","Auditing the same scope and methods each time helps comparison of results, so do not reflect past audit results in planning","The organization sets audit frequency and method but decides only by process importance, not considering earlier audit results","Audit only high-importance processes and exclude all other processes from the AIMS internal audit"],"eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires planning an audit programme defining frequency, methods, responsibilities and planning, considering the importance of processes and results of previous audits. Repeating the same scope without prior results, deciding only by importance, or auditing only important processes does not meet it. Claiming the certification body drafts it is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の内部監査では、監査の範囲も基準も監査ごとに定められず、結果は監査員から担当者へ口頭で伝えられただけで、関連する管理層には報告されていません。Clause 9.2の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["各監査の基準と範囲は年間の監査プログラムに一括して定めれば足り、個々の監査ごとに定める必要はない","監査結果は被監査部門の管理者に伝えた段階で報告が完了し、関連する管理層への報告は次回のマネジメントレビューの議題にまとめればよい","各監査の基準と範囲を定め、客観的で公平な監査を実施し、結果を関連する管理層に報告し、その証拠を保持する","監査の実施の証拠と結果は、不適合が見つかった場合に限って文書化情報として保持すればよい"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 9.2では、各監査の基準と範囲を定め、客観的で公平な監査を実施し、結果を関連する管理層に報告し、監査プログラムの実施と結果の証拠を文書化情報として保持します。年間計画への一括記載、被監査部門への伝達で済ませる報告、不適合時のみの記録保持は、いずれも要求を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company's internal audits, neither scope nor criteria are set per audit, results are conveyed orally from auditor to staff, and relevant management is not informed. Under Clause 9.2, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Audit criteria and scope can be set collectively in the annual audit programme and need not be set for each audit","Reporting is complete once results are told to the audited department's manager, and reporting to relevant management can be bundled into the next management review","Define criteria and scope per audit, audit objectively and impartially, report to relevant management, and retain evidence","Evidence of audits and results need be retained as documented information only when nonconformities are found"],"eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires defining criteria and scope for each audit, conducting objective and impartial audits, reporting results to relevant management, and retaining evidence of the programme and results. Setting criteria collectively in an annual programme, reporting only to the audited department, or keeping records only on nonconformity does not meet it."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社のマネジメントレビューは、各部門が活動報告を順に読み上げるだけの会議で、AIMSの変更や改善の決定は何も出ていません。Clause 9.3の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["レビューの結果は議題ごとの発言要旨を議事録に残せば足り、改善の機会やAIMS変更の必要性についての決定の記録までは求められない","マネジメントレビューは、AIMSの有効性の確認だけを行うもので、改善の機会や変更の必要性についての決定は、扱わない","マネジメントレビューは内部監査員が主催し、トップマネジメントは結果の報告を受けるだけでよい","適切性・妥当性・有効性を評価し、改善の機会やAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定を得て、結果を文書化して保持する"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 9.3では、トップマネジメントが計画した間隔でAIMSをレビューし、適切性・妥当性・有効性を評価し、改善の機会やAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定を得て、結果を文書化して保持します。決定を記録しない議事録、内部監査員の主催、有効性の確認だけに限る扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's management review is a meeting where each department reads out activity reports in turn, and no decisions on AIMS changes or improvement result. Under Clause 9.3, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Minutes of remarks per agenda item suffice, and recording decisions on improvement opportunities or the need for AIMS changes is not required","Management review only confirms AIMS effectiveness, and does not deal with decisions on improvement opportunities or need for changes","Management review is chaired by the internal auditor and top management only receives the results","Evaluate suitability, adequacy and effectiveness, decide on improvements and AIMS changes, and retain the results documented"],"eEn":"Under Clause 9.3 top management reviews the AIMS at planned intervals, evaluates suitability, adequacy and effectiveness, reaches decisions on improvement opportunities and the need for AIMS changes, and retains the results. Minutes without decisions, auditor-chaired review, or limiting to confirming effectiveness does not meet it."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社が、AIに関する新しい法規制の施行と、重大なAIインシデントを受けて、マネジメントレビューを開催します。Clause 9.3のインプットとして考慮に含めるべき事項として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["内部監査の結果と不適合の状況だけをインプットとし、外部の課題の変化や利害関係者のフィードバックは4.1・4.2の見直しで扱うため、レビューでは扱わない","内外の課題の変化、利害関係者のフィードバック、不適合と是正処置、監視・測定の結果、監査結果の状況","前回のレビューで決めた処置の状況に加えて予算の執行状況を中心に取り上げ、監査結果は内部監査の報告書に委ねる","法規制の変化は法務部門の管理事項なので、AIMSの有効性とは別に、インシデントの件数だけをインプットにすればよい"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 9.3のインプットには、前回のレビューの処置の状況、内外の課題の変化、利害関係者のフィードバック、不適合と是正処置、監視・測定の結果、監査結果などを含めます。外部の変化を4.1・4.2に任せて除く扱い、予算の執行状況に偏る扱い、インシデント件数だけにする扱いは、インプットの要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company will hold a management review following the enforcement of new AI-related regulation and a serious AI incident. Which items should be considered as Clause 9.3 inputs?","oEn":["Use only internal audit results and nonconformities as inputs, treating changes in external issues and stakeholder feedback in the 4.1/4.2 reviews rather than in management review","Changes in issues relevant to the AIMS, feedback, nonconformities and corrective actions, measurement results, and audit results","Besides actions from the previous review, focus on budget execution and leave audit results to the internal audit report","Changes in law are a legal department matter, so use only the number of incidents as input, separate from AIMS effectiveness"],"eEn":"Clause 9.3 inputs include the status of actions from previous reviews, changes in internal and external issues, stakeholder feedback, nonconformities and corrective actions, monitoring and measurement results and audit results. Excluding external change by deferring to 4.1/4.2, focusing on budget execution, or using only incident counts does not meet the input requirements."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の担当者は「AIMSの改善は、監査で不適合が指摘されたときに是正する活動のことで、それ以外では改善は不要だ」と考えています。Clause 10.1「継続的改善」の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に改善する必要があり、是正処置に限らず監視・監査の結果も活用する","継続的改善は是正処置と同義であり、不適合が指摘されていない期間は、改善のための活動を行わなくても、要求に適合する","継続的改善の対象はAIMSの有効性だけで、適切性と妥当性は認証機関の審査が評価する事項であり、組織が改善を図る対象ではない","継続的改善はマネジメントレビューで経営層が決定した事項に限って行えばよく、監視や監査の結果から独自に改善を検討する必要はない"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 10.1では、AIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を継続的に改善します。改善は是正処置に限らず、監視・測定や監査の結果も活用します。有効性だけを対象とする扱い、経営層の決定事項に限る扱い、是正処置と同義とする扱いは範囲を狭めており、期間を区切る扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A staff member thinks, 'Improvement of the AIMS means correcting when an audit points out a nonconformity, and otherwise improvement is unnecessary.' Under Clause 10.1 'continual improvement', what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Continually improve the AIMS's suitability, adequacy and effectiveness, proactively using monitoring and audit results as well as corrective action","Continual improvement is synonymous with corrective action, so periods with no nonconformities pointed out need no improvement activity to conform","Continual improvement targets only AIMS effectiveness, while suitability and adequacy are assessed by the certification body and are not for the organization to improve","Continual improvement is limited to matters decided at management review and does not require considering improvements from monitoring or audit results"],"eEn":"Clause 10.1 requires continually improving the suitability, adequacy and effectiveness of the AIMS, not only through corrective action but also using monitoring, measurement and audit results. Limiting to effectiveness, to management-review decisions, or equating it with corrective action narrows the scope, and a time-limited view is also wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"内部監査で、あるAIシステムのAIシステム影響評価が実施されていない不適合が見つかりました。Clause 10.2「不適合及び是正処置」の観点で、最初の対応として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["原因の分析を先に長期間行い、不適合そのものへの対処は、原因の特定が完了した後にまとめて実施する","当該システムの影響評価を実施して不適合に対処した後、原因の評価と他システムの確認は次回の内部監査の結果を待って行う","不適合に対処して管理・修正し、結果として生じた影響にも対処したうえで、その原因を評価して再発の防止策を検討しておく","不適合の是正は内部監査員の責任で行い、被監査部門は監査報告書の確認のみを担う"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 10.2では、不適合に対処して管理・修正し、結果として生じた影響にも対処したうえで、原因を評価して再発の防止を検討します。原因分析を先にして対処を遅らせる扱い、原因の評価を次回監査まで待つ扱い、是正を監査員の責任とする扱いは、手順や責任を取り違えています。","qEn":"An internal audit found a nonconformity: no AI system impact assessment had been performed for an AI system. Under Clause 10.2 'nonconformity and corrective action', what is the most appropriate first response?","oEn":["Analyze the cause first over a long period, and handle the nonconformity itself together after cause identification is complete","Address the nonconformity by performing the impact assessment, then evaluate causes and check other systems only after the next internal audit","Control and correct the nonconformity and deal with consequences, then evaluate the cause and consider preventing recurrence","Correction of nonconformities is the internal auditor's responsibility and the audited department only reviews the audit report"],"eEn":"Clause 10.2 requires reacting to the nonconformity, controlling and correcting it and dealing with its consequences, then evaluating the cause and considering prevention of recurrence. Delaying the reaction for cause analysis, waiting for the next audit to evaluate causes, or making the auditor responsible misplaces the procedure and responsibility."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社は、特定のAIシステムの影響評価漏れを是正した後、同じ手順を使う他のAIシステムの状況は確認していません。Clause 10.2の是正処置の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["是正処置は発見された不適合に限って実施するものであり、類似の不適合が他に存在する可能性は、確認の対象に含まれない","類似の不適合の有無は内部監査の次回の実施まで待って、監査員に確認してもらうことで足りる","是正処置は、不適合の再発を防ぐために担当者への再教育を行えば完了し、手順や仕組みの見直しは含まれない","原因を明確にし、類似の不適合が他にも存在するか、あるいは発生し得るかを判定したうえで、必要な処置をすみやかにとる"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 10.2では、原因を明確にし、類似の不適合が他にも存在するか、または発生し得るかを判定したうえで、必要な処置をとります。発見された不適合に限る扱い、次回監査まで待つ扱い、担当者の再教育だけで手順の見直しを含めない扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"After correcting an omitted impact assessment for one AI system, a company did not check the status of other AI systems using the same procedure. Under Clause 10.2 corrective action, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Corrective action is carried out only for the nonconformity found, and the possibility of similar nonconformities elsewhere is not a subject of checking","Whether similar nonconformities exist can wait until the next internal audit, where the auditor can check it","Corrective action is complete with retraining of the staff member, and does not include review of procedures or mechanisms","Determine the causes and whether similar nonconformities exist or could potentially occur elsewhere, then take the necessary action"],"eEn":"Clause 10.2 requires determining the causes and whether similar nonconformities exist or could occur, then taking needed action. Limiting to the found nonconformity, waiting for the next audit, or limiting to retraining without reviewing procedures does not meet the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の経営企画担当は「Clause 9.3の要求事項は当社の事業に合わないため、適用除外にしてAIMSの適合を主張したい」と提案しています。規格上の扱いとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["Clause 4から10の要求事項も、事業に合わないと判断すれば、理由を記載して任意に除外でき、除外しても適合を主張できる","Clause 4から10の要求事項は、適合を主張する以上は適用除外にできず、選択して外せるのはAnnex Aの管理策である","Clause 9.3に限っては、小規模な組織に対して適用除外が認められているので、規模を理由に除外して差し支えない","要求事項の除外は適用宣言書に記載すれば認められるため、除外するClauseと理由をSoAに載せる運用にする"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 4から10の要求事項は、規格への適合を主張する場合に除外できません。リスク対応の結果に応じて採用・除外を選べるのはAnnex Aの管理策で、その理由はSoAに記載します。本文の自由な除外、小規模組織の除外、本文の除外をSoAで行うとする説明は誤りです。","qEn":"A company's corporate planning staff proposes, 'Clause 9.3 requirements do not suit our business, so exclude them and still claim AIMS conformity.' What is the most appropriate treatment under the standard?","oEn":["Clause 4 to 10 requirements too can be freely excluded with a stated reason if judged unsuited to the business, and conformity can still be claimed","Requirements of Clauses 4 to 10 cannot be excluded while claiming conformity; what can be selectively excluded is Annex A controls","For Clause 9.3 alone, exemption is permitted for small organizations, so excluding it on grounds of size is acceptable","Exclusion of requirements is permitted if stated in the Statement of Applicability, so list the excluded clause and reason in the SoA"],"eEn":"Requirements in Clauses 4 to 10 cannot be excluded when claiming conformity; what is chosen to include or exclude based on risk treatment is Annex A controls, with reasons in the SoA. Free exclusion, small-organization exemption, or excluding clauses via the SoA is wrong."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社では、AIの運用を委託している外部の要員が、AIモデルの監視と異常時の一次対応を担当していますが、AIMSに関する教育や力量の確認の対象に含まれていません。Clause 7.2の観点で最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["組織の管理下でAIMSの成果に影響する業務を行う人（外部要員も含む）の必要な力量を決定し、確保する","力量の確保は組織が直接雇用する要員の責任であり、委託先の要員の力量は委託先の責任として8章の委託管理で扱う","外部要員は、委託先の契約書に力量の要件を記載してあれば、実際の力量を確認する手段は、組織に求められない","力量の確保は監視担当者に対しては実施するが、異常時の一次対応を担う要員の力量は事後の振り返りで確認する"],"a":0,"e":"Clause 7.2では、組織の管理下でAIMSの成果に影響する業務を行う人（外部要員も含む）に必要な力量を決定し、確保します。直接雇用の要員に限る扱いや、委託管理に委ねる扱い、異常時の対応要員の力量を事後確認とする扱い、契約書の記載だけに頼る扱いは、要求を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company, external staff to whom AI operations are outsourced handle AI model monitoring and first response to anomalies, but are not covered by AIMS education or competence checks. Under Clause 7.2, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Determine and ensure the necessary competence of persons doing work under the organization's control that affects AIMS performance, including external staff","Securing competence is for directly employed staff, and contractor staff competence is handled under outsourcing control in Clause 8 as the contractor's responsibility","If the contractor's contract states competence requirements, the organization needs no means to confirm actual competence","Competence is secured for monitoring staff, while that of personnel handling first response is checked in a retrospective afterwards"],"eEn":"Clause 7.2 requires determining and ensuring necessary competence of people doing work under the organization's control that affects AIMS performance, including external personnel. Limiting to employees, leaving it to outsourcing control, checking first-response competence only afterwards, or relying on contract wording alone does not meet the requirement."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある企業が、AIインシデントの再発防止のために、原因分析の結果として規程を改訂しました。その後、改訂した規程が実際に再発防止に効果を上げているかを確認していません。Clause 10.2の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["規程を改訂した時点で是正処置は完了しており、有効性は改訂時の承認で担保されるため、改訂後のレビューは求められない","とった是正処置の有効性をレビューし、必要に応じてAIMSの変更を行う","是正処置の有効性は、次回の認証更新の審査で認証機関が確認するので、組織が自らレビューする必要はない","AIMSの変更の要否は是正処置の有効性とは別に、次回の更新審査で認証機関と協議して決める"],"a":1,"e":"Clause 10.2では、とった是正処置の有効性をレビューし、必要に応じてAIMSの変更を行います。改訂時の承認で有効性が担保されるとする扱い、認証機関の審査に委ねる扱い、AIMSの変更を更新審査での協議に回す扱いは、組織自身による有効性のレビューと変更を欠きます。","qEn":"To prevent recurrence of an AI incident, a company revised a regulation as a result of cause analysis. It has not checked whether the revised regulation actually prevents recurrence. Under Clause 10.2, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Corrective action is complete upon revising the rule and effectiveness is assured by approval at revision, so review afterwards is not required","Review the effectiveness of the corrective action taken, and make changes to the AIMS if necessary","The certification body confirms corrective action effectiveness at the next recertification audit, so the organization need not review it itself","Whether the AIMS needs change is decided separately from corrective action effectiveness by consulting the certification body at the next renewal audit"],"eEn":"Clause 10.2 requires reviewing the effectiveness of corrective action taken and making changes to the AIMS if necessary. Assuming approval at revision assures effectiveness, leaving review to the certification body, or deferring AIMS change to renewal consultation lacks the organization's own effectiveness review and change."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社の役員が、AIの新サービスを予定どおり公開したいため、リスクアセスメントの結果が出てから、残余リスクの受容基準を結果に合わせて決めることを提案しました。Clause 6.1.2の観点で最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["公開日程の優先度が高い場合は、評価結果に合わせて受容基準を決めたほうが、事業の意思決定として合理的である","リスク基準は評価の前に暫定的に置いてよいが、結果を見て担当者が都度調整し、調整の根拠は記録しなくてよい","受容できるリスクとできないリスクを区別するリスク基準を、評価の前に確立し、維持しておく","リスク基準を事前に決める必要があるのは、リスク対応の段階で残余リスクの受容を判断するときであり、評価の段階では求められない"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 6.1.2では、受容できるリスクとできないリスクを区別するリスク基準を、評価の前に確立し、維持します。結果に合わせて基準を決める扱い、結果を見て都度調整する扱い、リスク基準が必要なのはリスク対応の段階だけとする扱いは、評価の一貫性と客観性を損ないます。","qEn":"A company director, wanting to release a new AI service on schedule, proposed deciding the residual risk acceptance criteria to fit the results after the risk assessment results come out. What is the most appropriate response under Clause 6.1.2?","oEn":["When the release date is a high priority, deciding the acceptance criteria to fit the results is more rational as a business decision","Risk criteria may be provisional before assessment, adjusted by staff each time after seeing results, without recording the rationale","Establish and maintain, before assessment, the risk criteria that distinguish acceptable from unacceptable risks","Risk criteria need to be set in advance for judging residual risk acceptance at the treatment stage, not at the assessment stage"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.2 requires establishing and maintaining risk criteria that distinguish acceptable from unacceptable risk before assessment. Setting criteria to fit results, adjusting them case by case, or treating criteria as needed only at the treatment stage undermines consistency and objectivity."},
{"d":"D2","q":"ある会社では、AIモデルの検証プロセスの内部監査を、そのプロセスを運用しているAI開発チームのリーダー自身が担当しています。Clause 9.2の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["最も詳しい運用者が監査したほうが、問題を見逃しにくいので、運用の責任者が自らの活動を監査する運用を維持する","客観性は監査報告書の文面で補えるため、運用者自身による監査でも、表現を中立にすれば公平性の要求を満たす","監査員は被監査部門の理解を重視して、そのプロセスの設計に関わった者から選び、客観性は監査報告書の確認で担保する","監査対象の活動から独立した監査員を選び、監査プロセスの客観性と公平性を確保する"],"a":3,"e":"Clause 9.2では、監査員を選定して監査を実施し、監査プロセスの客観性と公平性を確保します。自らの活動を監査する運用、報告書の文面で客観性を補う扱い、プロセスの設計に関わった者を選ぶ扱いは、いずれも監査対象の活動からの独立を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company, the internal audit of the AI model validation process is done by the leader of the AI development team that runs that process. Under Clause 9.2, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["The most knowledgeable operator is less likely to overlook problems, so keep the practice of the process owner auditing his own activity","Objectivity can be supplemented by the wording of the audit report, so an audit by the operator himself meets impartiality if the wording is neutral","Choose auditors from those who helped design the process for their understanding, securing objectivity by reviewing the audit report","Select auditors independent of the activity audited so as to ensure objectivity and impartiality of the audit process"],"eEn":"Clause 9.2 requires selecting auditors and conducting audits so as to ensure the objectivity and impartiality of the audit process. Auditing one's own activity, compensating with report wording, or choosing those who designed the process all lack independence from the audited activity."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の適用宣言書（SoA）は、採用した管理策の名称を一覧にしただけで、採用の理由も実施状況も除外した管理策の扱いも書かれていません。SoAの記載事項として最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["必要な管理策、その採用の理由、実施済みか否か、除外した管理策とその除外の理由を記載する","採用した管理策の名称だけで足りるので、採用の理由や実施状況は審査の場で口頭で説明できるよう用意しておく","SoAには採用した管理策と採用の理由を載せ、除外した管理策とその理由はリスク対応計画の側に記載してSoAには載せない","採用の理由と除外の理由は書くが、実施済みか否かの記載はマネジメントレビューの記録に委ね、SoAには記載しない"],"a":0,"e":"SoAには、必要な管理策、その採用の理由、実施済みか否か、除外した管理策とその除外の理由を記載します。名称だけの一覧、除外の記載を別文書に回す扱い、実施状況を別の記録に委ねる扱いは、SoAの記載事項を満たしません。実施状況はSoAの一部です。","qEn":"A company's Statement of Applicability (SoA) merely lists the names of adopted controls, with no reasons for adoption, implementation status, or treatment of excluded controls. What is the most appropriate corrective regarding SoA content?","oEn":["State the necessary controls, the reasons for including them, whether they are implemented, and the excluded controls with reasons for exclusion","Names alone suffice, so prepare to explain reasons for adoption and implementation status orally at audit","The SoA lists adopted controls and reasons, and excluded controls and their reasons are written in the risk treatment plan, not the SoA","Write reasons for adoption and exclusion but leave implementation status to management review records and do not include it in the SoA"],"eEn":"The SoA states the necessary controls, reasons for their inclusion, whether implemented, and excluded controls with reasons. A name-only list, moving exclusions to another document, or leaving implementation status to other records does not meet SoA content. Implementation status is part of the SoA."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、AIを自社開発せず、外部のAIサービスを利用するだけです。担当者は設計・開発に関する管理策をSoAで除外するつもりです。最も適切な扱いはどれですか。","o":["自社開発しない組織は設計・開発に関する管理策を除外できるが、除外の根拠はリスクアセスメントではなく組織の規模から示せばよい","自社の状況とリスク対応の結果に基づく除外理由を記載できる範囲で除外し、利用に伴う管理策は採用する","除外の理由が自社開発をしないという事実のときは、認証機関の事前承認を得なければSoAに除外として記載できない","利用に関する管理策は採用するが、第三者との関係に関する管理策は自社開発しない組織には当てはまらないため除外できる"],"a":1,"e":"除外は自社の状況とリスク対応の結果に基づく理由を記載できる範囲で行い、利用に伴う管理策は採用します。組織規模を根拠にする扱い、認証機関の事前承認を要するとする扱いは誤りです。外部AIを利用する組織こそ第三者との関係の管理策が必要で、Annex A全体を除外することも認められません。","qEn":"A company does not develop AI itself and only uses external AI services. The staff member intends to exclude design and development controls in the SoA. What is the most appropriate handling?","oEn":["An organization not developing AI may exclude design and development controls, justifying the exclusion by organization size rather than the risk assessment","Exclude them to the extent a reason based on its situation and risk treatment results can be stated, while adopting controls related to use","When the reason is not developing AI itself, exclusion cannot be listed in the SoA without prior approval of the certification body","Adopt controls for use but exclude third-party relationship controls as they do not apply to organizations that do not develop AI"],"eEn":"Exclusion is made only where reasons based on the organization's situation and risk treatment can be stated, and controls tied to use are adopted. Basing exclusion on size, or requiring certification body pre-approval, is wrong. An organization using external AI needs third-party relationship controls, and excluding all of Annex A is not allowed."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、他社のSoAの雛形をそのまま流用し、自社のAIリスクアセスメントの結果と照らさずに管理策の採否を決めました。Clause 6.1.3の観点で最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["SoAは認証取得のための様式なので、他社の雛形と自社のリスク対応計画が異なっていても、整合は審査員が判断する事項である","SoAの作成は、リスクアセスメントの前に済ませておき、リスク評価の結果は、SoAの内容に影響させない","管理策の採否はAIリスクアセスメントとリスク対応の結果に基づいて決定し、その結果をSoAにも確実に反映させる必要がある","雛形を流用する場合は、リスクアセスメントの結果ではなく、雛形が参照している規格の版が最新であることを確認すれば足りる"],"a":2,"e":"Clause 6.1.3では、管理策の採否はAIリスクアセスメントとリスク対応の結果に基づいて決め、その結果をSoAにも反映します。他社の雛形をそのまま使う扱い、整合を審査員に委ねる扱い、SoAを先に作ってリスク評価を影響させない扱い、版の確認だけで足りるとする扱いは、リスク対応との整合を欠きます。","qEn":"A company reused another company's SoA template as is and decided control adoption without checking it against its own AI risk assessment results. What is the most appropriate point under Clause 6.1.3?","oEn":["The SoA is a certification form, so any mismatch between another firm's template and one's own risk treatment plan is for the auditor to judge","Complete the SoA before the risk assessment and do not let risk evaluation results affect its content","Decide control adoption based on AI risk assessment and risk treatment results, and reflect them in the SoA","When reusing a template, it suffices to confirm that the standard version it cites is current, rather than checking the risk assessment results"],"eEn":"Clause 6.1.3 decides controls based on the AI risk assessment and risk treatment results and reflects them in the SoA. Using another firm's template as is, leaving consistency to the auditor, preparing the SoA before the risk assessment without influence, or only checking the version lacks consistency with risk treatment."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が別のAIシステムを新たに導入して適用範囲に追加しましたが、SoAは認証取得時に作成したままになっています。SoAの維持の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["SoAは認証取得時の状態を保つ文書であり、AIシステムが追加されても、次の更新審査までは内容を変更しない","新たなAIシステムの管理策はリスク対応計画に記載すればSoAの更新を要さず、SoAは適用範囲の変更があった場合だけ更新する","SoAの更新は、管理策を除外する場合にのみ必要であり、新たに管理策を採用する場合は、更新する必要はない","新たなAIシステムに関するリスクの評価・対応の結果を十分に踏まえて管理策の採否を改めて見直し、SoAを最新の内容に更新する"],"a":3,"e":"新たなAIシステムに関するリスクの評価・対応の結果を踏まえて管理策の採否を見直し、SoAを最新に更新します。次の更新審査まで変更しない扱い、リスク対応計画だけに記載してSoAを更新しない扱い、除外時にのみ更新する扱いは、SoAを最新に維持する要求に反します。","qEn":"A company newly introduced another AI system and added it to the scope, but the SoA remains as created at certification. What is the most appropriate response from the viewpoint of maintaining the SoA?","oEn":["The SoA is a document that preserves the state at certification, so do not change it until the next renewal audit even if AI systems are added","Controls for the new AI system recorded in the risk treatment plan need not be added to the SoA, which is updated only when scope changes","The SoA needs updating only when excluding controls, and not when newly adopting controls","Review control adoption in light of the risk assessment and treatment results for the new AI system, and update the SoA"],"eEn":"Review the adoption of controls based on the risk assessment and treatment for the new AI system and bring the SoA up to date. Not changing it until the next renewal, recording only in the risk treatment plan, or updating only when excluding controls contradicts keeping the SoA current."},
{"d":"D3","q":"内部監査員がSoAで「実施済み」とされた管理策の証拠を求めたところ、担当部署は「実施している」と口頭で答えるだけで、記録や成果物を示せませんでした。最も適切な評価はどれですか。","o":["担当部署が実施していると明言すれば証拠は足りるので、実施済みの記載は口頭の確認で十分に裏づけられる","SoAで実施済みとした管理策は、実施を裏づける記録や証拠で確認でき、示せなければ不適合にもなり得る","SoAの『実施済み』は管理策の採用が決定したことを示す記載であり、実施の裏づけは認証審査までに整えれば不適合には当たらない","内部監査員への証拠の提示は、被監査部門の管理者の承認が得られた場合に限り行えばよい"],"a":1,"e":"SoAで実施済みとした管理策は、実施を裏づける記録や証拠で確認でき、示せなければ不適合にもなり得ます。口頭の確認だけで足りるとする扱い、実施済みを採用決定の意味に読み替える扱い、管理者の承認がなければ証拠を示さない扱いは、監査の客観的証拠の要求に反します。","qEn":"When an internal auditor requested evidence for a control marked 'implemented' in the SoA, the responsible department merely answered orally that it was implemented and could not show records or deliverables. What is the most appropriate evaluation?","oEn":["The department's assertion that it is implemented suffices as evidence, so oral confirmation is enough to support an implemented entry","A control stated as implemented in the SoA must be verifiable by records or evidence, and failing to show them can be a nonconformity","'Implemented' in the SoA indicates a control's adoption was decided, and evidence can be prepared by the certification audit without being a nonconformity","Evidence need be shown to internal auditors only when the audited department's manager approves"],"eEn":"A control marked implemented in the SoA can be verified by records or evidence supporting implementation, and failure to show them can be a nonconformity. Verbal confirmation only, reinterpreting 'implemented' as 'adopted', or showing evidence only with manager approval contradicts the audit requirement for objective evidence."},
{"d":"D3","q":"認証審査を控えた会社で、SoAの管理策の一部がまだ実施中ですが、担当者は審査対策として実態にかかわらずすべてを「実施済み」と記載しようとしています。最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["実施中の管理策は実施状況を『一部実施』とだけ記載し、未実施部分の内容や実施の計画は審査の場で質問があったときに説明する","実施中の管理策は、審査後の最初のマネジメントレビューで実施状況を確定してからSoAに記載する","実際の実施状況をありのままに記載し、未実施の管理策には実施の計画を示す","実施中の管理策は、SoAに載せずにリスク対応計画だけに記載しておけば、審査では指摘されない"],"a":2,"e":"実際の実施状況をありのままに記載し、未実施の管理策には実施の計画を示します。『一部実施』とだけ書いて内容を質問時に説明する扱いや、審査後まで記載を待つ扱い、SoAに載せない扱いは、実態を審査前に正しく示す要求を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company about to undergo a certification audit, some SoA controls are still being implemented, but the staff member intends to mark all as 'implemented' regardless of reality as audit preparation. What is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["For controls in progress state only 'partly implemented' and explain what remains and the plan only when asked at the audit","Controls in progress are entered in the SoA after status is fixed at the first management review following the audit","State the actual implementation status as it is, and show an implementation plan for controls not yet implemented","Controls in progress should be left out of the SoA and recorded only in the risk treatment plan, so the audit will not flag them"],"eEn":"State the actual implementation status as it is and show an implementation plan for unimplemented controls. Writing only 'partly implemented' and explaining on request, delaying entry until after the audit, or omitting from the SoA fails to present the actual state correctly before the audit."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が、リスクアセスメントで必要と判断された管理策を、「予算が足りない」という理由だけでSoAから除外しようとしています。この除外の理由の扱いとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["費用は事業運営上の正当な制約であり、予算不足を除外の理由としてSoAに記載すれば、必要な管理策でも除外できる","必要と判断された管理策は予算確保の見込みが立つまでSoAでは『実施予定』として扱い、残余リスクの承認は予算確保後に行う","除外の判断は予算を管理する部門長が行えばよく、リスク所有者による残余リスクの承認は求められない","予算が不足しているだけでは除外の正当な理由にならず、管理策を実施するか、リスク所有者が残余リスクを承認する手続きで扱う"],"a":3,"e":"予算不足だけでは除外の正当な理由になりません。管理策を実施するか、リスク所有者が残余リスクを承認する手続きで扱います。残余リスクの承認を後回しにする扱い、予算管理部門長の判断に任せる扱い、予算不足を理由に除外する扱いは、いずれもリスク所有者の承認という手続きを欠きます。","qEn":"A company intends to exclude from the SoA a control judged necessary in risk assessment solely because 'the budget is insufficient.' What is the most appropriate handling of this reason for exclusion?","oEn":["Cost is a legitimate business constraint, so stating budget shortage as the reason in the SoA allows excluding even a necessary control","Treat the needed control as 'planned' in the SoA until budget is expected and approve residual risk only after budget is secured","The budget-holding department head may decide the exclusion, and risk owner approval of residual risk is not required","Insufficient budget alone is not a valid reason for exclusion; handle it by implementing, or via a procedure where the risk owner approves the residual risk"],"eEn":"Budget shortage alone is not a legitimate reason for exclusion. Either implement the control or handle it through the risk owner's approval of residual risk. Postponing approval, leaving it to the budget-holding head, or excluding for budget reasons all lack the risk owner's approval procedure."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の担当者は「リスク1件につき管理策は1つだけ対応づければよく、1つの管理策が複数のリスクに効くことはない」と考えて、対応表を作っています。管理策とリスクの関係として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["1つの管理策が複数のリスクに対応することも、1つのリスクに複数の管理策を組み合わせることもあり得る","管理策とリスクは1対1で対応づけることが望ましく、1つの管理策が複数のリスクに効く場合は管理策を複製して別々に記載する","1つのリスクに複数の管理策を組み合わせることはできるが、1つの管理策を複数のリスクに紐づけることは重複評価になるため認められない","1つの管理策が複数のリスクに効く場合は、リスクのうち最も大きいものだけをSoAの根拠として記載する"],"a":0,"e":"1つの管理策が複数のリスクに対応することも、1つのリスクに複数の管理策を組み合わせることもあり得ます。1対1に限る扱い、複製して記載する扱い、複数のリスクへの紐づけを認めない扱い、最大のリスクだけを根拠にする扱いは、いずれも管理策とリスクの実際の関係に合いません。","qEn":"A staff member builds a mapping table believing 'each risk needs only one control, and one control never works on multiple risks.' What is the most appropriate point about the relationship between controls and risks?","oEn":["One control can address multiple risks, and multiple controls can be combined for one risk","Link controls and risks one to one, and where one control addresses several risks, duplicate the control and list it separately","Several controls may combine for one risk, but linking one control to several risks is not allowed as duplicate evaluation","When one control addresses multiple risks, state only the largest of those risks as the basis in the SoA"],"eEn":"One control may address several risks and several controls may combine for one risk. Limiting to one-to-one, duplicating controls, disallowing links to multiple risks, or citing only the largest risk does not reflect the actual relationship between controls and risks."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAI方針は3年前に策定されたままで、その後にAIの重大なインシデントと組織変更がありましたが、見直しは行われていません。AI方針に関する管理策の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["AI方針を計画した間隔や重大な変更時にレビューし、他の方針との整合を確認して必要なら改訂する","AI方針は策定時の理念を示すものとして維持し、インシデントや組織変更への対応は個別の手順書の改訂で行う","AI方針のレビューは組織変更が生じた場合にだけ行い、インシデントの教訓は方針ではなく運用手順に反映する","AI方針の改訂は、法令が変わった場合に限り必要であり、組織内部の事情による見直しは求められない"],"a":0,"e":"AI方針は、計画した間隔や重大な変更時にレビューし、他の方針との整合を確認して必要なら改訂します。理念として維持する扱い、組織変更時だけに限る扱い、法令変更に限る扱いは、方針の見直しの契機を狭めます。経営層の関与を外す扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company's AI policy remains as drafted three years ago, and since then there have been a serious AI incident and an organizational change, but no review was done. From the viewpoint of the control on AI policy, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Review the AI policy at planned intervals or on significant change, confirm alignment with the organization's other policies, and revise as needed","Keep the AI policy as an expression of original ideals and respond to incidents and reorganization by revising individual procedures","Review the AI policy only on organizational change and reflect incident lessons in operating procedures rather than the policy","Revising the AI policy is needed only when laws change, and review for internal circumstances is not required"],"eEn":"The AI policy should be reviewed at planned intervals and on significant change, checked for consistency with other policies and revised as needed. Keeping it as an ideal, limiting review to reorganization, or to legal change narrows the triggers for review. Excluding management is also wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の従業員は、AIの挙動に懸念を感じても、報告先も報告後の扱いも不明で、不利益を恐れて声を上げません。内部組織に関する管理策の観点で、最も適切な整備はどれですか。","o":["懸念は内部監査員への報告に一本化して受け付け、報告後の扱いや報告者の保護は個別の事案ごとに判断する","AIシステムに関する懸念を報告できる手段と対応のプロセスを定め、周知する","報告は匿名では受け付けず、氏名と所属を明記した場合に限って受け付けることで、虚偽の報告を防止する","報告手段は定めるが、周知は管理職に限り、一般の従業員は上長を通じて報告することとする"],"a":1,"e":"AIシステムに関する懸念を報告できる手段と対応のプロセスを定め、周知します。報告後の扱いを事案ごとに決める扱いや、上長経由にする扱いは、不利益を恐れる従業員が報告しにくい状況を解消しません。匿名を認めない扱いや、インシデント後に限る扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"At a company, employees who feel concerned about AI behavior do not speak up, since the reporting destination and handling afterward are unclear and they fear disadvantage. From the viewpoint of the controls on internal organization, what is the most appropriate arrangement?","oEn":["Concentrate concern reports on internal auditors and decide handling and reporter protection case by case","Define and publicize a means for reporting concerns about AI systems and a process for handling them","Do not accept anonymous reports and accept only reports with name and affiliation stated, to prevent false reports","Define a reporting means but publicize it only to managers, with general employees reporting through their supervisor"],"eEn":"Define a means for reporting concerns about AI systems and a response process, and publicize them. Deciding handling case by case, or routing through supervisors, does not relieve employees who fear repercussions. Disallowing anonymity or limiting to after incidents is also wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムの運用に必要なデータ、ツール、計算資源、人材などの情報が部署ごとに散在し、全体を把握している人がいません。資源に関する管理策の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["資源の文書化は組織全体の人員配置表に集約すれば足り、AIシステムごとのデータやツール、計算資源の特定までは求められない","資源として文書化するのは人材だけで十分であり、データや計算資源は、技術的な詳細なので文書化しない","AIシステムごとに必要な資源（データ、ツール、計算資源、人材など）を特定して文書化し、リスクの評価や見直しにも活用する","資源は開発段階の計画時に一度文書化すれば足り、運用中に資源の構成が変わっても文書の更新は求められない"],"a":2,"e":"AIシステムごとに必要な資源（データ、ツール、計算資源、人材など）を特定して文書化し、評価に活用します。人員配置表への集約、人材だけの文書化、開発時の一度きりの文書化は、AIシステムごとの資源の把握と維持を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company, information on data, tools, computing resources and personnel needed to run AI systems is scattered across departments and nobody has the whole picture. From the viewpoint of the controls on resources, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Documenting resources in an organization-wide staffing table suffices, and identifying data, tools and compute per AI system is not required","Documenting only personnel as resources suffices, and data and computing resources are technical details not to be documented","Identify and document the resources each AI system needs (data, tools, computing resources, personnel, etc.) and use them in risk and impact assessment","Resources are documented once at the development planning stage and need not be updated when the configuration changes in operation"],"eEn":"Identify and document the resources each AI system needs (data, tools, compute, people) and use them in assessment. Aggregating into a staffing table, documenting only people, or documenting once at development lacks per-system, maintained grasp of resources."},
{"d":"D3","q":"あるAIシステムの影響評価を実施した会社が、評価結果を担当者のPCに保存しただけで、後日、関係部署も内部監査員も参照できませんでした。AIシステムの影響評価に関する管理策の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["影響評価の結果は文書化するが、保管先は担当者の判断に任せ、関係部署や内部監査員が参照できるかどうかは保管の要件に含めない","結果は関係部署の管理者だけが参照できればよく、内部監査員には開示せず、監査の際は担当者が口頭で説明する","結果は文書化して共有フォルダに保存するが、AIシステムの変更に応じた更新や保持期間の取決めは、規格上求められない","影響評価の結果を文書化し、保持して、必要な関係者が参照できるようにする"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステムの影響評価の結果を文書化し、保持して、必要な関係者が参照できるようにします。保管先を担当者任せにする扱い、内部監査員に開示しない扱い、更新や保持の取決めを置かない扱いは、必要な関係者が参照できる保持の要件を満たしません。","qEn":"A company that performed an AI system impact assessment only saved the results on the staff member's PC, and later neither related departments nor internal auditors could refer to them. From the viewpoint of the control on AI system impact assessment, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Document impact assessment results but leave storage to the staff member, with accessibility to related departments and internal auditors not a storage requirement","Results need be viewable only by related department managers, not disclosed to internal auditors, with the staff member explaining orally at audit","Save results to a shared folder but updates on AI system changes and retention periods are not required by the standard","Document and retain the impact assessment results so that the necessary parties can refer to them"],"eEn":"Document the AI system impact assessment results, retain them and make them available to relevant parties. Leaving storage to the staff member, not disclosing to internal auditors, or setting no update or retention rules fails the requirement for retention accessible to those who need it."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAIモデル開発チームは、要件を定めずにモデル構築に着手し、完成後に「期待した用途に合わない」と判明しました。AIライフサイクルの管理策（A.6）の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["要件はモデルの構築と並行して定めればよく、設計の着手前には意図した用途と制約を暫定のメモにとどめ、文書化は完成後に行う","意図した用途、性能、制約条件、責任あるAIの観点を含む要件を、設計と開発の前に明確にして文書として残しておく必要がある","要件は性能の数値だけを定めれば足り、意図した用途や利用上の制約は、営業部門の説明資料に任せればよい","責任あるAIに関する要件は、設計の段階ではなく検証の段階で検討すれば足り、要件定義の時点では性能と用途に絞る"],"a":1,"e":"AIライフサイクルの管理策では、意図した用途、性能、制約、責任あるAIの観点を含む要件を、設計と開発の前に明確にして文書として残します。構築と並行して定める扱い、検証段階まで責任あるAIの要件を先送りする扱い、性能の数値だけを定める扱いは、設計前の要件定義という順序を欠きます。","qEn":"A company's AI model development team started building the model without defining requirements and found after completion that it did not suit the expected use. From the viewpoint of the AI life cycle controls (A.6), what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Define requirements in parallel with building the model, keeping intended use and constraints as provisional notes before design and documenting after completion","Clarify and document AI system requirements, including intended use, performance, constraints and responsible AI aspects, before design and development","Requirements need only state performance figures, and the intended use and usage constraints can be left to sales explanatory materials","Responsible AI requirements can be considered at verification rather than design, and requirements definition covers only performance and use"],"eEn":"Under the life cycle controls, requirements covering intended use, performance, constraints and responsible AI viewpoints are clarified and documented before design and development. Defining them in parallel, deferring responsible AI to verification, or defining only performance figures lacks requirements definition ahead of design."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、AIモデルの検証で、開発に使ったデータと同じ分布のデータだけで評価し、実運用の多様な条件では試験していません。A.6の検証・妥当性確認の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["開発時と同じ分布のデータで高い精度が出ていれば、運用の条件が異なっていても、妥当性の確認は完了したものとみなす","基準と方法は定めるが、意図した用途に即した条件での評価は導入先での試行で代替でき、開発中は同一分布のデータで足りる","検証・妥当性確認の基準と方法を定め、意図した用途に即した多様な条件で、性能や堅牢性を評価する","妥当性確認は精度と堅牢性を対象とするが、利用状況に即した評価は顧客からのフィードバックを待って行うものである"],"a":2,"e":"検証・妥当性確認の基準と方法を定め、意図した用途に即した多様な条件で性能や堅牢性を評価します。同一分布のデータだけで足りるとする扱い、導入先の試行やフィードバックに回す扱いは、リリース前の妥当性確認として不十分です。基準を結果の後から定める扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"In verifying an AI model, a company evaluated only with data of the same distribution as used in development and did not test under the diverse conditions of real operation. From the A.6 verification and validation viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["If high accuracy is obtained on data of the same distribution as development, validation is deemed complete even if operating conditions differ","Define criteria and methods, but evaluation under conditions matching the intended use can be replaced by trials at the customer site, with same-distribution data sufficing during development","Define criteria and methods for verification and validation, and evaluate performance and robustness under diverse conditions that match the intended use","Validation covers accuracy and robustness, but evaluation under real usage is done after waiting for customer feedback"],"eEn":"Define criteria and methods for verification and validation and evaluate performance and robustness under diverse conditions matching the intended use. Same-distribution data only, or deferring to customer-site trials or feedback, is inadequate pre-release validation. Setting criteria after seeing results is also wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムを本番環境へ展開する際、展開の可否を判断する基準や準備状況の確認を行わず、開発完了とともに公開しました。A.6の展開に関する観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["展開前の確認は開発完了時のレビューで行った試験結果を引用すれば足り、展開先の環境での準備状況は公開後に確認する","展開計画は大規模なAIシステムにのみ必要であり、小規模なAIシステムには、展開前の確認の手順を設けなくてよい","展開前の確認は行うが、基準は担当者ごとに判断し、確認の結果は問題が見つかった場合にのみ記録する","展開計画を立て、展開前に満たすべき要件の充足を確認する手順を定める"],"a":3,"e":"展開計画を立て、展開前に満たすべき要件の充足を確認する手順を定めます。開発時の試験結果の引用で済ませて展開先の確認を公開後に回す扱い、基準を担当者任せにして問題時のみ記録する扱い、小規模なら不要とする扱いは、展開前の確認の手順を満たしません。","qEn":"When deploying an AI system to production, a company released it as soon as development finished, without criteria for deciding on deployment or readiness checks. From the A.6 deployment viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Pre-deployment checking can cite test results from the development-completion review, with readiness in the target environment checked after release","A deployment plan is needed only for large AI systems, and small ones need no pre-deployment check procedure","Perform pre-deployment checks but let each person judge the criteria and record results only when problems are found","Make a deployment plan and define a procedure to confirm, before deployment, that the requirements to be met are satisfied"],"eEn":"Prepare a deployment plan and define a procedure to confirm that requirements to be met before deployment are fulfilled. Citing development tests and checking the target environment after release, leaving criteria to individuals with records only on problems, or skipping for small systems does not meet the pre-deployment procedure."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の運用中のAIシステムは、判断の経緯を追跡できるログが残っておらず、顧客から苦情を受けても原因を特定できません。A.6の運用に関する観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["運用中の性能監視とあわせて、事象を追跡できるイベントログを記録し、不具合の修復や更新の手順も整える","ログは苦情対応の際に利用者から提出された画面の記録を使い、運用中のイベントログの継続的な記録は行わない","運用中のログは性能監視のための集計値だけを記録し、個々の事象を追跡できる詳細な記録は保管コストの観点から省く","不具合の修復の手順は設けるが、更新の手順は開発チームの判断に任せ、修復や更新の結果の記録は保持しない"],"a":0,"e":"運用の管理策では、運用中の性能監視とあわせて、事象を追跡できるイベントログを記録し、不具合の修復や更新の手順も整えます。利用者提出の画面記録に頼る扱い、集計値だけを記録して個々の事象を追跡できない扱い、更新を担当任せにして記録を残さない扱いは、原因の特定を可能にする要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's AI system in operation keeps no logs that allow tracing how decisions were made, so it cannot identify causes even when customers complain. From the A.6 operation viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Alongside performance monitoring in operation, record event logs that allow events to be traced, and prepare procedures for repair and update","Use screen captures submitted by users when handling complaints and do not continuously record event logs in operation","Record only aggregate values for performance monitoring and omit detailed records that trace individual events for storage cost reasons","Set repair procedures but leave updates to the development team and keep no records of repairs or updates"],"eEn":"The operation controls require recording event logs that allow tracing events alongside operational performance monitoring, and having repair and update procedures. Relying on user-submitted screenshots, recording only aggregates, or leaving updates to the team without records fails to enable root cause identification."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAIシステムには、技術文書がほとんどなく、利用者向けの説明も担当者の頭の中にしかありません。そのため担当者の異動で運用が止まりかけました。A.6の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["AIシステムの技術文書（設計、データ、検証結果、運用手順など）を整備し、関係者が利用できる状態に維持する","技術文書は開発者が個人で保管する作業メモとして作成し、組織の管理下に置く必要はなく、異動時には口頭で引き継ぐ","技術文書は監査の直前に一度だけまとめればよく、その後の変更や更新に追随して改訂する必要はない","技術文書には設計の内容だけを残し、データや検証結果は、容量を圧迫するため、保管の対象としない"],"a":0,"e":"AIシステムの技術文書（設計、データ、検証結果、運用手順など）を整備し、関係者が利用できる状態に維持します。個人の作業メモにとどめて口頭で引き継ぐ扱い、監査の直前に一度だけまとめる扱い、設計だけを残す扱いは、利用可能で最新の技術文書という要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's AI system has almost no technical documentation, and explanations for users exist only in a staff member's head, so operation nearly stopped when that person was transferred. From the A.6 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Prepare technical documentation of the AI system (design, data, verification results, operating procedures, etc.) and keep it available to relevant parties","Create technical documents as developers' personal working notes outside organizational control and hand over orally at transfers","Technical documents need be compiled once just before an audit, and need not be revised to follow later changes","Keep only design content in technical documentation, and do not retain data and verification results because they strain storage"],"eEn":"Prepare technical documentation of the AI system (design, data, verification results, operating procedures) and keep it available to relevant parties. Keeping personal notes with oral handover, compiling once before audit, or keeping only the design does not meet the requirement for available, current documentation."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、出所の不明な外部データセットをそのままAIの学習に使い、あとで来歴を問われても説明できませんでした。データに関する管理策（A.7）の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["データの取得元の確認は有償で購入したデータに限って行えば足り、無償で公開されているデータは出所の確認を省いてよい","データの取得元や来歴、品質、利用の権利を確認して記録に残し、データの準備作業のプロセスを定めて管理する必要がある","データの来歴は個人情報を含む場合にだけ記録すれば足り、その他のデータは、品質の確認も記録も求められない","データの品質は学習後のモデルの精度で代替して評価できるため、学習前のデータそのものの品質の確認は省ける"],"a":1,"e":"データの取得元や来歴、品質、利用の権利を確認して記録し、データの準備のプロセスを定めて管理します。無償公開のデータの出所確認を省く扱い、個人情報を含む場合だけ記録する扱い、学習後の精度で品質を代替する扱いは、データの来歴と品質の管理を満たしません。","qEn":"A company used an external dataset of unknown origin as is for AI training and could not explain its provenance when later asked. From the data controls (A.7) viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Confirming data sources is needed only for purchased data, and freely published data may skip source checks","Confirm and record the data's source, provenance, quality and usage rights, and define and manage a data preparation process","Provenance need be recorded only when data contains personal information, and other data need neither quality checks nor records","Data quality can be evaluated by the trained model's accuracy instead, so checking the quality of the data itself before training can be skipped"],"eEn":"Confirm and record the source, provenance, quality and usage rights of data, and define and manage data preparation processes. Skipping source checks for free public data, recording only personal data, or substituting post-training accuracy for data quality does not meet data provenance and quality management."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社では、AIの学習データのラベル付けを複数の外部作業者に任せた結果、同じ画像に作業者ごとに異なるラベルが付き、モデルの精度が不安定になりました。A.7の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["ラベル付けの基準は定めるが、品質の確認は学習後のモデルの精度の変化で代替し、ラベル付けの時点での確認や記録は行わない","データ準備の基準と手順は文書化するが、運用するのは開発者だけとし、外部作業者には基準を共有せず成果物のみを受け取る","ラベル付けやクリーニングなどデータ準備の基準と手順を定め、品質の確認と記録を行う","ラベル付けの品質は、外部作業者の完了報告で十分に確認できるため、抜取り確認などの手順は設けない"],"a":2,"e":"ラベル付けやクリーニングなどデータ準備の基準と手順を定め、品質の確認と記録を行います。学習後の精度で品質確認を代替する扱い、基準を外部作業者と共有しない扱い、自己申告に頼る扱いは、ラベルの一貫性を保てません。基準を統一せず多数決に頼る扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"At a company, labeling of AI training data was entrusted to multiple external workers, and the same image received different labels per worker, making model accuracy unstable. From the A.7 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Define labeling criteria but replace quality checks with changes in model accuracy after training, with no checks or records at labeling time","Document data preparation criteria and procedures but have only developers use them, not sharing them with external workers and receiving only deliverables","Define criteria and procedures for data preparation such as labeling and cleaning, and check and record quality","Labeling quality can be adequately confirmed by external workers' self-reports, so set no procedure such as sampling checks"],"eEn":"Define criteria and procedures for data preparation such as labeling and cleaning, and check and record quality. Replacing checks with post-training accuracy, not sharing criteria with external workers, or relying on self-reports cannot keep labels consistent. Relying on majority vote without unified criteria is also wrong."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が提供するAIサービスの利用者向け資料には、機能の紹介だけが書かれ、性能の限界や不適切な使い方は書かれていません。利害関係者への情報提供の管理策（A.8）の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["利用者向け資料には機能と性能の実績値を載せ、限界や不適切な使い方は社内の開発文書に記載して、利用者には公開しない","利用者向けの情報は、契約書に記載する免責事項だけで足り、製品資料の側で性能の限界や使い方を説明する必要はない","利用者への情報提供は販売時の説明で完結するため、運用開始後に更新された性能や限界の情報を提供し直す必要はない","利用者が適切に使えるよう、意図した用途、性能と限界、不適切な使用の例などの情報を提供する"],"a":3,"e":"利用者が適切に使えるよう、意図した用途、性能と限界、不適切な使用の例などの情報を提供します。限界を社内文書にとどめる扱い、免責事項だけに頼る扱い、販売時で完結させ更新情報を提供しない扱いは、利用者が適切に使えるための情報提供を欠きます。","qEn":"User materials for a company's AI service describe only features, without performance limits or inappropriate uses. From the viewpoint of the control on providing information to interested parties (A.8), what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Put functions and performance results in user materials and keep limits and misuse examples in internal development documents without disclosing them to users","User information suffices as a disclaimer in the contract, and the product materials need not explain performance limits or usage","Information to users is complete with the sales explanation, and updated performance or limits after operation need not be provided again","Provide information so users can use the AI system appropriately, such as intended use, performance and limits, and examples of inappropriate use"],"eEn":"Provide information such as intended use, performance and limits, and examples of inappropriate use so users can use the system appropriately. Keeping limits internal, relying on disclaimers, or completing information at sale without updates lacks information that enables appropriate use."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAIシステムで、利用者に影響する不具合が発生しましたが、誰にどの時点で何を知らせるかの計画がなく、利用者への連絡が遅れました。A.8の観点で、最も適切な備えはどれですか。","o":["インシデントについて、関係する利害関係者へ知らせる内容と手順をあらかじめ決めておく","利用者への連絡は、原因の調査が完全に終わり、再発防止策が確定してから、まとめて行うことが最も誠実な対応である","インシデントの連絡は、規制当局に報告義務がある場合に限って行えば足り、利用者への連絡の計画までは求められない","連絡の内容と手順は顧客対応部門が個別に判断できるようにし、全社で共通の手順はインシデントの定義が固まるまで定めない"],"a":0,"e":"インシデントについて、関係する利害関係者へ知らせる内容と手順をあらかじめ決めておきます。調査完了後にまとめて連絡する扱い、規制当局への報告に限る扱い、個別判断に任せて全社共通の手順を後回しにする扱いは、事前に決めた連絡の備えになっていません。","qEn":"After a defect affecting users occurred in a company's AI system, contact with users was delayed because there was no plan for who is told what and when. From the A.8 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate preparation?","oEn":["Decide in advance the content and procedure for informing relevant interested parties about incidents","The most sincere response is to inform users together only after cause investigation is fully complete and preventive measures are fixed","Incident notification need be made only where a regulator has a reporting obligation, and a plan for contacting users is unnecessary","Let the customer support department judge content and procedure individually and set no company-wide procedure until the incident definition is fixed"],"eEn":"Decide in advance what to tell relevant stakeholders about incidents and the procedure. Notifying after investigation completes, limiting to regulators, or leaving it to individual judgment without a common procedure is not an advance-defined communication preparation."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の営業担当者が、社内で承認された用途ではない顧客向けの判断業務にも、AIツールを使い始めました。AIシステムの利用に関する管理策の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["用途の逸脱は営業部門の管理者の許可で足り、AIの利用に関するプロセスの策定や意図した用途との整合の確認は情報システム部門に任せる","責任あるAIの利用に関するプロセスを定め、意図した用途に沿った利用であることを確認し、逸脱の扱いを決める","承認された用途以外での利用は、成果が出た場合に限り、事後に追認して正式な用途として登録すればよい","用途を逸脱した利用への対応はAI方針の改訂時に一括して検討すれば足り、個別の逸脱の扱いを事前に決めておく必要はない"],"a":1,"e":"責任あるAIの利用に関するプロセスを定め、意図した用途に沿った利用であることを確認し、逸脱の扱いを決めます。営業管理者の許可だけで済ませる扱い、成果が出た後に追認する扱い、方針改訂時まで逸脱の扱いを決めない扱いは、利用プロセスの要求を満たしません。","qEn":"A company's sales staff began using an AI tool for customer-facing judgment work that is not an internally approved use. From the viewpoint of the controls on use of AI systems, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["A deviation need only a sales manager's permission, leaving the AI use process and intended-use checks to the IT department","Define a process for responsible use, confirm that use follows the intended purpose, and decide how deviations are handled","Use outside approved purposes may be ratified afterward and registered as a formal use if results are good","Handle deviations in bulk when revising the AI policy, with no need to decide beforehand how individual deviations are treated"],"eEn":"Define a process for responsible use of AI, confirm that use matches the intended purpose and decide how deviations are handled. Relying on a sales manager's permission, ratifying after success, or leaving deviations undecided until policy revision does not meet the use process requirement."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が、AIモデルの提供を外部ベンダーから受けていますが、契約には、モデルの不具合が起きた場合の責任の所在も、情報提供の範囲も書かれていません。第三者・顧客関係の管理策（A.10）の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["責任の配分は契約に記載するが、AIの不具合に関する条項は一般的なITサービスの責任条項で足り、AI固有の事項は定めない","ベンダーが提供するモデルの不具合の責任は、契約の有無にかかわらず、自動的にベンダーだけに帰属するため、契約での配分は求められない","自社とベンダー（および顧客）の間のAIに関する責任の配分を明確にし、契約等に反映する","責任の配分は、顧客との契約にだけ必要であり、ベンダーとの契約には、AIに関する責任の条項を含めなくてよい"],"a":2,"e":"自社とベンダー（および顧客）の間のAIに関する責任の配分を明確にし、契約等に反映します。交渉に任せる扱い、自動的にベンダーへ帰属するとみなす扱い、顧客との契約だけに限る扱い、一般的な条項でAI固有の事項を定めない扱いは、AIに関する責任配分の明確化を欠きます。","qEn":"A company receives an AI model from an external vendor, but the contract states neither where responsibility lies if the model malfunctions nor the scope of information provided. From the third-party and customer relationship controls (A.10) viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Describe responsibility allocation in the contract but a generic IT service liability clause suffices without AI-specific matters","Responsibility for a vendor-provided model's defects automatically falls only on the vendor regardless of the contract, so allocation in the contract is unnecessary","Clarify the allocation of AI-related responsibilities between the company and the vendor (and customers) and reflect it in contracts and similar","Allocation of responsibility is needed only in contracts with customers, and contracts with vendors need not include AI responsibility clauses"],"eEn":"Clarify the allocation of AI-related responsibilities among the company, vendor and customers and reflect it in contracts. Leaving it to negotiation, assuming automatic vendor attribution, limiting to customer contracts, or using generic clauses without AI-specific matters lacks clarification of AI responsibility allocation."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が、AI画像認識サービスの外部ベンダーを選定します。経営層は価格が最も安い会社を選ぶよう指示しました。第三者関係の管理策（A.10）の観点で、最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["ベンダーの確認は情報セキュリティの認証の有無に限り、AI固有の取組みや提供情報の水準は導入後の運用で確認すればよい","ベンダーの責任あるAIの取組みは、ベンダー自身が公表している資料だけを確認すれば、十分な裏づけになる","選定の基準を設けて確認はするが、その結果は購買部門の稟議書にだけ残し、AIの管理を担う部門とは共有しない","ベンダーの責任あるAIへの取組みや提供情報の水準を確認し、自社の方針や要求との整合を選定の基準に含める"],"a":3,"e":"ベンダーの責任あるAIへの取組みや提供情報の水準を確認し、自社の方針や要求との整合を選定の基準に含めます。価格と納期だけで選ぶ扱い、情報セキュリティの認証だけを見る扱い、自己申告資料だけで足りるとする扱い、確認結果をAI管理部門と共有しない扱いは、整合の確認を欠きます。","qEn":"A company is selecting an external vendor for an AI image recognition service. Management instructed it to choose the cheapest company. From the third-party relationship controls (A.10) viewpoint, what is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["Limit vendor checks to information security certification and confirm AI-specific efforts and information levels during operation after introduction","The vendor's responsible AI efforts are sufficiently supported by checking only the self-declared materials the vendor itself publishes","Set selection criteria and check, but keep results only in the purchasing department's approval document, not sharing them with the department managing AI","Confirm the vendor's responsible AI efforts and the level of information provided, and include alignment with the company's policy and requirements in the selection criteria"],"eEn":"Check the vendor's responsible AI efforts and level of provided information, and include alignment with the company's policies and requirements in selection criteria. Selecting by price and delivery, checking only security certification, relying on self-declared documents, or not sharing results with the AI management department lacks alignment checking."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社が利用している外部のAIモデルが、ベンダー側の判断で突然更新され、自社サービスの出力傾向が変わりました。事前の通知はありませんでした。A.10の観点で、最も適切な再発防止策はどれですか。","o":["モデルの変更の通知や情報提供を契約等で取り決め、ベンダーのパフォーマンスを継続的に監視する仕組みを設ける","ベンダーのモデルの更新は性能の改善が目的であるため、通知を求めずに、出力の変化があれば、その都度利用者に注意を促す","契約で通知を取り決めるが、運用中のベンダーの性能の監視はベンダーの自己報告に依存し、自社では出力の傾向を測定しない","ベンダーの変更の通知は年次の契約更新時にまとめて受け取る取決めとし、運用中の個別の変更ごとの通知は求めない"],"a":0,"e":"モデルの変更の通知や情報提供を契約等で取り決め、ベンダーのパフォーマンスを継続的に監視する仕組みを設けます。自己報告への依存、年次のまとめ通知、通知を求めない扱い、責任範囲外とする扱いは、変更を適時に把握して自社サービスへの影響を管理するという要求を満たしません。","qEn":"An external AI model a company uses was suddenly updated at the vendor's discretion, changing its service's output tendencies, with no advance notice. From the A.10 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate preventive measure?","oEn":["Agree on notification of model changes and information provision by contract or similar, and set up a mechanism to continually monitor the vendor's performance","Vendor model updates aim at improvement, so do not ask for notice and merely warn users each time output changes","Agree notification by contract but rely on the vendor's self-reports for performance and do not measure output trends in-house","Agree to receive vendor change notices in bulk at the annual contract renewal and not request notice of individual changes during operation"],"eEn":"Agree on notice of model changes and information provision by contract and set up continuous monitoring of vendor performance. Relying on self-reports, annual bulk notices, not requesting notice, or treating it as outside responsibility does not meet timely awareness and management of impact on the service."},
{"d":"D3","q":"あるAI提供企業が、顧客企業から「自社の用途で想定外の出力が出たときの対応窓口を明確にしてほしい」と要望されました。A.10の顧客関係の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["窓口の取決めは顧客の規模が大きい場合に限って行い、それ以外の顧客は一般の問い合わせ窓口で対応する","顧客のニーズと期待を考慮し、責任ある利用のための情報と、問題発生時の連絡や対応の取決めを提供する","窓口の連絡先は伝えるが、想定外の出力時の対応の範囲と責任は問題が発生してから顧客と協議して決める","顧客への情報提供は販売時点の説明資料で完結し、運用開始後に把握した性能の限界や制約は顧客に追加提供しない"],"a":1,"e":"顧客のニーズと期待を考慮し、責任ある利用のための情報と、問題発生時の連絡や対応の取決めを提供します。規模で限る扱い、対応の範囲と責任を事後に決める扱い、販売後の情報を追加提供しない扱いは、顧客関係の管理策を満たしません。","qEn":"A corporate customer asked an AI provider to clarify a contact point for responding when unexpected outputs arise in its use. From the A.10 customer relationship viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Agree on a contact point only for large customers and handle others through the general inquiry desk","Consider the customer's needs and expectations, and provide information for responsible use and arrangements for contact and response when problems arise","Share the contact point but decide the scope of response and responsibility for unexpected outputs after a problem occurs","Information to customers is complete with sales-time materials and limits or constraints learned after operation are not provided additionally"],"eEn":"Consider customer needs and expectations and provide information for responsible use and arrangements for contact and response when problems occur. Limiting by customer size, deciding response scope after problems, or not providing later information does not meet the customer relationship controls."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社はAnnex Aの管理策を文言どおりに実施した記録を揃えましたが、管理目的が実際に達成できているかを確認していません。管理目的と管理策の関係として、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["実施した記録があれば管理策の有効性は確認できるので、管理目的の達成度の確認は次回の認証審査で認証機関が行う事項である","管理目的は管理策の見出しにすぎないため、達成度の確認ではなく、管理策の件数の充足率だけを評価すればよい","各管理策は管理目的を達成するための手段であり、実施するだけにとどまらず、管理目的の達成度と有効性を確認する必要がある","有効性の確認は内部監査で重要性の高い管理策に限って行えばよく、他の管理策は実施の記録の有無を確認すれば足りる"],"a":2,"e":"管理策は管理目的を達成するための手段であり、実施するだけでなく、管理目的の達成度と有効性を確認します。記録があれば達成とみなす扱い、達成度の確認を認証機関に委ねる扱い、重要な管理策に限る扱い、件数の充足率だけを見る扱いは、管理目的の達成の確認を欠きます。","qEn":"A company assembled records of implementing Annex A controls to the letter but has not checked whether the control objectives are actually achieved. What is the most appropriate point about the relationship between control objectives and controls?","oEn":["Records of implementation confirm effectiveness, and checking whether control objectives are achieved is for the certification body at the next audit","Control objectives are mere headings of controls, so evaluate only the fulfillment rate of the number of controls rather than achievement","Controls are means to achieve control objectives, so beyond implementing them, confirm the degree of achievement of the objectives and their effectiveness","Check effectiveness only for important controls at internal audit and confirm the existence of implementation records for the others"],"eEn":"Controls are means to achieve control objectives, so confirm not only implementation but also achievement and effectiveness. Regarding records as achievement, leaving checks to the certification body, checking only important controls, or looking at fulfillment counts lacks confirmation of objective achievement."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ISO/IEC 27001のISMSを運用している会社が、AIMSのAnnex A対応で、既存の情報セキュリティの管理策をそのまま「AIの管理策も満たす」として流用しようとしています。最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["ISMSの管理策は情報セキュリティの全領域を網羅しているので、AI固有の管理策を追加せずに、そのままAIMSの要求を満たす","ISMSの管理策をAnnex Aの項目名に当てはめた対応表を作れば、内容の差異を検討せずにそのまま流用できる","AI固有のリスクは情報セキュリティのインシデントとして扱えるため、バイアスや影響評価に関する管理策は求められない","既存の管理策を活用できるか確認しつつ、AI固有のリスク（バイアス、影響評価など）に対するギャップを洗い出して補う必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"既存の管理策を活用できるか確認しつつ、AI固有のリスク（バイアス、影響評価など）に対するギャップを洗い出して補います。追加なしでそのまま満たすとする扱い、項目名の対応表だけで流用する扱い、AI固有のリスクを情報セキュリティのインシデントとして扱い不要とする扱いは、ギャップの洗い出しを欠きます。","qEn":"A company operating an ISO/IEC 27001 ISMS plans, for Annex A, to reuse existing information security controls as is, claiming they 'also satisfy the AI controls.' What is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["ISMS controls cover the entire information security domain, so they satisfy the AIMS requirements as is without adding AI-specific controls","Mapping ISMS controls to Annex A item names allows direct reuse without examining content differences","AI-specific risks can be handled as information security incidents, so controls on bias and impact assessment are unnecessary","Check whether existing controls can be leveraged, while identifying and filling gaps against AI-specific risks such as bias and impact assessment"],"eEn":"Check whether existing controls can be used and identify and fill gaps for AI-specific risks such as bias and impact assessment. Satisfying requirements as is, reusing through a name-mapping table, or treating AI risks as security incidents lacks gap identification."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社の担当者は、SoAとリスク対応計画を同じ文書だと考え、監査に備えて片方しか作成していません。管理策の採否と実施の計画という観点から、両者の違いとして最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["両者は名称が異なるだけで内容は同一なので、どちらか一方を作成すれば、規格の要求は両方とも満たされる","SoAは実施の内容と責任者と時期を定める文書で、リスク対応計画は管理策の採否と除外の理由だけを示す文書である","SoAは必要な管理策と採否・実施状況・理由を示し、リスク対応計画は実施の内容、責任者、時期、資源などを定める","SoAはAnnex Aの管理策を対象に作成し、リスク対応計画はAnnex A以外の管理策だけを対象に作成する"],"a":2,"e":"SoAは必要な管理策と採否・実施状況・理由を示し、リスク対応計画は実施の内容、責任者、時期、資源などを定めます。同一の文書とする扱い、役割を逆に捉える扱い、対象をAnnex Aの内外で分ける扱いは、両者の役割の取り違えです。","qEn":"A company's staff member considers the SoA and the risk treatment plan the same document and, preparing for the audit, has prepared only one. From the viewpoint of control adoption versus implementation planning, what is the most appropriate difference between them?","oEn":["They differ only in name and are identical in content, so preparing either one satisfies the standard's requirements for both","The SoA defines content, responsible persons and timing of implementation, while the risk treatment plan only shows adoption of controls and reasons for exclusion","The SoA shows necessary controls with adoption, implementation status and reasons, while the risk treatment plan defines what is done, by whom, when and with what resources","The SoA covers Annex A controls and the risk treatment plan covers only controls outside Annex A"],"eEn":"The SoA shows necessary controls, adoption, implementation status and reasons, while the risk treatment plan defines implementation content, owners, timing and resources. Treating them as one document, reversing their roles, or splitting them by inside or outside Annex A confuses their roles."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムの利用者や影響を受ける人々から寄せられた苦情や指摘を、担当者の対応で終わらせ、影響評価の見直しに活用していません。A.5の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["苦情や指摘はリスクアセスメントの見直しには反映させるが、影響評価は導入判断のための評価なので導入後の入力には使わない","寄せられた苦情や指摘を、AIシステムの影響評価の見直しの入力として扱い、必要に応じ評価を更新する","苦情や指摘が影響評価の見直しにつながるのは、規制当局から指導があった場合に限られる","影響評価の見直しは、新しい機能を追加するときにだけ必要で、利用者の指摘は、見直しの契機にならない"],"a":1,"e":"寄せられた苦情や指摘を、AIシステムの影響評価の見直しの入力として扱い、必要に応じ評価を更新します。リスクアセスメントにだけ反映して影響評価の見直しに使わない扱い、規制当局の指導や機能追加に限る扱いは、見直しの契機を狭めます。","qEn":"A company closes complaints and remarks from users and affected people of an AI system with the responder's handling and does not use them to revisit the impact assessment. From the A.5 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Reflect complaints in risk assessment review, but impact assessment is for the introduction decision and is not updated with post-introduction inputs","Treat complaints and remarks received as input for revisiting the AI system impact assessment, and update the assessment as needed","Complaints and remarks lead to revisiting the impact assessment only when a regulator has given guidance","Revisiting the impact assessment is needed only when adding a new function, and user remarks are not a trigger for review"],"eEn":"Treat complaints and comments as inputs to review the AI system impact assessment and update it as needed. Reflecting them only in risk assessment, or limiting review to regulator guidance or feature additions, narrows the triggers for review."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社では、学習データの収集、モデル開発、検証、運用監視、人間による確認の各段階の責任者が決まっておらず、問題が起きても誰も判断しません。A.3の観点で、最も適切な整備はどれですか。","o":["各段階の責任はAIMS責任者が一人で負い、各段階の担当者には責任を割り当てず、作業の実施だけを担わせる","役割の割当ては開発段階のみで十分であり、運用段階や廃止段階の責任者は、各段階の担当者が自然に決まるのを待てばよい","責任と権限を持つ役割はプロジェクトごとに開発開始時に定めればよく、組織としての役割の割当てはAIMSの要求に含まれない","AIシステムのライフサイクルの各段階にわたって、責任と権限を持つ役割を定め、割り当てる"],"a":3,"e":"AIシステムのライフサイクルの各段階にわたって、責任と権限を持つ役割を定め、割り当てます。一人に集中させる扱い、開発段階しか定めない扱い、プロジェクトごとの開発開始時に限る扱い、外部に委ねる扱いは、各段階の責任の所在を明確にしません。","qEn":"At a company, no one is designated as responsible for each stage of data collection, model development, verification, operational monitoring and human review, and nobody makes decisions when problems arise. From the A.3 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate arrangement?","oEn":["The AIMS manager alone bears responsibility for every stage, and stage staff carry out work without assigned responsibility","Role assignment is enough at the development stage only, and responsible persons for operation and retirement can be left to emerge naturally","Roles with responsibility and authority are set per project at the start of development, and organization-wide assignment is not part of AIMS requirements","Define and assign roles with responsibility and authority across each stage of the AI system life cycle"],"eEn":"Define and assign roles with responsibility and authority across each stage of the AI system life cycle. Concentrating in one person, defining only for development, setting only per project at development start, or outsourcing does not clarify responsibility at each stage."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAI開発は担当者ごとに進め方が異なり、公平性や説明可能性への配慮の有無も案件によってばらつき、品質の説明が難しくなっています。A.6の観点で、最も適切な整備はどれですか。","o":["責任ある開発の目的と、設計・開発の各段階で確認すべき事項を定めた開発プロセスを確立し、案件に適用する","開発プロセスは案件ごとの特性に合わせて開発チームが策定してよく、全社で共通して確認する事項は定めず、案件終了後にレビューで共有する","責任あるAIの配慮は、開発の完了後に別チームが評価すれば足り、設計や開発の各段階で確認を行う必要はない","開発プロセスは定めて文書化するが、責任あるAIの観点は設計の段階で定義せず、内部監査で評価基準を後から示す"],"a":0,"e":"責任ある開発の目的と、設計・開発の各段階で確認すべき事項を定めた開発プロセスを確立し、案件に適用します。案件ごとに策定して共通の確認事項を持たない扱い、完了後に別チームが評価する扱い、観点を内部監査で後から示す扱いは、案件間のばらつきを防げません。","qEn":"At a company, AI development proceeds differently by individual, and consideration of fairness and explainability varies by project, making quality hard to explain. From the A.6 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate arrangement?","oEn":["Establish a development process that sets responsible development objectives and items to confirm at each design and development stage, and apply it to projects","Let the development team define the process per case, set no company-wide checks and share lessons in post-project reviews","Responsible AI consideration can be evaluated by a separate team after development, so no confirmation at each design and development stage is needed","Define and document the process, but do not define responsible AI viewpoints at design and show evaluation criteria later at internal audit"],"eEn":"Establish a development process defining responsible development objectives and checks at each design and development stage, and apply it to projects. Defining per case without common checks, evaluating afterwards by another team, or showing criteria later at audit cannot prevent variation across projects."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある会社のAIサービスでは、利用者がAIの不適切な出力に気づいても、報告する手段が分からず、苦情が公開の場に出てから初めて把握されました。A.8の観点で、最も適切な整備はどれですか。","o":["利用者からの報告は、SNSの書き込みを担当者が定期的に検索して拾う運用で足りるので、専用の報告手段は設けない","報告の手段は、有料プランの契約者に限って提供すれば十分であり、無料の利用者の報告は受け付けなくてよい","報告手段は設けるが、受け付けた報告は開発部門だけが保管し、対応状況の管理や利害関係者への周知は行わない","利用者などの外部の利害関係者が、不具合や悪影響を報告できる手段を用意し、周知して、受けた報告の対応を管理する"],"a":3,"e":"利用者などの外部の利害関係者が、不具合や悪影響を報告できる手段を用意し、周知して、受けた報告の対応を管理します。SNSの検索に頼る扱い、有料契約者に限る扱い、報告を保管するだけで対応を管理しない扱いは、報告の受付と対応管理を満たしません。","qEn":"At a company's AI service, users who noticed inappropriate AI outputs did not know how to report them, and the company learned of the issue only after complaints appeared publicly. From the A.8 viewpoint, what is the most appropriate arrangement?","oEn":["Staff periodically searching social media posts is enough to pick up user reports, so set up no dedicated reporting means","Provide the reporting means only to paid-plan contractors, and reports from free-plan users need not be accepted","Provide a reporting channel but keep reports only in the development department with no management of response status or publicizing to stakeholders","Provide and publicize a means for external interested parties such as users to report defects and adverse effects, and manage the handling of reports received"],"eEn":"Provide a means for external stakeholders such as users to report defects and adverse effects, publicize it and manage responses to reports received. Relying on social media searches, limiting to paid users, or only storing reports without managing responses does not meet intake and response management."},
{"d":"D3","q":"ある小売会社は、地方店舗の販売データに欠損が多いまま需要予測AIを学習させ、地方店舗で予測が大きく外れました。データに関する管理策（A.7）の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["データの品質の問題はモデルの検証の段階で精度の低下として捉えられるので、学習の前にデータそのものの要件を定めて評価する必要はない","意図した用途に応じたデータ品質の要件を定め、学習前にデータがその要件を満たすか評価し、満たさない場合には補完や用途の見直しを行う","データの量と多様性が確保されていれば足りるので、欠損の補完は予測の誤差が大きい店舗が判明した時点で検討する","データ品質の要件は全社で一律の数値に固定すべきであり、用途ごとに定める必要はない"],"a":1,"e":"意図した用途に応じたデータ品質の要件を定め、学習前にデータがその要件を満たすか評価し、満たさない場合は補完や用途の見直しを行います。検証段階で捉えればよいとする扱い、量で質を補うとする扱い、後から補完を検討する扱い、一律の数値に固定する扱いは、学習前の品質管理を欠きます。","qEn":"A retailer trained a demand forecasting AI on data with many gaps for regional stores, and forecasts missed widely at regional stores. From the data controls (A.7) viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Data quality issues show up as accuracy loss at model verification, so there is no need to define and evaluate data requirements before training","Define data quality requirements according to the intended use, assess before training whether the data meets them, and supplement the data or revisit the use if not","Securing data volume and diversity suffices, and filling missing values is considered when stores with large errors are identified","Data quality requirements should be fixed to uniform company-wide figures, and need not be set per use"],"eEn":"Define data quality requirements suited to the intended use, assess before training whether data meets them, and fill gaps or revise the use if not. Catching issues at verification, compensating quality with volume, considering fill-in later, or fixing a uniform figure lacks pre-training quality control."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社のAIリスクアセスメントでは、「モデルに偏りがある」と書かれた項目だけが並び、それが誰にどんな結果をもたらすかや、起こりやすさの記述がありません。リスクアセスメントの進め方として最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["リスク源を列挙したうえで結果の重大さを分析すれば足り、起こりやすさの推定は情報が不確実なので影響評価の段階に回す","リスクの大きさは起こりやすさだけで決まり、結果の重大さは影響評価で扱うので、リスクアセスメントでは分析しない","リスク源を特定したうえで、起こり得る結果と起こりやすさを分析し、リスク基準に照らして評価する","リスクの分析は行うが、評価は受容のリスク基準ではなく過去の他社の事故件数との比較で行えば足りる"],"a":2,"e":"リスク源を特定したうえで、起こり得る結果と起こりやすさを分析し、リスク基準に照らして評価します。起こりやすさを影響評価に回す扱い、結果の重大さを影響評価に回す扱い、他社の事故件数と比較する扱いは、リスクアセスメント自身が結果と起こりやすさを分析しリスク基準で評価するという構成を欠きます。","qEn":"A company's AI risk assessment contains only items like 'the model is biased,' with no description of who would suffer what consequences or how likely it is. What is the most appropriate revision of how the risk assessment proceeds?","oEn":["After listing risk sources it suffices to analyze consequence severity, and likelihood estimation is deferred to the impact assessment because information is uncertain","Risk magnitude depends only on likelihood, and consequence severity is handled in the impact assessment, so it is not analyzed in risk assessment","After identifying risk sources, analyze the possible consequences and their likelihood, and evaluate them against the risk criteria","Perform risk analysis but evaluate by comparison with other companies' past incident counts rather than risk acceptance criteria"],"eEn":"Identify risk sources, analyze possible consequences and likelihood and evaluate them against risk criteria. Deferring likelihood or consequence to the impact assessment, or comparing with other firms' incident counts, lacks the structure in which the risk assessment itself analyzes both and evaluates against risk criteria."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社のリスク評価の担当者は、リスクが「高」と評価された項目を、どの順に対応するかを決めかねています。評価の目的として、リスク評価（risk evaluation）の役割を踏まえた最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["リスク評価はリスクの発生可能性を数値化する工程であり、対応の要否や優先順位を判断する工程には含まれない","高と評価された項目は金額が大きい順に、リスク基準との比較をせず一律に同じ水準の管理策を適用する","リスク評価は優先順位の決定に使うが、受容できるかどうかの判断はリスク対応の段階で改めて行うので、評価の段階では行わない","分析で得られたリスクのレベルをリスク基準と比較し、受容できるか、対応が必要かどうかを判断して、対応の優先順位を決定する"],"a":3,"e":"リスク評価では、分析で得たリスクのレベルをリスク基準と比較し、受容できるか、対応が必要かを判断して、対応の優先順位を決めます。発生可能性の数値化に限る扱い、基準との比較なしに一律の管理策を適用する扱い、受容の判断を対応の段階に回す扱いは、評価の役割を取り違えています。","qEn":"A risk assessor is unsure in which order to handle the items rated 'high.' Given the role of risk evaluation, what is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["Risk evaluation is the step of quantifying likelihood and does not include judging the need or priority of treatment","Apply the same level of controls uniformly to items rated high in order of monetary size without comparing against risk criteria","Risk evaluation is used to set priority, but judging acceptability is done at the treatment stage and not at evaluation","Compare the risk levels obtained in analysis with the risk criteria, judge whether they are acceptable or need treatment, and set treatment priorities"],"eEn":"Risk evaluation compares the risk level from analysis with the risk criteria, judges whether it is acceptable or needs treatment, and sets treatment priorities. Limiting to likelihood quantification, applying uniform controls without comparison, or deferring acceptability to treatment misreads the role of evaluation."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある自治体が、効果は限定的ですが誤認による住民への重大な不利益の可能性が高い顔認識AIの導入を検討しています。リスク対応の選択肢の観点で、最も適切な判断はどれですか。","o":["低減しても受容基準を超えるなら、そのAI利用を行わない、または中止する回避も選択肢に含めて検討する","リスク対応の選択肢には低減・回避・移転・受容があるが、導入を決めた以上、回避は選べないため低減か移転から選ぶ","重大な不利益の可能性は保険に加入すれば移転できるため、導入を進めたうえで、保険で不利益の問題を解消する","残余リスクを調べたうえで、リスク所有者の承認を後回しにして導入を進め、運用開始後の最初の見直しで承認を得る"],"a":0,"e":"低減しても受容基準を超えるなら、そのAI利用を行わない、または中止する回避も選択肢に含めて検討します。導入を前提とする扱い、保険で解消できるとする扱い、導入後に承認を得る扱いは、回避を含む選択肢の検討と事前の承認を欠きます。","qEn":"A municipality is considering a facial recognition AI whose benefit is limited but which has a high possibility of serious disadvantage to residents through misidentification. From the risk treatment options viewpoint, what is the most appropriate judgment?","oEn":["If the risk still exceeds the acceptance criteria after reduction, consider avoidance, meaning not using or discontinuing that AI use, among the options","Treatment options include reduction, avoidance, transfer and acceptance, but since deployment is decided avoidance is unavailable, so choose reduction or transfer","The possibility of serious disadvantage can be transferred by taking out insurance, so proceed and resolve residents' disadvantage through insurance","After examining residual risk, proceed with deployment postponing owner approval until the first review after operation starts"],"eEn":"If risk still exceeds acceptance criteria after reduction, consider avoidance, meaning not using or discontinuing the AI, among the options. Presuming deployment, resolving it by insurance, or approving after launch lacks consideration of options including avoidance and advance approval."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、AIの誤判断で顧客が被る損害に備えて賠償責任保険に加入し、「これでAIの誤判断に関するリスク対応は完了した」と報告しました。リスク対応の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["保険は損害を第三者へ移転する手段であり、移転を選んだ時点でリスク対応は完了し、他の管理策は求められず残余リスクの確認も求められない","保険は損害を第三者と分担する手段で、誤判断の起こりやすさや個人への影響そのものは下げず、他の管理策との併用を検討する必要がある","保険は移転の選択肢に含まれるが、リスク対応の完了は保険金額が損害の見積額を上回った時点で判断できる","保険に加入した場合、誤判断で顧客に生じた損害は補償されるので、顧客への影響の評価は省略できる"],"a":1,"e":"保険は損害を第三者と分担する手段で、誤判断の起こりやすさや個人への影響そのものは下げないため、他の管理策との併用を検討します。移転で完了とする扱い、保険金額で完了を判断する扱い、影響評価を省く扱いは、保険の限界を見落としています。","qEn":"A company took out liability insurance against customer losses from AI misjudgments and reported, 'Risk treatment for AI misjudgment is now complete.' What is the most appropriate point from the risk treatment viewpoint?","oEn":["Insurance transfers loss to a third party, so selecting transfer completes risk treatment with no other controls or residual risk check","Insurance is a means of sharing part of the loss with a third party and does not lower the likelihood of misjudgment or the impact on individuals, so consider using it with other controls","Insurance is a transfer option, and risk treatment is complete once the insured amount exceeds the estimated loss","With insurance, damage to customers from misjudgments is compensated, so the assessment of impact on customers can be omitted"],"eEn":"Insurance shares loss with a third party and does not itself lower the likelihood of misjudgment or impact on individuals, so combine it with other controls. Treating transfer as completion, judging completion by insured amount, or omitting impact assessment overlooks the limits of insurance."},
{"d":"D4","q":"AIリスク対応を実施した後、残余リスクの一部がリスク基準の受容水準を上回っています。担当者は「運用開始が優先なので、このまま受容したことにする」と提案しています。最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["運用開始を優先して担当者が受容し、リスク所有者の承認は運用開始後の定例会議で事後に得れば足りる","追加の対応を検討するが、その結果にかかわらず、運用開始後の最初のマネジメントレビューで受容の可否を経営層が判断する","追加の対応策を検討するか、運用を見直し、それでもなお残る場合はリスク所有者の承認を得たうえで受容の記録を残しておく","受容水準を超えた残余リスクは、内部監査員が受容の可否を判断し、リスク所有者の承認は求められない"],"a":2,"e":"追加の対応を検討するか運用を見直し、それでも残る場合はリスク所有者の承認を得たうえで受容の記録を残します。担当者の受容と事後承認、運用開始後まで判断を持ち越す扱い、内部監査員の判断に委ねる扱いは、運用開始前のリスク所有者の承認を欠きます。","qEn":"After AI risk treatment, some residual risk exceeds the acceptance level in the risk criteria. A staff member proposes, 'Starting operation is the priority, so let's just treat it as accepted.' What is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Prioritize launch by having the staff member accept it, with owner approval obtained afterwards at a regular meeting","Consider additional measures but regardless of results management decides acceptance at the first management review after launch","Consider additional treatment or revise operation, and if risk still remains, obtain the risk owner's approval and record the acceptance","For residual risk above the acceptance level the internal auditor decides acceptance and owner approval is not required"],"eEn":"Consider additional measures or revise operation, and if risk remains obtain the risk owner's approval before recording acceptance. Staff acceptance with later approval, carrying the decision past launch, or leaving it to an internal auditor lacks the risk owner's approval before operation."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、あるAIシステムのリスクを「リスク管理委員会全体」が所有するとして、個人の責任者を置いていません。リスク所有者の考え方として最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["リスクを管理する説明責任と権限を持つ個人または役割をリスク所有者として明確に割り当てる","リスクは委員会の全員が共同で所有するほうが公平であり、特定の個人を割り当てると責任の押し付け合いが生じるため、避ける","リスク所有者は組織内の人員が務めるが、権限は付与せず説明責任のみを負う役割とし、管理策の決定はリスク管理委員会が行う","リスク所有者はリスク対応計画の承認後に、実施を担当する部門の担当者から選任すればよい"],"a":0,"e":"リスクを管理する説明責任と権限を持つ個人または役割をリスク所有者として明確に割り当てます。委員会の共同所有とする扱い、権限なしの説明責任のみとする扱い、計画承認後に選任する扱い、外部の者とする扱いは、リスク対応計画の承認と残余リスクの受容を担える所有者の割当てを欠きます。","qEn":"A company says a 'risk management committee as a whole' owns the risks of an AI system and has placed no individual in charge. What is the most appropriate corrective on the idea of a risk owner?","oEn":["Clearly assign as risk owner an individual or role with the accountability and authority to manage the risk","Joint ownership by all committee members is fairer, and assigning a specific individual would cause blame shifting, so avoid it","The risk owner is an internal person but is given accountability without authority, and the risk committee decides controls","Select the risk owner after approval of the risk treatment plan from staff of the implementing department"],"eEn":"Clearly assign as risk owner an individual or role with accountability and authority to manage the risk. Joint committee ownership, accountability without authority, appointment after plan approval, or an external party lacks an owner able to approve the plan and accept residual risk."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社が与信審査AIの影響評価を行い、評価対象を「申込者本人の経済的利益」だけにしました。AIシステム影響評価の対象範囲として最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["個人だけでなく、特定の集団や社会への潜在的な影響も、権利、安全、公平性などの観点から含めて評価する","影響評価は申込者本人への影響に加え集団間の公平性も対象にするが、社会全体への影響は組織の範囲を超えるため評価の対象としない","影響評価の対象は、AIシステムの導入によって利益を得る側の利害関係者に限られ、不利益を被る側の影響は、評価対象に含めない","社会への影響も評価の対象に含めるが、権利と安全に関する影響に限り、公平性に関する影響はリスクアセスメントで扱う"],"a":0,"e":"個人だけでなく、特定の集団や社会への潜在的な影響も、権利、安全、公平性などの観点から含めて評価します。社会全体への影響を除く扱い、利益を得る側に限る扱い、数値で表せるものに限る扱い、公平性をリスクアセスメントに回す扱いは、影響評価の対象範囲を狭めます。","qEn":"A company assessed the impact of its credit-screening AI but limited the subject to 'the applicant's own financial interest.' What is the most appropriate revision of the scope of AI system impact assessment?","oEn":["Include potential impacts not only on individuals but also on specific groups and society, from viewpoints such as rights, safety and fairness","Include fairness between groups as well as the applicant's own impact, but exclude societal impact as beyond the organization's scope","The subject of impact assessment is limited to interested parties who benefit from introduction, and effects on those who suffer disadvantage are excluded","Include societal impact but only on rights and safety, with fairness impacts handled in the risk assessment"],"eEn":"Assess potential impacts not only on individuals but also on specific groups and society, from viewpoints such as rights, safety and fairness. Excluding societal impact, limiting to beneficiaries or quantifiable effects, or moving fairness to the risk assessment narrows the impact assessment scope."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムを本番に展開してから数か月後に初めて影響評価を実施しようとしています。影響評価の実施時期として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["影響評価は、本番での実績データが蓄積してから行うほうが正確なので、展開前には実施せず、数か月の運用後に一度だけ行えばよい","重大な影響を設計や展開の判断に反映できるよう、展開前から実施し、変更や運用の状況に応じて見直す","影響評価は設計時には簡易に行い、展開後の最初の内部監査で詳細に実施すれば、重大な影響の反映は間に合う","影響評価は展開の直前に一度実施すれば、以後の機能変更や用途の拡大があっても、再実施は求められない"],"a":1,"e":"重大な影響を設計や展開の判断に反映できるよう、展開前から実施し、変更や運用の状況に応じて見直します。展開後の実績を待つ扱い、展開後の内部監査で詳細化する扱い、直前に一度だけ行う扱いは、展開判断への反映を欠きます。","qEn":"A company is about to perform an impact assessment for the first time several months after deploying an AI system to production. What is the most appropriate point about the timing of impact assessment?","oEn":["Impact assessment is more accurate after production data accumulates, so skip it before deployment and do it once only after several months of operation","Perform it from before deployment so significant impacts can be reflected in design and deployment decisions, and revisit it as changes and operations warrant","Perform a light impact assessment at design and a detailed one at the first internal audit after deployment, which is in time to reflect significant impacts","Impact assessment once just before deployment suffices, and redoing it is not required even if functions change or use expands afterward"],"eEn":"Conduct the impact assessment from before deployment so significant impacts feed design and deployment decisions, and review it as changes and operations require. Waiting for post-deployment data, detailing at a later audit, or doing it once just before deployment fails to inform the deployment decision."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、AIシステムの影響評価で、意図した用途での影響だけを検討し、利用者が想定外の使い方をした場合の影響は検討していません。影響評価の観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["想定外の使い方は利用者の責任であり、提供者が検討すると、かえって誤用を助長するため、意図した用途の範囲だけを評価する","誤用の影響は意図した用途の評価が完了した後の運用段階で、利用状況の監視結果をもとに評価すればよい","意図した用途に加え、合理的に予見できる誤用や想定外の使い方がもたらし得る影響も、評価の対象に含める","合理的に予見できる誤用であっても、利用規約で禁止していれば、その影響の評価は、不要になる"],"a":2,"e":"意図した用途に加え、合理的に予見できる誤用や想定外の使い方がもたらし得る影響も、評価の対象に含めます。利用者の責任とする扱い、運用段階の監視結果を待つ扱い、利用規約での禁止で評価を省く扱いは、予見可能な誤用の事前の評価を欠きます。","qEn":"In an AI system impact assessment, a company considered only impacts under the intended use and not impacts when users use it in unexpected ways. From the impact assessment viewpoint, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Unexpected use is the user's responsibility, and the provider considering it would encourage misuse, so assess only the intended use","Assess the effects of misuse in the operation stage after the intended-use assessment, based on usage monitoring results","Include in the assessment, beyond the intended use, the impacts that reasonably foreseeable misuse or unexpected uses could cause","Even reasonably foreseeable misuse needs no impact assessment if prohibited in the terms of use"],"eEn":"Include in the assessment, besides the intended use, impacts that reasonably foreseeable misuse or unexpected use could cause. Treating it as the user's responsibility, waiting for operational monitoring, or skipping it because terms prohibit it lacks advance assessment of foreseeable misuse."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、AIシステム影響評価の結果を独立した報告書として保管しただけで、リスクアセスメントやリスク対応には使っていません。影響評価とリスクマネジメントの関係として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["影響評価とリスクアセスメントは別の工程であり、結果の反映は内部監査の指摘があった場合に限って行い、通常は独立して実施する","影響評価の結果は、利害関係者への説明資料としてのみ使うものであり、管理策の選択や設計判断には用いない","影響評価の結果は管理策の選択には用いるが、リスクの特定・評価には用いない","影響評価の結果は、リスクの特定・評価やリスク対応、管理策の選択に反映し、結果を活用する必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"影響評価の結果は、リスクの特定・評価やリスク対応、管理策の選択に反映し、結果を活用します。独立した工程として監査の指摘があるまで反映しない扱い、管理策の選択にだけ使う扱い、説明資料にとどめる扱い、リスク対応計画に含めない扱いは、影響評価とリスクマネジメントの連携を欠きます。","qEn":"A company only stored its AI system impact assessment results as a separate report and did not use them in risk assessment or risk treatment. What is the most appropriate point about the relationship between impact assessment and risk management?","oEn":["Impact assessment and risk assessment are separate steps and results are reflected only when internal audit points it out, normally running independently","Impact assessment results are used only as explanatory material for interested parties and not for control selection or design decisions","Use impact assessment results to select controls but not for risk identification or evaluation","Impact assessment results should be reflected in risk identification and evaluation, risk treatment and control selection, and put to use"],"eEn":"Reflect impact assessment results in risk identification and evaluation, risk treatment and control selection. Running independently until an audit points it out, using it only for control selection, keeping it as explanatory material, or leaving it out of the treatment plan lacks the link between impact assessment and risk management."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、社内の文書要約にだけ使う軽微なAIツールについて、「影響は小さいから影響評価は不要」と判断し、評価した記録も残していません。影響評価の扱いとして最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["影響評価の深さは影響の大きさに比例させてよいが、影響が小さいと判断した根拠も評価として記録する","影響が小さいAIには影響評価に代えて軽微な利用の届出を求めれば足り、影響が小さいと判断した根拠の記録はリスクアセスメントの側に残す","影響が小さいと考える場合でも、重大な影響があるAIと全く同じ深さと様式で、評価を実施しなければならない","既存の外部ツールの利用は提供者が評価しているため、自社では評価を行わず、導入の判断を稟議で承認すれば足りる"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価の深さは影響の大きさに比例させてよいものの、影響が小さいと判断した根拠も評価として記録します。届出で代える扱い、提供者の評価に依拠して自社では評価しない扱い、重大なAIと全く同じ深さを求める扱いはいずれも、根拠を記録した比例的な評価という考え方に合いません。","qEn":"For a minor AI tool used only for internal document summarization, a company judged 'impact is small, so impact assessment is unnecessary' and left no record of the assessment. What is the most appropriate point about handling impact assessment?","oEn":["The depth of impact assessment may be proportionate to the size of impact, but the grounds for judging impact small should also be recorded as an assessment","For low-impact AI, a light usage notification replaces impact assessment, and the rationale for judging impact low is recorded on the risk assessment side","Even where impact is thought small, assessment must be done at exactly the same depth and format as for AI with serious impact","Use of an existing external tool is assessed by its provider, so no in-house assessment is needed and approval of introduction by internal sign-off suffices"],"eEn":"The depth of impact assessment may be proportionate to impact, but the rationale for judging impact small is also recorded as an assessment. Replacing it with a notification, relying on the provider's assessment, or demanding identical depth to significant AI all depart from proportionate assessment with a recorded rationale."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社が、外部ベンダーの基盤モデルを組み込んだサービスのAIリスクアセスメントを行っています。ベンダーが提供する情報は限られています。リスク特定の観点で、最も適切な進め方はどれですか。","o":["ベンダーのモデルの内部は自社の管理外なので、その部分のリスクは評価の対象外とし、自社で開発した部分のリスクだけを評価する","ベンダー提供の情報の範囲と限界を把握し、第三者のモデルに依存することで生じるリスクを特定して、契約や追加の検証などで補う","ベンダーが提供する情報の範囲で評価し、情報が限られる部分はベンダーの認証や公表資料があることを根拠に、リスクが低いものとして扱う","ベンダー依存のリスクは契約に免責条項を入れて責任を移転できるので、リスクの特定は自社が開発した部分に絞る"],"a":1,"e":"ベンダー提供の情報の範囲と限界を把握し、第三者のモデルに依存することで生じるリスクを特定して、契約や追加の検証などで補います。モデルの内部を評価対象外とする扱い、認証や公表資料だけを根拠に低リスクとする扱い、免責条項で消滅するとして特定を自社部分に絞る扱いは、依存リスクの特定を欠きます。","qEn":"A company is performing an AI risk assessment of a service embedding a foundation model from an external vendor, and the vendor provides limited information. From the risk identification viewpoint, what is the most appropriate way to proceed?","oEn":["The vendor model's inside is outside the company's control, so exclude that part's risk from assessment and assess only the parts the company developed","Grasp the scope and limits of the vendor-provided information, identify risks arising from dependence on a third party's model, and compensate through contracts or additional verification","Assess within the information the vendor provides and treat the limited-information parts as low risk on the basis of the vendor's certification or published materials","Vendor dependency risk can be transferred by an exculpatory clause, so restrict risk identification to the self-developed parts"],"eEn":"Grasp the scope and limits of vendor-provided information, identify risks arising from reliance on a third-party model, and compensate through contracts and additional verification. Excluding the model internals, treating it as low risk on certifications, or restricting identification to own parts because of an exculpatory clause lacks identification of dependency risk."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある法律事務所が、生成AIで契約書の草案を作成させ、AIが存在しない判例を引用する誤りが見つかりました。AIリスクの特定と対応の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["プロンプトの工夫で誤りを減らせるので、プロンプトの書き方の研修を管理策とし、出力の根拠の検証手順は設けない","個別の事案として当該契約書の誤りだけを修正し、生成AIの利用に関するリスクとしての特定や管理策の見直しは、同様の事案が複数回起きた場合に行う","もっともらしい誤りを出し得ることをリスク源として特定し、専門家の確認や出力の根拠の検証手順を管理策に含める","出力を第二の生成AIで再検証する仕組みを管理策とし、専門家の確認は誤りが検出されなかった案件では省略する"],"a":2,"e":"もっともらしい誤りを出し得ることをリスク源として特定し、専門家の確認や出力の根拠の検証手順を管理策に含めます。研修だけに頼る扱い、複数回の発生を待つ扱い、別の生成AIによる再検証に頼って専門家の確認を省く扱いは、存在しない判例のような誤りを人が検証する管理策を欠きます。","qEn":"A law firm had generative AI draft contracts and found the AI cited non-existent precedents. From the viewpoint of AI risk identification and treatment, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Prompt techniques reduce errors, so make prompt writing training the control and set no procedure to verify the basis of outputs","Correct only the faulty contract as an individual case and identify the risk and review controls only if similar cases occur several times","Identify as a risk source that the AI can produce plausible errors, and include mandatory expert review and procedures to verify the basis of outputs in the controls","Make re-verification of outputs by a second generative AI the control and skip expert review for cases where no error is detected"],"eEn":"Identify the possibility of plausible errors as a risk source and include expert review and procedures to verify the basis of outputs among controls. Relying on training, waiting for repeated cases, or relying on another generative AI while skipping expert review lacks human verification of errors like nonexistent precedents."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社がAIリスク基準を新たに定めます。担当者は「財務上の損失の大きさ」だけを基準に書こうとしています。リスク基準の定め方として最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["リスク基準は財務上の損失の大きさだけで定めたほうが客観的であるため、個人や社会への影響は、基準に含めずに別の説明資料にまとめる","リスク基準は業界団体が公表する標準的な基準値を採用すればよく、組織の目的や利害関係者の見方は基準の設定では考慮しない","リスク基準は組織として統一するが、見直しは認証の更新時にだけ行い、事業環境や法規制が変わっても改訂しない","組織の目的に加え、個人や社会への影響、法的要求、利害関係者の見方も考慮して、受容できるリスクの水準を定める"],"a":3,"e":"組織の目的に加え、個人や社会への影響、法的要求、利害関係者の見方も考慮して、受容できるリスクの水準を定めます。財務損失だけに限る扱い、外部の標準値を丸ごと採用する扱い、更新時以外に改訂しない扱いは、基準の設定と維持の考え方を欠きます。担当者が都度設定する扱いも誤りです。","qEn":"A company will newly set AI risk criteria, and the staff member intends to write them solely on 'size of financial loss.' What is the most appropriate revision of how risk criteria are set?","oEn":["Setting criteria by financial loss alone is more objective, so leave impacts on individuals and society out of the criteria and put them in separate explanatory materials","Adopt standard values published by an industry body as risk criteria, without considering the organization's objectives or stakeholder views","Unify risk criteria organization-wide but revise them only at certification renewal, not when business conditions or regulations change","Set the acceptable level of risk considering, in addition to organizational objectives, impacts on individuals and society, legal requirements and interested parties' views"],"eEn":"Define the acceptable level of risk considering, besides the organization's objectives, impact on individuals and society, legal requirements and stakeholder views. Limiting to financial loss, adopting external standard values wholesale, or revising only at renewal lacks the approach to setting and maintaining criteria. Per-assessment staff setting is also wrong."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、顧客のサポート履歴をAIの学習に使うにあたり、個人情報の漏えいや再識別のリスクを評価していません。AIリスクアセスメントの観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["学習データに起因するプライバシー上のリスクを特定して評価し、データの最小化や匿名化などの管理策を検討する","個人情報の保護は法務部門の領域であり、AIリスクアセスメントの対象は、モデルの精度に関するリスクだけに限る","学習済みモデルからの再識別は理論上の懸念にとどまるため、学習データそのものの保管時の漏えいに限ってセキュリティ部門が評価すれば足りる","プライバシーのリスクは学習の完了後にモデルの検証と同時に評価すれば足り、学習前のデータの最小化や匿名化の検討は求められない"],"a":0,"e":"学習データに起因するプライバシー上のリスクを特定して評価し、データの最小化や匿名化などの管理策を検討します。モデルの精度だけに限る扱い、保管時の漏えいだけを見る扱い、学習後に評価する扱いは、学習前に再識別のリスクを評価し管理策を検討するという要求を欠きます。","qEn":"In using customer support history for AI training, a company has not assessed the risk of personal data leakage or re-identification. From the AI risk assessment viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Identify and evaluate privacy risks arising from training data, and consider controls such as data minimization and anonymization","Personal data protection is the legal department's domain, so limit the AI risk assessment to risks about model accuracy","Re-identification from the trained model is only theoretical, so the security department need only assess leakage of the stored training data","Privacy risk can be assessed after training together with model validation, and considering data minimization or anonymization before training is not required"],"eEn":"Identify and assess privacy risks arising from training data and consider controls such as data minimization and anonymization. Limiting to model accuracy, looking only at storage leakage, or assessing after training lacks assessing re-identification risk and considering controls before training."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある配信サービスのレコメンドAIは、利用者の反応を学習し続けた結果、似た内容ばかりを提示するようになり、利用者の視野が狭まる懸念が出ています。リスクの観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["利用者の反応に基づく学習は満足度の指標で評価できるので、満足度が下がらない限り、偏りの強まりをリスクとして特定する必要はない","出力が次の入力値を変える循環によって偏りが強まっていくリスクとして特定し、多様性などの指標を継続的に監視して見直す必要がある","偏りの強まりは、モデルの初期の学習データに原因があるはずなので、運用中の監視ではなく、初期データの再収集だけで対処する","多様性の指標は測定するが、出力の傾向の見直しは年次のモデル更新時にまとめて行えば足り、運用中の継続的な監視までは必要ない"],"a":1,"e":"出力が次の入力を変える循環によって偏りが強まるリスクとして特定し、多様性などの指標を継続的に監視して見直します。満足度だけで判断する扱い、初期データの再収集だけで対処する扱い、年次の更新時にまとめて見直す扱いは、運用中に偏りが強まる循環を継続的に把握することを欠きます。","qEn":"A streaming service's recommendation AI, which keeps learning from user reactions, has begun presenting only similar content, raising concern that users' horizons narrow. From the risk viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Learning from user responses can be judged by satisfaction metrics, so bias reinforcement need not be identified as a risk unless satisfaction falls","Identify as a risk the strengthening of bias through a loop where outputs change the next inputs, and continually monitor and review indicators such as diversity","Strengthening bias must stem from the model's initial training data, so handle it only by recollecting initial data, not by monitoring in operation","Measure diversity metrics but review output trends at the annual model update, with continuous monitoring in operation not needed"],"eEn":"Identify the risk of bias intensifying through a loop in which outputs change the next inputs, and continuously monitor and review diversity and similar indicators. Judging by satisfaction, recollecting initial data only, or reviewing once a year lacks continuous grasp of the loop during operation."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、採用AIの影響評価を社内の技術者だけで行い、影響を受ける求職者や支援団体の見方を取り入れていません。影響評価の質を高める観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["意見は聞くが、影響を受ける側の意見は技術的な根拠に乏しいため参考情報にとどめ、評価の結論には反映しない","利害関係者の意見は評価の結果を公表した後の意見募集で聞けば足り、評価の段階では技術者の判断で進めてよい","影響を受ける個人や集団の代表、関連分野の専門家など、多様な視点からの意見を評価に取り入れる","意見聴取は行うが、対象は社内の人事部門と法務部門に限り、求職者や支援団体のような外部の視点は取り入れない"],"a":2,"e":"影響を受ける個人や集団の代表、関連分野の専門家など、多様な視点からの意見を評価に取り入れます。意見を結論に反映しない扱い、公表後に聞く扱い、社内部門に限る扱い、技術者のみで完結させる扱いは、影響を受ける側の視点を評価の中に取り入れることを欠きます。","qEn":"A company performed its hiring AI impact assessment only with in-house engineers, without taking in views of affected job seekers or support organizations. From the viewpoint of improving assessment quality, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Listen to opinions but treat those of affected parties as reference lacking technical basis and do not reflect them in the conclusion","Stakeholder opinions can be gathered in a consultation after publishing the results, with the assessment itself proceeding on technicians' judgment","Take into the assessment views from diverse perspectives, such as representatives of affected individuals and groups and experts in related fields","Gather opinions but only from internal HR and legal departments, without external viewpoints such as job applicants or support groups"],"eEn":"Bring opinions from diverse perspectives into the assessment, such as representatives of affected individuals and groups and experts in related fields. Not reflecting opinions in the conclusion, asking after publication, limiting to internal departments, or relying on engineers alone lacks bringing affected parties' perspectives into the assessment."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、導入時に作成したAIリスク登録簿を更新しないまま、重大なインシデントと新たな法規制の施行を経験しました。リスクアセスメントの見直しの契機として、最も適切な考え方はどれですか。","o":["リスク登録簿は導入時の状態を維持するものなので、インシデントや法規制の変化があっても、次の更新審査まで再評価はしない","再評価はAIモデルを変更した場合にのみ必要であり、インシデントや法規制の変化は、再評価の契機にならない","再評価は計画した間隔でのみ行えばよく、インシデントや法規制の変化が間隔の途中で生じた場合は次の計画日まで待つ","計画した間隔に加えて、インシデント、重大な変更、法規制や利用状況の変化などをきっかけに、リスクを再評価する必要がある"],"a":3,"e":"計画した間隔に加え、インシデント、重大な変更、法規制や利用状況の変化などをきっかけに、リスクを再評価します。次の更新審査まで待つ扱い、モデル変更時に限る扱い、次の計画日まで待つ扱い、損害確定後に一度だけ行う扱いは、再評価の契機を狭めます。","qEn":"A company experienced a serious incident and the enforcement of new regulation without updating the AI risk register created at introduction. What is the most appropriate thinking about triggers for revisiting risk assessment?","oEn":["The risk register preserves the state at introduction, so do not reassess even after incidents or regulatory changes until the next renewal audit","Reassessment is needed only when the AI model is changed, and incidents or regulatory changes are not triggers for reassessment","Reassess only at planned intervals and wait until the next scheduled date if incidents or regulatory changes occur in between","Besides planned intervals, reassess risks when triggered by incidents, significant changes, and changes in regulations or usage"],"eEn":"Reassess risk at planned intervals and also when triggered by incidents, significant changes, or changes in regulation or usage. Waiting for the renewal audit, limiting to model changes, waiting for the next scheduled date, or doing it once after damage is fixed narrows the triggers for reassessment."},
{"d":"D4","q":"AIリスクマネジメントの具体的な進め方に迷った担当者が、ISO/IEC 23894を参照しようとしています。ISO/IEC 42001との関係を踏まえた位置づけとして、最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["23894は42001の要求事項の一部であり、42001の認証を取得するには、23894の全項目を満たしていることの審査を別に受ける","23894はAIリスクマネジメントの指針で、42001のリスクアセスメントと対応の進め方を考える際の参考にできるガイダンス文書である","23894は42001の附属書として位置づけられ、42001の認証範囲に含まれるため、42001と別に参照する必要はない","23894は一般的なリスクマネジメントの原則を示す指針で、AI特有のリスクには触れないため、AI固有のリスクの検討には参考にならない"],"a":1,"e":"23894はAIリスクマネジメントの指針で、42001のリスクアセスメントと対応の進め方を考える際の参考にできるガイダンス文書です。42001の要求事項の一部とする扱い、附属書として認証範囲に含まれるとする扱い、一般的な原則でAI固有のリスクに触れないとする扱いは、いずれも文書の位置づけを取り違えています。","qEn":"A staff member unsure how to concretely proceed with AI risk management plans to refer to ISO/IEC 23894. Given its relationship with ISO/IEC 42001, what is the most appropriate positioning?","oEn":["23894 is part of 42001's requirements, and to obtain 42001 certification one separately undergoes an audit of satisfying all items of 23894","23894 is guidance on AI risk management that can serve as a reference when working out how to conduct 42001's risk assessment and treatment","23894 is positioned as an annex of 42001 and falls within its certification scope, so it need not be referred to separately","23894 sets general risk management principles without touching AI-specific risk, so it is no help in considering AI-specific risks"],"eEn":"23894 is guidance on AI risk management and can be used as a reference when considering how to carry out 42001 risk assessment and treatment. Treating it as part of 42001's requirements, as an annex within certification scope, or as general principles untouched by AI-specific risk all misjudge its position."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある会社は、管理策の導入後に再評価したところ残余リスクは「中」でしたが、報告書には導入前のリスクの「高」だけを載せました。リスクの報告の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["報告は導入後の残余リスクだけを示せばよく、管理策の導入前のリスクの水準は、管理策の効果を示す必要がないので記載しない","残余リスクは、管理策の効果が確認されても、報告の対象ではなく、内部の記録にとどめておく","管理策の導入前のリスクと導入後の残余リスクを区別して示し、残余リスクの受容の状況も報告する","導入前後のリスクは区別して示すが、残余リスクの受容は担当者の判断で足りるため、受容の状況の報告は求められない"],"a":2,"e":"管理策の導入前のリスクと導入後の残余リスクを区別して示し、残余リスクの受容の状況も報告します。導入前だけを報告する扱い、導入後だけを報告する扱い、残余リスクを内部の記録にとどめる扱い、受容の報告を省く扱い、「中」に統一する扱いは、管理策の効果と受容の状況を正確に伝える報告になりません。","qEn":"After controls were introduced and risk reassessed, residual risk was 'medium,' but the company's report listed only the pre-control risk of 'high.' From the risk reporting viewpoint, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Report only the post-implementation residual risk and omit the pre-control level since showing the control effect is unnecessary","Residual risk is not a subject of reporting even when control effectiveness is confirmed, and is kept in internal records","Show the pre-control risk and the post-control residual risk separately, and also report the status of accepting the residual risk","Show pre- and post-control risk separately, but acceptance of residual risk is the staff member's call, so reporting acceptance status is unnecessary"],"eEn":"Show the risk before controls and the residual risk after them separately, and also report the status of residual risk acceptance. Reporting only before-control risk, only after-control risk, keeping residual risk internal, omitting the acceptance report, or unifying to 'medium' does not accurately convey control effect and acceptance status."},
{"d":"D4","q":"新しい種類のAIの導入で、過去のデータが乏しく、起こりやすさを数値で見積もれません。担当者は「数値化できないのでリスク分析は実施できない」と主張しています。リスク分析の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["数値化できないリスクは分析を保留して暫定的に低リスクとして扱い、運用で十分なデータが得られた段階で初めて分析する","数値化できないリスクは類似するAIの他社事例の数値を借りて定量的に見積もり、見積りの根拠の記録は省いてよい","不確実性は分析の信頼性を損なうため、定性的な尺度の使用は規格上認められず、数値化できないリスクは評価対象から外す","定性的な尺度を用い、見積りの根拠と不確実性を記録したうえで分析を行い、運用で得た知見で見直す"],"a":3,"e":"定性的な尺度を用い、見積りの根拠と不確実性を記録したうえで分析を行い、運用で得た知見で見直します。分析を保留して低リスク扱いにする扱い、他社の数値を借りて根拠を記録しない扱い、導入の無期限延期、定性的な尺度を認めない扱いは、不確実性を記録しつつ分析を進めるという考え方を欠きます。","qEn":"For a new type of AI with scarce past data, likelihood cannot be estimated numerically. The staff member argues, 'We cannot quantify it, so risk analysis cannot be done.' From the risk analysis viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Hold analysis of unquantifiable risks and treat them provisionally as low, analyzing only when operation yields enough data","Estimate unquantifiable risks quantitatively by borrowing figures from other companies' similar AI and omit recording the basis","Uncertainty undermines analysis reliability, so qualitative scales are not permitted by the standard and unquantifiable risks are excluded","Use qualitative scales, record the basis of estimates and uncertainty, perform the analysis, and revise it with knowledge gained in operation"],"eEn":"Use qualitative scales, record the basis of estimates and uncertainty, perform the analysis and revise it with knowledge gained in operation. Holding analysis and treating risk as low, borrowing figures without recording the basis, indefinite postponement, or rejecting qualitative scales lacks analyzing while recording uncertainty."},
{"d":"D4","q":"ある銀行は、与信AIの出力を担当者が最終承認する運用をリスク対応として挙げていますが、担当者は件数が多く、ほとんどAIの出力をそのまま承認しています。リスク対応の有効性の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["人が最終承認する運用を採用している以上、リスク対応は有効であり、実際にどの程度確認されているかの測定は、必要がない","件数が多い場合は確認者を増員すれば承認の実質が確保されるので、確認の実質の測定は求められない","承認の記録が残っていれば有効性の証拠として足り、審査時間や覆した割合のような実質の測定は、内部監査の指摘があった場合に行う","人による確認が形骸化して有効でない可能性があるため、確認の実質（審査時間、覆した割合）を測定し、体制や手順を見直す"],"a":3,"e":"人による確認が形骸化して有効でない可能性があるため、確認の実質（審査時間、覆した割合）を測定し、体制や手順を見直します。採用しただけで有効とする扱い、増員すれば足りるとする扱い、承認の記録を有効性の証拠とする扱いは、リスク対応の有効性を実績で確かめることを欠きます。","qEn":"A bank lists final approval by staff of the credit AI's output as risk treatment, but staff, facing high volume, mostly approve AI outputs as they are. From the viewpoint of risk treatment effectiveness, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["As long as human final approval is adopted, the risk treatment is effective, and there is no need to measure how much real checking happens","If volume is high, adding reviewers secures substantive approval, so measuring the substance of review is unnecessary","Approval records suffice as evidence of effectiveness, and measuring substance such as review time or override rate is done only if internal audit raises it","Human review may have become a formality and ineffective, so measure its substance (review time, rate of overriding, etc.) and revise structure and procedures"],"eEn":"Because human review may have become a formality, measure its substance (review time, override rate) and revise structure and procedures. Treating adoption as effective, adding reviewers, or regarding approval records as proof lacks verifying effectiveness of risk treatment through actual results."},
{"d":"D4","q":"情報セキュリティのリスクアセスメントを毎年実施している会社が、「同じ手順でAIのリスクも評価済みだ」と述べています。AIリスクアセスメントとの違いを踏まえた最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["セキュリティ中心の評価ではバイアス、透明性、人への影響などAI固有のリスク源や結果が捉えきれず、AIの観点を追加する","情報セキュリティの評価手順を流用してよく、AI固有のリスクはその評価の補足資料として添付すれば、AIリスクアセスメントとして扱える","AIのリスクアセスメントは、AIシステムの機密性・完全性・可用性の三つの観点だけを評価すれば足りる","セキュリティの評価結果の流用は認められるが、リスク基準はAIの場合にも同一にすべきで、AI固有の基準を新たに設けることは認められない"],"a":0,"e":"セキュリティ中心の評価ではバイアス、透明性、人への影響などAI固有のリスク源や結果が捉えきれないため、AIの観点を追加します。包含されるとして自動的に評価されるとみなす扱い、補足資料の添付で済ませる扱い、機密性・完全性・可用性だけで足りるとする扱い、AI固有の基準を認めない扱いは、AI固有の評価を欠きます。","qEn":"A company that conducts information security risk assessments every year says, 'The same procedure has already assessed AI risks.' Given the difference from AI risk assessment, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["A security-centered assessment cannot capture AI-specific risk sources and consequences such as bias, transparency and impact on people, so add AI viewpoints to the assessment","The security assessment procedure may be reused, and attaching AI-specific risks as supplementary material lets it be treated as the AI risk assessment","AI risk assessment need only evaluate the three viewpoints of confidentiality, integrity and availability of the AI system","Reuse of security assessment results is allowed, but risk criteria must be identical for AI and AI-specific criteria may not be added"],"eEn":"A security-centered assessment cannot capture AI-specific risk sources and consequences such as bias, transparency and impact on people, so AI viewpoints are added. Assuming inclusion, attaching supplementary material, relying on confidentiality, integrity and availability alone, or forbidding AI-specific criteria lacks AI-specific assessment."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社のAIMS推進室が、運用の記録は十分に取っているものの、その記録を評価して計画や目的に反映する仕組みがなく、同じ問題が繰り返されています。PDCAの観点で、最も不足している段階はどれですか。","o":["Plan（計画）の段階であり、記録をさらに詳細に取れば、評価や改善の仕組みがなくても、問題の繰り返しは自然に解消される","Check（評価）からAct（改善）、Plan（計画）への流れで、結果を分析・評価して改善と見直しにつなげる段階","Do（実行）の段階であり、運用の頻度を上げれば、分析・評価の仕組みがなくても、同じ問題は繰り返されなくなる","是正処置の迅速化が不足しており、不適合が発生するたびに速やかに対処する仕組みを整えれば、評価結果を計画や目的に反映する仕組みがなくても繰り返しは防げる"],"a":1,"e":"記録は取れているのに評価と改善に結びついていないため、不足しているのはCheck（評価）からAct（改善）、Plan（計画）への流れです。記録を詳細にする、運用の頻度を上げる、個別の事象への対処を速める対応は、いずれも結果を分析・評価して計画や目的に反映するという流れを欠きます。","qEn":"A company's AIMS office keeps sufficient operation records but has no mechanism to evaluate them and reflect the results in plans and objectives, so the same problems recur. From the PDCA viewpoint, which stage is most lacking?","oEn":["The Plan stage; recording in more detail will naturally stop the same problems recurring even without evaluation and improvement mechanisms","The Check-to-Act-to-Plan flow that turns evaluated results into improvement and re-planning","The Do stage; raising operation frequency will stop the same problems recurring even without analysis and evaluation mechanisms","Corrective action speed is lacking, and a mechanism to respond promptly to each nonconformity prevents repeats even without a mechanism to reflect evaluation results in plans and objectives"],"eEn":"Records are being kept but not linked to evaluation and improvement, so what is lacking is the flow from Check to Act and Plan. More detailed records, higher operating frequency, or faster reaction to individual events all lack the flow of analyzing results and reflecting them in plans and objectives."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、AIMSの指標として「実施したAI研修の回数」を報告していますが、AIの運用ミスは減っていません。パフォーマンス評価の観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["研修の回数は力量の向上と相関するため、研修の満足度アンケートの点数を指標に加えれば、有効性を十分に把握できる","運用ミスの件数は外部要因に左右されるため、指標としては不適切であり、実施した活動の量だけを報告する","研修の回数に加え、研修後の力量の向上や運用ミスの件数の変化など、目的の達成度や有効性を示す指標を測定しておく","指標は変更できるが、変更は認証の更新審査の際に限られるので、次の更新審査まで現在の指標で報告を続ける"],"a":2,"e":"研修の回数に加え、研修後の力量や運用ミスの件数の変化など、目的の達成度や有効性を示す指標を測定します。満足度の点数を足す扱い、活動量だけを報告する扱い、更新審査まで指標を変えない扱いは、いずれも実際の有効性を示しません。","qEn":"A company reports 'number of AI training sessions held' as an AIMS indicator, yet AI operating errors have not decreased. From the performance evaluation viewpoint, what is the most appropriate revision?","oEn":["Training counts correlate with competence, so adding satisfaction survey scores gives enough grasp of effectiveness","Error counts depend on external factors so they are unsuitable as an indicator; report only the volume of activities performed","Also measure indicators of effectiveness, such as post-training competence and changes in error counts","Indicators can be changed, but only at certification renewal, so continue reporting with the current indicator until the next renewal"],"eEn":"In addition to training counts, measure indicators of achievement and effectiveness such as competence after training and changes in operational errors. Adding satisfaction scores, reporting only activity volume, or keeping indicators until renewal does not show actual effectiveness."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社の内部監査で、SoAに「実施済み」とある管理策について、監査員は規程の存在だけを確認して適合と判断しました。実際の運用記録は確認していません。監査の進め方として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["規程の存在に加え、運用記録のサンプルや聞き取りなどの客観的な監査証拠で、実際の運用を確認する","規程の存在に加えて規程の改訂履歴が最新であることを確認できれば、運用記録の確認は被監査部門の自己点検の結果で代替できる","監査証拠は担当者の口頭の説明で足りるので、記録の確認は、被監査者が提示を希望した場合にのみ行う","運用記録の確認は被監査部門の責任者が行い、内部監査員は規程の整備と責任者による確認結果の報告を受けることを監査の範囲とする"],"a":0,"e":"規程の存在に加え、運用記録のサンプルや聞き取りなどの客観的な監査証拠で、実際の運用を確認します。自己点検の結果での代替、責任者の報告を受けるだけの監査、口頭の説明で足りるとする扱い、記録確認を省く扱いは、客観的な監査証拠による確認を欠きます。","qEn":"In a company's internal audit, for a control marked 'implemented' in the SoA, the auditor confirmed only the existence of the procedure and judged it conforming, without checking actual operating records. What is the most appropriate point about how the audit proceeds?","oEn":["Confirm actual operation with objective evidence such as sampled records and interviews, not just the procedure's existence","If the rule exists and its revision history is current, checking operation records can be replaced by the audited department's self-check results","Audit evidence suffices as the staff's oral explanation, and records are checked only if the auditee wishes to present them","The audited department head checks operation records, and the auditor's scope is to confirm the rules exist and receive the head's report"],"eEn":"In addition to the existence of rules, confirm actual operation with objective audit evidence such as sampled operation records and interviews. Substituting self-check results, merely receiving the head's report, relying on oral explanation, or omitting record checks lacks confirmation by objective audit evidence."},
{"d":"D5","q":"内部監査で、AIシステムの監視手順は文書化され実施もされていますが、検出された異常に誰も対応しておらず、目的の達成に結びついていません。この状況の判定として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["管理策が計画どおりに実施されていても有効でない場合は、有効性の観点から不適合として扱い得る","手順が文書化され実施もされている以上、目的の達成に結びついていなくても、適合しており、指摘の対象にはならない","有効性は内部監査の対象ではなく、マネジメントレビューだけで評価する事項なので、内部監査では指摘しない","目的の達成に結びつかない状況は、監査員の個人的な意見にすぎないので、不適合ではなく感想として口頭で伝えるにとどめる"],"a":0,"e":"AIMSは要求事項への適合に加え、有効に実施され維持されていることも確認されます。手順が実施されていても、異常への対応がなく目的の達成に結びつかなければ、有効性の観点から不適合となり得ます。適合とみなす、有効性は監査の対象外とする、感想にとどめる扱いは誤りです。","qEn":"In an internal audit, the AI system monitoring procedure is documented and carried out, but nobody responds to detected anomalies and it does not lead to achieving objectives. What is the most appropriate determination?","oEn":["A control run as planned but not effective can be treated as a nonconformity on effectiveness","As long as the procedure is documented and carried out, it conforms and is not subject to findings, even if it does not lead to objectives","Effectiveness is not an audit subject and is evaluated only in management review, so internal audit does not flag it","A situation not leading to objectives is merely the auditor's personal opinion, so convey it orally as an impression instead of a nonconformity"],"eEn":"The AIMS is checked for conformity and for being effectively implemented and maintained. A procedure that is run but whose detected anomalies are not acted on and which does not lead to objectives can be a nonconformity on effectiveness. Deeming it conforming, excluding effectiveness from audits, or reducing it to an impression is wrong."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、内部監査で指摘された不適合に是正処置をとりましたが、処置が実際に効果を上げたかを確認しないまま、指摘事項を「完了」として閉じています。是正処置のフォローアップとして最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["処置を実施した時点で指摘事項は解決しているため、有効性の確認は次回の内部監査の対象にしないで、完了として扱う","処置の実施だけで閉じず、原因が除去され再発していないことを確実に確認し、有効性を判断してから閉じるようにする","指摘事項を閉じる判断は被監査部門の責任者が行い、その確認は処置を実施した担当者の報告に基づけばよい","是正処置の有効性は実施直後に一度確認すれば足り、一定期間の経過後に再発の有無を追って確認する必要はない"],"a":1,"e":"処置の実施だけで閉じず、原因が除去され再発していないことを確認し、有効性を判断してから閉じます。実施した時点で完了とする扱い、実施者の報告だけで閉じる扱い、実施直後の一度の確認で足りるとする扱いは、有効性を客観的に確認することを欠きます。","qEn":"A company took corrective action on a nonconformity pointed out in an internal audit but closed the finding as 'complete' without confirming whether the action actually worked. What is the most appropriate point about corrective action follow-up?","oEn":["The finding is resolved at the time of the action, so treat it as complete without making effectiveness confirmation a subject of the next internal audit","Close it only after follow-up confirms the cause was eliminated and the problem has not recurred","The audited department's head decides when to close findings, based on the report of the staff member who carried out the action","Effectiveness of corrective action need only be checked once right after implementation, without following up for recurrence after a period"],"eEn":"Do not close on implementation alone; confirm that the cause is removed and has not recurred, and judge effectiveness before closing. Treating implementation as completion, closing on the implementer's report, or a single check right after implementation lacks objective confirmation of effectiveness."},
{"d":"D5","q":"従業員が少ない会社で、AIMSの運用者全員が自部門の内部監査を担当せざるを得ません。内部監査の客観性を保つ方法として、最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["少人数の組織では独立性の確保が難しいため、運用者が自部門を監査し、客観性は監査チェックリストの標準化で補えば足りる","運用者が自部門を監査する場合でも、監査後に報告書へ署名をすれば、客観性は確保されたものとみなされる","自分の担当業務は監査せず、部門を相互に入れ替える、あるいは外部の専門家に監査を委託して、独立性を確保するようにする","外部の専門家に委託してもよいが、その場合は内部監査ではなく第二者監査に当たり、AIMSの内部監査の要求を満たさない"],"a":2,"e":"自分の担当業務は監査せず、部門を相互に入れ替える、または外部の専門家に監査を委託して、独立性を確保します。チェックリストで客観性を補うとして自己監査を続ける扱い、署名で足りるとする扱い、外部委託では要求を満たさないとする扱いは、監査員の独立性の確保を欠きます。","qEn":"At a company with few employees, every AIMS operator must audit their own department. What is the most appropriate way to maintain the objectivity of internal audit?","oEn":["In small organizations independence is hard, so operators audit their own department and objectivity is supplemented by standardizing the checklist","Even when operators audit their own department, signing the report after the audit is deemed to secure objectivity","Never audit one's own work: swap departments or commission an external expert to secure independence","An external expert may be used, but that is a second-party audit rather than an internal audit and does not meet the AIMS internal audit requirement"],"eEn":"Do not audit your own work; swap departments or outsource to an external expert to secure independence. Continuing self-audit supplemented by a checklist, relying on signatures, or claiming external outsourcing fails the requirement lacks securing auditor independence."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社が、認証機関のサーベイランス審査があるので、その年は自社の内部監査を行わなくてよいと考えています。AIMSの要求の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["認証機関の審査が内部監査を代替するため、審査のある年は、内部監査を省略しても、要求を満たす","内部監査は認証の取得前に一度実施すればよく、取得後は認証機関の審査だけが、継続的な確認になる","内部監査は計画的に実施するが、結果の報告先はAIMS責任者に限り、マネジメントレビューへの入力とはしない","内部監査は審査とは別の要求で、計画した間隔で行い、レビューの入力にもなる"],"a":3,"e":"内部監査は認証機関の審査とは別の要求で、計画した間隔で行い、結果は関連する管理層に報告されマネジメントレビューの入力にもなります。審査で代替する扱い、取得前に一度で足りるとする扱い、報告先を限定してレビューの入力にしない扱いは、内部監査の位置づけを取り違えています。","qEn":"A company thinks it need not perform its own internal audit this year because the certification body's surveillance audit will occur. From the AIMS requirement viewpoint, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["The certification body's audit substitutes for internal audit, so skipping it in a year with an audit still meets the requirement","Internal audit need be performed once before obtaining certification, after which only the certification body's audits provide continuing checking","Conduct internal audits as planned but report only to the AIMS manager, not as an input to management review","Internal audit is a separate AIMS requirement, done at planned intervals, and feeds management review"],"eEn":"Internal audit is a requirement separate from the certification body's audit, conducted at planned intervals, with results reported to relevant management and serving as an input to management review. Substituting certification audits, doing it once before certification, or limiting reporting without feeding the review misreads its role."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社の内部監査は、監査基準を規格本文の条文だけに設定しており、自社のAI方針や手順書、適用される法令の要求は基準に含まれていません。監査基準の設定として最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["規格の要求事項に加え、自社のAIMSの文書（方針、手順）や、組織が取り組むと決めた要求事項も監査基準に含める","監査基準は規格の条文だけに限るべきであり、自社の手順書への適合を確認すると、規格への適合の判定が不明確になるため、含めない","自社の手順書は規格の要求を満たしている場合に限って監査基準に含め、規格に対応しない手順書の項目は監査の対象から外す","法令の要求事項は監査基準に含めてよいが、適合の判定は法務部門の見解に従い、監査員が独自に確認することはできない"],"a":0,"e":"規格の要求事項に加え、自社のAIMSの文書（方針、手順）や、組織が取り組むと決めた要求事項も監査基準に含めます。条文だけに限る扱い、規格に対応しない手順を外す扱い、日常管理に回す扱い、法令の確認を監査員が行えないとする扱いは、監査基準の範囲を狭めます。","qEn":"A company's internal audit sets audit criteria only as the standard's clause text, and does not include its own AI policy, procedures, or applicable legal requirements. What is the most appropriate revision of setting audit criteria?","oEn":["Add the company's own AIMS documents and the requirements it decided to address to the standard's","Audit criteria should be limited to the standard's text, and checking conformity to the company's own procedures would blur the judgment of conformity to the standard, so exclude them","Include company procedures in audit criteria only when they meet the standard, excluding procedure items that do not correspond to it","Legal requirements may be audit criteria, but conformity is determined by the legal department's view and auditors may not check independently"],"eEn":"Audit criteria include, besides the standard's requirements, the organization's own AIMS documents (policies, procedures) and requirements it has decided to address. Limiting to clauses, dropping procedures with no corresponding clause, leaving to daily management, or barring auditors from checking legal requirements narrows the scope."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、新しいAI関連法規制の公表を受けて、現在の目的や管理策の見直しが必要かを判断したいと考えています。PDCAの観点で、この情報を扱うのに最も適切な経路はどれですか。","o":["法務部門が法規制の影響を評価し、必要と判断した場合に限って管理策を変更するが、目的の見直しやマネジメントレビューへの報告は行わない","組織の課題や要求事項の変化として把握し、マネジメントレビューの検討事項として、目的や管理策の変更要否を判断する","変更の要否は次回の認証更新の審査で認証機関が判断するので、組織は、それまで現行の目的や管理策を維持する","法規制の変化は次回の内部監査の準備として監査基準に追加するにとどめ、目的や管理策の変更要否の判断は監査で不適合が指摘された後に行う"],"a":1,"e":"組織の課題や要求事項の変化として把握し、マネジメントレビューの検討事項として、目的や管理策の変更要否を判断します。法務部門だけで扱う扱い、認証機関の判断を待つ扱い、監査基準への追加にとどめて不適合の指摘後に判断する扱いは、PDCAの流れで変更要否を判断することを欠きます。","qEn":"After new AI-related regulation was published, a company wants to judge whether its current objectives and controls need review. From the PDCA viewpoint, what is the most appropriate path to handle this information?","oEn":["The legal department assesses the effect and changes controls only if it judges necessary, without reviewing objectives or reporting to management review","Treat it as a change in issues and requirements and decide at management review whether objectives and controls change","The certification body judges whether changes are needed at the next renewal audit, so maintain current objectives and controls until then","Add regulatory change to audit criteria in preparation for the next audit and judge changes to objectives and controls only after a nonconformity is found"],"eEn":"Grasp it as a change in the organization's issues and requirements and judge in management review whether to change objectives and controls. Handling it only in the legal department, waiting for the certification body, or just adding to audit criteria until a nonconformity appears lacks judging the need for change within the PDCA flow."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社のAI苦情の件数は毎月集計されて報告されていますが、増減の原因分析も、対応が必要かの評価も行われていません。Clause 9.1の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["苦情件数の集計と報告で監視は行われており、分析・評価は内部監査で実施する事項なので、日常の運用では行わない","分析・評価は年に一度の外部審査の直前にまとめて実施すればよく、日常の運用では、集計値の報告で十分である","監視・測定で得たデータを分析・評価し、傾向や原因を把握して、必要な対応や改善につなげる","分析は行うが、結果を対応や改善につなげる判断はマネジメントレビューでのみ行い、それまでは傾向を把握しても対応を決めない"],"a":2,"e":"監視・測定で得たデータを分析・評価し、傾向や原因を把握して、必要な対応や改善につなげます。集計だけで済ませる扱い、分析・評価を内部監査に回す扱い、外部審査の直前にまとめる扱い、対応の判断をレビューまで保留する扱いは、日常の運用の中で分析・評価を活かすことを欠きます。","qEn":"A company tallies and reports AI complaint counts monthly but performs no cause analysis of increases or decreases and no evaluation of whether action is needed. Under Clause 9.1, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Counting and reporting complaints constitutes monitoring, and analysis and evaluation are for internal audit, not routine operation","Analysis and evaluation can be done in a batch just before the annual external audit, and reporting tallies suffices in daily operation","Analyze and evaluate monitoring data to grasp trends and causes and link them to action","Analyze but make decisions to act or improve only at management review, deciding no response in the meantime even when trends are grasped"],"eEn":"Analyze and evaluate the data from monitoring and measurement, grasp trends and causes, and lead to needed action and improvement. Counting only, moving analysis to internal audit, bunching before external audits, or holding decisions until review lacks using analysis and evaluation in daily operation."},
{"d":"D5","q":"AIMSの目的として「AIシステムの影響評価の完了率100%」を掲げていた会社が、1年で達成しました。継続的改善の観点で、最も適切な次の一手はどれですか。","o":["目的の達成はAIMSの有効性が確認されたことを意味するので、以後の改善は目的の達成状況ではなく、不適合が指摘されたときにのみ検討する","達成した目的は取り下げ、翌年は新たな目的を設定せず、AIMSの有効性を内部監査の結果だけで評価する","目的は達成後も同じ水準で維持し、達成率が100%を保てているかを毎年確認することが継続的改善に当たる","達成状況をレビューし、目的を更新するか、より高い水準や別の領域の目的を設定する"],"a":3,"e":"達成状況をレビューし、目的を更新するか、より高い水準や別の領域の目的を設定します。達成で改善を終える扱い、目的を設定しなくなる扱い、同じ水準の維持を改善とみなす扱いは、継続的改善に必要な新たな挑戦を欠きます。","qEn":"A company that set the AIMS objective 'completion rate of 100% for AI system impact assessments' achieved it in one year. From the continual improvement viewpoint, what is the most appropriate next step?","oEn":["Achieving the objective means AIMS effectiveness is confirmed, so further improvement is considered only when nonconformities are pointed out","Withdraw the achieved objective, set no new one next year, and evaluate effectiveness only from internal audit results","Maintain the objective at the same level and confirm yearly that 100% is retained, which constitutes continual improvement","Review the result and update the objective or set higher or new-area objectives"],"eEn":"Review the achievement and update the objective, or set objectives at a higher level or in another area. Ending improvement upon achievement, no longer setting objectives, or regarding maintenance at the same level as improvement lacks the new challenge continual improvement needs."},
{"d":"D5","q":"AIインシデントの対応後、ある会社は担当者への注意喚起だけで終えました。同種のインシデントが別の部署でも起きています。不適合の根本的な是正の観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["担当者への再教育と手順書の周知を実施し、原因の分析は同種のインシデントが3回発生した場合に行う","同種のインシデントは偶発的なものとして扱い、傾向として分析できる程度の件数に達するまでは原因の分析を当面は保留する","個人への注意喚起で終えず、原因を分析して仕組み上の要因を特定し、手順や管理策、教育の見直しなど再発防止の処置をとる","再発防止策は、インシデントを起こした部署の中でのみ実施すれば足り、他の部署へ展開する必要はない"],"a":2,"e":"個人への注意喚起で終えず、原因を分析して仕組み上の要因を特定し、手順や管理策、教育の見直しなど再発防止の処置をとります。再教育のあとの分析を3回目まで待つ扱い、件数がたまるまで保留する扱い、処分で足りるとする扱い、部署内にとどめる扱いは、原因の分析と横展開を欠きます。","qEn":"After responding to an AI incident, a company ended with warnings to the staff member. The same type of incident has occurred in another department. From the viewpoint of fundamental correction of nonconformity, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Retrain staff and circulate the procedures, analyzing causes only if the same kind of incident occurs three times","Treat similar incidents as incidental and hold cause analysis until enough accumulate to analyze as a trend","Analyze the cause, find systemic factors, and fix procedures, controls and training instead of only warning an individual","Preventive measures need be implemented only within the department that caused the incident, with no need to spread them to other departments"],"eEn":"Do not stop at individual warnings; analyze causes, identify systemic factors and take preventive action such as revising procedures, controls and training. Waiting for a third occurrence, holding analysis until counts accumulate, relying on discipline, or keeping it within the department lacks cause analysis and rollout."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、マネジメントレビューを年1回の定例としていますが、期の途中で重大なAIインシデントが起き、新しい法規制も公表されました。レビューの実施時期として最も適切な判断はどれですか。","o":["年1回の定例でのレビューは維持し、インシデントや法規制は担当部署の報告書にまとめて、次の定例のインプットとして扱う","計画した間隔での定例に加え、重大な事態や環境の変化に応じて、必要なら臨時にレビューを行って対応を判断する必要がある","マネジメントレビューは内部監査の完了後に開催するものなので、監査の日程が決まるまでは臨時の開催を検討しない","重大なインシデントへの対応は担当部署が決めればよく、トップマネジメントがレビューの場で判断する必要はない"],"a":1,"e":"計画した間隔での定例に加え、重大な事態や変化に応じて、必要なら臨時にレビューを行って対応を判断します。次の定例まで保留する扱い、内部監査の日程に縛られる扱い、担当部署に任せる扱いは、重大な事態にトップマネジメントが速やかに判断することを欠きます。","qEn":"A company holds management review as an annual routine, but mid-period a serious AI incident occurred and new regulation was published. What is the most appropriate judgment on timing of the review?","oEn":["Keep the annual regular review and compile the incident and regulations into a department report to serve as input to the next regular review","Besides the planned routine, hold an extra review as needed for serious events or changes","Management review follows completion of internal audit, so ad hoc sessions are not considered until the audit schedule is fixed","The responsible department may decide how to respond to a serious incident, and top management need not judge it at review"],"eEn":"In addition to regular planned reviews, hold ad hoc reviews as needed in response to significant events or changes to judge the response. Holding matters until the next regular session, tying it to the audit schedule, or leaving it to departments lacks prompt top management judgment on significant events."},
{"d":"D5","q":"マネジメントレビューで、AIMSの改善に追加の人員と予算が必要だと分かりましたが、会議では議論だけで終わり、資源に関する決定は出ませんでした。レビューの出力として最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["資源の手当てはマネジメントレビューではなく予算編成の会議で決めるものなので、レビューの出力には改善の機会とAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定だけを含める","出力は改善の機会に関する意見の一覧で足り、実施するかどうかの決定は、各部署が自主的に判断する","決定事項は文書化せず、議事録には議論の要旨のみを残し、決定の内容は担当部署への指示メールで伝える","レビューの出力には、改善の機会とAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定を含め、必要な資源の手当ても決めて文書化する"],"a":3,"e":"レビューの出力には、改善の機会とAIMS変更の必要性に関する決定を含め、必要な資源の手当ても決めて文書化します。資源の決定を予算会議に回す扱い、意見の一覧にとどめる扱い、決定を文書化せず指示メールで伝える扱いは、レビューの出力として決定を文書化して保持することを欠きます。","qEn":"At a management review it became clear that improving the AIMS requires additional staff and budget, but the meeting ended with discussion only and no decision on resources. What is the most appropriate point about review outputs?","oEn":["Resource provision is decided at the budget meeting, so the review output contains only decisions on improvement opportunities and need for AIMS change","Outputs suffice as a list of opinions on improvement opportunities, and each department voluntarily decides whether to implement them","Do not document decisions, keeping only a summary of the discussion in the minutes and conveying decisions by instruction emails to departments","Include decisions on improvement opportunities and need for AIMS changes in outputs, also decide the resources needed, and document them"],"eEn":"The review output includes decisions on improvement opportunities and the need for AIMS change, and decides needed resources, documented. Deferring resources to a budget meeting, limiting to a list of opinions, or conveying decisions by email without documentation lacks documented, retained decisions as review outputs."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、AI研修を受けた人数を力量の確保の実績として報告しています。受講後に実務で必要な力量が身についたかは確認していません。Clause 7.2の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["とった処置が力量の確保に有効だったかを評価し、実務での確認や試験などの結果を、証拠として保持する","受講者の人数が目標に達していれば、力量は確保されたとみなせるので、受講後の力量の確認は、受講者の自己評価に任せる","力量の評価は人事評価の領域であり、AIMSの観点では、教育・訓練の実施の事実だけが記録の対象になる","受講後の確認は行わず、翌年の研修の計画の際に受講者へのアンケート結果を参考にして処置の有効性を判断する"],"a":0,"e":"とった処置が力量の確保に有効だったかを評価し、実務での確認や試験などの結果を、証拠として保持します。受講人数で力量を示す扱い、受講の事実だけを記録する扱い、翌年のアンケートで判断する扱いは、実務での力量を確かめることを欠きます。","qEn":"A company reports the number of people who took AI training as evidence of securing competence, without confirming whether the competence needed in practice was acquired. Under Clause 7.2, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Evaluate whether the actions taken were effective, and keep results of practical checks or tests as evidence","If participant numbers reach the target, competence is deemed secured, so leave post-training checks to participants' self-assessment","Competence evaluation is the domain of personnel evaluation, and in the AIMS view only the fact that training was held is recorded","Do no post-training check and judge effectiveness from a survey of attendees when planning next year's training"],"eEn":"Evaluate whether the action taken was effective in securing competence and retain results of practical checks or tests as evidence. Showing competence by attendance counts, recording only attendance, or judging by next year's survey lacks confirming competence in practice."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社の年間内部監査計画は、毎年同じ数部門だけを対象にしており、AIの高リスクな用途を扱う部門が何年も監査されていません。監査プログラムの観点で、最も適切な見直しはどれですか。","o":["リスクの大きさやプロセスの重要性に応じて頻度を決め、一定期間でAIMSの全体が対象になるようにする","監査の対象部門は固定したほうが、年ごとの比較が容易で、被監査部門の負担も一定になるため、現行の対象を維持する","高リスクの部門は、日常の運用管理で十分に監視されているので、内部監査の対象から外して、他の部門に集中する","監査の対象は前回の指摘が多かった部門を優先して決め、指摘のなかった部門は数年間監査の対象から外す"],"a":0,"e":"リスクの大きさやプロセスの重要性に応じて頻度を決め、一定期間でAIMSの全体が対象になるようにします。対象部門の固定、高リスク部門の除外、指摘の多い部門への偏り、自主申告に頼る扱いは、リスクと重要性に応じた頻度と全体の網羅を欠きます。","qEn":"A company's annual internal audit plan covers the same few departments every year, and a department handling high-risk AI uses has gone unaudited for years. What is the most appropriate revision from the audit programme viewpoint?","oEn":["Set frequency by risk size and process importance so the whole AIMS is covered within a set period","Fixing audited departments makes year-to-year comparison easier and keeps the burden on audited departments constant, so keep the current targets","High-risk departments are adequately watched by daily operation management, so remove them from internal audit and concentrate on others","Choose audit targets by prioritizing departments with many earlier findings and exclude those without findings for several years"],"eEn":"Set frequency according to risk and process importance so the whole AIMS is covered over a period. Fixing targets, excluding high-risk departments, concentrating on departments with many findings, or relying on self-declaration lacks risk-based frequency and full coverage."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、AIの誤出力を見つけるたびにその場で修正していますが、なぜ起きたかは調べていません。「修正」と「是正処置」の違いの観点で、最も適切な指摘はどれですか。","o":["修正と是正処置は同じ意味の用語であり、その場で誤りを修正すれば、是正処置も実施したことになる","是正処置は修正よりも軽微な応急措置を指すため、重大な不適合には修正だけを行い、軽微な場合に是正処置を選ぶ","修正は検出された不適合を取り除く応急処置で、是正処置は原因を除去し再発を防ぐ処置であり、両方が必要になる","原因の除去は是正処置として行うが、修正は検出された不適合を記録に残すことを指すので、誤出力の修正そのものは要求に含まれない"],"a":2,"e":"修正は検出された不適合を取り除く応急処置で、是正処置は原因を除去し再発を防ぐ処置であり、両方が必要になります。同じ意味とする扱い、定義を逆にする扱い、修正を記録の意味にすり替える扱いは、修正と是正処置の取り違えです。","qEn":"A company fixes AI erroneous outputs on the spot each time it finds one but does not investigate why they occur. From the viewpoint of the difference between correction and corrective action, what is the most appropriate point?","oEn":["Correction and corrective action are synonyms, so fixing an error on the spot also counts as having carried out corrective action","Corrective action means a lighter stopgap than correction, so apply only correction to serious nonconformities and corrective action to minor ones","Correction removes a detected nonconformity as an immediate fix; corrective action removes the cause to prevent recurrence, and both are needed","Cause removal is corrective action, and correction means recording the detected nonconformity, so fixing the faulty output itself is not covered by the requirements"],"eEn":"Correction is the immediate action eliminating a detected nonconformity, while corrective action removes the cause to prevent recurrence, so both are needed. Treating them as identical, reversing the definitions, or redefining correction as recording confuses correction with corrective action."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、不適合の内容や取った処置、その結果を記録として残しておらず、同じ指摘が数年おきに繰り返されています。Clause 10.2の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["記録は不適合の発生件数の集計だけで十分であり、内容や処置の詳細を残すと運用の負担が増えるため、詳細は取り扱わない","不適合の記録は、重大な事案に限って作成すればよく、軽微なものは記録せずに、口頭での是正で済ませる","処置の結果の記録は是正処置を実施した部門が保持するが、傾向の分析は認証機関が行うので、組織で分析に使う必要はない","不適合の性質ととった処置、是正処置の結果を文書化情報として保持し、傾向の分析や継続的な改善に使えるようにしておく"],"a":3,"e":"不適合の性質ととった処置、是正処置の結果を文書化情報として保持し、傾向の分析や改善に使えるようにします。集計だけの扱い、重大な事案に限る扱い、傾向の分析を認証機関に委ねる扱いは、記録を組織の改善に使うことを欠きます。","qEn":"A company keeps no records of the content of nonconformities, actions taken or their results, and the same findings recur every few years. Under Clause 10.2, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Records need be only a tally of how many nonconformities occurred, and details of content and actions are omitted since they add operational burden","Nonconformity records need be created only for serious cases, and minor ones are handled by oral correction without records","The department that took action keeps the results, but trend analysis is done by the certification body so the organization need not use them for analysis","Keep documented information on the nature of nonconformities, actions taken and results so it can be used for trend analysis and improvement"],"eEn":"Retain the nature of nonconformities, actions taken and corrective action results as documented information so they can be used for trend analysis and improvement. Keeping only counts, limiting to serious cases, or leaving trend analysis to the certification body lacks using records for the organization's improvement."},
{"d":"D5","q":"あるAIシステムの重大インシデントの教訓が、担当チーム内の反省会で終わり、他のAIシステムの開発や運用に共有されていません。継続的改善の観点で、最も適切な仕組みはどれですか。","o":["教訓は担当チームの再発防止策として手順書に反映すれば足り、他のAIシステムの担当者へは、次回のマネジメントレビューの議題として年1回共有する","インシデントの分析結果を、手順や管理策、教育に反映し、他のAIシステムの担当者にも共有する仕組みを設ける","教訓はAIMSの責任者が一括して管理し、必要になった担当者から問い合わせがあった場合にのみ提供する","教訓の共有は、外部の公開資料に載った他社の事例に限り、自社内のインシデントは、共有の対象としない方針とする"],"a":1,"e":"インシデントの分析結果を、手順や管理策、教育に反映し、他のAIシステムの担当者にも共有する仕組みを設けます。チーム内にとどめる扱い、年1回の共有、問い合わせがあったときだけ提供する扱い、他社事例に限る扱いは、教訓を組織全体に速やかに行き渡らせる仕組みを欠きます。","qEn":"Lessons from a serious incident in one AI system ended in a debrief within the responsible team and were not shared with development and operation of other AI systems. From the continual improvement viewpoint, what is the most appropriate mechanism?","oEn":["Reflect lessons in the team's procedures and share with other AI system staff once a year as a management review agenda item","Build a mechanism to reflect analysis results in procedures, controls and training and share them with staff of other AI systems","The AIMS manager holds lessons centrally and provides them only when a staff member who needs them asks","Sharing lessons is limited to other companies' cases in public materials, and the policy is not to share in-house incidents"],"eEn":"Set up a mechanism to reflect incident analysis in procedures, controls and training, and to share it with staff of other AI systems. Keeping it within the team, annual sharing, providing only on request, or limiting to other firms' cases lacks a mechanism to spread lessons promptly across the organization."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、AIの重大な不具合が起きてから件数を数える指標だけを使っています。不具合を未然に防ぐ観点で、追加すべき指標として最も適切なのはどれですか。","o":["影響評価が未完了の高リスクAIの数や、管理策の実施遅れの件数など、問題の発生前に兆候を示す先行指標","先行指標は不具合の件数の予測値として算出するもので、実績の件数による評価に代わるため、現行の遅行指標は廃止して予測値だけを使う","先行指標は、不具合が発生した後にその原因として判明した事項を、遡って記録した指標のことである","先行指標は、外部の認証機関が定める共通の指標に限られるため、組織が自ら設定することはできない"],"a":0,"e":"影響評価が未完了の高リスクAIの数や、管理策の実施遅れの件数など、問題の発生前に兆候を示す先行指標を追加します。遅行指標だけを使う扱い、予測値だけに置き換える扱い、先行指標を遡及記録と取り違える扱い、組織が設定できないとする扱いは、先行指標の性質を誤っています。","qEn":"A company uses only an indicator that counts serious AI defects after they occur. From the viewpoint of preventing defects beforehand, what is the most appropriate indicator to add?","oEn":["Leading indicators that signal trouble beforehand, such as high-risk AI lacking impact assessments or delayed control implementation","Leading indicators are computed as forecast failure counts replacing evaluation by actual counts, so drop the current lagging indicators and use only forecasts","A leading indicator is one that records, retroactively, matters found to be causes after a defect has occurred","Leading indicators are limited to common indicators set by the external certification body, so the organization cannot set its own"],"eEn":"Add leading indicators that show signs before problems occur, such as the number of high-risk AI without completed impact assessment or controls with delayed implementation. Using only lagging indicators, replacing them with forecasts, confusing leading indicators with retrospective records, or saying the organization cannot set them misjudges their nature."},
{"d":"D5","q":"内部監査の指摘に対し、被監査部門が「現場の実態は問題ない」と反論し、監査員は担当者の説明に押されて指摘を取り下げようとしています。監査の進め方として最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["被監査部門の管理者の了承が得られた場合に限り指摘を取り下げ、その場合は取り下げの理由の記録を省略できる","客観的な監査証拠に基づいて判断し、反論があれば追加の証拠を確認したうえで、指摘の維持か修正かを決める","監査員の判断は常に絶対であり、被監査部門の反論は、内容を問わず、聞かずに指摘を維持する","反論があった場合は被監査部門の責任者の判断で指摘の可否を決め、監査員は証拠の追加確認を行わない"],"a":1,"e":"客観的な監査証拠に基づいて判断し、反論があれば追加の証拠を確認したうえで、指摘の維持か修正かを決めます。管理者の了承で取り下げる扱い、被監査部門の責任者が決める扱い、聞かずに維持する扱い、多数決とする扱いは、客観的な証拠に基づく判断を欠きます。","qEn":"An audited department rebuts an internal audit finding saying 'the field situation is fine,' and the auditor, pressed by the staff's explanation, is about to withdraw the finding. What is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Withdraw the finding only with the audited department manager's approval, and the reason for withdrawal need not be recorded","Judge from objective audit evidence, check further evidence on rebuttal, and then decide whether to maintain or amend the finding","The auditor's judgment is always absolute, so maintain the finding without hearing the audited department's rebuttal regardless of content","If objections are raised the audited department head decides whether the finding stands, and the auditor makes no further evidence checks"],"eEn":"Decide on the basis of objective audit evidence, and if objections arise, confirm additional evidence before deciding whether to maintain or revise the finding. Withdrawing on manager approval, letting the audited head decide, maintaining without listening, or voting lacks evidence-based judgment."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社は、AIMSの文書は整っているものの、現場でAI運用の手順が使われているかを確認しておらず、文書と実際の運用が乖離しています。PDCAのDo（実行）の観点で、最も適切な対応はどれですか。","o":["文書の整備でDo（実行）は完了するので、現場での実施の確認はCheck（評価）の段階で内部監査が行うものであり、日常の運用管理の範囲に含めない","手順と異なる運用は現場の工夫として扱い、手順書の改訂は四半期ごとの見直しで追認するが、差異の把握そのものは求められない","計画した運用プロセスを現場で実施・管理し、実施の確信を得るのに必要な記録を保持して、乖離を監視で把握する","文書と運用の乖離は、文書が古いことだけが原因なので、現場の運用を確認せず、文書を毎年全面改訂すれば解消する"],"a":2,"e":"計画した運用プロセスを現場で実施・管理し、実施の確信を得るのに必要な記録を保持して、乖離を監視で把握します。文書整備でDoが終わるとする扱い、現場の工夫として追認する扱い、文書の全面改訂だけで解消するとする扱いは、現場での実施の管理と乖離の把握を欠きます。","qEn":"A company has AIMS documents in order but does not check whether AI operating procedures are used in the field, so documents and actual operation diverge. From the PDCA Do viewpoint, what is the most appropriate response?","oEn":["Documentation completes Do, and checking field implementation is for internal audit in Check, outside day-to-day operational control","Treat deviations from procedure as field ingenuity, ratify them in quarterly revisions, but identifying the differences is not required","Carry out and control planned processes in the field, keep the records needed for confidence, and detect divergence through monitoring","Divergence is caused only by outdated documents, so fully revising documents every year resolves it without checking field operation"],"eEn":"Implement and control the planned operating processes in the field, retain the records needed for confidence in implementation, and grasp deviations through monitoring. Treating documentation as completing Do, ratifying deviations as ingenuity, or relying on full revisions lacks field control and deviation awareness."},
{"d":"D5","q":"ある会社では、AIの公平性指標を拠点ごとに異なる方法と異なる時期で測定しており、結果を比較できず、評価の根拠にも使えません。Clause 9.1の観点で、最も適切な是正はどれですか。","o":["拠点ごとの事情を尊重して測定の方法も時期も各拠点の裁量に任せ、結果の比較は、全社の評価では行わないことにする","測定の方法は全社で統一するが、実施時期は各拠点の繁忙期を避けて任意に決められるようにし、結果の比較は同一時期のものに限らない","測定は内部監査の実施時に合わせて行えば足り、日常の監視・測定の方法や時期を定める必要はない","妥当な結果が得られる監視・測定の方法と実施時期を定め、拠点間で比較できる形に統一する"],"a":3,"e":"妥当な結果が得られる監視・測定の方法と実施時期を定め、拠点間で比較できる形に統一します。拠点任せで比較しない扱い、時期をそろえずに比較する扱い、内部監査時だけ測定する扱いは、比較可能な結果を得る方法と時期の統一を欠きます。","qEn":"A company measures AI fairness indicators with different methods and at different times at each site, so results cannot be compared or used as grounds for evaluation. Under Clause 9.1, what is the most appropriate corrective?","oEn":["Respect each site's circumstances by leaving methods and timing to each site's discretion, and do not compare results in the company-wide evaluation","Unify the measurement method company-wide but let sites choose timing to avoid busy periods, comparing results not limited to the same period","Measure at the time of internal audit and there is no need to define the routine monitoring and measurement method or timing","Define measurement methods and timing that yield valid results, and unify them so sites are comparable"],"eEn":"Determine monitoring and measurement methods and timing that yield valid results, and unify them so sites are comparable. Leaving it to sites without comparison, comparing results from differing periods, or measuring only at internal audit lacks unified methods and timing for comparable results."}
];
  const EXAM_SETS = buildHardSets_AB(ISO42001F_HARD, { D1:10, D2:14, D3:10, D4:7, D5:7 }, 5);
const DOMAIN_SETS = Object.fromEntries(DOMAINS.map(d => [d.id, BANK.filter(q => q.d === d.id)]));

const CONFUSE = [
  ["リスクアセスメント / 影響評価", "リスクアセスメントは組織にとってのリスクを特定・分析・評価する。AIシステム影響評価は個人・社会（データ主体等）への影響に焦点を当てる。", "組織リスク中心ならリスクアセスメント、個人・社会への影響中心なら影響評価。", "Risk assessment / Impact assessment", "Risk assessment identifies/analyzes/evaluates risk to the organization. AI system impact assessment focuses on effects on individuals and society.", "Org-risk focus = risk assessment; individual/society impact = impact assessment."],
  ["Annex A / 適用宣言書（SoA）", "Annex Aは参照用の管理策の一覧。SoAはそのうちどれを適用し・除外するか、理由とともに示す文書。", "管理策の一覧がAnnex A、適用可否と理由を示すのがSoA。", "Annex A / Statement of Applicability (SoA)", "Annex A is a reference list of controls. The SoA states which are applied or excluded, with justification.", "Controls list = Annex A; applicability and rationale = SoA."],
  ["内部監査 / 認証審査", "内部監査は組織自身がAIMSの適合・有効性を確認する。認証審査は外部の認証機関が適合を審査する。", "自組織が行うのが内部監査、外部機関が行うのが認証審査。", "Internal audit / Certification audit", "Internal audit is the organization checking its own AIMS conformity/effectiveness. Certification audit is an external body assessing conformity.", "Self = internal audit; external body = certification audit."],
  ["是正処置 / 継続的改善", "是正処置は発生した不適合の原因を除去する対応。継続的改善はAIMS全体の有効性を継続的に高める広い活動。", "不適合への個別対応が是正処置、全体を継続的に高めるのが継続的改善。", "Corrective action / Continual improvement", "Corrective action removes the cause of an occurred nonconformity. Continual improvement is the broader ongoing enhancement of the AIMS.", "Fixing a nonconformity = corrective action; ongoing enhancement = continual improvement."],
  ["ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 23894", "42001はAIマネジメントシステムの要求事項（認証可能）。23894はAIリスクマネジメントの指針（ガイダンス）。", "認証可能なMS規格が42001、リスク管理の指針が23894。", "ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 23894", "42001 sets requirements for an AI management system (certifiable). 23894 gives guidance on AI risk management.", "Certifiable MS standard = 42001; risk-management guidance = 23894."],

  ["ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 22989", "42001はAIMSの要求事項（認証可能）。22989はAIの概念と用語を定めるガイダンス（用語の共通基盤）。", "要求事項の規格が42001、AIの用語・概念を定めるのが22989。", "ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 22989", "42001 sets certifiable AIMS requirements. 22989 provides AI concepts and terminology (a shared vocabulary).", "Requirements standard = 42001; AI concepts/terminology = 22989."],
  ["ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 27001", "42001はAIの責任ある管理（AIMS）。27001は情報セキュリティ管理（ISMS）。ともにHLSで統合しやすいが対象領域が異なる。", "対象がAI管理なら42001、情報セキュリティなら27001。", "ISO/IEC 42001 / ISO/IEC 27001", "42001 manages responsible AI (AIMS). 27001 manages information security (ISMS). Both share the HLS but cover different domains.", "AI management = 42001; information security = 27001."],
  ["AI方針 / AI目的", "AI方針はトップが示す意図・方向性の枠組み。AI目的は方針と整合し、測定可能で達成すべき具体的な狙い。", "方向性の枠組みが方針、測定可能な具体目標が目的。", "AI policy / AI objectives", "The AI policy is top management's framework of intent and direction. AI objectives are specific, measurable aims consistent with the policy.", "Direction/framework = policy; measurable targets = objectives."],
  ["力量 / 認識", "力量は意図した結果を出すのに必要な知識・技能。認識は方針・自らの貢献・不適合の意味などを理解している状態。", "できる能力が力量、理解している状態が認識。", "Competence / Awareness", "Competence is the knowledge/skills needed to achieve intended results. Awareness is understanding the policy, one's contribution, and implications of nonconformity.", "Ability to perform = competence; understanding/knowing = awareness."],
  ["監視・測定 / 内部監査", "監視・測定（9.1）はパフォーマンスや管理策の状態を継続的に把握する活動。内部監査（9.2）は基準への適合を計画的に検証する監査。", "日常的な把握が監視・測定、計画的な適合検証が内部監査。", "Monitoring/measurement / Internal audit", "Monitoring and measurement (9.1) continuously tracks performance and controls. Internal audit (9.2) is a planned check of conformity against criteria.", "Ongoing tracking = monitoring; planned conformity check = internal audit."],
  ["マネジメントレビュー / 内部監査", "内部監査は担当者が適合・有効性を検証する。マネジメントレビューはトップがAIMSの適切性・妥当性・有効性を評価し方向づける。", "実務者が検証するのが内部監査、トップが評価・方向づけするのがレビュー。", "Management review / Internal audit", "Internal audit verifies conformity/effectiveness. Management review is top management evaluating the AIMS's suitability, adequacy, and effectiveness and setting direction.", "Practitioner verification = internal audit; top-management evaluation = management review."],
  ["修正 / 是正処置", "修正（correction）は検出された不適合を直ちに取り除く応急処置。是正処置はその原因を除去し再発を防ぐ処置。", "その場の手当てが修正、原因除去と再発防止が是正処置。", "Correction / Corrective action", "Correction is the immediate action to eliminate a detected nonconformity. Corrective action removes its cause to prevent recurrence.", "Immediate fix = correction; cause removal/prevention = corrective action."],
  ["リスク評価 / リスク対応", "リスク評価（evaluation）はリスクを基準と照らして優先順位づけする判断。リスク対応（treatment）は回避・低減・移転・受容などの選択と実施。", "優先順位づけの判断がリスク評価、対策の選択・実施がリスク対応。", "Risk evaluation / Risk treatment", "Risk evaluation compares risk against criteria to prioritize. Risk treatment selects and applies options such as avoid, reduce, share, or accept.", "Prioritization decision = evaluation; selecting/applying measures = treatment."],
  ["認証 / 認定", "認証（certification）は認証機関が組織のAIMSの適合を証明すること。認定（accreditation）は認定機関がその認証機関の力量を公式に承認すること。", "組織を認めるのが認証、認証機関を認めるのが認定。", "Certification / Accreditation", "Certification is a certification body attesting an organization's AIMS conformity. Accreditation is an accreditation body formally recognizing that certification body's competence.", "Recognizing the organization = certification; recognizing the certification body = accreditation."],
  ["管理策 / 管理目的", "管理策（control）はリスクを修正する個々の手段。管理目的（control objective）はその管理策群が達成すべき狙い・到達点。", "個々の手段が管理策、達成すべき狙いが管理目的。", "Control / Control objective", "A control is an individual measure that modifies risk. A control objective is the aim the related controls are meant to achieve.", "Individual measure = control; the aim to achieve = control objective."],
];

